<span id="S2.SS1.SSS2.p6.pic1.1" class="ltx_inline-block ltx_minipage ltx_align_bottom" style="width:25.16em;">
<span id="S2.SS1.SSS2.p6.pic1.1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S2.SS1.SSS2.p6.pic1.1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold" style="font-size:80%;--ltx-fg-color:#FFFFFF;">Problem 0: SLE concepts and transformation laws</span></span>
</span></span></span></foreignObject></g><g fill-opacity="1.0" transform="matrix(1.0 0.0 0.0 1.0 20.38 127.75)"><foreignObject style="--ltx-fo-width:29.01em;--ltx-fo-height:3.9em;--ltx-fo-depth:8.33em;font-size:10pt;" height="169.16" overflow="visible" transform="matrix(1 0 0 -1 0 53.9)" width="401.42"><span class="ltx_foreignobject_container"><span class="ltx_foreignobject_content">
<span id="S2.SS1.SSS2.p6.pic1.2" class="ltx_inline-block ltx_minipage ltx_align_bottom" style="width:29.01em;">
<span id="S2.SS1.SSS2.p6.pic1.2.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S2.SS1.SSS2.p6.pic1.2.1.1" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:80%;--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">Schramm–Loewner Evolution (SLE) is a vibrant field in modern probability theory. Please address the following two parts:</span></span>
<span id="S2.I5" class="ltx_enumerate">
<span id="S2.I5.i1" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">1.</span> 
<span id="S2.I5.i1.p1" class="ltx_para">
<span id="S2.I5.i1.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S2.I5.i1.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:80%;--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">Provide the precise definition of SLE, emphasizing its construction via the Loewner equation driven by a random function </span><math id="S2.I5.i1.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="W_{t}=\sqrt{\kappa}B_{t}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" mathsize="0.800em">W</mi><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" mathsize="0.800em">t</mi></msub><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" mathsize="0.800em">=</mo><mrow><msqrt style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000"><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" mathsize="0.800em">κ</mi></msqrt><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" mathsize="0.800em">B</mi><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" mathsize="0.800em">t</mi></msub></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">W_{t}=\sqrt{\kappa}B_{t}</annotation></semantics></math><span id="S2.I5.i1.p1.1.2" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:80%;--ltx-fg-color:#000000;"> where </span><math id="S2.I5.i1.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="B_{t}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" mathsize="0.800em">B</mi><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" mathsize="0.800em">t</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">B_{t}</annotation></semantics></math><span id="S2.I5.i1.p1.1.3" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:80%;--ltx-fg-color:#000000;"> is the standard Brownian motion.</span></span>
</span></span>
<span id="S2.I5.i2" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">2.</span> 
<span id="S2.I5.i2.p1" class="ltx_para">
<span id="S2.I5.i2.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S2.I5.i2.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:80%;--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">Please state the transformation law of the driving functions of Loewner chain under conformal Maps.</span></span>
</span>
<span id="S2.I5.i2.p2" class="ltx_para"><span class="ltx_inline-block"><svg id="S2.I5.i2.p2.pic1" class="ltx_picture" color="#FF0000" height="18.24" overflow="visible" style="vertical-align:-4.1px" version="1.1" viewBox="0 0 18.24 18.24" width="18.24"><g style="--ltx-stroke-color:#FF0000;--ltx-fill-color:#FF0000;" fill="#FF0000" stroke="#FF0000" stroke-width="1.8pt" transform="translate(0,18.24) matrix(1 0 0 -1 0 0) translate(1.25,0) translate(0,1.25)"><path style="fill:none" d="M 0 0 L 15.75 15.75 M 0 15.75 L 15.75 0"></path></g></svg></span>
<span id="S2.I5.i2.p2.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S2.I5.i2.p2.1.1" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:80%;--ltx-fg-color:#FF0000;">GPT-5 thinking failed</span></span>
</span></span>
</span>
</span></span></span></foreignObject></g></g></svg></span>
</div>
          
</div></div></div>
</figure>
</section>
</section>
<section id="S2.SS2" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">2 </span>Understanding Knowledge and Theory Mastery</h3>

<div id="S2.SS2.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S2.SS2.p1.1" class="ltx_p">This category assesses the ability to comprehend and correctly apply established mathematical results and theorems.</p>
</div>
<section id="S2.SS2.SSS1" class="ltx_subsubsection">
<h4 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsubsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsubsection">(a) </span>Understanding theorems</h4>

<div id="S2.SS2.SSS1.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S2.SS2.SSS1.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Demonstrate accurate recall of classical theorems, including their assumptions, conclusions, and logical structure. For example, recognizing that the Extreme Value Theorem requires continuity over a compact interval, and understanding its dependence on the completeness of real numbers.</p>
</div>
<div id="S2.SS2.SSS1.p2" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S2.SS2.SSS1.p2.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S2.SS2.SSS1.p2.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Design Principles:</span>
Include content that is well-known among experts but rarely emphasized in standard textbooks.</p>
</div>
<div id="S2.SS2.SSS1.p3" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S2.SS2.SSS1.p3.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S2.SS2.SSS1.p3.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Sample Problems:</span></p>
</div>
<figure id="S2.SS2.SSS1.fig1" class="ltx_figure">
<div id="S2.SS2.SSS1.fig1.1" class="ltx_logical-block ltx_minipage ltx_align_center ltx_align_top" style="width:276.0pt;">
            
<div id="S2.SS2.SSS1.p4" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent"><span class="ltx_inline-block"><svg id="S2.SS2.SSS1.p4.pic1" class="ltx_picture" height="104.91" overflow="visible" version="1.1" viewBox="0 0 381.9 104.91" width="381.9"><g style="--ltx-stroke-color:#000000;--ltx-fill-color:#000000;" fill="#000000" stroke="#000000" stroke-width="0.4pt" transform="translate(0,104.91) matrix(1 0 0 -1 0 0)"><g style="--ltx-fill-color:#3D6666;" fill="#3D6666" fill-opacity="1.0"><path style="stroke:none" d="M 0 4.63 L 0 100.28 C 0 102.84 2.07 104.91 4.63 104.91 L 377.27 104.91 C 379.83 104.91 381.9 102.84 381.9 100.28 L 381.9 4.63 C 381.9 2.07 379.83 0 377.27 0 L 4.63 0 C 2.07 0 0 2.07 0 4.63 Z"></path></g><g style="--ltx-fill-color:#FFFFFF;" fill="#FFFFFF" fill-opacity="1.0"><path style="stroke:none" d="M 0.69 4.63 L 0.69 69.21 L 381.21 69.21 L 381.21 4.63 C 381.21 2.45 379.45 0.69 377.27 0.69 L 4.63 0.69 C 2.45 0.69 0.69 2.45 0.69 4.63 Z"></path></g><g fill-opacity="1.0" transform="matrix(1.0 0.0 0.0 1.0 20.38 92.6)"><foreignObject style="--ltx-fo-width:25.16em;--ltx-fo-height:0.56em;--ltx-fo-depth:1.36em;font-size:10pt;" height="26.44" overflow="visible" transform="matrix(1 0 0 -1 0 7.69)" width="348.14"><span class="ltx_foreignobject_container"><span class="ltx_foreignobject_content">
<span id="S2.SS2.SSS1.p4.pic1.1" class="ltx_inline-block ltx_minipage ltx_align_bottom" style="width:25.16em;">
<span id="S2.SS2.SSS1.p4.pic1.1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S2.SS2.SSS1.p4.pic1.1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold" style="font-size:80%;--ltx-fg-color:#FFFFFF;">Problem 0: Derive null vector equations for multiple SLE systems</span></span>
</span></span></span></foreignObject></g><g fill-opacity="1.0" transform="matrix(1.0 0.0 0.0 1.0 20.38 14.66)"><foreignObject style="--ltx-fo-width:29.01em;--ltx-fo-height:3.66em;--ltx-fo-depth:0.16em;font-size:10pt;" height="52.77" overflow="visible" transform="matrix(1 0 0 -1 0 50.62)" width="401.42"><span class="ltx_foreignobject_container"><span class="ltx_foreignobject_content">
<span id="S2.SS2.SSS1.p4.pic1.2" class="ltx_inline-block ltx_minipage ltx_align_bottom" style="width:29.01em;">
<span id="S2.SS2.SSS1.p4.pic1.2.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S2.SS2.SSS1.p4.pic1.2.1.1" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:80%;--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">Derive the null vector equations from commutation relations of multiple chordal SLE(<math id="S2.SS2.SSS1.p4.pic1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\kappa" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">κ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\kappa</annotation></semantics></math>).</span></span><span class="ltx_inline-block"><svg id="S2.SS2.SSS1.p4.pic1.pic1" class="ltx_picture" color="#FF0000" height="18.24" overflow="visible" style="vertical-align:-4.1px" version="1.1" viewBox="0 0 18.24 18.24" width="18.24"><g style="--ltx-stroke-color:#FF0000;--ltx-fill-color:#FF0000;" fill="#FF0000" stroke="#FF0000" stroke-width="1.8pt" transform="translate(0,18.24) matrix(1 0 0 -1 0 0) translate(1.25,0) translate(0,1.25)"><path style="fill:none" d="M 0 0 L 15.75 15.75 M 0 15.75 L 15.75 0"></path></g></svg></span>
<span id="S2.SS2.SSS1.p4.pic1.2.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="S2.SS2.SSS1.p4.pic1.2.2.1" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:80%;--ltx-fg-color:#FF0000;">GPT-5 thinking failed</span></span>
</span></span></span></foreignObject></g></g></svg></span>
</div>
          
</div>
</figure>
</section>
<section id="S2.SS2.SSS2" class="ltx_subsubsection">
<h4 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsubsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsubsection">(b) </span>Applying classical results</h4>

<div id="S2.SS2.SSS2.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S2.SS2.SSS2.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Fluently use known theorems to solve standard, composite, or multi-step problems.</p>
</div>
<div id="S2.SS2.SSS2.p2" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S2.SS2.SSS2.p2.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S2.SS2.SSS2.p2.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Design Principles:</span>
Choose problems that require straightforward applications of a very complicated theorem.</p>
</div>
<div id="S2.SS2.SSS2.p3" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S2.SS2.SSS2.p3.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S2.SS2.SSS2.p3.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Sample Problems:</span></p>
</div>
<figure id="S2.SS2.SSS2.fig1" class="ltx_figure">
<div id="S2.SS2.SSS2.fig1.1" class="ltx_logical-block ltx_minipage ltx_align_center ltx_align_top" style="width:276.0pt;">
            
<div id="S2.SS2.SSS2.p4" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent"><span class="ltx_inline-block"><svg id="S2.SS2.SSS2.p4.pic1" class="ltx_picture" height="120.9" overflow="visible" version="1.1" viewBox="0 0 381.9 120.9" width="381.9"><g style="--ltx-stroke-color:#000000;--ltx-fill-color:#000000;" fill="#000000" stroke="#000000" stroke-width="0.4pt" transform="translate(0,120.9) matrix(1 0 0 -1 0 0)"><g style="--ltx-fill-color:#3D6666;" fill="#3D6666" fill-opacity="1.0"><path style="stroke:none" d="M 0 4.63 L 0 116.27 C 0 118.83 2.07 120.9 4.63 120.9 L 377.27 120.9 C 379.83 120.9 381.9 118.83 381.9 116.27 L 381.9 4.63 C 381.9 2.07 379.83 0 377.27 0 L 4.63 0 C 2.07 0 0 2.07 0 4.63 Z"></path></g><g style="--ltx-fill-color:#FFFFFF;" fill="#FFFFFF" fill-opacity="1.0"><path style="stroke:none" d="M 0.69 4.63 L 0.69 101.8 L 381.21 101.8 L 381.21 4.63 C 381.21 2.45 379.45 0.69 377.27 0.69 L 4.63 0.69 C 2.45 0.69 0.69 2.45 0.69 4.63 Z"></path></g><g fill-opacity="1.0" transform="matrix(1.0 0.0 0.0 1.0 20.38 108.59)"><foreignObject style="--ltx-fo-width:25.16em;--ltx-fo-height:0.56em;--ltx-fo-depth:0.16em;font-size:10pt;" height="9.84" overflow="visible" transform="matrix(1 0 0 -1 0 7.69)" width="348.14"><span class="ltx_foreignobject_container"><span class="ltx_foreignobject_content">
<span id="S2.SS2.SSS2.p4.pic1.1" class="ltx_inline-block ltx_minipage ltx_align_bottom" style="width:25.16em;">
<span id="S2.SS2.SSS2.p4.pic1.1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S2.SS2.SSS2.p4.pic1.1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold" style="font-size:80%;--ltx-fg-color:#FFFFFF;">Problem 0: Apply s-cobordism to show diffeomorphism</span></span>
</span></span></span></foreignObject></g><g fill-opacity="1.0" transform="matrix(1.0 0.0 0.0 1.0 20.38 14.66)"><foreignObject style="--ltx-fo-width:29.01em;--ltx-fo-height:6.01em;--ltx-fo-depth:0.16em;font-size:10pt;" height="85.37" overflow="visible" transform="matrix(1 0 0 -1 0 83.21)" width="401.42"><span class="ltx_foreignobject_container"><span class="ltx_foreignobject_content">
<span id="S2.SS2.SSS2.p4.pic1.2" class="ltx_inline-block ltx_minipage ltx_align_bottom" style="width:29.01em;">
<span id="S2.SS2.SSS2.p4.pic1.2.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S2.SS2.SSS2.p4.pic1.2.1.1" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:80%;--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">Apply the s-cobordism theorem to show that if <math id="S2.SS2.SSS2.p4.pic1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="M" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">M</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">M</annotation></semantics></math> is a smooth <math id="S2.SS2.SSS2.p4.pic1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="7" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">7</mn><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">7</annotation></semantics></math>-manifold homotopy equivalent to <math id="S2.SS2.SSS2.p4.pic1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="S^{1}\times S^{6}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msup><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">S</mi><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">1</mn></msup><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" lspace="0.222em" mathcolor="#000000" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><msup><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">S</mi><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">6</mn></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">S^{1}\times S^{6}</annotation></semantics></math>, which bounds an <math id="S2.SS2.SSS2.p4.pic1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="8" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">8</mn><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">8</annotation></semantics></math>-manifold <math id="S2.SS2.SSS2.p4.pic1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="W" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">W</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">W</annotation></semantics></math> homotopy equivalent to <math id="S2.SS2.SSS2.p4.pic1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="S^{1}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">S</mi><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">1</mn></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">S^{1}</annotation></semantics></math>, then <math id="S2.SS2.SSS2.p4.pic1.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="M" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">M</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">M</annotation></semantics></math> is diffeomorphic to <math id="S2.SS2.SSS2.p4.pic1.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="S^{1}\times S^{6}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msup><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">S</mi><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">1</mn></msup><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" lspace="0.222em" mathcolor="#000000" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><msup><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">S</mi><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">6</mn></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">S^{1}\times S^{6}</annotation></semantics></math>.</span></span><span class="ltx_inline-block"><svg id="S2.SS2.SSS2.p4.pic1.pic1" class="ltx_picture" color="#FF0000" height="18.24" overflow="visible" style="vertical-align:-4.1px" version="1.1" viewBox="0 0 18.24 18.24" width="18.24"><g style="--ltx-stroke-color:#FF0000;--ltx-fill-color:#FF0000;" fill="#FF0000" stroke="#FF0000" stroke-width="1.8pt" transform="translate(0,18.24) matrix(1 0 0 -1 0 0) translate(1.25,0) translate(0,1.25)"><path style="fill:none" d="M 0 0 L 15.75 15.75 M 0 15.75 L 15.75 0"></path></g></svg></span>
<span id="S2.SS2.SSS2.p4.pic1.2.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="S2.SS2.SSS2.p4.pic1.2.2.1" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:80%;--ltx-fg-color:#FF0000;">GPT-5 thinking failed</span></span>
</span></span></span></foreignObject></g></g></svg></span>
</div>
          
</div>
</figure>
</section>
</section>
<section id="S2.SS3" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">3 </span>Computational and Analytical Skills</h3>

<div id="S2.SS3.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S2.SS3.p1.1" class="ltx_p">This category evaluates a model’s ability to perform accurate computations and symbolic manipulation.</p>
</div>
<section id="S2.SS3.SSS1" class="ltx_subsubsection">
<h4 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsubsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsubsection">(a) </span>Computational fluency</h4>

<div id="S2.SS3.SSS1.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S2.SS3.SSS1.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Accurately compute integrals, derivatives, limits, matrix operations, and other standard calculations.</p>
</div>
<div id="S2.SS3.SSS1.p2" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S2.SS3.SSS1.p2.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S2.SS3.SSS1.p2.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Design Principles:</span>
Choose problems that require difficult, complicated computations.</p>
</div>
<div id="S2.SS3.SSS1.p3" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S2.SS3.SSS1.p3.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S2.SS3.SSS1.p3.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Sample Problems:</span></p>
</div>
<figure id="S2.SS3.SSS1.fig1" class="ltx_figure">
<div id="S2.SS3.SSS1.fig1.1" class="ltx_logical-block ltx_minipage ltx_align_center ltx_align_top" style="width:276.0pt;">
            
<div id="S2.SS3.SSS1.p4" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent"><span class="ltx_inline-block"><svg id="S2.SS3.SSS1.p4.pic1" class="ltx_picture" height="123.42" overflow="visible" version="1.1" viewBox="0 0 381.9 123.42" width="381.9"><g style="--ltx-stroke-color:#000000;--ltx-fill-color:#000000;" fill="#000000" stroke="#000000" stroke-width="0.4pt" transform="translate(0,123.42) matrix(1 0 0 -1 0 0)"><g style="--ltx-fill-color:#3D6666;" fill="#3D6666" fill-opacity="1.0"><path style="stroke:none" d="M 0 4.63 L 0 118.79 C 0 121.35 2.07 123.42 4.63 123.42 L 377.27 123.42 C 379.83 123.42 381.9 121.35 381.9 118.79 L 381.9 4.63 C 381.9 2.07 379.83 0 377.27 0 L 4.63 0 C 2.07 0 0 2.07 0 4.63 Z"></path></g><g style="--ltx-fill-color:#FFFFFF;" fill="#FFFFFF" fill-opacity="1.0"><path style="stroke:none" d="M 0.69 4.63 L 0.69 104.32 L 381.21 104.32 L 381.21 4.63 C 381.21 2.45 379.45 0.69 377.27 0.69 L 4.63 0.69 C 2.45 0.69 0.69 2.45 0.69 4.63 Z"></path></g><g fill-opacity="1.0" transform="matrix(1.0 0.0 0.0 1.0 20.38 111.11)"><foreignObject style="--ltx-fo-width:25.16em;--ltx-fo-height:0.56em;--ltx-fo-depth:0.16em;font-size:10pt;" height="9.84" overflow="visible" transform="matrix(1 0 0 -1 0 7.69)" width="348.14"><span class="ltx_foreignobject_container"><span class="ltx_foreignobject_content">
<span id="S2.SS3.SSS1.p4.pic1.1" class="ltx_inline-block ltx_minipage ltx_align_bottom" style="width:25.16em;">
<span id="S2.SS3.SSS1.p4.pic1.1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S2.SS3.SSS1.p4.pic1.1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold" style="font-size:80%;--ltx-fg-color:#FFFFFF;">Problem 0: Evaluate the integral</span></span>
</span></span></span></foreignObject></g><g fill-opacity="1.0" transform="matrix(1.0 0.0 0.0 1.0 20.38 14.66)"><foreignObject style="--ltx-fo-width:29.01em;--ltx-fo-height:6.2em;--ltx-fo-depth:0.16em;font-size:10pt;" height="87.89" overflow="visible" transform="matrix(1 0 0 -1 0 85.73)" width="401.42"><span class="ltx_foreignobject_container"><span class="ltx_foreignobject_content">
<span id="S2.SS3.SSS1.p4.pic1.2" class="ltx_inline-block ltx_minipage ltx_align_bottom" style="width:29.01em;">
<span id="S2.Ex1" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<span><span class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<span class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></span>
<span class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S2.Ex1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="I=\int_{0}^{1}\frac{\log\left(1+x^{2+\sqrt{3}}\right)}{1+x}\,dx." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" mathsize="0.800em">I</mi><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" mathsize="0.800em" rspace="0.111em">=</mo><mrow><msubsup><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" maxsize="0.800em" minsize="0.800em" stretchy="true">∫</mo><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" mathsize="0.800em">0</mn><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" mathsize="0.800em">1</mn></msubsup><mrow><mfrac style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000"><mrow><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" mathsize="0.800em">log</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">(</mo><mrow><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" mathsize="0.800em">1</mn><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" mathsize="0.800em">+</mo><msup><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" mathsize="0.800em">x</mi><mrow><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" mathsize="0.800em">2</mn><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" mathsize="0.800em">+</mo><msqrt style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000"><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" mathsize="0.800em">3</mn></msqrt></mrow></msup></mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mrow><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" mathsize="0.800em">1</mn><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" mathsize="0.800em">+</mo><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" mathsize="0.800em">x</mi></mrow></mfrac><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" mathsize="0.800em" rspace="0em">𝑑</mo><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" mathsize="0.800em">x</mi></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" lspace="0em" mathcolor="#000000" mathsize="0.800em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">I=\int_{0}^{1}\frac{\log\left(1+x^{2+\sqrt{3}}\right)}{1+x}\,dx.</annotation></semantics></math></span>
<span class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></span></span></span>
</span>
<span id="S2.SS3.SSS1.p4.pic1.2.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S2.SS3.SSS1.p4.pic1.2.1.1" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:80%;--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">Evaluate this definite integral and express your answer in terms of elementary functions (such as logarithms, powers, trigonometric functions, etc.).</span></span><span class="ltx_inline-block"><svg id="S2.SS3.SSS1.p4.pic1.pic1" class="ltx_picture" color="#FF0000" height="18.24" overflow="visible" style="vertical-align:-4.1px" version="1.1" viewBox="0 0 18.24 18.24" width="18.24"><g style="--ltx-stroke-color:#FF0000;--ltx-fill-color:#FF0000;" fill="#FF0000" stroke="#FF0000" stroke-width="1.8pt" transform="translate(0,18.24) matrix(1 0 0 -1 0 0) translate(1.25,0) translate(0,1.25)"><path style="fill:none" d="M 0 0 L 15.75 15.75 M 0 15.75 L 15.75 0"></path></g></svg></span>
<span id="S2.SS3.SSS1.p4.pic1.2.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="S2.SS3.SSS1.p4.pic1.2.2.1" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:80%;--ltx-fg-color:#FF0000;">GPT-5 thinking failed</span></span>
</span></span></span></foreignObject></g></g></svg></span>
</div>
          
</div>
</figure>
</section>
<section id="S2.SS3.SSS2" class="ltx_subsubsection">
<h4 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsubsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsubsection">(b) </span>Symbolic manipulation</h4>

<div id="S2.SS3.SSS2.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S2.SS3.SSS2.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Simplify or transform algebraic expressions through substitution, factoring, expansion, or equation rearrangement. (The software Mathematica might be easy to solve)</p>
</div>
<div id="S2.SS3.SSS2.p2" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S2.SS3.SSS2.p2.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S2.SS3.SSS2.p2.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Design Principles:</span>
Choose problems that require complicated symbolic transformation to reach the solution.</p>
</div>
<div id="S2.SS3.SSS2.p3" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S2.SS3.SSS2.p3.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S2.SS3.SSS2.p3.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Sample Problems:</span></p>
</div>
<figure id="S2.SS3.SSS2.fig1" class="ltx_figure">
<div id="S2.SS3.SSS2.fig1.1" class="ltx_logical-block ltx_minipage ltx_align_center ltx_align_top" style="width:276.0pt;">
            
<div id="S2.SS3.SSS2.p4" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent"><span class="ltx_inline-block"><svg id="S2.SS3.SSS2.p4.pic1" class="ltx_picture" height="146.42" overflow="visible" version="1.1" viewBox="0 0 381.9 146.42" width="381.9"><g style="--ltx-stroke-color:#000000;--ltx-fill-color:#000000;" fill="#000000" stroke="#000000" stroke-width="0.4pt" transform="translate(0,146.42) matrix(1 0 0 -1 0 0)"><g style="--ltx-fill-color:#3D6666;" fill="#3D6666" fill-opacity="1.0"><path style="stroke:none" d="M 0 4.63 L 0 141.79 C 0 144.35 2.07 146.42 4.63 146.42 L 377.27 146.42 C 379.83 146.42 381.9 144.35 381.9 141.79 L 381.9 4.63 C 381.9 2.07 379.83 0 377.27 0 L 4.63 0 C 2.07 0 0 2.07 0 4.63 Z"></path></g><g style="--ltx-fill-color:#FFFFFF;" fill="#FFFFFF" fill-opacity="1.0"><path style="stroke:none" d="M 0.69 4.63 L 0.69 127.33 L 381.21 127.33 L 381.21 4.63 C 381.21 2.45 379.45 0.69 377.27 0.69 L 4.63 0.69 C 2.45 0.69 0.69 2.45 0.69 4.63 Z"></path></g><g fill-opacity="1.0" transform="matrix(1.0 0.0 0.0 1.0 20.38 134.11)"><foreignObject style="--ltx-fo-width:25.16em;--ltx-fo-height:0.56em;--ltx-fo-depth:0.16em;font-size:10pt;" height="9.84" overflow="visible" transform="matrix(1 0 0 -1 0 7.69)" width="348.14"><span class="ltx_foreignobject_container"><span class="ltx_foreignobject_content">
<span id="S2.SS3.SSS2.p4.pic1.1" class="ltx_inline-block ltx_minipage ltx_align_bottom" style="width:25.16em;">
<span id="S2.SS3.SSS2.p4.pic1.1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S2.SS3.SSS2.p4.pic1.1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold" style="font-size:80%;--ltx-fg-color:#FFFFFF;">Problem 0: Sum of squares</span></span>
</span></span></span></foreignObject></g><g fill-opacity="1.0" transform="matrix(1.0 0.0 0.0 1.0 20.38 14.66)"><foreignObject style="--ltx-fo-width:29.01em;--ltx-fo-height:7.86em;--ltx-fo-depth:0.16em;font-size:10pt;" height="110.89" overflow="visible" transform="matrix(1 0 0 -1 0 108.74)" width="401.42"><span class="ltx_foreignobject_container"><span class="ltx_foreignobject_content">
<span id="S2.SS3.SSS2.p4.pic1.2" class="ltx_inline-block ltx_minipage ltx_align_bottom" style="width:29.01em;">
<span id="S2.SS3.SSS2.p4.pic1.2.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S2.SS3.SSS2.p4.pic1.2.1.1" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:80%;--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">Let <math id="S2.SS3.SSS2.p4.pic1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="X" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">X</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">X</annotation></semantics></math> be a homogeneous expression in terms of <math id="S2.SS3.SSS2.p4.pic1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="a,b,c" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">a</mi><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">,</mo><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">b</mi><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">,</mo><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">c</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">a,b,c</annotation></semantics></math>, and suppose we want to prove <math id="S2.SS3.SSS2.p4.pic1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="X\geq 0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">X</mi><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">≥</mo><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">X\geq 0</annotation></semantics></math>.
Write <math id="S2.SS3.SSS2.p4.pic1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="X" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">X</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">X</annotation></semantics></math> in the following form:</span></span>
<span id="S2.Ex2" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<span><span class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<span class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></span>
<span class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S2.Ex2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(a-b)^{2}\cdot S_{c}+(b-c)^{2}\cdot S_{a}+(c-a)^{2}\cdot S_{b}." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><msup><mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" maxsize="0.800em" minsize="0.800em">(</mo><mrow><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" mathsize="0.800em">a</mi><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" mathsize="0.800em">−</mo><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" mathsize="0.800em">b</mi></mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" maxsize="0.800em" minsize="0.800em">)</mo></mrow><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" mathsize="0.800em">2</mn></msup><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" lspace="0.222em" mathcolor="#000000" mathsize="0.800em" rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><msub><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" mathsize="0.800em">S</mi><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" mathsize="0.800em">c</mi></msub></mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" mathsize="0.800em">+</mo><mrow><msup><mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" maxsize="0.800em" minsize="0.800em">(</mo><mrow><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" mathsize="0.800em">b</mi><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" mathsize="0.800em">−</mo><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" mathsize="0.800em">c</mi></mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" maxsize="0.800em" minsize="0.800em" rspace="0.055em">)</mo></mrow><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" mathsize="0.800em">2</mn></msup><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" mathsize="0.800em" rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><msub><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" mathsize="0.800em">S</mi><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" mathsize="0.800em">a</mi></msub></mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" mathsize="0.800em">+</mo><mrow><msup><mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" maxsize="0.800em" minsize="0.800em">(</mo><mrow><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" mathsize="0.800em">c</mi><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" mathsize="0.800em">−</mo><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" mathsize="0.800em">a</mi></mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" maxsize="0.800em" minsize="0.800em" rspace="0.055em">)</mo></mrow><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" mathsize="0.800em">2</mn></msup><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" mathsize="0.800em" rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><msub><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" mathsize="0.800em">S</mi><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" mathsize="0.800em">b</mi></msub></mrow></mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" lspace="0em" mathcolor="#000000" mathsize="0.800em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(a-b)^{2}\cdot S_{c}+(b-c)^{2}\cdot S_{a}+(c-a)^{2}\cdot S_{b}.</annotation></semantics></math></span>
<span class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></span></span></span>
</span>
<span id="S2.SS3.SSS2.p4.pic1.2.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="S2.SS3.SSS2.p4.pic1.2.2.1" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:80%;--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">Apply the sum of squares (SOS) method to show that:</span></span>
<span id="S2.Ex3" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<span><span class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<span class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></span>
<span class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S2.Ex3.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="16\sum x^{4}-20\sum x^{3}(y+z)+9\sum y^{2}z^{2}+25\sum x^{2}yz\geq 0." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mrow><mrow><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" mathsize="0.800em">16</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" maxsize="0.800em" minsize="0.800em" movablelimits="false" stretchy="true">∑</mo><msup><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" mathsize="0.800em">x</mi><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" mathsize="0.800em">4</mn></msup></mrow></mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" mathsize="0.800em">−</mo><mrow><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" mathsize="0.800em">20</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" maxsize="0.800em" minsize="0.800em" movablelimits="false" stretchy="true">∑</mo><mrow><msup><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" mathsize="0.800em">x</mi><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" mathsize="0.800em">3</mn></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" maxsize="0.800em" minsize="0.800em">(</mo><mrow><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" mathsize="0.800em">y</mi><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" mathsize="0.800em">+</mo><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" mathsize="0.800em">z</mi></mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" maxsize="0.800em" minsize="0.800em">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" mathsize="0.800em">+</mo><mrow><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" mathsize="0.800em">9</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" maxsize="0.800em" minsize="0.800em" movablelimits="false" stretchy="true">∑</mo><mrow><msup><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" mathsize="0.800em">y</mi><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" mathsize="0.800em">2</mn></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" mathsize="0.800em">z</mi><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" mathsize="0.800em">2</mn></msup></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" mathsize="0.800em">+</mo><mrow><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" mathsize="0.800em">25</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" maxsize="0.800em" minsize="0.800em" movablelimits="false" stretchy="true">∑</mo><mrow><msup><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" mathsize="0.800em">x</mi><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" mathsize="0.800em">2</mn></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" mathsize="0.800em">y</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" mathsize="0.800em">z</mi></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" mathsize="0.800em">≥</mo><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" mathsize="0.800em">0</mn></mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" lspace="0em" mathcolor="#000000" mathsize="0.800em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">16\sum x^{4}-20\sum x^{3}(y+z)+9\sum y^{2}z^{2}+25\sum x^{2}yz\geq 0.</annotation></semantics></math></span>
<span class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></span></span></span>
</span><span class="ltx_inline-block"><svg id="S2.SS3.SSS2.p4.pic1.pic1" class="ltx_picture" color="#FF0000" height="18.24" overflow="visible" style="vertical-align:-4.1px" version="1.1" viewBox="0 0 18.24 18.24" width="18.24"><g style="--ltx-stroke-color:#FF0000;--ltx-fill-color:#FF0000;" fill="#FF0000" stroke="#FF0000" stroke-width="1.8pt" transform="translate(0,18.24) matrix(1 0 0 -1 0 0) translate(1.25,0) translate(0,1.25)"><path style="fill:none" d="M 0 0 L 15.75 15.75 M 0 15.75 L 15.75 0"></path></g></svg></span>
<span id="S2.SS3.SSS2.p4.pic1.2.3" class="ltx_p"><span id="S2.SS3.SSS2.p4.pic1.2.3.1" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:80%;--ltx-fg-color:#FF0000;">GPT-5 thinking failed</span></span>
</span></span></span></foreignObject></g></g></svg></span>
</div>
          
</div>
</figure>
</section>
</section>
<section id="S2.SS4" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">4 </span>Problem-Solving Framework</h3>

<div id="S2.SS4.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S2.SS4.p1.1" class="ltx_p">This category evaluates a model’s ability to approach unfamiliar mathematical problems using structured reasoning. It consists of two key components:</p>
</div>
<section id="S2.SS4.SSS1" class="ltx_subsubsection">
<h4 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsubsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsubsection">(a) </span>Problem interpretation and analysis</h4>

<div id="S2.SS4.SSS1.p1" class="ltx_para">
<ol id="S2.I6" class="ltx_enumerate">
<li id="S2.I6.i1" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">1.</span> 
<div id="S2.I6.i1.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S2.I6.i1.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Parse the problem statement and convert it into a structured representation that reveals variables, constraints, and objectives.</p>
</div></li>
<li id="S2.I6.i2" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">2.</span> 
<div id="S2.I6.i2.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S2.I6.i2.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Generate and test simple or edge-case examples to explore possible behaviors and build preliminary insight.</p>
</div></li>
</ol>
<p id="S2.SS4.SSS1.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S2.SS4.SSS1.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Design Principles:</span>
Choose problems where understanding the question clearly is key to solving it. Focus on problems that involve tricky wording, hidden assumptions, or subtle edge cases. Good problems in this category often confuse solvers who rush in without first carefully analyzing what’s being asked.</p>
</div>
<div id="S2.SS4.SSS1.p2" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S2.SS4.SSS1.p2.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S2.SS4.SSS1.p2.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Sample Problems:</span></p>
</div>
<figure id="S2.SS4.SSS1.fig1" class="ltx_figure">
<div class="ltx_flex_figure">
<div class="ltx_flex_cell ltx_flex_size_1">
<div id="S2.SS4.SSS1.fig1.1" class="ltx_logical-block ltx_figure_panel ltx_minipage ltx_align_center ltx_align_top" style="width:276.0pt;">
            
<div id="S2.SS4.SSS1.p3" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent"><span class="ltx_inline-block"><svg id="S2.SS4.SSS1.p3.pic1" class="ltx_picture" height="260.81" overflow="visible" version="1.1" viewBox="0 0 381.9 260.81" width="381.9"><g style="--ltx-stroke-color:#000000;--ltx-fill-color:#000000;" fill="#000000" stroke="#000000" stroke-width="0.4pt" transform="translate(0,260.81) matrix(1 0 0 -1 0 0)"><g style="--ltx-fill-color:#3D6666;" fill="#3D6666" fill-opacity="1.0"><path style="stroke:none" d="M 0 4.63 L 0 256.18 C 0 258.74 2.07 260.81 4.63 260.81 L 377.27 260.81 C 379.83 260.81 381.9 258.74 381.9 256.18 L 381.9 4.63 C 381.9 2.07 379.83 0 377.27 0 L 4.63 0 C 2.07 0 0 2.07 0 4.63 Z"></path></g><g style="--ltx-fill-color:#FFFFFF;" fill="#FFFFFF" fill-opacity="1.0"><path style="stroke:none" d="M 0.69 4.63 L 0.69 241.71 L 381.21 241.71 L 381.21 4.63 C 381.21 2.45 379.45 0.69 377.27 0.69 L 4.63 0.69 C 2.45 0.69 0.69 2.45 0.69 4.63 Z"></path></g><g fill-opacity="1.0" transform="matrix(1.0 0.0 0.0 1.0 20.38 248.49)"><foreignObject style="--ltx-fo-width:25.16em;--ltx-fo-height:0.56em;--ltx-fo-depth:0.16em;font-size:10pt;" height="9.84" overflow="visible" transform="matrix(1 0 0 -1 0 7.69)" width="348.14"><span class="ltx_foreignobject_container"><span class="ltx_foreignobject_content">
<span id="S2.SS4.SSS1.p3.pic1.1" class="ltx_inline-block ltx_minipage ltx_align_bottom" style="width:25.16em;">
<span id="S2.SS4.SSS1.p3.pic1.1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S2.SS4.SSS1.p3.pic1.1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold" style="font-size:80%;--ltx-fg-color:#FFFFFF;">Problem 0: Boy return rupees</span></span>
</span></span></span></foreignObject></g><g fill-opacity="1.0" transform="matrix(1.0 0.0 0.0 1.0 20.38 14.66)"><foreignObject style="--ltx-fo-width:29.01em;--ltx-fo-height:16.13em;--ltx-fo-depth:0.16em;font-size:10pt;" height="225.27" overflow="visible" transform="matrix(1 0 0 -1 0 223.12)" width="401.42"><span class="ltx_foreignobject_container"><span class="ltx_foreignobject_content">
<span id="S2.SS4.SSS1.p3.pic1.2" class="ltx_inline-block ltx_minipage ltx_align_bottom" style="width:29.01em;">
<span id="S2.SS4.SSS1.p3.pic1.2.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S2.SS4.SSS1.p3.pic1.2.1.1" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:80%;--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">A boy borrowed 1000 rupees from one of his friends (X). And he borrowed 500 from another friend(Y). And he lost 1000 rupees from his hand on the way to the shop. And he purchased it for only 300 rupees. So he left only 200. And he gave <math id="S2.SS4.SSS1.p3.pic1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\$100" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" mathsize="1.250em" rspace="0.167em">$</mo><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">100</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\$100</annotation></semantics></math> each to those friends (<math id="S2.SS4.SSS1.p3.pic1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="X" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">X</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">X</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="S2.SS4.SSS1.p3.pic1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="Y" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">Y</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">Y</annotation></semantics></math>). And he made a calculation.</span></span>
<span id="S2.I7" class="ltx_itemize">
<span id="S2.I7.i1" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">•</span> 
<span id="S2.I7.i1.p1" class="ltx_para">
<span id="S2.I7.i1.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S2.I7.i1.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:80%;--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">He have to give 900 to </span><math id="S2.I7.i1.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="X" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" mathsize="0.800em">X</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">X</annotation></semantics></math></span>
</span></span>
<span id="S2.I7.i2" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">•</span> 
<span id="S2.I7.i2.p1" class="ltx_para">
<span id="S2.I7.i2.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S2.I7.i2.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:80%;--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">He has to give 400 to </span><math id="S2.I7.i2.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="Y" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" mathsize="0.800em">Y</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">Y</annotation></semantics></math></span>
</span></span>
<span id="S2.I7.i3" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">•</span> 
<span id="S2.I7.i3.p1" class="ltx_para">
<span id="S2.I7.i3.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S2.I7.i3.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:80%;--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">He have product of 300</span></span>
</span></span>
</span>
<span id="S2.SS4.SSS1.p3.pic1.2.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="S2.SS4.SSS1.p3.pic1.2.2.1" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:80%;--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">So total <math id="S2.SS4.SSS1.p3.pic1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="900+400+300=1600" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">900</mn><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">+</mo><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">400</mn><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">+</mo><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">300</mn></mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">=</mo><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">1600</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">900+400+300=1600</annotation></semantics></math>. How that extra 100 comes from. Please help to solve.</span></span><span class="ltx_inline-block"><svg id="S2.SS4.SSS1.p3.pic1.pic1" class="ltx_picture" color="#008000" height="18.24" overflow="visible" style="vertical-align:-4.1px" version="1.1" viewBox="0 0 18.24 18.24" width="18.24"><g style="--ltx-stroke-color:#009900;--ltx-fill-color:#009900;--ltx-fg-color:#009900;" color="#009900" fill="#009900" stroke="#009900" stroke-width="1.8pt" transform="translate(0,18.24) matrix(1 0 0 -1 0 0) translate(1.25,0) translate(0,1.25)"><path style="fill:none" d="M 0 7.87 L 5.51 0 L 15.75 15.75"></path></g></svg></span>
<span id="S2.SS4.SSS1.p3.pic1.2.3" class="ltx_p"><span id="S2.SS4.SSS1.p3.pic1.2.3.1" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:80%;--ltx-fg-color:#008000;">GPT-5 thinking passed</span></span>
</span></span></span></foreignObject></g></g></svg></span>
</div>
          
</div></div><div class="ltx_flex_break"></div><div class="ltx_flex_cell ltx_flex_size_1">
<div id="S2.SS4.SSS1.fig1.2" class="ltx_logical-block ltx_figure_panel ltx_minipage ltx_align_center ltx_align_top" style="width:276.0pt;">
            
<div id="S2.SS4.SSS1.p4" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent"><span class="ltx_inline-block"><svg id="S2.SS4.SSS1.p4.pic1" class="ltx_picture" height="384.42" overflow="visible" version="1.1" viewBox="0 0 381.9 384.42" width="381.9"><g style="--ltx-stroke-color:#000000;--ltx-fill-color:#000000;" fill="#000000" stroke="#000000" stroke-width="0.4pt" transform="translate(0,384.42) matrix(1 0 0 -1 0 0)"><g style="--ltx-fill-color:#3D6666;" fill="#3D6666" fill-opacity="1.0"><path style="stroke:none" d="M 0 4.63 L 0 379.79 C 0 382.35 2.07 384.42 4.63 384.42 L 377.27 384.42 C 379.83 384.42 381.9 382.35 381.9 379.79 L 381.9 4.63 C 381.9 2.07 379.83 0 377.27 0 L 4.63 0 C 2.07 0 0 2.07 0 4.63 Z"></path></g><g style="--ltx-fill-color:#FFFFFF;" fill="#FFFFFF" fill-opacity="1.0"><path style="stroke:none" d="M 0.69 4.63 L 0.69 365.32 L 381.21 365.32 L 381.21 4.63 C 381.21 2.45 379.45 0.69 377.27 0.69 L 4.63 0.69 C 2.45 0.69 0.69 2.45 0.69 4.63 Z"></path></g><g fill-opacity="1.0" transform="matrix(1.0 0.0 0.0 1.0 20.38 372.1)"><foreignObject style="--ltx-fo-width:25.16em;--ltx-fo-height:0.56em;--ltx-fo-depth:0.16em;font-size:10pt;" height="9.84" overflow="visible" transform="matrix(1 0 0 -1 0 7.69)" width="348.14"><span class="ltx_foreignobject_container"><span class="ltx_foreignobject_content">
<span id="S2.SS4.SSS1.p4.pic1.1" class="ltx_inline-block ltx_minipage ltx_align_bottom" style="width:25.16em;">
<span id="S2.SS4.SSS1.p4.pic1.1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S2.SS4.SSS1.p4.pic1.1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold" style="font-size:80%;--ltx-fg-color:#FFFFFF;">Problem 0: Six man wearing hats</span></span>
</span></span></span></foreignObject></g><g fill-opacity="1.0" transform="matrix(1.0 0.0 0.0 1.0 20.38 14.66)"><foreignObject style="--ltx-fo-width:29.01em;--ltx-fo-height:25.06em;--ltx-fo-depth:0.16em;font-size:10pt;" height="348.89" overflow="visible" transform="matrix(1 0 0 -1 0 346.73)" width="401.42"><span class="ltx_foreignobject_container"><span class="ltx_foreignobject_content">
<span id="S2.SS4.SSS1.p4.pic1.2" class="ltx_inline-block ltx_minipage ltx_align_bottom" style="width:29.01em;">
<span id="S2.SS4.SSS1.p4.pic1.2.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S2.SS4.SSS1.p4.pic1.2.1.1" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:80%;--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">A, B, C, D, E, and F are sitting in a circle, each wearing a hat. Each hat is either pure black, pure white, or has an integer written on it. Everyone knows that there is at least one black hat, one white hat, and one numbered hat, and that the numbers on the numbered hats are exactly a sequence of consecutive integers (which can be just one number).</span></span>
<span id="S2.SS4.SSS1.p4.pic1.2.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="S2.SS4.SSS1.p4.pic1.2.2.1" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:80%;--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">Each person can see everyone else’s hat, but not their own. The host asks if they know what hat they are wearing (they must know the exact color or the exact number, unless they know they are the only one with a numbered hat—in which case, even without knowing the number’s value, it is considered “knowing” their hat). They answer in turn as follows (everyone is perfectly logical and honest):</span></span>
<span id="S2.SS4.SSS1.p4.pic1.2.3" class="ltx_p"><span id="S2.SS4.SSS1.p4.pic1.2.3.1" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:80%;--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">A: I know.
B: I don’t know.
C: I know.
D: I know.
E: I don’t know.
F: I know.</span></span>
<span id="S2.SS4.SSS1.p4.pic1.2.4" class="ltx_p"><span id="S2.SS4.SSS1.p4.pic1.2.4.1" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:80%;--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">Seeing E’s puzzled expression, D adds:
“I didn’t know what hat I was wearing at first, but after hearing what C said, I knew.”</span></span>
<span id="S2.SS4.SSS1.p4.pic1.2.5" class="ltx_p"><span id="S2.SS4.SSS1.p4.pic1.2.5.1" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:80%;--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">E suddenly understands.</span></span>
<span id="S2.SS4.SSS1.p4.pic1.2.6" class="ltx_p"><span id="S2.SS4.SSS1.p4.pic1.2.6.1" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:80%;--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">Question: Who is wearing colored hats, and who is wearing numbered hats?</span></span><span class="ltx_inline-block"><svg id="S2.SS4.SSS1.p4.pic1.pic1" class="ltx_picture" color="#FF0000" height="18.24" overflow="visible" style="vertical-align:-4.1px" version="1.1" viewBox="0 0 18.24 18.24" width="18.24"><g style="--ltx-stroke-color:#FF0000;--ltx-fill-color:#FF0000;" fill="#FF0000" stroke="#FF0000" stroke-width="1.8pt" transform="translate(0,18.24) matrix(1 0 0 -1 0 0) translate(1.25,0) translate(0,1.25)"><path style="fill:none" d="M 0 0 L 15.75 15.75 M 0 15.75 L 15.75 0"></path></g></svg></span>
<span id="S2.SS4.SSS1.p4.pic1.2.7" class="ltx_p"><span id="S2.SS4.SSS1.p4.pic1.2.7.1" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:80%;--ltx-fg-color:#FF0000;">GPT-5 thinking failed</span></span>
</span></span></span></foreignObject></g></g></svg></span>
</div>
          
</div></div></div>
</figure>
</section>
<section id="S2.SS4.SSS2" class="ltx_subsubsection">
<h4 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsubsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsubsection">(b) </span>Application of problem-solving strategies</h4>

<div id="S2.SS4.SSS2.p1" class="ltx_para">
<ol id="S2.I8" class="ltx_enumerate">
<li id="S2.I8.i1" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">1.</span> 
<div id="S2.I8.i1.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S2.I8.i1.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S2.I8.i1.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">Analogy</span> – Map the problem to a previously solved or canonical problem.</p>
</div></li>
<li id="S2.I8.i2" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">2.</span> 
<div id="S2.I8.i2.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S2.I8.i2.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S2.I8.i2.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">Induction</span> – Establish general truths by proving a base case and showing how one case leads to the next.</p>
</div></li>
<li id="S2.I8.i3" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">3.</span> 
<div id="S2.I8.i3.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S2.I8.i3.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S2.I8.i3.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">Contradiction</span> – Explore the negation of a target claim and find inconsistencies.</p>
</div></li>
<li id="S2.I8.i4" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">4.</span> 
<div id="S2.I8.i4.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S2.I8.i4.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S2.I8.i4.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">Working Backwards</span> – Start from the desired outcome and trace backwards to known results.</p>
</div></li>
<li id="S2.I8.i5" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">5.</span> 
<div id="S2.I8.i5.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S2.I8.i5.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S2.I8.i5.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">Substitution</span> – Reformulate the problem using variable changes or structural simplifications.</p>
</div></li>
<li id="S2.I8.i6" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">6.</span> 
<div id="S2.I8.i6.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S2.I8.i6.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S2.I8.i6.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">Extremal Principle</span> – Consider extreme or limiting cases (e.g., minimal, maximal, or boundary values).</p>
</div></li>
<li id="S2.I8.i7" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">7.</span> 
<div id="S2.I8.i7.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S2.I8.i7.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S2.I8.i7.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">Problem Decomposition</span> – Divide the task into smaller subproblems and recursively solve them.</p>
</div></li>
</ol>
<p id="S2.SS4.SSS2.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S2.SS4.SSS2.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Design Principles:</span>
See if there are problems that require a specific strategy. Ensure that the most effective solution path relies on recognizing and applying a specific strategy.</p>
</div>
<div id="S2.SS4.SSS2.p2" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S2.SS4.SSS2.p2.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S2.SS4.SSS2.p2.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Sample Problems:</span></p>
</div>
<figure id="S2.SS4.SSS2.fig1" class="ltx_figure">
<div class="ltx_flex_figure">
<div class="ltx_flex_cell ltx_flex_size_1">
<div id="S2.SS4.SSS2.fig1.1" class="ltx_logical-block ltx_figure_panel ltx_minipage ltx_align_center ltx_align_top" style="width:276.0pt;">
            
<div id="S2.SS4.SSS2.p3" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent"><span class="ltx_inline-block"><svg id="S2.SS4.SSS2.p3.pic1" class="ltx_picture" height="202.39" overflow="visible" version="1.1" viewBox="0 0 381.9 202.39" width="381.9"><g style="--ltx-stroke-color:#000000;--ltx-fill-color:#000000;" fill="#000000" stroke="#000000" stroke-width="0.4pt" transform="translate(0,202.39) matrix(1 0 0 -1 0 0)"><g style="--ltx-fill-color:#3D6666;" fill="#3D6666" fill-opacity="1.0"><path style="stroke:none" d="M 0 4.63 L 0 197.76 C 0 200.31 2.07 202.39 4.63 202.39 L 377.27 202.39 C 379.83 202.39 381.9 200.31 381.9 197.76 L 381.9 4.63 C 381.9 2.07 379.83 0 377.27 0 L 4.63 0 C 2.07 0 0 2.07 0 4.63 Z"></path></g><g style="--ltx-fill-color:#FFFFFF;" fill="#FFFFFF" fill-opacity="1.0"><path style="stroke:none" d="M 0.69 4.63 L 0.69 183.29 L 381.21 183.29 L 381.21 4.63 C 381.21 2.45 379.45 0.69 377.27 0.69 L 4.63 0.69 C 2.45 0.69 0.69 2.45 0.69 4.63 Z"></path></g><g fill-opacity="1.0" transform="matrix(1.0 0.0 0.0 1.0 20.38 190.07)"><foreignObject style="--ltx-fo-width:25.16em;--ltx-fo-height:0.56em;--ltx-fo-depth:0.16em;font-size:10pt;" height="9.84" overflow="visible" transform="matrix(1 0 0 -1 0 7.69)" width="348.14"><span class="ltx_foreignobject_container"><span class="ltx_foreignobject_content">
<span id="S2.SS4.SSS2.p3.pic1.1" class="ltx_inline-block ltx_minipage ltx_align_bottom" style="width:25.16em;">
<span id="S2.SS4.SSS2.p3.pic1.1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S2.SS4.SSS2.p3.pic1.1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold" style="font-size:80%;--ltx-fg-color:#FFFFFF;">Problem 0: Color grids</span></span>
</span></span></span></foreignObject></g><g fill-opacity="1.0" transform="matrix(1.0 0.0 0.0 1.0 20.38 14.66)"><foreignObject style="--ltx-fo-width:29.01em;--ltx-fo-height:11.9em;--ltx-fo-depth:0.16em;font-size:10pt;" height="166.85" overflow="visible" transform="matrix(1 0 0 -1 0 164.7)" width="401.42"><span class="ltx_foreignobject_container"><span class="ltx_foreignobject_content">
<span id="S2.SS4.SSS2.p3.pic1.2" class="ltx_inline-block ltx_minipage ltx_align_bottom" style="width:29.01em;">
<span id="S2.SS4.SSS2.p3.pic1.2.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S2.SS4.SSS2.p3.pic1.2.1.1" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:80%;--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">(<em id="S2.SS4.SSS2.p3.pic1.2.1.1.1" class="ltx_emph ltx_font_italic">Induction</em>) Let <math id="S2.SS4.SSS2.p3.pic1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="n\geq 3" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">n</mi><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">≥</mo><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">3</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">n\geq 3</annotation></semantics></math> be an odd integer. Color each cell of an <math id="S2.SS4.SSS2.p3.pic1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="n\times n" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">n</mi><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" lspace="0.222em" mathcolor="#000000" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">n</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">n\times n</annotation></semantics></math> grid either black or white. Two cells of the same color that share a vertex are called <em id="S2.SS4.SSS2.p3.pic1.2.1.1.2" class="ltx_emph ltx_font_italic">adjacent</em>. For any two cells <math id="S2.SS4.SSS2.p3.pic1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="a,b" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">a</mi><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">,</mo><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">b</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">a,b</annotation></semantics></math>, we say <math id="S2.SS4.SSS2.p3.pic1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="a" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">a</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">a</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="S2.SS4.SSS2.p3.pic1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="b" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">b</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">b</annotation></semantics></math> are <em id="S2.SS4.SSS2.p3.pic1.2.1.1.3" class="ltx_emph ltx_font_italic">connected</em> if there exists a sequence of cells</span></span>
<span id="S2.Ex4" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<span><span class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<span class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></span>
<span class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S2.Ex4.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="c_{1},\,c_{2},\,\dots,\,c_{k}" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" mathsize="0.800em">c</mi><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" mathsize="0.800em">1</mn></msub><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" mathsize="0.800em" rspace="0.337em">,</mo><msub><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" mathsize="0.800em">c</mi><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" mathsize="0.800em">2</mn></msub><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" mathsize="0.800em" rspace="0.337em">,</mo><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" mathsize="0.800em" mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" mathsize="0.800em" rspace="0.337em">,</mo><msub><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" mathsize="0.800em">c</mi><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" mathsize="0.800em">k</mi></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">c_{1},\,c_{2},\,\dots,\,c_{k}</annotation></semantics></math></span>
<span class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></span></span></span>
</span>
<span id="S2.SS4.SSS2.p3.pic1.2.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="S2.SS4.SSS2.p3.pic1.2.2.1" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:80%;--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">with <math id="S2.SS4.SSS2.p3.pic1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="c_{1}=a" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">c</mi><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">1</mn></msub><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">=</mo><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">a</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">c_{1}=a</annotation></semantics></math>, <math id="S2.SS4.SSS2.p3.pic1.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="c_{k}=b" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">c</mi><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">k</mi></msub><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">=</mo><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">b</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">c_{k}=b</annotation></semantics></math>, and each <math id="S2.SS4.SSS2.p3.pic1.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="c_{i}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">c</mi><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">i</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">c_{i}</annotation></semantics></math> is adjacent to <math id="S2.SS4.SSS2.p3.pic1.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="c_{i+1}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">c</mi><mrow><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">i</mi><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">+</mo><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">1</mn></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">c_{i+1}</annotation></semantics></math> for <math id="S2.SS4.SSS2.p3.pic1.m10" class="ltx_Math" alttext="i=1,2,\dots,k-1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">i</mi><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">=</mo><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">1</mn></mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">,</mo><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">2</mn><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">,</mo><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">,</mo><mrow><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">k</mi><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">−</mo><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">1</mn></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">i=1,2,\dots,k-1</annotation></semantics></math>. Determine the largest positive integer <math id="S2.SS4.SSS2.p3.pic1.m11" class="ltx_Math" alttext="M" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">M</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">M</annotation></semantics></math> for which there is a coloring having <math id="S2.SS4.SSS2.p3.pic1.m12" class="ltx_Math" alttext="M" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">M</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">M</annotation></semantics></math> cells that are pairwise non<span id="S2.SS4.SSS2.p3.pic1.2.2.1.1" class="ltx_text">-</span>connected.</span></span><span class="ltx_inline-block"><svg id="S2.SS4.SSS2.p3.pic1.pic1" class="ltx_picture" color="#FF0000" height="18.24" overflow="visible" style="vertical-align:-4.1px" version="1.1" viewBox="0 0 18.24 18.24" width="18.24"><g style="--ltx-stroke-color:#FF0000;--ltx-fill-color:#FF0000;" fill="#FF0000" stroke="#FF0000" stroke-width="1.8pt" transform="translate(0,18.24) matrix(1 0 0 -1 0 0) translate(1.25,0) translate(0,1.25)"><path style="fill:none" d="M 0 0 L 15.75 15.75 M 0 15.75 L 15.75 0"></path></g></svg></span>
<span id="S2.SS4.SSS2.p3.pic1.2.3" class="ltx_p"><span id="S2.SS4.SSS2.p3.pic1.2.3.1" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:80%;--ltx-fg-color:#FF0000;">GPT-5 thinking failed</span></span>
</span></span></span></foreignObject></g></g></svg></span>
</div>
          
</div></div><div class="ltx_flex_break"></div><div class="ltx_flex_cell ltx_flex_size_1">
<div id="S2.SS4.SSS2.fig1.2" class="ltx_logical-block ltx_figure_panel ltx_minipage ltx_align_center ltx_align_top" style="width:276.0pt;">
            
<div id="S2.SS4.SSS2.p4" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent"><span class="ltx_inline-block"><svg id="S2.SS4.SSS2.p4.pic1" class="ltx_picture" height="137.51" overflow="visible" version="1.1" viewBox="0 0 381.9 137.51" width="381.9"><g style="--ltx-stroke-color:#000000;--ltx-fill-color:#000000;" fill="#000000" stroke="#000000" stroke-width="0.4pt" transform="translate(0,137.51) matrix(1 0 0 -1 0 0)"><g style="--ltx-fill-color:#3D6666;" fill="#3D6666" fill-opacity="1.0"><path style="stroke:none" d="M 0 4.63 L 0 132.88 C 0 135.43 2.07 137.51 4.63 137.51 L 377.27 137.51 C 379.83 137.51 381.9 135.43 381.9 132.88 L 381.9 4.63 C 381.9 2.07 379.83 0 377.27 0 L 4.63 0 C 2.07 0 0 2.07 0 4.63 Z"></path></g><g style="--ltx-fill-color:#FFFFFF;" fill="#FFFFFF" fill-opacity="1.0"><path style="stroke:none" d="M 0.69 4.63 L 0.69 118.41 L 381.21 118.41 L 381.21 4.63 C 381.21 2.45 379.45 0.69 377.27 0.69 L 4.63 0.69 C 2.45 0.69 0.69 2.45 0.69 4.63 Z"></path></g><g fill-opacity="1.0" transform="matrix(1.0 0.0 0.0 1.0 20.38 125.19)"><foreignObject style="--ltx-fo-width:25.16em;--ltx-fo-height:0.56em;--ltx-fo-depth:0.16em;font-size:10pt;" height="9.84" overflow="visible" transform="matrix(1 0 0 -1 0 7.69)" width="348.14"><span class="ltx_foreignobject_container"><span class="ltx_foreignobject_content">
<span id="S2.SS4.SSS2.p4.pic1.1" class="ltx_inline-block ltx_minipage ltx_align_bottom" style="width:25.16em;">
<span id="S2.SS4.SSS2.p4.pic1.1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S2.SS4.SSS2.p4.pic1.1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold" style="font-size:80%;--ltx-fg-color:#FFFFFF;">Problem 0: Hamiltonian paths on grids</span></span>
</span></span></span></foreignObject></g><g fill-opacity="1.0" transform="matrix(1.0 0.0 0.0 1.0 20.38 14.66)"><foreignObject style="--ltx-fo-width:29.01em;--ltx-fo-height:7.21em;--ltx-fo-depth:0.16em;font-size:10pt;" height="101.97" overflow="visible" transform="matrix(1 0 0 -1 0 99.82)" width="401.42"><span class="ltx_foreignobject_container"><span class="ltx_foreignobject_content">
<span id="S2.SS4.SSS2.p4.pic1.2" class="ltx_inline-block ltx_minipage ltx_align_bottom" style="width:29.01em;">
<span id="S2.SS4.SSS2.p4.pic1.2.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S2.SS4.SSS2.p4.pic1.2.1.1" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:80%;--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">On a <math id="S2.SS4.SSS2.p4.pic1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="99\times 99" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">99</mn><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" lspace="0.222em" mathcolor="#000000" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">99</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">99\times 99</annotation></semantics></math> grid, you begin at the bottom<span id="S2.SS4.SSS2.p4.pic1.2.1.1.1" class="ltx_text">-</span>left cell and make a path that visits every cell exactly once. At each step you move to an unvisited cell sharing a side with your current position. After you have covered all cells, in how many distinct cells could your path end? Please rigorously justify your answer.</span></span><span class="ltx_inline-block"><svg id="S2.SS4.SSS2.p4.pic1.pic1" class="ltx_picture" color="#FF0000" height="18.24" overflow="visible" style="vertical-align:-4.1px" version="1.1" viewBox="0 0 18.24 18.24" width="18.24"><g style="--ltx-stroke-color:#FF0000;--ltx-fill-color:#FF0000;" fill="#FF0000" stroke="#FF0000" stroke-width="1.8pt" transform="translate(0,18.24) matrix(1 0 0 -1 0 0) translate(1.25,0) translate(0,1.25)"><path style="fill:none" d="M 0 0 L 15.75 15.75 M 0 15.75 L 15.75 0"></path></g></svg></span>
<span id="S2.SS4.SSS2.p4.pic1.2.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="S2.SS4.SSS2.p4.pic1.2.2.1" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:80%;--ltx-fg-color:#FF0000;">GPT-5 thinking failed</span></span>
</span></span></span></foreignObject></g></g></svg></span>
</div>
          
</div></div><div class="ltx_flex_break"></div><div class="ltx_flex_cell ltx_flex_size_1">
<div id="S2.SS4.SSS2.fig1.3" class="ltx_logical-block ltx_figure_panel ltx_minipage ltx_align_center ltx_align_top" style="width:276.0pt;">
            
<div id="S2.SS4.SSS2.p5" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent"><span class="ltx_inline-block"><svg id="S2.SS4.SSS2.p5.pic1" class="ltx_picture" height="134.8" overflow="visible" version="1.1" viewBox="0 0 381.9 134.8" width="381.9"><g style="--ltx-stroke-color:#000000;--ltx-fill-color:#000000;" fill="#000000" stroke="#000000" stroke-width="0.4pt" transform="translate(0,134.8) matrix(1 0 0 -1 0 0)"><g style="--ltx-fill-color:#3D6666;" fill="#3D6666" fill-opacity="1.0"><path style="stroke:none" d="M 0 4.63 L 0 130.17 C 0 132.73 2.07 134.8 4.63 134.8 L 377.27 134.8 C 379.83 134.8 381.9 132.73 381.9 130.17 L 381.9 4.63 C 381.9 2.07 379.83 0 377.27 0 L 4.63 0 C 2.07 0 0 2.07 0 4.63 Z"></path></g><g style="--ltx-fill-color:#FFFFFF;" fill="#FFFFFF" fill-opacity="1.0"><path style="stroke:none" d="M 0.69 4.63 L 0.69 115.7 L 381.21 115.7 L 381.21 4.63 C 381.21 2.45 379.45 0.69 377.27 0.69 L 4.63 0.69 C 2.45 0.69 0.69 2.45 0.69 4.63 Z"></path></g><g fill-opacity="1.0" transform="matrix(1.0 0.0 0.0 1.0 20.38 122.48)"><foreignObject style="--ltx-fo-width:25.16em;--ltx-fo-height:0.56em;--ltx-fo-depth:0.16em;font-size:10pt;" height="9.84" overflow="visible" transform="matrix(1 0 0 -1 0 7.69)" width="348.14"><span class="ltx_foreignobject_container"><span class="ltx_foreignobject_content">
<span id="S2.SS4.SSS2.p5.pic1.1" class="ltx_inline-block ltx_minipage ltx_align_bottom" style="width:25.16em;">
<span id="S2.SS4.SSS2.p5.pic1.1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S2.SS4.SSS2.p5.pic1.1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold" style="font-size:80%;--ltx-fg-color:#FFFFFF;">Problem 0: Extrema of algebraic expression</span></span>
</span></span></span></foreignObject></g><g fill-opacity="1.0" transform="matrix(1.0 0.0 0.0 1.0 20.38 14.66)"><foreignObject style="--ltx-fo-width:29.01em;--ltx-fo-height:7.02em;--ltx-fo-depth:0.16em;font-size:10pt;" height="99.26" overflow="visible" transform="matrix(1 0 0 -1 0 97.11)" width="401.42"><span class="ltx_foreignobject_container"><span class="ltx_foreignobject_content">
<span id="S2.SS4.SSS2.p5.pic1.2" class="ltx_inline-block ltx_minipage ltx_align_bottom" style="width:29.01em;">
<span id="S2.SS4.SSS2.p5.pic1.2.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S2.SS4.SSS2.p5.pic1.2.1.1" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:80%;--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">(<em id="S2.SS4.SSS2.p5.pic1.2.1.1.1" class="ltx_emph ltx_font_italic">Problem Decoposition</em>) Let <math id="S2.SS4.SSS2.p5.pic1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="a,b,c,d,e\geq-1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">a</mi><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">,</mo><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">b</mi><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">,</mo><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">c</mi><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">,</mo><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">d</mi><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">,</mo><mrow><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">e</mi><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">≥</mo><mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">−</mo><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">1</mn></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">a,b,c,d,e\geq-1</annotation></semantics></math> be real numbers such that</span></span>
<span id="S2.Ex5" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<span><span class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<span class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></span>
<span class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S2.Ex5.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="a+b+c+d+e=5." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" mathsize="0.800em">a</mi><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" mathsize="0.800em">+</mo><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" mathsize="0.800em">b</mi><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" mathsize="0.800em">+</mo><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" mathsize="0.800em">c</mi><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" mathsize="0.800em">+</mo><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" mathsize="0.800em">d</mi><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" mathsize="0.800em">+</mo><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" mathsize="0.800em">e</mi></mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" mathsize="0.800em">=</mo><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" mathsize="0.800em">5</mn></mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" lspace="0em" mathcolor="#000000" mathsize="0.800em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">a+b+c+d+e=5.</annotation></semantics></math></span>
<span class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></span></span></span>
</span>
<span id="S2.SS4.SSS2.p5.pic1.2.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="S2.SS4.SSS2.p5.pic1.2.2.1" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:80%;--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">Find the minimum and maximum values of the expression</span></span>
<span id="S2.Ex6" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<span><span class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<span class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></span>
<span class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S2.Ex6.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="S=(a+b)(b+c)(c+d)(d+e)(e+a)." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" mathsize="0.800em">S</mi><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" mathsize="0.800em">=</mo><mrow><mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" maxsize="0.800em" minsize="0.800em">(</mo><mrow><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" mathsize="0.800em">a</mi><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" mathsize="0.800em">+</mo><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" mathsize="0.800em">b</mi></mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" maxsize="0.800em" minsize="0.800em">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" maxsize="0.800em" minsize="0.800em">(</mo><mrow><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" mathsize="0.800em">b</mi><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" mathsize="0.800em">+</mo><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" mathsize="0.800em">c</mi></mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" maxsize="0.800em" minsize="0.800em">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" maxsize="0.800em" minsize="0.800em">(</mo><mrow><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" mathsize="0.800em">c</mi><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" mathsize="0.800em">+</mo><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" mathsize="0.800em">d</mi></mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" maxsize="0.800em" minsize="0.800em">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" maxsize="0.800em" minsize="0.800em">(</mo><mrow><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" mathsize="0.800em">d</mi><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" mathsize="0.800em">+</mo><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" mathsize="0.800em">e</mi></mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" maxsize="0.800em" minsize="0.800em">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" maxsize="0.800em" minsize="0.800em">(</mo><mrow><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" mathsize="0.800em">e</mi><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" mathsize="0.800em">+</mo><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" mathsize="0.800em">a</mi></mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" maxsize="0.800em" minsize="0.800em">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" lspace="0em" mathcolor="#000000" mathsize="0.800em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">S=(a+b)(b+c)(c+d)(d+e)(e+a).</annotation></semantics></math></span>
<span class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></span></span></span>
</span><span class="ltx_inline-block"><svg id="S2.SS4.SSS2.p5.pic1.pic1" class="ltx_picture" color="#FF0000" height="18.24" overflow="visible" style="vertical-align:-4.1px" version="1.1" viewBox="0 0 18.24 18.24" width="18.24"><g style="--ltx-stroke-color:#FF0000;--ltx-fill-color:#FF0000;" fill="#FF0000" stroke="#FF0000" stroke-width="1.8pt" transform="translate(0,18.24) matrix(1 0 0 -1 0 0) translate(1.25,0) translate(0,1.25)"><path style="fill:none" d="M 0 0 L 15.75 15.75 M 0 15.75 L 15.75 0"></path></g></svg></span>
<span id="S2.SS4.SSS2.p5.pic1.2.3" class="ltx_p"><span id="S2.SS4.SSS2.p5.pic1.2.3.1" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:80%;--ltx-fg-color:#FF0000;">GPT-5 thinking failed</span></span>
</span></span></span></foreignObject></g></g></svg></span>
</div>
          
</div></div><div class="ltx_flex_break"></div><div class="ltx_flex_cell ltx_flex_size_1">
<div id="S2.SS4.SSS2.fig1.4" class="ltx_logical-block ltx_figure_panel ltx_minipage ltx_align_center ltx_align_top" style="width:276.0pt;">
            
<div id="S2.SS4.SSS2.p6" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent"><span class="ltx_inline-block"><svg id="S2.SS4.SSS2.p6.pic1" class="ltx_picture" height="286.02" overflow="visible" version="1.1" viewBox="0 0 381.9 286.02" width="381.9"><g style="--ltx-stroke-color:#000000;--ltx-fill-color:#000000;" fill="#000000" stroke="#000000" stroke-width="0.4pt" transform="translate(0,286.02) matrix(1 0 0 -1 0 0)"><g style="--ltx-fill-color:#3D6666;" fill="#3D6666" fill-opacity="1.0"><path style="stroke:none" d="M 0 4.63 L 0 281.39 C 0 283.95 2.07 286.02 4.63 286.02 L 377.27 286.02 C 379.83 286.02 381.9 283.95 381.9 281.39 L 381.9 4.63 C 381.9 2.07 379.83 0 377.27 0 L 4.63 0 C 2.07 0 0 2.07 0 4.63 Z"></path></g><g style="--ltx-fill-color:#FFFFFF;" fill="#FFFFFF" fill-opacity="1.0"><path style="stroke:none" d="M 0.69 4.63 L 0.69 269.08 L 381.21 269.08 L 381.21 4.63 C 381.21 2.45 379.45 0.69 377.27 0.69 L 4.63 0.69 C 2.45 0.69 0.69 2.45 0.69 4.63 Z"></path></g><g fill-opacity="1.0" transform="matrix(1.0 0.0 0.0 1.0 20.38 273.71)"><foreignObject style="--ltx-fo-width:25.16em;--ltx-fo-height:0.56em;--ltx-fo-depth:0em;font-size:10pt;" height="7.69" overflow="visible" transform="matrix(1 0 0 -1 0 7.69)" width="348.14"><span class="ltx_foreignobject_container"><span class="ltx_foreignobject_content">
<span id="S2.SS4.SSS2.p6.pic1.1" class="ltx_inline-block ltx_minipage ltx_align_bottom" style="width:25.16em;">
<span id="S2.SS4.SSS2.p6.pic1.1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S2.SS4.SSS2.p6.pic1.1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold" style="font-size:80%;--ltx-fg-color:#FFFFFF;">Problem 0: Cake on round table</span></span>
</span></span></span></foreignObject></g><g fill-opacity="1.0" transform="matrix(1.0 0.0 0.0 1.0 20.38 14.66)"><foreignObject style="--ltx-fo-width:29.01em;--ltx-fo-height:18.1em;--ltx-fo-depth:0.16em;font-size:10pt;" height="252.64" overflow="visible" transform="matrix(1 0 0 -1 0 250.49)" width="401.42"><span class="ltx_foreignobject_container"><span class="ltx_foreignobject_content">
<span id="S2.SS4.SSS2.p6.pic1.2" class="ltx_inline-block ltx_minipage ltx_align_bottom" style="width:29.01em;">
<span id="S2.SS4.SSS2.p6.pic1.2.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S2.SS4.SSS2.p6.pic1.2.1.1" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:80%;--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">(<em id="S2.SS4.SSS2.p6.pic1.2.1.1.1" class="ltx_emph ltx_font_italic">Contradiction</em>) On a round table, there are <math id="S2.SS4.SSS2.p6.pic1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="5" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">5</mn><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">5</annotation></semantics></math> plates, called plate <math id="S2.SS4.SSS2.p6.pic1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="1,2,3,4,5" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">1</mn><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">,</mo><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">2</mn><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">,</mo><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">3</mn><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">,</mo><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">4</mn><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">,</mo><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">5</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">1,2,3,4,5</annotation></semantics></math>, placed clockwise evenly. A birthday cake has been divided into <math id="S2.SS4.SSS2.p6.pic1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="4" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">4</mn><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">4</annotation></semantics></math> portions containing <math id="S2.SS4.SSS2.p6.pic1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="1,2,3,4" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">1</mn><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">,</mo><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">2</mn><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">,</mo><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">3</mn><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">,</mo><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">4</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">1,2,3,4</annotation></semantics></math> pieces respectively. These <math id="S2.SS4.SSS2.p6.pic1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="4" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">4</mn><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">4</annotation></semantics></math> portions are placed, starting from plate <math id="S2.SS4.SSS2.p6.pic1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">1</mn><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">1</annotation></semantics></math> and going clockwise, into <math id="S2.SS4.SSS2.p6.pic1.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="4" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">4</mn><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">4</annotation></semantics></math> consecutive plates.</span></span>
<span id="S2.SS4.SSS2.p6.pic1.2.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="S2.SS4.SSS2.p6.pic1.2.2.1" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:80%;--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">Now, <math id="S2.SS4.SSS2.p6.pic1.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="5" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">5</mn><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">5</annotation></semantics></math> people sit down at the table, and a game begins. The rules are as follows:</span></span>
<span id="S2.SS4.SSS2.p6.pic1.2.3" class="ltx_p"><span id="S2.SS4.SSS2.p6.pic1.2.3.1" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:80%;--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">1. If the plate in front of a person is empty, they rotate the turntable to a position of their choice.</span></span>
<span id="S2.SS4.SSS2.p6.pic1.2.4" class="ltx_p"><span id="S2.SS4.SSS2.p6.pic1.2.4.1" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:80%;--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">2. Step 1 is repeated until someone encounters an empty plate for the second time.</span></span>
<span id="S2.SS4.SSS2.p6.pic1.2.5" class="ltx_p"><span id="S2.SS4.SSS2.p6.pic1.2.5.1" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:80%;--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">3. Then each person takes the plate in front of them.</span></span>
<span id="S2.SS4.SSS2.p6.pic1.2.6" class="ltx_p"><span id="S2.SS4.SSS2.p6.pic1.2.6.1" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:80%;--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">Question:
Where should you sit in order to get the most cake? (Assume each person is greedy and smart enough.)</span></span><span class="ltx_inline-block"><svg id="S2.SS4.SSS2.p6.pic1.pic1" class="ltx_picture" color="#FF0000" height="18.24" overflow="visible" style="vertical-align:-4.1px" version="1.1" viewBox="0 0 18.24 18.24" width="18.24"><g style="--ltx-stroke-color:#FF0000;--ltx-fill-color:#FF0000;" fill="#FF0000" stroke="#FF0000" stroke-width="1.8pt" transform="translate(0,18.24) matrix(1 0 0 -1 0 0) translate(1.25,0) translate(0,1.25)"><path style="fill:none" d="M 0 0 L 15.75 15.75 M 0 15.75 L 15.75 0"></path></g></svg></span>
<span id="S2.SS4.SSS2.p6.pic1.2.7" class="ltx_p"><span id="S2.SS4.SSS2.p6.pic1.2.7.1" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:80%;--ltx-fg-color:#FF0000;">GPT-5 thinking failed</span></span>
</span></span></span></foreignObject></g></g></svg></span>
</div>
          
</div></div></div>
</figure>
</section>
</section>
<section id="S2.SS5" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">5 </span>Logical Thinking and Reasoning</h3>

<div id="S2.SS5.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S2.SS5.p1.1" class="ltx_p">This category evaluates the model’s ability to construct and evaluate formal mathematical arguments.</p>
</div>
<section id="S2.SS5.SSS1" class="ltx_subsubsection">
<h4 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsubsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsubsection">(a) </span>Constructing valid proofs</h4>

<div id="S2.SS5.SSS1.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S2.SS5.SSS1.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Develop logically rigorous and complete arguments using standard proof techniques such as direct proof, contradiction, induction, and case analysis.</p>
</div>
<div id="S2.SS5.SSS1.p2" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S2.SS5.SSS1.p2.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S2.SS5.SSS1.p2.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Design Principles:</span>
Select problems that require extended logical reasoning, including:</p>
<ul id="S2.I9" class="ltx_itemize">
<li id="S2.I9.i1" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">•</span> 
<div id="S2.I9.i1.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S2.I9.i1.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Long chains of deductions or multi-step logical constructions.</p>
</div></li>
<li id="S2.I9.i2" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">•</span> 
<div id="S2.I9.i2.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S2.I9.i2.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Careful case analysis with subtle distinctions or edge conditions.</p>
</div></li>
<li id="S2.I9.i3" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">•</span> 
<div id="S2.I9.i3.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S2.I9.i3.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Proofs involving intricate dependencies between assumptions and conclusions.</p>
</div></li>
</ul>
<p id="S2.SS5.SSS1.p2.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="S2.SS5.SSS1.p2.2.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Sample Problems:</span></p>
</div>
<figure id="S2.SS5.SSS1.fig1" class="ltx_figure">
<div id="S2.SS5.SSS1.fig1.1" class="ltx_logical-block ltx_minipage ltx_align_center ltx_align_top" style="width:276.0pt;">
            
<div id="S2.SS5.SSS1.p3" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent"><span class="ltx_inline-block"><svg id="S2.SS5.SSS1.p3.pic1" class="ltx_picture" height="118.75" overflow="visible" version="1.1" viewBox="0 0 381.9 118.75" width="381.9"><g style="--ltx-stroke-color:#000000;--ltx-fill-color:#000000;" fill="#000000" stroke="#000000" stroke-width="0.4pt" transform="translate(0,118.75) matrix(1 0 0 -1 0 0)"><g style="--ltx-fill-color:#3D6666;" fill="#3D6666" fill-opacity="1.0"><path style="stroke:none" d="M 0 4.63 L 0 114.12 C 0 116.68 2.07 118.75 4.63 118.75 L 377.27 118.75 C 379.83 118.75 381.9 116.68 381.9 114.12 L 381.9 4.63 C 381.9 2.07 379.83 0 377.27 0 L 4.63 0 C 2.07 0 0 2.07 0 4.63 Z"></path></g><g style="--ltx-fill-color:#FFFFFF;" fill="#FFFFFF" fill-opacity="1.0"><path style="stroke:none" d="M 0.69 4.63 L 0.69 101.8 L 381.21 101.8 L 381.21 4.63 C 381.21 2.45 379.45 0.69 377.27 0.69 L 4.63 0.69 C 2.45 0.69 0.69 2.45 0.69 4.63 Z"></path></g><g fill-opacity="1.0" transform="matrix(1.0 0.0 0.0 1.0 20.38 106.43)"><foreignObject style="--ltx-fo-width:25.16em;--ltx-fo-height:0.56em;--ltx-fo-depth:0em;font-size:10pt;" height="7.69" overflow="visible" transform="matrix(1 0 0 -1 0 7.69)" width="348.14"><span class="ltx_foreignobject_container"><span class="ltx_foreignobject_content">
<span id="S2.SS5.SSS1.p3.pic1.1" class="ltx_inline-block ltx_minipage ltx_align_bottom" style="width:25.16em;">
<span id="S2.SS5.SSS1.p3.pic1.1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S2.SS5.SSS1.p3.pic1.1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold" style="font-size:80%;--ltx-fg-color:#FFFFFF;">Problem 0: 56 elements set</span></span>
</span></span></span></foreignObject></g><g fill-opacity="1.0" transform="matrix(1.0 0.0 0.0 1.0 20.38 14.66)"><foreignObject style="--ltx-fo-width:29.01em;--ltx-fo-height:6.01em;--ltx-fo-depth:0.16em;font-size:10pt;" height="85.37" overflow="visible" transform="matrix(1 0 0 -1 0 83.21)" width="401.42"><span class="ltx_foreignobject_container"><span class="ltx_foreignobject_content">
<span id="S2.SS5.SSS1.p3.pic1.2" class="ltx_inline-block ltx_minipage ltx_align_bottom" style="width:29.01em;">
<span id="S2.SS5.SSS1.p3.pic1.2.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S2.SS5.SSS1.p3.pic1.2.1.1" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:80%;--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">Let <math id="S2.SS5.SSS1.p3.pic1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="X" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">X</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">X</annotation></semantics></math> be a set with 56 elements. Find the smallest positive integer <math id="S2.SS5.SSS1.p3.pic1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="n" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">n</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">n</annotation></semantics></math> such that, for any collection of 15 subsets of <math id="S2.SS5.SSS1.p3.pic1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="X" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">X</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">X</annotation></semantics></math>, if the union of any 7 of them contains at least <math id="S2.SS5.SSS1.p3.pic1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="n" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">n</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">n</annotation></semantics></math> elements, then there must exist 3 of these subsets whose intersection is nonempty.</span></span><span class="ltx_inline-block"><svg id="S2.SS5.SSS1.p3.pic1.pic1" class="ltx_picture" color="#FF0000" height="18.24" overflow="visible" style="vertical-align:-4.1px" version="1.1" viewBox="0 0 18.24 18.24" width="18.24"><g style="--ltx-stroke-color:#FF0000;--ltx-fill-color:#FF0000;" fill="#FF0000" stroke="#FF0000" stroke-width="1.8pt" transform="translate(0,18.24) matrix(1 0 0 -1 0 0) translate(1.25,0) translate(0,1.25)"><path style="fill:none" d="M 0 0 L 15.75 15.75 M 0 15.75 L 15.75 0"></path></g></svg></span>
<span id="S2.SS5.SSS1.p3.pic1.2.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="S2.SS5.SSS1.p3.pic1.2.2.1" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:80%;--ltx-fg-color:#FF0000;">GPT-5 thinking failed</span></span>
</span></span></span></foreignObject></g></g></svg></span>
</div>
          
</div>
</figure>
</section>
<section id="S2.SS5.SSS2" class="ltx_subsubsection">
<h4 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsubsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsubsection">(b) </span>Evaluating existing arguments</h4>

<div id="S2.SS5.SSS2.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S2.SS5.SSS2.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Check whether a given proof or explanation is logically valid, complete, and free of unjustified assumptions or reasoning gaps.</p>
</div>
<div id="S2.SS5.SSS2.p2" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S2.SS5.SSS2.p2.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S2.SS5.SSS2.p2.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Design Principles:</span>
Provide arguments that appear plausible but contain subtle errors, missing steps, or unjustified claims.</p>
</div>
<div id="S2.SS5.SSS2.p3" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S2.SS5.SSS2.p3.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S2.SS5.SSS2.p3.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Sample Problems:</span></p>
</div>
<figure id="S2.SS5.SSS2.fig1" class="ltx_figure">
<div id="S2.SS5.SSS2.fig1.1" class="ltx_logical-block ltx_minipage ltx_align_center ltx_align_top" style="width:276.0pt;">
            
<div id="S2.SS5.SSS2.p4" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent"><span class="ltx_inline-block"><svg id="S2.SS5.SSS2.p4.pic1" class="ltx_picture" height="348.85" overflow="visible" version="1.1" viewBox="0 0 381.9 348.85" width="381.9"><g style="--ltx-stroke-color:#000000;--ltx-fill-color:#000000;" fill="#000000" stroke="#000000" stroke-width="0.4pt" transform="translate(0,348.85) matrix(1 0 0 -1 0 0)"><g style="--ltx-fill-color:#3D6666;" fill="#3D6666" fill-opacity="1.0"><path style="stroke:none" d="M 0 4.63 L 0 344.22 C 0 346.78 2.07 348.85 4.63 348.85 L 377.27 348.85 C 379.83 348.85 381.9 346.78 381.9 344.22 L 381.9 4.63 C 381.9 2.07 379.83 0 377.27 0 L 4.63 0 C 2.07 0 0 2.07 0 4.63 Z"></path></g><g style="--ltx-fill-color:#FFFFFF;" fill="#FFFFFF" fill-opacity="1.0"><path style="stroke:none" d="M 0.69 4.63 L 0.69 329.75 L 381.21 329.75 L 381.21 4.63 C 381.21 2.45 379.45 0.69 377.27 0.69 L 4.63 0.69 C 2.45 0.69 0.69 2.45 0.69 4.63 Z"></path></g><g fill-opacity="1.0" transform="matrix(1.0 0.0 0.0 1.0 20.38 336.53)"><foreignObject style="--ltx-fo-width:25.16em;--ltx-fo-height:0.56em;--ltx-fo-depth:0.16em;font-size:10pt;" height="9.84" overflow="visible" transform="matrix(1 0 0 -1 0 7.69)" width="348.14"><span class="ltx_foreignobject_container"><span class="ltx_foreignobject_content">
<span id="S2.SS5.SSS2.p4.pic1.1" class="ltx_inline-block ltx_minipage ltx_align_bottom" style="width:25.16em;">
<span id="S2.SS5.SSS2.p4.pic1.1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S2.SS5.SSS2.p4.pic1.1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold" style="font-size:80%;--ltx-fg-color:#FFFFFF;">Problem 0: The Banach space paradox</span></span>
</span></span></span></foreignObject></g><g fill-opacity="1.0" transform="matrix(1.0 0.0 0.0 1.0 20.38 14.66)"><foreignObject style="--ltx-fo-width:29.01em;--ltx-fo-height:22.49em;--ltx-fo-depth:0.16em;font-size:10pt;" height="313.31" overflow="visible" transform="matrix(1 0 0 -1 0 311.16)" width="401.42"><span class="ltx_foreignobject_container"><span class="ltx_foreignobject_content">
<span id="S2.SS5.SSS2.p4.pic1.2" class="ltx_inline-block ltx_minipage ltx_align_bottom" style="width:29.01em;">
<span id="S2.SS5.SSS2.p4.pic1.2.1" class="ltx_p"><a href="https://mathoverflow.net/questions/44716/counterexample-for-the-open-mapping-theorem" title="" class="ltx_ref ltx_href" style="font-size:80%;--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">(MathOverflow Problem)</a><cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citep"><span id="S2.SS5.SSS2.p4.pic1.2.1.1" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:80%;--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">(</span><a href="#bib.bib12" title="" class="ltx_ref">Rekalo, 2010</a><span id="S2.SS5.SSS2.p4.pic1.2.1.3" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:80%;--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">)</span></cite><span id="S2.SS5.SSS2.p4.pic1.2.1.4" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:80%;--ltx-fg-color:#000000;"> Check the following proof:
All Banach norms on a real vector space <math id="S2.SS5.SSS2.p4.pic1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="X" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">X</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">X</annotation></semantics></math> are equivalent.</span></span>
<span id="S2.I10" class="ltx_itemize">
<span id="S2.I10.i1" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">•</span> 
<span id="S2.I10.i1.p1" class="ltx_para">
<span id="S2.I10.i1.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S2.I10.i1.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:80%;--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">Let </span><math id="S2.I10.i1.p1.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\|\cdot\|_{1}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" mathsize="0.800em" rspace="0em">∥</mo><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" lspace="0em" mathcolor="#000000" mathsize="0.800em" rspace="0em">⋅</mo><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" lspace="0em" mathcolor="#000000" mathsize="0.800em">∥</mo><msub><mrow></mrow><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" mathsize="0.800em">1</mn></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\|\cdot\|_{1}</annotation></semantics></math><span id="S2.I10.i1.p1.1.2" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:80%;--ltx-fg-color:#000000;"> and </span><math id="S2.I10.i1.p1.m2" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\|\cdot\|_{2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" mathsize="0.800em" rspace="0em">∥</mo><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" lspace="0em" mathcolor="#000000" mathsize="0.800em" rspace="0em">⋅</mo><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" lspace="0em" mathcolor="#000000" mathsize="0.800em">∥</mo><msub><mrow></mrow><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" mathsize="0.800em">2</mn></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\|\cdot\|_{2}</annotation></semantics></math><span id="S2.I10.i1.p1.1.3" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:80%;--ltx-fg-color:#000000;"> two Banach norms on </span><math id="S2.I10.i1.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="X" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" mathsize="0.800em">X</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">X</annotation></semantics></math><span id="S2.I10.i1.p1.1.4" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:80%;--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">. Consider </span><math id="S2.I10.i1.p1.m4" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\|\cdot\|_{3}:=\|\cdot\|_{1}+\|\cdot\|_{2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" mathsize="0.800em" rspace="0em">∥</mo><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" lspace="0em" mathcolor="#000000" mathsize="0.800em" rspace="0em">⋅</mo><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" lspace="0em" mathcolor="#000000" mathsize="0.800em" rspace="0.0835em">∥</mo><msub><mrow></mrow><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" mathsize="0.800em">3</mn></msub><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" lspace="0.0835em" mathcolor="#000000" mathsize="0.800em" rspace="0em">:=</mo><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" lspace="0em" mathcolor="#000000" mathsize="0.800em" rspace="0em">∥</mo><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" lspace="0em" mathcolor="#000000" mathsize="0.800em" rspace="0em">⋅</mo><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" lspace="0em" mathcolor="#000000" mathsize="0.800em" rspace="0em">∥</mo><msub><mrow></mrow><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" mathsize="0.800em">1</mn></msub><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" lspace="0em" mathcolor="#000000" mathsize="0.800em" rspace="0em">+</mo><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" lspace="0em" mathcolor="#000000" mathsize="0.800em" rspace="0em">∥</mo><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" lspace="0em" mathcolor="#000000" mathsize="0.800em" rspace="0em">⋅</mo><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" lspace="0em" mathcolor="#000000" mathsize="0.800em">∥</mo><msub><mrow></mrow><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" mathsize="0.800em">2</mn></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\|\cdot\|_{3}:=\|\cdot\|_{1}+\|\cdot\|_{2}</annotation></semantics></math><span id="S2.I10.i1.p1.1.5" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:80%;--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">. Prove that it is actually a norm.</span></span>
</span></span>
<span id="S2.I10.i2" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">•</span> 
<span id="S2.I10.i2.p1" class="ltx_para">
<span id="S2.I10.i2.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S2.I10.i2.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:80%;--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">Prove that a sequence converge to </span><math id="S2.I10.i2.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="x\in X" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" mathsize="0.800em">x</mi><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" mathsize="0.800em">∈</mo><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" mathsize="0.800em">X</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">x\in X</annotation></semantics></math><span id="S2.I10.i2.p1.1.2" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:80%;--ltx-fg-color:#000000;"> w.r.to </span><math id="S2.I10.i2.p1.m2" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\|\cdot\|_{3}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" mathsize="0.800em" rspace="0em">∥</mo><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" lspace="0em" mathcolor="#000000" mathsize="0.800em" rspace="0em">⋅</mo><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" lspace="0em" mathcolor="#000000" mathsize="0.800em">∥</mo><msub><mrow></mrow><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" mathsize="0.800em">3</mn></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\|\cdot\|_{3}</annotation></semantics></math><span id="S2.I10.i2.p1.1.3" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:80%;--ltx-fg-color:#000000;"> if and only if it converges to </span><math id="S2.I10.i2.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="x" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" mathsize="0.800em">x</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">x</annotation></semantics></math><span id="S2.I10.i2.p1.1.4" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:80%;--ltx-fg-color:#000000;"> both w.r.to </span><math id="S2.I10.i2.p1.m4" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\|\cdot\|_{1}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" mathsize="0.800em" rspace="0em">∥</mo><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" lspace="0em" mathcolor="#000000" mathsize="0.800em" rspace="0em">⋅</mo><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" lspace="0em" mathcolor="#000000" mathsize="0.800em">∥</mo><msub><mrow></mrow><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" mathsize="0.800em">1</mn></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\|\cdot\|_{1}</annotation></semantics></math><span id="S2.I10.i2.p1.1.5" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:80%;--ltx-fg-color:#000000;"> and w.r.to </span><math id="S2.I10.i2.p1.m5" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\|\cdot\|_{2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" mathsize="0.800em" rspace="0em">∥</mo><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" lspace="0em" mathcolor="#000000" mathsize="0.800em" rspace="0em">⋅</mo><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" lspace="0em" mathcolor="#000000" mathsize="0.800em">∥</mo><msub><mrow></mrow><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" mathsize="0.800em">2</mn></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\|\cdot\|_{2}</annotation></semantics></math><span id="S2.I10.i2.p1.1.6" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:80%;--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">.</span></span>
</span></span>
<span id="S2.I10.i3" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">•</span> 
<span id="S2.I10.i3.p1" class="ltx_para">
<span id="S2.I10.i3.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S2.I10.i3.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:80%;--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">Prove that a sequence is Cauchy wrto </span><math id="S2.I10.i3.p1.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\|\cdot\|_{3}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" mathsize="0.800em" rspace="0em">∥</mo><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" lspace="0em" mathcolor="#000000" mathsize="0.800em" rspace="0em">⋅</mo><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" lspace="0em" mathcolor="#000000" mathsize="0.800em">∥</mo><msub><mrow></mrow><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" mathsize="0.800em">3</mn></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\|\cdot\|_{3}</annotation></semantics></math><span id="S2.I10.i3.p1.1.2" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:80%;--ltx-fg-color:#000000;"> if and only if it is Cauchy both w.r.to </span><math id="S2.I10.i3.p1.m2" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\|\cdot\|_{1}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" mathsize="0.800em" rspace="0em">∥</mo><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" lspace="0em" mathcolor="#000000" mathsize="0.800em" rspace="0em">⋅</mo><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" lspace="0em" mathcolor="#000000" mathsize="0.800em">∥</mo><msub><mrow></mrow><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" mathsize="0.800em">1</mn></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\|\cdot\|_{1}</annotation></semantics></math><span id="S2.I10.i3.p1.1.3" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:80%;--ltx-fg-color:#000000;"> and w.r.to </span><math id="S2.I10.i3.p1.m3" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\|\cdot\|_{2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" mathsize="0.800em" rspace="0em">∥</mo><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" lspace="0em" mathcolor="#000000" mathsize="0.800em" rspace="0em">⋅</mo><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" lspace="0em" mathcolor="#000000" mathsize="0.800em">∥</mo><msub><mrow></mrow><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" mathsize="0.800em">2</mn></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\|\cdot\|_{2}</annotation></semantics></math><span id="S2.I10.i3.p1.1.4" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:80%;--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">. Deduce that </span><math id="S2.I10.i3.p1.m4" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\|\cdot\|_{3}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" mathsize="0.800em" rspace="0em">∥</mo><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" lspace="0em" mathcolor="#000000" mathsize="0.800em" rspace="0em">⋅</mo><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" lspace="0em" mathcolor="#000000" mathsize="0.800em">∥</mo><msub><mrow></mrow><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" mathsize="0.800em">3</mn></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\|\cdot\|_{3}</annotation></semantics></math><span id="S2.I10.i3.p1.1.5" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:80%;--ltx-fg-color:#000000;"> is complete.</span></span>
</span></span>
<span id="S2.I10.i4" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">•</span> 
<span id="S2.I10.i4.p1" class="ltx_para">
<span id="S2.I10.i4.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S2.I10.i4.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:80%;--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">Apply the open mapping theorem tho the identity from </span><math id="S2.I10.i4.p1.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\left(X,\|\cdot\|_{3}\right)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">(</mo><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" mathsize="0.800em">X</mi><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" mathsize="0.800em">,</mo><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" lspace="0em" mathcolor="#000000" mathsize="0.800em" rspace="0em">∥</mo><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" lspace="0em" mathcolor="#000000" mathsize="0.800em" rspace="0em">⋅</mo><msub><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" lspace="0em" mathcolor="#000000" mathsize="0.800em" rspace="0.167em">∥</mo><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" mathsize="0.800em">3</mn></msub><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\left(X,\|\cdot\|_{3}\right)</annotation></semantics></math><span id="S2.I10.i4.p1.1.2" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:80%;--ltx-fg-color:#000000;"> to </span><math id="S2.I10.i4.p1.m2" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\left(X,\|\cdot\|_{1}\right)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">(</mo><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" mathsize="0.800em">X</mi><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" mathsize="0.800em">,</mo><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" lspace="0em" mathcolor="#000000" mathsize="0.800em" rspace="0em">∥</mo><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" lspace="0em" mathcolor="#000000" mathsize="0.800em" rspace="0em">⋅</mo><msub><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" lspace="0em" mathcolor="#000000" mathsize="0.800em" rspace="0.167em">∥</mo><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" mathsize="0.800em">1</mn></msub><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\left(X,\|\cdot\|_{1}\right)</annotation></semantics></math><span id="S2.I10.i4.p1.1.3" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:80%;--ltx-fg-color:#000000;"> and from </span><math id="S2.I10.i4.p1.m3" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\left(X,\|\cdot\|_{3}\right)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">(</mo><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" mathsize="0.800em">X</mi><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" mathsize="0.800em">,</mo><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" lspace="0em" mathcolor="#000000" mathsize="0.800em" rspace="0em">∥</mo><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" lspace="0em" mathcolor="#000000" mathsize="0.800em" rspace="0em">⋅</mo><msub><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" lspace="0em" mathcolor="#000000" mathsize="0.800em" rspace="0.167em">∥</mo><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" mathsize="0.800em">3</mn></msub><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\left(X,\|\cdot\|_{3}\right)</annotation></semantics></math><span id="S2.I10.i4.p1.1.4" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:80%;--ltx-fg-color:#000000;"> to </span><math id="S2.I10.i4.p1.m4" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\left(X,\|\cdot\|_{2}\right)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">(</mo><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" mathsize="0.800em">X</mi><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" mathsize="0.800em">,</mo><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" lspace="0em" mathcolor="#000000" mathsize="0.800em" rspace="0em">∥</mo><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" lspace="0em" mathcolor="#000000" mathsize="0.800em" rspace="0em">⋅</mo><msub><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" lspace="0em" mathcolor="#000000" mathsize="0.800em" rspace="0.167em">∥</mo><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" mathsize="0.800em">2</mn></msub><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\left(X,\|\cdot\|_{2}\right)</annotation></semantics></math><span id="S2.I10.i4.p1.1.5" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:80%;--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">, and deduce that the three norms are equivalent.</span></span>
</span></span>
</span><span class="ltx_inline-block"><svg id="S2.SS5.SSS2.p4.pic1.pic1" class="ltx_picture" color="#FF0000" height="18.24" overflow="visible" style="vertical-align:-4.1px" version="1.1" viewBox="0 0 18.24 18.24" width="18.24"><g style="--ltx-stroke-color:#FF0000;--ltx-fill-color:#FF0000;" fill="#FF0000" stroke="#FF0000" stroke-width="1.8pt" transform="translate(0,18.24) matrix(1 0 0 -1 0 0) translate(1.25,0) translate(0,1.25)"><path style="fill:none" d="M 0 0 L 15.75 15.75 M 0 15.75 L 15.75 0"></path></g></svg></span>
<span id="S2.SS5.SSS2.p4.pic1.2.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="S2.SS5.SSS2.p4.pic1.2.2.1" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:80%;--ltx-fg-color:#FF0000;">o4-mini-high failed<span id="S2.SS5.SSS2.p4.pic1.2.2.1.1" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;"> <span class="ltx_inline-block"><svg id="S2.SS5.SSS2.p4.pic1.pic2" class="ltx_picture" color="#008000" height="18.24" overflow="visible" style="vertical-align:-4.1px" version="1.1" viewBox="0 0 18.24 18.24" width="18.24"><g style="--ltx-stroke-color:#009900;--ltx-fill-color:#009900;--ltx-fg-color:#009900;" color="#009900" fill="#009900" stroke="#009900" stroke-width="1.8pt" transform="translate(0,18.24) matrix(1 0 0 -1 0 0) translate(1.25,0) translate(0,1.25)"><path style="fill:none" d="M 0 7.87 L 5.51 0 L 15.75 15.75"></path></g></svg></span><span id="S2.SS5.SSS2.p4.pic1.2.2.1.1.1" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-fg-color:#008000;">
GPT-5 thinking passed</span></span></span></span>
</span></span></span></foreignObject></g></g></svg></span>
</div>
          
</div>
</figure>
<figure id="S2.SS5.SSS2.fig2" class="ltx_figure">
<div id="S2.SS5.SSS2.fig2.1" class="ltx_logical-block ltx_minipage ltx_align_center ltx_align_top" style="width:276.0pt;">
            
<div id="S2.SS5.SSS2.p5" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent"><span class="ltx_inline-block"><svg id="S2.SS5.SSS2.p5.pic1" class="ltx_picture" height="189.58" overflow="visible" version="1.1" viewBox="0 0 381.9 189.58" width="381.9"><g style="--ltx-stroke-color:#000000;--ltx-fill-color:#000000;" fill="#000000" stroke="#000000" stroke-width="0.4pt" transform="translate(0,189.58) matrix(1 0 0 -1 0 0)"><g style="--ltx-fill-color:#3D6666;" fill="#3D6666" fill-opacity="1.0"><path style="stroke:none" d="M 0 4.63 L 0 184.95 C 0 187.51 2.07 189.58 4.63 189.58 L 377.27 189.58 C 379.83 189.58 381.9 187.51 381.9 184.95 L 381.9 4.63 C 381.9 2.07 379.83 0 377.27 0 L 4.63 0 C 2.07 0 0 2.07 0 4.63 Z"></path></g><g style="--ltx-fill-color:#FFFFFF;" fill="#FFFFFF" fill-opacity="1.0"><path style="stroke:none" d="M 0.69 4.63 L 0.69 170.48 L 381.21 170.48 L 381.21 4.63 C 381.21 2.45 379.45 0.69 377.27 0.69 L 4.63 0.69 C 2.45 0.69 0.69 2.45 0.69 4.63 Z"></path></g><g fill-opacity="1.0" transform="matrix(1.0 0.0 0.0 1.0 20.38 177.26)"><foreignObject style="--ltx-fo-width:25.16em;--ltx-fo-height:0.56em;--ltx-fo-depth:0.16em;font-size:10pt;" height="9.84" overflow="visible" transform="matrix(1 0 0 -1 0 7.69)" width="348.14"><span class="ltx_foreignobject_container"><span class="ltx_foreignobject_content">
<span id="S2.SS5.SSS2.p5.pic1.1" class="ltx_inline-block ltx_minipage ltx_align_bottom" style="width:25.16em;">
<span id="S2.SS5.SSS2.p5.pic1.1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S2.SS5.SSS2.p5.pic1.1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold" style="font-size:80%;--ltx-fg-color:#FFFFFF;">Problem 0: All perfect numbers are even</span></span>
</span></span></span></foreignObject></g><g fill-opacity="1.0" transform="matrix(1.0 0.0 0.0 1.0 20.38 14.66)"><foreignObject style="--ltx-fo-width:29.01em;--ltx-fo-height:10.98em;--ltx-fo-depth:0.16em;font-size:10pt;" height="154.05" overflow="visible" transform="matrix(1 0 0 -1 0 151.89)" width="401.42"><span class="ltx_foreignobject_container"><span class="ltx_foreignobject_content">
<span id="S2.SS5.SSS2.p5.pic1.2" class="ltx_inline-block ltx_minipage ltx_align_bottom" style="width:29.01em;">
<span id="S2.SS5.SSS2.p5.pic1.2.1" class="ltx_p"><a href="https://math.stackexchange.com/questions/348198/best-fake-proofs-a-m-se-april-fools-day-collection" title="" class="ltx_ref ltx_href" style="font-size:80%;--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">(MathStackExchange Problem)</a><cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citep"><span id="S2.SS5.SSS2.p5.pic1.2.1.1" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:80%;--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">(</span><a href="#bib.bib5" title="" class="ltx_ref">Did, 2013</a><span id="S2.SS5.SSS2.p5.pic1.2.1.3" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:80%;--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">)</span></cite><span id="S2.SS5.SSS2.p5.pic1.2.1.4" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:80%;--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">
Check the following proof: all perfect numbers are even.</span></span>
<span id="S2.SS5.SSS2.p5.pic1.2.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="S2.SS5.SSS2.p5.pic1.2.2.1" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:80%;--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">Assume</span></span>
<span id="S2.Ex7" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<span><span class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<span class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></span>
<span class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S2.Ex7.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="2n=\sum_{d\mid n}d" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" mathsize="0.800em">2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" mathsize="0.800em">n</mi></mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" mathsize="0.800em" rspace="0.111em">=</mo><mrow><munder><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" maxsize="0.800em" minsize="0.800em" movablelimits="false" stretchy="true">∑</mo><mrow><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" mathsize="0.800em">d</mi><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" fence="false" mathcolor="#000000">|</mo><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" mathsize="0.800em">n</mi></mrow></munder><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" mathsize="0.800em">d</mi></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">2n=\sum_{d\mid n}d</annotation></semantics></math></span>
<span class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></span></span></span>
</span>
<span id="S2.SS5.SSS2.p5.pic1.2.3" class="ltx_p"><span id="S2.SS5.SSS2.p5.pic1.2.3.1" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:80%;--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">Then by Möbius inversion:</span></span>
<span id="S2.Ex8" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<span><span class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<span class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></span>
<span class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S2.Ex8.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="n=\sum_{d\mid n}2d\cdot\mu\left(\frac{n}{d}\right)" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" mathsize="0.800em">n</mi><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" mathsize="0.800em" rspace="0.111em">=</mo><mrow><mrow><munder><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" maxsize="0.800em" minsize="0.800em" movablelimits="false" stretchy="true">∑</mo><mrow><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" mathsize="0.800em">d</mi><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" fence="false" mathcolor="#000000">|</mo><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" mathsize="0.800em">n</mi></mrow></munder><mrow><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" mathsize="0.800em">2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" mathsize="0.800em">d</mi></mrow></mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" lspace="0.222em" mathcolor="#000000" mathsize="0.800em" rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><mrow><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" mathsize="0.800em">μ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">(</mo><mfrac style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000"><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" mathsize="0.800em">n</mi><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" mathsize="0.800em">d</mi></mfrac><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">n=\sum_{d\mid n}2d\cdot\mu\left(\frac{n}{d}\right)</annotation></semantics></math></span>
<span class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></span></span></span>
</span>
<span id="S2.SS5.SSS2.p5.pic1.2.4" class="ltx_p"><span id="S2.SS5.SSS2.p5.pic1.2.4.1" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:80%;--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">and therefore <math id="S2.SS5.SSS2.p5.pic1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="n" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">n</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">n</annotation></semantics></math> is even.</span></span><span class="ltx_inline-block"><svg id="S2.SS5.SSS2.p5.pic1.pic1" class="ltx_picture" color="#008000" height="18.24" overflow="visible" style="vertical-align:-4.1px" version="1.1" viewBox="0 0 18.24 18.24" width="18.24"><g style="--ltx-stroke-color:#009900;--ltx-fill-color:#009900;--ltx-fg-color:#009900;" color="#009900" fill="#009900" stroke="#009900" stroke-width="1.8pt" transform="translate(0,18.24) matrix(1 0 0 -1 0 0) translate(1.25,0) translate(0,1.25)"><path style="fill:none" d="M 0 7.87 L 5.51 0 L 15.75 15.75"></path></g></svg></span>
<span id="S2.SS5.SSS2.p5.pic1.2.5" class="ltx_p"><span id="S2.SS5.SSS2.p5.pic1.2.5.1" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:80%;--ltx-fg-color:#008000;">GPT-5 thinking passed</span></span>
</span></span></span></foreignObject></g></g></svg></span>
</div>
          
</div>
</figure>
</section>
</section>
<section id="S2.SS6" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">6 </span>Writing and Presentation</h3>

<div id="S2.SS6.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S2.SS6.p1.1" class="ltx_p">This category evaluates the ability to communicate mathematical ideas clearly and effectively, both formally and pedagogically.</p>
</div>
<section id="S2.SS6.SSS1" class="ltx_subsubsection">
<h4 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsubsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsubsection">(a) </span>Writing clean, structured proofs and definitions</h4>

<div id="S2.SS6.SSS1.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S2.SS6.SSS1.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Express arguments and definitions in a precise, logically organized, and readable format suitable for formal assessment or publication.</p>
</div>
<div id="S2.SS6.SSS1.p2" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S2.SS6.SSS1.p2.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S2.SS6.SSS1.p2.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Design Principles:</span> Use problems that require clear, well-organized, and rigorous proofs, especially ones where the arguments are nontrivial to write, so that clarity and structure are essential to the solution.</p>
</div>
<div id="S2.SS6.SSS1.p3" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S2.SS6.SSS1.p3.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S2.SS6.SSS1.p3.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Rubric:</span></p>
</div>
<div id="S2.SS6.SSS1.p4" class="ltx_para">
<table id="S2.SS6.SSS1.p4.1" class="ltx_tabular ltx_align_middle">
<tr id="S2.SS6.SSS1.p4.1.1" class="ltx_tr">
<td id="S2.SS6.SSS1.p4.1.1.1" class="ltx_td ltx_align_center ltx_border_tt"><span id="S2.SS6.SSS1.p4.1.1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Score</span></td>
<td id="S2.SS6.SSS1.p4.1.1.2" class="ltx_td ltx_nopad_r ltx_align_left ltx_align_top ltx_border_tt">
<span id="S2.SS6.SSS1.p4.1.1.2.1" class="ltx_inline-block ltx_align_top" style="width:284.5pt;">
<span id="S2.SS6.SSS1.p4.1.1.2.1.1" class="ltx_p">Description</span>
</span></td></tr>
<tr id="S2.SS6.SSS1.p4.1.2" class="ltx_tr">
<td id="S2.SS6.SSS1.p4.1.2.1" class="ltx_td ltx_align_center ltx_border_t"><span id="S2.SS6.SSS1.p4.1.2.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">3 (Excellent)</span></td>
<td id="S2.SS6.SSS1.p4.1.2.2" class="ltx_td ltx_nopad_r ltx_align_left ltx_align_top ltx_border_t">
<span id="S2.SS6.SSS1.p4.1.2.2.1" class="ltx_inline-block ltx_align_top" style="width:284.5pt;">
<span id="S2.SS6.SSS1.p4.1.2.2.1.1" class="ltx_p">Response is clearly articulated, well-structured, and easy to follow. Ideas are fully developed and effectively communicated.</span>
</span></td></tr>
<tr id="S2.SS6.SSS1.p4.1.3" class="ltx_tr">
<td id="S2.SS6.SSS1.p4.1.3.1" class="ltx_td ltx_align_center"><span id="S2.SS6.SSS1.p4.1.3.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">2 (Good)</span></td>
<td id="S2.SS6.SSS1.p4.1.3.2" class="ltx_td ltx_nopad_r ltx_align_left ltx_align_top">
<span id="S2.SS6.SSS1.p4.1.3.2.1" class="ltx_inline-block ltx_align_top" style="width:284.5pt;">
<span id="S2.SS6.SSS1.p4.1.3.2.1.1" class="ltx_p">Response is generally clear and organized, with minor lapses in structure or explanation.</span>
</span></td></tr>
<tr id="S2.SS6.SSS1.p4.1.4" class="ltx_tr">
<td id="S2.SS6.SSS1.p4.1.4.1" class="ltx_td ltx_align_center"><span id="S2.SS6.SSS1.p4.1.4.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">1 (Satisfactory)</span></td>
<td id="S2.SS6.SSS1.p4.1.4.2" class="ltx_td ltx_nopad_r ltx_align_left ltx_align_top">
<span id="S2.SS6.SSS1.p4.1.4.2.1" class="ltx_inline-block ltx_align_top" style="width:284.5pt;">
<span id="S2.SS6.SSS1.p4.1.4.2.1.1" class="ltx_p">Response includes relevant ideas but lacks clarity or organization. Transitions or explanations may be confusing.</span>
</span></td></tr>
<tr id="S2.SS6.SSS1.p4.1.5" class="ltx_tr">
<td id="S2.SS6.SSS1.p4.1.5.1" class="ltx_td ltx_align_center ltx_border_bb"><span id="S2.SS6.SSS1.p4.1.5.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">0 (Bad)</span></td>
<td id="S2.SS6.SSS1.p4.1.5.2" class="ltx_td ltx_nopad_r ltx_align_left ltx_align_top ltx_border_bb">
<span id="S2.SS6.SSS1.p4.1.5.2.1" class="ltx_inline-block ltx_align_top" style="width:284.5pt;">
<span id="S2.SS6.SSS1.p4.1.5.2.1.1" class="ltx_p">Response is disorganized, vague, or hard to follow. Ideas are poorly expressed or not communicated effectively.</span>
</span></td></tr>
</table>
</div>
<div id="S2.SS6.SSS1.p5" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S2.SS6.SSS1.p5.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S2.SS6.SSS1.p5.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Sample Problems:</span></p>
</div>
<figure id="S2.SS6.SSS1.fig1" class="ltx_figure">
<div id="S2.SS6.SSS1.fig1.1" class="ltx_logical-block ltx_minipage ltx_align_center ltx_align_top" style="width:276.0pt;">
            
<div id="S2.SS6.SSS1.p6" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent"><span class="ltx_inline-block"><svg id="S2.SS6.SSS1.p6.pic1" class="ltx_picture" height="435.59" overflow="visible" version="1.1" viewBox="0 0 381.9 435.59" width="381.9"><g style="--ltx-stroke-color:#000000;--ltx-fill-color:#000000;" fill="#000000" stroke="#000000" stroke-width="0.4pt" transform="translate(0,435.59) matrix(1 0 0 -1 0 0)"><g style="--ltx-fill-color:#3D6666;" fill="#3D6666" fill-opacity="1.0"><path style="stroke:none" d="M 0 4.63 L 0 430.96 C 0 433.52 2.07 435.59 4.63 435.59 L 377.27 435.59 C 379.83 435.59 381.9 433.52 381.9 430.96 L 381.9 4.63 C 381.9 2.07 379.83 0 377.27 0 L 4.63 0 C 2.07 0 0 2.07 0 4.63 Z"></path></g><g style="--ltx-fill-color:#FFFFFF;" fill="#FFFFFF" fill-opacity="1.0"><path style="stroke:none" d="M 0.69 4.63 L 0.69 416.49 L 381.21 416.49 L 381.21 4.63 C 381.21 2.45 379.45 0.69 377.27 0.69 L 4.63 0.69 C 2.45 0.69 0.69 2.45 0.69 4.63 Z"></path></g><g fill-opacity="1.0" transform="matrix(1.0 0.0 0.0 1.0 20.38 423.27)"><foreignObject style="--ltx-fo-width:25.16em;--ltx-fo-height:0.56em;--ltx-fo-depth:0.16em;font-size:10pt;" height="9.84" overflow="visible" transform="matrix(1 0 0 -1 0 7.69)" width="348.14"><span class="ltx_foreignobject_container"><span class="ltx_foreignobject_content">
<span id="S2.SS6.SSS1.p6.pic1.1" class="ltx_inline-block ltx_minipage ltx_align_bottom" style="width:25.16em;">
<span id="S2.SS6.SSS1.p6.pic1.1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S2.SS6.SSS1.p6.pic1.1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold" style="font-size:80%;--ltx-fg-color:#FFFFFF;">Problem 0: Big fish eats small fish</span></span>
</span></span></span></foreignObject></g><g fill-opacity="1.0" transform="matrix(1.0 0.0 0.0 1.0 20.38 14.66)"><foreignObject style="--ltx-fo-width:29.01em;--ltx-fo-height:28.76em;--ltx-fo-depth:0.16em;font-size:10pt;" height="400.06" overflow="visible" transform="matrix(1 0 0 -1 0 397.91)" width="401.42"><span class="ltx_foreignobject_container"><span class="ltx_foreignobject_content">
<span id="S2.SS6.SSS1.p6.pic1.2" class="ltx_inline-block ltx_minipage ltx_align_bottom" style="width:29.01em;">
<span id="S2.SS6.SSS1.p6.pic1.2.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S2.SS6.SSS1.p6.pic1.2.1.1" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:80%;--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">(<em id="S2.SS6.SSS1.p6.pic1.2.1.1.1" class="ltx_emph ltx_font_italic">Induction</em>) Suppose there are 10000 fish, numbered from 1 to 10000 in increasing size.
The rules are as follows:</span></span>
<span id="S2.I11" class="ltx_itemize">
<span id="S2.I11.i1" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">•</span> 
<span id="S2.I11.i1.p1" class="ltx_para">
<span id="S2.I11.i1.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S2.I11.i1.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:80%;--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">A fish can only eat the fish that is exactly one rank smaller than itself (that is, fish </span><math id="S2.I11.i1.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="i" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" mathsize="0.800em">i</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">i</annotation></semantics></math><span id="S2.I11.i1.p1.1.2" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:80%;--ltx-fg-color:#000000;"> can only eat fish </span><math id="S2.I11.i1.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="i-1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" mathsize="0.800em">i</mi><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" mathsize="0.800em">−</mo><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" mathsize="0.800em">1</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">i-1</annotation></semantics></math><span id="S2.I11.i1.p1.1.3" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:80%;--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">).</span></span>
</span></span>
<span id="S2.I11.i2" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">•</span> 
<span id="S2.I11.i2.p1" class="ltx_para">
<span id="S2.I11.i2.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S2.I11.i2.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:80%;--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">Furthermore, fish </span><math id="S2.I11.i2.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="i+1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" mathsize="0.800em">i</mi><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" mathsize="0.800em">+</mo><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" mathsize="0.800em">1</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">i+1</annotation></semantics></math><span id="S2.I11.i2.p1.1.2" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:80%;--ltx-fg-color:#000000;"> can only eat fish </span><math id="S2.I11.i2.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="i" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" mathsize="0.800em">i</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">i</annotation></semantics></math><span id="S2.I11.i2.p1.1.3" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:80%;--ltx-fg-color:#000000;"> after fish </span><math id="S2.I11.i2.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="i" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" mathsize="0.800em">i</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">i</annotation></semantics></math><span id="S2.I11.i2.p1.1.4" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:80%;--ltx-fg-color:#000000;"> has eaten fish </span><math id="S2.I11.i2.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="i-1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" mathsize="0.800em">i</mi><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" mathsize="0.800em">−</mo><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" mathsize="0.800em">1</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">i-1</annotation></semantics></math><span id="S2.I11.i2.p1.1.5" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:80%;--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">.</span></span>
</span></span>
<span id="S2.I11.i3" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">•</span> 
<span id="S2.I11.i3.p1" class="ltx_para">
<span id="S2.I11.i3.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S2.I11.i3.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:80%;--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">Fish 1 cannot eat any other fish; it can only be eaten.</span></span>
</span></span>
</span>
<span id="S2.SS6.SSS1.p6.pic1.2.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="S2.SS6.SSS1.p6.pic1.2.2.1" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:80%;--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">We assume:</span></span>
<span id="S2.I12" class="ltx_itemize">
<span id="S2.I12.i1" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">•</span> 
<span id="S2.I12.i1.p1" class="ltx_para">
<span id="S2.I12.i1.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S2.I12.i1.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:80%;--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">If there is a smaller fish available to eat, a larger fish will not pass up the opportunity.</span></span>
</span></span>
<span id="S2.I12.i2" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">•</span> 
<span id="S2.I12.i2.p1" class="ltx_para">
<span id="S2.I12.i2.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S2.I12.i2.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:80%;--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">However, self-preservation takes priority: before eating a smaller fish, a fish must ensure that doing so will not lead to it being eaten.</span></span>
</span></span>
<span id="S2.I12.i3" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">•</span> 
<span id="S2.I12.i3.p1" class="ltx_para">
<span id="S2.I12.i3.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S2.I12.i3.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:80%;--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">Every fish is infinitely intelligent, and they all know that, and they all know that they all know that, and so on (common knowledge).</span></span>
</span></span>
</span>
<span id="S2.SS6.SSS1.p6.pic1.2.3" class="ltx_p"><span id="S2.SS6.SSS1.p6.pic1.2.3.1" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:80%;--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">Question: Will fish 1,2,3 survive?</span></span><span class="ltx_inline-block"><svg id="S2.SS6.SSS1.p6.pic1.pic1" class="ltx_picture" color="#FF0000" height="18.24" overflow="visible" style="vertical-align:-4.1px" version="1.1" viewBox="0 0 18.24 18.24" width="18.24"><g style="--ltx-stroke-color:#FF0000;--ltx-fill-color:#FF0000;" fill="#FF0000" stroke="#FF0000" stroke-width="1.8pt" transform="translate(0,18.24) matrix(1 0 0 -1 0 0) translate(1.25,0) translate(0,1.25)"><path style="fill:none" d="M 0 0 L 15.75 15.75 M 0 15.75 L 15.75 0"></path></g></svg></span>
<span id="S2.SS6.SSS1.p6.pic1.2.4" class="ltx_p"><span id="S2.SS6.SSS1.p6.pic1.2.4.1" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:80%;--ltx-fg-color:#FF0000;">o4-mini-high failed<span id="S2.SS6.SSS1.p6.pic1.2.4.1.1" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;"> <span class="ltx_inline-block"><svg id="S2.SS6.SSS1.p6.pic1.pic2" class="ltx_picture" color="#008000" height="18.24" overflow="visible" style="vertical-align:-4.1px" version="1.1" viewBox="0 0 18.24 18.24" width="18.24"><g style="--ltx-stroke-color:#009900;--ltx-fill-color:#009900;--ltx-fg-color:#009900;" color="#009900" fill="#009900" stroke="#009900" stroke-width="1.8pt" transform="translate(0,18.24) matrix(1 0 0 -1 0 0) translate(1.25,0) translate(0,1.25)"><path style="fill:none" d="M 0 7.87 L 5.51 0 L 15.75 15.75"></path></g></svg></span><span id="S2.SS6.SSS1.p6.pic1.2.4.1.1.1" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-fg-color:#008000;">
GPT-5 thinking passed</span></span></span></span>
</span></span></span></foreignObject></g></g></svg></span>
</div>
          
</div>
</figure>
</section>
<section id="S2.SS6.SSS2" class="ltx_subsubsection">
<h4 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsubsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsubsection">(b) </span>Communicating ideas to different audiences</h4>

<div id="S2.SS6.SSS2.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S2.SS6.SSS2.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Adapt the depth, vocabulary, and structure of explanations to match the target audience, ranging from domain experts to general learners or automated evaluators.</p>
</div>
<div id="S2.SS6.SSS2.p2" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S2.SS6.SSS2.p2.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S2.SS6.SSS2.p2.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Design Principles:</span>
Choose problems that involve explaining a concept to different audiences—for instance, a high school student, a novice learner, and a domain expert. The goal is to assess the ability to adapt clarity, depth, and presentation style based on the listener’s background.</p>
</div>
<div id="S2.SS6.SSS2.p3" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S2.SS6.SSS2.p3.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S2.SS6.SSS2.p3.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Rubric:</span></p>
</div>
<div id="S2.SS6.SSS2.p4" class="ltx_para">
<table id="S2.SS6.SSS2.p4.1" class="ltx_tabular ltx_align_middle">
<tr id="S2.SS6.SSS2.p4.1.1" class="ltx_tr">
<td id="S2.SS6.SSS2.p4.1.1.1" class="ltx_td ltx_align_center ltx_border_tt"><span id="S2.SS6.SSS2.p4.1.1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Level</span></td>
<td id="S2.SS6.SSS2.p4.1.1.2" class="ltx_td ltx_nopad_r ltx_align_left ltx_align_top ltx_border_tt">
<span id="S2.SS6.SSS2.p4.1.1.2.1" class="ltx_inline-block ltx_align_top" style="width:284.5pt;">
<span id="S2.SS6.SSS2.p4.1.1.2.1.1" class="ltx_p">Description</span>
</span></td></tr>
<tr id="S2.SS6.SSS2.p4.1.2" class="ltx_tr">
<td id="S2.SS6.SSS2.p4.1.2.1" class="ltx_td ltx_align_center ltx_border_t"><span id="S2.SS6.SSS2.p4.1.2.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">3 (Excellent)</span></td>
<td id="S2.SS6.SSS2.p4.1.2.2" class="ltx_td ltx_nopad_r ltx_align_left ltx_align_top ltx_border_t">
<span id="S2.SS6.SSS2.p4.1.2.2.1" class="ltx_inline-block ltx_align_top" style="width:284.5pt;">
<span id="S2.SS6.SSS2.p4.1.2.2.1.1" class="ltx_p">Explanation is accurate, clear, and fully adapted to the intended audience. Tone, vocabulary, and structure are consistently effective and appropriate.</span>
</span></td></tr>
<tr id="S2.SS6.SSS2.p4.1.3" class="ltx_tr">
<td id="S2.SS6.SSS2.p4.1.3.1" class="ltx_td ltx_align_center"><span id="S2.SS6.SSS2.p4.1.3.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">2 (Good)</span></td>
<td id="S2.SS6.SSS2.p4.1.3.2" class="ltx_td ltx_nopad_r ltx_align_left ltx_align_top">
<span id="S2.SS6.SSS2.p4.1.3.2.1" class="ltx_inline-block ltx_align_top" style="width:284.5pt;">
<span id="S2.SS6.SSS2.p4.1.3.2.1.1" class="ltx_p">Explanation is with only minor lapses in clarity, tone, or level of detail.</span>
</span></td></tr>
<tr id="S2.SS6.SSS2.p4.1.4" class="ltx_tr">
<td id="S2.SS6.SSS2.p4.1.4.1" class="ltx_td ltx_align_center"><span id="S2.SS6.SSS2.p4.1.4.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">1 (Satisfactory)</span></td>
<td id="S2.SS6.SSS2.p4.1.4.2" class="ltx_td ltx_nopad_r ltx_align_left ltx_align_top">
<span id="S2.SS6.SSS2.p4.1.4.2.1" class="ltx_inline-block ltx_align_top" style="width:284.5pt;">
<span id="S2.SS6.SSS2.p4.1.4.2.1.1" class="ltx_p">Explanation is overly technical, or too shallow for the intended audience. Tone or structure may hinder understanding.</span>
</span></td></tr>
<tr id="S2.SS6.SSS2.p4.1.5" class="ltx_tr">
<td id="S2.SS6.SSS2.p4.1.5.1" class="ltx_td ltx_align_center ltx_border_bb"><span id="S2.SS6.SSS2.p4.1.5.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">0 (Bad)</span></td>
<td id="S2.SS6.SSS2.p4.1.5.2" class="ltx_td ltx_nopad_r ltx_align_left ltx_align_top ltx_border_bb">
<span id="S2.SS6.SSS2.p4.1.5.2.1" class="ltx_inline-block ltx_align_top" style="width:284.5pt;">
<span id="S2.SS6.SSS2.p4.1.5.2.1.1" class="ltx_p">Explanation is confusing, or poorly matched to the audience.</span>
</span></td></tr>
</table>
</div>
<div id="S2.SS6.SSS2.p5" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S2.SS6.SSS2.p5.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S2.SS6.SSS2.p5.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Note:</span> The explanation must be correct and accurate. Evaluation is based on the appropriateness of tone, depth, and structure for the target audience.</p>
</div>
<div id="S2.SS6.SSS2.p6" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S2.SS6.SSS2.p6.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S2.SS6.SSS2.p6.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Sample Problems:</span></p>
</div>
<figure id="S2.SS6.SSS2.fig1" class="ltx_figure">
<div id="S2.SS6.SSS2.fig1.1" class="ltx_logical-block ltx_minipage ltx_align_center ltx_align_top" style="width:276.0pt;">
            
<div id="S2.SS6.SSS2.p7" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent"><span class="ltx_inline-block"><svg id="S2.SS6.SSS2.p7.pic1" class="ltx_picture" height="87.69" overflow="visible" version="1.1" viewBox="0 0 381.9 87.69" width="381.9"><g style="--ltx-stroke-color:#000000;--ltx-fill-color:#000000;" fill="#000000" stroke="#000000" stroke-width="0.4pt" transform="translate(0,87.69) matrix(1 0 0 -1 0 0)"><g style="--ltx-fill-color:#3D6666;" fill="#3D6666" fill-opacity="1.0"><path style="stroke:none" d="M 0 4.63 L 0 83.06 C 0 85.62 2.07 87.69 4.63 87.69 L 377.27 87.69 C 379.83 87.69 381.9 85.62 381.9 83.06 L 381.9 4.63 C 381.9 2.07 379.83 0 377.27 0 L 4.63 0 C 2.07 0 0 2.07 0 4.63 Z"></path></g><g style="--ltx-fill-color:#FFFFFF;" fill="#FFFFFF" fill-opacity="1.0"><path style="stroke:none" d="M 0.69 4.63 L 0.69 68.6 L 381.21 68.6 L 381.21 4.63 C 381.21 2.45 379.45 0.69 377.27 0.69 L 4.63 0.69 C 2.45 0.69 0.69 2.45 0.69 4.63 Z"></path></g><g fill-opacity="1.0" transform="matrix(1.0 0.0 0.0 1.0 20.38 75.38)"><foreignObject style="--ltx-fo-width:25.16em;--ltx-fo-height:0.56em;--ltx-fo-depth:0.16em;font-size:10pt;" height="9.84" overflow="visible" transform="matrix(1 0 0 -1 0 7.69)" width="348.14"><span class="ltx_foreignobject_container"><span class="ltx_foreignobject_content">
<span id="S2.SS6.SSS2.p7.pic1.1" class="ltx_inline-block ltx_minipage ltx_align_bottom" style="width:25.16em;">
<span id="S2.SS6.SSS2.p7.pic1.1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S2.SS6.SSS2.p7.pic1.1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold" style="font-size:80%;--ltx-fg-color:#FFFFFF;">Problem 0: Symplectic geometry</span></span>
</span></span></span></foreignObject></g><g fill-opacity="1.0" transform="matrix(1.0 0.0 0.0 1.0 20.38 14.66)"><foreignObject style="--ltx-fo-width:29.01em;--ltx-fo-height:3.61em;--ltx-fo-depth:0.16em;font-size:10pt;" height="52.16" overflow="visible" transform="matrix(1 0 0 -1 0 50)" width="401.42"><span class="ltx_foreignobject_container"><span class="ltx_foreignobject_content">
<span id="S2.SS6.SSS2.p7.pic1.2" class="ltx_inline-block ltx_minipage ltx_align_bottom" style="width:29.01em;">
<span id="S2.SS6.SSS2.p7.pic1.2.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S2.SS6.SSS2.p7.pic1.2.1.1" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:80%;--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">Explain to a mathematician why symplectic geometry is the correct setting for classical mechanics.</span></span><span class="ltx_inline-block"><svg id="S2.SS6.SSS2.p7.pic1.pic1" class="ltx_picture" color="#FF0000" height="18.24" overflow="visible" style="vertical-align:-4.1px" version="1.1" viewBox="0 0 18.24 18.24" width="18.24"><g style="--ltx-stroke-color:#FF0000;--ltx-fill-color:#FF0000;" fill="#FF0000" stroke="#FF0000" stroke-width="1.8pt" transform="translate(0,18.24) matrix(1 0 0 -1 0 0) translate(1.25,0) translate(0,1.25)"><path style="fill:none" d="M 0 0 L 15.75 15.75 M 0 15.75 L 15.75 0"></path></g></svg></span>
<span id="S2.SS6.SSS2.p7.pic1.2.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="S2.SS6.SSS2.p7.pic1.2.2.1" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:80%;--ltx-fg-color:#FF0000;">GPT-5 thinking failed</span></span>
</span></span></span></foreignObject></g></g></svg></span>
</div>
          
</div>
</figure>
</section>
</section>
<section id="S2.SS7" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">7 </span>Intuition</h3>

<div id="S2.SS7.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S2.SS7.p1.1" class="ltx_p">This category assesses a model’s ability to reason beyond formal steps, relying on geometric insight, estimation, and qualitative judgment to support or critique solutions.</p>
</div>
<section id="S2.SS7.SSS1" class="ltx_subsubsection">
<h4 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsubsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsubsection">(a) </span>Geometric intuition</h4>

<div id="S2.SS7.SSS1.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S2.SS7.SSS1.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Understand and visualize problems via diagrams and spatial reasoning.</p>
</div>
<div id="S2.SS7.SSS1.p2" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S2.SS7.SSS1.p2.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S2.SS7.SSS1.p2.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Design Principles:</span>
Select problems where geometric insight—through diagrams, symmetry, or spatial structure—is essential to understanding or solving the problem. Emphasize reasoning that cannot be easily replaced by pure algebra.</p>
</div>
<div id="S2.SS7.SSS1.p3" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S2.SS7.SSS1.p3.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S2.SS7.SSS1.p3.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Sample Problems:</span></p>
</div>
<figure id="S2.SS7.SSS1.fig1" class="ltx_figure">
<div class="ltx_flex_figure">
<div class="ltx_flex_cell ltx_flex_size_1">
<div id="S2.SS7.SSS1.fig1.1" class="ltx_logical-block ltx_figure_panel ltx_minipage ltx_align_center ltx_align_top" style="width:276.0pt;">
            
