</span></span></span></foreignObject></g><g fill-opacity="1.0" transform="matrix(1.0 0.0 0.0 1.0 20.38 14.66)"><foreignObject style="--ltx-fo-width:29.01em;--ltx-fo-height:5.86em;--ltx-fo-depth:0.16em;font-size:10pt;" height="83.21" overflow="visible" transform="matrix(1 0 0 -1 0 81.06)" width="401.42"><span class="ltx_foreignobject_container"><span class="ltx_foreignobject_content">
<span id="S2.SS7.SSS1.p5.pic1.2" class="ltx_inline-block ltx_minipage ltx_align_bottom" style="width:29.01em;">
<span id="S2.SS7.SSS1.p5.pic1.2.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S2.SS7.SSS1.p5.pic1.2.1.1" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:80%;--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">Show that every smoothly embedded closed orientable connected surface in the <math id="S2.SS7.SSS1.p5.pic1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="3" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">3</mn><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">3</annotation></semantics></math>-sphere bounds a smoothly embedded <math id="S2.SS7.SSS1.p5.pic1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="3" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">3</mn><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">3</annotation></semantics></math>-dimensional handlebody (i.e. a boundary sum of solid tori) in the <math id="S2.SS7.SSS1.p5.pic1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="4" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">4</mn><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">4</annotation></semantics></math>-ball.</span></span><span class="ltx_inline-block"><svg id="S2.SS7.SSS1.p5.pic1.pic1" class="ltx_picture" color="#FF0000" height="18.24" overflow="visible" style="vertical-align:-4.1px" version="1.1" viewBox="0 0 18.24 18.24" width="18.24"><g style="--ltx-stroke-color:#FF0000;--ltx-fill-color:#FF0000;" fill="#FF0000" stroke="#FF0000" stroke-width="1.8pt" transform="translate(0,18.24) matrix(1 0 0 -1 0 0) translate(1.25,0) translate(0,1.25)"><path style="fill:none" d="M 0 0 L 15.75 15.75 M 0 15.75 L 15.75 0"></path></g></svg></span>
<span id="S2.SS7.SSS1.p5.pic1.2.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="S2.SS7.SSS1.p5.pic1.2.2.1" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:80%;--ltx-fg-color:#FF0000;">GPT-5 thinking failed</span></span>
</span></span></span></foreignObject></g></g></svg></span>
</div>
          
</div></div></div>
</figure>
</section>
<section id="S2.SS7.SSS2" class="ltx_subsubsection">
<h4 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsubsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsubsection">(b) </span>Performing plausibility checks</h4>

<div id="S2.SS7.SSS2.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S2.SS7.SSS2.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Use heuristics such as dimensional analysis, trying extreme values, order-of-magnitude reasoning, or test cases to assess the validity of results.</p>
</div>
<div id="S2.SS7.SSS2.p2" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S2.SS7.SSS2.p2.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S2.SS7.SSS2.p2.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Design Principles:</span>
Construct problems where direct computation or rigorous proof is difficult or impractical, but a clever use of heuristics, such as trying extreme cases, checking units, or order-of-magnitude reasoning, can reveal whether the answer is plausible.</p>
</div>
<div id="S2.SS7.SSS2.p3" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S2.SS7.SSS2.p3.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S2.SS7.SSS2.p3.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Sample Problems:</span></p>
</div>
<figure id="S2.SS7.SSS2.fig1" class="ltx_figure">
<div id="S2.SS7.SSS2.fig1.1" class="ltx_logical-block ltx_minipage ltx_align_center ltx_align_top" style="width:276.0pt;">
            
<div id="S2.SS7.SSS2.p4" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent"><span class="ltx_inline-block"><svg id="S2.SS7.SSS2.p4.pic1" class="ltx_picture" height="143.29" overflow="visible" version="1.1" viewBox="0 0 381.9 143.29" width="381.9"><g style="--ltx-stroke-color:#000000;--ltx-fill-color:#000000;" fill="#000000" stroke="#000000" stroke-width="0.4pt" transform="translate(0,143.29) matrix(1 0 0 -1 0 0)"><g style="--ltx-fill-color:#3D6666;" fill="#3D6666" fill-opacity="1.0"><path style="stroke:none" d="M 0 4.63 L 0 138.66 C 0 141.22 2.07 143.29 4.63 143.29 L 377.27 143.29 C 379.83 143.29 381.9 141.22 381.9 138.66 L 381.9 4.63 C 381.9 2.07 379.83 0 377.27 0 L 4.63 0 C 2.07 0 0 2.07 0 4.63 Z"></path></g><g style="--ltx-fill-color:#FFFFFF;" fill="#FFFFFF" fill-opacity="1.0"><path style="stroke:none" d="M 0.69 4.63 L 0.69 124.19 L 381.21 124.19 L 381.21 4.63 C 381.21 2.45 379.45 0.69 377.27 0.69 L 4.63 0.69 C 2.45 0.69 0.69 2.45 0.69 4.63 Z"></path></g><g fill-opacity="1.0" transform="matrix(1.0 0.0 0.0 1.0 20.38 130.98)"><foreignObject style="--ltx-fo-width:25.16em;--ltx-fo-height:0.56em;--ltx-fo-depth:0.16em;font-size:10pt;" height="9.84" overflow="visible" transform="matrix(1 0 0 -1 0 7.69)" width="348.14"><span class="ltx_foreignobject_container"><span class="ltx_foreignobject_content">
<span id="S2.SS7.SSS2.p4.pic1.1" class="ltx_inline-block ltx_minipage ltx_align_bottom" style="width:25.16em;">
<span id="S2.SS7.SSS2.p4.pic1.1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S2.SS7.SSS2.p4.pic1.1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold" style="font-size:80%;--ltx-fg-color:#FFFFFF;">Problem 0: Shortest geodesic vs volume</span></span>
</span></span></span></foreignObject></g><g fill-opacity="1.0" transform="matrix(1.0 0.0 0.0 1.0 20.38 14.66)"><foreignObject style="--ltx-fo-width:29.01em;--ltx-fo-height:7.63em;--ltx-fo-depth:0.16em;font-size:10pt;" height="107.76" overflow="visible" transform="matrix(1 0 0 -1 0 105.6)" width="401.42"><span class="ltx_foreignobject_container"><span class="ltx_foreignobject_content">
<span id="S2.SS7.SSS2.p4.pic1.2" class="ltx_inline-block ltx_minipage ltx_align_bottom" style="width:29.01em;">
<span id="S2.SS7.SSS2.p4.pic1.2.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S2.SS7.SSS2.p4.pic1.2.1.1" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:80%;--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">Let <math id="S2.SS7.SSS2.p4.pic1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="M" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">M</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">M</annotation></semantics></math> be a closed Riemannian aspherical <math id="S2.SS7.SSS2.p4.pic1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="n" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">n</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">n</annotation></semantics></math>-manifold, <math id="S2.SS7.SSS2.p4.pic1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="n\geq 3" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">n</mi><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">≥</mo><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">3</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">n\geq 3</annotation></semantics></math>. Let <math id="S2.SS7.SSS2.p4.pic1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathrm{sys}(M)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">sys</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" stretchy="false">(</mo><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">M</mi><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathrm{sys}(M)</annotation></semantics></math> denote the length of the shortest nontrivial geodesic on <math id="S2.SS7.SSS2.p4.pic1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="M" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">M</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">M</annotation></semantics></math>, and <math id="S2.SS7.SSS2.p4.pic1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathrm{vol}(M)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">vol</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" stretchy="false">(</mo><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">M</mi><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathrm{vol}(M)</annotation></semantics></math> denote the volume of <math id="S2.SS7.SSS2.p4.pic1.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="M" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">M</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">M</annotation></semantics></math>. Is it true that <math id="S2.SS7.SSS2.p4.pic1.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="C\cdot\mathrm{sys}(M)^{n}\geq\mathrm{vol}(M)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">C</mi><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" lspace="0.222em" mathcolor="#000000" rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">sys</mi></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" stretchy="false">(</mo><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">M</mi><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">n</mi></msup></mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">≥</mo><mrow><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">vol</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" stretchy="false">(</mo><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">M</mi><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">C\cdot\mathrm{sys}(M)^{n}\geq\mathrm{vol}(M)</annotation></semantics></math> for some <math id="S2.SS7.SSS2.p4.pic1.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="C=C(n)&gt;0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">C</mi><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">=</mo><mrow><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">C</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" stretchy="false">(</mo><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">n</mi><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">&gt;</mo><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">C=C(n)&gt;0</annotation></semantics></math> independent of <math id="S2.SS7.SSS2.p4.pic1.m10" class="ltx_Math" alttext="M" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">M</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">M</annotation></semantics></math>?</span></span><span class="ltx_inline-block"><svg id="S2.SS7.SSS2.p4.pic1.pic1" class="ltx_picture" color="#FF0000" height="18.24" overflow="visible" style="vertical-align:-4.1px" version="1.1" viewBox="0 0 18.24 18.24" width="18.24"><g style="--ltx-stroke-color:#FF0000;--ltx-fill-color:#FF0000;" fill="#FF0000" stroke="#FF0000" stroke-width="1.8pt" transform="translate(0,18.24) matrix(1 0 0 -1 0 0) translate(1.25,0) translate(0,1.25)"><path style="fill:none" d="M 0 0 L 15.75 15.75 M 0 15.75 L 15.75 0"></path></g></svg></span>
<span id="S2.SS7.SSS2.p4.pic1.2.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="S2.SS7.SSS2.p4.pic1.2.2.1" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:80%;--ltx-fg-color:#FF0000;">o4-mini-high failed<span id="S2.SS7.SSS2.p4.pic1.2.2.1.1" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;"> <span class="ltx_inline-block"><svg id="S2.SS7.SSS2.p4.pic1.pic2" class="ltx_picture" color="#008000" height="18.24" overflow="visible" style="vertical-align:-4.1px" version="1.1" viewBox="0 0 18.24 18.24" width="18.24"><g style="--ltx-stroke-color:#009900;--ltx-fill-color:#009900;--ltx-fg-color:#009900;" color="#009900" fill="#009900" stroke="#009900" stroke-width="1.8pt" transform="translate(0,18.24) matrix(1 0 0 -1 0 0) translate(1.25,0) translate(0,1.25)"><path style="fill:none" d="M 0 7.87 L 5.51 0 L 15.75 15.75"></path></g></svg></span><span id="S2.SS7.SSS2.p4.pic1.2.2.1.1.1" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-fg-color:#008000;">
GPT-5 thinking passed</span></span></span></span>
</span></span></span></foreignObject></g></g></svg></span>
</div>
          
</div>
</figure>
</section>
<section id="S2.SS7.SSS3" class="ltx_subsubsection">
<h4 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsubsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsubsection">(c) </span>Estimating numerically or asymptotically</h4>

<div id="S2.SS7.SSS3.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S2.SS7.SSS3.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Provide approximate solutions using asymptotic analysis or numerical methods when exact results are intractable.</p>
</div>
<div id="S2.SS7.SSS3.p2" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S2.SS7.SSS3.p2.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S2.SS7.SSS3.p2.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Design Principles:</span>
Use problems that involve complex estimation, requiring order-of-magnitude reasoning or bounding techniques to make progress.</p>
</div>
<div id="S2.SS7.SSS3.p3" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S2.SS7.SSS3.p3.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S2.SS7.SSS3.p3.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Sample Problems:</span></p>
</div>
<figure id="S2.SS7.SSS3.fig1" class="ltx_figure">
<div id="S2.SS7.SSS3.fig1.1" class="ltx_logical-block ltx_minipage ltx_align_center ltx_align_top" style="width:276.0pt;">
            
<div id="S2.SS7.SSS3.p4" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent"><span class="ltx_inline-block"><svg id="S2.SS7.SSS3.p4.pic1" class="ltx_picture" height="104.91" overflow="visible" version="1.1" viewBox="0 0 381.9 104.91" width="381.9"><g style="--ltx-stroke-color:#000000;--ltx-fill-color:#000000;" fill="#000000" stroke="#000000" stroke-width="0.4pt" transform="translate(0,104.91) matrix(1 0 0 -1 0 0)"><g style="--ltx-fill-color:#3D6666;" fill="#3D6666" fill-opacity="1.0"><path style="stroke:none" d="M 0 4.63 L 0 100.28 C 0 102.84 2.07 104.91 4.63 104.91 L 377.27 104.91 C 379.83 104.91 381.9 102.84 381.9 100.28 L 381.9 4.63 C 381.9 2.07 379.83 0 377.27 0 L 4.63 0 C 2.07 0 0 2.07 0 4.63 Z"></path></g><g style="--ltx-fill-color:#FFFFFF;" fill="#FFFFFF" fill-opacity="1.0"><path style="stroke:none" d="M 0.69 4.63 L 0.69 85.81 L 381.21 85.81 L 381.21 4.63 C 381.21 2.45 379.45 0.69 377.27 0.69 L 4.63 0.69 C 2.45 0.69 0.69 2.45 0.69 4.63 Z"></path></g><g fill-opacity="1.0" transform="matrix(1.0 0.0 0.0 1.0 20.38 92.6)"><foreignObject style="--ltx-fo-width:25.16em;--ltx-fo-height:0.56em;--ltx-fo-depth:0.16em;font-size:10pt;" height="9.84" overflow="visible" transform="matrix(1 0 0 -1 0 7.69)" width="348.14"><span class="ltx_foreignobject_container"><span class="ltx_foreignobject_content">
<span id="S2.SS7.SSS3.p4.pic1.1" class="ltx_inline-block ltx_minipage ltx_align_bottom" style="width:25.16em;">
<span id="S2.SS7.SSS3.p4.pic1.1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S2.SS7.SSS3.p4.pic1.1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold" style="font-size:80%;--ltx-fg-color:#FFFFFF;">Problem 0: Asymptotic expansion of a sequence</span></span>
</span></span></span></foreignObject></g><g fill-opacity="1.0" transform="matrix(1.0 0.0 0.0 1.0 20.38 14.66)"><foreignObject style="--ltx-fo-width:29.01em;--ltx-fo-height:4.86em;--ltx-fo-depth:0.16em;font-size:10pt;" height="69.38" overflow="visible" transform="matrix(1 0 0 -1 0 67.22)" width="401.42"><span class="ltx_foreignobject_container"><span class="ltx_foreignobject_content">
<span id="S2.SS7.SSS3.p4.pic1.2" class="ltx_inline-block ltx_minipage ltx_align_bottom" style="width:29.01em;">
<span id="S2.SS7.SSS3.p4.pic1.2.1" class="ltx_p"><a href="https://mathoverflow.net/questions/384047/asymptotic-analysis-of-x-n1-fracx-nn2-fracn2x-n-2" title="" class="ltx_ref ltx_href" style="font-size:80%;--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">(MathOverflow Problem)</a><cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citep"><span id="S2.SS7.SSS3.p4.pic1.2.1.1" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:80%;--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">(</span><a href="#bib.bib10" title="" class="ltx_ref">Li, 2021</a><span id="S2.SS7.SSS3.p4.pic1.2.1.3" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:80%;--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">)</span></cite><span id="S2.SS7.SSS3.p4.pic1.2.1.4" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:80%;--ltx-fg-color:#000000;"> Let <math id="S2.SS7.SSS3.p4.pic1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="x_{1}=1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">x</mi><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">1</mn></msub><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">=</mo><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">1</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">x_{1}=1</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="S2.SS7.SSS3.p4.pic1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="x_{n+1}=\frac{x_{n}}{n^{2}}+\frac{n^{2}}{x_{n}}+2,n\geqslant 1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">x</mi><mrow><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">n</mi><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">+</mo><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">1</mn></mrow></msub><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">=</mo><mrow><mfrac style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000"><msub><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">x</mi><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">n</mi></msub><msup><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">n</mi><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">2</mn></msup></mfrac><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">+</mo><mfrac style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000"><msup><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">n</mi><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">2</mn></msup><msub><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">x</mi><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">n</mi></msub></mfrac><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">+</mo><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">2</mn></mrow></mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">,</mo><mrow><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">n</mi><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">⩾</mo><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">1</mn></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">x_{n+1}=\frac{x_{n}}{n^{2}}+\frac{n^{2}}{x_{n}}+2,n\geqslant 1</annotation></semantics></math>. Is the coefficient of the third term in the asymptotic expansion of <math id="S2.SS7.SSS3.p4.pic1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="x_{n}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">x</mi><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">n</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">x_{n}</annotation></semantics></math> equal to <math id="S2.SS7.SSS3.p4.pic1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\frac{5}{8}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mfrac style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000"><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">5</mn><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">8</mn></mfrac><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\frac{5}{8}</annotation></semantics></math>?</span></span><span class="ltx_inline-block"><svg id="S2.SS7.SSS3.p4.pic1.pic1" class="ltx_picture" color="#FF0000" height="18.24" overflow="visible" style="vertical-align:-4.1px" version="1.1" viewBox="0 0 18.24 18.24" width="18.24"><g style="--ltx-stroke-color:#FF0000;--ltx-fill-color:#FF0000;" fill="#FF0000" stroke="#FF0000" stroke-width="1.8pt" transform="translate(0,18.24) matrix(1 0 0 -1 0 0) translate(1.25,0) translate(0,1.25)"><path style="fill:none" d="M 0 0 L 15.75 15.75 M 0 15.75 L 15.75 0"></path></g></svg></span>
<span id="S2.SS7.SSS3.p4.pic1.2.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="S2.SS7.SSS3.p4.pic1.2.2.1" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:80%;--ltx-fg-color:#FF0000;">GPT-5 thinking failed</span></span>
</span></span></span></foreignObject></g></g></svg></span>
</div>
          
</div>
</figure>
</section>
<section id="S2.SS7.SSS4" class="ltx_subsubsection">
<h4 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsubsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsubsection">(d) </span>Aesthetic judgment</h4>

<div id="S2.SS7.SSS4.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S2.SS7.SSS4.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Recognize when a solution is elegant, overly convoluted, or violates natural mathematical principles (e.g., symmetry, minimality). (linear algebra choose without basis or with basis; category problems with universal proof)</p>
</div>
<div id="S2.SS7.SSS4.p2" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S2.SS7.SSS4.p2.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S2.SS7.SSS4.p2.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Design Principles:</span>
Choose problems with multiple valid approaches, encouraging solvers to recognize and prefer solutions that reflect mathematical elegance—such as symmetry, minimal assumptions, or conceptual clarity—over ad hoc or overly technical methods.</p>
</div>
<div id="S2.SS7.SSS4.p3" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S2.SS7.SSS4.p3.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S2.SS7.SSS4.p3.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Rubric:</span></p>
</div>
<div id="S2.SS7.SSS4.p4" class="ltx_para">
<table id="S2.SS7.SSS4.p4.1" class="ltx_tabular ltx_align_middle">
<tr id="S2.SS7.SSS4.p4.1.1" class="ltx_tr">
<td id="S2.SS7.SSS4.p4.1.1.1" class="ltx_td ltx_align_center ltx_border_tt"><span id="S2.SS7.SSS4.p4.1.1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Level</span></td>
<td id="S2.SS7.SSS4.p4.1.1.2" class="ltx_td ltx_nopad_r ltx_align_left ltx_align_top ltx_border_tt">
<span id="S2.SS7.SSS4.p4.1.1.2.1" class="ltx_inline-block ltx_align_top" style="width:284.5pt;">
<span id="S2.SS7.SSS4.p4.1.1.2.1.1" class="ltx_p">Description</span>
</span></td></tr>
<tr id="S2.SS7.SSS4.p4.1.2" class="ltx_tr">
<td id="S2.SS7.SSS4.p4.1.2.1" class="ltx_td ltx_align_center ltx_border_t"><span id="S2.SS7.SSS4.p4.1.2.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">3 (Excellent)</span></td>
<td id="S2.SS7.SSS4.p4.1.2.2" class="ltx_td ltx_nopad_r ltx_align_left ltx_align_top ltx_border_t">
<span id="S2.SS7.SSS4.p4.1.2.2.1" class="ltx_inline-block ltx_align_top" style="width:284.5pt;">
<span id="S2.SS7.SSS4.p4.1.2.2.1.1" class="ltx_p">Consistently prefers elegant solutions that are minimal, symmetric, or conceptually insightful, and articulates their aesthetic value clearly.</span>
</span></td></tr>
<tr id="S2.SS7.SSS4.p4.1.3" class="ltx_tr">
<td id="S2.SS7.SSS4.p4.1.3.1" class="ltx_td ltx_align_center"><span id="S2.SS7.SSS4.p4.1.3.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">2 (Good)</span></td>
<td id="S2.SS7.SSS4.p4.1.3.2" class="ltx_td ltx_nopad_r ltx_align_left ltx_align_top">
<span id="S2.SS7.SSS4.p4.1.3.2.1" class="ltx_inline-block ltx_align_top" style="width:284.5pt;">
<span id="S2.SS7.SSS4.p4.1.3.2.1.1" class="ltx_p">Recognizes elegant ideas and tends to favor them, with some ability to explain why they are preferable.</span>
</span></td></tr>
<tr id="S2.SS7.SSS4.p4.1.4" class="ltx_tr">
<td id="S2.SS7.SSS4.p4.1.4.1" class="ltx_td ltx_align_center"><span id="S2.SS7.SSS4.p4.1.4.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">1 (Satisfactory)</span></td>
<td id="S2.SS7.SSS4.p4.1.4.2" class="ltx_td ltx_nopad_r ltx_align_left ltx_align_top">
<span id="S2.SS7.SSS4.p4.1.4.2.1" class="ltx_inline-block ltx_align_top" style="width:284.5pt;">
<span id="S2.SS7.SSS4.p4.1.4.2.1.1" class="ltx_p">Sometimes notices elegance but does not consistently prefer or explain it. Shows limited aesthetic awareness.</span>
</span></td></tr>
<tr id="S2.SS7.SSS4.p4.1.5" class="ltx_tr">
<td id="S2.SS7.SSS4.p4.1.5.1" class="ltx_td ltx_align_center ltx_border_bb"><span id="S2.SS7.SSS4.p4.1.5.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">0 (Bad)</span></td>
<td id="S2.SS7.SSS4.p4.1.5.2" class="ltx_td ltx_nopad_r ltx_align_left ltx_align_top ltx_border_bb">
<span id="S2.SS7.SSS4.p4.1.5.2.1" class="ltx_inline-block ltx_align_top" style="width:284.5pt;">
<span id="S2.SS7.SSS4.p4.1.5.2.1.1" class="ltx_p">Accepts or produces valid solutions without distinguishing elegant from technical or inelegant methods.</span>
</span></td></tr>
</table>
</div>
<div id="S2.SS7.SSS4.p5" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S2.SS7.SSS4.p5.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S2.SS7.SSS4.p5.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Note:</span> All solutions must be mathematically correct. This rubric evaluates preference for elegant, natural, and conceptually clear approaches.</p>
</div>
<div id="S2.SS7.SSS4.p6" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S2.SS7.SSS4.p6.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S2.SS7.SSS4.p6.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Sample Problems:</span></p>
</div>
<figure id="S2.SS7.SSS4.fig1" class="ltx_figure">
<div id="S2.SS7.SSS4.fig1.1" class="ltx_logical-block ltx_minipage ltx_align_center ltx_align_top" style="width:276.0pt;">
            
<div id="S2.SS7.SSS4.p7" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent"><span class="ltx_inline-block"><svg id="S2.SS7.SSS4.p7.pic1" class="ltx_picture" height="290.48" overflow="visible" version="1.1" viewBox="0 0 381.9 290.48" width="381.9"><g style="--ltx-stroke-color:#000000;--ltx-fill-color:#000000;" fill="#000000" stroke="#000000" stroke-width="0.4pt" transform="translate(0,290.48) matrix(1 0 0 -1 0 0)"><g style="--ltx-fill-color:#3D6666;" fill="#3D6666" fill-opacity="1.0"><path style="stroke:none" d="M 0 4.63 L 0 285.85 C 0 288.41 2.07 290.48 4.63 290.48 L 377.27 290.48 C 379.83 290.48 381.9 288.41 381.9 285.85 L 381.9 4.63 C 381.9 2.07 379.83 0 377.27 0 L 4.63 0 C 2.07 0 0 2.07 0 4.63 Z"></path></g><g style="--ltx-fill-color:#FFFFFF;" fill="#FFFFFF" fill-opacity="1.0"><path style="stroke:none" d="M 0.69 4.63 L 0.69 271.38 L 381.21 271.38 L 381.21 4.63 C 381.21 2.45 379.45 0.69 377.27 0.69 L 4.63 0.69 C 2.45 0.69 0.69 2.45 0.69 4.63 Z"></path></g><g fill-opacity="1.0" transform="matrix(1.0 0.0 0.0 1.0 20.38 278.17)"><foreignObject style="--ltx-fo-width:25.16em;--ltx-fo-height:0.56em;--ltx-fo-depth:0.16em;font-size:10pt;" height="9.84" overflow="visible" transform="matrix(1 0 0 -1 0 7.69)" width="348.14"><span class="ltx_foreignobject_container"><span class="ltx_foreignobject_content">
<span id="S2.SS7.SSS4.p7.pic1.1" class="ltx_inline-block ltx_minipage ltx_align_bottom" style="width:25.16em;">
<span id="S2.SS7.SSS4.p7.pic1.1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S2.SS7.SSS4.p7.pic1.1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold" style="font-size:80%;--ltx-fg-color:#FFFFFF;">Problem 0: Trace of tensor product of linear maps</span></span>
</span></span></span></foreignObject></g><g fill-opacity="1.0" transform="matrix(1.0 0.0 0.0 1.0 20.38 14.66)"><foreignObject style="--ltx-fo-width:29.01em;--ltx-fo-height:18.27em;--ltx-fo-depth:0.16em;font-size:10pt;" height="254.95" overflow="visible" transform="matrix(1 0 0 -1 0 252.8)" width="401.42"><span class="ltx_foreignobject_container"><span class="ltx_foreignobject_content">
<span id="S2.SS7.SSS4.p7.pic1.2" class="ltx_inline-block ltx_minipage ltx_align_bottom" style="width:29.01em;">
<span id="S2.SS7.SSS4.p7.pic1.2.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S2.SS7.SSS4.p7.pic1.2.1.1" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:80%;--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">Comparing the following two proofs of the following problem. Which one do you like more? Why?</span></span>
<span id="S2.SS7.SSS4.p7.pic1.2.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="S2.SS7.SSS4.p7.pic1.2.2.1" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:80%;--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">Problem: Let <math id="S2.SS7.SSS4.p7.pic1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="V,W" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">V</mi><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">,</mo><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">W</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">V,W</annotation></semantics></math> be finite-dimensional vector spaces and <math id="S2.SS7.SSS4.p7.pic1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="S\colon V\to V" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">S</mi><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" lspace="0.278em" mathcolor="#000000" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mrow><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">V</mi><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" stretchy="false">→</mo><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">V</mi></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">S\colon V\to V</annotation></semantics></math>, <math id="S2.SS7.SSS4.p7.pic1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="T\colon W\to W" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">T</mi><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" lspace="0.278em" mathcolor="#000000" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mrow><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">W</mi><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" stretchy="false">→</mo><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">W</mi></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">T\colon W\to W</annotation></semantics></math> be linear operators. Show that <math id="S2.SS7.SSS4.p7.pic1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="tr(S\otimes T)=tr(S)tr(T)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">t</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">r</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">S</mi><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" lspace="0.222em" mathcolor="#000000" rspace="0.222em">⊗</mo><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">T</mi></mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">=</mo><mrow><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">t</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">r</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" stretchy="false">(</mo><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">S</mi><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">t</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">r</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" stretchy="false">(</mo><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">T</mi><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">tr(S\otimes T)=tr(S)tr(T)</annotation></semantics></math>.</span></span>
<span id="S2.SS7.SSS4.p7.pic1.2.3" class="ltx_p"><span id="S2.SS7.SSS4.p7.pic1.2.3.1" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:80%;--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">Solution 1: Pick bases for <math id="S2.SS7.SSS4.p7.pic1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="V" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">V</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">V</annotation></semantics></math>, <math id="S2.SS7.SSS4.p7.pic1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="W" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">W</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">W</annotation></semantics></math>, and regard <math id="S2.SS7.SSS4.p7.pic1.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="S,T" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">S</mi><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">,</mo><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">T</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">S,T</annotation></semantics></math> as square matrices, with entries <math id="S2.SS7.SSS4.p7.pic1.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="S_{i,j}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">S</mi><mrow><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">i</mi><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">,</mo><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">j</mi></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">S_{i,j}</annotation></semantics></math>, <math id="S2.SS7.SSS4.p7.pic1.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="T_{i,j}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">T</mi><mrow><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">i</mi><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">,</mo><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">j</mi></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">T_{i,j}</annotation></semantics></math>. Then <math id="S2.SS7.SSS4.p7.pic1.m10" class="ltx_Math" alttext="tr(S\otimes T)=\sum_{i,j}S_{i,i}T_{j,j}=(\sum_{i}S_{i})(\sum_{j}T_{j})=tr(S)tr(T)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">t</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">r</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">S</mi><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" lspace="0.222em" mathcolor="#000000" rspace="0.222em">⊗</mo><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">T</mi></mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" rspace="0.111em">=</mo><mrow><msub><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">∑</mo><mrow><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">i</mi><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">,</mo><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">j</mi></mrow></msub><mrow><msub><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">S</mi><mrow><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">i</mi><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">,</mo><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">i</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">T</mi><mrow><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">j</mi><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">,</mo><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">j</mi></mrow></msub></mrow></mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">=</mo><mrow><mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" lspace="0em" mathcolor="#000000">∑</mo><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">i</mi></msub><msub><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">S</mi><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">i</mi></msub></mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" lspace="0em" mathcolor="#000000">∑</mo><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">j</mi></msub><msub><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">T</mi><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">j</mi></msub></mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">=</mo><mrow><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">t</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">r</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" stretchy="false">(</mo><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">S</mi><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">t</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">r</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" stretchy="false">(</mo><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">T</mi><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">tr(S\otimes T)=\sum_{i,j}S_{i,i}T_{j,j}=(\sum_{i}S_{i})(\sum_{j}T_{j})=tr(S)tr(T)</annotation></semantics></math>.</span></span>
<span id="S2.SS7.SSS4.p7.pic1.2.4" class="ltx_p"><span id="S2.SS7.SSS4.p7.pic1.2.4.1" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:80%;--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">Solution 2: We have a canonical isomorphism <math id="S2.SS7.SSS4.p7.pic1.m11" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\phi\colon V^{*}\otimes W^{*}\cong(V\otimes W)^{*}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">ϕ</mi><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" lspace="0.278em" mathcolor="#000000" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mrow><mrow><msup><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">V</mi><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">∗</mo></msup><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" lspace="0.222em" mathcolor="#000000" rspace="0.222em">⊗</mo><msup><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">W</mi><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">∗</mo></msup></mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">≅</mo><msup><mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">V</mi><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" lspace="0.222em" mathcolor="#000000" rspace="0.222em">⊗</mo><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">W</mi></mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">∗</mo></msup></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\phi\colon V^{*}\otimes W^{*}\cong(V\otimes W)^{*}</annotation></semantics></math> by <math id="S2.SS7.SSS4.p7.pic1.m12" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\phi(\ell\otimes\eta)(v\otimes w):=\ell(v)\eta(w)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">ϕ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" lspace="0.222em" mathcolor="#000000" rspace="0.222em">⊗</mo><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">η</mi></mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">v</mi><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" lspace="0.222em" mathcolor="#000000" rspace="0.222em">⊗</mo><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">w</mi></mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">:=</mo><mrow><mrow><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" stretchy="false">(</mo><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">v</mi><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">η</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" stretchy="false">(</mo><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">w</mi><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\phi(\ell\otimes\eta)(v\otimes w):=\ell(v)\eta(w)</annotation></semantics></math>. This shows the two trace maps <math id="S2.SS7.SSS4.p7.pic1.m13" class="ltx_Math" alttext="V^{*}\otimes W^{*}\otimes V\otimes W\to F" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msup><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">V</mi><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">∗</mo></msup><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" lspace="0.222em" mathcolor="#000000" rspace="0.222em">⊗</mo><msup><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">W</mi><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">∗</mo></msup><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" lspace="0.222em" mathcolor="#000000" rspace="0.222em">⊗</mo><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">V</mi><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" lspace="0.222em" mathcolor="#000000" rspace="0.222em">⊗</mo><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">W</mi></mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" stretchy="false">→</mo><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">F</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">V^{*}\otimes W^{*}\otimes V\otimes W\to F</annotation></semantics></math> (<math id="S2.SS7.SSS4.p7.pic1.m14" class="ltx_Math" alttext="F" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">F</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">F</annotation></semantics></math> is the base field) given by tracing off <math id="S2.SS7.SSS4.p7.pic1.m15" class="ltx_Math" alttext="V\otimes W" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">V</mi><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" lspace="0.222em" mathcolor="#000000" rspace="0.222em">⊗</mo><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">W</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">V\otimes W</annotation></semantics></math> or tracing off <math id="S2.SS7.SSS4.p7.pic1.m16" class="ltx_Math" alttext="V" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">V</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">V</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="S2.SS7.SSS4.p7.pic1.m17" class="ltx_Math" alttext="W" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">W</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">W</annotation></semantics></math> respectively are equal. Since <math id="S2.SS7.SSS4.p7.pic1.m18" class="ltx_Math" alttext="S\in V^{*}\otimes V" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">S</mi><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">∈</mo><mrow><msup><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">V</mi><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">∗</mo></msup><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" lspace="0.222em" mathcolor="#000000" rspace="0.222em">⊗</mo><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">V</mi></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">S\in V^{*}\otimes V</annotation></semantics></math>, <math id="S2.SS7.SSS4.p7.pic1.m19" class="ltx_Math" alttext="T\in W^{*}\otimes W" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">T</mi><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">∈</mo><mrow><msup><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">W</mi><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">∗</mo></msup><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" lspace="0.222em" mathcolor="#000000" rspace="0.222em">⊗</mo><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">W</mi></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">T\in W^{*}\otimes W</annotation></semantics></math>, this finishes the proof.</span></span><span class="ltx_inline-block"><svg id="S2.SS7.SSS4.p7.pic1.pic1" class="ltx_picture" color="#008000" height="18.24" overflow="visible" style="vertical-align:-4.1px" version="1.1" viewBox="0 0 18.24 18.24" width="18.24"><g style="--ltx-stroke-color:#009900;--ltx-fill-color:#009900;--ltx-fg-color:#009900;" color="#009900" fill="#009900" stroke="#009900" stroke-width="1.8pt" transform="translate(0,18.24) matrix(1 0 0 -1 0 0) translate(1.25,0) translate(0,1.25)"><path style="fill:none" d="M 0 7.87 L 5.51 0 L 15.75 15.75"></path></g></svg></span>
<span id="S2.SS7.SSS4.p7.pic1.2.5" class="ltx_p"><span id="S2.SS7.SSS4.p7.pic1.2.5.1" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:80%;--ltx-fg-color:#008000;">GPT-5 thinking passed</span></span>
</span></span></span></foreignObject></g></g></svg></span>
</div>
          
</div>
</figure>
<figure id="S2.SS7.SSS4.fig2" class="ltx_figure">
<div id="S2.SS7.SSS4.fig2.1" class="ltx_logical-block ltx_minipage ltx_align_center ltx_align_top" style="width:276.0pt;">
            
<div id="S2.SS7.SSS4.p8" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent"><span class="ltx_inline-block"><svg id="S2.SS7.SSS4.p8.pic1" class="ltx_picture" height="550.45" overflow="visible" version="1.1" viewBox="0 0 381.9 550.45" width="381.9"><g style="--ltx-stroke-color:#000000;--ltx-fill-color:#000000;" fill="#000000" stroke="#000000" stroke-width="0.4pt" transform="translate(0,550.45) matrix(1 0 0 -1 0 0)"><g style="--ltx-fill-color:#3D6666;" fill="#3D6666" fill-opacity="1.0"><path style="stroke:none" d="M 0 4.63 L 0 545.82 C 0 548.37 2.07 550.45 4.63 550.45 L 377.27 550.45 C 379.83 550.45 381.9 548.37 381.9 545.82 L 381.9 4.63 C 381.9 2.07 379.83 0 377.27 0 L 4.63 0 C 2.07 0 0 2.07 0 4.63 Z"></path></g><g style="--ltx-fill-color:#FFFFFF;" fill="#FFFFFF" fill-opacity="1.0"><path style="stroke:none" d="M 0.69 4.63 L 0.69 533.5 L 381.21 533.5 L 381.21 4.63 C 381.21 2.45 379.45 0.69 377.27 0.69 L 4.63 0.69 C 2.45 0.69 0.69 2.45 0.69 4.63 Z"></path></g><g fill-opacity="1.0" transform="matrix(1.0 0.0 0.0 1.0 20.38 538.13)"><foreignObject style="--ltx-fo-width:25.16em;--ltx-fo-height:0.56em;--ltx-fo-depth:0em;font-size:10pt;" height="7.69" overflow="visible" transform="matrix(1 0 0 -1 0 7.69)" width="348.14"><span class="ltx_foreignobject_container"><span class="ltx_foreignobject_content">
<span id="S2.SS7.SSS4.p8.pic1.1" class="ltx_inline-block ltx_minipage ltx_align_bottom" style="width:25.16em;">
<span id="S2.SS7.SSS4.p8.pic1.1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S2.SS7.SSS4.p8.pic1.1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold" style="font-size:80%;--ltx-fg-color:#FFFFFF;">Problem 0: 17 consecutive numbers</span></span>
</span></span></span></foreignObject></g><g fill-opacity="1.0" transform="matrix(1.0 0.0 0.0 1.0 20.38 14.66)"><foreignObject style="--ltx-fo-width:29.01em;--ltx-fo-height:37.21em;--ltx-fo-depth:0.16em;font-size:10pt;" height="517.07" overflow="visible" transform="matrix(1 0 0 -1 0 514.92)" width="401.42"><span class="ltx_foreignobject_container"><span class="ltx_foreignobject_content">
<span id="S2.SS7.SSS4.p8.pic1.2" class="ltx_inline-block ltx_minipage ltx_align_bottom" style="width:29.01em;">
<span id="S2.SS7.SSS4.p8.pic1.2.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S2.SS7.SSS4.p8.pic1.2.1.1" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:80%;--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">In a finite sequence of real numbers the sum of any seven successive terms is negative and the sum of any eleven successive terms is positive. Determine the maximum number of terms in the sequence.</span></span>
<span id="S2.SS7.SSS4.p8.pic1.2.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="S2.SS7.SSS4.p8.pic1.2.2.1" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:80%;--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">Solution 1: Construction for <math id="S2.SS7.SSS4.p8.pic1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="n=16" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">n</mi><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">=</mo><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">16</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">n=16</annotation></semantics></math>. Define</span></span>
<span id="S2.Ex9" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<span><span class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<span class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></span>
<span class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S2.Ex9.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="a_{j}=\begin{cases}-13,&amp;j\in\{3,7,10,14\},\\
5,&amp;\text{otherwise}.\end{cases}" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" mathsize="0.800em">a</mi><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" mathsize="0.800em">j</mi></msub><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" mathsize="0.800em">=</mo><mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">{</mo><mtable columnspacing="5pt" displaystyle="true" rowspacing="0pt"><mtr><mtd class="ltx_align_left" columnalign="left"><mrow><mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" mathsize="0.800em">−</mo><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" mathsize="0.800em">13</mn></mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" mathsize="0.800em">,</mo></mrow></mtd><mtd class="ltx_align_left" columnalign="left"><mrow><mrow><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" mathsize="0.800em">j</mi><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" mathsize="0.800em">∈</mo><mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" stretchy="false">{</mo><mrow><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" mathsize="0.800em">3</mn><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" mathsize="0.800em">,</mo><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" mathsize="0.800em">7</mn><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" mathsize="0.800em">,</mo><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" mathsize="0.800em">10</mn><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" mathsize="0.800em">,</mo><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" mathsize="0.800em">14</mn></mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow></mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" mathsize="0.800em">,</mo></mrow></mtd></mtr><mtr><mtd class="ltx_align_left" columnalign="left"><mrow><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" mathsize="0.800em">5</mn><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" mathsize="0.800em">,</mo></mrow></mtd><mtd class="ltx_align_left" columnalign="left"><mrow><mtext style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" mathsize="0.800em">otherwise</mtext><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" lspace="0em" mathcolor="#000000" mathsize="0.800em">.</mo></mrow></mtd></mtr></mtable></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">a_{j}=\begin{cases}-13,&amp;j\in\{3,7,10,14\},\\
5,&amp;\text{otherwise}.\end{cases}</annotation></semantics></math></span>
<span class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></span></span></span>
</span>
<span id="S2.SS7.SSS4.p8.pic1.2.3" class="ltx_p"><span id="S2.SS7.SSS4.p8.pic1.2.3.1" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:80%;--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">Any block of 7 consecutive terms then has exactly two entries equal to <math id="S2.SS7.SSS4.p8.pic1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="-13" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">−</mo><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">13</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">-13</annotation></semantics></math> and five entries equal to <math id="S2.SS7.SSS4.p8.pic1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="5" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">5</mn><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">5</annotation></semantics></math>, so
<math id="S2.SS7.SSS4.p8.pic1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="5\cdot 5-2\cdot 13=-1&lt;0." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mrow><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">5</mn><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" lspace="0.222em" mathcolor="#000000" rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">5</mn></mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">−</mo><mrow><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">2</mn><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" lspace="0.222em" mathcolor="#000000" rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">13</mn></mrow></mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">=</mo><mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">−</mo><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">1</mn></mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">&lt;</mo><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">0</mn></mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" lspace="0em" mathcolor="#000000">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">5\cdot 5-2\cdot 13=-1&lt;0.</annotation></semantics></math>
Any block of 11 consecutive terms has exactly three entries equal to <math id="S2.SS7.SSS4.p8.pic1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="-13" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">−</mo><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">13</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">-13</annotation></semantics></math> and eight entries equal to <math id="S2.SS7.SSS4.p8.pic1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="5" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">5</mn><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">5</annotation></semantics></math>, so
<math id="S2.SS7.SSS4.p8.pic1.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="8\cdot 5-3\cdot 13=1&gt;0." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mrow><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">8</mn><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" lspace="0.222em" mathcolor="#000000" rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">5</mn></mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">−</mo><mrow><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">3</mn><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" lspace="0.222em" mathcolor="#000000" rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">13</mn></mrow></mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">=</mo><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">1</mn><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">&gt;</mo><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">0</mn></mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" lspace="0em" mathcolor="#000000">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">8\cdot 5-3\cdot 13=1&gt;0.</annotation></semantics></math>
Thus the sequence meets the requirements.</span></span>
<span id="S2.SS7.SSS4.p8.pic1.2.4" class="ltx_p"><span id="S2.SS7.SSS4.p8.pic1.2.4.1" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:80%;--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">Non<span id="S2.SS7.SSS4.p8.pic1.2.4.1.1" class="ltx_text">-</span>existence for <math id="S2.SS7.SSS4.p8.pic1.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="n\geq 17" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">n</mi><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">≥</mo><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">17</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">n\geq 17</annotation></semantics></math>. One checks (for example by linear<span id="S2.SS7.SSS4.p8.pic1.2.4.1.2" class="ltx_text">-</span>programming or averaging arguments) that the system</span></span>
<span id="S2.Ex10" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<span><span class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<span class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></span>
<span class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S2.Ex10.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\sum_{j=i}^{i+6}a_{j}&lt;0,\hskip 8.50012pt\sum_{j=i}^{i+10}a_{j}&gt;0" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><munderover><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" maxsize="0.800em" minsize="0.800em" movablelimits="false" stretchy="true">∑</mo><mrow><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" mathsize="0.800em">j</mi><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" mathsize="0.800em">=</mo><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" mathsize="0.800em">i</mi></mrow><mrow><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" mathsize="0.800em">i</mi><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" mathsize="0.800em">+</mo><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" mathsize="0.800em">6</mn></mrow></munderover><mrow><msub><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" mathsize="0.800em">a</mi><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" mathsize="0.800em">j</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" mathsize="0.800em">&lt;</mo><mrow><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" mathsize="0.800em">0</mn><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" mathsize="0.800em" rspace="0.850em">,</mo><mrow><munderover><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" maxsize="0.800em" minsize="0.800em" movablelimits="false" stretchy="true">∑</mo><mrow><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" mathsize="0.800em">j</mi><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" mathsize="0.800em">=</mo><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" mathsize="0.800em">i</mi></mrow><mrow><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" mathsize="0.800em">i</mi><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" mathsize="0.800em">+</mo><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" mathsize="0.800em">10</mn></mrow></munderover><msub><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" mathsize="0.800em">a</mi><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" mathsize="0.800em">j</mi></msub></mrow></mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" mathsize="0.800em">&gt;</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" mathsize="0.800em">0</mn></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\sum_{j=i}^{i+6}a_{j}&lt;0,\hskip 8.50012pt\sum_{j=i}^{i+10}a_{j}&gt;0</annotation></semantics></math></span>
<span class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></span></span></span>
</span>
<span id="S2.SS7.SSS4.p8.pic1.2.5" class="ltx_p"><span id="S2.SS7.SSS4.p8.pic1.2.5.1" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:80%;--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">for <math id="S2.SS7.SSS4.p8.pic1.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="1\leq i\leq n-6" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">1</mn><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">≤</mo><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">i</mi><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">≤</mo><mrow><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">n</mi><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">−</mo><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">6</mn></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">1\leq i\leq n-6</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="S2.SS7.SSS4.p8.pic1.m10" class="ltx_Math" alttext="1\leq i\leq n-10" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">1</mn><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">≤</mo><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">i</mi><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">≤</mo><mrow><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">n</mi><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">−</mo><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">10</mn></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">1\leq i\leq n-10</annotation></semantics></math> has no solution once <math id="S2.SS7.SSS4.p8.pic1.m11" class="ltx_Math" alttext="n\geq 17" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">n</mi><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">≥</mo><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">17</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">n\geq 17</annotation></semantics></math>.</span></span>
<span id="S2.SS7.SSS4.p8.pic1.2.6" class="ltx_p"><span id="S2.SS7.SSS4.p8.pic1.2.6.1" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:80%;--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">Hence the maximum possible length is <math id="S2.SS7.SSS4.p8.pic1.m12" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\boxed{16}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><menclose notation="box"><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">16</mn></menclose><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\boxed{16}</annotation></semantics></math>.</span></span>
<span id="S2.SS7.SSS4.p8.pic1.2.7" class="ltx_p"><span id="S2.SS7.SSS4.p8.pic1.2.7.1" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:80%;--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">Solution 2:
Let <math id="S2.SS7.SSS4.p8.pic1.m13" class="ltx_Math" alttext="x_{1},x_{2},\ldots" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">x</mi><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">1</mn></msub><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">,</mo><msub><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">x</mi><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">2</mn></msub><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">,</mo><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" mathvariant="normal">…</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">x_{1},x_{2},\ldots</annotation></semantics></math> be the given sequence and let <math id="S2.SS7.SSS4.p8.pic1.m14" class="ltx_Math" alttext="s_{n}=x_{1}+x_{2}+\ldots+x_{n}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">s</mi><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">n</mi></msub><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">=</mo><mrow><msub><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">x</mi><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">1</mn></msub><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">+</mo><msub><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">x</mi><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">2</mn></msub><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">+</mo><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">+</mo><msub><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">x</mi><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">n</mi></msub></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">s_{n}=x_{1}+x_{2}+\ldots+x_{n}</annotation></semantics></math>. The conditions from the hypothesis can be now written as <math id="S2.SS7.SSS4.p8.pic1.m15" class="ltx_Math" alttext="s_{n+7}&lt;s_{n}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">s</mi><mrow><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">n</mi><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">+</mo><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">7</mn></mrow></msub><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">&lt;</mo><msub><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">s</mi><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">n</mi></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">s_{n+7}&lt;s_{n}</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="S2.SS7.SSS4.p8.pic1.m16" class="ltx_Math" alttext="s_{n+11}&gt;s_{n}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">s</mi><mrow><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">n</mi><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">+</mo><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">11</mn></mrow></msub><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">&gt;</mo><msub><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">s</mi><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">n</mi></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">s_{n+11}&gt;s_{n}</annotation></semantics></math> for all <math id="S2.SS7.SSS4.p8.pic1.m17" class="ltx_Math" alttext="n\geq 1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">n</mi><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">≥</mo><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">1</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">n\geq 1</annotation></semantics></math>. We then have:
<math id="S2.SS7.SSS4.p8.pic1.m18" class="ltx_Math" alttext="0&lt;s_{11}&lt;s_{4}&lt;s_{15}&lt;s_{8}&lt;s_{1}&lt;s_{12}&lt;s_{5}&lt;s_{16}&lt;s_{9}&lt;s_{2}&lt;s_{13}&lt;s_{6}&lt;s_{17}&lt;s_{10}&lt;s_{3}&lt;s_{14}&lt;s_{7}&lt;0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">0</mn><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">&lt;</mo><msub><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">s</mi><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">11</mn></msub><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">&lt;</mo><msub><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">s</mi><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">4</mn></msub><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">&lt;</mo><msub><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">s</mi><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">15</mn></msub><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">&lt;</mo><msub><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">s</mi><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">8</mn></msub><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">&lt;</mo><msub><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">s</mi><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">1</mn></msub><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">&lt;</mo><msub><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">s</mi><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">12</mn></msub><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">&lt;</mo><msub><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">s</mi><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">5</mn></msub><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">&lt;</mo><msub><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">s</mi><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">16</mn></msub><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">&lt;</mo><msub><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">s</mi><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">9</mn></msub><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">&lt;</mo><msub><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">s</mi><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">2</mn></msub><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">&lt;</mo><msub><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">s</mi><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">13</mn></msub><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">&lt;</mo><msub><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">s</mi><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">6</mn></msub><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">&lt;</mo><msub><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">s</mi><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">17</mn></msub><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">&lt;</mo><msub><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">s</mi><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">10</mn></msub><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">&lt;</mo><msub><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">s</mi><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">3</mn></msub><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">&lt;</mo><msub><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">s</mi><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">14</mn></msub><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">&lt;</mo><msub><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">s</mi><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">7</mn></msub><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">&lt;</mo><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">0&lt;s_{11}&lt;s_{4}&lt;s_{15}&lt;s_{8}&lt;s_{1}&lt;s_{12}&lt;s_{5}&lt;s_{16}&lt;s_{9}&lt;s_{2}&lt;s_{13}&lt;s_{6}&lt;s_{17}&lt;s_{10}&lt;s_{3}&lt;s_{14}&lt;s_{7}&lt;0</annotation></semantics></math>, a contradiction.
Therefore, the sequence cannot have 17 terms. In order to show that 16 is the answer, just take 16 real numbers satisfying <math id="S2.SS7.SSS4.p8.pic1.m19" class="ltx_Math" alttext="s_{10}&lt;s_{3}&lt;s_{14}&lt;s_{7}&lt;0&lt;s_{11}&lt;s_{4}&lt;s_{15}&lt;s_{8}&lt;s_{1}&lt;s_{12}&lt;s_{5}&lt;s_{16}&lt;s_{9}&lt;s_{2}&lt;s_{13}&lt;s_{6}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">s</mi><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">10</mn></msub><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">&lt;</mo><msub><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">s</mi><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">3</mn></msub><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">&lt;</mo><msub><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">s</mi><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">14</mn></msub><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">&lt;</mo><msub><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">s</mi><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">7</mn></msub><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">&lt;</mo><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">0</mn><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">&lt;</mo><msub><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">s</mi><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">11</mn></msub><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">&lt;</mo><msub><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">s</mi><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">4</mn></msub><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">&lt;</mo><msub><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">s</mi><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">15</mn></msub><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">&lt;</mo><msub><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">s</mi><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">8</mn></msub><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">&lt;</mo><msub><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">s</mi><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">1</mn></msub><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">&lt;</mo><msub><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">s</mi><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">12</mn></msub><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">&lt;</mo><msub><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">s</mi><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">5</mn></msub><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">&lt;</mo><msub><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">s</mi><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">16</mn></msub><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">&lt;</mo><msub><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">s</mi><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">9</mn></msub><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">&lt;</mo><msub><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">s</mi><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">2</mn></msub><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">&lt;</mo><msub><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">s</mi><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">13</mn></msub><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">&lt;</mo><msub><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">s</mi><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">6</mn></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">s_{10}&lt;s_{3}&lt;s_{14}&lt;s_{7}&lt;0&lt;s_{11}&lt;s_{4}&lt;s_{15}&lt;s_{8}&lt;s_{1}&lt;s_{12}&lt;s_{5}&lt;s_{16}&lt;s_{9}&lt;s_{2}&lt;s_{13}&lt;s_{6}</annotation></semantics></math>. We have <math id="S2.SS7.SSS4.p8.pic1.m20" class="ltx_Math" alttext="x_{1}=s_{1}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">x</mi><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">1</mn></msub><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">=</mo><msub><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">s</mi><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">1</mn></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">x_{1}=s_{1}</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="S2.SS7.SSS4.p8.pic1.m21" class="ltx_Math" alttext="x_{n}=s_{n}-s_{n-1}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">x</mi><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">n</mi></msub><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">=</mo><mrow><msub><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">s</mi><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">n</mi></msub><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">−</mo><msub><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">s</mi><mrow><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">n</mi><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">−</mo><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">1</mn></mrow></msub></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">x_{n}=s_{n}-s_{n-1}</annotation></semantics></math> for <math id="S2.SS7.SSS4.p8.pic1.m22" class="ltx_Math" alttext="n\geq 2" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">n</mi><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">≥</mo><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">2</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">n\geq 2</annotation></semantics></math>. Thus we found all sequences with the given properties.</span></span>
<span id="S2.SS7.SSS4.p8.pic1.2.8" class="ltx_p"><span id="S2.SS7.SSS4.p8.pic1.2.8.1" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:80%;--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">Which do you find more elegant, and why? Discuss in terms of simplicity, symmetry, or conceptual insight.</span></span><span class="ltx_inline-block"><svg id="S2.SS7.SSS4.p8.pic1.pic1" class="ltx_picture" color="#008000" height="18.24" overflow="visible" style="vertical-align:-4.1px" version="1.1" viewBox="0 0 18.24 18.24" width="18.24"><g style="--ltx-stroke-color:#009900;--ltx-fill-color:#009900;--ltx-fg-color:#009900;" color="#009900" fill="#009900" stroke="#009900" stroke-width="1.8pt" transform="translate(0,18.24) matrix(1 0 0 -1 0 0) translate(1.25,0) translate(0,1.25)"><path style="fill:none" d="M 0 7.87 L 5.51 0 L 15.75 15.75"></path></g></svg></span>
<span id="S2.SS7.SSS4.p8.pic1.2.9" class="ltx_p"><span id="S2.SS7.SSS4.p8.pic1.2.9.1" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:80%;--ltx-fg-color:#008000;">GPT-5 thinking passed</span></span>
</span></span></span></foreignObject></g></g></svg></span>
</div>
          
</div>
</figure>
</section>
</section>
<section id="S2.SS8" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">8 </span>Meta Skills</h3>

<div id="S2.SS8.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S2.SS8.p1.1" class="ltx_p">This category captures high-level thinking abilities that transcend specific problem types, enabling flexible reasoning across abstract and unfamiliar domains.</p>
</div>
<section id="S2.SS8.SSS1" class="ltx_subsubsection">
<h4 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsubsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsubsection">(a) </span>Thinking abstractly</h4>

<div id="S2.SS8.SSS1.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S2.SS8.SSS1.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Engage with general structures such as groups, graphs, or vector spaces, and reason about idealized systems rather than specific instances.</p>
</div>
<div id="S2.SS8.SSS1.p2" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S2.SS8.SSS1.p2.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S2.SS8.SSS1.p2.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Design Principles:</span>
Select problems that emphasize reasoning about abstract mathematical structures, such as vector spaces, groups, or categories.</p>
</div>
<div id="S2.SS8.SSS1.p3" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S2.SS8.SSS1.p3.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S2.SS8.SSS1.p3.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Sample Problems:</span></p>
</div>
<figure id="S2.SS8.SSS1.fig1" class="ltx_figure">
<div class="ltx_flex_figure">
<div class="ltx_flex_cell ltx_flex_size_1">
<div id="S2.SS8.SSS1.fig1.1" class="ltx_logical-block ltx_figure_panel ltx_minipage ltx_align_center ltx_align_top" style="width:276.0pt;">
            
<div id="S2.SS8.SSS1.p4" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent"><span class="ltx_inline-block"><svg id="S2.SS8.SSS1.p4.pic1" class="ltx_picture" height="87.69" overflow="visible" version="1.1" viewBox="0 0 381.9 87.69" width="381.9"><g style="--ltx-stroke-color:#000000;--ltx-fill-color:#000000;" fill="#000000" stroke="#000000" stroke-width="0.4pt" transform="translate(0,87.69) matrix(1 0 0 -1 0 0)"><g style="--ltx-fill-color:#3D6666;" fill="#3D6666" fill-opacity="1.0"><path style="stroke:none" d="M 0 4.63 L 0 83.06 C 0 85.62 2.07 87.69 4.63 87.69 L 377.27 87.69 C 379.83 87.69 381.9 85.62 381.9 83.06 L 381.9 4.63 C 381.9 2.07 379.83 0 377.27 0 L 4.63 0 C 2.07 0 0 2.07 0 4.63 Z"></path></g><g style="--ltx-fill-color:#FFFFFF;" fill="#FFFFFF" fill-opacity="1.0"><path style="stroke:none" d="M 0.69 4.63 L 0.69 68.6 L 381.21 68.6 L 381.21 4.63 C 381.21 2.45 379.45 0.69 377.27 0.69 L 4.63 0.69 C 2.45 0.69 0.69 2.45 0.69 4.63 Z"></path></g><g fill-opacity="1.0" transform="matrix(1.0 0.0 0.0 1.0 20.38 75.38)"><foreignObject style="--ltx-fo-width:25.16em;--ltx-fo-height:0.56em;--ltx-fo-depth:0.16em;font-size:10pt;" height="9.84" overflow="visible" transform="matrix(1 0 0 -1 0 7.69)" width="348.14"><span class="ltx_foreignobject_container"><span class="ltx_foreignobject_content">
<span id="S2.SS8.SSS1.p4.pic1.1" class="ltx_inline-block ltx_minipage ltx_align_bottom" style="width:25.16em;">
<span id="S2.SS8.SSS1.p4.pic1.1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S2.SS8.SSS1.p4.pic1.1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold" style="font-size:80%;--ltx-fg-color:#FFFFFF;">Problem 0: Open interval</span></span>
</span></span></span></foreignObject></g><g fill-opacity="1.0" transform="matrix(1.0 0.0 0.0 1.0 20.38 14.66)"><foreignObject style="--ltx-fo-width:29.01em;--ltx-fo-height:3.61em;--ltx-fo-depth:0.16em;font-size:10pt;" height="52.16" overflow="visible" transform="matrix(1 0 0 -1 0 50)" width="401.42"><span class="ltx_foreignobject_container"><span class="ltx_foreignobject_content">
<span id="S2.SS8.SSS1.p4.pic1.2" class="ltx_inline-block ltx_minipage ltx_align_bottom" style="width:29.01em;">
<span id="S2.SS8.SSS1.p4.pic1.2.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S2.SS8.SSS1.p4.pic1.2.1.1" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:80%;--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">Can a nonempty open interval be covered by countably many disjoint closed intervals?</span></span><span class="ltx_inline-block"><svg id="S2.SS8.SSS1.p4.pic1.pic1" class="ltx_picture" color="#FF0000" height="18.24" overflow="visible" style="vertical-align:-4.1px" version="1.1" viewBox="0 0 18.24 18.24" width="18.24"><g style="--ltx-stroke-color:#FF0000;--ltx-fill-color:#FF0000;" fill="#FF0000" stroke="#FF0000" stroke-width="1.8pt" transform="translate(0,18.24) matrix(1 0 0 -1 0 0) translate(1.25,0) translate(0,1.25)"><path style="fill:none" d="M 0 0 L 15.75 15.75 M 0 15.75 L 15.75 0"></path></g></svg></span>
<span id="S2.SS8.SSS1.p4.pic1.2.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="S2.SS8.SSS1.p4.pic1.2.2.1" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:80%;--ltx-fg-color:#FF0000;">GPT-5 thinking failed</span></span>
</span></span></span></foreignObject></g></g></svg></span>
</div>
          
</div></div><div class="ltx_flex_break"></div><div class="ltx_flex_cell ltx_flex_size_1">
<div id="S2.SS8.SSS1.fig1.2" class="ltx_logical-block ltx_figure_panel ltx_minipage ltx_align_center ltx_align_top" style="width:276.0pt;">
            
<div id="S2.SS8.SSS1.p5" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent"><span class="ltx_inline-block"><svg id="S2.SS8.SSS1.p5.pic1" class="ltx_picture" height="200.6" overflow="visible" version="1.1" viewBox="0 0 381.9 200.6" width="381.9"><g style="--ltx-stroke-color:#000000;--ltx-fill-color:#000000;" fill="#000000" stroke="#000000" stroke-width="0.4pt" transform="translate(0,200.6) matrix(1 0 0 -1 0 0)"><g style="--ltx-fill-color:#3D6666;" fill="#3D6666" fill-opacity="1.0"><path style="stroke:none" d="M 0 4.63 L 0 195.97 C 0 198.53 2.07 200.6 4.63 200.6 L 377.27 200.6 C 379.83 200.6 381.9 198.53 381.9 195.97 L 381.9 4.63 C 381.9 2.07 379.83 0 377.27 0 L 4.63 0 C 2.07 0 0 2.07 0 4.63 Z"></path></g><g style="--ltx-fill-color:#FFFFFF;" fill="#FFFFFF" fill-opacity="1.0"><path style="stroke:none" d="M 0.69 4.63 L 0.69 181.5 L 381.21 181.5 L 381.21 4.63 C 381.21 2.45 379.45 0.69 377.27 0.69 L 4.63 0.69 C 2.45 0.69 0.69 2.45 0.69 4.63 Z"></path></g><g fill-opacity="1.0" transform="matrix(1.0 0.0 0.0 1.0 20.38 188.29)"><foreignObject style="--ltx-fo-width:25.16em;--ltx-fo-height:0.56em;--ltx-fo-depth:0.16em;font-size:10pt;" height="9.84" overflow="visible" transform="matrix(1 0 0 -1 0 7.69)" width="348.14"><span class="ltx_foreignobject_container"><span class="ltx_foreignobject_content">
<span id="S2.SS8.SSS1.p5.pic1.1" class="ltx_inline-block ltx_minipage ltx_align_bottom" style="width:25.16em;">
<span id="S2.SS8.SSS1.p5.pic1.1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S2.SS8.SSS1.p5.pic1.1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold" style="font-size:80%;--ltx-fg-color:#FFFFFF;">Problem 0: <math id="S2.SS8.SSS1.p5.pic1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="*" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#FFFFFF;" mathcolor="#FFFFFF">∗</mo><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">*</annotation></semantics></math> operation</span></span>
</span></span></span></foreignObject></g><g fill-opacity="1.0" transform="matrix(1.0 0.0 0.0 1.0 20.38 14.66)"><foreignObject style="--ltx-fo-width:29.01em;--ltx-fo-height:11.77em;--ltx-fo-depth:0.16em;font-size:10pt;" height="165.07" overflow="visible" transform="matrix(1 0 0 -1 0 162.91)" width="401.42"><span class="ltx_foreignobject_container"><span class="ltx_foreignobject_content">
<span id="S2.SS8.SSS1.p5.pic1.2" class="ltx_inline-block ltx_minipage ltx_align_bottom" style="width:29.01em;">
<span id="S2.SS8.SSS1.p5.pic1.2.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S2.SS8.SSS1.p5.pic1.2.1.1" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:80%;--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">Let <math id="S2.SS8.SSS1.p5.pic1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="*" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">∗</mo><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">*</annotation></semantics></math> denote an arbitrary binary operation The constant property <math id="S2.SS8.SSS1.p5.pic1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="x*y=z*w" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">x</mi><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" lspace="0.222em" mathcolor="#000000" rspace="0.222em">∗</mo><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">y</mi></mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">=</mo><mrow><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">z</mi><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" lspace="0.222em" mathcolor="#000000" rspace="0.222em">∗</mo><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">w</mi></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">x*y=z*w</annotation></semantics></math> implies the commutative property <math id="S2.SS8.SSS1.p5.pic1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="x*y=y*x" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">x</mi><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" lspace="0.222em" mathcolor="#000000" rspace="0.222em">∗</mo><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">y</mi></mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">=</mo><mrow><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">y</mi><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" lspace="0.222em" mathcolor="#000000" rspace="0.222em">∗</mo><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">x</mi></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">x*y=y*x</annotation></semantics></math>, but the commutative property does not imply the constant property. Is there a property strictly in between these? So that it is implied by the constant property and it implies the commutative properties, but both of these implications are false in the opposite direction. Your property cannot refer to auxiliary fixed elements or use quantifiers and it must be expressed by a single equation (so you cannot say commutative+associative)</span></span><span class="ltx_inline-block"><svg id="S2.SS8.SSS1.p5.pic1.pic1" class="ltx_picture" color="#FF0000" height="18.24" overflow="visible" style="vertical-align:-4.1px" version="1.1" viewBox="0 0 18.24 18.24" width="18.24"><g style="--ltx-stroke-color:#FF0000;--ltx-fill-color:#FF0000;" fill="#FF0000" stroke="#FF0000" stroke-width="1.8pt" transform="translate(0,18.24) matrix(1 0 0 -1 0 0) translate(1.25,0) translate(0,1.25)"><path style="fill:none" d="M 0 0 L 15.75 15.75 M 0 15.75 L 15.75 0"></path></g></svg></span>
<span id="S2.SS8.SSS1.p5.pic1.2.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="S2.SS8.SSS1.p5.pic1.2.2.1" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:80%;--ltx-fg-color:#FF0000;">GPT-5 thinking failed</span></span>
</span></span></span></foreignObject></g></g></svg></span>
</div>
          
</div></div><div class="ltx_flex_break"></div><div class="ltx_flex_cell ltx_flex_size_1">
<div id="S2.SS8.SSS1.fig1.3" class="ltx_logical-block ltx_figure_panel ltx_minipage ltx_align_center ltx_align_top" style="width:276.0pt;">
            
<div id="S2.SS8.SSS1.p6" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent"><span class="ltx_inline-block"><svg id="S2.SS8.SSS1.p6.pic1" class="ltx_picture" height="104.91" overflow="visible" version="1.1" viewBox="0 0 381.9 104.91" width="381.9"><g style="--ltx-stroke-color:#000000;--ltx-fill-color:#000000;" fill="#000000" stroke="#000000" stroke-width="0.4pt" transform="translate(0,104.91) matrix(1 0 0 -1 0 0)"><g style="--ltx-fill-color:#3D6666;" fill="#3D6666" fill-opacity="1.0"><path style="stroke:none" d="M 0 4.63 L 0 100.28 C 0 102.84 2.07 104.91 4.63 104.91 L 377.27 104.91 C 379.83 104.91 381.9 102.84 381.9 100.28 L 381.9 4.63 C 381.9 2.07 379.83 0 377.27 0 L 4.63 0 C 2.07 0 0 2.07 0 4.63 Z"></path></g><g style="--ltx-fill-color:#FFFFFF;" fill="#FFFFFF" fill-opacity="1.0"><path style="stroke:none" d="M 0.69 4.63 L 0.69 85.81 L 381.21 85.81 L 381.21 4.63 C 381.21 2.45 379.45 0.69 377.27 0.69 L 4.63 0.69 C 2.45 0.69 0.69 2.45 0.69 4.63 Z"></path></g><g fill-opacity="1.0" transform="matrix(1.0 0.0 0.0 1.0 20.38 92.6)"><foreignObject style="--ltx-fo-width:25.16em;--ltx-fo-height:0.56em;--ltx-fo-depth:0.16em;font-size:10pt;" height="9.84" overflow="visible" transform="matrix(1 0 0 -1 0 7.69)" width="348.14"><span class="ltx_foreignobject_container"><span class="ltx_foreignobject_content">
<span id="S2.SS8.SSS1.p6.pic1.1" class="ltx_inline-block ltx_minipage ltx_align_bottom" style="width:25.16em;">
<span id="S2.SS8.SSS1.p6.pic1.1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S2.SS8.SSS1.p6.pic1.1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold" style="font-size:80%;--ltx-fg-color:#FFFFFF;">Problem 0: Subtraction in Abelian group</span></span>
</span></span></span></foreignObject></g><g fill-opacity="1.0" transform="matrix(1.0 0.0 0.0 1.0 20.38 14.66)"><foreignObject style="--ltx-fo-width:29.01em;--ltx-fo-height:4.86em;--ltx-fo-depth:0.16em;font-size:10pt;" height="69.38" overflow="visible" transform="matrix(1 0 0 -1 0 67.22)" width="401.42"><span class="ltx_foreignobject_container"><span class="ltx_foreignobject_content">
<span id="S2.SS8.SSS1.p6.pic1.2" class="ltx_inline-block ltx_minipage ltx_align_bottom" style="width:29.01em;">
<span id="S2.SS8.SSS1.p6.pic1.2.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S2.SS8.SSS1.p6.pic1.2.1.1" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:80%;--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">Let <math id="S2.SS8.SSS1.p6.pic1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="*" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">∗</mo><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">*</annotation></semantics></math> be an arbitrary binary relation on a set <math id="S2.SS8.SSS1.p6.pic1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="S" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">S</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">S</annotation></semantics></math>. Show that <math id="S2.SS8.SSS1.p6.pic1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="*" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">∗</mo><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">*</annotation></semantics></math> defines subtraction in an Abelian group if and only if <math id="S2.SS8.SSS1.p6.pic1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="x*(y*(z*(x*y)))=z" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">x</mi><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" lspace="0.222em" mathcolor="#000000" rspace="0.222em">∗</mo><mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">y</mi><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" lspace="0.222em" mathcolor="#000000" rspace="0.222em">∗</mo><mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">z</mi><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" lspace="0.222em" mathcolor="#000000" rspace="0.222em">∗</mo><mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">x</mi><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" lspace="0.222em" mathcolor="#000000" rspace="0.222em">∗</mo><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">y</mi></mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">=</mo><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">z</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">x*(y*(z*(x*y)))=z</annotation></semantics></math> for all <math id="S2.SS8.SSS1.p6.pic1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="x,y,z\in S" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">x</mi><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">,</mo><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">y</mi><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">,</mo><mrow><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">z</mi><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">∈</mo><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">S</mi></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">x,y,z\in S</annotation></semantics></math>.</span></span><span class="ltx_inline-block"><svg id="S2.SS8.SSS1.p6.pic1.pic1" class="ltx_picture" color="#008000" height="18.24" overflow="visible" style="vertical-align:-4.1px" version="1.1" viewBox="0 0 18.24 18.24" width="18.24"><g style="--ltx-stroke-color:#009900;--ltx-fill-color:#009900;--ltx-fg-color:#009900;" color="#009900" fill="#009900" stroke="#009900" stroke-width="1.8pt" transform="translate(0,18.24) matrix(1 0 0 -1 0 0) translate(1.25,0) translate(0,1.25)"><path style="fill:none" d="M 0 7.87 L 5.51 0 L 15.75 15.75"></path></g></svg></span>
<span id="S2.SS8.SSS1.p6.pic1.2.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="S2.SS8.SSS1.p6.pic1.2.2.1" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:80%;--ltx-fg-color:#008000;">GPT-5 thinking passed</span></span>
</span></span></span></foreignObject></g></g></svg></span>
</div>
          
</div></div></div>
</figure>
</section>
<section id="S2.SS8.SSS2" class="ltx_subsubsection">
<h4 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsubsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsubsection">(b) </span>Transferring methods across domains</h4>

<div id="S2.SS8.SSS2.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S2.SS8.SSS2.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Apply tools or strategies from one area (e.g., probability) to solve problems in another (e.g., number theory), showcasing flexible conceptual adaptation.</p>
</div>
<div id="S2.SS8.SSS2.p2" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S2.SS8.SSS2.p2.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S2.SS8.SSS2.p2.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Design Principles:</span>
Design problems that can be approached using techniques from other mathematical domains. Emphasize conceptual reuse, creative mappings, or analogies between seemingly unrelated fields.</p>
</div>
<div id="S2.SS8.SSS2.p3" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S2.SS8.SSS2.p3.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S2.SS8.SSS2.p3.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Sample Problems:</span></p>
</div>
<figure id="S2.SS8.SSS2.fig1" class="ltx_figure">
<div class="ltx_flex_figure">
<div class="ltx_flex_cell ltx_flex_size_1">
<div id="S2.SS8.SSS2.fig1.1" class="ltx_logical-block ltx_figure_panel ltx_minipage ltx_align_center ltx_align_top" style="width:276.0pt;">
            
<div id="S2.SS8.SSS2.p4" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent"><span class="ltx_inline-block"><svg id="S2.SS8.SSS2.p4.pic1" class="ltx_picture" height="102.76" overflow="visible" version="1.1" viewBox="0 0 381.9 102.76" width="381.9"><g style="--ltx-stroke-color:#000000;--ltx-fill-color:#000000;" fill="#000000" stroke="#000000" stroke-width="0.4pt" transform="translate(0,102.76) matrix(1 0 0 -1 0 0)"><g style="--ltx-fill-color:#3D6666;" fill="#3D6666" fill-opacity="1.0"><path style="stroke:none" d="M 0 4.63 L 0 98.13 C 0 100.69 2.07 102.76 4.63 102.76 L 377.27 102.76 C 379.83 102.76 381.9 100.69 381.9 98.13 L 381.9 4.63 C 381.9 2.07 379.83 0 377.27 0 L 4.63 0 C 2.07 0 0 2.07 0 4.63 Z"></path></g><g style="--ltx-fill-color:#FFFFFF;" fill="#FFFFFF" fill-opacity="1.0"><path style="stroke:none" d="M 0.69 4.63 L 0.69 85.81 L 381.21 85.81 L 381.21 4.63 C 381.21 2.45 379.45 0.69 377.27 0.69 L 4.63 0.69 C 2.45 0.69 0.69 2.45 0.69 4.63 Z"></path></g><g fill-opacity="1.0" transform="matrix(1.0 0.0 0.0 1.0 20.38 90.44)"><foreignObject style="--ltx-fo-width:25.16em;--ltx-fo-height:0.56em;--ltx-fo-depth:0em;font-size:10pt;" height="7.69" overflow="visible" transform="matrix(1 0 0 -1 0 7.69)" width="348.14"><span class="ltx_foreignobject_container"><span class="ltx_foreignobject_content">
<span id="S2.SS8.SSS2.p4.pic1.1" class="ltx_inline-block ltx_minipage ltx_align_bottom" style="width:25.16em;">
<span id="S2.SS8.SSS2.p4.pic1.1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S2.SS8.SSS2.p4.pic1.1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold" style="font-size:80%;--ltx-fg-color:#FFFFFF;">Problem 0: Probabilistic construction of a set</span></span>
</span></span></span></foreignObject></g><g fill-opacity="1.0" transform="matrix(1.0 0.0 0.0 1.0 20.38 14.66)"><foreignObject style="--ltx-fo-width:29.01em;--ltx-fo-height:4.86em;--ltx-fo-depth:0.16em;font-size:10pt;" height="69.38" overflow="visible" transform="matrix(1 0 0 -1 0 67.22)" width="401.42"><span class="ltx_foreignobject_container"><span class="ltx_foreignobject_content">
<span id="S2.SS8.SSS2.p4.pic1.2" class="ltx_inline-block ltx_minipage ltx_align_bottom" style="width:29.01em;">
<span id="S2.SS8.SSS2.p4.pic1.2.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S2.SS8.SSS2.p4.pic1.2.1.1" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:80%;--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">Find a measurable subset <math id="S2.SS8.SSS2.p4.pic1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="A" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">A</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">A</annotation></semantics></math> of <math id="S2.SS8.SSS2.p4.pic1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="[0,1]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" stretchy="false">[</mo><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">0</mn><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">,</mo><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">1</mn><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">[0,1]</annotation></semantics></math> such that for any subinterval <math id="S2.SS8.SSS2.p4.pic1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="I" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">I</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">I</annotation></semantics></math> of <math id="S2.SS8.SSS2.p4.pic1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="[0,1]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" stretchy="false">[</mo><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">0</mn><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">,</mo><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">1</mn><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">[0,1]</annotation></semantics></math>, the Lebesgue measure <math id="S2.SS8.SSS2.p4.pic1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mu(A\cap I)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">μ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">A</mi><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">∩</mo><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">I</mi></mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mu(A\cap I)</annotation></semantics></math> has <math id="S2.SS8.SSS2.p4.pic1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="0&lt;\mu(A\cap I)&lt;\mu(I)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">0</mn><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">&lt;</mo><mrow><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">μ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">A</mi><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">∩</mo><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">I</mi></mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">&lt;</mo><mrow><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">μ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" stretchy="false">(</mo><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">I</mi><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">0&lt;\mu(A\cap I)&lt;\mu(I)</annotation></semantics></math>. Try to find a probabilistic construction.</span></span><span class="ltx_inline-block"><svg id="S2.SS8.SSS2.p4.pic1.pic1" class="ltx_picture" color="#008000" height="18.24" overflow="visible" style="vertical-align:-4.1px" version="1.1" viewBox="0 0 18.24 18.24" width="18.24"><g style="--ltx-stroke-color:#009900;--ltx-fill-color:#009900;--ltx-fg-color:#009900;" color="#009900" fill="#009900" stroke="#009900" stroke-width="1.8pt" transform="translate(0,18.24) matrix(1 0 0 -1 0 0) translate(1.25,0) translate(0,1.25)"><path style="fill:none" d="M 0 7.87 L 5.51 0 L 15.75 15.75"></path></g></svg></span>
<span id="S2.SS8.SSS2.p4.pic1.2.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="S2.SS8.SSS2.p4.pic1.2.2.1" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:80%;--ltx-fg-color:#008000;">GPT-5 thinking passed</span></span>
</span></span></span></foreignObject></g></g></svg></span>
</div>
          
</div></div><div class="ltx_flex_break"></div><div class="ltx_flex_cell ltx_flex_size_1">
<div id="S2.SS8.SSS2.fig1.2" class="ltx_logical-block ltx_figure_panel ltx_minipage ltx_align_center ltx_align_top" style="width:276.0pt;">
            
<div id="S2.SS8.SSS2.p5" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent"><span class="ltx_inline-block"><svg id="S2.SS8.SSS2.p5.pic1" class="ltx_picture" height="176.5" overflow="visible" version="1.1" viewBox="0 0 381.9 176.5" width="381.9"><g style="--ltx-stroke-color:#000000;--ltx-fill-color:#000000;" fill="#000000" stroke="#000000" stroke-width="0.4pt" transform="translate(0,176.5) matrix(1 0 0 -1 0 0)"><g style="--ltx-fill-color:#3D6666;" fill="#3D6666" fill-opacity="1.0"><path style="stroke:none" d="M 0 4.63 L 0 171.87 C 0 174.43 2.07 176.5 4.63 176.5 L 377.27 176.5 C 379.83 176.5 381.9 174.43 381.9 171.87 L 381.9 4.63 C 381.9 2.07 379.83 0 377.27 0 L 4.63 0 C 2.07 0 0 2.07 0 4.63 Z"></path></g><g style="--ltx-fill-color:#FFFFFF;" fill="#FFFFFF" fill-opacity="1.0"><path style="stroke:none" d="M 0.69 4.63 L 0.69 157.4 L 381.21 157.4 L 381.21 4.63 C 381.21 2.45 379.45 0.69 377.27 0.69 L 4.63 0.69 C 2.45 0.69 0.69 2.45 0.69 4.63 Z"></path></g><g fill-opacity="1.0" transform="matrix(1.0 0.0 0.0 1.0 20.38 164.18)"><foreignObject style="--ltx-fo-width:25.16em;--ltx-fo-height:0.56em;--ltx-fo-depth:0.16em;font-size:10pt;" height="9.84" overflow="visible" transform="matrix(1 0 0 -1 0 7.69)" width="348.14"><span class="ltx_foreignobject_container"><span class="ltx_foreignobject_content">
<span id="S2.SS8.SSS2.p5.pic1.1" class="ltx_inline-block ltx_minipage ltx_align_bottom" style="width:25.16em;">
<span id="S2.SS8.SSS2.p5.pic1.1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S2.SS8.SSS2.p5.pic1.1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold" style="font-size:80%;--ltx-fg-color:#FFFFFF;">Problem 0: Beside the point</span></span>
</span></span></span></foreignObject></g><g fill-opacity="1.0" transform="matrix(1.0 0.0 0.0 1.0 20.38 14.66)"><foreignObject style="--ltx-fo-width:29.01em;--ltx-fo-height:10.03em;--ltx-fo-depth:0.16em;font-size:10pt;" height="140.96" overflow="visible" transform="matrix(1 0 0 -1 0 138.81)" width="401.42"><span class="ltx_foreignobject_container"><span class="ltx_foreignobject_content">
<span id="S2.SS8.SSS2.p5.pic1.2" class="ltx_inline-block ltx_minipage ltx_align_bottom" style="width:29.01em;">
<span id="S2.SS8.SSS2.p5.pic1.2.1" class="ltx_p"><a href="https://www.janestreet.com/puzzles/beside-the-point-index/" title="" class="ltx_ref ltx_href" style="font-size:80%;--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">(Jane Stree Puzzle)</a><cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citep"><span id="S2.SS8.SSS2.p5.pic1.2.1.1" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:80%;--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">(</span><a href="#bib.bib9" title="" class="ltx_ref">Jane Street, 2024</a><span id="S2.SS8.SSS2.p5.pic1.2.1.3" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:80%;--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">)</span></cite><span id="S2.SS8.SSS2.p5.pic1.2.1.4" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:80%;--ltx-fg-color:#000000;"> Two random points, one red and one blue, are chosen uniformly and independently from the interior of a square. To ten decimal places, what is the probability that there exists a point on the side of the square closest to the blue point that is equidistant to both the blue point and the red point?</span></span><span class="ltx_inline-block"><svg id="S2.SS8.SSS2.p5.pic1.pic1" class="ltx_picture" color="#FF0000" height="18.24" overflow="visible" style="vertical-align:-4.1px" version="1.1" viewBox="0 0 18.24 18.24" width="18.24"><g style="--ltx-stroke-color:#FF0000;--ltx-fill-color:#FF0000;" fill="#FF0000" stroke="#FF0000" stroke-width="1.8pt" transform="translate(0,18.24) matrix(1 0 0 -1 0 0) translate(1.25,0) translate(0,1.25)"><path style="fill:none" d="M 0 0 L 15.75 15.75 M 0 15.75 L 15.75 0"></path></g></svg></span>
<span id="S2.SS8.SSS2.p5.pic1.2.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="S2.SS8.SSS2.p5.pic1.2.2.1" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:80%;--ltx-fg-color:#FF0000;">o4-mini-high failed<span id="S2.SS8.SSS2.p5.pic1.2.2.1.1" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;"> <span class="ltx_inline-block"><svg id="S2.SS8.SSS2.p5.pic1.pic2" class="ltx_picture" color="#008000" height="18.24" overflow="visible" style="vertical-align:-4.1px" version="1.1" viewBox="0 0 18.24 18.24" width="18.24"><g style="--ltx-stroke-color:#009900;--ltx-fill-color:#009900;--ltx-fg-color:#009900;" color="#009900" fill="#009900" stroke="#009900" stroke-width="1.8pt" transform="translate(0,18.24) matrix(1 0 0 -1 0 0) translate(1.25,0) translate(0,1.25)"><path style="fill:none" d="M 0 7.87 L 5.51 0 L 15.75 15.75"></path></g></svg></span><span id="S2.SS8.SSS2.p5.pic1.2.2.1.1.1" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-fg-color:#008000;">
GPT-5 thinking passed</span></span></span></span>
</span></span></span></foreignObject></g></g></svg></span>
</div>
          
