</section>
</section>
<section id="S2.SS9" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">9 </span>Learning New Knowledge</h3>

<div id="S2.SS9.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S2.SS9.p1.1" class="ltx_p">This category assesses how well a model can assimilate new mathematical concepts or techniques from reading or self-guided exploration.</p>
</div>
<section id="S2.SS9.SSS1" class="ltx_subsubsection">
<h4 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsubsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsubsection">(a) </span>Reading and understanding advanced materials</h4>

<div id="S2.SS9.SSS1.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S2.SS9.SSS1.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Comprehend definitions, theorems, and complex derivations in textbooks, research articles, or competition solutions.</p>
</div>
<div id="S2.SS9.SSS1.p2" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S2.SS9.SSS1.p2.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S2.SS9.SSS1.p2.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Design Principles:</span> Problems should go beyond rote recall, requiring solvers to internalize definitions, follow intricate derivations, and recognize how results interact across contexts, while emphasizing subtle assumptions or technical conditions to test genuine comprehension over surface familiarity.</p>
</div>
<div id="S2.SS9.SSS1.p3" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S2.SS9.SSS1.p3.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S2.SS9.SSS1.p3.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Sample Problems:</span></p>
</div>
<figure id="S2.SS9.SSS1.fig1" class="ltx_figure">
<div class="ltx_flex_figure">
<div class="ltx_flex_cell ltx_flex_size_1">
<div id="S2.SS9.SSS1.fig1.1" class="ltx_logical-block ltx_figure_panel ltx_minipage ltx_align_center ltx_align_top" style="width:276.0pt;">
            
<div id="S2.SS9.SSS1.p4" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent"><span class="ltx_inline-block"><svg id="S2.SS9.SSS1.p4.pic1" class="ltx_picture" height="264.96" overflow="visible" version="1.1" viewBox="0 0 381.9 264.96" width="381.9"><g style="--ltx-stroke-color:#000000;--ltx-fill-color:#000000;" fill="#000000" stroke="#000000" stroke-width="0.4pt" transform="translate(0,264.96) matrix(1 0 0 -1 0 0)"><g style="--ltx-fill-color:#3D6666;" fill="#3D6666" fill-opacity="1.0"><path style="stroke:none" d="M 0 4.63 L 0 260.33 C 0 262.89 2.07 264.96 4.63 264.96 L 377.27 264.96 C 379.83 264.96 381.9 262.89 381.9 260.33 L 381.9 4.63 C 381.9 2.07 379.83 0 377.27 0 L 4.63 0 C 2.07 0 0 2.07 0 4.63 Z"></path></g><g style="--ltx-fill-color:#FFFFFF;" fill="#FFFFFF" fill-opacity="1.0"><path style="stroke:none" d="M 0.69 4.63 L 0.69 245.86 L 381.21 245.86 L 381.21 4.63 C 381.21 2.45 379.45 0.69 377.27 0.69 L 4.63 0.69 C 2.45 0.69 0.69 2.45 0.69 4.63 Z"></path></g><g fill-opacity="1.0" transform="matrix(1.0 0.0 0.0 1.0 20.38 252.64)"><foreignObject style="--ltx-fo-width:25.16em;--ltx-fo-height:0.56em;--ltx-fo-depth:0.16em;font-size:10pt;" height="9.84" overflow="visible" transform="matrix(1 0 0 -1 0 7.69)" width="348.14"><span class="ltx_foreignobject_container"><span class="ltx_foreignobject_content">
<span id="S2.SS9.SSS1.p4.pic1.1" class="ltx_inline-block ltx_minipage ltx_align_bottom" style="width:25.16em;">
<span id="S2.SS9.SSS1.p4.pic1.1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S2.SS9.SSS1.p4.pic1.1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold" style="font-size:80%;--ltx-fg-color:#FFFFFF;">Problem 0: Loewner Energy</span></span>
</span></span></span></foreignObject></g><g fill-opacity="1.0" transform="matrix(1.0 0.0 0.0 1.0 20.38 14.66)"><foreignObject style="--ltx-fo-width:29.01em;--ltx-fo-height:16.43em;--ltx-fo-depth:0.16em;font-size:10pt;" height="229.43" overflow="visible" transform="matrix(1 0 0 -1 0 227.27)" width="401.42"><span class="ltx_foreignobject_container"><span class="ltx_foreignobject_content">
<span id="S2.SS9.SSS1.p4.pic1.2" class="ltx_inline-block ltx_minipage ltx_align_bottom" style="width:29.01em;">
<span id="S2.SS9.SSS1.p4.pic1.2.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S2.SS9.SSS1.p4.pic1.2.1.1" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:80%;--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">You are reading the paper <a href="https://arxiv.org/pdf/2006.08574" title="" class="ltx_ref ltx_href">Large deviations of multichordal <math class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathrm{SLE}_{0+}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">SLE</mi><mrow><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">0</mn><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">+</mo></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathrm{SLE}_{0+}</annotation></semantics></math>, real rational functions, and zeta-regularized determinants of Laplacians</a> <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citep">(<a href="#bib.bib11" title="" class="ltx_ref">Peltola and Wang, 2024</a>)</cite> and encounter the following concept:</span></span>
<span id="S2.SS9.SSS1.p4.pic1.2.2" class="ltx_quote">
<span id="S2.SS9.SSS1.p4.pic1.2.2.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S2.SS9.SSS1.p4.pic1.2.2.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold" style="font-size:80%;--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">Loewner potential</span></span>
</span>
<span id="S2.I13" class="ltx_enumerate">
<span id="S2.I13.i1" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">1.</span> 
<span id="S2.I13.i1.p1" class="ltx_para">
<span id="S2.I13.i1.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S2.I13.i1.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:80%;--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">Identify the concept and explain its context.</span></span>
</span></span>
<span id="S2.I13.i2" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">2.</span> 
<span id="S2.I13.i2.p1" class="ltx_para">
<span id="S2.I13.i2.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S2.I13.i2.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:80%;--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">What are the relations between Loewner energy and Loewner potential?</span></span>
</span></span>
<span id="S2.I13.i3" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">3.</span> 
<span id="S2.I13.i3.p1" class="ltx_para">
<span id="S2.I13.i3.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S2.I13.i3.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:80%;--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">How do we apply it to the deterministic limit of multiple chordal SLE systems?</span></span>
</span></span>
</span><span class="ltx_inline-block"><svg id="S2.SS9.SSS1.p4.pic1.pic1" class="ltx_picture" color="#008000" height="18.24" overflow="visible" style="vertical-align:-4.1px" version="1.1" viewBox="0 0 18.24 18.24" width="18.24"><g style="--ltx-stroke-color:#009900;--ltx-fill-color:#009900;--ltx-fg-color:#009900;" color="#009900" fill="#009900" stroke="#009900" stroke-width="1.8pt" transform="translate(0,18.24) matrix(1 0 0 -1 0 0) translate(1.25,0) translate(0,1.25)"><path style="fill:none" d="M 0 7.87 L 5.51 0 L 15.75 15.75"></path></g></svg></span>
<span id="S2.SS9.SSS1.p4.pic1.2.3" class="ltx_p"><span id="S2.SS9.SSS1.p4.pic1.2.3.1" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:80%;--ltx-fg-color:#008000;">GPT-5 thinking passed</span></span>
</span></span></span></foreignObject></g></g></svg></span>
</div>
          
</div></div><div class="ltx_flex_break"></div><div class="ltx_flex_cell ltx_flex_size_1">
