<span id="S2.SS9.SSS1.p5.pic1.1" class="ltx_inline-block ltx_minipage ltx_align_bottom" style="width:25.16em;">
<span id="S2.SS9.SSS1.p5.pic1.1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S2.SS9.SSS1.p5.pic1.1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold" style="font-size:80%;--ltx-fg-color:#FFFFFF;">Problem 0: Local multiple SLE systems</span></span>
</span></span></span></foreignObject></g><g fill-opacity="1.0" transform="matrix(1.0 0.0 0.0 1.0 20.38 14.66)"><foreignObject style="--ltx-fo-width:29.01em;--ltx-fo-height:17.6em;--ltx-fo-depth:0.16em;font-size:10pt;" height="245.67" overflow="visible" transform="matrix(1 0 0 -1 0 243.51)" width="401.42"><span class="ltx_foreignobject_container"><span class="ltx_foreignobject_content">
<span id="S2.SS9.SSS1.p5.pic1.2" class="ltx_inline-block ltx_minipage ltx_align_bottom" style="width:29.01em;">
<span id="S2.SS9.SSS1.p5.pic1.2.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S2.SS9.SSS1.p5.pic1.2.1.1" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:80%;--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">You are reading the paper <a href="https://arxiv.org/abs/2505.16093" title="" class="ltx_ref ltx_href">Multiple chordal SLE(<math class="ltx_Math" alttext="\kappa" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">κ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\kappa</annotation></semantics></math>) and quantum Calogero-Moser system</a> <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citep">(<a href="#bib.bib16" title="" class="ltx_ref">Zhang, 2025</a>)</cite> and encounter the following concept:</span></span>
<span id="S2.SS9.SSS1.p5.pic1.2.2" class="ltx_quote">
<span id="S2.SS9.SSS1.p5.pic1.2.2.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S2.SS9.SSS1.p5.pic1.2.2.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold" style="font-size:80%;--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">Local chordal multiple SLE systems</span></span>
</span>
<span id="S2.I14" class="ltx_enumerate">
<span id="S2.I14.i1" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">1.</span> 
<span id="S2.I14.i1.p1" class="ltx_para">
<span id="S2.I14.i1.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S2.I14.i1.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:80%;--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">Identify the concept and explain its context.</span></span>
</span></span>
<span id="S2.I14.i2" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">2.</span> 
<span id="S2.I14.i2.p1" class="ltx_para">
<span id="S2.I14.i2.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S2.I14.i2.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:80%;--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">Restate the assumptions formally.</span></span>
</span></span>
<span id="S2.I14.i3" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">3.</span> 
<span id="S2.I14.i3.p1" class="ltx_para">
<span id="S2.I14.i3.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S2.I14.i3.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:80%;--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">Why do we call it a local system?</span></span>
</span></span>
<span id="S2.I14.i4" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">4.</span> 
<span id="S2.I14.i4.p1" class="ltx_para">
<span id="S2.I14.i4.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S2.I14.i4.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:80%;--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">How do we define the compatible family of measures?</span></span>
</span></span>
</span><span class="ltx_inline-block"><svg id="S2.SS9.SSS1.p5.pic1.pic1" class="ltx_picture" color="#FF0000" height="18.24" overflow="visible" style="vertical-align:-4.1px" version="1.1" viewBox="0 0 18.24 18.24" width="18.24"><g style="--ltx-stroke-color:#FF0000;--ltx-fill-color:#FF0000;" fill="#FF0000" stroke="#FF0000" stroke-width="1.8pt" transform="translate(0,18.24) matrix(1 0 0 -1 0 0) translate(1.25,0) translate(0,1.25)"><path style="fill:none" d="M 0 0 L 15.75 15.75 M 0 15.75 L 15.75 0"></path></g></svg></span>
<span id="S2.SS9.SSS1.p5.pic1.2.3" class="ltx_p"><span id="S2.SS9.SSS1.p5.pic1.2.3.1" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:80%;--ltx-fg-color:#FF0000;">o4-mini-high failed<span id="S2.SS9.SSS1.p5.pic1.2.3.1.1" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;"> <span class="ltx_inline-block"><svg id="S2.SS9.SSS1.p5.pic1.pic2" class="ltx_picture" color="#008000" height="18.24" overflow="visible" style="vertical-align:-4.1px" version="1.1" viewBox="0 0 18.24 18.24" width="18.24"><g style="--ltx-stroke-color:#009900;--ltx-fill-color:#009900;--ltx-fg-color:#009900;" color="#009900" fill="#009900" stroke="#009900" stroke-width="1.8pt" transform="translate(0,18.24) matrix(1 0 0 -1 0 0) translate(1.25,0) translate(0,1.25)"><path style="fill:none" d="M 0 7.87 L 5.51 0 L 15.75 15.75"></path></g></svg></span><span id="S2.SS9.SSS1.p5.pic1.2.3.1.1.1" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-fg-color:#008000;">
GPT-5 thinking passed</span></span></span></span>
</span></span></span></foreignObject></g></g></svg></span>
