</section>
<section id="S2.SS9.SSS2" class="ltx_subsubsection">
<h4 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsubsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsubsection">(b) </span>Self-directed learning</h4>

<div id="S2.SS9.SSS2.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S2.SS9.SSS2.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Independently acquire new tools, techniques, or concepts from unfamiliar topics, and apply them to solve problems or extend known results.</p>
</div>
<div id="S2.SS9.SSS2.p2" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S2.SS9.SSS2.p2.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S2.SS9.SSS2.p2.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Design Principles:</span>
Design tasks that combine a technical question with a short excerpt from an advanced paper or textbook introducing unfamiliar definitions or methods. These tasks should test the learner’s ability to apply them to solve problems or extend known results.</p>
</div>
<div id="S2.SS9.SSS2.p3" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S2.SS9.SSS2.p3.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S2.SS9.SSS2.p3.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Sample Problems:</span></p>
</div>
<figure id="S2.SS9.SSS2.fig1" class="ltx_figure">
<div id="S2.SS9.SSS2.fig1.1" class="ltx_logical-block ltx_minipage ltx_align_center ltx_align_top" style="width:276.0pt;">
            
<div id="S2.SS9.SSS2.p4" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent"><span class="ltx_inline-block"><svg id="S2.SS9.SSS2.p4.pic1" class="ltx_picture" height="220.68" overflow="visible" version="1.1" viewBox="0 0 381.9 220.68" width="381.9"><g style="--ltx-stroke-color:#000000;--ltx-fill-color:#000000;" fill="#000000" stroke="#000000" stroke-width="0.4pt" transform="translate(0,220.68) matrix(1 0 0 -1 0 0)"><g style="--ltx-fill-color:#3D6666;" fill="#3D6666" fill-opacity="1.0"><path style="stroke:none" d="M 0 4.63 L 0 216.05 C 0 218.61 2.07 220.68 4.63 220.68 L 377.27 220.68 C 379.83 220.68 381.9 218.61 381.9 216.05 L 381.9 4.63 C 381.9 2.07 379.83 0 377.27 0 L 4.63 0 C 2.07 0 0 2.07 0 4.63 Z"></path></g><g style="--ltx-fill-color:#FFFFFF;" fill="#FFFFFF" fill-opacity="1.0"><path style="stroke:none" d="M 0.69 4.63 L 0.69 201.58 L 381.21 201.58 L 381.21 4.63 C 381.21 2.45 379.45 0.69 377.27 0.69 L 4.63 0.69 C 2.45 0.69 0.69 2.45 0.69 4.63 Z"></path></g><g fill-opacity="1.0" transform="matrix(1.0 0.0 0.0 1.0 20.38 208.37)"><foreignObject style="--ltx-fo-width:25.16em;--ltx-fo-height:0.56em;--ltx-fo-depth:0.16em;font-size:10pt;" height="9.84" overflow="visible" transform="matrix(1 0 0 -1 0 7.69)" width="348.14"><span class="ltx_foreignobject_container"><span class="ltx_foreignobject_content">
<span id="S2.SS9.SSS2.p4.pic1.1" class="ltx_inline-block ltx_minipage ltx_align_bottom" style="width:25.16em;">
<span id="S2.SS9.SSS2.p4.pic1.1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S2.SS9.SSS2.p4.pic1.1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold" style="font-size:80%;--ltx-fg-color:#FFFFFF;">Problem 0: Generalize multiple SLE systems</span></span>
</span></span></span></foreignObject></g><g fill-opacity="1.0" transform="matrix(1.0 0.0 0.0 1.0 20.38 14.66)"><foreignObject style="--ltx-fo-width:29.01em;--ltx-fo-height:13.22em;--ltx-fo-depth:0.16em;font-size:10pt;" height="185.15" overflow="visible" transform="matrix(1 0 0 -1 0 182.99)" width="401.42"><span class="ltx_foreignobject_container"><span class="ltx_foreignobject_content">
<span id="S2.SS9.SSS2.p4.pic1.2" class="ltx_inline-block ltx_minipage ltx_align_bottom" style="width:29.01em;">
<span id="S2.SS9.SSS2.p4.pic1.2.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S2.SS9.SSS2.p4.pic1.2.1.1" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:80%;--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">You are reading <a href="https://arxiv.org/abs/2505.16093" title="" class="ltx_ref ltx_href">Multiple chordal SLE(<math class="ltx_Math" alttext="\kappa" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">κ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\kappa</annotation></semantics></math>) and quantum Calogero-Moser system</a> <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citep">(<a href="#bib.bib16" title="" class="ltx_ref">Zhang, 2025</a>)</cite> and encounter the following concept:</span></span>
<span id="S2.SS9.SSS2.p4.pic1.2.2" class="ltx_quote">
<span id="S2.SS9.SSS2.p4.pic1.2.2.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S2.SS9.SSS2.p4.pic1.2.2.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold" style="font-size:80%;--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">Local chordal multiple SLE systems</span></span>
</span>
<span id="S2.I15" class="ltx_enumerate">
<span id="S2.I15.i1" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">1.</span> 
<span id="S2.I15.i1.p1" class="ltx_para">
<span id="S2.I15.i1.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S2.I15.i1.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:80%;--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">Please generalize the concept to the multiple radial case.</span></span>
</span></span>
<span id="S2.I15.i2" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">2.</span> 
<span id="S2.I15.i2.p1" class="ltx_para">
<span id="S2.I15.i2.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S2.I15.i2.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:80%;--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">Please define the compatible family of measures for multiple radial SLE systems.</span></span>
</span></span>
</span><span class="ltx_inline-block"><svg id="S2.SS9.SSS2.p4.pic1.pic1" class="ltx_picture" color="#FF0000" height="18.24" overflow="visible" style="vertical-align:-4.1px" version="1.1" viewBox="0 0 18.24 18.24" width="18.24"><g style="--ltx-stroke-color:#FF0000;--ltx-fill-color:#FF0000;" fill="#FF0000" stroke="#FF0000" stroke-width="1.8pt" transform="translate(0,18.24) matrix(1 0 0 -1 0 0) translate(1.25,0) translate(0,1.25)"><path style="fill:none" d="M 0 0 L 15.75 15.75 M 0 15.75 L 15.75 0"></path></g></svg></span>
<span id="S2.SS9.SSS2.p4.pic1.2.3" class="ltx_p"><span id="S2.SS9.SSS2.p4.pic1.2.3.1" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:80%;--ltx-fg-color:#FF0000;">GPT-5 thinking failed</span></span>
</span></span></span></foreignObject></g></g></svg></span>
</div>
          
</div>
</figure>
</section>
</section>
<section id="S2.SS10" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">10 </span>Mathematical Modeling</h3>

<div id="S2.SS10.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S2.SS10.p1.1" class="ltx_p">This category measures the ability to represent real-world or theoretical situations using appropriate mathematical structures.</p>
</div>
<section id="S2.SS10.SSS1" class="ltx_subsubsection">
<h4 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsubsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsubsection">(a) </span>Translating real-world problems into math</h4>

<div id="S2.SS10.SSS1.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S2.SS10.SSS1.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Build well-defined mathematical models that accurately capture the key features of physical, social, or economic phenomena.</p>
</div>
<div id="S2.SS10.SSS1.p2" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S2.SS10.SSS1.p2.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S2.SS10.SSS1.p2.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Design Principles:</span>
Create problems that describe complex real-world scenarios and require solvers to construct precise mathematical models.</p>
</div>
<div id="S2.SS10.SSS1.p3" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S2.SS10.SSS1.p3.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S2.SS10.SSS1.p3.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Sample Problems:</span></p>
</div>
<figure id="S2.SS10.SSS1.fig1" class="ltx_figure">
<div id="S2.SS10.SSS1.fig1.1" class="ltx_logical-block ltx_minipage ltx_align_center ltx_align_top" style="width:276.0pt;">
            
<div id="S2.SS10.SSS1.p4" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent"><span class="ltx_inline-block"><svg id="S2.SS10.SSS1.p4.pic1" class="ltx_picture" height="697.29" overflow="visible" version="1.1" viewBox="0 0 381.9 697.29" width="381.9"><g style="--ltx-stroke-color:#000000;--ltx-fill-color:#000000;" fill="#000000" stroke="#000000" stroke-width="0.4pt" transform="translate(0,697.29) matrix(1 0 0 -1 0 0)"><g style="--ltx-fill-color:#3D6666;" fill="#3D6666" fill-opacity="1.0"><path style="stroke:none" d="M 0 4.63 L 0 692.66 C 0 695.22 2.07 697.29 4.63 697.29 L 377.27 697.29 C 379.83 697.29 381.9 695.22 381.9 692.66 L 381.9 4.63 C 381.9 2.07 379.83 0 377.27 0 L 4.63 0 C 2.07 0 0 2.07 0 4.63 Z"></path></g><g style="--ltx-fill-color:#FFFFFF;" fill="#FFFFFF" fill-opacity="1.0"><path style="stroke:none" d="M 0.69 4.63 L 0.69 678.19 L 381.21 678.19 L 381.21 4.63 C 381.21 2.45 379.45 0.69 377.27 0.69 L 4.63 0.69 C 2.45 0.69 0.69 2.45 0.69 4.63 Z"></path></g><g fill-opacity="1.0" transform="matrix(1.0 0.0 0.0 1.0 20.38 684.97)"><foreignObject style="--ltx-fo-width:25.16em;--ltx-fo-height:0.56em;--ltx-fo-depth:0.16em;font-size:10pt;" height="9.84" overflow="visible" transform="matrix(1 0 0 -1 0 7.69)" width="348.14"><span class="ltx_foreignobject_container"><span class="ltx_foreignobject_content">
<span id="S2.SS10.SSS1.p4.pic1.1" class="ltx_inline-block ltx_minipage ltx_align_bottom" style="width:25.16em;">
<span id="S2.SS10.SSS1.p4.pic1.1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S2.SS10.SSS1.p4.pic1.1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold" style="font-size:80%;--ltx-fg-color:#FFFFFF;">Problem 0: Sea lampreys sex ratio</span></span>
</span></span></span></foreignObject></g><g fill-opacity="1.0" transform="matrix(1.0 0.0 0.0 1.0 20.38 155.43)"><foreignObject style="--ltx-fo-width:29.01em;--ltx-fo-height:37.5em;--ltx-fo-depth:10.33em;font-size:10pt;" height="661.76" overflow="visible" transform="matrix(1 0 0 -1 0 518.83)" width="401.42"><span class="ltx_foreignobject_container"><span class="ltx_foreignobject_content">
<span id="S2.SS10.SSS1.p4.pic1.2" class="ltx_inline-block ltx_minipage ltx_align_bottom" style="width:29.01em;">
<span id="S2.SS10.SSS1.p4.pic1.2.1" class="ltx_p"><a href="https://www.contest.comap.com/undergraduate/contests/mcm/contests/2024/problems/" title="" class="ltx_ref ltx_href" style="font-size:80%;--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">(MCM 2024 Problem A)</a><cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citep"><span id="S2.SS10.SSS1.p4.pic1.2.1.1" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:80%;--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">(</span><a href="#bib.bib3" title="" class="ltx_ref">COMAP, 2024</a><span id="S2.SS10.SSS1.p4.pic1.2.1.3" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:80%;--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">)</span></cite><span id="S2.SS10.SSS1.p4.pic1.2.1.4" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:80%;--ltx-fg-color:#000000;"> While some animal species exist outside of the usual male or female sexes, most species are substantially either male or female. Although many species exhibit a 1:1 sex ratio at birth, other species deviate from an even sex ratio. This is called adaptive sex ratio variation. For example, the temperature of the nest incubating eggs of the American alligator influences the sex ratios at birth.</span></span>
<span id="S2.SS10.SSS1.p4.pic1.2.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="S2.SS10.SSS1.p4.pic1.2.2.1" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:80%;--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">The role of lampreys is complex. In some lake habitats, they are seen as parasites with a significant impact on the ecosystem, whereas lampreys are also a food source in some regions of the world, such as Scandinavia, the Baltics, and for some Indigenous peoples of the Pacific Northwest in North America.</span></span>
<span id="S2.SS10.SSS1.p4.pic1.2.3" class="ltx_p"><span id="S2.SS10.SSS1.p4.pic1.2.3.1" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:80%;--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">The sex ratio of sea lampreys can vary based on external circumstances. Sea lampreys become male or female depending on how quickly they grow during the larval stage. These larval growth rates are influenced by the availability of food. In environments where food availability is low, growth rates will be lower, and the percentage of males can reach approximately <math id="S2.SS10.SSS1.p4.pic1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="78\%" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">78</mn><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" mathsize="1.250em">%</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">78\%</annotation></semantics></math> of the population. In environments where food is more readily available, the percentage of males has been observed to be approximately <math id="S2.SS10.SSS1.p4.pic1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="56\%" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">56</mn><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" mathsize="1.250em">%</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">56\%</annotation></semantics></math> of the population.</span></span>
<span id="S2.SS10.SSS1.p4.pic1.2.4" class="ltx_p"><span id="S2.SS10.SSS1.p4.pic1.2.4.1" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:80%;--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">We focus on the question of sex ratios and their dependence on local conditions, specifically for sea lampreys. Sea lampreys live in lake or sea habitats and migrate up rivers to spawn. The task is to examine the advantages and disadvantages of the ability for a species to alter its sex ratio depending on resource availability. Your team should develop and examine a model to provide insights into the resulting interactions in an ecosystem.</span></span>
<span id="S2.SS10.SSS1.p4.pic1.2.5" class="ltx_p"><span id="S2.SS10.SSS1.p4.pic1.2.5.1" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:80%;--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">Questions to examine include the following:</span></span>
<span id="S2.I16" class="ltx_enumerate">
<span id="S2.I16.i1" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">1.</span> 
<span id="S2.I16.i1.p1" class="ltx_para">
<span id="S2.I16.i1.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S2.I16.i1.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:80%;--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">What is the impact on the larger ecological system when the population of lampreys can alter its sex ratio?</span></span>
</span></span>
<span id="S2.I16.i2" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">2.</span> 
<span id="S2.I16.i2.p1" class="ltx_para">
<span id="S2.I16.i2.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S2.I16.i2.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:80%;--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">What are the advantages and disadvantages to the population of lampreys?</span></span>
</span></span>
<span id="S2.I16.i3" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">3.</span> 
<span id="S2.I16.i3.p1" class="ltx_para">
<span id="S2.I16.i3.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S2.I16.i3.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:80%;--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">What is the impact on the stability of the ecosystem given the changes in the sex ratios of lampreys?</span></span>
</span>
<span id="S2.I16.i3.p2" class="ltx_para"><span class="ltx_inline-block"><svg id="S2.I16.i3.p2.pic1" class="ltx_picture" color="#FF0000" height="18.24" overflow="visible" style="vertical-align:-4.1px" version="1.1" viewBox="0 0 18.24 18.24" width="18.24"><g style="--ltx-stroke-color:#FF0000;--ltx-fill-color:#FF0000;" fill="#FF0000" stroke="#FF0000" stroke-width="1.8pt" transform="translate(0,18.24) matrix(1 0 0 -1 0 0) translate(1.25,0) translate(0,1.25)"><path style="fill:none" d="M 0 0 L 15.75 15.75 M 0 15.75 L 15.75 0"></path></g></svg></span>
<span id="S2.I16.i3.p2.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S2.I16.i3.p2.1.1" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:80%;--ltx-fg-color:#FF0000;">GPT-5 thinking failed</span></span>
</span></span>
</span>
</span></span></span></foreignObject></g></g></svg></span>
</div>
          
</div>
</figure>
</section>
</section>
<section id="S2.SS11" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">11 </span>Generalization</h3>

<div id="S2.SS11.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S2.SS11.p1.1" class="ltx_p">This category concerns recognizing and extending patterns from specific cases to broader mathematical truths.</p>
</div>
<section id="S2.SS11.SSS1" class="ltx_subsubsection">
<h4 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsubsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsubsection">(a) </span>Identifying patterns from examples</h4>

<div id="S2.SS11.SSS1.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S2.SS11.SSS1.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Detect recurring structures or behaviors in small-scale problems and use them to predict or conjecture more general results.</p>
</div>
<div id="S2.SS11.SSS1.p2" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S2.SS11.SSS1.p2.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S2.SS11.SSS1.p2.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Design Principles:</span>
Present a sequence of concrete examples or small cases that exhibit an underlying mathematical pattern.</p>
</div>
<div id="S2.SS11.SSS1.p3" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S2.SS11.SSS1.p3.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S2.SS11.SSS1.p3.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Sample Problems:</span></p>
</div>
<figure id="S2.SS11.SSS1.fig1" class="ltx_figure">
<div id="S2.SS11.SSS1.fig1.1" class="ltx_logical-block ltx_minipage ltx_align_center ltx_align_top" style="width:276.0pt;">
            
<div id="S2.SS11.SSS1.p4" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent"><span class="ltx_inline-block"><svg id="S2.SS11.SSS1.p4.pic1" class="ltx_picture" height="203.92" overflow="visible" version="1.1" viewBox="0 0 381.9 203.92" width="381.9"><g style="--ltx-stroke-color:#000000;--ltx-fill-color:#000000;" fill="#000000" stroke="#000000" stroke-width="0.4pt" transform="translate(0,203.92) matrix(1 0 0 -1 0 0)"><g style="--ltx-fill-color:#3D6666;" fill="#3D6666" fill-opacity="1.0"><path style="stroke:none" d="M 0 4.63 L 0 199.29 C 0 201.85 2.07 203.92 4.63 203.92 L 377.27 203.92 C 379.83 203.92 381.9 201.85 381.9 199.29 L 381.9 4.63 C 381.9 2.07 379.83 0 377.27 0 L 4.63 0 C 2.07 0 0 2.07 0 4.63 Z"></path></g><g style="--ltx-fill-color:#FFFFFF;" fill="#FFFFFF" fill-opacity="1.0"><path style="stroke:none" d="M 0.69 4.63 L 0.69 184.83 L 381.21 184.83 L 381.21 4.63 C 381.21 2.45 379.45 0.69 377.27 0.69 L 4.63 0.69 C 2.45 0.69 0.69 2.45 0.69 4.63 Z"></path></g><g fill-opacity="1.0" transform="matrix(1.0 0.0 0.0 1.0 20.38 191.61)"><foreignObject style="--ltx-fo-width:25.16em;--ltx-fo-height:0.56em;--ltx-fo-depth:0.16em;font-size:10pt;" height="9.84" overflow="visible" transform="matrix(1 0 0 -1 0 7.69)" width="348.14"><span class="ltx_foreignobject_container"><span class="ltx_foreignobject_content">
<span id="S2.SS11.SSS1.p4.pic1.1" class="ltx_inline-block ltx_minipage ltx_align_bottom" style="width:25.16em;">
<span id="S2.SS11.SSS1.p4.pic1.1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S2.SS11.SSS1.p4.pic1.1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold" style="font-size:80%;--ltx-fg-color:#FFFFFF;">Problem 0: k-set containing three sums</span></span>
</span></span></span></foreignObject></g><g fill-opacity="1.0" transform="matrix(1.0 0.0 0.0 1.0 20.38 14.66)"><foreignObject style="--ltx-fo-width:29.01em;--ltx-fo-height:12.01em;--ltx-fo-depth:0.16em;font-size:10pt;" height="168.39" overflow="visible" transform="matrix(1 0 0 -1 0 166.24)" width="401.42"><span class="ltx_foreignobject_container"><span class="ltx_foreignobject_content">
<span id="S2.SS11.SSS1.p4.pic1.2" class="ltx_inline-block ltx_minipage ltx_align_bottom" style="width:29.01em;">
<span id="S2.SS11.SSS1.p4.pic1.2.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S2.SS11.SSS1.p4.pic1.2.1.1" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:80%;--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">Find the smallest positive integer <math id="S2.SS11.SSS1.p4.pic1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="k" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">k</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">k</annotation></semantics></math> such that for every <math id="S2.SS11.SSS1.p4.pic1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="k" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">k</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">k</annotation></semantics></math>-element subset <math id="S2.SS11.SSS1.p4.pic1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="A" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">A</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">A</annotation></semantics></math> of the set</span></span>
<span id="S2.Ex11" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<span><span class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<span class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></span>
<span class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S2.Ex11.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="S=\{1,2,\dots,2012\}," display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" mathsize="0.800em">S</mi><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" mathsize="0.800em">=</mo><mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" stretchy="false">{</mo><mrow><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" mathsize="0.800em">1</mn><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" mathsize="0.800em">,</mo><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" mathsize="0.800em">2</mn><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" mathsize="0.800em">,</mo><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" mathsize="0.800em" mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" mathsize="0.800em">,</mo><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" mathsize="0.800em">2012</mn></mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow></mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" mathsize="0.800em">,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">S=\{1,2,\dots,2012\},</annotation></semantics></math></span>
<span class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></span></span></span>
</span>
<span id="S2.SS11.SSS1.p4.pic1.2.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="S2.SS11.SSS1.p4.pic1.2.2.1" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:80%;--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">there exist three <span id="S2.SS11.SSS1.p4.pic1.2.2.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">distinct</span> elements <math id="S2.SS11.SSS1.p4.pic1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="a,b,c\in S" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">a</mi><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">,</mo><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">b</mi><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">,</mo><mrow><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">c</mi><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">∈</mo><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">S</mi></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">a,b,c\in S</annotation></semantics></math> such that all three sums</span></span>
<span id="S2.Ex12" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<span><span class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<span class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></span>
<span class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S2.Ex12.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="a+b,\hskip 8.50012ptb+c,\hskip 8.50012ptc+a" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" mathsize="0.800em">a</mi><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" mathsize="0.800em">+</mo><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" mathsize="0.800em">b</mi></mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" mathsize="0.800em" rspace="1.017em">,</mo><mrow><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" mathsize="0.800em">b</mi><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" mathsize="0.800em">+</mo><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" mathsize="0.800em">c</mi></mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" mathsize="0.800em" rspace="1.017em">,</mo><mrow><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" mathsize="0.800em">c</mi><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" mathsize="0.800em">+</mo><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" mathsize="0.800em">a</mi></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">a+b,\hskip 8.50012ptb+c,\hskip 8.50012ptc+a</annotation></semantics></math></span>
<span class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></span></span></span>
</span>
<span id="S2.SS11.SSS1.p4.pic1.2.3" class="ltx_p"><span id="S2.SS11.SSS1.p4.pic1.2.3.1" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:80%;--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">are contained in <math id="S2.SS11.SSS1.p4.pic1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="A" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">A</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">A</annotation></semantics></math>. Try small cases to find a pattern then prove your conjecture.</span></span><span class="ltx_inline-block"><svg id="S2.SS11.SSS1.p4.pic1.pic1" class="ltx_picture" color="#FF0000" height="18.24" overflow="visible" style="vertical-align:-4.1px" version="1.1" viewBox="0 0 18.24 18.24" width="18.24"><g style="--ltx-stroke-color:#FF0000;--ltx-fill-color:#FF0000;" fill="#FF0000" stroke="#FF0000" stroke-width="1.8pt" transform="translate(0,18.24) matrix(1 0 0 -1 0 0) translate(1.25,0) translate(0,1.25)"><path style="fill:none" d="M 0 0 L 15.75 15.75 M 0 15.75 L 15.75 0"></path></g></svg></span>
<span id="S2.SS11.SSS1.p4.pic1.2.4" class="ltx_p"><span id="S2.SS11.SSS1.p4.pic1.2.4.1" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:80%;--ltx-fg-color:#FF0000;">GPT-5 thinking failed</span></span>
</span></span></span></foreignObject></g></g></svg></span>
</div>
          
</div>
</figure>
</section>
<section id="S2.SS11.SSS2" class="ltx_subsubsection">
<h4 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsubsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsubsection">(b) </span>Developing unifying theories</h4>

<div id="S2.SS11.SSS2.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S2.SS11.SSS2.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Create general frameworks that consolidate seemingly unrelated theorems or observations into a coherent structure.</p>
</div>
<div id="S2.SS11.SSS2.p2" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S2.SS11.SSS2.p2.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S2.SS11.SSS2.p2.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Design Principles:</span>
Design problems that involve multiple related results. Challenge solvers to discover the shared principles or structural similarities behind them, and to formulate a unifying framework—such as a general theorem—that explains all cases and suggests further extensions.</p>
</div>
<div id="S2.SS11.SSS2.p3" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S2.SS11.SSS2.p3.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S2.SS11.SSS2.p3.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Sample Problems:</span></p>
</div>
<figure id="S2.SS11.SSS2.fig1" class="ltx_figure">
<div class="ltx_flex_figure">
<div class="ltx_flex_cell ltx_flex_size_1">
<div id="S2.SS11.SSS2.fig1.1" class="ltx_logical-block ltx_figure_panel ltx_minipage ltx_align_center ltx_align_top" style="width:276.0pt;">
            
<div id="S2.SS11.SSS2.p4" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent"><span class="ltx_inline-block"><svg id="S2.SS11.SSS2.p4.pic1" class="ltx_picture" height="423.62" overflow="visible" version="1.1" viewBox="0 0 381.9 423.62" width="381.9"><g style="--ltx-stroke-color:#000000;--ltx-fill-color:#000000;" fill="#000000" stroke="#000000" stroke-width="0.4pt" transform="translate(0,423.62) matrix(1 0 0 -1 0 0)"><g style="--ltx-fill-color:#3D6666;" fill="#3D6666" fill-opacity="1.0"><path style="stroke:none" d="M 0 4.63 L 0 419 C 0 421.55 2.07 423.62 4.63 423.62 L 377.27 423.62 C 379.83 423.62 381.9 421.55 381.9 419 L 381.9 4.63 C 381.9 2.07 379.83 0 377.27 0 L 4.63 0 C 2.07 0 0 2.07 0 4.63 Z"></path></g><g style="--ltx-fill-color:#FFFFFF;" fill="#FFFFFF" fill-opacity="1.0"><path style="stroke:none" d="M 0.69 4.63 L 0.69 406.68 L 381.21 406.68 L 381.21 4.63 C 381.21 2.45 379.45 0.69 377.27 0.69 L 4.63 0.69 C 2.45 0.69 0.69 2.45 0.69 4.63 Z"></path></g><g fill-opacity="1.0" transform="matrix(1.0 0.0 0.0 1.0 20.38 411.31)"><foreignObject style="--ltx-fo-width:25.16em;--ltx-fo-height:0.56em;--ltx-fo-depth:0em;font-size:10pt;" height="7.69" overflow="visible" transform="matrix(1 0 0 -1 0 7.69)" width="348.14"><span class="ltx_foreignobject_container"><span class="ltx_foreignobject_content">
<span id="S2.SS11.SSS2.p4.pic1.1" class="ltx_inline-block ltx_minipage ltx_align_bottom" style="width:25.16em;">
<span id="S2.SS11.SSS2.p4.pic1.1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S2.SS11.SSS2.p4.pic1.1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold" style="font-size:80%;--ltx-fg-color:#FFFFFF;">Problem 0: Generalize Dehn twists</span></span>
</span></span></span></foreignObject></g><g fill-opacity="1.0" transform="matrix(1.0 0.0 0.0 1.0 20.38 14.66)"><foreignObject style="--ltx-fo-width:29.01em;--ltx-fo-height:28.05em;--ltx-fo-depth:0.16em;font-size:10pt;" height="390.24" overflow="visible" transform="matrix(1 0 0 -1 0 388.09)" width="401.42"><span class="ltx_foreignobject_container"><span class="ltx_foreignobject_content">
<span id="S2.SS11.SSS2.p4.pic1.2" class="ltx_inline-block ltx_minipage ltx_align_bottom" style="width:29.01em;">
<span id="S2.SS11.SSS2.p4.pic1.2.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S2.SS11.SSS2.p4.pic1.2.1.1" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:80%;--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">Consider the following three “twist” operations:</span></span>
<span id="S2.I17" class="ltx_enumerate">
<span id="S2.I17.ix1" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">(1)</span> 
<span id="S2.I17.ix1.p1" class="ltx_para">
<span id="S2.I17.ix1.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S2.I17.ix1.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:80%;--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">If </span><math id="S2.I17.ix1.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Sigma" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" mathsize="0.800em" mathvariant="normal">Σ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Sigma</annotation></semantics></math><span id="S2.I17.ix1.p1.1.2" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:80%;--ltx-fg-color:#000000;"> is an oriented surface and </span><math id="S2.I17.ix1.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\gamma\subset\Sigma" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" mathsize="0.800em">γ</mi><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" mathsize="0.800em">⊂</mo><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" mathsize="0.800em" mathvariant="normal">Σ</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\gamma\subset\Sigma</annotation></semantics></math><span id="S2.I17.ix1.p1.1.3" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:80%;--ltx-fg-color:#000000;"> is an embedded curve, one can perform a Dehn twist along </span><math id="S2.I17.ix1.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\gamma" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" mathsize="0.800em">γ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\gamma</annotation></semantics></math><span id="S2.I17.ix1.p1.1.4" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:80%;--ltx-fg-color:#000000;"> to create a mapping class of </span><math id="S2.I17.ix1.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Sigma" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" mathsize="0.800em" mathvariant="normal">Σ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Sigma</annotation></semantics></math><span id="S2.I17.ix1.p1.1.5" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:80%;--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">.</span></span>
</span></span>
<span id="S2.I17.ix2" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">(2)</span> 
<span id="S2.I17.ix2.p1" class="ltx_para">
<span id="S2.I17.ix2.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S2.I17.ix2.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:80%;--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">If </span><math id="S2.I17.ix2.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="M" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" mathsize="0.800em">M</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">M</annotation></semantics></math><span id="S2.I17.ix2.p1.1.2" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:80%;--ltx-fg-color:#000000;"> is an oriented </span><math id="S2.I17.ix2.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="3" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" mathsize="0.800em">3</mn><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">3</annotation></semantics></math><span id="S2.I17.ix2.p1.1.3" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:80%;--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">-manifold and </span><math id="S2.I17.ix2.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="T\subset M" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" mathsize="0.800em">T</mi><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" mathsize="0.800em">⊂</mo><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" mathsize="0.800em">M</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">T\subset M</annotation></semantics></math><span id="S2.I17.ix2.p1.1.4" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:80%;--ltx-fg-color:#000000;"> is an embedded torus, </span><math id="S2.I17.ix2.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\gamma\subset T" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" mathsize="0.800em">γ</mi><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" mathsize="0.800em">⊂</mo><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" mathsize="0.800em">T</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\gamma\subset T</annotation></semantics></math><span id="S2.I17.ix2.p1.1.5" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:80%;--ltx-fg-color:#000000;"> is an essential simple closed curve, one can perform a Dehn twist along </span><math id="S2.I17.ix2.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="T" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" mathsize="0.800em">T</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">T</annotation></semantics></math><span id="S2.I17.ix2.p1.1.6" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:80%;--ltx-fg-color:#000000;"> in the </span><math id="S2.I17.ix2.p1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\gamma" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" mathsize="0.800em">γ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\gamma</annotation></semantics></math><span id="S2.I17.ix2.p1.1.7" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:80%;--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">-direction to create a mapping class of </span><math id="S2.I17.ix2.p1.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="M" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" mathsize="0.800em">M</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">M</annotation></semantics></math><span id="S2.I17.ix2.p1.1.8" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:80%;--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">.</span></span>
</span></span>
<span id="S2.I17.ix3" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">(3)</span> 
<span id="S2.I17.ix3.p1" class="ltx_para">
<span id="S2.I17.ix3.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S2.I17.ix3.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:80%;--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">If </span><math id="S2.I17.ix3.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="X" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" mathsize="0.800em">X</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">X</annotation></semantics></math><span id="S2.I17.ix3.p1.1.2" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:80%;--ltx-fg-color:#000000;"> is a smooth oriented </span><math id="S2.I17.ix3.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="4" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" mathsize="0.800em">4</mn><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">4</annotation></semantics></math><span id="S2.I17.ix3.p1.1.3" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:80%;--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">-manifold and </span><math id="S2.I17.ix3.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="S\subset X" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" mathsize="0.800em">S</mi><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" mathsize="0.800em">⊂</mo><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" mathsize="0.800em">X</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">S\subset X</annotation></semantics></math><span id="S2.I17.ix3.p1.1.4" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:80%;--ltx-fg-color:#000000;"> is smoothly embedded </span><math id="S2.I17.ix3.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="2" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" mathsize="0.800em">2</mn><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">2</annotation></semantics></math><span id="S2.I17.ix3.p1.1.5" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:80%;--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">-sphere with self-intersection number </span><math id="S2.I17.ix3.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="-2" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" mathsize="0.800em">−</mo><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" mathsize="0.800em">2</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">-2</annotation></semantics></math><span id="S2.I17.ix3.p1.1.6" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:80%;--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">, one can construct a mapping class of </span><math id="S2.I17.ix3.p1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="X" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" mathsize="0.800em">X</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">X</annotation></semantics></math><span id="S2.I17.ix3.p1.1.7" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:80%;--ltx-fg-color:#000000;"> obtained by the identity outside a tubular neighborhood </span><math id="S2.I17.ix3.p1.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\nu S" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" mathsize="0.800em">ν</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" mathsize="0.800em">S</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\nu S</annotation></semantics></math><span id="S2.I17.ix3.p1.1.8" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:80%;--ltx-fg-color:#000000;"> of </span><math id="S2.I17.ix3.p1.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="S" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" mathsize="0.800em">S</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">S</annotation></semantics></math><span id="S2.I17.ix3.p1.1.9" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:80%;--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">, and the time </span><math id="S2.I17.ix3.p1.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\pi" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" mathsize="0.800em">π</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\pi</annotation></semantics></math><span id="S2.I17.ix3.p1.1.10" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:80%;--ltx-fg-color:#000000;"> map of the geodesic flow on </span><math id="S2.I17.ix3.p1.m10" class="ltx_Math" alttext="DTS^{2}\cong\nu S" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" mathsize="0.800em">D</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" mathsize="0.800em">T</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" mathsize="0.800em">S</mi><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" mathsize="0.800em">2</mn></msup></mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" mathsize="0.800em">≅</mo><mrow><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" mathsize="0.800em">ν</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" mathsize="0.800em">S</mi></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">DTS^{2}\cong\nu S</annotation></semantics></math><span id="S2.I17.ix3.p1.1.11" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:80%;--ltx-fg-color:#000000;"> inside </span><math id="S2.I17.ix3.p1.m11" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\nu S" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" mathsize="0.800em">ν</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" mathsize="0.800em">S</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\nu S</annotation></semantics></math><span id="S2.I17.ix3.p1.1.12" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:80%;--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">, where </span><math id="S2.I17.ix3.p1.m12" class="ltx_Math" alttext="DTS^{2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" mathsize="0.800em">D</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" mathsize="0.800em">T</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" mathsize="0.800em">S</mi><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" mathsize="0.800em">2</mn></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">DTS^{2}</annotation></semantics></math><span id="S2.I17.ix3.p1.1.13" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:80%;--ltx-fg-color:#000000;"> denotes the unit disk bundle of the tangent bundle of the unit sphere </span><math id="S2.I17.ix3.p1.m13" class="ltx_Math" alttext="S^{2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" mathsize="0.800em">S</mi><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" mathsize="0.800em">2</mn></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">S^{2}</annotation></semantics></math><span id="S2.I17.ix3.p1.1.14" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:80%;--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">.</span></span>
</span></span>
</span>
<span id="S2.SS11.SSS2.p4.pic1.2.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="S2.SS11.SSS2.p4.pic1.2.2.1" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:80%;--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">What is essentially going on that allows one to perform such twist operations? Please:</span></span>
<span id="S2.I18" class="ltx_enumerate">
<span id="S2.I18.ix1" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">i.</span> 
<span id="S2.I18.ix1.p1" class="ltx_para">
<span id="S2.I18.ix1.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S2.I18.ix1.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:80%;--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">Formulate a generalization of the twist operation that encompasses all three operations above as special cases.</span></span>
</span></span>
<span id="S2.I18.ix2" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">ii.</span> 
<span id="S2.I18.ix2.p1" class="ltx_para">
<span id="S2.I18.ix2.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S2.I18.ix2.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:80%;--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">Formulate a generalization of the first two twist operations that is not a generalization of the third operation.</span></span>
</span></span>
</span><span class="ltx_inline-block"><svg id="S2.SS11.SSS2.p4.pic1.pic1" class="ltx_picture" color="#FF0000" height="18.24" overflow="visible" style="vertical-align:-4.1px" version="1.1" viewBox="0 0 18.24 18.24" width="18.24"><g style="--ltx-stroke-color:#FF0000;--ltx-fill-color:#FF0000;" fill="#FF0000" stroke="#FF0000" stroke-width="1.8pt" transform="translate(0,18.24) matrix(1 0 0 -1 0 0) translate(1.25,0) translate(0,1.25)"><path style="fill:none" d="M 0 0 L 15.75 15.75 M 0 15.75 L 15.75 0"></path></g></svg></span>
<span id="S2.SS11.SSS2.p4.pic1.2.3" class="ltx_p"><span id="S2.SS11.SSS2.p4.pic1.2.3.1" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:80%;--ltx-fg-color:#FF0000;">GPT-5 thinking failed</span></span>
</span></span></span></foreignObject></g></g></svg></span>
</div>
          
</div></div><div class="ltx_flex_break"></div><div class="ltx_flex_cell ltx_flex_size_1">
<div id="S2.SS11.SSS2.fig1.2" class="ltx_logical-block ltx_figure_panel ltx_minipage ltx_align_center ltx_align_top" style="width:276.0pt;">
            
<div id="S2.SS11.SSS2.p5" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent"><span class="ltx_inline-block"><svg id="S2.SS11.SSS2.p5.pic1" class="ltx_picture" height="168.56" overflow="visible" version="1.1" viewBox="0 0 381.9 168.56" width="381.9"><g style="--ltx-stroke-color:#000000;--ltx-fill-color:#000000;" fill="#000000" stroke="#000000" stroke-width="0.4pt" transform="translate(0,168.56) matrix(1 0 0 -1 0 0)"><g style="--ltx-fill-color:#3D6666;" fill="#3D6666" fill-opacity="1.0"><path style="stroke:none" d="M 0 4.63 L 0 163.93 C 0 166.49 2.07 168.56 4.63 168.56 L 377.27 168.56 C 379.83 168.56 381.9 166.49 381.9 163.93 L 381.9 4.63 C 381.9 2.07 379.83 0 377.27 0 L 4.63 0 C 2.07 0 0 2.07 0 4.63 Z"></path></g><g style="--ltx-fill-color:#FFFFFF;" fill="#FFFFFF" fill-opacity="1.0"><path style="stroke:none" d="M 0.69 4.63 L 0.69 151.62 L 381.21 151.62 L 381.21 4.63 C 381.21 2.45 379.45 0.69 377.27 0.69 L 4.63 0.69 C 2.45 0.69 0.69 2.45 0.69 4.63 Z"></path></g><g fill-opacity="1.0" transform="matrix(1.0 0.0 0.0 1.0 20.38 156.25)"><foreignObject style="--ltx-fo-width:25.16em;--ltx-fo-height:0.56em;--ltx-fo-depth:0em;font-size:10pt;" height="7.69" overflow="visible" transform="matrix(1 0 0 -1 0 7.69)" width="348.14"><span class="ltx_foreignobject_container"><span class="ltx_foreignobject_content">
<span id="S2.SS11.SSS2.p5.pic1.1" class="ltx_inline-block ltx_minipage ltx_align_bottom" style="width:25.16em;">
<span id="S2.SS11.SSS2.p5.pic1.1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S2.SS11.SSS2.p5.pic1.1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold" style="font-size:80%;--ltx-fg-color:#FFFFFF;">Problem 0: Clock strikes</span></span>
</span></span></span></foreignObject></g><g fill-opacity="1.0" transform="matrix(1.0 0.0 0.0 1.0 20.38 14.66)"><foreignObject style="--ltx-fo-width:29.01em;--ltx-fo-height:9.61em;--ltx-fo-depth:0.16em;font-size:10pt;" height="135.18" overflow="visible" transform="matrix(1 0 0 -1 0 133.03)" width="401.42"><span class="ltx_foreignobject_container"><span class="ltx_foreignobject_content">
<span id="S2.SS11.SSS2.p5.pic1.2" class="ltx_inline-block ltx_minipage ltx_align_bottom" style="width:29.01em;">
<span id="S2.SS11.SSS2.p5.pic1.2.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S2.SS11.SSS2.p5.pic1.2.1.1" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:80%;--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">A clock is built based on the following repeating sequence
1,2,3,4,3,2,1,2,3,4,3,2,…
At the first hour it strikes 1 time. At the second hour it strikes 2 times. At the third hour it strikes 3 times. At the fourth hour it strikes 4 times. At the fifth hour it strikes 3+2 times. At the sixth hour it strikes 1+2+3 times. Etc.
Explain what is going on, develop the theory that explains why it works, and then suggest some generalizations.</span></span><span class="ltx_inline-block"><svg id="S2.SS11.SSS2.p5.pic1.pic1" class="ltx_picture" color="#FF0000" height="18.24" overflow="visible" style="vertical-align:-4.1px" version="1.1" viewBox="0 0 18.24 18.24" width="18.24"><g style="--ltx-stroke-color:#FF0000;--ltx-fill-color:#FF0000;" fill="#FF0000" stroke="#FF0000" stroke-width="1.8pt" transform="translate(0,18.24) matrix(1 0 0 -1 0 0) translate(1.25,0) translate(0,1.25)"><path style="fill:none" d="M 0 0 L 15.75 15.75 M 0 15.75 L 15.75 0"></path></g></svg></span>
<span id="S2.SS11.SSS2.p5.pic1.2.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="S2.SS11.SSS2.p5.pic1.2.2.1" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:80%;--ltx-fg-color:#FF0000;">GPT-5 thinking failed</span></span>
</span></span></span></foreignObject></g></g></svg></span>
</div>
          
</div></div></div>
</figure>
<figure id="S2.SS11.SSS2.fig2" class="ltx_figure">
<div id="S2.SS11.SSS2.fig2.1" class="ltx_logical-block ltx_minipage ltx_align_center ltx_align_top" style="width:276.0pt;">
            
<div id="S2.SS11.SSS2.p6" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent"><span class="ltx_inline-block"><svg id="S2.SS11.SSS2.p6.pic1" class="ltx_picture" height="254.51" overflow="visible" version="1.1" viewBox="0 0 381.9 254.51" width="381.9"><g style="--ltx-stroke-color:#000000;--ltx-fill-color:#000000;" fill="#000000" stroke="#000000" stroke-width="0.4pt" transform="translate(0,254.51) matrix(1 0 0 -1 0 0)"><g style="--ltx-fill-color:#3D6666;" fill="#3D6666" fill-opacity="1.0"><path style="stroke:none" d="M 0 4.63 L 0 249.88 C 0 252.43 2.07 254.51 4.63 254.51 L 377.27 254.51 C 379.83 254.51 381.9 252.43 381.9 249.88 L 381.9 4.63 C 381.9 2.07 379.83 0 377.27 0 L 4.63 0 C 2.07 0 0 2.07 0 4.63 Z"></path></g><g style="--ltx-fill-color:#FFFFFF;" fill="#FFFFFF" fill-opacity="1.0"><path style="stroke:none" d="M 0.69 4.63 L 0.69 235.41 L 381.21 235.41 L 381.21 4.63 C 381.21 2.45 379.45 0.69 377.27 0.69 L 4.63 0.69 C 2.45 0.69 0.69 2.45 0.69 4.63 Z"></path></g><g fill-opacity="1.0" transform="matrix(1.0 0.0 0.0 1.0 20.38 242.19)"><foreignObject style="--ltx-fo-width:25.16em;--ltx-fo-height:0.56em;--ltx-fo-depth:0.16em;font-size:10pt;" height="9.84" overflow="visible" transform="matrix(1 0 0 -1 0 7.69)" width="348.14"><span class="ltx_foreignobject_container"><span class="ltx_foreignobject_content">
<span id="S2.SS11.SSS2.p6.pic1.1" class="ltx_inline-block ltx_minipage ltx_align_bottom" style="width:25.16em;">
<span id="S2.SS11.SSS2.p6.pic1.1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S2.SS11.SSS2.p6.pic1.1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold" style="font-size:80%;--ltx-fg-color:#FFFFFF;">Problem 0: Group scheme and classifying space</span></span>
</span></span></span></foreignObject></g><g fill-opacity="1.0" transform="matrix(1.0 0.0 0.0 1.0 20.38 14.66)"><foreignObject style="--ltx-fo-width:29.01em;--ltx-fo-height:15.67em;--ltx-fo-depth:0.16em;font-size:10pt;" height="218.97" overflow="visible" transform="matrix(1 0 0 -1 0 216.82)" width="401.42"><span class="ltx_foreignobject_container"><span class="ltx_foreignobject_content">
<span id="S2.SS11.SSS2.p6.pic1.2" class="ltx_inline-block ltx_minipage ltx_align_bottom" style="width:29.01em;">
<span id="S2.SS11.SSS2.p6.pic1.2.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S2.SS11.SSS2.p6.pic1.2.1.1" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:80%;--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">Explain the connection between the following two observations. Then propose a unifying theory that predicts decompositions for an arbitrary group.</span></span>
<span id="S2.I19" class="ltx_enumerate">
<span id="S2.I19.i1" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">1.</span> 
<span id="S2.I19.i1.p1" class="ltx_para">
<span id="S2.I19.i1.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S2.I19.i1.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:80%;--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">Let </span><math id="S2.I19.i1.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbb{G}_{m}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" mathsize="0.800em">𝔾</mi><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" mathsize="0.800em">m</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbb{G}_{m}</annotation></semantics></math><span id="S2.I19.i1.p1.1.2" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:80%;--ltx-fg-color:#000000;"> be the multiplicative group scheme. It has exactly </span><math id="S2.I19.i1.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="q-1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" mathsize="0.800em">q</mi><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" mathsize="0.800em">−</mo><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" mathsize="0.800em">1</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">q-1</annotation></semantics></math><span id="S2.I19.i1.p1.1.3" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:80%;--ltx-fg-color:#000000;"> </span><math id="S2.I19.i1.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbb{F}_{q}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" mathsize="0.800em">𝔽</mi><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" mathsize="0.800em">q</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbb{F}_{q}</annotation></semantics></math><span id="S2.I19.i1.p1.1.4" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:80%;--ltx-fg-color:#000000;"> points.</span></span>
</span></span>
<span id="S2.I19.i2" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">2.</span> 
<span id="S2.I19.i2.p1" class="ltx_para">
<span id="S2.I19.i2.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S2.I19.i2.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:80%;--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">Let </span><math id="S2.I19.i2.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="B\mathbb{G}_{m}=\mathrm{pt}/\mathbb{G}_{m}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" mathsize="0.800em">B</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" mathsize="0.800em">𝔾</mi><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" mathsize="0.800em">m</mi></msub></mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" mathsize="0.800em">=</mo><mrow><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" mathsize="0.800em">pt</mi><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" maxsize="0.800em" minsize="0.800em" stretchy="true" symmetric="true">/</mo><msub><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" mathsize="0.800em">𝔾</mi><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" mathsize="0.800em">m</mi></msub></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">B\mathbb{G}_{m}=\mathrm{pt}/\mathbb{G}_{m}</annotation></semantics></math><span id="S2.I19.i2.p1.1.2" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:80%;--ltx-fg-color:#000000;"> be the classifying stack of </span><math id="S2.I19.i2.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbb{G}_{m}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" mathsize="0.800em">𝔾</mi><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" mathsize="0.800em">m</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbb{G}_{m}</annotation></semantics></math><span id="S2.I19.i2.p1.1.3" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:80%;--ltx-fg-color:#000000;"> bundles. Over the complex numbers it is represented by the homotopy type </span><math id="S2.I19.i2.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbb{CP}^{\infty}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" mathsize="0.800em">ℂ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" mathsize="0.800em">ℙ</mi><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" mathsize="0.800em" mathvariant="normal">∞</mi></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbb{CP}^{\infty}</annotation></semantics></math><span id="S2.I19.i2.p1.1.4" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:80%;--ltx-fg-color:#000000;"> which admits a decomposition </span><math id="S2.I19.i2.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbb{C}^{0}+\mathbb{C}^{1}+\mathbb{C}^{2}+\dots" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msup><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" mathsize="0.800em">ℂ</mi><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" mathsize="0.800em">0</mn></msup><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" mathsize="0.800em">+</mo><msup><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" mathsize="0.800em">ℂ</mi><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" mathsize="0.800em">1</mn></msup><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" mathsize="0.800em">+</mo><msup><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" mathsize="0.800em">ℂ</mi><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" mathsize="0.800em">2</mn></msup><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" mathsize="0.800em">+</mo><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" mathsize="0.800em" mathvariant="normal">…</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbb{C}^{0}+\mathbb{C}^{1}+\mathbb{C}^{2}+\dots</annotation></semantics></math><span id="S2.I19.i2.p1.1.5" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:80%;--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">. If we instead “counted </span><math id="S2.I19.i2.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbb{F}_{q}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" mathsize="0.800em">𝔽</mi><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" mathsize="0.800em">q</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbb{F}_{q}</annotation></semantics></math><span id="S2.I19.i2.p1.1.6" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:80%;--ltx-fg-color:#000000;"> points", we would get the non-convergent series </span><math id="S2.I19.i2.p1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="1+q+q^{2}+\dots=1/(1-q)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" mathsize="0.800em">1</mn><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" mathsize="0.800em">+</mo><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" mathsize="0.800em">q</mi><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" mathsize="0.800em">+</mo><msup><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" mathsize="0.800em">q</mi><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" mathsize="0.800em">2</mn></msup><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" mathsize="0.800em">+</mo><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" mathsize="0.800em" mathvariant="normal">⋯</mi></mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" mathsize="0.800em">=</mo><mrow><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" mathsize="0.800em">1</mn><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" maxsize="0.800em" minsize="0.800em" stretchy="true" symmetric="true">/</mo><mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" maxsize="0.800em" minsize="0.800em">(</mo><mrow><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" mathsize="0.800em">1</mn><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" mathsize="0.800em">−</mo><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" mathsize="0.800em">q</mi></mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" maxsize="0.800em" minsize="0.800em">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">1+q+q^{2}+\dots=1/(1-q)</annotation></semantics></math><span id="S2.I19.i2.p1.1.7" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:80%;--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">.</span></span>
</span></span>
</span><span class="ltx_inline-block"><svg id="S2.SS11.SSS2.p6.pic1.pic1" class="ltx_picture" color="#008000" height="18.24" overflow="visible" style="vertical-align:-4.1px" version="1.1" viewBox="0 0 18.24 18.24" width="18.24"><g style="--ltx-stroke-color:#009900;--ltx-fill-color:#009900;--ltx-fg-color:#009900;" color="#009900" fill="#009900" stroke="#009900" stroke-width="1.8pt" transform="translate(0,18.24) matrix(1 0 0 -1 0 0) translate(1.25,0) translate(0,1.25)"><path style="fill:none" d="M 0 7.87 L 5.51 0 L 15.75 15.75"></path></g></svg></span>
<span id="S2.SS11.SSS2.p6.pic1.2.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="S2.SS11.SSS2.p6.pic1.2.2.1" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:80%;--ltx-fg-color:#008000;">GPT-5 thinking passed</span></span>
</span></span></span></foreignObject></g></g></svg></span>
</div>
          
</div>
</figure>
</section>
</section>
<section id="S2.SS12" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">12 </span>Creativity</h3>

<div id="S2.SS12.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S2.SS12.p1.1" class="ltx_p">This category measures originality and innovation in mathematical thinking, beyond standard methods or known results.</p>
</div>
<section id="S2.SS12.SSS1" class="ltx_subsubsection">
<h4 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsubsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsubsection">(a) </span>Posing new problems and defining new concepts</h4>

<div id="S2.SS12.SSS1.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S2.SS12.SSS1.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Formulate original mathematical questions or introduce novel definitions that open up new lines of inquiry.</p>
</div>
<div id="S2.SS12.SSS1.p2" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S2.SS12.SSS1.p2.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S2.SS12.SSS1.p2.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Design Principles:</span>
Design tasks that ask solvers to formulate original questions or definitions inspired by familiar patterns or concepts. Prompts should encourage open-ended exploration, with emphasis on novelty and potential for generalization or further investigation.</p>
</div>
<div id="S2.SS12.SSS1.p3" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S2.SS12.SSS1.p3.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S2.SS12.SSS1.p3.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Rubric</span></p>
</div>
<div id="S2.SS12.SSS1.p4" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S2.SS12.SSS1.p4.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S2.SS12.SSS1.p4.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Note:</span> Responses must be mathematically well-formed and valid. Evaluation focuses on novelty, clarity, and potential for exploration.</p>
</div>
<div id="S2.SS12.SSS1.p5" class="ltx_para">
<table id="S2.SS12.SSS1.p5.1" class="ltx_tabular ltx_align_middle">
<tr id="S2.SS12.SSS1.p5.1.1" class="ltx_tr">
<td id="S2.SS12.SSS1.p5.1.1.1" class="ltx_td ltx_align_center ltx_border_tt"><span id="S2.SS12.SSS1.p5.1.1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Level</span></td>
<td id="S2.SS12.SSS1.p5.1.1.2" class="ltx_td ltx_nopad_r ltx_align_left ltx_align_top ltx_border_tt">
<span id="S2.SS12.SSS1.p5.1.1.2.1" class="ltx_inline-block ltx_align_top" style="width:284.5pt;">
<span id="S2.SS12.SSS1.p5.1.1.2.1.1" class="ltx_p">Description</span>
</span></td></tr>
<tr id="S2.SS12.SSS1.p5.1.2" class="ltx_tr">
<td id="S2.SS12.SSS1.p5.1.2.1" class="ltx_td ltx_align_center ltx_border_t"><span id="S2.SS12.SSS1.p5.1.2.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">2 (Excellent)</span></td>
<td id="S2.SS12.SSS1.p5.1.2.2" class="ltx_td ltx_nopad_r ltx_align_left ltx_align_top ltx_border_t">
<span id="S2.SS12.SSS1.p5.1.2.2.1" class="ltx_inline-block ltx_align_top" style="width:284.5pt;">
<span id="S2.SS12.SSS1.p5.1.2.2.1.1" class="ltx_p">Poses a novel and well-formulated problem or definition with clear mathematical structure. Opens a path for meaningful exploration or generalization. Shows originality and insight.</span>
</span></td></tr>
<tr id="S2.SS12.SSS1.p5.1.3" class="ltx_tr">
<td id="S2.SS12.SSS1.p5.1.3.1" class="ltx_td ltx_align_center"><span id="S2.SS12.SSS1.p5.1.3.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">1 (Good)</span></td>
<td id="S2.SS12.SSS1.p5.1.3.2" class="ltx_td ltx_nopad_r ltx_align_left ltx_align_top">
<span id="S2.SS12.SSS1.p5.1.3.2.1" class="ltx_inline-block ltx_align_top" style="width:284.5pt;">
<span id="S2.SS12.SSS1.p5.1.3.2.1.1" class="ltx_p">Problem or concept is mathematically sound and somewhat novel. May resemble known ideas but reframed with fresh perspective or extension.</span>
</span></td></tr>
<tr id="S2.SS12.SSS1.p5.1.4" class="ltx_tr">
<td id="S2.SS12.SSS1.p5.1.4.1" class="ltx_td ltx_align_center ltx_border_bb"><span id="S2.SS12.SSS1.p5.1.4.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">0 (Satisfactory)</span></td>
<td id="S2.SS12.SSS1.p5.1.4.2" class="ltx_td ltx_nopad_r ltx_align_left ltx_align_top ltx_border_bb">
<span id="S2.SS12.SSS1.p5.1.4.2.1" class="ltx_inline-block ltx_align_top" style="width:284.5pt;">
<span id="S2.SS12.SSS1.p5.1.4.2.1.1" class="ltx_p">Problem or concept is valid but closely mirrors standard material. Shows basic understanding but lacks originality or direction for further inquiry.</span>
</span></td></tr>
</table>
</div>
<div id="S2.SS12.SSS1.p6" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S2.SS12.SSS1.p6.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S2.SS12.SSS1.p6.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Sample Problems:</span></p>
</div>
<figure id="S2.SS12.SSS1.fig1" class="ltx_figure">
<div id="S2.SS12.SSS1.fig1.1" class="ltx_logical-block ltx_minipage ltx_align_center ltx_align_top" style="width:276.0pt;">
            
<div id="S2.SS12.SSS1.p7" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent"><span class="ltx_inline-block"><svg id="S2.SS12.SSS1.p7.pic1" class="ltx_picture" height="85.54" overflow="visible" version="1.1" viewBox="0 0 381.9 85.54" width="381.9"><g style="--ltx-stroke-color:#000000;--ltx-fill-color:#000000;" fill="#000000" stroke="#000000" stroke-width="0.4pt" transform="translate(0,85.54) matrix(1 0 0 -1 0 0)"><g style="--ltx-fill-color:#3D6666;" fill="#3D6666" fill-opacity="1.0"><path style="stroke:none" d="M 0 4.63 L 0 80.91 C 0 83.47 2.07 85.54 4.63 85.54 L 377.27 85.54 C 379.83 85.54 381.9 83.47 381.9 80.91 L 381.9 4.63 C 381.9 2.07 379.83 0 377.27 0 L 4.63 0 C 2.07 0 0 2.07 0 4.63 Z"></path></g><g style="--ltx-fill-color:#FFFFFF;" fill="#FFFFFF" fill-opacity="1.0"><path style="stroke:none" d="M 0.69 4.63 L 0.69 68.6 L 381.21 68.6 L 381.21 4.63 C 381.21 2.45 379.45 0.69 377.27 0.69 L 4.63 0.69 C 2.45 0.69 0.69 2.45 0.69 4.63 Z"></path></g><g fill-opacity="1.0" transform="matrix(1.0 0.0 0.0 1.0 20.38 73.22)"><foreignObject style="--ltx-fo-width:25.16em;--ltx-fo-height:0.56em;--ltx-fo-depth:0em;font-size:10pt;" height="7.69" overflow="visible" transform="matrix(1 0 0 -1 0 7.69)" width="348.14"><span class="ltx_foreignobject_container"><span class="ltx_foreignobject_content">
<span id="S2.SS12.SSS1.p7.pic1.1" class="ltx_inline-block ltx_minipage ltx_align_bottom" style="width:25.16em;">
<span id="S2.SS12.SSS1.p7.pic1.1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S2.SS12.SSS1.p7.pic1.1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold" style="font-size:80%;--ltx-fg-color:#FFFFFF;">Problem 0: Massive SLE</span></span>
</span></span></span></foreignObject></g><g fill-opacity="1.0" transform="matrix(1.0 0.0 0.0 1.0 20.38 14.66)"><foreignObject style="--ltx-fo-width:29.01em;--ltx-fo-height:3.61em;--ltx-fo-depth:0.16em;font-size:10pt;" height="52.16" overflow="visible" transform="matrix(1 0 0 -1 0 50)" width="401.42"><span class="ltx_foreignobject_container"><span class="ltx_foreignobject_content">
<span id="S2.SS12.SSS1.p7.pic1.2" class="ltx_inline-block ltx_minipage ltx_align_bottom" style="width:29.01em;">
<span id="S2.SS12.SSS1.p7.pic1.2.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S2.SS12.SSS1.p7.pic1.2.1.1" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:80%;--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">Define massive SLE and describe the new questions and properties it may raise.</span></span><span class="ltx_inline-block"><svg id="S2.SS12.SSS1.p7.pic1.pic1" class="ltx_picture" color="#008000" height="18.24" overflow="visible" style="vertical-align:-4.1px" version="1.1" viewBox="0 0 18.24 18.24" width="18.24"><g style="--ltx-stroke-color:#009900;--ltx-fill-color:#009900;--ltx-fg-color:#009900;" color="#009900" fill="#009900" stroke="#009900" stroke-width="1.8pt" transform="translate(0,18.24) matrix(1 0 0 -1 0 0) translate(1.25,0) translate(0,1.25)"><path style="fill:none" d="M 0 7.87 L 5.51 0 L 15.75 15.75"></path></g></svg></span>
<span id="S2.SS12.SSS1.p7.pic1.2.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="S2.SS12.SSS1.p7.pic1.2.2.1" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:80%;--ltx-fg-color:#008000;">GPT-5 thinking passed</span></span>
</span></span></span></foreignObject></g></g></svg></span>
</div>
          
</div>
</figure>
</section>
<section id="S2.SS12.SSS2" class="ltx_subsubsection">
<h4 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsubsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsubsection">(b) </span>Inventing new methods or approaches</h4>

<div id="S2.SS12.SSS2.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S2.SS12.SSS2.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Devise alternative strategies, techniques, or algorithms that offer new ways of solving old problems.</p>
</div>
<div id="S2.SS12.SSS2.p2" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S2.SS12.SSS2.p2.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S2.SS12.SSS2.p2.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Design Principles:</span>
Select problems that can be solved using standard methods but also admit a simpler or more elegant solution through unconventional reasoning.</p>
</div>
<div id="S2.SS12.SSS2.p3" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S2.SS12.SSS2.p3.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S2.SS12.SSS2.p3.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Sample Problems:</span></p>
</div>
<figure id="S2.SS12.SSS2.fig1" class="ltx_figure">
<div id="S2.SS12.SSS2.fig1.1" class="ltx_logical-block ltx_minipage ltx_align_center ltx_align_top" style="width:276.0pt;">
            
<div id="S2.SS12.SSS2.p4" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent"><span class="ltx_inline-block"><svg id="S2.SS12.SSS2.p4.pic1" class="ltx_picture" height="150.17" overflow="visible" version="1.1" viewBox="0 0 381.9 150.17" width="381.9"><g style="--ltx-stroke-color:#000000;--ltx-fill-color:#000000;" fill="#000000" stroke="#000000" stroke-width="0.4pt" transform="translate(0,150.17) matrix(1 0 0 -1 0 0)"><g style="--ltx-fill-color:#3D6666;" fill="#3D6666" fill-opacity="1.0"><path style="stroke:none" d="M 0 4.63 L 0 145.54 C 0 148.1 2.07 150.17 4.63 150.17 L 377.27 150.17 C 379.83 150.17 381.9 148.1 381.9 145.54 L 381.9 4.63 C 381.9 2.07 379.83 0 377.27 0 L 4.63 0 C 2.07 0 0 2.07 0 4.63 Z"></path></g><g style="--ltx-fill-color:#FFFFFF;" fill="#FFFFFF" fill-opacity="1.0"><path style="stroke:none" d="M 0.69 4.63 L 0.69 131.08 L 381.21 131.08 L 381.21 4.63 C 381.21 2.45 379.45 0.69 377.27 0.69 L 4.63 0.69 C 2.45 0.69 0.69 2.45 0.69 4.63 Z"></path></g><g fill-opacity="1.0" transform="matrix(1.0 0.0 0.0 1.0 20.38 137.86)"><foreignObject style="--ltx-fo-width:25.16em;--ltx-fo-height:0.56em;--ltx-fo-depth:0.16em;font-size:10pt;" height="9.84" overflow="visible" transform="matrix(1 0 0 -1 0 7.69)" width="348.14"><span class="ltx_foreignobject_container"><span class="ltx_foreignobject_content">
<span id="S2.SS12.SSS2.p4.pic1.1" class="ltx_inline-block ltx_minipage ltx_align_bottom" style="width:25.16em;">
<span id="S2.SS12.SSS2.p4.pic1.1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S2.SS12.SSS2.p4.pic1.1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold" style="font-size:80%;--ltx-fg-color:#FFFFFF;">Problem 0: Maximum allowable sequence</span></span>
</span></span></span></foreignObject></g><g fill-opacity="1.0" transform="matrix(1.0 0.0 0.0 1.0 20.38 14.66)"><foreignObject style="--ltx-fo-width:29.01em;--ltx-fo-height:8.13em;--ltx-fo-depth:0.16em;font-size:10pt;" height="114.64" overflow="visible" transform="matrix(1 0 0 -1 0 112.49)" width="401.42"><span class="ltx_foreignobject_container"><span class="ltx_foreignobject_content">
<span id="S2.SS12.SSS2.p4.pic1.2" class="ltx_inline-block ltx_minipage ltx_align_bottom" style="width:29.01em;">
<span id="S2.SS12.SSS2.p4.pic1.2.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S2.SS12.SSS2.p4.pic1.2.1.1" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:80%;--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">Find at least two solutions to <a href="https://www.imo-official.org/problems/1977/eng.pdf" title="" class="ltx_ref ltx_href">1977 IMO Problem 2</a><cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citep">(<a href="#bib.bib8" title="" class="ltx_ref">IMO Board, 1977</a>)</cite>:
In a finite sequence of real numbers the sum of any seven successive terms is negative and the sum of any eleven successive terms is positive. Determine the maximum number of terms in the sequence.</span></span><span class="ltx_inline-block"><svg id="S2.SS12.SSS2.p4.pic1.pic1" class="ltx_picture" color="#008000" height="18.24" overflow="visible" style="vertical-align:-4.1px" version="1.1" viewBox="0 0 18.24 18.24" width="18.24"><g style="--ltx-stroke-color:#009900;--ltx-fill-color:#009900;--ltx-fg-color:#009900;" color="#009900" fill="#009900" stroke="#009900" stroke-width="1.8pt" transform="translate(0,18.24) matrix(1 0 0 -1 0 0) translate(1.25,0) translate(0,1.25)"><path style="fill:none" d="M 0 7.87 L 5.51 0 L 15.75 15.75"></path></g></svg></span>
<span id="S2.SS12.SSS2.p4.pic1.2.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="S2.SS12.SSS2.p4.pic1.2.2.1" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:80%;--ltx-fg-color:#008000;">GPT-5 thinking passed</span></span>
</span></span></span></foreignObject></g></g></svg></span>
</div>
          
</div>
</figure>
</section>
<section id="S2.SS12.SSS3" class="ltx_subsubsection">
<h4 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsubsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsubsection">(c) </span>Lateral thinking</h4>

<div id="S2.SS12.SSS3.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S2.SS12.SSS3.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Apply non-obvious insights, analogies, or reversals to reframe a problem and reach a solution creatively.</p>
</div>
<div id="S2.SS12.SSS3.p2" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S2.SS12.SSS3.p2.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S2.SS12.SSS3.p2.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Design Principles:</span>
Design brain-teaser-style problems that resist direct or conventional approaches and instead require solvers to adopt unexpected perspectives, reinterpret elements of the problem, or make surprising conceptual connections.</p>
</div>
<div id="S2.SS12.SSS3.p3" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S2.SS12.SSS3.p3.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S2.SS12.SSS3.p3.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Sample Problems:</span></p>
</div>
<figure id="S2.SS12.SSS3.fig1" class="ltx_figure">
<div id="S2.SS12.SSS3.fig1.1" class="ltx_logical-block ltx_minipage ltx_align_center ltx_align_top" style="width:276.0pt;">
            
<div id="S2.SS12.SSS3.p4" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent"><span class="ltx_inline-block"><svg id="S2.SS12.SSS3.p4.pic1" class="ltx_picture" height="71.09" overflow="visible" version="1.1" viewBox="0 0 381.9 71.09" width="381.9"><g style="--ltx-stroke-color:#000000;--ltx-fill-color:#000000;" fill="#000000" stroke="#000000" stroke-width="0.4pt" transform="translate(0,71.09) matrix(1 0 0 -1 0 0)"><g style="--ltx-fill-color:#3D6666;" fill="#3D6666" fill-opacity="1.0"><path style="stroke:none" d="M 0 4.63 L 0 66.46 C 0 69.02 2.07 71.09 4.63 71.09 L 377.27 71.09 C 379.83 71.09 381.9 69.02 381.9 66.46 L 381.9 4.63 C 381.9 2.07 379.83 0 377.27 0 L 4.63 0 C 2.07 0 0 2.07 0 4.63 Z"></path></g><g style="--ltx-fill-color:#FFFFFF;" fill="#FFFFFF" fill-opacity="1.0"><path style="stroke:none" d="M 0.69 4.63 L 0.69 51.99 L 381.21 51.99 L 381.21 4.63 C 381.21 2.45 379.45 0.69 377.27 0.69 L 4.63 0.69 C 2.45 0.69 0.69 2.45 0.69 4.63 Z"></path></g><g fill-opacity="1.0" transform="matrix(1.0 0.0 0.0 1.0 20.38 58.77)"><foreignObject style="--ltx-fo-width:25.16em;--ltx-fo-height:0.56em;--ltx-fo-depth:0.16em;font-size:10pt;" height="9.84" overflow="visible" transform="matrix(1 0 0 -1 0 7.69)" width="348.14"><span class="ltx_foreignobject_container"><span class="ltx_foreignobject_content">
<span id="S2.SS12.SSS3.p4.pic1.1" class="ltx_inline-block ltx_minipage ltx_align_bottom" style="width:25.16em;">
<span id="S2.SS12.SSS3.p4.pic1.1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S2.SS12.SSS3.p4.pic1.1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold" style="font-size:80%;--ltx-fg-color:#FFFFFF;">Problem 0: Make the equation valid</span></span>
</span></span></span></foreignObject></g><g fill-opacity="1.0" transform="matrix(1.0 0.0 0.0 1.0 20.38 14.66)"><foreignObject style="--ltx-fo-width:29.01em;--ltx-fo-height:2.41em;--ltx-fo-depth:0.16em;font-size:10pt;" height="35.55" overflow="visible" transform="matrix(1 0 0 -1 0 33.4)" width="401.42"><span class="ltx_foreignobject_container"><span class="ltx_foreignobject_content">
<span id="S2.SS12.SSS3.p4.pic1.2" class="ltx_inline-block ltx_minipage ltx_align_bottom" style="width:29.01em;">
<span id="S2.SS12.SSS3.p4.pic1.2.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S2.SS12.SSS3.p4.pic1.2.1.1" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:80%;--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">Move any one digit to make this equation true:
<math id="S2.SS12.SSS3.p4.pic1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="62-63=1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">62</mn><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">−</mo><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">63</mn></mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">=</mo><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">1</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">62-63=1</annotation></semantics></math>.</span></span><span class="ltx_inline-block"><svg id="S2.SS12.SSS3.p4.pic1.pic1" class="ltx_picture" color="#FF0000" height="18.24" overflow="visible" style="vertical-align:-4.1px" version="1.1" viewBox="0 0 18.24 18.24" width="18.24"><g style="--ltx-stroke-color:#FF0000;--ltx-fill-color:#FF0000;" fill="#FF0000" stroke="#FF0000" stroke-width="1.8pt" transform="translate(0,18.24) matrix(1 0 0 -1 0 0) translate(1.25,0) translate(0,1.25)"><path style="fill:none" d="M 0 0 L 15.75 15.75 M 0 15.75 L 15.75 0"></path></g></svg></span>
<span id="S2.SS12.SSS3.p4.pic1.2.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="S2.SS12.SSS3.p4.pic1.2.2.1" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:80%;--ltx-fg-color:#FF0000;">GPT-5 thinking failed</span></span>
</span></span></span></foreignObject></g></g></svg></span>
</div>
          
</div>
</figure>
<div class="ltx_pagination ltx_role_newpage"></div>
</section>
</section>
</section>
<section id="S3" class="ltx_section">
<h2 class="ltx_title ltx_title_section"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_section">3 </span>Skills Profile for GPT-5 thinking and Comparison with o4-mini-high </h2>

<div id="S3.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S3.p1.1" class="ltx_p">The Math Skills Breakdown evaluation provides a structured and fine-grained profile of GPT-5-thinking’s mathematical abilities across twelve core skill dimensions, each comprising specific sub-skills. This framework enables the assessment of both overall competence and localized strengths or weaknesses in mathematical abilities. All scores are reported on a 0–100 scale.</p>
</div>
<section id="S3.SS0.SSS0.Px1" class="ltx_paragraph">
<h5 class="ltx_title ltx_title_paragraph">Scoring Methodology.</h5>

<div id="S3.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S3.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Each skill category <math id="S3.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="i" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>i</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">i</annotation></semantics></math> has <math id="S3.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="m_{i}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>m</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">m_{i}</annotation></semantics></math> sub-skills indexed by <math id="S3.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="j" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>j</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">j</annotation></semantics></math>. For sub-skill <math id="S3.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(i,j)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>i</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>j</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(i,j)</annotation></semantics></math>,</p>
<table id="S3.Ex13" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S3.Ex13.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\text{SubScore}_{i,j}=100\cdot\frac{n_{\mathrm{pass},i,j}}{n_{\mathrm{total},i,j}}." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mtext>SubScore</mtext><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><mn>100</mn><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><mfrac><msub><mi>n</mi><mrow><mi>pass</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>i</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow></msub><msub><mi>n</mi><mrow><mi>total</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>i</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow></msub></mfrac></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\text{SubScore}_{i,j}=100\cdot\frac{n_{\mathrm{pass},i,j}}{n_{\mathrm{total},i,j}}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S3.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p1.2" class="ltx_p">Here, <math id="S3.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="n_{\mathrm{pass},i,j}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>n</mi><mrow><mi>pass</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>i</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">n_{\mathrm{pass},i,j}</annotation></semantics></math> denotes the number of correctly solved problems for sub-skill <math id="S3.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(i,j)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>i</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>j</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(i,j)</annotation></semantics></math>, and <math id="S3.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p1.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="n_{\mathrm{total},i,j}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>n</mi><mrow><mi>total</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>i</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">n_{\mathrm{total},i,j}</annotation></semantics></math> is the total number of problems assigned to that sub-skill. If a problem spans multiple skills, its weight will be proportionally assigned to each skill.</p>
</div>
<div id="S3.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p2" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S3.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p2.1" class="ltx_p">The <em id="S3.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p2.1.1" class="ltx_emph ltx_font_italic">balanced score</em> is defined as the uniform (equal-weighted) average of its sub-skill scores:</p>
<table id="S3.Ex14" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S3.Ex14.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\text{BalancedScore}_{i}:=\frac{1}{m_{i}}\sum_{j=1}^{m_{i}}\text{SubScore}_{i,j}." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mtext>BalancedScore</mtext><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>:=</mo><mrow><mfrac><mn>1</mn><msub><mi>m</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></mfrac><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>j</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><msub><mi>m</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></munderover><msub><mtext>SubScore</mtext><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow></msub></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\text{BalancedScore}_{i}:=\frac{1}{m_{i}}\sum_{j=1}^{m_{i}}\text{SubScore}_{i,j}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
<div id="S3.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p3" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S3.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p3.1" class="ltx_p">For comparison, we also report the <em id="S3.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p3.1.1" class="ltx_emph ltx_font_italic">weighted score</em>, which aggregates performance across all problems in the category:</p>
<table id="S3.Ex15" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S3.Ex15.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\text{WeightedScore}_{i}:=100\cdot\frac{\sum_{j=1}^{m_{i}}n_{\mathrm{pass},i,j}}{\sum_{j=1}^{m_{i}}n_{\mathrm{total},i,j}}." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mtext>WeightedScore</mtext><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>:=</mo><mrow><mn>100</mn><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><mfrac><mrow><msubsup><mo>∑</mo><mrow><mi>j</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><msub><mi>m</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></msubsup><msub><mi>n</mi><mrow><mi>pass</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>i</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow></msub></mrow><mrow><msubsup><mo>∑</mo><mrow><mi>j</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><msub><mi>m</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></msubsup><msub><mi>n</mi><mrow><mi>total</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>i</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow></msub></mrow></mfrac></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\text{WeightedScore}_{i}:=100\cdot\frac{\sum_{j=1}^{m_{i}}n_{\mathrm{pass},i,j}}{\sum_{j=1}^{m_{i}}n_{\mathrm{total},i,j}}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S3.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p3.2" class="ltx_p">Here, the numerator counts the total number of correctly solved problems across all sub-skills in category <math id="S3.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p3.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="i" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>i</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">i</annotation></semantics></math>, while the denominator is the total number of problems assigned to that category.
Equivalently,</p>
<table id="S3.Ex16" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S3.Ex16.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\text{WeightedScore}_{i}=\frac{\sum_{j=1}^{m_{i}}n_{\mathrm{total},i,j}\,\text{SubScore}_{i,j}}{\sum_{j=1}^{m_{i}}n_{\mathrm{total},i,j}}." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mtext>WeightedScore</mtext><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mrow><msubsup><mo>∑</mo><mrow><mi>j</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><msub><mi>m</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></msubsup><mrow><msub><mi>n</mi><mrow><mi>total</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>i</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mtext>SubScore</mtext><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow></msub></mrow></mrow><mrow><msubsup><mo>∑</mo><mrow><mi>j</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><msub><mi>m</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></msubsup><msub><mi>n</mi><mrow><mi>total</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>i</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow></msub></mrow></mfrac></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\text{WeightedScore}_{i}=\frac{\sum_{j=1}^{m_{i}}n_{\mathrm{total},i,j}\,\text{SubScore}_{i,j}}{\sum_{j=1}^{m_{i}}n_{\mathrm{total},i,j}}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
<div id="S3.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p4" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S3.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p4.1" class="ltx_p">Thus, <math id="S3.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p4.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\text{BalancedScore}_{i}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mtext>BalancedScore</mtext><mi>i</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\text{BalancedScore}_{i}</annotation></semantics></math> treats each sub-skill equally, while <math id="S3.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p4.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\text{WeightedScore}_{i}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mtext>WeightedScore</mtext><mi>i</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\text{WeightedScore}_{i}</annotation></semantics></math> reflects overall accuracy across all problems. In our evaluation, the balanced score is reported as the <em id="S3.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p4.1.1" class="ltx_emph ltx_font_italic">primary metric</em>, since it prevents categories with larger sub-skill problem sets from dominating the overall assessment.</p>
</div>
<div id="S3.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p5" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S3.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p5.1" class="ltx_p">To carry out the evaluation, we first collected GPT-5-thinking’s responses across the curated problem sets.
The raw results, organized by skill category and sub-skill, are summarized in Table <a href="#S3.T1" title="Table 1 ‣ Scoring Methodology. ‣ 3 Skills Profile for GPT-5 thinking and Comparison with o4-mini-high ‣ GAUSS: Benchmarking Structured Mathematical Skills for Large Language Models" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">1</span></a>,
which records the number of problems attempted under each sub-skill, together with counts of correct and incorrect responses.</p>
</div>
