<div class="ltx_pagination ltx_role_newpage"></div>
<div id="S3.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p6" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S3.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p6.1" class="ltx_p">We then compute per-subskill accuracies (<em id="S3.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p6.1.1" class="ltx_emph ltx_font_italic">SubScores</em>), as well as aggregate <em id="S3.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p6.1.2" class="ltx_emph ltx_font_italic">Balanced</em> and <em id="S3.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p6.1.3" class="ltx_emph ltx_font_italic">Weighted</em> scores for each category.
These results are reported in Table <a href="#S3.T2" title="Table 2 ‣ Scoring Methodology. ‣ 3 Skills Profile for GPT-5 thinking and Comparison with o4-mini-high ‣ GAUSS: Benchmarking Structured Mathematical Skills for Large Language Models" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">2</span></a>, enabling comparison across skills that differ in the number and distribution of problems.</p>
</div>
<figure id="S3.T2" class="ltx_table">
<figcaption class="ltx_caption"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_table"><span id="S3.T2.3" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:90%;">Table 2</span>: </span><span id="S3.T2.4" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:90%;">Skill Categories and Subskills with Balanced and Weighted Scores</span></figcaption>
<table id="S3.T2.5" class="ltx_tabular ltx_align_middle">
<tr id="S3.T2.5.1" class="ltx_tr">
<td id="S3.T2.5.1.1" class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_align_top ltx_border_tt">
<span id="S3.T2.5.1.1.1" class="ltx_inline-block ltx_align_top" style="width:102.4pt;">
<span id="S3.T2.5.1.1.1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S3.T2.5.1.1.1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Skill Category</span></span>
</span></td>
<td id="S3.T2.5.1.2" class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_align_top ltx_border_tt">
<span id="S3.T2.5.1.2.1" class="ltx_inline-block ltx_align_top" style="width:102.4pt;">
<span id="S3.T2.5.1.2.1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S3.T2.5.1.2.1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Subskill</span></span>
</span></td>
