</span></span></span></foreignObject></g><g fill-opacity="1.0" transform="matrix(1.0 0.0 0.0 1.0 20.38 14.66)"><foreignObject style="--ltx-fo-width:33.06em;--ltx-fo-height:0.56em;--ltx-fo-depth:0.16em;font-size:10pt;" height="9.84" overflow="visible" transform="matrix(1 0 0 -1 0 7.69)" width="457.46"><span class="ltx_foreignobject_container"><span class="ltx_foreignobject_content">
<span id="A1.I1.i5.p4.pic1.2" class="ltx_inline-block ltx_minipage ltx_align_bottom" style="width:33.06em;">
<span id="A1.I1.i5.p4.pic1.2.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.I1.i5.p4.pic1.2.1.1" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:80%;--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">The model correctly applied the s-cobordism theorem…</span></span>
</span></span></span></foreignObject></g></g></svg></span>
</div></li>
</ol>
</div>
<div id="A1.p4" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A1.p4.1" class="ltx_p">All box environments use  font and 90% width for clean layout. The proof-style environments for responses and solutions preserve a natural mathematical flow without decorative frames.</p>
</div>
<div id="A1.p5" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A1.p5.1" class="ltx_p ltx_align_center"><span id="A1.p5.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Problem → GPT-5-thinking Response → Solution → Rubric → Score + Evaluation. </span></p>
</div>
<div id="A1.p6" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A1.p6.1" class="ltx_p">This pipeline enables consistent analysis and evaluation of LLM-generated solutions.</p>
</div>
<div class="ltx_pagination ltx_role_newpage"></div>
</section>
<section id="A2" class="ltx_appendix">
<h2 class="ltx_title ltx_title_appendix"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_appendix">Appendix B </span>Model Responses and Evaluations</h2>

<section id="A2.SS1" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">1 </span>Memory of Math Knowledge</h3>

<section id="A2.SS1.SSS1" class="ltx_subsubsection">
<h4 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsubsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsubsection">(a) </span>Taxonomy of Subjects</h4>

<section id="A2.SS1.SSS1.Px1" class="ltx_paragraph">
<h5 class="ltx_title ltx_title_paragraph" style="--ltx-fg-color:#00E000;">Problem 1a1</h5>

<div id="A2.SS1.SSS1.Px1.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A2.SS1.SSS1.Px1.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.SS1.SSS1.Px1.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text"></span>
<br class="ltx_break" style="--ltx-break-space:-10.0pt;"></p>
</div>
<div id="A2.SS1.SSS1.Px1.p2" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent"><span class="ltx_inline-block"><svg id="A2.SS1.SSS1.Px1.p2.pic1" class="ltx_picture" height="232.69" overflow="visible" version="1.1" viewBox="0 0 429.64 232.69" width="429.64"><g style="--ltx-stroke-color:#000000;--ltx-fill-color:#000000;" fill="#000000" stroke="#000000" stroke-width="0.4pt" transform="translate(0,232.69) matrix(1 0 0 -1 0 0)"><g style="--ltx-fill-color:#3D6666;" fill="#3D6666" fill-opacity="1.0"><path style="stroke:none" d="M 0 4.63 L 0 228.06 C 0 230.62 2.07 232.69 4.63 232.69 L 425.01 232.69 C 427.56 232.69 429.64 230.62 429.64 228.06 L 429.64 4.63 C 429.64 2.07 427.56 0 425.01 0 L 4.63 0 C 2.07 0 0 2.07 0 4.63 Z"></path></g><g style="--ltx-fill-color:#F9F9F9;" fill="#F9F9F9" fill-opacity="1.0"><path style="stroke:none" d="M 0.69 4.63 L 0.69 213.82 L 428.94 213.82 L 428.94 4.63 C 428.94 2.45 427.18 0.69 425.01 0.69 L 4.63 0.69 C 2.45 0.69 0.69 2.45 0.69 4.63 Z"></path></g><g fill-opacity="1.0" transform="matrix(1.0 0.0 0.0 1.0 20.38 218.45)"><foreignObject style="--ltx-fo-width:24.44em;--ltx-fo-height:0.69em;--ltx-fo-depth:0em;font-size:10pt;" height="9.61" overflow="visible" transform="matrix(1 0 0 -1 0 9.61)" width="338.18"><span class="ltx_foreignobject_container"><span class="ltx_foreignobject_content">
<span id="A2.SS1.SSS1.Px1.p2.pic1.1" class="ltx_inline-block ltx_minipage ltx_align_bottom" style="width:24.44em;">
<span id="A2.SS1.SSS1.Px1.p2.pic1.1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.SS1.SSS1.Px1.p2.pic1.1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold" style="--ltx-fg-color:#FFFFFF;">Problem</span></span>
</span></span></span></foreignObject></g><g fill-opacity="1.0" transform="matrix(1.0 0.0 0.0 1.0 20.38 14.66)"><foreignObject style="--ltx-fo-width:32.01em;--ltx-fo-height:13.54em;--ltx-fo-depth:0.16em;font-size:10pt;" height="189.51" overflow="visible" transform="matrix(1 0 0 -1 0 187.36)" width="442.93"><span class="ltx_foreignobject_container"><span class="ltx_foreignobject_content">
<span id="A2.SS1.SSS1.Px1.p2.pic1.2" class="ltx_inline-block ltx_minipage ltx_align_bottom" style="width:32.01em;">
<span id="A2.SS1.SSS1.Px1.p2.pic1.2.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.SS1.SSS1.Px1.p2.pic1.2.1.1" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:80%;--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">Floer homology is a powerful tool for studying symplectic geometry and low-dimensional topology.</span></span>
<span id="A2.I1" class="ltx_itemize">
<span id="A2.I1.i1" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">•</span> 
<span id="A2.I1.i1.p1" class="ltx_para">
<span id="A2.I1.i1.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.I1.i1.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:80%;--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">Please name three distinct Floer homology theories that play important roles in low-dimensional topology.</span></span>
</span></span>
<span id="A2.I1.i2" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">•</span> 
<span id="A2.I1.i2.p1" class="ltx_para">
<span id="A2.I1.i2.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.I1.i2.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:80%;--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">For each theory, provide an example of a significant topological application. Your applications should not mention explicitly the Floer homology theory in the statement.</span></span>
</span></span>
</span><span class="ltx_inline-block"><svg id="A2.SS1.SSS1.Px1.p2.pic1.pic1" class="ltx_picture" color="#008000" height="18.24" overflow="visible" style="vertical-align:-4.1px" version="1.1" viewBox="0 0 18.24 18.24" width="18.24"><g style="--ltx-stroke-color:#009900;--ltx-fill-color:#009900;--ltx-fg-color:#009900;" color="#009900" fill="#009900" stroke="#009900" stroke-width="1.8pt" transform="translate(0,18.24) matrix(1 0 0 -1 0 0) translate(1.25,0) translate(0,1.25)"><path style="fill:none" d="M 0 7.87 L 5.51 0 L 15.75 15.75"></path></g></svg></span>
<span id="A2.SS1.SSS1.Px1.p2.pic1.2.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.SS1.SSS1.Px1.p2.pic1.2.2.1" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:80%;--ltx-fg-color:#008000;">GPT-5 thinking passed</span></span>
<span id="A2.SS1.SSS1.Px1.p2.pic1.2.3" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.SS1.SSS1.Px1.p2.pic1.2.3.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic" style="font-size:80%;--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">Proposed by Qiuyu Ren</span></span>
</span></span></span></foreignObject></g></g></svg></span>
</div>
<div id="A2.SS1.SSS1.Px1.1" class="ltx_proof">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_font_italic ltx_title_proof"><span id="A2.SS1.SSS1.Px1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Response of GPT-5-thinking</span>.</h6>
<div id="A2.SS1.SSS1.Px1.p3" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A2.SS1.SSS1.Px1.p3.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.SS1.SSS1.Px1.p3.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Instanton Floer homology.<span id="A2.SS1.SSS1.Px1.p3.1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_medium">
<em id="A2.SS1.SSS1.Px1.p3.1.1.1.1" class="ltx_emph ltx_font_italic">Application:</em> For any nontrivial knot <math id="A2.SS1.SSS1.Px1.p3.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="K\subset S^{3}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>K</mi><mo>⊂</mo><msup><mi>S</mi><mn>3</mn></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">K\subset S^{3}</annotation></semantics></math>, every non-meridional Dehn surgery on <math id="A2.SS1.SSS1.Px1.p3.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="K" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>K</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">K</annotation></semantics></math> produces a 3-manifold with nontrivial fundamental group (i.e., no such surgery yields a homotopy 3-sphere). (Kronheimer–Mrowka, “Property P for knots,” 2004.)</span></span></p>
</div>
<div id="A2.SS1.SSS1.Px1.p4" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A2.SS1.SSS1.Px1.p4.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.SS1.SSS1.Px1.p4.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Monopole (Seiberg–Witten) Floer homology.<span id="A2.SS1.SSS1.Px1.p4.1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_medium">
<em id="A2.SS1.SSS1.Px1.p4.1.1.1.1" class="ltx_emph ltx_font_italic">Application:</em> There exist topological manifolds in every dimension <math id="A2.SS1.SSS1.Px1.p4.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="n\geq 5" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>≥</mo><mn>5</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">n\geq 5</annotation></semantics></math> that admit no simplicial triangulation. (Manolescu’s disproof of the high-dimensional triangulation conjecture via Pin(2)-equivariant methods, 2013.)</span></span></p>
</div>
<div id="A2.SS1.SSS1.Px1.p5" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A2.SS1.SSS1.Px1.p5.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.SS1.SSS1.Px1.p5.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Heegaard Floer homology.<span id="A2.SS1.SSS1.Px1.p5.1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_medium">
<em id="A2.SS1.SSS1.Px1.p5.1.1.1.1" class="ltx_emph ltx_font_italic">Application:</em> If a Dehn surgery on a knot in <math id="A2.SS1.SSS1.Px1.p5.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="S^{3}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi>S</mi><mn>3</mn></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">S^{3}</annotation></semantics></math> yields a lens space, then the knot is fibered. (Ozsváth–Szabó framework with results of Ghiggini and Ni, 2007–2008.)</span></span></p>
</div>
<div id="A2.SS1.SSS1.Px1.p6" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A2.SS1.SSS1.Px1.p6.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.SS1.SSS1.Px1.p6.1.1" class="ltx_text">∎</span></p>
</div>
</div>
<div id="A2.SS1.SSS1.Px1.2" class="ltx_proof">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_font_italic ltx_title_proof"><span id="A2.SS1.SSS1.Px1.2.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Standard Solution</span>.</h6>
<div id="A2.SS1.SSS1.Px1.p7" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A2.SS1.SSS1.Px1.p7.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.SS1.SSS1.Px1.p7.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Heegaard Floer homology<span id="A2.SS1.SSS1.Px1.p7.1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_medium">. Application: branched double covers of alternating knots in <math id="A2.SS1.SSS1.Px1.p7.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="S^{3}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi>S</mi><mn>3</mn></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">S^{3}</annotation></semantics></math> do not admit co-orientable taut foliations.</span></span></p>
</div>
<div id="A2.SS1.SSS1.Px1.p8" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A2.SS1.SSS1.Px1.p8.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.SS1.SSS1.Px1.p8.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Instanton Floer homology<span id="A2.SS1.SSS1.Px1.p8.1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_medium">. Application: Khovanov homology detects the unknot.</span></span></p>
</div>
<div id="A2.SS1.SSS1.Px1.p9" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A2.SS1.SSS1.Px1.p9.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.SS1.SSS1.Px1.p9.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Monopole Floer homology<span id="A2.SS1.SSS1.Px1.p9.1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_medium">. Application: Disproof of the triangulation conjecture.
∎</span></span></p>
</div>
</div>
<div id="A2.SS1.SSS1.Px1.p10" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent"><span class="ltx_inline-block"><svg id="A2.SS1.SSS1.Px1.p10.pic1" class="ltx_picture" height="86.23" overflow="visible" version="1.1" viewBox="0 0 429.64 86.23" width="429.64"><g style="--ltx-stroke-color:#000000;--ltx-fill-color:#000000;" fill="#000000" stroke="#000000" stroke-width="0.4pt" transform="translate(0,86.23) matrix(1 0 0 -1 0 0)"><g style="--ltx-fill-color:#4D4D4D;" fill="#4D4D4D" fill-opacity="1.0"><path style="stroke:none" d="M 0 4.63 L 0 81.6 C 0 84.16 2.07 86.23 4.63 86.23 L 425.01 86.23 C 427.56 86.23 429.64 84.16 429.64 81.6 L 429.64 4.63 C 429.64 2.07 427.56 0 425.01 0 L 4.63 0 C 2.07 0 0 2.07 0 4.63 Z"></path></g><g style="--ltx-fill-color:#F9F9F9;" fill="#F9F9F9" fill-opacity="1.0"><path style="stroke:none" d="M 0.69 4.63 L 0.69 67.36 L 428.94 67.36 L 428.94 4.63 C 428.94 2.45 427.18 0.69 425.01 0.69 L 4.63 0.69 C 2.45 0.69 0.69 2.45 0.69 4.63 Z"></path></g><g fill-opacity="1.0" transform="matrix(1.0 0.0 0.0 1.0 20.38 71.99)"><foreignObject style="--ltx-fo-width:24.44em;--ltx-fo-height:0.69em;--ltx-fo-depth:0em;font-size:10pt;" height="9.61" overflow="visible" transform="matrix(1 0 0 -1 0 9.61)" width="338.18"><span class="ltx_foreignobject_container"><span class="ltx_foreignobject_content">
<span id="A2.SS1.SSS1.Px1.p10.pic1.1" class="ltx_inline-block ltx_minipage ltx_align_bottom" style="width:24.44em;">
<span id="A2.SS1.SSS1.Px1.p10.pic1.1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.SS1.SSS1.Px1.p10.pic1.1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold" style="--ltx-fg-color:#FFFFFF;">Rubric</span></span>
</span></span></span></foreignObject></g><g fill-opacity="1.0" transform="matrix(1.0 0.0 0.0 1.0 20.38 14.66)"><foreignObject style="--ltx-fo-width:33.06em;--ltx-fo-height:2.96em;--ltx-fo-depth:0.16em;font-size:10pt;" height="43.05" overflow="visible" transform="matrix(1 0 0 -1 0 40.9)" width="457.46"><span class="ltx_foreignobject_container"><span class="ltx_foreignobject_content">
<span id="A2.SS1.SSS1.Px1.p10.pic1.2" class="ltx_inline-block ltx_minipage ltx_align_bottom" style="width:33.06em;">
<span id="A2.SS1.SSS1.Px1.p10.pic1.2.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.SS1.SSS1.Px1.p10.pic1.2.1.1" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:80%;--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">1 point for naming three Floer theories fundamental in low-dimensional topology.
<br class="ltx_break">2 points for giving correct topological applications.</span></span>
</span></span></span></foreignObject></g></g></svg></span>
</div>
<div id="A2.SS1.SSS1.Px1.p11" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent"><span class="ltx_inline-block"><svg id="A2.SS1.SSS1.Px1.p11.pic1" class="ltx_picture" height="54.13" overflow="visible" version="1.1" viewBox="0 0 429.64 54.13" width="429.64"><g style="--ltx-stroke-color:#000000;--ltx-fill-color:#000000;" fill="#000000" stroke="#000000" stroke-width="0.4pt" transform="translate(0,54.13) matrix(1 0 0 -1 0 0)"><g style="--ltx-fill-color:#5A996B;" fill="#5A996B" fill-opacity="1.0"><path style="stroke:none" d="M 0 4.63 L 0 49.51 C 0 52.06 2.07 54.13 4.63 54.13 L 425.01 54.13 C 427.56 54.13 429.64 52.06 429.64 49.51 L 429.64 4.63 C 429.64 2.07 427.56 0 425.01 0 L 4.63 0 C 2.07 0 0 2.07 0 4.63 Z"></path></g><g style="--ltx-fill-color:#F6FFF9;" fill="#F6FFF9" fill-opacity="1.0"><path style="stroke:none" d="M 0.69 4.63 L 0.69 35.38 L 428.94 35.38 L 428.94 4.63 C 428.94 2.45 427.18 0.69 425.01 0.69 L 4.63 0.69 C 2.45 0.69 0.69 2.45 0.69 4.63 Z"></path></g><g fill-opacity="1.0" transform="matrix(1.0 0.0 0.0 1.0 20.38 40.01)"><foreignObject style="--ltx-fo-width:24.44em;--ltx-fo-height:0.69em;--ltx-fo-depth:0em;font-size:10pt;" height="9.49" overflow="visible" transform="matrix(1 0 0 -1 0 9.49)" width="338.18"><span class="ltx_foreignobject_container"><span class="ltx_foreignobject_content">
