</span></span></span></foreignObject></g></g></svg></span>
</div>
</section>
<section id="A2.SS1.SSS1.Px2" class="ltx_paragraph">
<h5 class="ltx_title ltx_title_paragraph" style="--ltx-fg-color:#00E000;">Problm 1a2</h5>

<div id="A2.SS1.SSS1.Px2.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A2.SS1.SSS1.Px2.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.SS1.SSS1.Px2.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text"></span>
<br class="ltx_break" style="--ltx-break-space:-10.0pt;"></p>
</div>
<div id="A2.SS1.SSS1.Px2.p2" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent"><span class="ltx_inline-block"><svg id="A2.SS1.SSS1.Px2.p2.pic1" class="ltx_picture" height="181.34" overflow="visible" version="1.1" viewBox="0 0 429.64 181.34" width="429.64"><g style="--ltx-stroke-color:#000000;--ltx-fill-color:#000000;" fill="#000000" stroke="#000000" stroke-width="0.4pt" transform="translate(0,181.34) matrix(1 0 0 -1 0 0)"><g style="--ltx-fill-color:#3D6666;" fill="#3D6666" fill-opacity="1.0"><path style="stroke:none" d="M 0 4.63 L 0 176.71 C 0 179.27 2.07 181.34 4.63 181.34 L 425.01 181.34 C 427.56 181.34 429.64 179.27 429.64 176.71 L 429.64 4.63 C 429.64 2.07 427.56 0 425.01 0 L 4.63 0 C 2.07 0 0 2.07 0 4.63 Z"></path></g><g style="--ltx-fill-color:#F9F9F9;" fill="#F9F9F9" fill-opacity="1.0"><path style="stroke:none" d="M 0.69 4.63 L 0.69 162.47 L 428.94 162.47 L 428.94 4.63 C 428.94 2.45 427.18 0.69 425.01 0.69 L 4.63 0.69 C 2.45 0.69 0.69 2.45 0.69 4.63 Z"></path></g><g fill-opacity="1.0" transform="matrix(1.0 0.0 0.0 1.0 20.38 167.1)"><foreignObject style="--ltx-fo-width:24.44em;--ltx-fo-height:0.69em;--ltx-fo-depth:0em;font-size:10pt;" height="9.61" overflow="visible" transform="matrix(1 0 0 -1 0 9.61)" width="338.18"><span class="ltx_foreignobject_container"><span class="ltx_foreignobject_content">
<span id="A2.SS1.SSS1.Px2.p2.pic1.1" class="ltx_inline-block ltx_minipage ltx_align_bottom" style="width:24.44em;">
<span id="A2.SS1.SSS1.Px2.p2.pic1.1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.SS1.SSS1.Px2.p2.pic1.1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold" style="--ltx-fg-color:#FFFFFF;">Problem</span></span>
</span></span></span></foreignObject></g><g fill-opacity="1.0" transform="matrix(1.0 0.0 0.0 1.0 20.38 14.66)"><foreignObject style="--ltx-fo-width:32.01em;--ltx-fo-height:9.83em;--ltx-fo-depth:0.16em;font-size:10pt;" height="138.16" overflow="visible" transform="matrix(1 0 0 -1 0 136.01)" width="442.93"><span class="ltx_foreignobject_container"><span class="ltx_foreignobject_content">
<span id="A2.SS1.SSS1.Px2.p2.pic1.2" class="ltx_inline-block ltx_minipage ltx_align_bottom" style="width:32.01em;">
<span id="A2.SS1.SSS1.Px2.p2.pic1.2.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.SS1.SSS1.Px2.p2.pic1.2.1.1" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:80%;--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">Liouville quantum gravity (LQG) is a central topic in modern probability theory. List several of its subfields and, for each subfield:</span></span>
<span id="A2.I2" class="ltx_enumerate">
<span id="A2.I2.ix1" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">i.</span> 
<span id="A2.I2.ix1.p1" class="ltx_para">
<span id="A2.I2.ix1.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.I2.ix1.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:80%;--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">Name a central concept or structure;</span></span>
</span></span>
<span id="A2.I2.ix2" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">ii.</span> 
<span id="A2.I2.ix2.p1" class="ltx_para">
<span id="A2.I2.ix2.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.I2.ix2.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:80%;--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">State one foundational result from that subfield.</span></span>
</span></span>
</span><span class="ltx_inline-block"><svg id="A2.SS1.SSS1.Px2.p2.pic1.pic1" class="ltx_picture" color="#008000" height="18.24" overflow="visible" style="vertical-align:-4.1px" version="1.1" viewBox="0 0 18.24 18.24" width="18.24"><g style="--ltx-stroke-color:#009900;--ltx-fill-color:#009900;--ltx-fg-color:#009900;" color="#009900" fill="#009900" stroke="#009900" stroke-width="1.8pt" transform="translate(0,18.24) matrix(1 0 0 -1 0 0) translate(1.25,0) translate(0,1.25)"><path style="fill:none" d="M 0 7.87 L 5.51 0 L 15.75 15.75"></path></g></svg></span>
<span id="A2.SS1.SSS1.Px2.p2.pic1.2.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.SS1.SSS1.Px2.p2.pic1.2.2.1" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:80%;--ltx-fg-color:#008000;">GPT-5 thinking passed</span></span>
<span id="A2.SS1.SSS1.Px2.p2.pic1.2.3" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.SS1.SSS1.Px2.p2.pic1.2.3.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic" style="font-size:80%;--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">Proposed by Jiaxin Zhang</span></span>
</span></span></span></foreignObject></g></g></svg></span>
</div>
<div id="A2.SS1.SSS1.Px2.1" class="ltx_proof">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_font_italic ltx_title_proof"><span id="A2.SS1.SSS1.Px2.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Response of GPT-5-thinking</span>.</h6>
<div id="A2.SS1.SSS1.Px2.p3" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A2.SS1.SSS1.Px2.p3.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.SS1.SSS1.Px2.p3.1.1" class="ltx_text">Great question. Here’s a compact map of major LQG subfields—each with a central object and one canonical theorem/result.</span></p>
</div>
<div id="A2.SS1.SSS1.Px2.p4" class="ltx_para">
<ol id="A2.I3" class="ltx_enumerate">
<li id="A2.I3.i1" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">1.</span> 
<div id="A2.I3.i1.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A2.I3.i1.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.I3.i1.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Gaussian multiplicative chaos (GMC) &amp; the LQG measure</span></p>
<ol id="A2.I3.i1.I1" class="ltx_enumerate">
<li id="A2.I3.i1.I1.ix1" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">i.</span> 
<div id="A2.I3.i1.I1.ix1.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A2.I3.i1.I1.ix1.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><em id="A2.I3.i1.I1.ix1.p1.1.1" class="ltx_emph ltx_font_italic">Central concept:</em> The <math id="A2.I3.i1.I1.ix1.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\gamma" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>γ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\gamma</annotation></semantics></math>-Liouville area measure <math id="A2.I3.i1.I1.ix1.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mu_{h}=e^{\gamma h}\,dx\,dy" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>μ</mi><mi>h</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><msup><mi>e</mi><mrow><mi>γ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>h</mi></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>d</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>x</mi><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>d</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>y</mi></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mu_{h}=e^{\gamma h}\,dx\,dy</annotation></semantics></math> defined from a Gaussian Free Field via GMC.</p>
</div></li>
<li id="A2.I3.i1.I1.ix2" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">ii.</span> 
<div id="A2.I3.i1.I1.ix2.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A2.I3.i1.I1.ix2.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><em id="A2.I3.i1.I1.ix2.p1.1.1" class="ltx_emph ltx_font_italic">Foundational result:</em> The KPZ relation rigorously linking Euclidean and quantum scaling exponents, and the construction/coordinate-change rule for the LQG measure.</p>
</div></li>
</ol>
</div></li>
<li id="A2.I3.i2" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">2.</span> 
<div id="A2.I3.i2.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A2.I3.i2.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.I3.i2.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Quantum surfaces (disks, spheres, wedges, cones)</span></p>
<ol id="A2.I3.i2.I1" class="ltx_enumerate">
<li id="A2.I3.i2.I1.ix1" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">i.</span> 
<div id="A2.I3.i2.I1.ix1.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A2.I3.i2.I1.ix1.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><em id="A2.I3.i2.I1.ix1.p1.1.1" class="ltx_emph ltx_font_italic">Central concept:</em> Equivalence classes of <math id="A2.I3.i2.I1.ix1.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(D,h)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>D</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>h</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(D,h)</annotation></semantics></math> modulo additive constants and conformal maps, with canonical families: quantum disk/sphere/wedge/cone.</p>
</div></li>
<li id="A2.I3.i2.I1.ix2" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">ii.</span> 
<div id="A2.I3.i2.I1.ix2.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A2.I3.i2.I1.ix2.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><em id="A2.I3.i2.I1.ix2.p1.1.1" class="ltx_emph ltx_font_italic">Foundational result:</em> Duplantier–Miller–Sheffield (DMS) construct these surfaces and their operations (e.g., welding, Poissonian decompositions) in the <math id="A2.I3.i2.I1.ix2.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\gamma\in(0,2)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>γ</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>2</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\gamma\in(0,2)</annotation></semantics></math> regime.</p>
</div></li>
</ol>
</div></li>
<li id="A2.I3.i3" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">3.</span> 
<div id="A2.I3.i3.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A2.I3.i3.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.I3.i3.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">SLE/LQG coupling (welding &amp; the quantum zipper)</span></p>
<ol id="A2.I3.i3.I1" class="ltx_enumerate">
<li id="A2.I3.i3.I1.ix1" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">i.</span> 
<div id="A2.I3.i3.I1.ix1.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A2.I3.i3.I1.ix1.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><em id="A2.I3.i3.I1.ix1.p1.1.1" class="ltx_emph ltx_font_italic">Central concept:</em> Conformal welding of quantum boundaries; interfaces are SLE with <math id="A2.I3.i3.I1.ix1.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\kappa=\gamma^{2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>κ</mi><mo>=</mo><msup><mi>γ</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\kappa=\gamma^{2}</annotation></semantics></math> (and <math id="A2.I3.i3.I1.ix1.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\kappa^{\prime}=16/\gamma^{2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msup><mi>κ</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo>=</mo><mrow><mn>16</mn><mo>/</mo><msup><mi>γ</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\kappa^{\prime}=16/\gamma^{2}</annotation></semantics></math> for space-filling variants).</p>
</div></li>
<li id="A2.I3.i3.I1.ix2" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">ii.</span> 
<div id="A2.I3.i3.I1.ix2.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A2.I3.i3.I1.ix2.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><em id="A2.I3.i3.I1.ix2.p1.1.1" class="ltx_emph ltx_font_italic">Foundational result:</em> Sheffield’s “quantum gravity zipper”: welding two LQG surfaces along boundary lengths produces an SLE interface, with precise conformal-covariance and symmetry properties.</p>
</div></li>
</ol>
</div></li>
<li id="A2.I3.i4" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">4.</span> 
<div id="A2.I3.i4.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A2.I3.i4.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.I3.i4.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Mating-of-trees / peanosphere</span></p>
<ol id="A2.I3.i4.I1" class="ltx_enumerate">
<li id="A2.I3.i4.I1.ix1" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">i.</span> 
<div id="A2.I3.i4.I1.ix1.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A2.I3.i4.I1.ix1.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><em id="A2.I3.i4.I1.ix1.p1.1.1" class="ltx_emph ltx_font_italic">Central concept:</em> Encode an LQG surface decorated by a space-filling SLE as a correlated two-dimensional Brownian motion (“CRT–CRT” mating).</p>
</div></li>
<li id="A2.I3.i4.I1.ix2" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">ii.</span> 
<div id="A2.I3.i4.I1.ix2.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A2.I3.i4.I1.ix2.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><em id="A2.I3.i4.I1.ix2.p1.1.1" class="ltx_emph ltx_font_italic">Foundational result:</em> The DMS mating-of-trees theorem gives a canonical Brownian encoding of <math id="A2.I3.i4.I1.ix2.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\gamma" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>γ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\gamma</annotation></semantics></math>-LQG with SLE<math id="A2.I3.i4.I1.ix2.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{}_{\kappa^{\prime}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mrow></mrow><msup><mi>κ</mi><mo>′</mo></msup></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{}_{\kappa^{\prime}}</annotation></semantics></math> decoration.</p>
</div></li>
</ol>
</div></li>
<li id="A2.I3.i5" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">5.</span> 
<div id="A2.I3.i5.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A2.I3.i5.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.I3.i5.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Imaginary geometry</span></p>
<ol id="A2.I3.i5.I1" class="ltx_enumerate">
<li id="A2.I3.i5.I1.ix1" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">i.</span> 
<div id="A2.I3.i5.I1.ix1.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A2.I3.i5.I1.ix1.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><em id="A2.I3.i5.I1.ix1.p1.1.1" class="ltx_emph ltx_font_italic">Central concept:</em> GFF flow lines <math id="A2.I3.i5.I1.ix1.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="e^{i(h/\chi+\theta)}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi>e</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>h</mi><mo>/</mo><mi>χ</mi></mrow><mo>+</mo><mi>θ</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">e^{i(h/\chi+\theta)}</annotation></semantics></math> realizing SLE<sub id="A2.I3.i5.I1.ix1.p1.1.2" class="ltx_sub"><span id="A2.I3.i5.I1.ix1.p1.1.2.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">κ</span></sub> curves and their interactions.</p>
</div></li>
<li id="A2.I3.i5.I1.ix2" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">ii.</span> 
<div id="A2.I3.i5.I1.ix2.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A2.I3.i5.I1.ix2.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><em id="A2.I3.i5.I1.ix2.p1.1.1" class="ltx_emph ltx_font_italic">Foundational result:</em> Existence/uniqueness of flow lines and identification with SLE<sub id="A2.I3.i5.I1.ix2.p1.1.2" class="ltx_sub"><span id="A2.I3.i5.I1.ix2.p1.1.2.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">κ</span></sub> (and counterflow with SLE<sub id="A2.I3.i5.I1.ix2.p1.1.3" class="ltx_sub"><span id="A2.I3.i5.I1.ix2.p1.1.3.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">16/κ</span></sub>); reversibility and interaction theorems.</p>
</div></li>
</ol>
</div></li>
<li id="A2.I3.i6" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">6.</span> 
<div id="A2.I3.i6.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A2.I3.i6.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.I3.i6.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Metric structure &amp; QLE</span></p>
<ol id="A2.I3.i6.I1" class="ltx_enumerate">
<li id="A2.I3.i6.I1.ix1" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">i.</span> 
<div id="A2.I3.i6.I1.ix1.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A2.I3.i6.I1.ix1.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><em id="A2.I3.i6.I1.ix1.p1.1.1" class="ltx_emph ltx_font_italic">Central concept:</em> The LQG metric <math id="A2.I3.i6.I1.ix1.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="D_{h}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>D</mi><mi>h</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">D_{h}</annotation></semantics></math> (distance) obtained via Quantum Loewner Evolution and Liouville first-passage percolation limits.</p>
</div></li>
<li id="A2.I3.i6.I1.ix2" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">ii.</span> 
<div id="A2.I3.i6.I1.ix2.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A2.I3.i6.I1.ix2.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><em id="A2.I3.i6.I1.ix2.p1.1.1" class="ltx_emph ltx_font_italic">Foundational result:</em> Existence and uniqueness of the <math id="A2.I3.i6.I1.ix2.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\gamma" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>γ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\gamma</annotation></semantics></math>-LQG metric for all <math id="A2.I3.i6.I1.ix2.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\gamma\in(0,2)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>γ</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>2</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\gamma\in(0,2)</annotation></semantics></math>; at <math id="A2.I3.i6.I1.ix2.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\gamma=\sqrt{8/3}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>γ</mi><mo>=</mo><msqrt><mrow><mn>8</mn><mo>/</mo><mn>3</mn></mrow></msqrt></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\gamma=\sqrt{8/3}</annotation></semantics></math>, QLE constructs the metric and matches Brownian map geometry.</p>
</div></li>
</ol>
</div></li>
<li id="A2.I3.i7" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">7.</span> 
<div id="A2.I3.i7.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A2.I3.i7.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.I3.i7.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Random planar maps <math id="A2.I3.i7.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\longleftrightarrow" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mo stretchy="false">⟷</mo><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\longleftrightarrow</annotation></semantics></math> LQG</span></p>
<ol id="A2.I3.i7.I1" class="ltx_enumerate">
<li id="A2.I3.i7.I1.ix1" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">i.</span> 
<div id="A2.I3.i7.I1.ix1.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A2.I3.i7.I1.ix1.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><em id="A2.I3.i7.I1.ix1.p1.1.1" class="ltx_emph ltx_font_italic">Central concept:</em> Scaling limits of uniform random maps (quadrangulations, etc.) as metric-measure spheres.</p>
</div></li>
<li id="A2.I3.i7.I1.ix2" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">ii.</span> 
<div id="A2.I3.i7.I1.ix2.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A2.I3.i7.I1.ix2.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><em id="A2.I3.i7.I1.ix2.p1.1.1" class="ltx_emph ltx_font_italic">Foundational result:</em> The Brownian map is the universal scaling limit of large random quadrangulations (and related classes); subsequently identified with <math id="A2.I3.i7.I1.ix2.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\sqrt{8/3}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msqrt><mrow><mn>8</mn><mo>/</mo><mn>3</mn></mrow></msqrt><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\sqrt{8/3}</annotation></semantics></math>-LQG.</p>
</div></li>
</ol>
</div></li>
<li id="A2.I3.i8" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">8.</span> 
<div id="A2.I3.i8.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A2.I3.i8.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.I3.i8.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Liouville CFT &amp; structure constants</span></p>
<ol id="A2.I3.i8.I1" class="ltx_enumerate">
<li id="A2.I3.i8.I1.ix1" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">i.</span> 
<div id="A2.I3.i8.I1.ix1.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A2.I3.i8.I1.ix1.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><em id="A2.I3.i8.I1.ix1.p1.1.1" class="ltx_emph ltx_font_italic">Central concept:</em> Probabilistic Liouville conformal field theory built from the GFF; correlation functions and structure constants.</p>
</div></li>
<li id="A2.I3.i8.I1.ix2" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">ii.</span> 
<div id="A2.I3.i8.I1.ix2.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A2.I3.i8.I1.ix2.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><em id="A2.I3.i8.I1.ix2.p1.1.1" class="ltx_emph ltx_font_italic">Foundational result:</em> Probabilistic proof of the DOZZ formula for LCFT three-point structure constants, via GMC.</p>
</div></li>
</ol>
</div></li>
<li id="A2.I3.i9" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">9.</span> 
<div id="A2.I3.i9.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A2.I3.i9.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.I3.i9.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Diffusions on LQG (Liouville Brownian motion)</span></p>
<ol id="A2.I3.i9.I1" class="ltx_enumerate">
<li id="A2.I3.i9.I1.ix1" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">i.</span> 
<div id="A2.I3.i9.I1.ix1.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A2.I3.i9.I1.ix1.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><em id="A2.I3.i9.I1.ix1.p1.1.1" class="ltx_emph ltx_font_italic">Central concept:</em> Brownian motion associated to the random Riemannian metric <math id="A2.I3.i9.I1.ix1.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="e^{\gamma h}(dx^{2}+dy^{2})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msup><mi>e</mi><mrow><mi>γ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>h</mi></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>x</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>y</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">e^{\gamma h}(dx^{2}+dy^{2})</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>
</div></li>
<li id="A2.I3.i9.I1.ix2" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">ii.</span> 
<div id="A2.I3.i9.I1.ix2.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A2.I3.i9.I1.ix2.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><em id="A2.I3.i9.I1.ix2.p1.1.1" class="ltx_emph ltx_font_italic">Foundational result:</em> Construction of Liouville Brownian motion as a Feller diffusion with <math id="A2.I3.i9.I1.ix2.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mu_{h}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>μ</mi><mi>h</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mu_{h}</annotation></semantics></math> as invariant measure for all <math id="A2.I3.i9.I1.ix2.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\gamma&lt;2" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>γ</mi><mo>&lt;</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\gamma&lt;2</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>
</div></li>
</ol>
</div></li>
</ol>
</div>
<div id="A2.SS1.SSS1.Px2.p5" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A2.SS1.SSS1.Px2.p5.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.SS1.SSS1.Px2.p5.1.1" class="ltx_text">If you want, I can turn this into a one-page LaTeX handout with short references and the <math id="A2.SS1.SSS1.Px2.p5.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(\gamma,\kappa)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>γ</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>κ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(\gamma,\kappa)</annotation></semantics></math> dictionary summarized.</span></p>
</div>
<div id="A2.SS1.SSS1.Px2.p6" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A2.SS1.SSS1.Px2.p6.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.SS1.SSS1.Px2.p6.1.1" class="ltx_text">∎</span></p>
</div>
</div>
<div id="A2.SS1.SSS1.Px2.2" class="ltx_proof">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_font_italic ltx_title_proof"><span id="A2.SS1.SSS1.Px2.2.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Standard Solution</span>.</h6>
<div id="A2.SS1.SSS1.Px2.p7" class="ltx_para">
<ol id="A2.I4" class="ltx_enumerate">
<li id="A2.I4.i1" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">1.</span> 
<div id="A2.I4.i1.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A2.I4.i1.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.I4.i1.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">GMC &amp; the LQG measure</span></p>
<ol id="A2.I4.i1.I1" class="ltx_enumerate">
<li id="A2.I4.i1.I1.ix1" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">i.</span> 
<div id="A2.I4.i1.I1.ix1.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A2.I4.i1.I1.ix1.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><em id="A2.I4.i1.I1.ix1.p1.1.1" class="ltx_emph ltx_font_italic">Concept:</em> The <math id="A2.I4.i1.I1.ix1.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\gamma" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>γ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\gamma</annotation></semantics></math>-LQG area measure <math id="A2.I4.i1.I1.ix1.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mu_{h}:=e^{\gamma h}\,dx\,dy" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>μ</mi><mi>h</mi></msub><mo>:=</mo><mrow><msup><mi>e</mi><mrow><mi>γ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>h</mi></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>d</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>x</mi><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>d</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>y</mi></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mu_{h}:=e^{\gamma h}\,dx\,dy</annotation></semantics></math> from a GFF via Gaussian multiplicative chaos.</p>
</div></li>
<li id="A2.I4.i1.I1.ix2" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">ii.</span> 
<div id="A2.I4.i1.I1.ix2.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A2.I4.i1.I1.ix2.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><em id="A2.I4.i1.I1.ix2.p1.1.1" class="ltx_emph ltx_font_italic">Theorem:</em>the LQG measure is well-defined and obeys the conformal coordinate-change rule for <math id="A2.I4.i1.I1.ix2.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\gamma\in(0,2)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>γ</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>2</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\gamma\in(0,2)</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>
</div></li>
</ol>
</div></li>
<li id="A2.I4.i2" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">2.</span> 
<div id="A2.I4.i2.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A2.I4.i2.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.I4.i2.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Quantum surfaces &amp; SLE welding</span></p>
<ol id="A2.I4.i2.I1" class="ltx_enumerate">
<li id="A2.I4.i2.I1.ix1" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">i.</span> 
<div id="A2.I4.i2.I1.ix1.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A2.I4.i2.I1.ix1.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><em id="A2.I4.i2.I1.ix1.p1.1.1" class="ltx_emph ltx_font_italic">Concept:</em> Quantum disks/spheres/wedges/cones as equivalence classes of <math id="A2.I4.i2.I1.ix1.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(D,h)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>D</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>h</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(D,h)</annotation></semantics></math> modulo additive constants and conformal maps; boundary length comes from LQG.</p>
</div></li>
<li id="A2.I4.i2.I1.ix2" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">ii.</span> 
<div id="A2.I4.i2.I1.ix2.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A2.I4.i2.I1.ix2.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><em id="A2.I4.i2.I1.ix2.p1.1.1" class="ltx_emph ltx_font_italic">Theorem:</em> (Quantum zipper / conformal welding) Welding LQG boundaries by quantum length produces SLE interfaces with <math id="A2.I4.i2.I1.ix2.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\kappa=\gamma^{2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>κ</mi><mo>=</mo><msup><mi>γ</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\kappa=\gamma^{2}</annotation></semantics></math> (and space-filling <math id="A2.I4.i2.I1.ix2.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\kappa^{\prime}=16/\gamma^{2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msup><mi>κ</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo>=</mo><mrow><mn>16</mn><mo>/</mo><msup><mi>γ</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\kappa^{\prime}=16/\gamma^{2}</annotation></semantics></math>), with precise conformal-covariance and symmetry.</p>
</div></li>
</ol>
</div></li>
<li id="A2.I4.i3" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">3.</span> 
<div id="A2.I4.i3.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A2.I4.i3.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.I4.i3.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Mating-of-trees / peanosphere</span></p>
<ol id="A2.I4.i3.I1" class="ltx_enumerate">
<li id="A2.I4.i3.I1.ix1" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">i.</span> 
<div id="A2.I4.i3.I1.ix1.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A2.I4.i3.I1.ix1.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><em id="A2.I4.i3.I1.ix1.p1.1.1" class="ltx_emph ltx_font_italic">Concept:</em> Encode an LQG surface decorated by a space-filling SLE as a correlated 2D Brownian motion (a “CRT–CRT” mating).</p>
</div></li>
<li id="A2.I4.i3.I1.ix2" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">ii.</span> 
<div id="A2.I4.i3.I1.ix2.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A2.I4.i3.I1.ix2.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><em id="A2.I4.i3.I1.ix2.p1.1.1" class="ltx_emph ltx_font_italic">Theorem:</em> (DMS mating-of-trees) <math id="A2.I4.i3.I1.ix2.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\gamma" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>γ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\gamma</annotation></semantics></math>-LQG with SLE<math id="A2.I4.i3.I1.ix2.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{}_{\kappa^{\prime}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mrow></mrow><msup><mi>κ</mi><mo>′</mo></msup></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{}_{\kappa^{\prime}}</annotation></semantics></math> decoration has a canonical Brownian encoding that determines the surface and curve, and conversely.</p>
</div></li>
</ol>
</div></li>
<li id="A2.I4.i4" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">4.</span> 
<div id="A2.I4.i4.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A2.I4.i4.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.I4.i4.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Metric structure (QLE) &amp; Brownian map</span></p>
<ol id="A2.I4.i4.I1" class="ltx_enumerate">
<li id="A2.I4.i4.I1.ix1" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">i.</span> 
<div id="A2.I4.i4.I1.ix1.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A2.I4.i4.I1.ix1.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><em id="A2.I4.i4.I1.ix1.p1.1.1" class="ltx_emph ltx_font_italic">Concept:</em> The LQG metric <math id="A2.I4.i4.I1.ix1.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="D_{h}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>D</mi><mi>h</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">D_{h}</annotation></semantics></math> built via Quantum Loewner Evolution / Liouville FPP, yielding a random metric-measure surface.</p>
</div></li>
<li id="A2.I4.i4.I1.ix2" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">ii.</span> 
<div id="A2.I4.i4.I1.ix2.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A2.I4.i4.I1.ix2.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><em id="A2.I4.i4.I1.ix2.p1.1.1" class="ltx_emph ltx_font_italic">Theorem:</em> (Existence/uniqueness &amp; <math id="A2.I4.i4.I1.ix2.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\sqrt{8/3}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msqrt><mrow><mn>8</mn><mo>/</mo><mn>3</mn></mrow></msqrt><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\sqrt{8/3}</annotation></semantics></math> identification) The <math id="A2.I4.i4.I1.ix2.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\gamma" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>γ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\gamma</annotation></semantics></math>-LQG metric exists and is unique for <math id="A2.I4.i4.I1.ix2.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\gamma\in(0,2)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>γ</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>2</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\gamma\in(0,2)</annotation></semantics></math>; at <math id="A2.I4.i4.I1.ix2.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\gamma=\sqrt{8/3}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>γ</mi><mo>=</mo><msqrt><mrow><mn>8</mn><mo>/</mo><mn>3</mn></mrow></msqrt></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\gamma=\sqrt{8/3}</annotation></semantics></math>, the resulting metric-measure sphere agrees with the Brownian map.</p>
</div></li>
</ol>
</div></li>
</ol>
</div>
<div id="A2.SS1.SSS1.Px2.p8" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A2.SS1.SSS1.Px2.p8.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.SS1.SSS1.Px2.p8.1.1" class="ltx_text">∎</span></p>
</div>
</div>
<div id="A2.SS1.SSS1.Px2.p9" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent"><span class="ltx_inline-block"><svg id="A2.SS1.SSS1.Px2.p9.pic1" class="ltx_picture" height="54.25" overflow="visible" version="1.1" viewBox="0 0 429.64 54.25" width="429.64"><g style="--ltx-stroke-color:#000000;--ltx-fill-color:#000000;" fill="#000000" stroke="#000000" stroke-width="0.4pt" transform="translate(0,54.25) matrix(1 0 0 -1 0 0)"><g style="--ltx-fill-color:#4D4D4D;" fill="#4D4D4D" fill-opacity="1.0"><path style="stroke:none" d="M 0 4.63 L 0 49.62 C 0 52.18 2.07 54.25 4.63 54.25 L 425.01 54.25 C 427.56 54.25 429.64 52.18 429.64 49.62 L 429.64 4.63 C 429.64 2.07 427.56 0 425.01 0 L 4.63 0 C 2.07 0 0 2.07 0 4.63 Z"></path></g><g style="--ltx-fill-color:#F9F9F9;" fill="#F9F9F9" fill-opacity="1.0"><path style="stroke:none" d="M 0.69 4.63 L 0.69 35.38 L 428.94 35.38 L 428.94 4.63 C 428.94 2.45 427.18 0.69 425.01 0.69 L 4.63 0.69 C 2.45 0.69 0.69 2.45 0.69 4.63 Z"></path></g><g fill-opacity="1.0" transform="matrix(1.0 0.0 0.0 1.0 20.38 40.01)"><foreignObject style="--ltx-fo-width:24.44em;--ltx-fo-height:0.69em;--ltx-fo-depth:0em;font-size:10pt;" height="9.61" overflow="visible" transform="matrix(1 0 0 -1 0 9.61)" width="338.18"><span class="ltx_foreignobject_container"><span class="ltx_foreignobject_content">
<span id="A2.SS1.SSS1.Px2.p9.pic1.1" class="ltx_inline-block ltx_minipage ltx_align_bottom" style="width:24.44em;">
<span id="A2.SS1.SSS1.Px2.p9.pic1.1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.SS1.SSS1.Px2.p9.pic1.1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold" style="--ltx-fg-color:#FFFFFF;">Rubric</span></span>
</span></span></span></foreignObject></g><g fill-opacity="1.0" transform="matrix(1.0 0.0 0.0 1.0 20.38 15.27)"><foreignObject style="--ltx-fo-width:33.06em;--ltx-fo-height:0.6em;--ltx-fo-depth:0.2em;font-size:10pt;" height="11.07" overflow="visible" transform="matrix(1 0 0 -1 0 8.3)" width="457.46"><span class="ltx_foreignobject_container"><span class="ltx_foreignobject_content">
<span id="A2.SS1.SSS1.Px2.p9.pic1.2" class="ltx_inline-block ltx_minipage ltx_align_bottom" style="width:33.06em;">
<span id="A2.SS1.SSS1.Px2.p9.pic1.2.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.SS1.SSS1.Px2.p9.pic1.2.1.1" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:80%;--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">Got 3/3 if it correctly lists at least three points.</span></span>
</span></span></span></foreignObject></g></g></svg></span>
</div>
<div id="A2.SS1.SSS1.Px2.p10" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent"><span class="ltx_inline-block"><svg id="A2.SS1.SSS1.Px2.p10.pic1" class="ltx_picture" height="54.13" overflow="visible" version="1.1" viewBox="0 0 429.64 54.13" width="429.64"><g style="--ltx-stroke-color:#000000;--ltx-fill-color:#000000;" fill="#000000" stroke="#000000" stroke-width="0.4pt" transform="translate(0,54.13) matrix(1 0 0 -1 0 0)"><g style="--ltx-fill-color:#5A996B;" fill="#5A996B" fill-opacity="1.0"><path style="stroke:none" d="M 0 4.63 L 0 49.51 C 0 52.06 2.07 54.13 4.63 54.13 L 425.01 54.13 C 427.56 54.13 429.64 52.06 429.64 49.51 L 429.64 4.63 C 429.64 2.07 427.56 0 425.01 0 L 4.63 0 C 2.07 0 0 2.07 0 4.63 Z"></path></g><g style="--ltx-fill-color:#F6FFF9;" fill="#F6FFF9" fill-opacity="1.0"><path style="stroke:none" d="M 0.69 4.63 L 0.69 35.38 L 428.94 35.38 L 428.94 4.63 C 428.94 2.45 427.18 0.69 425.01 0.69 L 4.63 0.69 C 2.45 0.69 0.69 2.45 0.69 4.63 Z"></path></g><g fill-opacity="1.0" transform="matrix(1.0 0.0 0.0 1.0 20.38 40.01)"><foreignObject style="--ltx-fo-width:24.44em;--ltx-fo-height:0.69em;--ltx-fo-depth:0em;font-size:10pt;" height="9.49" overflow="visible" transform="matrix(1 0 0 -1 0 9.49)" width="338.18"><span class="ltx_foreignobject_container"><span class="ltx_foreignobject_content">
<span id="A2.SS1.SSS1.Px2.p10.pic1.1" class="ltx_inline-block ltx_minipage ltx_align_bottom" style="width:24.44em;">
<span id="A2.SS1.SSS1.Px2.p10.pic1.1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.SS1.SSS1.Px2.p10.pic1.1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold" style="--ltx-fg-color:#FFFFFF;">Score</span></span>
</span></span></span></foreignObject></g><g fill-opacity="1.0" transform="matrix(1.0 0.0 0.0 1.0 20.38 15.27)"><foreignObject style="--ltx-fo-width:33.06em;--ltx-fo-height:0.6em;--ltx-fo-depth:0.2em;font-size:10pt;" height="11.07" overflow="visible" transform="matrix(1 0 0 -1 0 8.3)" width="457.46"><span class="ltx_foreignobject_container"><span class="ltx_foreignobject_content">
<span id="A2.SS1.SSS1.Px2.p10.pic1.2" class="ltx_inline-block ltx_minipage ltx_align_bottom" style="width:33.06em;">
<span id="A2.SS1.SSS1.Px2.p10.pic1.2.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.SS1.SSS1.Px2.p10.pic1.2.1.1" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:80%;--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">3/3</span></span>
</span></span></span></foreignObject></g></g></svg></span>
</div>
<div id="A2.SS1.SSS1.Px2.p11" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent"><span class="ltx_inline-block"><svg id="A2.SS1.SSS1.Px2.p11.pic1" class="ltx_picture" height="69.62" overflow="visible" version="1.1" viewBox="0 0 429.64 69.62" width="429.64"><g style="--ltx-stroke-color:#000000;--ltx-fill-color:#000000;" fill="#000000" stroke="#000000" stroke-width="0.4pt" transform="translate(0,69.62) matrix(1 0 0 -1 0 0)"><g style="--ltx-fill-color:#B33674;" fill="#B33674" fill-opacity="1.0"><path style="stroke:none" d="M 0 4.63 L 0 65 C 0 67.55 2.07 69.62 4.63 69.62 L 425.01 69.62 C 427.56 69.62 429.64 67.55 429.64 65 L 429.64 4.63 C 429.64 2.07 427.56 0 425.01 0 L 4.63 0 C 2.07 0 0 2.07 0 4.63 Z"></path></g><g style="--ltx-fill-color:#FFF2F9;" fill="#FFF2F9" fill-opacity="1.0"><path style="stroke:none" d="M 0.69 4.63 L 0.69 50.76 L 428.94 50.76 L 428.94 4.63 C 428.94 2.45 427.18 0.69 425.01 0.69 L 4.63 0.69 C 2.45 0.69 0.69 2.45 0.69 4.63 Z"></path></g><g fill-opacity="1.0" transform="matrix(1.0 0.0 0.0 1.0 20.38 55.39)"><foreignObject style="--ltx-fo-width:24.44em;--ltx-fo-height:0.69em;--ltx-fo-depth:0em;font-size:10pt;" height="9.61" overflow="visible" transform="matrix(1 0 0 -1 0 9.61)" width="338.18"><span class="ltx_foreignobject_container"><span class="ltx_foreignobject_content">
<span id="A2.SS1.SSS1.Px2.p11.pic1.1" class="ltx_inline-block ltx_minipage ltx_align_bottom" style="width:24.44em;">
<span id="A2.SS1.SSS1.Px2.p11.pic1.1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.SS1.SSS1.Px2.p11.pic1.1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold" style="--ltx-fg-color:#FFFFFF;">Evaluation</span></span>
</span></span></span></foreignObject></g><g fill-opacity="1.0" transform="matrix(1.0 0.0 0.0 1.0 20.38 14.66)"><foreignObject style="--ltx-fo-width:33.06em;--ltx-fo-height:1.76em;--ltx-fo-depth:0.16em;font-size:10pt;" height="26.44" overflow="visible" transform="matrix(1 0 0 -1 0 24.29)" width="457.46"><span class="ltx_foreignobject_container"><span class="ltx_foreignobject_content">
<span id="A2.SS1.SSS1.Px2.p11.pic1.2" class="ltx_inline-block ltx_minipage ltx_align_bottom" style="width:33.06em;">
<span id="A2.SS1.SSS1.Px2.p11.pic1.2.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.SS1.SSS1.Px2.p11.pic1.2.1.1" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:80%;--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">It correctly identifies at least 3 major SLE subfields, each with a central concept and a foundational result.</span></span>
</span></span></span></foreignObject></g></g></svg></span>
</div>
</section>
</section>
<section id="A2.SS1.SSS2" class="ltx_subsubsection">
<h4 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsubsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsubsection">(b) </span>Key Mathematical Statements</h4>

<section id="A2.SS1.SSS2.Px1" class="ltx_paragraph">
<h5 class="ltx_title ltx_title_paragraph" style="--ltx-fg-color:#FF0000;">Problem 1b1 </h5>

<div id="A2.SS1.SSS2.Px1.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A2.SS1.SSS2.Px1.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.SS1.SSS2.Px1.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text"></span>
<br class="ltx_break" style="--ltx-break-space:-10.0pt;"></p>
</div>
<div id="A2.SS1.SSS2.Px1.p2" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent"><span class="ltx_inline-block"><svg id="A2.SS1.SSS2.Px1.p2.pic1" class="ltx_picture" height="227.92" overflow="visible" version="1.1" viewBox="0 0 429.64 227.92" width="429.64"><g style="--ltx-stroke-color:#000000;--ltx-fill-color:#000000;" fill="#000000" stroke="#000000" stroke-width="0.4pt" transform="translate(0,227.92) matrix(1 0 0 -1 0 0)"><g style="--ltx-fill-color:#3D6666;" fill="#3D6666" fill-opacity="1.0"><path style="stroke:none" d="M 0 4.63 L 0 223.3 C 0 225.85 2.07 227.92 4.63 227.92 L 425.01 227.92 C 427.56 227.92 429.64 225.85 429.64 223.3 L 429.64 4.63 C 429.64 2.07 427.56 0 425.01 0 L 4.63 0 C 2.07 0 0 2.07 0 4.63 Z"></path></g><g style="--ltx-fill-color:#F9F9F9;" fill="#F9F9F9" fill-opacity="1.0"><path style="stroke:none" d="M 0.69 4.63 L 0.69 209.06 L 428.94 209.06 L 428.94 4.63 C 428.94 2.45 427.18 0.69 425.01 0.69 L 4.63 0.69 C 2.45 0.69 0.69 2.45 0.69 4.63 Z"></path></g><g fill-opacity="1.0" transform="matrix(1.0 0.0 0.0 1.0 20.38 213.69)"><foreignObject style="--ltx-fo-width:24.44em;--ltx-fo-height:0.69em;--ltx-fo-depth:0em;font-size:10pt;" height="9.61" overflow="visible" transform="matrix(1 0 0 -1 0 9.61)" width="338.18"><span class="ltx_foreignobject_container"><span class="ltx_foreignobject_content">
<span id="A2.SS1.SSS2.Px1.p2.pic1.1" class="ltx_inline-block ltx_minipage ltx_align_bottom" style="width:24.44em;">
<span id="A2.SS1.SSS2.Px1.p2.pic1.1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.SS1.SSS2.Px1.p2.pic1.1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold" style="--ltx-fg-color:#FFFFFF;">Problem</span></span>
</span></span></span></foreignObject></g><g fill-opacity="1.0" transform="matrix(1.0 0.0 0.0 1.0 20.38 14.66)"><foreignObject style="--ltx-fo-width:32.01em;--ltx-fo-height:13.2em;--ltx-fo-depth:0.16em;font-size:10pt;" height="184.75" overflow="visible" transform="matrix(1 0 0 -1 0 182.59)" width="442.93"><span class="ltx_foreignobject_container"><span class="ltx_foreignobject_content">
<span id="A2.SS1.SSS2.Px1.p2.pic1.2" class="ltx_inline-block ltx_minipage ltx_align_bottom" style="width:32.01em;">
<span id="A2.SS1.SSS2.Px1.p2.pic1.2.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.SS1.SSS2.Px1.p2.pic1.2.1.1" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:80%;--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">Schramm–Loewner Evolution (SLE) is a vibrant field in modern probability theory. Please address the following two parts:</span></span>
<span id="A2.I5" class="ltx_enumerate">
<span id="A2.I5.i1" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">1.</span> 
<span id="A2.I5.i1.p1" class="ltx_para">
<span id="A2.I5.i1.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.I5.i1.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:80%;--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">Provide the precise definition of SLE, emphasizing its construction via the Loewner equation driven by a random function </span><math id="A2.I5.i1.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="W_{t}=\sqrt{\kappa}B_{t}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" mathsize="0.800em">W</mi><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" mathsize="0.800em">t</mi></msub><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" mathsize="0.800em">=</mo><mrow><msqrt style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000"><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" mathsize="0.800em">κ</mi></msqrt><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" mathsize="0.800em">B</mi><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" mathsize="0.800em">t</mi></msub></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">W_{t}=\sqrt{\kappa}B_{t}</annotation></semantics></math><span id="A2.I5.i1.p1.1.2" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:80%;--ltx-fg-color:#000000;"> where </span><math id="A2.I5.i1.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="B_{t}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" mathsize="0.800em">B</mi><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" mathsize="0.800em">t</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">B_{t}</annotation></semantics></math><span id="A2.I5.i1.p1.1.3" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:80%;--ltx-fg-color:#000000;"> is the standard Brownian motion.</span></span>
</span></span>
<span id="A2.I5.i2" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">2.</span> 
<span id="A2.I5.i2.p1" class="ltx_para">
<span id="A2.I5.i2.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.I5.i2.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:80%;--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">Please state the transformation law of the driving functions of Loewner chain under conformal Maps.</span></span>
</span>
<span id="A2.I5.i2.p2" class="ltx_para"><span class="ltx_inline-block"><svg id="A2.I5.i2.p2.pic1" class="ltx_picture" color="#FF0000" height="18.24" overflow="visible" style="vertical-align:-4.1px" version="1.1" viewBox="0 0 18.24 18.24" width="18.24"><g style="--ltx-stroke-color:#FF0000;--ltx-fill-color:#FF0000;" fill="#FF0000" stroke="#FF0000" stroke-width="1.8pt" transform="translate(0,18.24) matrix(1 0 0 -1 0 0) translate(1.25,0) translate(0,1.25)"><path style="fill:none" d="M 0 0 L 15.75 15.75 M 0 15.75 L 15.75 0"></path></g></svg></span>
<span id="A2.I5.i2.p2.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.I5.i2.p2.1.1" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:80%;--ltx-fg-color:#FF0000;">GPT-5 thinking failed</span></span>
</span></span>
</span>
<span id="A2.SS1.SSS2.Px1.p2.pic1.2.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.SS1.SSS2.Px1.p2.pic1.2.2.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic" style="font-size:80%;--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">Proposed by Jiaxin Zhang</span></span>
</span></span></span></foreignObject></g></g></svg></span>
</div>
<div id="A2.SS1.SSS2.Px1.1" class="ltx_proof">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_font_italic ltx_title_proof"><span id="A2.SS1.SSS2.Px1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Response of GPT-5-thinking</span>.</h6>
<div id="A2.SS1.SSS2.Px1.p3" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A2.SS1.SSS2.Px1.p3.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.SS1.SSS2.Px1.p3.1.1" class="ltx_text">Here’s a clean, standard formulation that matches the way SLE is defined and used in the literature.</span></p>
</div>
<div id="A2.SS1.SSS2.Px1.p4" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A2.SS1.SSS2.Px1.p4.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.SS1.SSS2.Px1.p4.1.1" class="ltx_text">1) Definition of <math id="A2.SS1.SSS2.Px1.p4.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathrm{SLE}_{\kappa}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>SLE</mi><mi>κ</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathrm{SLE}_{\kappa}</annotation></semantics></math> via Loewner’s equation</span></p>
</div>
<div id="A2.SS1.SSS2.Px1.p5" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A2.SS1.SSS2.Px1.p5.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.SS1.SSS2.Px1.p5.1.1" class="ltx_text">Chordal case (from <math id="A2.SS1.SSS2.Px1.p5.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mn>0</mn><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">0</annotation></semantics></math> to <math id="A2.SS1.SSS2.Px1.p5.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\infty" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi mathvariant="normal">∞</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\infty</annotation></semantics></math> in <math id="A2.SS1.SSS2.Px1.p5.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbb{H}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>ℍ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbb{H}</annotation></semantics></math>)</span></p>
</div>
<div id="A2.SS1.SSS2.Px1.p6" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A2.SS1.SSS2.Px1.p6.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.SS1.SSS2.Px1.p6.1.1" class="ltx_text">Let <math id="A2.SS1.SSS2.Px1.p6.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="W:[0,\infty)\to\mathbb{R}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>W</mi><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">∞</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><mi>ℝ</mi></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">W:[0,\infty)\to\mathbb{R}</annotation></semantics></math> be a continuous function (the *driving function*). For each <math id="A2.SS1.SSS2.Px1.p6.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="z\in\overline{\mathbb{H}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>z</mi><mo>∈</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>ℍ</mi><mo stretchy="true">¯</mo></mover></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">z\in\overline{\mathbb{H}}</annotation></semantics></math>, define <math id="A2.SS1.SSS2.Px1.p6.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="g_{t}(z)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>g</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>z</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">g_{t}(z)</annotation></semantics></math> as the maximal solution (in <math id="A2.SS1.SSS2.Px1.p6.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="t" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>t</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">t</annotation></semantics></math>) to the Loewner ODE</span></p>
</div>
<div id="A2.SS1.SSS2.Px1.p7" class="ltx_para">
<table id="A2.Ex17" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A2.Ex17.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\partial_{t}g_{t}(z)=\frac{2}{g_{t}(z)-W_{t}},\qquad g_{0}(z)=z," display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mrow><msub><mo>∂</mo><mi>t</mi></msub><mrow><msub><mi>g</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>z</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mn>2</mn><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>g</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>z</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>W</mi><mi>t</mi></msub></mrow></mfrac></mrow><mo rspace="2.167em">,</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>g</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>z</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mi>z</mi></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\partial_{t}g_{t}(z)=\frac{2}{g_{t}(z)-W_{t}},\qquad g_{0}(z)=z,</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
<div id="A2.SS1.SSS2.Px1.p8" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A2.SS1.SSS2.Px1.p8.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.SS1.SSS2.Px1.p8.1.1" class="ltx_text">with swallowing time</span></p>
</div>
<div id="A2.SS1.SSS2.Px1.p9" class="ltx_para">
<table id="A2.Ex18" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A2.Ex18.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\tau(z):=\sup\{\,t\geq 0:\ \min_{s\in[0,t]}|g_{s}(z)-W_{s}|&gt;0\,\}." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>τ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>z</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.1389em">:=</mo><mrow><mo lspace="0.1389em" movablelimits="false" rspace="0em">sup</mo><mrow><mo rspace="0.170em" stretchy="false">{</mo><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>≥</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.778em">:</mo><mrow><mrow><munder><mi>min</mi><mrow><mi>s</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow></munder><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>g</mi><mi>s</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>z</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>W</mi><mi>s</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>&gt;</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><mo lspace="0.170em" stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\tau(z):=\sup\{\,t\geq 0:\ \min_{s\in[0,t]}|g_{s}(z)-W_{s}|&gt;0\,\}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
<div id="A2.SS1.SSS2.Px1.p10" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A2.SS1.SSS2.Px1.p10.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.SS1.SSS2.Px1.p10.1.1" class="ltx_text">Set the *hulls* <math id="A2.SS1.SSS2.Px1.p10.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="K_{t}:=\{z\in\overline{\mathbb{H}}:\ \tau(z)\leq t\}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>K</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo>:=</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mrow><mi>z</mi><mo>∈</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>ℍ</mi><mo stretchy="true">¯</mo></mover></mrow><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.778em">:</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>τ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>z</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">K_{t}:=\{z\in\overline{\mathbb{H}}:\ \tau(z)\leq t\}</annotation></semantics></math> and note that</span></p>
</div>
<div id="A2.SS1.SSS2.Px1.p11" class="ltx_para">
<table id="A2.Ex19" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A2.Ex19.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="g_{t}:\mathbb{H}\setminus K_{t}\longrightarrow\mathbb{H}" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>g</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>ℍ</mi><mo>∖</mo><msub><mi>K</mi><mi>t</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟶</mo><mi>ℍ</mi></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">g_{t}:\mathbb{H}\setminus K_{t}\longrightarrow\mathbb{H}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
<div id="A2.SS1.SSS2.Px1.p12" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A2.SS1.SSS2.Px1.p12.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.SS1.SSS2.Px1.p12.1.1" class="ltx_text">is conformal and satisfies the hydrodynamic normalization</span></p>
</div>
<div id="A2.SS1.SSS2.Px1.p13" class="ltx_para">
<table id="A2.Ex20" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A2.Ex20.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="g_{t}(z)=z+\frac{2t}{z}+O\!\left(\frac{1}{z^{2}}\right)\quad\text{as }z\to\infty." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>g</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>z</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>z</mi><mo>+</mo><mfrac><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow><mi>z</mi></mfrac><mo>+</mo><mrow><mpadded style="width:0.621em;" width="0.621em"><mi>O</mi></mpadded><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mfrac><mn>1</mn><msup><mi>z</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></mfrac><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mspace style="width:1em;" width="1em"></mspace><mrow><mrow><mtext>as </mtext><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>z</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">∞</mi></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">g_{t}(z)=z+\frac{2t}{z}+O\!\left(\frac{1}{z^{2}}\right)\quad\text{as }z\to\infty.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
<div id="A2.SS1.SSS2.Px1.p14" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A2.SS1.SSS2.Px1.p14.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.SS1.SSS2.Px1.p14.1.1" class="ltx_text">(Equivalently, <math id="A2.SS1.SSS2.Px1.p14.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathrm{hcap}(K_{t})=2t" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>hcap</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>K</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathrm{hcap}(K_{t})=2t</annotation></semantics></math>.)</span></p>
</div>
<div id="A2.SS1.SSS2.Px1.p15" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A2.SS1.SSS2.Px1.p15.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.SS1.SSS2.Px1.p15.1.1" class="ltx_text">**Chordal <math id="A2.SS1.SSS2.Px1.p15.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathrm{SLE}_{\kappa}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>SLE</mi><mi>κ</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathrm{SLE}_{\kappa}</annotation></semantics></math>** is the random Loewner chain <math id="A2.SS1.SSS2.Px1.p15.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(K_{t})_{t\geq 0}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>K</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>≥</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(K_{t})_{t\geq 0}</annotation></semantics></math> (equivalently, <math id="A2.SS1.SSS2.Px1.p15.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(g_{t})_{t\geq 0}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>g</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>≥</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(g_{t})_{t\geq 0}</annotation></semantics></math>) obtained by taking the driving function to be</span></p>
</div>
<div id="A2.SS1.SSS2.Px1.p16" class="ltx_para">
<table id="A2.Ex21" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A2.Ex21.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="W_{t}=\sqrt{\kappa}\,B_{t},\qquad t\geq 0," display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>W</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><msqrt><mi>κ</mi></msqrt><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>B</mi><mi>t</mi></msub></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="2.167em">,</mo><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>≥</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">W_{t}=\sqrt{\kappa}\,B_{t},\qquad t\geq 0,</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
<div id="A2.SS1.SSS2.Px1.p17" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A2.SS1.SSS2.Px1.p17.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.SS1.SSS2.Px1.p17.1.1" class="ltx_text">where <math id="A2.SS1.SSS2.Px1.p17.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(B_{t})_{t\geq 0}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>B</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>≥</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(B_{t})_{t\geq 0}</annotation></semantics></math> is standard one-dimensional Brownian motion with <math id="A2.SS1.SSS2.Px1.p17.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="B_{0}=0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>B</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">B_{0}=0</annotation></semantics></math>.
We then say “<math id="A2.SS1.SSS2.Px1.p17.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(K_{t})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>K</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(K_{t})</annotation></semantics></math> is chordal <math id="A2.SS1.SSS2.Px1.p17.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathrm{SLE}_{\kappa}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>SLE</mi><mi>κ</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathrm{SLE}_{\kappa}</annotation></semantics></math> in <math id="A2.SS1.SSS2.Px1.p17.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbb{H}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>ℍ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbb{H}</annotation></semantics></math> from <math id="A2.SS1.SSS2.Px1.p17.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mn>0</mn><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">0</annotation></semantics></math> to <math id="A2.SS1.SSS2.Px1.p17.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\infty" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi mathvariant="normal">∞</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\infty</annotation></semantics></math>.”</span></p>
</div>
<div id="A2.SS1.SSS2.Px1.p18" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A2.SS1.SSS2.Px1.p18.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.SS1.SSS2.Px1.p18.1.1" class="ltx_text">*(Remarks: One often also speaks of the random curve <math id="A2.SS1.SSS2.Px1.p18.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\gamma" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>γ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\gamma</annotation></semantics></math> — the Loewner trace — whose filled-in hull is <math id="A2.SS1.SSS2.Px1.p18.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="K_{t}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>K</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">K_{t}</annotation></semantics></math>; this exists for all <math id="A2.SS1.SSS2.Px1.p18.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\kappa" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>κ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\kappa</annotation></semantics></math> and is simple for <math id="A2.SS1.SSS2.Px1.p18.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\kappa\leq 4" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>κ</mi><mo>≤</mo><mn>4</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\kappa\leq 4</annotation></semantics></math>, etc., but the definition above is in terms of the Loewner chain.)*</span></p>
</div>
<div id="A2.SS1.SSS2.Px1.p19" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A2.SS1.SSS2.Px1.p19.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.SS1.SSS2.Px1.p19.1.1" class="ltx_text">Radial case (from <math id="A2.SS1.SSS2.Px1.p19.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mn>1</mn><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">1</annotation></semantics></math> to <math id="A2.SS1.SSS2.Px1.p19.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mn>0</mn><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">0</annotation></semantics></math> in <math id="A2.SS1.SSS2.Px1.p19.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbb{D}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>𝔻</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbb{D}</annotation></semantics></math>)</span></p>
</div>
<div id="A2.SS1.SSS2.Px1.p20" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A2.SS1.SSS2.Px1.p20.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.SS1.SSS2.Px1.p20.1.1" class="ltx_text">Let <math id="A2.SS1.SSS2.Px1.p20.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="W:[0,\infty)\to\mathbb{R}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>W</mi><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">∞</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><mi>ℝ</mi></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">W:[0,\infty)\to\mathbb{R}</annotation></semantics></math> be continuous and define <math id="A2.SS1.SSS2.Px1.p20.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="g_{t}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>g</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">g_{t}</annotation></semantics></math> by the *radial* Loewner ODE</span></p>
</div>
<div id="A2.SS1.SSS2.Px1.p21" class="ltx_para">
<table id="A2.Ex22" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A2.Ex22.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\partial_{t}g_{t}(z)\;=\;-\,g_{t}(z)\,\frac{e^{iW_{t}}+g_{t}(z)}{e^{iW_{t}}-g_{t}(z)},\qquad g_{0}(z)=z," display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mrow><msub><mo>∂</mo><mi>t</mi></msub><mrow><msub><mi>g</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>z</mi><mo rspace="0.280em" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.558em">=</mo><mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><msub><mi>g</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>z</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mfrac><mrow><msup><mi>e</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>W</mi><mi>t</mi></msub></mrow></msup><mo>+</mo><mrow><msub><mi>g</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>z</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mrow><msup><mi>e</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>W</mi><mi>t</mi></msub></mrow></msup><mo>−</mo><mrow><msub><mi>g</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>z</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mfrac></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="2.167em">,</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>g</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>z</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mi>z</mi></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\partial_{t}g_{t}(z)\;=\;-\,g_{t}(z)\,\frac{e^{iW_{t}}+g_{t}(z)}{e^{iW_{t}}-g_{t}(z)},\qquad g_{0}(z)=z,</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
<div id="A2.SS1.SSS2.Px1.p22" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A2.SS1.SSS2.Px1.p22.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.SS1.SSS2.Px1.p22.1.1" class="ltx_text">with normalization <math id="A2.SS1.SSS2.Px1.p22.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="g_{t}(0)=0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>g</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>0</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">g_{t}(0)=0</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="A2.SS1.SSS2.Px1.p22.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="g_{t}^{\prime}(0)=e^{t}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msubsup><mi>g</mi><mi>t</mi><mo>′</mo></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>0</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><msup><mi>e</mi><mi>t</mi></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">g_{t}^{\prime}(0)=e^{t}</annotation></semantics></math>. For <math id="A2.SS1.SSS2.Px1.p22.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="W_{t}=\sqrt{\kappa}\,B_{t}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>W</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><msqrt><mi>κ</mi></msqrt><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>B</mi><mi>t</mi></msub></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">W_{t}=\sqrt{\kappa}\,B_{t}</annotation></semantics></math> this chain is **radial <math id="A2.SS1.SSS2.Px1.p22.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathrm{SLE}_{\kappa}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>SLE</mi><mi>κ</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathrm{SLE}_{\kappa}</annotation></semantics></math>** in <math id="A2.SS1.SSS2.Px1.p22.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbb{D}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>𝔻</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbb{D}</annotation></semantics></math> from <math id="A2.SS1.SSS2.Px1.p22.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mn>1</mn><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">1</annotation></semantics></math> to <math id="A2.SS1.SSS2.Px1.p22.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mn>0</mn><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">0</annotation></semantics></math>.</span></p>
</div>
<div id="A2.SS1.SSS2.Px1.p23" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A2.SS1.SSS2.Px1.p23.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.SS1.SSS2.Px1.p23.1.1" class="ltx_text">—</span></p>
</div>
<div id="A2.SS1.SSS2.Px1.p24" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A2.SS1.SSS2.Px1.p24.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.SS1.SSS2.Px1.p24.1.1" class="ltx_text">2) How driving functions transform under conformal maps</span></p>
</div>
<div id="A2.SS1.SSS2.Px1.p25" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A2.SS1.SSS2.Px1.p25.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.SS1.SSS2.Px1.p25.1.1" class="ltx_text">The transformation is most cleanly stated in *conformal coordinates adapted at each time*. Below is the standard chordal statement; the radial version is analogous (replace <math id="A2.SS1.SSS2.Px1.p25.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbb{H},\infty" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>ℍ</mi><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">∞</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbb{H},\infty</annotation></semantics></math> by the appropriate simply connected domain and interior target, and half-plane capacity by the relevant capacity).</span></p>
</div>
<div id="A2.SS1.SSS2.Px1.p26" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A2.SS1.SSS2.Px1.p26.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.SS1.SSS2.Px1.p26.1.1" class="ltx_text">General conformal covariance (chordal)</span></p>
</div>
<div id="A2.SS1.SSS2.Px1.p27" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A2.SS1.SSS2.Px1.p27.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.SS1.SSS2.Px1.p27.1.1" class="ltx_text">Let <math id="A2.SS1.SSS2.Px1.p27.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(g_{t})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>g</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(g_{t})</annotation></semantics></math> be a chordal Loewner chain in <math id="A2.SS1.SSS2.Px1.p27.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbb{H}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>ℍ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbb{H}</annotation></semantics></math> driven by a continuous <math id="A2.SS1.SSS2.Px1.p27.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="W_{t}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>W</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">W_{t}</annotation></semantics></math>, with hulls <math id="A2.SS1.SSS2.Px1.p27.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="K_{t}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>K</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">K_{t}</annotation></semantics></math>. Let <math id="A2.SS1.SSS2.Px1.p27.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\phi:\mathbb{H}\to\mathbb{H}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>ϕ</mi><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mrow><mi>ℍ</mi><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><mi>ℍ</mi></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\phi:\mathbb{H}\to\mathbb{H}</annotation></semantics></math> be conformal, and let <math id="A2.SS1.SSS2.Px1.p27.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\tilde{K}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mover accent="true"><mi>K</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\tilde{K}</annotation></semantics></math> be the image chain <math id="A2.SS1.SSS2.Px1.p27.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\tilde{K}_{u(t)}:=\phi(K_{t})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>K</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mrow><mi>u</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></msub><mo>:=</mo><mrow><mi>ϕ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>K</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\tilde{K}_{u(t)}:=\phi(K_{t})</annotation></semantics></math>. Denote by <math id="A2.SS1.SSS2.Px1.p27.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\tilde{g}_{u}:\mathbb{H}\setminus\tilde{K}_{u}\to\mathbb{H}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>g</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mi>u</mi></msub><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>ℍ</mi><mo>∖</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>K</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mi>u</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><mi>ℍ</mi></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\tilde{g}_{u}:\mathbb{H}\setminus\tilde{K}_{u}\to\mathbb{H}</annotation></semantics></math> the hydrodynamically normalized maps of the image chain. Define the *time-dependent conjugating map*</span></p>
</div>
<div id="A2.SS1.SSS2.Px1.p28" class="ltx_para">
<table id="A2.Ex23" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A2.Ex23.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\phi_{t}\ :=\ \tilde{g}_{u(t)}\circ\phi\circ g_{t}^{-1}:\ \mathbb{H}\longrightarrow\mathbb{H}." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>ϕ</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo lspace="0.778em" rspace="0.778em">:=</mo><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>g</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mrow><mi>u</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">∘</mo><mi>ϕ</mi><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">∘</mo><msubsup><mi>g</mi><mi>t</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msubsup></mrow><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.778em">:</mo><mrow><mi>ℍ</mi><mo stretchy="false">⟶</mo><mi>ℍ</mi></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\phi_{t}\ :=\ \tilde{g}_{u(t)}\circ\phi\circ g_{t}^{-1}:\ \mathbb{H}\longrightarrow\mathbb{H}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
<div id="A2.SS1.SSS2.Px1.p29" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A2.SS1.SSS2.Px1.p29.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.SS1.SSS2.Px1.p29.1.1" class="ltx_text">Then the image chain <math id="A2.SS1.SSS2.Px1.p29.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(\tilde{g}_{u})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>g</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mi>u</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(\tilde{g}_{u})</annotation></semantics></math> is again a chordal Loewner chain, driven by <math id="A2.SS1.SSS2.Px1.p29.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\tilde{W}_{u}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>W</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mi>u</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\tilde{W}_{u}</annotation></semantics></math> related to <math id="A2.SS1.SSS2.Px1.p29.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="W_{t}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>W</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">W_{t}</annotation></semantics></math> by</span></p>
</div>
<div id="A2.SS1.SSS2.Px1.p30" class="ltx_para">
<table id="A2.Ex24" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A2.Ex24.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\boxed{\quad\tilde{W}_{\,u(t)}\ =\ \phi_{t}\big(W_{t}\big),\qquad\frac{du}{dt}\ =\ \big(\phi_{t}^{\prime}(W_{t})\big)^{\!2}.\quad}" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><menclose notation="box"><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi>W</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><msub><mrow></mrow><mrow><mi>u</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></msub><mo rspace="0.778em">=</mo><mi>ϕ</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>t</mi></msub><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">(</mo><mi>W</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>t</mi></msub><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">)</mo><mo rspace="2.167em">,</mo><mfrac><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>u</mi></mrow><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></mfrac><mo lspace="0.778em" rspace="0.778em">=</mo><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">(</mo><mi>ϕ</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>t</mi></msub><msup><mrow></mrow><mo>′</mo></msup><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>W</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>t</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">)</mo><msup><mrow></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow></menclose><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\boxed{\quad\tilde{W}_{\,u(t)}\ =\ \phi_{t}\big(W_{t}\big),\qquad\frac{du}{dt}\ =\ \big(\phi_{t}^{\prime}(W_{t})\big)^{\!2}.\quad}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
<div id="A2.SS1.SSS2.Px1.p31" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A2.SS1.SSS2.Px1.p31.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.SS1.SSS2.Px1.p31.1.1" class="ltx_text">In words: *compose the instantaneous driving point with the current conformal change of coordinates <math id="A2.SS1.SSS2.Px1.p31.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\phi_{t}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>ϕ</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\phi_{t}</annotation></semantics></math>, and reparametrize time by the square of the derivative at the driving point* (reflecting the conformal covariance of half-plane capacity).</span></p>
</div>
<div id="A2.SS1.SSS2.Px1.p32" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A2.SS1.SSS2.Px1.p32.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.SS1.SSS2.Px1.p32.1.1" class="ltx_text">Affine automorphisms as a special case</span></p>
</div>
<div id="A2.SS1.SSS2.Px1.p33" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A2.SS1.SSS2.Px1.p33.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.SS1.SSS2.Px1.p33.1.1" class="ltx_text">If <math id="A2.SS1.SSS2.Px1.p33.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\phi(z)=az+b" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>ϕ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>z</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>a</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>z</mi></mrow><mo>+</mo><mi>b</mi></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\phi(z)=az+b</annotation></semantics></math> with <math id="A2.SS1.SSS2.Px1.p33.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="a&gt;0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>a</mi><mo>&gt;</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">a&gt;0</annotation></semantics></math>, <math id="A2.SS1.SSS2.Px1.p33.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="b\in\mathbb{R}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>b</mi><mo>∈</mo><mi>ℝ</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">b\in\mathbb{R}</annotation></semantics></math> (so <math id="A2.SS1.SSS2.Px1.p33.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\phi" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>ϕ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\phi</annotation></semantics></math> preserves <math id="A2.SS1.SSS2.Px1.p33.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\infty" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi mathvariant="normal">∞</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\infty</annotation></semantics></math> and the hydrodynamic normalization), then <math id="A2.SS1.SSS2.Px1.p33.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\phi_{t}\equiv\phi" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>ϕ</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo>≡</mo><mi>ϕ</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\phi_{t}\equiv\phi</annotation></semantics></math> and the rule simplifies to</span></p>
</div>
<div id="A2.SS1.SSS2.Px1.p34" class="ltx_para">
<table id="A2.Ex25" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A2.Ex25.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\boxed{\quad\tilde{W}_{t}\ =\ a^{-1}\big(W_{a^{2}t}-b\big).\quad}" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><menclose notation="box"><mrow><mrow><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>W</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mi>t</mi></msub><mo lspace="0.778em" rspace="0.778em">=</mo><mrow><msup><mi>a</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>W</mi><mrow><msup><mi>a</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></msub><mo>−</mo><mi>b</mi></mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><mspace style="width:1.167em;" width="1.167em"></mspace></mrow></menclose><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\boxed{\quad\tilde{W}_{t}\ =\ a^{-1}\big(W_{a^{2}t}-b\big).\quad}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
<div id="A2.SS1.SSS2.Px1.p35" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A2.SS1.SSS2.Px1.p35.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.SS1.SSS2.Px1.p35.1.1" class="ltx_text">This encodes translation invariance (<math id="A2.SS1.SSS2.Px1.p35.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="b" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>b</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">b</annotation></semantics></math>) and scale covariance (<math id="A2.SS1.SSS2.Px1.p35.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="a" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>a</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">a</annotation></semantics></math>) of the chordal Loewner equation.</span></p>
</div>
<div id="A2.SS1.SSS2.Px1.p36" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A2.SS1.SSS2.Px1.p36.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.SS1.SSS2.Px1.p36.1.1" class="ltx_text">Consequence for SLE</span></p>
</div>
<div id="A2.SS1.SSS2.Px1.p37" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A2.SS1.SSS2.Px1.p37.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.SS1.SSS2.Px1.p37.1.1" class="ltx_text">If <math id="A2.SS1.SSS2.Px1.p37.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="W_{t}=\sqrt{\kappa}B_{t}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>W</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><msqrt><mi>κ</mi></msqrt><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>B</mi><mi>t</mi></msub></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">W_{t}=\sqrt{\kappa}B_{t}</annotation></semantics></math> (chordal <math id="A2.SS1.SSS2.Px1.p37.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathrm{SLE}_{\kappa}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>SLE</mi><mi>κ</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathrm{SLE}_{\kappa}</annotation></semantics></math> in <math id="A2.SS1.SSS2.Px1.p37.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbb{H}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>ℍ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbb{H}</annotation></semantics></math> from <math id="A2.SS1.SSS2.Px1.p37.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mn>0</mn><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">0</annotation></semantics></math> to <math id="A2.SS1.SSS2.Px1.p37.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\infty" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi mathvariant="normal">∞</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\infty</annotation></semantics></math>), then for any conformal <math id="A2.SS1.SSS2.Px1.p37.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\phi" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>ϕ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\phi</annotation></semantics></math> between simply connected domains sending the start/target boundary points appropriately, the image chain <math id="A2.SS1.SSS2.Px1.p37.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\phi(K_{t})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>ϕ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>K</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\phi(K_{t})</annotation></semantics></math>, reparametrized by <math id="A2.SS1.SSS2.Px1.p37.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="u" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>u</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">u</annotation></semantics></math> as above, is again <math id="A2.SS1.SSS2.Px1.p37.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathrm{SLE}_{\kappa}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>SLE</mi><mi>κ</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathrm{SLE}_{\kappa}</annotation></semantics></math>, i.e.</span></p>
</div>
<div id="A2.SS1.SSS2.Px1.p38" class="ltx_para">
<table id="A2.Ex26" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A2.Ex26.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\tilde{W}_{u}\ \stackrel{{\scriptstyle d}}{{=}}\ \sqrt{\kappa}\,\tilde{B}_{u}," display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>W</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mi>u</mi></msub><mover><mo lspace="0.778em">=</mo><mi>d</mi></mover><mrow><msqrt><mi>κ</mi></msqrt><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>B</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mi>u</mi></msub></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\tilde{W}_{u}\ \stackrel{{\scriptstyle d}}{{=}}\ \sqrt{\kappa}\,\tilde{B}_{u},</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
<div id="A2.SS1.SSS2.Px1.p39" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A2.SS1.SSS2.Px1.p39.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.SS1.SSS2.Px1.p39.1.1" class="ltx_text">with <math id="A2.SS1.SSS2.Px1.p39.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(\tilde{B}_{u})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>B</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mi>u</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(\tilde{B}_{u})</annotation></semantics></math> a standard Brownian motion (now in the new capacity time <math id="A2.SS1.SSS2.Px1.p39.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="u" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>u</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">u</annotation></semantics></math>). This is the conformal covariance of SLE.</span></p>
</div>
<div id="A2.SS1.SSS2.Px1.p40" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A2.SS1.SSS2.Px1.p40.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.SS1.SSS2.Px1.p40.1.1" class="ltx_text">∎</span></p>
</div>
</div>
<div id="A2.SS1.SSS2.Px1.2" class="ltx_proof">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_font_italic ltx_title_proof"><span id="A2.SS1.SSS2.Px1.2.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Standard Solution</span>.</h6>
<div id="A2.SS1.SSS2.Px1.p41" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A2.SS1.SSS2.Px1.p41.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.SS1.SSS2.Px1.p41.1.1" class="ltx_text">The chordal Schramm-Loewner Evolution (SLE <sub id="A2.SS1.SSS2.Px1.p41.1.1.1" class="ltx_sub"><span id="A2.SS1.SSS2.Px1.p41.1.1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">κ</span></sub> ) is defined as follows:
- Consider the upper half-plane <math id="A2.SS1.SSS2.Px1.p41.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbb{H}=\{z\in\mathbb{C}:\Im z&gt;0\}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>ℍ</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mrow><mi>z</mi><mo>∈</mo><mi>ℂ</mi></mrow><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mrow><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">ℑ</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><mi>z</mi></mrow><mo>&gt;</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbb{H}=\{z\in\mathbb{C}:\Im z&gt;0\}</annotation></semantics></math>.
- For a continuous real-valued function <math id="A2.SS1.SSS2.Px1.p41.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="W:[0,\infty)\rightarrow\mathbb{R}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>W</mi><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">∞</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><mi>ℝ</mi></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">W:[0,\infty)\rightarrow\mathbb{R}</annotation></semantics></math>, the Loewner chain <math id="A2.SS1.SSS2.Px1.p41.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\left\{g_{t}(z)\right\}_{t\geq 0}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mrow><mo>{</mo><mrow><msub><mi>g</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>z</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>}</mo></mrow><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>≥</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\left\{g_{t}(z)\right\}_{t\geq 0}</annotation></semantics></math> is given by the solution to the Loewner ODE</span></p>
</div>
<div id="A2.SS1.SSS2.Px1.p42" class="ltx_para">
<table id="A2.Ex27" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A2.Ex27.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\frac{d}{dt}g_{t}(z)=\frac{2}{g_{t}(z)-W_{t}},\quad g_{0}(z)=z,\quad z\in\mathbb{H}." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mrow><mfrac><mi>d</mi><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></mfrac><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>g</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>z</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mn>2</mn><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>g</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>z</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>W</mi><mi>t</mi></msub></mrow></mfrac></mrow><mo rspace="1.167em">,</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>g</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>z</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mi>z</mi></mrow><mo rspace="1.167em">,</mo><mrow><mi>z</mi><mo>∈</mo><mi>ℍ</mi></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\frac{d}{dt}g_{t}(z)=\frac{2}{g_{t}(z)-W_{t}},\quad g_{0}(z)=z,\quad z\in\mathbb{H}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
<div id="A2.SS1.SSS2.Px1.p43" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A2.SS1.SSS2.Px1.p43.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.SS1.SSS2.Px1.p43.1.1" class="ltx_text">- For each <math id="A2.SS1.SSS2.Px1.p43.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="t" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>t</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">t</annotation></semantics></math>, the solution <math id="A2.SS1.SSS2.Px1.p43.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="g_{t}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>g</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">g_{t}</annotation></semantics></math> is a conformal map from a simply connected domain <math id="A2.SS1.SSS2.Px1.p43.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="H_{t}\subseteq\mathbb{H}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>H</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo>⊆</mo><mi>ℍ</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">H_{t}\subseteq\mathbb{H}</annotation></semantics></math> onto <math id="A2.SS1.SSS2.Px1.p43.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbb{H}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>ℍ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbb{H}</annotation></semantics></math>, with hydrodynamic normalization</span></p>
</div>
<div id="A2.SS1.SSS2.Px1.p44" class="ltx_para">
<table id="A2.Ex28" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A2.Ex28.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="g_{t}(z)=z+\frac{2t}{z}+o\left(\frac{1}{z}\right),\quad z\rightarrow\infty." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>g</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>z</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>z</mi><mo>+</mo><mfrac><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow><mi>z</mi></mfrac><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi>o</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mi>z</mi></mfrac><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="1.167em">,</mo><mrow><mi>z</mi><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">∞</mi></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">g_{t}(z)=z+\frac{2t}{z}+o\left(\frac{1}{z}\right),\quad z\rightarrow\infty.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
<div id="A2.SS1.SSS2.Px1.p45" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A2.SS1.SSS2.Px1.p45.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.SS1.SSS2.Px1.p45.1.1" class="ltx_text">Now let <math id="A2.SS1.SSS2.Px1.p45.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\left\{B_{t}\right\}_{t\geq 0}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mrow><mo>{</mo><msub><mi>B</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo>}</mo></mrow><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>≥</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\left\{B_{t}\right\}_{t\geq 0}</annotation></semantics></math> be a standard one-dimensional Brownian motion. For a parameter <math id="A2.SS1.SSS2.Px1.p45.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\kappa\geq 0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>κ</mi><mo>≥</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\kappa\geq 0</annotation></semantics></math>, define the driving function</span></p>
</div>
<div id="A2.SS1.SSS2.Px1.p46" class="ltx_para">
<table id="A2.Ex29" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A2.Ex29.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="W_{t}=\sqrt{\kappa}B_{t}." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>W</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><msqrt><mi>κ</mi></msqrt><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>B</mi><mi>t</mi></msub></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">W_{t}=\sqrt{\kappa}B_{t}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
<div id="A2.SS1.SSS2.Px1.p47" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A2.SS1.SSS2.Px1.p47.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.SS1.SSS2.Px1.p47.1.1" class="ltx_text">The random family of conformal maps <math id="A2.SS1.SSS2.Px1.p47.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\left\{g_{t}\right\}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo>{</mo><msub><mi>g</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo>}</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\left\{g_{t}\right\}</annotation></semantics></math> generated by this Brownian-driven Loewner equation is called the chordal Schramm-Loewner Evolution with parameter <math id="A2.SS1.SSS2.Px1.p47.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\kappa" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>κ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\kappa</annotation></semantics></math>, denoted <math id="A2.SS1.SSS2.Px1.p47.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathrm{SLE}_{\kappa}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>SLE</mi><mi>κ</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathrm{SLE}_{\kappa}</annotation></semantics></math>. The associated random growing compact sets <math id="A2.SS1.SSS2.Px1.p47.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="K_{t}=\mathbb{H}\backslash H_{t}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>K</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>ℍ</mi><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">\</mo><msub><mi>H</mi><mi>t</mi></msub></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">K_{t}=\mathbb{H}\backslash H_{t}</annotation></semantics></math> form the SLE hulls (with boundary curves known as the SLE trace when well-defined).</span></p>
</div>
<div id="A2.SS1.SSS2.Px1.p48" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A2.SS1.SSS2.Px1.p48.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.SS1.SSS2.Px1.p48.1.1" class="ltx_text">Suppose the driving function <math id="A2.SS1.SSS2.Px1.p48.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="W_{t}\in\mathbb{R}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>W</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo>∈</mo><mi>ℝ</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">W_{t}\in\mathbb{R}</annotation></semantics></math> evolves according to the stochastic differential equation</span></p>
</div>
<div id="A2.SS1.SSS2.Px1.p49" class="ltx_para">
<table id="A2.Ex30" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A2.Ex30.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="dW_{t}=\sqrt{\kappa}dB_{t}+b\left(W_{t};\Psi_{t}\left(W_{1}\right),\ldots,\Psi_{t}\left(W_{n}\right)\right)dt," display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>W</mi><mi>t</mi></msub></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><msqrt><mi>κ</mi></msqrt><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>d</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>B</mi><mi>t</mi></msub></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>b</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><msub><mi>W</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><mrow><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Ψ</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><msub><mi>W</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>,</mo><mrow><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Ψ</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><msub><mi>W</mi><mi>n</mi></msub><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>d</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">dW_{t}=\sqrt{\kappa}dB_{t}+b\left(W_{t};\Psi_{t}\left(W_{1}\right),\ldots,\Psi_{t}\left(W_{n}\right)\right)dt,</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
<div id="A2.SS1.SSS2.Px1.p50" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A2.SS1.SSS2.Px1.p50.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.SS1.SSS2.Px1.p50.1.1" class="ltx_text">where <math id="A2.SS1.SSS2.Px1.p50.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="B_{t}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>B</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">B_{t}</annotation></semantics></math> is standard Brownian motion, and <math id="A2.SS1.SSS2.Px1.p50.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="b" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>b</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">b</annotation></semantics></math> is a drift term depending on the conformal images of marked points under the time-dependent conformal map</span></p>
</div>
<div id="A2.SS1.SSS2.Px1.p51" class="ltx_para">
<table id="A2.Ex31" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A2.Ex31.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Psi_{t}:=\widetilde{g}_{t}\circ\Psi\circ g_{t}^{-1}," display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Ψ</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo>:=</mo><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>g</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mi>t</mi></msub><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">∘</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">Ψ</mi><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">∘</mo><msubsup><mi>g</mi><mi>t</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msubsup></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Psi_{t}:=\widetilde{g}_{t}\circ\Psi\circ g_{t}^{-1},</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
<div id="A2.SS1.SSS2.Px1.p52" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A2.SS1.SSS2.Px1.p52.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.SS1.SSS2.Px1.p52.1.1" class="ltx_text">with <math id="A2.SS1.SSS2.Px1.p52.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Psi" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi mathvariant="normal">Ψ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Psi</annotation></semantics></math> conformal near <math id="A2.SS1.SSS2.Px1.p52.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="W_{0}\in\mathbb{R}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>W</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo>∈</mo><mi>ℝ</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">W_{0}\in\mathbb{R}</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="A2.SS1.SSS2.Px1.p52.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="g_{t},\widetilde{g}_{t}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>g</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>g</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mi>t</mi></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">g_{t},\widetilde{g}_{t}</annotation></semantics></math> the Loewner flows before and after coordinate change, respectively.</span></p>
</div>
<div id="A2.SS1.SSS2.Px1.p53" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A2.SS1.SSS2.Px1.p53.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.SS1.SSS2.Px1.p53.1.1" class="ltx_text">Define the transformed driving function <math id="A2.SS1.SSS2.Px1.p53.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\widetilde{W}_{t}:=\Psi_{t}\left(W_{t}\right)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>W</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mi>t</mi></msub><mo>:=</mo><mrow><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Ψ</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><msub><mi>W</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\widetilde{W}_{t}:=\Psi_{t}\left(W_{t}\right)</annotation></semantics></math>, and introduce the reparameterized time</span></p>
</div>
<div id="A2.SS1.SSS2.Px1.p54" class="ltx_para">
<table id="A2.Ex32" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A2.Ex32.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="s(t):=\int_{0}^{t}\left|\Psi_{u}^{\prime}\left(W_{u}\right)\right|^{2}du" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>s</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.111em">:=</mo><mrow><msubsup><mo rspace="0em">∫</mo><mn>0</mn><mi>t</mi></msubsup><mrow><msup><mrow><mo>|</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi mathvariant="normal">Ψ</mi><mi>u</mi><mo>′</mo></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><msub><mi>W</mi><mi>u</mi></msub><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>|</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo rspace="0em">𝑑</mo><mi>u</mi></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">s(t):=\int_{0}^{t}\left|\Psi_{u}^{\prime}\left(W_{u}\right)\right|^{2}du</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
<div id="A2.SS1.SSS2.Px1.p55" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A2.SS1.SSS2.Px1.p55.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.SS1.SSS2.Px1.p55.1.1" class="ltx_text">Then the time-changed process <math id="A2.SS1.SSS2.Px1.p55.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\widetilde{W}_{s}:=\widetilde{W}_{t(s)}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>W</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mi>s</mi></msub><mo>:=</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>W</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>s</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\widetilde{W}_{s}:=\widetilde{W}_{t(s)}</annotation></semantics></math> satisfies the stochastic differential equation</span></p>
</div>
<div id="A2.SS1.SSS2.Px1.p56" class="ltx_para">
<table id="A2.Ex33" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
