<span id="A2.SS1.SSS2.Px2.p2.pic1.1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.SS1.SSS2.Px2.p2.pic1.1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold" style="--ltx-fg-color:#FFFFFF;">Problem</span></span>
</span></span></span></foreignObject></g><g fill-opacity="1.0" transform="matrix(1.0 0.0 0.0 1.0 20.38 14.66)"><foreignObject style="--ltx-fo-width:32.01em;--ltx-fo-height:4.02em;--ltx-fo-depth:0.16em;font-size:10pt;" height="57.75" overflow="visible" transform="matrix(1 0 0 -1 0 55.6)" width="442.93"><span class="ltx_foreignobject_container"><span class="ltx_foreignobject_content">
<span id="A2.SS1.SSS2.Px2.p2.pic1.2" class="ltx_inline-block ltx_minipage ltx_align_bottom" style="width:32.01em;">
<span id="A2.SS1.SSS2.Px2.p2.pic1.2.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.SS1.SSS2.Px2.p2.pic1.2.1.1" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:80%;--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">Please explain the commutation relations for multiple chordal SLE(<math id="A2.SS1.SSS2.Px2.p2.pic1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\kappa" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">κ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\kappa</annotation></semantics></math>).</span></span><span class="ltx_inline-block"><svg id="A2.SS1.SSS2.Px2.p2.pic1.pic1" class="ltx_picture" color="#FF0000" height="18.24" overflow="visible" style="vertical-align:-4.1px" version="1.1" viewBox="0 0 18.24 18.24" width="18.24"><g style="--ltx-stroke-color:#FF0000;--ltx-fill-color:#FF0000;" fill="#FF0000" stroke="#FF0000" stroke-width="1.8pt" transform="translate(0,18.24) matrix(1 0 0 -1 0 0) translate(1.25,0) translate(0,1.25)"><path style="fill:none" d="M 0 0 L 15.75 15.75 M 0 15.75 L 15.75 0"></path></g></svg></span>
<span id="A2.SS1.SSS2.Px2.p2.pic1.2.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.SS1.SSS2.Px2.p2.pic1.2.2.1" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:80%;--ltx-fg-color:#FF0000;">GPT-5 thinking failed</span></span>
<span id="A2.SS1.SSS2.Px2.p2.pic1.2.3" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.SS1.SSS2.Px2.p2.pic1.2.3.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic" style="font-size:80%;--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">Proposed by Jiaxin Zhang</span></span>
</span></span></span></foreignObject></g></g></svg></span>
</div>
<div id="A2.SS1.SSS2.Px2.1" class="ltx_proof">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_font_italic ltx_title_proof"><span id="A2.SS1.SSS2.Px2.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Response of GPT-5-thinking</span>.</h6>
<div id="A2.SS1.SSS2.Px2.p3" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A2.SS1.SSS2.Px2.p3.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.SS1.SSS2.Px2.p3.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Set-up.<span id="A2.SS1.SSS2.Px2.p3.1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_medium">
Let <math id="A2.SS1.SSS2.Px2.p3.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="x_{1}&lt;\cdots&lt;x_{n}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>x</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo rspace="0.1389em">&lt;</mo><mo lspace="0.1389em" rspace="0.1389em">⋯</mo><mo lspace="0.1389em">&lt;</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>n</mi></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">x_{1}&lt;\cdots&lt;x_{n}</annotation></semantics></math> be marked boundary points on <math id="A2.SS1.SSS2.Px2.p3.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbb{R}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>ℝ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbb{R}</annotation></semantics></math> and write</span></span></p>
<table id="A2.Ex34" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A2.Ex34.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\mathcal{A}_{i}\;=\;\frac{\kappa}{2}\,\partial_{x_{i}}^{2}\;+\;\sum_{k\neq i}\frac{2}{x_{k}-x_{i}}\,\partial_{x_{k}}\qquad(i=1,\dots,n)," display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒜</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo lspace="0.558em" rspace="0.558em">=</mo><mfrac><mi>κ</mi><mn>2</mn></mfrac><msubsup><mo>∂</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mn>2</mn></msubsup><mo rspace="0.335em">+</mo><munder><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>≠</mo><mi>i</mi></mrow></munder><mfrac><mn>2</mn><mrow><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></mrow></mfrac><msub><mo>∂</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>k</mi></msub></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>i</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>n</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{A}_{i}\;=\;\frac{\kappa}{2}\,\partial_{x_{i}}^{2}\;+\;\sum_{k\neq i}\frac{2}{x_{k}-x_{i}}\,\partial_{x_{k}}\qquad(i=1,\dots,n),</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A2.SS1.SSS2.Px2.p3.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.SS1.SSS2.Px2.p3.2.1" class="ltx_text">the infinitesimal generator corresponding to growing an infinitesimal chordal Loewner slit at <math id="A2.SS1.SSS2.Px2.p3.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="x_{i}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">x_{i}</annotation></semantics></math> (half-plane capacity <math id="A2.SS1.SSS2.Px2.p3.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="2\,dt" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>d</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">2\,dt</annotation></semantics></math>).</span></p>
</div>
<div id="A2.SS1.SSS2.Px2.p4" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A2.SS1.SSS2.Px2.p4.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.SS1.SSS2.Px2.p4.1.1" class="ltx_text">A (positive, smooth) function <math id="A2.SS1.SSS2.Px2.p4.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="Z(x_{1},\dots,x_{n})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>Z</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>n</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">Z(x_{1},\dots,x_{n})</annotation></semantics></math> is called a <em id="A2.SS1.SSS2.Px2.p4.1.1.1" class="ltx_emph ltx_font_italic">partition function</em> if it is Möbius covariant with boundary weight</span></p>
<table id="A2.Ex35" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A2.Ex35.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="h=\frac{6-\kappa}{2\kappa}\qquad\text{and solves, for each }i," display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>h</mi><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mrow><mn>6</mn><mo>−</mo><mi>κ</mi></mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>κ</mi></mrow></mfrac></mrow><mspace style="width:2em;" width="2em"></mspace><mrow><mtext>and solves, for each </mtext><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>i</mi></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">h=\frac{6-\kappa}{2\kappa}\qquad\text{and solves, for each }i,</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A2.SS1.SSS2.Px2.p4.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.SS1.SSS2.Px2.p4.2.1" class="ltx_text">the level-two null-state (BPZ) PDE</span></p>
<table id="A2.Ex36" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A2.Ex36.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\boxed{\quad\frac{\kappa}{2}\,\partial_{x_{i}}^{2}Z\;+\;\sum_{k\neq i}\frac{2}{x_{k}-x_{i}}\,\partial_{x_{k}}Z\;+\;\sum_{k\neq i}\frac{2h}{(x_{k}-x_{i})^{2}}\,Z\;=\;0\quad}" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><menclose notation="box"><mrow><mrow><mrow><mrow><mfrac><mi>κ</mi><mn>2</mn></mfrac><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><msubsup><mo>∂</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mn>2</mn></msubsup><mi>Z</mi></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0.502em" rspace="0.335em">+</mo><mrow><munder><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>≠</mo><mi>i</mi></mrow></munder><mrow><mfrac><mn>2</mn><mrow><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></mrow></mfrac><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><msub><mo>∂</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>k</mi></msub></msub><mi>Z</mi></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0.502em" rspace="0.335em">+</mo><mrow><munder><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>≠</mo><mi>i</mi></mrow></munder><mrow><mfrac><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>h</mi></mrow><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup></mfrac><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>Z</mi></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0.558em">=</mo><mn> 0</mn></mrow><mspace style="width:1em;" width="1em"></mspace></mrow></menclose><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\boxed{\quad\frac{\kappa}{2}\,\partial_{x_{i}}^{2}Z\;+\;\sum_{k\neq i}\frac{2}{x_{k}-x_{i}}\,\partial_{x_{k}}Z\;+\;\sum_{k\neq i}\frac{2h}{(x_{k}-x_{i})^{2}}\,Z\;=\;0\quad}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
<div id="A2.SS1.SSS2.Px2.p5" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A2.SS1.SSS2.Px2.p5.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.SS1.SSS2.Px2.p5.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Commutation relations (Dubédat).<span id="A2.SS1.SSS2.Px2.p5.1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_medium">
Assume <math id="A2.SS1.SSS2.Px2.p5.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="Z" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>Z</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">Z</annotation></semantics></math> satisfies equation * and Möbius covariance. Define the (Doob–Girsanov tilted) operators</span></span></p>
<table id="A2.Ex38" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A2.Ex38.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{L}_{i}f\;:=\;Z^{-1}\,\mathcal{A}_{i}\,(Zf)\;=\;\mathcal{A}_{i}f\;+\;\kappa\,(\partial_{x_{i}}\log Z)\,\partial_{x_{i}}f\qquad\text{(using equation * to cancel the zero-order term).}" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℒ</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>f</mi></mrow><mo lspace="0.558em" rspace="0.558em">:=</mo><mrow><msup><mi>Z</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒜</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>Z</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>f</mi></mrow><mo rspace="0.280em" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.558em">=</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒜</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>f</mi></mrow><mo lspace="0.502em" rspace="0.502em">+</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>κ</mi><mo lspace="0.170em">⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.167em">∂</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></msub><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><mi>Z</mi></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><msub><mo>∂</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></msub><mi>f</mi></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mspace style="width:2em;" width="2em"></mspace><mtext>(using equation * to cancel the zero-order term).</mtext></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{L}_{i}f\;:=\;Z^{-1}\,\mathcal{A}_{i}\,(Zf)\;=\;\mathcal{A}_{i}f\;+\;\kappa\,(\partial_{x_{i}}\log Z)\,\partial_{x_{i}}f\qquad\text{(using equation * to cancel the zero-order term).}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A2.SS1.SSS2.Px2.p5.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.SS1.SSS2.Px2.p5.2.1" class="ltx_text">Then for all <math id="A2.SS1.SSS2.Px2.p5.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="i\neq j" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>≠</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">i\neq j</annotation></semantics></math>,</span></p>
<table id="A2.Ex39" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A2.Ex39.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\boxed{\ [\mathcal{L}_{i},\mathcal{L}_{j}]\,f\;=\;0\quad\text{for all smooth }f,\ }" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><menclose notation="box"><mrow><mrow><mrow><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℒ</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℒ</mi><mi>j</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>f</mi></mrow><mo lspace="0.558em">=</mo><mn> 0</mn></mrow><mspace style="width:1em;" width="1em"></mspace><mrow><mtext>for all smooth </mtext><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>f</mi></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow></menclose><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\boxed{\ [\mathcal{L}_{i},\mathcal{L}_{j}]\,f\;=\;0\quad\text{for all smooth }f,\ }</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A2.SS1.SSS2.Px2.p5.3" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.SS1.SSS2.Px2.p5.3.1" class="ltx_text">i.e. the infinitesimal evolutions <em id="A2.SS1.SSS2.Px2.p5.3.1.1" class="ltx_emph ltx_font_italic">commute</em>. Equivalently, if one first grows the <math id="A2.SS1.SSS2.Px2.p5.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="i" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>i</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">i</annotation></semantics></math>th slit for an infinitesimal time and then the <math id="A2.SS1.SSS2.Px2.p5.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="j" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>j</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">j</annotation></semantics></math>th (or in the reverse order), the resulting law of the configuration is the same (up to deterministic time-change). This is the precise meaning of <em id="A2.SS1.SSS2.Px2.p5.3.1.2" class="ltx_emph ltx_font_italic">commutation relations</em> for multiple chordal SLE<sub id="A2.SS1.SSS2.Px2.p5.3.1.3" class="ltx_sub"><span id="A2.SS1.SSS2.Px2.p5.3.1.3.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">κ</span></sub>.</span></p>
</div>
<div id="A2.SS1.SSS2.Px2.p6" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A2.SS1.SSS2.Px2.p6.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.SS1.SSS2.Px2.p6.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Driving SDE formulation (equivalent).<span id="A2.SS1.SSS2.Px2.p6.1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_medium">
Under the multiple-SLE measure determined by <math id="A2.SS1.SSS2.Px2.p6.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="Z" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>Z</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">Z</annotation></semantics></math>, the driving points solve</span></span></p>
<table id="A2.Ex40" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A2.Ex40.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="dX_{t}^{i}\;=\;\sqrt{\kappa}\,dB_{t}^{i}\;+\;\Bigg(\kappa\,\partial_{x_{i}}\log Z(X_{t})\;+\;\sum_{k\neq i}\frac{2}{X_{t}^{i}-X_{t}^{k}}\Bigg)dt," display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>X</mi><mi>t</mi><mi>i</mi></msubsup></mrow><mo rspace="0.558em">=</mo><mrow><mrow><msqrt><mi>κ</mi></msqrt><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>d</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>B</mi><mi>t</mi><mi>i</mi></msubsup></mrow><mo rspace="0.502em">+</mo><mrow><mrow><mo maxsize="2.600em" minsize="2.600em">(</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>κ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><msub><mo rspace="0.167em">∂</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></msub><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><mrow><mi>Z</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>X</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo rspace="0.280em" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.335em">+</mo><mrow><munder><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>≠</mo><mi>i</mi></mrow></munder><mfrac><mn>2</mn><mrow><msubsup><mi>X</mi><mi>t</mi><mi>i</mi></msubsup><mo>−</mo><msubsup><mi>X</mi><mi>t</mi><mi>k</mi></msubsup></mrow></mfrac></mrow></mrow><mo maxsize="2.600em" minsize="2.600em">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>d</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">dX_{t}^{i}\;=\;\sqrt{\kappa}\,dB_{t}^{i}\;+\;\Bigg(\kappa\,\partial_{x_{i}}\log Z(X_{t})\;+\;\sum_{k\neq i}\frac{2}{X_{t}^{i}-X_{t}^{k}}\Bigg)dt,</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A2.SS1.SSS2.Px2.p6.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.SS1.SSS2.Px2.p6.2.1" class="ltx_text">and the corresponding Markov generators are the commuting <math id="A2.SS1.SSS2.Px2.p6.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\{\mathcal{L}_{i}\}_{i=1}^{n}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℒ</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>n</mi></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\{\mathcal{L}_{i}\}_{i=1}^{n}</annotation></semantics></math> above. The commutation expresses that the joint law does not depend on the order in which the curves are explored.</span></p>
</div>
<div id="A2.SS1.SSS2.Px2.p7" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A2.SS1.SSS2.Px2.p7.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.SS1.SSS2.Px2.p7.1.1" class="ltx_text">∎</span></p>
</div>
</div>
<div id="A2.SS1.SSS2.Px2.2" class="ltx_proof">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_font_italic ltx_title_proof"><span id="A2.SS1.SSS2.Px2.2.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Standard Solution</span>.</h6>
<div id="A2.SS1.SSS2.Px2.p8" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A2.SS1.SSS2.Px2.p8.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.SS1.SSS2.Px2.p8.1.1" class="ltx_text">Please refer to the paper <a href="https://arxiv.org/abs/2505.16093" title="" class="ltx_ref ltx_href"> Multiple chordal SLE(<math class="ltx_Math" alttext="\kappa" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>κ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\kappa</annotation></semantics></math>) and quantum Calogero-Moser system </a></span></p>
</div>
<div id="A2.SS1.SSS2.Px2.p9" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A2.SS1.SSS2.Px2.p9.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.SS1.SSS2.Px2.p9.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Partition functions and null vector equations.<span id="A2.SS1.SSS2.Px2.p9.1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_medium">
Let <math id="A2.SS1.SSS2.Px2.p9.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="x_{1},\dots,x_{n}\in\mathbb{R}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>x</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>,</mo><mrow><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>n</mi></msub><mo>∈</mo><mi>ℝ</mi></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">x_{1},\dots,x_{n}\in\mathbb{R}</annotation></semantics></math> be distinct boundary points.
A smooth positive function <math id="A2.SS1.SSS2.Px2.p9.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="Z(x_{1},\dots,x_{n})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>Z</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>n</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">Z(x_{1},\dots,x_{n})</annotation></semantics></math> is called a <em id="A2.SS1.SSS2.Px2.p9.1.1.1.1" class="ltx_emph ltx_font_italic">partition function</em> if it is Möbius covariant with boundary weight</span></span></p>
<table id="A2.Ex41" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A2.Ex41.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="h=\frac{6-\kappa}{2\kappa}," display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>h</mi><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mrow><mn>6</mn><mo>−</mo><mi>κ</mi></mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>κ</mi></mrow></mfrac></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">h=\frac{6-\kappa}{2\kappa},</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A2.SS1.SSS2.Px2.p9.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.SS1.SSS2.Px2.p9.2.1" class="ltx_text">and for each <math id="A2.SS1.SSS2.Px2.p9.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="i=1,\dots,n" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>n</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">i=1,\dots,n</annotation></semantics></math> satisfies the level-two null vector (BPZ) equation</span></p>
<table id="A2.Ex42" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A2.Ex42.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\frac{\kappa}{2}\,\partial_{x_{i}x_{i}}Z+\sum_{k\neq i}\frac{2}{x_{k}-x_{i}}\,\partial_{x_{k}}Z+\sum_{k\neq i}\frac{2h}{(x_{k}-x_{i})^{2}}\,Z=0." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mrow><mfrac><mi>κ</mi><mn>2</mn></mfrac><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><msub><mo>∂</mo><mrow><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></mrow></msub><mi>Z</mi></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.055em">+</mo><mrow><munder><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>≠</mo><mi>i</mi></mrow></munder><mrow><mfrac><mn>2</mn><mrow><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></mrow></mfrac><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><msub><mo>∂</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>k</mi></msub></msub><mi>Z</mi></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.055em">+</mo><mrow><munder><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>≠</mo><mi>i</mi></mrow></munder><mrow><mfrac><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>h</mi></mrow><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup></mfrac><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>Z</mi></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\frac{\kappa}{2}\,\partial_{x_{i}x_{i}}Z+\sum_{k\neq i}\frac{2}{x_{k}-x_{i}}\,\partial_{x_{k}}Z+\sum_{k\neq i}\frac{2h}{(x_{k}-x_{i})^{2}}\,Z=0.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
<div id="A2.SS1.SSS2.Px2.p10" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A2.SS1.SSS2.Px2.p10.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.SS1.SSS2.Px2.p10.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Commutation relations.<span id="A2.SS1.SSS2.Px2.p10.1.1.1" class="ltx_text"></span></span></p>
</div>
<div id="A2.SS1.SSS2.Px2.p11" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A2.SS1.SSS2.Px2.p11.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.SS1.SSS2.Px2.p11.1.1" class="ltx_text">Given such a partition function <math id="A2.SS1.SSS2.Px2.p11.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="Z" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>Z</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">Z</annotation></semantics></math>, define for each <math id="A2.SS1.SSS2.Px2.p11.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="i" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>i</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">i</annotation></semantics></math></span></p>
<table id="A2.Ex44" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A2.Ex44.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\mathcal{L}_{i}=\frac{\kappa}{2}\,\partial_{x_{i}x_{i}}+\kappa\,(\partial_{x_{i}}\log Z)\,\partial_{x_{i}}+\sum_{k\neq i}\frac{2}{x_{k}-x_{i}}\,\partial_{x_{k}}." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℒ</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mi>κ</mi><mn>2</mn></mfrac><msub><mo>∂</mo><mrow><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></mrow></msub><mo>+</mo><mi>κ</mi><mrow><mo lspace="0.170em" stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.167em">∂</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></msub><mi>log</mi><mi>Z</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><msub><mo>∂</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></msub><mo rspace="0.055em">+</mo><munder><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>≠</mo><mi>i</mi></mrow></munder><mfrac><mn>2</mn><mrow><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></mrow></mfrac><msub><mo>∂</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>k</mi></msub></msub><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{L}_{i}=\frac{\kappa}{2}\,\partial_{x_{i}x_{i}}+\kappa\,(\partial_{x_{i}}\log Z)\,\partial_{x_{i}}+\sum_{k\neq i}\frac{2}{x_{k}-x_{i}}\,\partial_{x_{k}}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
<div id="A2.SS1.SSS2.Px2.p12" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A2.SS1.SSS2.Px2.p12.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.SS1.SSS2.Px2.p12.1.1" class="ltx_text">The operators <math id="A2.SS1.SSS2.Px2.p12.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{L}_{i}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℒ</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{L}_{i}</annotation></semantics></math> describe the infinitesimal evolution when a slit is grown at <math id="A2.SS1.SSS2.Px2.p12.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="x_{i}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">x_{i}</annotation></semantics></math>.</span></p>
</div>
<div id="A2.SS1.SSS2.Px2.p13" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A2.SS1.SSS2.Px2.p13.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.SS1.SSS2.Px2.p13.1.1" class="ltx_text">Probabilistically, commutation relations say that if one first grows the slit at <math id="A2.SS1.SSS2.Px2.p13.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="x_{i}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">x_{i}</annotation></semantics></math> for an infinitesimal time and then at <math id="A2.SS1.SSS2.Px2.p13.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="x_{j}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>j</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">x_{j}</annotation></semantics></math>, or reverses the order, the resulting law of the configuration is the same (up to reparametrization).</span></p>
</div>
<div id="A2.SS1.SSS2.Px2.p14" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A2.SS1.SSS2.Px2.p14.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.SS1.SSS2.Px2.p14.1.1" class="ltx_text">Dubédat’s commutation theorem asserts that for all <math id="A2.SS1.SSS2.Px2.p14.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="i\neq j" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>≠</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">i\neq j</annotation></semantics></math>,</span></p>
<table id="A2.Ex45" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A2.Ex45.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="[\mathcal{L}_{i},\mathcal{L}_{j}]=\frac{4}{(x_{j}-x_{i})^{2}}\,\bigl(\mathcal{L}_{j}-\mathcal{L}_{i}\bigr)." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℒ</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℒ</mi><mi>j</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mfrac><mn>4</mn><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>j</mi></msub><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup></mfrac><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℒ</mi><mi>j</mi></msub><mo>−</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℒ</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">[\mathcal{L}_{i},\mathcal{L}_{j}]=\frac{4}{(x_{j}-x_{i})^{2}}\,\bigl(\mathcal{L}_{j}-\mathcal{L}_{i}\bigr).</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
<div id="A2.SS1.SSS2.Px2.p15" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A2.SS1.SSS2.Px2.p15.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.SS1.SSS2.Px2.p15.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Driving SDE formulation.<span id="A2.SS1.SSS2.Px2.p15.1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_medium">
Under the probability measure determined by <math id="A2.SS1.SSS2.Px2.p15.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="Z" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>Z</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">Z</annotation></semantics></math>, the driving processes <math id="A2.SS1.SSS2.Px2.p15.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(X_{t}^{1},\dots,X_{t}^{n})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msubsup><mi>X</mi><mi>t</mi><mn>1</mn></msubsup><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>,</mo><msubsup><mi>X</mi><mi>t</mi><mi>n</mi></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(X_{t}^{1},\dots,X_{t}^{n})</annotation></semantics></math> satisfy</span></span></p>
<table id="A2.Ex46" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A2.Ex46.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="dX_{t}^{i}\;=\;\sqrt{\kappa}\,dB_{t}^{i}+\left(\kappa\,\partial_{x_{i}}\log Z(X_{t})+\sum_{k\neq i}\frac{2}{X_{t}^{i}-X_{t}^{k}}\right)\,dt,\qquad i=1,\dots,n," display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>d</mi><msubsup><mi>X</mi><mi>t</mi><mi>i</mi></msubsup><mo rspace="0.558em">=</mo><msqrt><mi>κ</mi></msqrt><mi>d</mi><msubsup><mi>B</mi><mi>t</mi><mi>i</mi></msubsup><mo>+</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mi>κ</mi><msub><mo rspace="0.167em">∂</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></msub><mi>log</mi><mi>Z</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>X</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo rspace="0.055em">+</mo><munder><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>≠</mo><mi>i</mi></mrow></munder><mfrac><mn>2</mn><mrow><msubsup><mi>X</mi><mi>t</mi><mi>i</mi></msubsup><mo>−</mo><msubsup><mi>X</mi><mi>t</mi><mi>k</mi></msubsup></mrow></mfrac><mo rspace="0.170em">)</mo></mrow><mi>d</mi><mi>t</mi><mo rspace="2.167em">,</mo><mi>i</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>n</mi><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">dX_{t}^{i}\;=\;\sqrt{\kappa}\,dB_{t}^{i}+\left(\kappa\,\partial_{x_{i}}\log Z(X_{t})+\sum_{k\neq i}\frac{2}{X_{t}^{i}-X_{t}^{k}}\right)\,dt,\qquad i=1,\dots,n,</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A2.SS1.SSS2.Px2.p15.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.SS1.SSS2.Px2.p15.2.1" class="ltx_text">where <math id="A2.SS1.SSS2.Px2.p15.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(B_{t}^{i})_{i=1}^{n}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msubsup><mi>B</mi><mi>t</mi><mi>i</mi></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>n</mi></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(B_{t}^{i})_{i=1}^{n}</annotation></semantics></math> are independent standard Brownian motions.
The infinitesimal generator of the <math id="A2.SS1.SSS2.Px2.p15.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="i" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>i</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">i</annotation></semantics></math>-th coordinate is precisely <math id="A2.SS1.SSS2.Px2.p15.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{L}_{i}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℒ</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{L}_{i}</annotation></semantics></math>, and the commutation relation shows that the joint law is independent of the order in which the curves are explored.</span></p>
</div>
<div id="A2.SS1.SSS2.Px2.p16" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A2.SS1.SSS2.Px2.p16.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.SS1.SSS2.Px2.p16.1.1" class="ltx_text">∎</span></p>
</div>
</div>
<div id="A2.SS1.SSS2.Px2.p17" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent"><span class="ltx_inline-block"><svg id="A2.SS1.SSS2.Px2.p17.pic1" class="ltx_picture" height="136.04" overflow="visible" version="1.1" viewBox="0 0 429.64 136.04" width="429.64"><g style="--ltx-stroke-color:#000000;--ltx-fill-color:#000000;" fill="#000000" stroke="#000000" stroke-width="0.4pt" transform="translate(0,136.04) matrix(1 0 0 -1 0 0)"><g style="--ltx-fill-color:#4D4D4D;" fill="#4D4D4D" fill-opacity="1.0"><path style="stroke:none" d="M 0 4.63 L 0 131.41 C 0 133.97 2.07 136.04 4.63 136.04 L 425.01 136.04 C 427.56 136.04 429.64 133.97 429.64 131.41 L 429.64 4.63 C 429.64 2.07 427.56 0 425.01 0 L 4.63 0 C 2.07 0 0 2.07 0 4.63 Z"></path></g><g style="--ltx-fill-color:#F9F9F9;" fill="#F9F9F9" fill-opacity="1.0"><path style="stroke:none" d="M 0.69 4.63 L 0.69 117.18 L 428.94 117.18 L 428.94 4.63 C 428.94 2.45 427.18 0.69 425.01 0.69 L 4.63 0.69 C 2.45 0.69 0.69 2.45 0.69 4.63 Z"></path></g><g fill-opacity="1.0" transform="matrix(1.0 0.0 0.0 1.0 20.38 121.8)"><foreignObject style="--ltx-fo-width:24.44em;--ltx-fo-height:0.69em;--ltx-fo-depth:0em;font-size:10pt;" height="9.61" overflow="visible" transform="matrix(1 0 0 -1 0 9.61)" width="338.18"><span class="ltx_foreignobject_container"><span class="ltx_foreignobject_content">
<span id="A2.SS1.SSS2.Px2.p17.pic1.1" class="ltx_inline-block ltx_minipage ltx_align_bottom" style="width:24.44em;">
<span id="A2.SS1.SSS2.Px2.p17.pic1.1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.SS1.SSS2.Px2.p17.pic1.1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold" style="--ltx-fg-color:#FFFFFF;">Rubric</span></span>
</span></span></span></foreignObject></g><g fill-opacity="1.0" transform="matrix(1.0 0.0 0.0 1.0 20.38 83.84)"><foreignObject style="--ltx-fo-width:33.06em;--ltx-fo-height:1.56em;--ltx-fo-depth:5.16em;font-size:10pt;" height="92.86" overflow="visible" transform="matrix(1 0 0 -1 0 21.52)" width="457.46"><span class="ltx_foreignobject_container"><span class="ltx_foreignobject_content">
<span id="A2.SS1.SSS2.Px2.p17.pic1.2" class="ltx_inline-block ltx_minipage ltx_align_bottom" style="width:33.06em;">
<span id="A2.I6" class="ltx_enumerate">
<span id="A2.I6.i1" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">1.</span> 
<span id="A2.I6.i1.p1" class="ltx_para">
<span id="A2.I6.i1.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.I6.i1.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:80%;--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">Explain the commutation relation from the order of growth of two points.</span></span>
</span></span>
<span id="A2.I6.i2" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">2.</span> 
<span id="A2.I6.i2.p1" class="ltx_para">
<span id="A2.I6.i2.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.I6.i2.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:80%;--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">Computes the commutator of the generators correctly.</span></span>
</span></span>
<span id="A2.I6.i3" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">3.</span> 
<span id="A2.I6.i3.p1" class="ltx_para">
<span id="A2.I6.i3.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.I6.i3.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:80%;--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">States the null-vector equations accurately.</span></span>
</span></span>
</span>
</span></span></span></foreignObject></g></g></svg></span>
</div>
<div id="A2.SS1.SSS2.Px2.p18" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent"><span class="ltx_inline-block"><svg id="A2.SS1.SSS2.Px2.p18.pic1" class="ltx_picture" height="54.13" overflow="visible" version="1.1" viewBox="0 0 429.64 54.13" width="429.64"><g style="--ltx-stroke-color:#000000;--ltx-fill-color:#000000;" fill="#000000" stroke="#000000" stroke-width="0.4pt" transform="translate(0,54.13) matrix(1 0 0 -1 0 0)"><g style="--ltx-fill-color:#5A996B;" fill="#5A996B" fill-opacity="1.0"><path style="stroke:none" d="M 0 4.63 L 0 49.51 C 0 52.06 2.07 54.13 4.63 54.13 L 425.01 54.13 C 427.56 54.13 429.64 52.06 429.64 49.51 L 429.64 4.63 C 429.64 2.07 427.56 0 425.01 0 L 4.63 0 C 2.07 0 0 2.07 0 4.63 Z"></path></g><g style="--ltx-fill-color:#F6FFF9;" fill="#F6FFF9" fill-opacity="1.0"><path style="stroke:none" d="M 0.69 4.63 L 0.69 35.38 L 428.94 35.38 L 428.94 4.63 C 428.94 2.45 427.18 0.69 425.01 0.69 L 4.63 0.69 C 2.45 0.69 0.69 2.45 0.69 4.63 Z"></path></g><g fill-opacity="1.0" transform="matrix(1.0 0.0 0.0 1.0 20.38 40.01)"><foreignObject style="--ltx-fo-width:24.44em;--ltx-fo-height:0.69em;--ltx-fo-depth:0em;font-size:10pt;" height="9.49" overflow="visible" transform="matrix(1 0 0 -1 0 9.49)" width="338.18"><span class="ltx_foreignobject_container"><span class="ltx_foreignobject_content">
<span id="A2.SS1.SSS2.Px2.p18.pic1.1" class="ltx_inline-block ltx_minipage ltx_align_bottom" style="width:24.44em;">
<span id="A2.SS1.SSS2.Px2.p18.pic1.1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.SS1.SSS2.Px2.p18.pic1.1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold" style="--ltx-fg-color:#FFFFFF;">Score</span></span>
</span></span></span></foreignObject></g><g fill-opacity="1.0" transform="matrix(1.0 0.0 0.0 1.0 20.38 15.27)"><foreignObject style="--ltx-fo-width:33.06em;--ltx-fo-height:0.6em;--ltx-fo-depth:0.2em;font-size:10pt;" height="11.07" overflow="visible" transform="matrix(1 0 0 -1 0 8.3)" width="457.46"><span class="ltx_foreignobject_container"><span class="ltx_foreignobject_content">
<span id="A2.SS1.SSS2.Px2.p18.pic1.2" class="ltx_inline-block ltx_minipage ltx_align_bottom" style="width:33.06em;">
<span id="A2.SS1.SSS2.Px2.p18.pic1.2.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.SS1.SSS2.Px2.p18.pic1.2.1.1" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:80%;--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">2/3</span></span>
</span></span></span></foreignObject></g></g></svg></span>
</div>
<div id="A2.SS1.SSS2.Px2.p19" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent"><span class="ltx_inline-block"><svg id="A2.SS1.SSS2.Px2.p19.pic1" class="ltx_picture" height="86.97" overflow="visible" version="1.1" viewBox="0 0 429.64 86.97" width="429.64"><g style="--ltx-stroke-color:#000000;--ltx-fill-color:#000000;" fill="#000000" stroke="#000000" stroke-width="0.4pt" transform="translate(0,86.97) matrix(1 0 0 -1 0 0)"><g style="--ltx-fill-color:#B33674;" fill="#B33674" fill-opacity="1.0"><path style="stroke:none" d="M 0 4.63 L 0 82.34 C 0 84.89 2.07 86.97 4.63 86.97 L 425.01 86.97 C 427.56 86.97 429.64 84.89 429.64 82.34 L 429.64 4.63 C 429.64 2.07 427.56 0 425.01 0 L 4.63 0 C 2.07 0 0 2.07 0 4.63 Z"></path></g><g style="--ltx-fill-color:#FFF2F9;" fill="#FFF2F9" fill-opacity="1.0"><path style="stroke:none" d="M 0.69 4.63 L 0.69 68.1 L 428.94 68.1 L 428.94 4.63 C 428.94 2.45 427.18 0.69 425.01 0.69 L 4.63 0.69 C 2.45 0.69 0.69 2.45 0.69 4.63 Z"></path></g><g fill-opacity="1.0" transform="matrix(1.0 0.0 0.0 1.0 20.38 72.73)"><foreignObject style="--ltx-fo-width:24.44em;--ltx-fo-height:0.69em;--ltx-fo-depth:0em;font-size:10pt;" height="9.61" overflow="visible" transform="matrix(1 0 0 -1 0 9.61)" width="338.18"><span class="ltx_foreignobject_container"><span class="ltx_foreignobject_content">
<span id="A2.SS1.SSS2.Px2.p19.pic1.1" class="ltx_inline-block ltx_minipage ltx_align_bottom" style="width:24.44em;">
<span id="A2.SS1.SSS2.Px2.p19.pic1.1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.SS1.SSS2.Px2.p19.pic1.1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold" style="--ltx-fg-color:#FFFFFF;">Evaluation</span></span>
</span></span></span></foreignObject></g><g fill-opacity="1.0" transform="matrix(1.0 0.0 0.0 1.0 20.38 15.39)"><foreignObject style="--ltx-fo-width:33.06em;--ltx-fo-height:2.96em;--ltx-fo-depth:0.21em;font-size:10pt;" height="43.79" overflow="visible" transform="matrix(1 0 0 -1 0 40.9)" width="457.46"><span class="ltx_foreignobject_container"><span class="ltx_foreignobject_content">
<span id="A2.SS1.SSS2.Px2.p19.pic1.2" class="ltx_inline-block ltx_minipage ltx_align_bottom" style="width:33.06em;">
<span id="A2.SS1.SSS2.Px2.p19.pic1.2.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.SS1.SSS2.Px2.p19.pic1.2.1.1" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:80%;--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">The response didn’t state the correct commutation relations of the generators.</span></span>
<span id="A2.Ex47" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<span><span class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<span class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></span>
<span class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A2.Ex47.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\left[\mathcal{L}_{i},\mathcal{L}_{j}\right]=\frac{4}{\left(x_{i}-x_{j}\right)^{2}}\left(\mathcal{L}_{j}-\mathcal{L}_{i}\right)" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">[</mo><mrow><msub><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic" mathcolor="#000000" mathsize="0.800em">ℒ</mi><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" mathsize="0.800em">i</mi></msub><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" mathsize="0.800em">,</mo><msub><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic" mathcolor="#000000" mathsize="0.800em">ℒ</mi><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" mathsize="0.800em">j</mi></msub></mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">]</mo></mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" mathsize="0.800em">=</mo><mrow><mfrac style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000"><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" mathsize="0.800em">4</mn><msup><mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" mathsize="0.800em">x</mi><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" mathsize="0.800em">i</mi></msub><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" mathsize="0.800em">−</mo><msub><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" mathsize="0.800em">x</mi><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" mathsize="0.800em">j</mi></msub></mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">)</mo></mrow><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" mathsize="0.800em">2</mn></msup></mfrac><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic" mathcolor="#000000" mathsize="0.800em">ℒ</mi><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" mathsize="0.800em">j</mi></msub><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" mathsize="0.800em">−</mo><msub><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic" mathcolor="#000000" mathsize="0.800em">ℒ</mi><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" mathsize="0.800em">i</mi></msub></mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\left[\mathcal{L}_{i},\mathcal{L}_{j}\right]=\frac{4}{\left(x_{i}-x_{j}\right)^{2}}\left(\mathcal{L}_{j}-\mathcal{L}_{i}\right)</annotation></semantics></math></span>
<span class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></span></span></span>
</span>
</span></span></span></foreignObject></g></g></svg></span>
</div>
</section>
</section>
</section>
<section id="A2.SS2" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">2 </span>Understanding Knowledge and Theory Mastery</h3>

<section id="A2.SS2.SSS1" class="ltx_subsubsection">
<h4 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsubsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsubsection">(a) </span>Understanding theorems</h4>

<section id="A2.SS2.SSS1.Px1" class="ltx_paragraph">
<h5 class="ltx_title ltx_title_paragraph" style="--ltx-fg-color:#FF0000;">Problem 2a1</h5>

<div id="A2.SS2.SSS1.Px1.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A2.SS2.SSS1.Px1.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.SS2.SSS1.Px1.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text"></span>
<br class="ltx_break" style="--ltx-break-space:-10.0pt;"></p>
</div>
<div id="A2.SS2.SSS1.Px1.p2" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent"><span class="ltx_inline-block"><svg id="A2.SS2.SSS1.Px1.p2.pic1" class="ltx_picture" height="116.92" overflow="visible" version="1.1" viewBox="0 0 429.64 116.92" width="429.64"><g style="--ltx-stroke-color:#000000;--ltx-fill-color:#000000;" fill="#000000" stroke="#000000" stroke-width="0.4pt" transform="translate(0,116.92) matrix(1 0 0 -1 0 0)"><g style="--ltx-fill-color:#3D6666;" fill="#3D6666" fill-opacity="1.0"><path style="stroke:none" d="M 0 4.63 L 0 112.29 C 0 114.85 2.07 116.92 4.63 116.92 L 425.01 116.92 C 427.56 116.92 429.64 114.85 429.64 112.29 L 429.64 4.63 C 429.64 2.07 427.56 0 425.01 0 L 4.63 0 C 2.07 0 0 2.07 0 4.63 Z"></path></g><g style="--ltx-fill-color:#F9F9F9;" fill="#F9F9F9" fill-opacity="1.0"><path style="stroke:none" d="M 0.69 4.63 L 0.69 98.05 L 428.94 98.05 L 428.94 4.63 C 428.94 2.45 427.18 0.69 425.01 0.69 L 4.63 0.69 C 2.45 0.69 0.69 2.45 0.69 4.63 Z"></path></g><g fill-opacity="1.0" transform="matrix(1.0 0.0 0.0 1.0 20.38 102.68)"><foreignObject style="--ltx-fo-width:24.44em;--ltx-fo-height:0.69em;--ltx-fo-depth:0em;font-size:10pt;" height="9.61" overflow="visible" transform="matrix(1 0 0 -1 0 9.61)" width="338.18"><span class="ltx_foreignobject_container"><span class="ltx_foreignobject_content">
<span id="A2.SS2.SSS1.Px1.p2.pic1.1" class="ltx_inline-block ltx_minipage ltx_align_bottom" style="width:24.44em;">
<span id="A2.SS2.SSS1.Px1.p2.pic1.1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.SS2.SSS1.Px1.p2.pic1.1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold" style="--ltx-fg-color:#FFFFFF;">Problem</span></span>
</span></span></span></foreignObject></g><g fill-opacity="1.0" transform="matrix(1.0 0.0 0.0 1.0 20.38 14.66)"><foreignObject style="--ltx-fo-width:32.01em;--ltx-fo-height:5.17em;--ltx-fo-depth:0.16em;font-size:10pt;" height="73.74" overflow="visible" transform="matrix(1 0 0 -1 0 71.59)" width="442.93"><span class="ltx_foreignobject_container"><span class="ltx_foreignobject_content">
<span id="A2.SS2.SSS1.Px1.p2.pic1.2" class="ltx_inline-block ltx_minipage ltx_align_bottom" style="width:32.01em;">
<span id="A2.SS2.SSS1.Px1.p2.pic1.2.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.SS2.SSS1.Px1.p2.pic1.2.1.1" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:80%;--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">Derive the null vector equations from commutation relations of multiple chordal SLE(<math id="A2.SS2.SSS1.Px1.p2.pic1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\kappa" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">κ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\kappa</annotation></semantics></math>)</span></span><span class="ltx_inline-block"><svg id="A2.SS2.SSS1.Px1.p2.pic1.pic1" class="ltx_picture" color="#FF0000" height="18.24" overflow="visible" style="vertical-align:-4.1px" version="1.1" viewBox="0 0 18.24 18.24" width="18.24"><g style="--ltx-stroke-color:#FF0000;--ltx-fill-color:#FF0000;" fill="#FF0000" stroke="#FF0000" stroke-width="1.8pt" transform="translate(0,18.24) matrix(1 0 0 -1 0 0) translate(1.25,0) translate(0,1.25)"><path style="fill:none" d="M 0 0 L 15.75 15.75 M 0 15.75 L 15.75 0"></path></g></svg></span>
<span id="A2.SS2.SSS1.Px1.p2.pic1.2.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.SS2.SSS1.Px1.p2.pic1.2.2.1" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:80%;--ltx-fg-color:#FF0000;">GPT-5 thinking failed</span></span>
<span id="A2.SS2.SSS1.Px1.p2.pic1.2.3" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.SS2.SSS1.Px1.p2.pic1.2.3.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic" style="font-size:80%;--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">Proposed by Jiaxin Zhang</span></span>
</span></span></span></foreignObject></g></g></svg></span>
</div>
<div id="A2.SS2.SSS1.Px1.1" class="ltx_proof">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_font_italic ltx_title_proof"><span id="A2.SS2.SSS1.Px1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Response of GPT-5-thinking</span>.</h6>
<div id="A2.SS2.SSS1.Px1.p3" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A2.SS2.SSS1.Px1.p3.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.SS2.SSS1.Px1.p3.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Set-up.<span id="A2.SS2.SSS1.Px1.p3.1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_medium">
Let <math id="A2.SS2.SSS1.Px1.p3.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="x_{1}&lt;\cdots&lt;x_{n}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>x</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo rspace="0.1389em">&lt;</mo><mo lspace="0.1389em" rspace="0.1389em">⋯</mo><mo lspace="0.1389em">&lt;</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>n</mi></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">x_{1}&lt;\cdots&lt;x_{n}</annotation></semantics></math> be marked boundary points on <math id="A2.SS2.SSS1.Px1.p3.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbb{R}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>ℝ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbb{R}</annotation></semantics></math>, and write the “bare” Loewner operators</span></span></p>
<table id="A2.Ex48" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A2.Ex48.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\mathcal{A}_{i}\;=\;\frac{\kappa}{2}\,\partial_{x_{i}}^{2}\;+\;\sum_{k\neq i}\frac{2}{x_{k}-x_{i}}\,\partial_{x_{k}}\qquad(i=1,\dots,n)." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒜</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo lspace="0.558em" rspace="0.558em">=</mo><mfrac><mi>κ</mi><mn>2</mn></mfrac><msubsup><mo>∂</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mn>2</mn></msubsup><mo rspace="0.335em">+</mo><munder><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>≠</mo><mi>i</mi></mrow></munder><mfrac><mn>2</mn><mrow><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></mrow></mfrac><msub><mo>∂</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>k</mi></msub></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>i</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>n</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{A}_{i}\;=\;\frac{\kappa}{2}\,\partial_{x_{i}}^{2}\;+\;\sum_{k\neq i}\frac{2}{x_{k}-x_{i}}\,\partial_{x_{k}}\qquad(i=1,\dots,n).</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A2.SS2.SSS1.Px1.p3.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.SS2.SSS1.Px1.p3.2.1" class="ltx_text">Let <math id="A2.SS2.SSS1.Px1.p3.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="Z=Z(x_{1},\dots,x_{n})&gt;0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>Z</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>Z</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>n</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>&gt;</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">Z=Z(x_{1},\dots,x_{n})&gt;0</annotation></semantics></math> be a smooth, Möbius–covariant partition function with boundary weight <math id="A2.SS2.SSS1.Px1.p3.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="h" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>h</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">h</annotation></semantics></math>, i.e.</span></p>
<table id="A2.Ex49" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A2.Ex49.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="Z(\phi(x_{1}),\dots,\phi(x_{n}))\;=\;\prod_{m=1}^{n}|\phi^{\prime}(x_{m})|^{h}\,Z(x_{1},\dots,x_{n})\quad\text{for all }\phi\in\mathrm{PSL}_{2}(\mathbb{R})." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>Z</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>ϕ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>,</mo><mrow><mi>ϕ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>n</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.280em" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.391em">=</mo><mrow><munderover><mo movablelimits="false" rspace="0em">∏</mo><mrow><mi>m</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>n</mi></munderover><mrow><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mrow><msup><mi>ϕ</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>m</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow><mi>h</mi></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>Z</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>n</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mspace style="width:1em;" width="1em"></mspace><mrow><mrow><mtext>for all </mtext><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>ϕ</mi></mrow><mo>∈</mo><mrow><msub><mi>PSL</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>ℝ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">Z(\phi(x_{1}),\dots,\phi(x_{n}))\;=\;\prod_{m=1}^{n}|\phi^{\prime}(x_{m})|^{h}\,Z(x_{1},\dots,x_{n})\quad\text{for all }\phi\in\mathrm{PSL}_{2}(\mathbb{R}).</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A2.SS2.SSS1.Px1.p3.3" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.SS2.SSS1.Px1.p3.3.1" class="ltx_text">Tilt the dynamics by <math id="A2.SS2.SSS1.Px1.p3.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="Z" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>Z</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">Z</annotation></semantics></math> (Doob transform) and define</span></p>
<table id="A2.Ex50" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A2.Ex50.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{L}_{i}f\;:=\;Z^{-1}\,\mathcal{A}_{i}\,(Zf)." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℒ</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>f</mi></mrow><mo lspace="0.558em" rspace="0.558em">:=</mo><mrow><msup><mi>Z</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒜</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>Z</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>f</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{L}_{i}f\;:=\;Z^{-1}\,\mathcal{A}_{i}\,(Zf).</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A2.SS2.SSS1.Px1.p3.4" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.SS2.SSS1.Px1.p3.4.1" class="ltx_text">A direct expansion gives</span></p>
<table id="A2.Ex51" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A2.Ex51.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\mathcal{L}_{i}\;=\;\frac{\kappa}{2}\,\partial_{x_{i}}^{2}\;+\;\sum_{k\neq i}\frac{2}{x_{k}-x_{i}}\,\partial_{x_{k}}\;+\;\kappa\,(\partial_{x_{i}}\log Z)\,\partial_{x_{i}}\;+\;V_{i}(x)\,," display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℒ</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo lspace="0.558em" rspace="0.558em">=</mo><mfrac><mi>κ</mi><mn>2</mn></mfrac><msubsup><mo>∂</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mn>2</mn></msubsup><mo rspace="0.335em">+</mo><munder><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>≠</mo><mi>i</mi></mrow></munder><mfrac><mn>2</mn><mrow><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></mrow></mfrac><msub><mo>∂</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>k</mi></msub></msub><mo rspace="0.502em">+</mo><mi>κ</mi><mrow><mo lspace="0.170em" stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.167em">∂</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></msub><mi>log</mi><mi>Z</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><msub><mo>∂</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></msub><mo rspace="0.502em">+</mo><msub><mi>V</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo rspace="0.170em" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{L}_{i}\;=\;\frac{\kappa}{2}\,\partial_{x_{i}}^{2}\;+\;\sum_{k\neq i}\frac{2}{x_{k}-x_{i}}\,\partial_{x_{k}}\;+\;\kappa\,(\partial_{x_{i}}\log Z)\,\partial_{x_{i}}\;+\;V_{i}(x)\,,</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A2.SS2.SSS1.Px1.p3.5" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.SS2.SSS1.Px1.p3.5.1" class="ltx_text">where the zero-th order term is</span></p>
<table id="A2.Ex52" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A2.Ex52.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="V_{i}(x)\;=\;\frac{\kappa}{2}\,\partial_{x_{i}}^{2}\log Z\;+\;\sum_{k\neq i}\frac{2}{x_{k}-x_{i}}\,\partial_{x_{k}}\log Z\;+\;\frac{\kappa}{2}\big(\partial_{x_{i}}\log Z\big)^{2}." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>V</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo rspace="0.280em" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.558em">=</mo><mrow><mrow><mfrac><mi>κ</mi><mn>2</mn></mfrac><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><msubsup><mo rspace="0.167em">∂</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mn>2</mn></msubsup><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><mi>Z</mi></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0.502em" rspace="0.335em">+</mo><mrow><munder><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>≠</mo><mi>i</mi></mrow></munder><mrow><mfrac><mn>2</mn><mrow><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></mrow></mfrac><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><msub><mo rspace="0.167em">∂</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>k</mi></msub></msub><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><mi>Z</mi></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0.502em" rspace="0.502em">+</mo><mrow><mfrac><mi>κ</mi><mn>2</mn></mfrac><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">(</mo><mrow><msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.167em">∂</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></msub><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><mi>Z</mi></mrow></mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">)</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">V_{i}(x)\;=\;\frac{\kappa}{2}\,\partial_{x_{i}}^{2}\log Z\;+\;\sum_{k\neq i}\frac{2}{x_{k}-x_{i}}\,\partial_{x_{k}}\log Z\;+\;\frac{\kappa}{2}\big(\partial_{x_{i}}\log Z\big)^{2}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
<div id="A2.SS2.SSS1.Px1.p4" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A2.SS2.SSS1.Px1.p4.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.SS2.SSS1.Px1.p4.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Commutation relations.<span id="A2.SS2.SSS1.Px1.p4.1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_medium">
The multiple-SLE commutation principle (Dubédat) is that <em id="A2.SS2.SSS1.Px1.p4.1.1.1.1" class="ltx_emph ltx_font_italic">the infinitesimal evolutions commute</em>:</span></span></p>
<table id="A2.Ex53" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A2.Ex53.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="[\mathcal{L}_{i},\mathcal{L}_{j}]\;=\;0\qquad\text{for all }i\neq j." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℒ</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℒ</mi><mi>j</mi></msub></mrow><mo rspace="0.280em" stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><mo>=</mo><mn> 0</mn></mrow><mspace style="width:2em;" width="2em"></mspace><mrow><mrow><mtext>for all </mtext><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>i</mi></mrow><mo>≠</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">[\mathcal{L}_{i},\mathcal{L}_{j}]\;=\;0\qquad\text{for all }i\neq j.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A2.SS2.SSS1.Px1.p4.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.SS2.SSS1.Px1.p4.2.1" class="ltx_text">One computes the bare commutator</span></p>
<table id="A2.Ex54" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A2.Ex54.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="[\mathcal{A}_{i},\mathcal{A}_{j}]\;=\;\frac{4}{(x_{j}-x_{i})^{2}}\,\big(\partial_{x_{j}}-\partial_{x_{i}}\big)," display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒜</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒜</mi><mi>j</mi></msub><mo rspace="0.280em" stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><mo rspace="0.558em">=</mo><mfrac><mn>4</mn><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>j</mi></msub><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup></mfrac><mrow><mo lspace="0.170em" maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">(</mo><msub><mo lspace="0em">∂</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>j</mi></msub></msub><mo rspace="0.055em">−</mo><msub><mo>∂</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></msub><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">)</mo></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">[\mathcal{A}_{i},\mathcal{A}_{j}]\;=\;\frac{4}{(x_{j}-x_{i})^{2}}\,\big(\partial_{x_{j}}-\partial_{x_{i}}\big),</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A2.SS2.SSS1.Px1.p4.3" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.SS2.SSS1.Px1.p4.3.1" class="ltx_text">so the extra terms in <math id="A2.SS2.SSS1.Px1.p4.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{L}_{i},\mathcal{L}_{j}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℒ</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℒ</mi><mi>j</mi></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{L}_{i},\mathcal{L}_{j}</annotation></semantics></math> must precisely cancel this vector field singularity. Tracking the coefficient of <math id="A2.SS2.SSS1.Px1.p4.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(x_{j}-x_{i})^{-2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>j</mi></msub><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(x_{j}-x_{i})^{-2}</annotation></semantics></math> in <math id="A2.SS2.SSS1.Px1.p4.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="[\mathcal{L}_{i},\mathcal{L}_{j}]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℒ</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℒ</mi><mi>j</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">[\mathcal{L}_{i},\mathcal{L}_{j}]</annotation></semantics></math> yields</span></p>
<table id="A2.Ex55" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A2.Ex55.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\partial_{x_{j}}V_{i}-\partial_{x_{i}}V_{j}\;=\;-\,\frac{4h}{(x_{j}-x_{i})^{3}}\,," display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mrow><msub><mo>∂</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>j</mi></msub></msub><msub><mi>V</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></mrow><mo rspace="0.055em">−</mo><mrow><msub><mo>∂</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></msub><msub><mi>V</mi><mi>j</mi></msub></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.558em">=</mo><mrow><mo>−</mo><mfrac><mrow><mn>4</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>h</mi></mrow><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>j</mi></msub><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mn>3</mn></msup></mfrac></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0.170em">,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\partial_{x_{j}}V_{i}-\partial_{x_{i}}V_{j}\;=\;-\,\frac{4h}{(x_{j}-x_{i})^{3}}\,,</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A2.SS2.SSS1.Px1.p4.4" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.SS2.SSS1.Px1.p4.4.1" class="ltx_text">which integrates (using permutation symmetry and Möbius covariance/Ward identities) to</span></p>
<table id="A2.Ex56" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A2.Ex56.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="V_{i}(x)\;=\;-\sum_{k\neq i}\frac{2h}{(x_{k}-x_{i})^{2}}\,." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>V</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo rspace="0.280em" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo rspace="0.058em">=</mo><mo rspace="0.055em">−</mo><munder><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>≠</mo><mi>i</mi></mrow></munder><mfrac><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>h</mi></mrow><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup></mfrac><mo lspace="0.170em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">V_{i}(x)\;=\;-\sum_{k\neq i}\frac{2h}{(x_{k}-x_{i})^{2}}\,.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A2.SS2.SSS1.Px1.p4.5" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.SS2.SSS1.Px1.p4.5.1" class="ltx_text">Equivalently, the vanishing of the zero-th order term in the conjugated family</span></p>
<table id="A2.Ex57" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A2.Ex57.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\boxed{\ \ \mathcal{T}_{i}\;:=\;Z\,\mathcal{L}_{i}\,Z^{-1}\;=\;\frac{\kappa}{2}\,\partial_{x_{i}}^{2}\;+\;\sum_{k\neq i}\frac{2}{x_{k}-x_{i}}\,\partial_{x_{k}}\;-\;\sum_{k\neq i}\frac{2h}{(x_{k}-x_{i})^{2}}\ \ }" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><menclose notation="box"><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒯</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>i</mi></msub><mo rspace="0.558em">:=</mo><mi>Z</mi><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℒ</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>i</mi></msub><mi>Z</mi><msup><mrow></mrow><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup><mo rspace="0.558em">=</mo><mfrac><mi>κ</mi><mn>2</mn></mfrac><mo>∂</mo><msub><mrow></mrow><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></msub><msup><mrow></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup><mo rspace="0.335em">+</mo><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><msub><mrow></mrow><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>≠</mo><mi>i</mi></mrow></msub><mfrac><mn>2</mn><mrow><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></mrow></mfrac><mo>∂</mo><msub><mrow></mrow><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>k</mi></msub></msub><mo rspace="0.335em">−</mo><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><msub><mrow></mrow><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>≠</mo><mi>i</mi></mrow></msub><mfrac><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>h</mi></mrow><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup></mfrac></mrow></menclose><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\boxed{\ \ \mathcal{T}_{i}\;:=\;Z\,\mathcal{L}_{i}\,Z^{-1}\;=\;\frac{\kappa}{2}\,\partial_{x_{i}}^{2}\;+\;\sum_{k\neq i}\frac{2}{x_{k}-x_{i}}\,\partial_{x_{k}}\;-\;\sum_{k\neq i}\frac{2h}{(x_{k}-x_{i})^{2}}\ \ }</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A2.SS2.SSS1.Px1.p4.6" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.SS2.SSS1.Px1.p4.6.1" class="ltx_text">is <em id="A2.SS2.SSS1.Px1.p4.6.1.1" class="ltx_emph ltx_font_italic">exactly</em> the condition that <math id="A2.SS2.SSS1.Px1.p4.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="Z" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>Z</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">Z</annotation></semantics></math> solves the level-two BPZ/null-vector equations:</span></p>
<table id="A2.Ex58" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A2.Ex58.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\boxed{\quad\frac{\kappa}{2}\,\partial_{x_{i}}^{2}Z\;+\;\sum_{k\neq i}\frac{2}{x_{k}-x_{i}}\,\partial_{x_{k}}Z\;-\;\sum_{k\neq i}\frac{2h}{(x_{k}-x_{i})^{2}}\,Z\;=\;0\,,\qquad i=1,\dots,n.\quad}" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><menclose notation="box"><mrow><mfrac><mi>κ</mi><mn>2</mn></mfrac><mo>∂</mo><msub><mrow></mrow><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></msub><msup><mrow></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup><mi>Z</mi><mo lspace="0.502em" rspace="0.335em">+</mo><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><msub><mrow></mrow><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>≠</mo><mi>i</mi></mrow></msub><mfrac><mn>2</mn><mrow><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></mrow></mfrac><mo>∂</mo><msub><mrow></mrow><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>k</mi></msub></msub><mi>Z</mi><mo lspace="0.502em" rspace="0.335em">−</mo><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><msub><mrow></mrow><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>≠</mo><mi>i</mi></mrow></msub><mfrac><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>h</mi></mrow><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup></mfrac><mi>Z</mi><mo lspace="0.558em">=</mo><mn> 0</mn><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="2.167em">,</mo><mi>i</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>n</mi><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow></menclose><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\boxed{\quad\frac{\kappa}{2}\,\partial_{x_{i}}^{2}Z\;+\;\sum_{k\neq i}\frac{2}{x_{k}-x_{i}}\,\partial_{x_{k}}Z\;-\;\sum_{k\neq i}\frac{2h}{(x_{k}-x_{i})^{2}}\,Z\;=\;0\,,\qquad i=1,\dots,n.\quad}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
<div id="A2.SS2.SSS1.Px1.p5" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A2.SS2.SSS1.Px1.p5.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.SS2.SSS1.Px1.p5.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Fixing the weight <math id="A2.SS2.SSS1.Px1.p5.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="h" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>h</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">h</annotation></semantics></math>.<span id="A2.SS2.SSS1.Px1.p5.1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_medium">
The Möbius covariance of <math id="A2.SS2.SSS1.Px1.p5.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="Z" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>Z</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">Z</annotation></semantics></math> (global conformal Ward identities)</span></span></p>
<table id="A2.Ex59" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A2.Ex59.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\sum_{m}\partial_{x_{m}}Z=0,\qquad\sum_{m}\big(x_{m}\partial_{x_{m}}+2h\big)Z=0,\qquad\sum_{m}\big(x_{m}^{2}\partial_{x_{m}}+2h\,x_{m}\big)Z=0" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><munder><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mi>m</mi></munder><msub><mo lspace="0.167em">∂</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>m</mi></msub></msub><mi>Z</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn><mo rspace="2.000em">,</mo><munder><mo movablelimits="false" rspace="0em">∑</mo><mi>m</mi></munder><mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">(</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>m</mi></msub><msub><mo lspace="0em">∂</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>m</mi></msub></msub><mo>+</mo><mn>2</mn><mi>h</mi><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">)</mo></mrow><mi>Z</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn><mo rspace="2.000em">,</mo><munder><mo movablelimits="false" rspace="0em">∑</mo><mi>m</mi></munder><mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">(</mo><msubsup><mi>x</mi><mi>m</mi><mn>2</mn></msubsup><msub><mo lspace="0em">∂</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>m</mi></msub></msub><mo>+</mo><mn>2</mn><mi>h</mi><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>m</mi></msub><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">)</mo></mrow><mi>Z</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\sum_{m}\partial_{x_{m}}Z=0,\qquad\sum_{m}\big(x_{m}\partial_{x_{m}}+2h\big)Z=0,\qquad\sum_{m}\big(x_{m}^{2}\partial_{x_{m}}+2h\,x_{m}\big)Z=0</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A2.SS2.SSS1.Px1.p5.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.SS2.SSS1.Px1.p5.2.1" class="ltx_text">is compatible with the commuting family <math id="A2.SS2.SSS1.Px1.p5.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\{\mathcal{T}_{i}\}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒯</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\{\mathcal{T}_{i}\}</annotation></semantics></math> only when</span></p>
<table id="A2.Ex60" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A2.Ex60.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\boxed{\quad h=\frac{6-\kappa}{2\kappa}\,.\quad}" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><menclose notation="box"><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>h</mi><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mrow><mn>6</mn><mo>−</mo><mi>κ</mi></mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>κ</mi></mrow></mfrac></mrow><mo lspace="0.170em">.</mo></mrow><mspace style="width:1.167em;" width="1.167em"></mspace></mrow></menclose><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\boxed{\quad h=\frac{6-\kappa}{2\kappa}\,.\quad}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A2.SS2.SSS1.Px1.p5.3" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.SS2.SSS1.Px1.p5.3.1" class="ltx_text">With this choice, the operators <math id="A2.SS2.SSS1.Px1.p5.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\{\mathcal{T}_{i}\}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒯</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\{\mathcal{T}_{i}\}</annotation></semantics></math> <em id="A2.SS2.SSS1.Px1.p5.3.1.1" class="ltx_emph ltx_font_italic">commute</em>, and the Doob-transformed generators <math id="A2.SS2.SSS1.Px1.p5.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\{\mathcal{L}_{i}\}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℒ</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\{\mathcal{L}_{i}\}</annotation></semantics></math> commute as required.</span></p>
</div>
<div id="A2.SS2.SSS1.Px1.p6" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A2.SS2.SSS1.Px1.p6.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.SS2.SSS1.Px1.p6.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Conclusion.<span id="A2.SS2.SSS1.Px1.p6.1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_medium">
Thus, the requirement that the infinitesimal multiple-SLE evolutions commute, together with Möbius covariance, forces the partition function <math id="A2.SS2.SSS1.Px1.p6.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="Z" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>Z</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">Z</annotation></semantics></math> to satisfy the <em id="A2.SS2.SSS1.Px1.p6.1.1.1.1" class="ltx_emph ltx_font_italic">level-two null-vector/BPZ equations</em> above (with <math id="A2.SS2.SSS1.Px1.p6.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="h=(6-\kappa)/(2\kappa)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>h</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>6</mn><mo>−</mo><mi>κ</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>/</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>κ</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">h=(6-\kappa)/(2\kappa)</annotation></semantics></math>). Conversely, any positive Möbius-covariant <math id="A2.SS2.SSS1.Px1.p6.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="Z" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>Z</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">Z</annotation></semantics></math> solving these PDEs yields a commuting family and hence a well-defined multiple chordal SLE<sub id="A2.SS2.SSS1.Px1.p6.1.1.1.2" class="ltx_sub"><span id="A2.SS2.SSS1.Px1.p6.1.1.1.2.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">κ</span></sub> law.</span></span></p>
</div>
<div id="A2.SS2.SSS1.Px1.p7" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A2.SS2.SSS1.Px1.p7.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.SS2.SSS1.Px1.p7.1.1" class="ltx_text">∎</span></p>
</div>
</div>
<div id="A2.SS2.SSS1.Px1.2" class="ltx_proof">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_font_italic ltx_title_proof"><span id="A2.SS2.SSS1.Px1.2.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Standard Solution</span>.</h6>
<div id="A2.SS2.SSS1.Px1.p8" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A2.SS2.SSS1.Px1.p8.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.SS2.SSS1.Px1.p8.1.1" class="ltx_text">Please refer to the paper <a href="https://Commutation%20relations%20for%20SLE" title="" class="ltx_ref ltx_href">https://arxiv.org/abs/math/0411299</a></span></p>
</div>
<div id="A2.SS2.SSS1.Px1.p9" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A2.SS2.SSS1.Px1.p9.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.SS2.SSS1.Px1.p9.1.1" class="ltx_text">We have seen natural examples where two SLEs could be grown in a common domain in a consistent fashion. In this section, discuss necessary infinitesimal conditions. We shall define a "global" commutation condition, of geometric nature, and express its consequence in terms of infinitesimal generators, which is of algebraic nature.</span></p>
</div>
<div id="A2.SS2.SSS1.Px1.p10" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A2.SS2.SSS1.Px1.p10.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.SS2.SSS1.Px1.p10.1.1" class="ltx_text">Let us consider the following chordal situation: the domain is <math id="A2.SS2.SSS1.Px1.p10.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbb{H}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>ℍ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbb{H}</annotation></semantics></math>, SLEs aim at <math id="A2.SS2.SSS1.Px1.p10.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\infty" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi mathvariant="normal">∞</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\infty</annotation></semantics></math>, and <math id="A2.SS2.SSS1.Px1.p10.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(x,y,z_{1},\ldots,z_{n})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>y</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>z</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>z</mi><mi>n</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(x,y,z_{1},\ldots,z_{n})</annotation></semantics></math> are <math id="A2.SS2.SSS1.Px1.p10.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(n+2)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(n+2)</annotation></semantics></math> (distinct) points on the real line; the point at infinity is also a marked point. We want to grow two infinitesimal hulls (with capacity of order <math id="A2.SS2.SSS1.Px1.p10.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\varepsilon" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>ε</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\varepsilon</annotation></semantics></math> ) at <math id="A2.SS2.SSS1.Px1.p10.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="x" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>x</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">x</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="A2.SS2.SSS1.Px1.p10.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="z" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>z</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">z</annotation></semantics></math> respectively. We can either grow a hull <math id="A2.SS2.SSS1.Px1.p10.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="K_{\varepsilon}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>K</mi><mi>ε</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">K_{\varepsilon}</annotation></semantics></math> at <math id="A2.SS2.SSS1.Px1.p10.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="x" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>x</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">x</annotation></semantics></math>, and then another one at <math id="A2.SS2.SSS1.Px1.p10.m10" class="ltx_Math" alttext="y" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>y</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">y</annotation></semantics></math> in the pertubed domain <math id="A2.SS2.SSS1.Px1.p10.m11" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbb{H}\backslash K_{\varepsilon}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>ℍ</mi><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">\</mo><msub><mi>K</mi><mi>ε</mi></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbb{H}\backslash K_{\varepsilon}</annotation></semantics></math>, or proceed in the other order. The coherence condition is that these two procedures yield the same result.</span></p>
</div>
<div id="A2.SS2.SSS1.Px1.p11" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A2.SS2.SSS1.Px1.p11.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.SS2.SSS1.Px1.p11.1.1" class="ltx_text">Let us make things more rigorous. Consider a Loewner chain <math id="A2.SS2.SSS1.Px1.p11.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\left(K_{s,t}\right)_{(s,t)\in\mathcal{T}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mrow><mo>(</mo><msub><mi>K</mi><mrow><mi>s</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></msub><mo>)</mo></mrow><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>s</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>∈</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒯</mi></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\left(K_{s,t}\right)_{(s,t)\in\mathcal{T}}</annotation></semantics></math> with a double time index, so that <math id="A2.SS2.SSS1.Px1.p11.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="K_{s,t}\subset K_{s^{\prime},t^{\prime}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>K</mi><mrow><mi>s</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></msub><mo>⊂</mo><msub><mi>K</mi><mrow><msup><mi>s</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo>,</mo><msup><mi>t</mi><mo>′</mo></msup></mrow></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">K_{s,t}\subset K_{s^{\prime},t^{\prime}}</annotation></semantics></math> if <math id="A2.SS2.SSS1.Px1.p11.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="s^{\prime}\geq s,t^{\prime}\geq t" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msup><mi>s</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo>≥</mo><mi>s</mi></mrow><mo>,</mo><mrow><msup><mi>t</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo>≥</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">s^{\prime}\geq s,t^{\prime}\geq t</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="A2.SS2.SSS1.Px1.p11.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="K_{s,t}\neq K_{s^{\prime},t^{\prime}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>K</mi><mrow><mi>s</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></msub><mo>≠</mo><msub><mi>K</mi><mrow><msup><mi>s</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo>,</mo><msup><mi>t</mi><mo>′</mo></msup></mrow></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">K_{s,t}\neq K_{s^{\prime},t^{\prime}}</annotation></semantics></math> if <math id="A2.SS2.SSS1.Px1.p11.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\left(s^{\prime},t^{\prime}\right)\neq(s,t)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mo>(</mo><msup><mi>s</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo>,</mo><msup><mi>t</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo>)</mo></mrow><mo>≠</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>s</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\left(s^{\prime},t^{\prime}\right)\neq(s,t)</annotation></semantics></math>. We only consider chains up to time reparameterization <math id="A2.SS2.SSS1.Px1.p11.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbb{R}_{+}^{2}\rightarrow\mathbb{R}_{+}^{2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msubsup><mi>ℝ</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>2</mn></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><msubsup><mi>ℝ</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>2</mn></msubsup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbb{R}_{+}^{2}\rightarrow\mathbb{R}_{+}^{2}</annotation></semantics></math>. We also assume that <math id="A2.SS2.SSS1.Px1.p11.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="K_{s,t}=K_{s,0}\cup K_{0,t}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>K</mi><mrow><mi>s</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><msub><mi>K</mi><mrow><mi>s</mi><mo>,</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow></msub><mo>∪</mo><msub><mi>K</mi><mrow><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></msub></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">K_{s,t}=K_{s,0}\cup K_{0,t}</annotation></semantics></math>. The time set <math id="A2.SS2.SSS1.Px1.p11.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{T}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒯</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{T}</annotation></semantics></math> may be random, but includes a.s. a neighbourhood of ( 0,0 ) in <math id="A2.SS2.SSS1.Px1.p11.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbb{R}_{+}^{2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mi>ℝ</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>2</mn></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbb{R}_{+}^{2}</annotation></semantics></math>. Also, if <math id="A2.SS2.SSS1.Px1.p11.m10" class="ltx_Math" alttext="s\leq s^{\prime},t\leq t^{\prime},\left(s^{\prime},t^{\prime}\right)\in\mathcal{T}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>s</mi><mo>≤</mo><msup><mi>s</mi><mo>′</mo></msup></mrow><mo>,</mo><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>≤</mo><msup><mi>t</mi><mo>′</mo></msup></mrow><mo>,</mo><mrow><mrow><mo>(</mo><msup><mi>s</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo>,</mo><msup><mi>t</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo>)</mo></mrow><mo>∈</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒯</mi></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">s\leq s^{\prime},t\leq t^{\prime},\left(s^{\prime},t^{\prime}\right)\in\mathcal{T}</annotation></semantics></math>, then <math id="A2.SS2.SSS1.Px1.p11.m11" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(s,t)\in\mathcal{T}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>s</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>∈</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒯</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(s,t)\in\mathcal{T}</annotation></semantics></math>. Define <math id="A2.SS2.SSS1.Px1.p11.m12" class="ltx_Math" alttext="g_{s,t}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>g</mi><mrow><mi>s</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">g_{s,t}</annotation></semantics></math> the conformal equivalence <math id="A2.SS2.SSS1.Px1.p11.m13" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbb{H}\backslash K_{s,t}\rightarrow\mathbb{H}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>ℍ</mi><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">\</mo><msub><mi>K</mi><mrow><mi>s</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><mi>ℍ</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbb{H}\backslash K_{s,t}\rightarrow\mathbb{H}</annotation></semantics></math> with hydrodynamic normalization at infinity ( <math id="A2.SS2.SSS1.Px1.p11.m14" class="ltx_Math" alttext="g_{s,t}=\phi_{K_{s,t}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>g</mi><mrow><mi>s</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></msub><mo>=</mo><msub><mi>ϕ</mi><msub><mi>K</mi><mrow><mi>s</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></msub></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">g_{s,t}=\phi_{K_{s,t}}</annotation></semantics></math> with the earlier notation), and the continuous traces <math id="A2.SS2.SSS1.Px1.p11.m15" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\gamma,\tilde{\gamma}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>γ</mi><mo>,</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>γ</mi><mo>~</mo></mover></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\gamma,\tilde{\gamma}</annotation></semantics></math>, such that:</span></p>
</div>
<div id="A2.SS2.SSS1.Px1.p12" class="ltx_para">
<table id="A2.Ex61" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A2.Ex61.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\gamma_{s,t}=\lim_{\varepsilon\searrow 0}\overline{g_{s,t}\left(K_{s+\varepsilon,t}\backslash K_{s,t}\right)},\tilde{\gamma}_{s,t}=\lim_{\varepsilon\searrow 0}\overline{g_{s,t}\left(K_{s,t+\varepsilon}\backslash K_{s,t}\right)}" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>γ</mi><mrow><mi>s</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></msub><mo rspace="0.1389em">=</mo><mrow><munder><mo lspace="0.1389em" movablelimits="false" rspace="0.167em">lim</mo><mrow><mi>ε</mi><mo>↘</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow></munder><mover accent="true"><mrow><msub><mi>g</mi><mrow><mi>s</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>K</mi><mrow><mrow><mi>s</mi><mo>+</mo><mi>ε</mi></mrow><mo>,</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">\</mo><msub><mi>K</mi><mrow><mi>s</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></msub></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="true">¯</mo></mover></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>γ</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mrow><mi>s</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></msub><mo rspace="0.1389em">=</mo><mrow><munder><mo lspace="0.1389em" movablelimits="false" rspace="0.167em">lim</mo><mrow><mi>ε</mi><mo>↘</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow></munder><mover accent="true"><mrow><msub><mi>g</mi><mrow><mi>s</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>K</mi><mrow><mi>s</mi><mo>,</mo><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>+</mo><mi>ε</mi></mrow></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">\</mo><msub><mi>K</mi><mrow><mi>s</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></msub></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="true">¯</mo></mover></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\gamma_{s,t}=\lim_{\varepsilon\searrow 0}\overline{g_{s,t}\left(K_{s+\varepsilon,t}\backslash K_{s,t}\right)},\tilde{\gamma}_{s,t}=\lim_{\varepsilon\searrow 0}\overline{g_{s,t}\left(K_{s,t+\varepsilon}\backslash K_{s,t}\right)}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
<div id="A2.SS2.SSS1.Px1.p13" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A2.SS2.SSS1.Px1.p13.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.SS2.SSS1.Px1.p13.1.1" class="ltx_text">where <math id="A2.SS2.SSS1.Px1.p13.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\gamma_{0,t}=x" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>γ</mi><mrow><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></msub><mo>=</mo><mi>x</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\gamma_{0,t}=x</annotation></semantics></math> for all <math id="A2.SS2.SSS1.Px1.p13.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(0,t)\in\mathcal{T}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>∈</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒯</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(0,t)\in\mathcal{T}</annotation></semantics></math>, and similarly <math id="A2.SS2.SSS1.Px1.p13.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\tilde{\gamma}_{s,0}=y" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>γ</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mrow><mi>s</mi><mo>,</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow></msub><mo>=</mo><mi>y</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\tilde{\gamma}_{s,0}=y</annotation></semantics></math> for all <math id="A2.SS2.SSS1.Px1.p13.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(s,0)\in\mathcal{T}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>s</mi><mo>,</mo><mn>0</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>∈</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒯</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(s,0)\in\mathcal{T}</annotation></semantics></math>.
Furthermore, assume that the following conditions are satisfied:
Definition 2. Let <math id="A2.SS2.SSS1.Px1.p13.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\left(K_{s,t}\right)_{(s,t)\in\mathcal{T}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mrow><mo>(</mo><msub><mi>K</mi><mrow><mi>s</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></msub><mo>)</mo></mrow><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>s</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>∈</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒯</mi></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\left(K_{s,t}\right)_{(s,t)\in\mathcal{T}}</annotation></semantics></math> be a random Loewner chain with double time indexing; the associated conformal equivalences are <math id="A2.SS2.SSS1.Px1.p13.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="g_{s,t}=\phi_{K_{s,t}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>g</mi><mrow><mi>s</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></msub><mo>=</mo><msub><mi>ϕ</mi><msub><mi>K</mi><mrow><mi>s</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></msub></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">g_{s,t}=\phi_{K_{s,t}}</annotation></semantics></math>. We say that ( <math id="A2.SS2.SSS1.Px1.p13.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="K_{s,t}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>K</mi><mrow><mi>s</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">K_{s,t}</annotation></semantics></math> ) is an <math id="A2.SS2.SSS1.Px1.p13.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\operatorname{SLE}(\kappa,b,\tilde{\kappa},\tilde{b})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>SLE</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>κ</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>b</mi><mo>,</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>κ</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mo>,</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>b</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\operatorname{SLE}(\kappa,b,\tilde{\kappa},\tilde{b})</annotation></semantics></math> if:
(i). The time set <math id="A2.SS2.SSS1.Px1.p13.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{T}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒯</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{T}</annotation></semantics></math> is a.s. open, connected, and a neighborhood of <math id="A2.SS2.SSS1.Px1.p13.m10" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(0,0)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>0</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(0,0)</annotation></semantics></math> in <math id="A2.SS2.SSS1.Px1.p13.m11" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbb{R}_{+}^{2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mi>ℝ</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>2</mn></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbb{R}_{+}^{2}</annotation></semantics></math>. The ranges of the traces <math id="A2.SS2.SSS1.Px1.p13.m12" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\gamma_{\mathcal{T}},\tilde{\gamma}_{\mathcal{T}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>γ</mi><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒯</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>γ</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒯</mi></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\gamma_{\mathcal{T}},\tilde{\gamma}_{\mathcal{T}}</annotation></semantics></math> are disjoint and <math id="A2.SS2.SSS1.Px1.p13.m13" class="ltx_Math" alttext="z_{1},\ldots,z_{n}\notin K_{s,t}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>z</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>,</mo><mrow><msub><mi>z</mi><mi>n</mi></msub><mo>∉</mo><msub><mi>K</mi><mrow><mi>s</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></msub></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">z_{1},\ldots,z_{n}\notin K_{s,t}</annotation></semantics></math> for <math id="A2.SS2.SSS1.Px1.p13.m14" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(s,t)\in\mathcal{T}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>s</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>∈</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒯</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(s,t)\in\mathcal{T}</annotation></semantics></math>.
(ii). Let <math id="A2.SS2.SSS1.Px1.p13.m15" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\sigma" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>σ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\sigma</annotation></semantics></math> (resp. <math id="A2.SS2.SSS1.Px1.p13.m16" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\tau" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>τ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\tau</annotation></semantics></math> ) be a stopping time in the filtration generated by <math id="A2.SS2.SSS1.Px1.p13.m17" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\left(K_{s,0}\right)_{(s,0)\in\mathcal{T}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mrow><mo>(</mo><msub><mi>K</mi><mrow><mi>s</mi><mo>,</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow></msub><mo>)</mo></mrow><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>s</mi><mo>,</mo><mn>0</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>∈</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒯</mi></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\left(K_{s,0}\right)_{(s,0)\in\mathcal{T}}</annotation></semantics></math> (resp. <math id="A2.SS2.SSS1.Px1.p13.m18" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\left(K_{0,t}\right)_{(0,t)\in\mathcal{T}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mrow><mo>(</mo><msub><mi>K</mi><mrow><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></msub><mo>)</mo></mrow><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>∈</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒯</mi></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\left(K_{0,t}\right)_{(0,t)\in\mathcal{T}}</annotation></semantics></math> ). Let also <math id="A2.SS2.SSS1.Px1.p13.m19" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{T}^{\prime}=\{(s,t):(s+\sigma,t+\tau)\in\mathcal{T}\}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒯</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>s</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>t</mi><mo rspace="0.278em" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>s</mi><mo>+</mo><mi>σ</mi></mrow><mo>,</mo><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>+</mo><mi>τ</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>∈</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒯</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{T}^{\prime}=\{(s,t):(s+\sigma,t+\tau)\in\mathcal{T}\}</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="A2.SS2.SSS1.Px1.p13.m20" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\left(K_{s,t}^{\prime}\right)_{(s,t)\in\mathcal{T}^{\prime}}=\left(\overline{g_{\sigma,\tau}\left(K_{s+\sigma,t+\tau}\backslash K_{s,t}\right)}\right)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mrow><mo>(</mo><msubsup><mi>K</mi><mrow><mi>s</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow><mo>′</mo></msubsup><mo>)</mo></mrow><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>s</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>∈</mo><msup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒯</mi><mo>′</mo></msup></mrow></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mover accent="true"><mrow><msub><mi>g</mi><mrow><mi>σ</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>τ</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>K</mi><mrow><mrow><mi>s</mi><mo>+</mo><mi>σ</mi></mrow><mo>,</mo><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>+</mo><mi>τ</mi></mrow></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">\</mo><msub><mi>K</mi><mrow><mi>s</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></msub></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="true">¯</mo></mover><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\left(K_{s,t}^{\prime}\right)_{(s,t)\in\mathcal{T}^{\prime}}=\left(\overline{g_{\sigma,\tau}\left(K_{s+\sigma,t+\tau}\backslash K_{s,t}\right)}\right)</annotation></semantics></math>. Then <math id="A2.SS2.SSS1.Px1.p13.m21" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\left(K_{s,0}^{\prime}\right)_{(s,0)\in\mathcal{T}^{\prime}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mrow><mo>(</mo><msubsup><mi>K</mi><mrow><mi>s</mi><mo>,</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><mo>′</mo></msubsup><mo>)</mo></mrow><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>s</mi><mo>,</mo><mn>0</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>∈</mo><msup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒯</mi><mo>′</mo></msup></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\left(K_{s,0}^{\prime}\right)_{(s,0)\in\mathcal{T}^{\prime}}</annotation></semantics></math> is distributed as a stopped <math id="A2.SS2.SSS1.Px1.p13.m22" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathrm{SLE}_{\kappa}(b)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>SLE</mi><mi>κ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>b</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathrm{SLE}_{\kappa}(b)</annotation></semantics></math>, i.e an SLE driven by:</span></p>
</div>
<div id="A2.SS2.SSS1.Px1.p14" class="ltx_para">
<table id="A2.Ex62" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A2.Ex62.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="dX_{s}=\sqrt{\kappa}dB_{s}+b\left(X_{s},g_{s}(y),\ldots,g_{s}\left(z_{i}\right),\ldots\right)dt." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>X</mi><mi>s</mi></msub></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><msqrt><mi>κ</mi></msqrt><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>d</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>B</mi><mi>s</mi></msub></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>b</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><msub><mi>X</mi><mi>s</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><mrow><msub><mi>g</mi><mi>s</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>y</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>,</mo><mrow><msub><mi>g</mi><mi>s</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><msub><mi>z</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>d</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">dX_{s}=\sqrt{\kappa}dB_{s}+b\left(X_{s},g_{s}(y),\ldots,g_{s}\left(z_{i}\right),\ldots\right)dt.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
<div id="A2.SS2.SSS1.Px1.p15" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A2.SS2.SSS1.Px1.p15.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.SS2.SSS1.Px1.p15.1.1" class="ltx_text">Likewise <math id="A2.SS2.SSS1.Px1.p15.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\left(K_{0,t}^{\prime}\right)_{(0,t)\in\mathcal{T}^{\prime}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mrow><mo>(</mo><msubsup><mi>K</mi><mrow><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow><mo>′</mo></msubsup><mo>)</mo></mrow><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>∈</mo><msup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒯</mi><mo>′</mo></msup></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\left(K_{0,t}^{\prime}\right)_{(0,t)\in\mathcal{T}^{\prime}}</annotation></semantics></math> is distributed as a stopped <math id="A2.SS2.SSS1.Px1.p15.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\operatorname{SLE}_{\tilde{\kappa}}(\tilde{b})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>SLE</mi><mover accent="true"><mi>κ</mi><mo>~</mo></mover></msub><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>b</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\operatorname{SLE}_{\tilde{\kappa}}(\tilde{b})</annotation></semantics></math>, i.e an SLE driven by:</span></p>
</div>
<div id="A2.SS2.SSS1.Px1.p16" class="ltx_para">
<table id="A2.Ex63" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A2.Ex63.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="dY_{t}=\sqrt{\tilde{\kappa}}d\tilde{B}_{t}+\tilde{b}\left(\tilde{g}_{t}(x),Y_{t},\ldots,\tilde{g}_{t}\left(z_{i}\right),\ldots\right)dt." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>Y</mi><mi>t</mi></msub></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><msqrt><mover accent="true"><mi>κ</mi><mo>~</mo></mover></msqrt><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>d</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>B</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mi>t</mi></msub></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi>b</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>g</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mi>t</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>Y</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>,</mo><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>g</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mi>t</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><msub><mi>z</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>d</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">dY_{t}=\sqrt{\tilde{\kappa}}d\tilde{B}_{t}+\tilde{b}\left(\tilde{g}_{t}(x),Y_{t},\ldots,\tilde{g}_{t}\left(z_{i}\right),\ldots\right)dt.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
<div id="A2.SS2.SSS1.Px1.p17" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A2.SS2.SSS1.Px1.p17.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.SS2.SSS1.Px1.p17.1.1" class="ltx_text">Here <math id="A2.SS2.SSS1.Px1.p17.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="B,\tilde{B}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>B</mi><mo>,</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>B</mi><mo>~</mo></mover></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">B,\tilde{B}</annotation></semantics></math> are standard Brownian motions, <math id="A2.SS2.SSS1.Px1.p17.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\left(g_{s}\right),\left(\tilde{g}_{t}\right)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mo>(</mo><msub><mi>g</mi><mi>s</mi></msub><mo>)</mo></mrow><mo>,</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>g</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mi>t</mi></msub><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\left(g_{s}\right),\left(\tilde{g}_{t}\right)</annotation></semantics></math> are the associated conformal equivalences, <math id="A2.SS2.SSS1.Px1.p17.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="b,\tilde{b}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>b</mi><mo>,</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>b</mi><mo>~</mo></mover></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">b,\tilde{b}</annotation></semantics></math> are some smooth, translation invariant, and homogeneous of degree ( -1 ) functions. If <math id="A2.SS2.SSS1.Px1.p17.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="A^{x},A^{y}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msup><mi>A</mi><mi>x</mi></msup><mo>,</mo><msup><mi>A</mi><mi>y</mi></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">A^{x},A^{y}</annotation></semantics></math> are two increasing functions of hulls growing at <math id="A2.SS2.SSS1.Px1.p17.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="x" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>x</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">x</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="A2.SS2.SSS1.Px1.p17.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="y" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>y</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">y</annotation></semantics></math> resp. (e.g. the half-plane capacity), we shall be particularly interested in stopping times of type <math id="A2.SS2.SSS1.Px1.p17.m7" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\sigma=\inf\left(s:A^{x}\left(K_{s,0}\right)\geq a^{x}\right),\tau=\inf\left(t:A^{y}\left(K_{0,t}\right)\geq a^{y}\right)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>σ</mi><mo rspace="0.1389em">=</mo><mo lspace="0.1389em" rspace="0em">inf</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mi>s</mi><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><msup><mi>A</mi><mi>x</mi></msup><mrow><mo>(</mo><msub><mi>K</mi><mrow><mi>s</mi><mo>,</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow></msub><mo>)</mo></mrow><mo>≥</mo><msup><mi>a</mi><mi>x</mi></msup><mo>)</mo></mrow><mo>,</mo><mi>τ</mi><mo rspace="0.1389em">=</mo><mo lspace="0.1389em" rspace="0em">inf</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><msup><mi>A</mi><mi>y</mi></msup><mrow><mo>(</mo><msub><mi>K</mi><mrow><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></msub><mo>)</mo></mrow><mo>≥</mo><msup><mi>a</mi><mi>y</mi></msup><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\sigma=\inf\left(s:A^{x}\left(K_{s,0}\right)\geq a^{x}\right),\tau=\inf\left(t:A^{y}\left(K_{0,t}\right)\geq a^{y}\right)</annotation></semantics></math>.</span></p>
</div>
<div id="A2.SS2.SSS1.Px1.p18" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A2.SS2.SSS1.Px1.p18.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.SS2.SSS1.Px1.p18.1.1" class="ltx_text">Note that <math id="A2.SS2.SSS1.Px1.p18.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\left(X_{s},\ldots,g_{t}\left(z_{i}\right),\ldots\right)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo>(</mo><msub><mi>X</mi><mi>s</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>,</mo><mrow><msub><mi>g</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><msub><mi>z</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\left(X_{s},\ldots,g_{t}\left(z_{i}\right),\ldots\right)</annotation></semantics></math> is a Markov process. Let <math id="A2.SS2.SSS1.Px1.p18.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="P" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>P</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">P</annotation></semantics></math> be its semigroup and <math id="A2.SS2.SSS1.Px1.p18.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{L}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℒ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{L}</annotation></semantics></math> its infinitesimal generator. Similarly, ( <math id="A2.SS2.SSS1.Px1.p18.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\tilde{g}_{t}(\hat{x}),Y_{t},\ldots" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>g</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mi>t</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>x</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>Y</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\tilde{g}_{t}(\hat{x}),Y_{t},\ldots</annotation></semantics></math> ) is a Markov process with semigroup <math id="A2.SS2.SSS1.Px1.p18.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="Q" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>Q</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">Q</annotation></semantics></math> and infinitesimal generator <math id="A2.SS2.SSS1.Px1.p18.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{M}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℳ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{M}</annotation></semantics></math>. We are interested in what conditions on the functions <math id="A2.SS2.SSS1.Px1.p18.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="b" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>b</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">b</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="A2.SS2.SSS1.Px1.p18.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\tilde{b}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mover accent="true"><mi>b</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\tilde{b}</annotation></semantics></math> are implied by these assumptions (the existence of an <math id="A2.SS2.SSS1.Px1.p18.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\operatorname{SLE}(\kappa,b,\tilde{\kappa},\tilde{b}))" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo fence="true" rspace="0em">OPEN</mo><mrow><mi>SLE</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>κ</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>b</mi><mo>,</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>κ</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mo>,</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>b</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\operatorname{SLE}(\kappa,b,\tilde{\kappa},\tilde{b}))</annotation></semantics></math>.</span></p>
</div>
<div id="A2.SS2.SSS1.Px1.p19" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A2.SS2.SSS1.Px1.p19.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.SS2.SSS1.Px1.p19.1.1" class="ltx_text">So let <math id="A2.SS2.SSS1.Px1.p19.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="F" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>F</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">F</annotation></semantics></math> be a test function <math id="A2.SS2.SSS1.Px1.p19.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbb{R}^{n+2}\rightarrow\mathbb{R}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msup><mi>ℝ</mi><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></msup><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><mi>ℝ</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbb{R}^{n+2}\rightarrow\mathbb{R}</annotation></semantics></math>, and <math id="A2.SS2.SSS1.Px1.p19.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="c&gt;0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>c</mi><mo>&gt;</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">c&gt;0</annotation></semantics></math> be some constant (ratio of speeds). We apply the previous assumptions with <math id="A2.SS2.SSS1.Px1.p19.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="A^{x}=A^{y}=" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msup><mi>A</mi><mi>x</mi></msup><mo>=</mo><msup><mi>A</mi><mi>y</mi></msup><mo>=</mo><mphantom></mphantom></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">A^{x}=A^{y}=</annotation></semantics></math> cap (the half-plane capacity), <math id="A2.SS2.SSS1.Px1.p19.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="a^{x}=2\varepsilon,a^{y}=2c\varepsilon" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msup><mi>a</mi><mi>x</mi></msup><mo>=</mo><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>ε</mi></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo><mrow><msup><mi>a</mi><mi>y</mi></msup><mo>=</mo><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>c</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>ε</mi></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">a^{x}=2\varepsilon,a^{y}=2c\varepsilon</annotation></semantics></math>. We are interested in the hull <math id="A2.SS2.SSS1.Px1.p19.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="K_{\sigma,\tau}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>K</mi><mrow><mi>σ</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>τ</mi></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">K_{\sigma,\tau}</annotation></semantics></math>. Two ways of getting from <math id="A2.SS2.SSS1.Px1.p19.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="K_{0,0}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>K</mi><mrow><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">K_{0,0}</annotation></semantics></math> to <math id="A2.SS2.SSS1.Px1.p19.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="K_{\sigma,\tau}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>K</mi><mrow><mi>σ</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>τ</mi></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">K_{\sigma,\tau}</annotation></semantics></math> are (symbolically):
and our assumptions give a description of these transitions.
So consider the following procedure:
- run the first SLE (i.e. <math id="A2.SS2.SSS1.Px1.p19.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathrm{SLE}_{\kappa}(b)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>SLE</mi><mi>κ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>b</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathrm{SLE}_{\kappa}(b)</annotation></semantics></math> ), started from ( <math id="A2.SS2.SSS1.Px1.p19.m10" class="ltx_Math" alttext="x,y,\ldots,z_{i},\ldots" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>y</mi><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>z</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">x,y,\ldots,z_{i},\ldots</annotation></semantics></math> ) until it reaches capacity <math id="A2.SS2.SSS1.Px1.p19.m11" class="ltx_Math" alttext="2\varepsilon" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>ε</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">2\varepsilon</annotation></semantics></math>.
- then run independently the second <math id="A2.SS2.SSS1.Px1.p19.m12" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\operatorname{SLE}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>SLE</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\operatorname{SLE}</annotation></semantics></math> (i.e. <math id="A2.SS2.SSS1.Px1.p19.m13" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\operatorname{SLE}_{\tilde{\kappa}}(\tilde{b})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>SLE</mi><mover accent="true"><mi>κ</mi><mo>~</mo></mover></msub><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>b</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\operatorname{SLE}_{\tilde{\kappa}}(\tilde{b})</annotation></semantics></math> ) in <math id="A2.SS2.SSS1.Px1.p19.m14" class="ltx_Math" alttext="g_{\varepsilon}^{-1}(\mathbb{H})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msubsup><mi>g</mi><mi>ε</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>ℍ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">g_{\varepsilon}^{-1}(\mathbb{H})</annotation></semantics></math> until it reaches capacity <math id="A2.SS2.SSS1.Px1.p19.m15" class="ltx_Math" alttext="2c\varepsilon" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>c</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>ε</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">2c\varepsilon</annotation></semantics></math>; this capacity is measured in the original half-plane. Let <math id="A2.SS2.SSS1.Px1.p19.m16" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\tilde{g}_{\tilde{\varepsilon}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>g</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mover accent="true"><mi>ε</mi><mo>~</mo></mover></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\tilde{g}_{\tilde{\varepsilon}}</annotation></semantics></math> be the corresponding conformal equivalence.
- one gets two hulls resp. at <math id="A2.SS2.SSS1.Px1.p19.m17" class="ltx_Math" alttext="x" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>x</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">x</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="A2.SS2.SSS1.Px1.p19.m18" class="ltx_Math" alttext="y" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>y</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">y</annotation></semantics></math> with capacity <math id="A2.SS2.SSS1.Px1.p19.m19" class="ltx_Math" alttext="2\varepsilon" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>ε</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">2\varepsilon</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="A2.SS2.SSS1.Px1.p19.m20" class="ltx_Math" alttext="2c\varepsilon" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>c</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>ε</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">2c\varepsilon</annotation></semantics></math>; let <math id="A2.SS2.SSS1.Px1.p19.m21" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\phi=\tilde{g}_{\tilde{\varepsilon}}\circ g_{\varepsilon}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>ϕ</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>g</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mover accent="true"><mi>ε</mi><mo>~</mo></mover></msub><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">∘</mo><msub><mi>g</mi><mi>ε</mi></msub></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\phi=\tilde{g}_{\tilde{\varepsilon}}\circ g_{\varepsilon}</annotation></semantics></math> be the normalized map removing these two hulls.
- expand <math id="A2.SS2.SSS1.Px1.p19.m22" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbb{E}\left(F\left(\tilde{g}_{\tilde{\varepsilon}}\left(X_{\varepsilon}\right),\tilde{Y}_{\tilde{\varepsilon}}\right)\right)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>𝔼</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mi>F</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>g</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mover accent="true"><mi>ε</mi><mo>~</mo></mover></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><msub><mi>X</mi><mi>ε</mi></msub><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>Y</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mover accent="true"><mi>ε</mi><mo>~</mo></mover></msub><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbb{E}\left(F\left(\tilde{g}_{\tilde{\varepsilon}}\left(X_{\varepsilon}\right),\tilde{Y}_{\tilde{\varepsilon}}\right)\right)</annotation></semantics></math> up to order two in <math id="A2.SS2.SSS1.Px1.p19.m23" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\varepsilon" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>ε</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\varepsilon</annotation></semantics></math>.</span></p>
</div>
<div id="A2.SS2.SSS1.Px1.p20" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A2.SS2.SSS1.Px1.p20.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.SS2.SSS1.Px1.p20.1.1" class="ltx_text">This describes (in distribution) how to get from <math id="A2.SS2.SSS1.Px1.p20.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="K_{0,0}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>K</mi><mrow><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">K_{0,0}</annotation></semantics></math> to <math id="A2.SS2.SSS1.Px1.p20.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="K_{\sigma,0}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>K</mi><mrow><mi>σ</mi><mo>,</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">K_{\sigma,0}</annotation></semantics></math>, and then from <math id="A2.SS2.SSS1.Px1.p20.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="K_{\sigma,0}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>K</mi><mrow><mi>σ</mi><mo>,</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">K_{\sigma,0}</annotation></semantics></math> to <math id="A2.SS2.SSS1.Px1.p20.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="K_{\sigma,\tau}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>K</mi><mrow><mi>σ</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>τ</mi></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">K_{\sigma,\tau}</annotation></semantics></math>.
From the Loewner equation, it appears that <math id="A2.SS2.SSS1.Px1.p20.m5" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\partial_{t}g_{t}^{\prime}(w)=-2g_{t}^{\prime}(w)/\left(g_{t}(w)-W_{t}\right)^{2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mo>∂</mo><mi>t</mi></msub><msubsup><mi>g</mi><mi>t</mi><mo>′</mo></msubsup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>w</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo rspace="0em">=</mo><mo lspace="0em">−</mo><mn>2</mn><msubsup><mi>g</mi><mi>t</mi><mo>′</mo></msubsup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>w</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>/</mo><msup><mrow><mo>(</mo><msub><mi>g</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>w</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>W</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo>)</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\partial_{t}g_{t}^{\prime}(w)=-2g_{t}^{\prime}(w)/\left(g_{t}(w)-W_{t}\right)^{2}</annotation></semantics></math>. Hence <math id="A2.SS2.SSS1.Px1.p20.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="g_{\varepsilon}^{\prime}(y)=1-2\varepsilon/(y-" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msubsup><mi>g</mi><mi>ε</mi><mo>′</mo></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>y</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>ε</mi></mrow><mo>/</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>y</mi><mo rspace="0em">−</mo></mrow><mo fence="true" lspace="0em">CLOSE</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">g_{\varepsilon}^{\prime}(y)=1-2\varepsilon/(y-</annotation></semantics></math> <math id="A2.SS2.SSS1.Px1.p20.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="x)^{2}+o(\varepsilon)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msup><mrow><mo fence="true" rspace="0em">OPEN</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi>o</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>ε</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">x)^{2}+o(\varepsilon)</annotation></semantics></math>. From the scaling property of half-plane capacity, we get:</span></p>
</div>
<div id="A2.SS2.SSS1.Px1.p21" class="ltx_para">
<table id="A2.Ex64" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A2.Ex64.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\tilde{\varepsilon}=c\varepsilon\left(1-\frac{4\varepsilon}{(y-x)^{2}}\right)+o\left(\varepsilon^{2}\right)" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi>ε</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>c</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>ε</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mfrac><mrow><mn>4</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>ε</mi></mrow><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>y</mi><mo>−</mo><mi>x</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup></mfrac></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi>o</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><msup><mi>ε</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\tilde{\varepsilon}=c\varepsilon\left(1-\frac{4\varepsilon}{(y-x)^{2}}\right)+o\left(\varepsilon^{2}\right)</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
<div id="A2.SS2.SSS1.Px1.p22" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A2.SS2.SSS1.Px1.p22.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.SS2.SSS1.Px1.p22.1.1" class="ltx_text">i.e <math id="A2.SS2.SSS1.Px1.p22.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\tilde{\varepsilon}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mover accent="true"><mi>ε</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\tilde{\varepsilon}</annotation></semantics></math> is deterministic up to order two in <math id="A2.SS2.SSS1.Px1.p22.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\varepsilon" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>ε</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\varepsilon</annotation></semantics></math>. Denote by <math id="A2.SS2.SSS1.Px1.p22.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{L}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℒ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{L}</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="A2.SS2.SSS1.Px1.p22.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{M}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℳ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{M}</annotation></semantics></math> the infinitesimal generators of the two SLEs:</span></p>
</div>
<div id="A2.SS2.SSS1.Px1.p23" class="ltx_para">
<table id="A2.Ex65" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A2.Ex65X"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A2.Ex65X.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\mathcal{L}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℒ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\mathcal{L}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A2.Ex65X.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=\frac{\kappa}{2}\partial_{xx}+b(x,y,\ldots)\partial_{x}+\frac{2}{y-x}\partial_{y}+\sum_{i=1}^{n}\frac{2}{z_{i}-x}\partial_{i}," display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo>=</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mi>κ</mi><mn>2</mn></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0em">∂</mo><msub><mrow></mrow><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>x</mi></mrow></msub><mo>+</mo><mi>b</mi><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>y</mi><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo><mo lspace="0em">∂</mo><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>x</mi></msub><mo>+</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mn>2</mn><mrow><mi>y</mi><mo>−</mo><mi>x</mi></mrow></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0em">∂</mo><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>y</mi></msub><mo>+</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo></mstyle><msub><mrow></mrow><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><msup><mrow></mrow><mi>n</mi></msup><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mn>2</mn><mrow><msub><mi>z</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>−</mo><mi>x</mi></mrow></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0em">∂</mo><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\frac{\kappa}{2}\partial_{xx}+b(x,y,\ldots)\partial_{x}+\frac{2}{y-x}\partial_{y}+\sum_{i=1}^{n}\frac{2}{z_{i}-x}\partial_{i},</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A2.Ex65Xa"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A2.Ex65Xa.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\mathcal{M}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℳ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\mathcal{M}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A2.Ex65Xa.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=\frac{\kappa}{2}\partial_{yy}+\tilde{b}(x,y,\ldots)\partial_{y}+\frac{2}{x-y}\partial_{x}+\sum_{i=1}^{n}\frac{2}{z_{i}-y}\partial_{i}," display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo>=</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mi>κ</mi><mn>2</mn></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0em">∂</mo><msub><mrow></mrow><mrow><mi>y</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>y</mi></mrow></msub><mo>+</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>b</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>y</mi><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo><mo lspace="0em">∂</mo><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>y</mi></msub><mo>+</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mn>2</mn><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>−</mo><mi>y</mi></mrow></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0em">∂</mo><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>x</mi></msub><mo>+</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo></mstyle><msub><mrow></mrow><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><msup><mrow></mrow><mi>n</mi></msup><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mn>2</mn><mrow><msub><mi>z</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>−</mo><mi>y</mi></mrow></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0em">∂</mo><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\frac{\kappa}{2}\partial_{yy}+\tilde{b}(x,y,\ldots)\partial_{y}+\frac{2}{x-y}\partial_{x}+\sum_{i=1}^{n}\frac{2}{z_{i}-y}\partial_{i},</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A2.SS2.SSS1.Px1.p23.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.SS2.SSS1.Px1.p23.1.1" class="ltx_text">where <math id="A2.SS2.SSS1.Px1.p23.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\partial_{i}=\partial_{z_{i}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo>∂</mo><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>i</mi></msub><mo rspace="0.111em">=</mo><mo>∂</mo><msub><mrow></mrow><msub><mi>z</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\partial_{i}=\partial_{z_{i}}</annotation></semantics></math>. Let <math id="A2.SS2.SSS1.Px1.p23.m2" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="w=\left(x,y,\ldots,z_{i},\ldots\right),w^{\prime}=\left(X_{\varepsilon},g_{\varepsilon}(y),\ldots g_{\varepsilon}\left(z_{i}\right),\ldots\right),w^{\prime\prime}=\left(\tilde{g}_{\tilde{\varepsilon}}\left(X_{\varepsilon}\right),\tilde{Y}_{\tilde{\varepsilon}},\ldots\tilde{g}_{\tilde{\varepsilon}}\circ\right." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>w</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>y</mi><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>z</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>)</mo></mrow><mo>,</mo><msup><mi>w</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><msub><mi>X</mi><mi>ε</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>g</mi><mi>ε</mi></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>y</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><msub><mi>g</mi><mi>ε</mi></msub><mrow><mo>(</mo><msub><mi>z</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>)</mo></mrow><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>)</mo></mrow><mo>,</mo><msup><mi>w</mi><mo>′′</mo></msup><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>g</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mover accent="true"><mi>ε</mi><mo>~</mo></mover></msub><mrow><mo>(</mo><msub><mi>X</mi><mi>ε</mi></msub><mo>)</mo></mrow><mo>,</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>Y</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mover accent="true"><mi>ε</mi><mo>~</mo></mover></msub><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>g</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mover accent="true"><mi>ε</mi><mo>~</mo></mover></msub><mo lspace="0.222em">∘</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">w=\left(x,y,\ldots,z_{i},\ldots\right),w^{\prime}=\left(X_{\varepsilon},g_{\varepsilon}(y),\ldots g_{\varepsilon}\left(z_{i}\right),\ldots\right),w^{\prime\prime}=\left(\tilde{g}_{\tilde{\varepsilon}}\left(X_{\varepsilon}\right),\tilde{Y}_{\tilde{\varepsilon}},\ldots\tilde{g}_{\tilde{\varepsilon}}\circ\right.</annotation></semantics></math> <math id="A2.SS2.SSS1.Px1.p23.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\left.g_{\varepsilon}\left(z_{i}\right),\ldots\right)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo fence="true" rspace="0em">OPEN</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>g</mi><mi>ε</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><msub><mi>z</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\left.g_{\varepsilon}\left(z_{i}\right),\ldots\right)</annotation></semantics></math>. Now:</span></p>
</div>
<div id="A2.SS2.SSS1.Px1.p24" class="ltx_para">
<table id="A2.Ex66" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A2.Ex66X"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A2.Ex66X.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\mathbb{E}\left(F\left(w^{\prime\prime}\right)\mid w\right)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>𝔼</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mi>F</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><msup><mi>w</mi><mo>′′</mo></msup><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo fence="true" lspace="0em" rspace="0em">∣</mo><mi>w</mi><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\mathbb{E}\left(F\left(w^{\prime\prime}\right)\mid w\right)</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A2.Ex66X.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=\mathbb{E}\left(F\left(w^{\prime\prime}\right)\left|w^{\prime}\right|w\right)=P_{\varepsilon}\mathbb{E}\left(Q_{\tilde{\varepsilon}}F\mid w^{\prime}\right)(w)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>𝔼</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>F</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><msup><mi>w</mi><mo>′′</mo></msup><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>|</mo><msup><mi>w</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo>|</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>w</mi></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><msub><mi>P</mi><mi>ε</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>𝔼</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>Q</mi><mover accent="true"><mi>ε</mi><mo>~</mo></mover></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>F</mi></mrow><mo fence="true" lspace="0em" rspace="0em">∣</mo><msup><mi>w</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo>)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>w</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\mathbb{E}\left(F\left(w^{\prime\prime}\right)\left|w^{\prime}\right|w\right)=P_{\varepsilon}\mathbb{E}\left(Q_{\tilde{\varepsilon}}F\mid w^{\prime}\right)(w)</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A2.Ex66Xa"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A2.Ex66Xa.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=P_{\varepsilon}\mathbb{E}\left(\left(1+\tilde{\varepsilon}\mathcal{M}+\frac{\tilde{\varepsilon}^{2}}{2}\mathcal{M}^{2}\right)F\left(w^{\prime}\right)\right)(w)=P_{\varepsilon}Q_{c\varepsilon\left(1-4\varepsilon/(y-x)^{2}\right)}F(w)+o\left(\varepsilon^{2}\right)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><msub><mi>P</mi><mi>ε</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>𝔼</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>+</mo><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi>ε</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℳ</mi></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><msup><mover accent="true"><mi>ε</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mn>2</mn></msup><mn>2</mn></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℳ</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>F</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><msup><mi>w</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>w</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>P</mi><mi>ε</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>Q</mi><mrow><mi>c</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>ε</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mrow><mrow><mn>4</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>ε</mi></mrow><mo>/</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>y</mi><mo>−</mo><mi>x</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>F</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>w</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi>o</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><msup><mi>ε</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=P_{\varepsilon}\mathbb{E}\left(\left(1+\tilde{\varepsilon}\mathcal{M}+\frac{\tilde{\varepsilon}^{2}}{2}\mathcal{M}^{2}\right)F\left(w^{\prime}\right)\right)(w)=P_{\varepsilon}Q_{c\varepsilon\left(1-4\varepsilon/(y-x)^{2}\right)}F(w)+o\left(\varepsilon^{2}\right)</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A2.Ex66Xb"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A2.Ex66Xb.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=\left(1+\varepsilon\mathcal{L}+\frac{\varepsilon^{2}}{2}\mathcal{L}^{2}\right)\left(1+c\varepsilon\left(1-\frac{4\varepsilon}{(y-x)^{2}}\right)\mathcal{M}+\frac{c^{2}\varepsilon^{2}}{2}\mathcal{M}^{2}\right)F(w)+o\left(\varepsilon^{2}\right)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi>ε</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℒ</mi></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><msup><mi>ε</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mn>2</mn></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℒ</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi>c</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>ε</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><mn>4</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>ε</mi></mrow><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>y</mi><mo>−</mo><mi>x</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup></mfrac></mstyle></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℳ</mi></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><msup><mi>c</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>ε</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow><mn>2</mn></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℳ</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>F</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>w</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi>o</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><msup><mi>ε</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\left(1+\varepsilon\mathcal{L}+\frac{\varepsilon^{2}}{2}\mathcal{L}^{2}\right)\left(1+c\varepsilon\left(1-\frac{4\varepsilon}{(y-x)^{2}}\right)\mathcal{M}+\frac{c^{2}\varepsilon^{2}}{2}\mathcal{M}^{2}\right)F(w)+o\left(\varepsilon^{2}\right)</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A2.Ex66Xc"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A2.Ex66Xc.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=\left(1+\varepsilon(\mathcal{L}+c\mathcal{M})+\varepsilon^{2}\left(\frac{1}{2}\mathcal{L}^{2}+\frac{c^{2}}{2}\mathcal{M}^{2}+c\mathcal{L}\mathcal{M}-\frac{4c}{(y-x)^{2}}\mathcal{M}\right)\right)F(w)+o\left(\varepsilon^{2}\right)." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi>ε</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℒ</mi><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi>c</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℳ</mi></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><msup><mi>ε</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mrow><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mn>2</mn></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℒ</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><msup><mi>c</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mn>2</mn></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℳ</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi>c</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℒ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℳ</mi></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><mn>4</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>c</mi></mrow><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>y</mi><mo>−</mo><mi>x</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℳ</mi></mrow></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>F</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>w</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi>o</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><msup><mi>ε</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\left(1+\varepsilon(\mathcal{L}+c\mathcal{M})+\varepsilon^{2}\left(\frac{1}{2}\mathcal{L}^{2}+\frac{c^{2}}{2}\mathcal{M}^{2}+c\mathcal{L}\mathcal{M}-\frac{4c}{(y-x)^{2}}\mathcal{M}\right)\right)F(w)+o\left(\varepsilon^{2}\right).</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
<div id="A2.SS2.SSS1.Px1.p25" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A2.SS2.SSS1.Px1.p25.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.SS2.SSS1.Px1.p25.1.1" class="ltx_text">If we first grow a hull at <math id="A2.SS2.SSS1.Px1.p25.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="z" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>z</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">z</annotation></semantics></math>, then at <math id="A2.SS2.SSS1.Px1.p25.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="x" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>x</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">x</annotation></semantics></math>, one gets instead:</span></p>
</div>
<div id="A2.SS2.SSS1.Px1.p26" class="ltx_para">
<table id="A2.Ex67" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A2.Ex67.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\left(1+\varepsilon(\mathcal{L}+c\mathcal{M})+\varepsilon^{2}\left(\frac{1}{2}\mathcal{L}^{2}+\frac{c^{2}}{2}\mathcal{M}^{2}+c\mathcal{M}\mathcal{L}-\frac{4c}{(z-x)^{2}}\mathcal{L}\right)\right)F(w)+o\left(\varepsilon^{2}\right)." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi>ε</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℒ</mi><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi>c</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℳ</mi></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><msup><mi>ε</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mrow><mrow><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mn>2</mn></mfrac><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℒ</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mfrac><msup><mi>c</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mn>2</mn></mfrac><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℳ</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi>c</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℳ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℒ</mi></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mfrac><mrow><mn>4</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>c</mi></mrow><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>z</mi><mo>−</mo><mi>x</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup></mfrac><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℒ</mi></mrow></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>F</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>w</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi>o</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><msup><mi>ε</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\left(1+\varepsilon(\mathcal{L}+c\mathcal{M})+\varepsilon^{2}\left(\frac{1}{2}\mathcal{L}^{2}+\frac{c^{2}}{2}\mathcal{M}^{2}+c\mathcal{M}\mathcal{L}-\frac{4c}{(z-x)^{2}}\mathcal{L}\right)\right)F(w)+o\left(\varepsilon^{2}\right).</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
<div id="A2.SS2.SSS1.Px1.p27" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A2.SS2.SSS1.Px1.p27.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.SS2.SSS1.Px1.p27.1.1" class="ltx_text">Hence the commutation condition reads:</span></p>
</div>
<div id="A2.SS2.SSS1.Px1.p28" class="ltx_para">
<table id="A2.Ex68" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A2.Ex68.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="[\mathcal{L},\mathcal{M}]=\frac{4}{(y-x)^{2}}(\mathcal{M}-\mathcal{L})." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℒ</mi><mo>,</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℳ</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mfrac><mn>4</mn><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>y</mi><mo>−</mo><mi>x</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup></mfrac><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℳ</mi><mo>−</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℒ</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">[\mathcal{L},\mathcal{M}]=\frac{4}{(y-x)^{2}}(\mathcal{M}-\mathcal{L}).</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
<div id="A2.SS2.SSS1.Px1.p29" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A2.SS2.SSS1.Px1.p29.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.SS2.SSS1.Px1.p29.1.1" class="ltx_text">After simplifications, one gets:</span></p>
</div>
<div id="A2.SS2.SSS1.Px1.p30" class="ltx_para">
<table id="A2.Ex69" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A2.Ex69X"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A2.Ex69X.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle{[\mathcal{L},\mathcal{M}]+\frac{4}{(y-x)^{2}}(\mathcal{L}-\mathcal{M})=}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℒ</mi><mo>,</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℳ</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mn>4</mn><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>y</mi><mo>−</mo><mi>x</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℒ</mi><mo>−</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℳ</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mphantom></mphantom></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle{[\mathcal{L},\mathcal{M}]+\frac{4}{(y-x)^{2}}(\mathcal{L}-\mathcal{M})=}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A2.Ex69X.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\left(\kappa\partial_{x}\tilde{b}-\tilde{\kappa}\partial_{y}b\right)\partial_{xy}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo>(</mo><mi>κ</mi><mo lspace="0em">∂</mo><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>x</mi></msub><mover accent="true"><mi>b</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mo>−</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>κ</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mo lspace="0em">∂</mo><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>y</mi></msub><mi>b</mi><mo>)</mo><mo lspace="0em">∂</mo><msub><mrow></mrow><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>y</mi></mrow></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\left(\kappa\partial_{x}\tilde{b}-\tilde{\kappa}\partial_{y}b\right)\partial_{xy}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A2.Ex69Xa"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A2.Ex69Xa.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle+\left[\frac{2\partial_{x}b}{y-x}+\sum_{i}\frac{2\partial_{i}b}{y-z_{i}}-\tilde{b}\partial_{y}b+\frac{2b}{(y-x)^{2}}+\frac{2\kappa-12}{(x-y)^{3}}-\frac{\tilde{\kappa}}{2}\partial_{yy}b\right]\partial_{x}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo>+</mo><mo>[</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><msub><mo>∂</mo><mi>x</mi></msub><mi>b</mi></mrow></mrow><mrow><mi>y</mi><mo>−</mo><mi>x</mi></mrow></mfrac></mstyle><mo>+</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo></mstyle><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>i</mi></msub><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><msub><mo>∂</mo><mi>i</mi></msub><mi>b</mi></mrow></mrow><mrow><mi>y</mi><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>z</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></mrow></mfrac></mstyle><mo>−</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>b</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mo lspace="0em">∂</mo><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>y</mi></msub><mi>b</mi><mo>+</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>b</mi></mrow><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>y</mi><mo>−</mo><mi>x</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup></mfrac></mstyle><mo>+</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>κ</mi></mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>12</mn></mrow><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>−</mo><mi>y</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mn>3</mn></msup></mfrac></mstyle><mo>−</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mover accent="true"><mi>κ</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mn>2</mn></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0em">∂</mo><msub><mrow></mrow><mrow><mi>y</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>y</mi></mrow></msub><mi>b</mi><mo>]</mo><mo lspace="0em">∂</mo><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>x</mi></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle+\left[\frac{2\partial_{x}b}{y-x}+\sum_{i}\frac{2\partial_{i}b}{y-z_{i}}-\tilde{b}\partial_{y}b+\frac{2b}{(y-x)^{2}}+\frac{2\kappa-12}{(x-y)^{3}}-\frac{\tilde{\kappa}}{2}\partial_{yy}b\right]\partial_{x}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A2.Ex69Xb"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A2.Ex69Xb.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle-\left[\frac{2\partial_{y}\tilde{b}}{x-y}+\sum_{i}\frac{2\partial_{i}\tilde{b}}{x-z_{i}}-b\partial_{x}\tilde{b}+\frac{2\tilde{b}}{(x-y)^{2}}+\frac{2\tilde{\kappa}-12}{(y-x)^{3}}-\frac{\kappa}{2}\partial_{xx}\tilde{b}\right]\partial_{y}." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo>−</mo><mo>[</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><msub><mo>∂</mo><mi>y</mi></msub><mover accent="true"><mi>b</mi><mo>~</mo></mover></mrow></mrow><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>−</mo><mi>y</mi></mrow></mfrac></mstyle><mo>+</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo></mstyle><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>i</mi></msub><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><msub><mo>∂</mo><mi>i</mi></msub><mover accent="true"><mi>b</mi><mo>~</mo></mover></mrow></mrow><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>z</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></mrow></mfrac></mstyle><mo>−</mo><mi>b</mi><mo lspace="0em">∂</mo><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>x</mi></msub><mover accent="true"><mi>b</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mo>+</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>b</mi><mo>~</mo></mover></mrow><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>−</mo><mi>y</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup></mfrac></mstyle><mo>+</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>κ</mi><mo>~</mo></mover></mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>12</mn></mrow><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>y</mi><mo>−</mo><mi>x</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mn>3</mn></msup></mfrac></mstyle><mo>−</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mi>κ</mi><mn>2</mn></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0em">∂</mo><msub><mrow></mrow><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>x</mi></mrow></msub><mover accent="true"><mi>b</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mo>]</mo><mo lspace="0em">∂</mo><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>y</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle-\left[\frac{2\partial_{y}\tilde{b}}{x-y}+\sum_{i}\frac{2\partial_{i}\tilde{b}}{x-z_{i}}-b\partial_{x}\tilde{b}+\frac{2\tilde{b}}{(x-y)^{2}}+\frac{2\tilde{\kappa}-12}{(y-x)^{3}}-\frac{\kappa}{2}\partial_{xx}\tilde{b}\right]\partial_{y}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
<div id="A2.SS2.SSS1.Px1.p31" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A2.SS2.SSS1.Px1.p31.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.SS2.SSS1.Px1.p31.1.1" class="ltx_text">So the commutation condition reduces to three differential conditions involving <math id="A2.SS2.SSS1.Px1.p31.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="b" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>b</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">b</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="A2.SS2.SSS1.Px1.p31.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\tilde{b}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mover accent="true"><mi>b</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\tilde{b}</annotation></semantics></math>; note the non-linear terms <math id="A2.SS2.SSS1.Px1.p31.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\tilde{b}\partial_{y}b" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi>b</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><msub><mo>∂</mo><mi>y</mi></msub><mi>b</mi></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\tilde{b}\partial_{y}b</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="A2.SS2.SSS1.Px1.p31.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="b\partial_{x}\tilde{b}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>b</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><msub><mo>∂</mo><mi>x</mi></msub><mover accent="true"><mi>b</mi><mo>~</mo></mover></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">b\partial_{x}\tilde{b}</annotation></semantics></math>.</span></p>
</div>
<div id="A2.SS2.SSS1.Px1.p32" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A2.SS2.SSS1.Px1.p32.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.SS2.SSS1.Px1.p32.1.1" class="ltx_text">In the previous paragraph, we derived the following commutation conditions:</span></p>
</div>
<div id="A2.SS2.SSS1.Px1.p33" class="ltx_para">
<table id="A2.Ex70" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A2.Ex70.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\left\{\begin{array}[]{l}\kappa\partial_{x}\tilde{b}-\tilde{\kappa}\partial_{y}b=0\\
\frac{2\partial_{x}b}{y-x}+\sum_{i}\frac{2\partial_{i}b}{y-z_{i}}-\tilde{b}\partial_{y}b+\frac{2b}{(y-x)^{2}}+\frac{2\kappa-12}{(x-y)^{3}}-\frac{\tilde{\kappa}}{2}\partial_{yy}b=0\\
\frac{2\partial_{y}\tilde{b}}{x-y}+\sum_{i}\frac{2\partial_{i}\tilde{b}}{x-z_{i}}-b\partial_{x}\tilde{b}+\frac{2\tilde{b}}{(x-y)^{2}}+\frac{2\tilde{\kappa}-12}{(y-x)^{3}}-\frac{\kappa}{2}\partial_{xx}\tilde{b}=0\end{array}\right.." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mo>{</mo><mtable displaystyle="true" rowspacing="0pt"><mtr><mtd class="ltx_align_left" columnalign="left"><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>κ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><msub><mo>∂</mo><mi>x</mi></msub><mover accent="true"><mi>b</mi><mo>~</mo></mover></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi>κ</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><msub><mo>∂</mo><mi>y</mi></msub><mi>b</mi></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow></mtd></mtr><mtr><mtd class="ltx_align_left" columnalign="left"><mrow><mrow><mrow><mrow><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="false"><mfrac><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><msub><mo>∂</mo><mi>x</mi></msub><mi>b</mi></mrow></mrow><mrow><mi>y</mi><mo>−</mo><mi>x</mi></mrow></mfrac></mstyle><mo>+</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="false"><msub><mo>∑</mo><mi>i</mi></msub></mstyle><mstyle displaystyle="false"><mfrac><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><msub><mo>∂</mo><mi>i</mi></msub><mi>b</mi></mrow></mrow><mrow><mi>y</mi><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>z</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></mrow></mfrac></mstyle></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi>b</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><msub><mo>∂</mo><mi>y</mi></msub><mi>b</mi></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mstyle displaystyle="false"><mfrac><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>b</mi></mrow><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>y</mi><mo>−</mo><mi>x</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup></mfrac></mstyle><mo>+</mo><mstyle displaystyle="false"><mfrac><mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>κ</mi></mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>12</mn></mrow><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>−</mo><mi>y</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mn>3</mn></msup></mfrac></mstyle></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="false"><mfrac><mover accent="true"><mi>κ</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mn>2</mn></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><msub><mo>∂</mo><mrow><mi>y</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>y</mi></mrow></msub><mi>b</mi></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow></mtd></mtr><mtr><mtd class="ltx_align_left" columnalign="left"><mrow><mrow><mrow><mrow><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="false"><mfrac><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><msub><mo>∂</mo><mi>y</mi></msub><mover accent="true"><mi>b</mi><mo>~</mo></mover></mrow></mrow><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>−</mo><mi>y</mi></mrow></mfrac></mstyle><mo>+</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="false"><msub><mo>∑</mo><mi>i</mi></msub></mstyle><mstyle displaystyle="false"><mfrac><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><msub><mo>∂</mo><mi>i</mi></msub><mover accent="true"><mi>b</mi><mo>~</mo></mover></mrow></mrow><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>z</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></mrow></mfrac></mstyle></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>b</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><msub><mo>∂</mo><mi>x</mi></msub><mover accent="true"><mi>b</mi><mo>~</mo></mover></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mstyle displaystyle="false"><mfrac><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>b</mi><mo>~</mo></mover></mrow><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>−</mo><mi>y</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup></mfrac></mstyle><mo>+</mo><mstyle displaystyle="false"><mfrac><mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>κ</mi><mo>~</mo></mover></mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>12</mn></mrow><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>y</mi><mo>−</mo><mi>x</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mn>3</mn></msup></mfrac></mstyle></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="false"><mfrac><mi>κ</mi><mn>2</mn></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><msub><mo>∂</mo><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>x</mi></mrow></msub><mover accent="true"><mi>b</mi><mo>~</mo></mover></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow></mtd></mtr></mtable><mphantom></mphantom></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\left\{\begin{array}[]{l}\kappa\partial_{x}\tilde{b}-\tilde{\kappa}\partial_{y}b=0\\
\frac{2\partial_{x}b}{y-x}+\sum_{i}\frac{2\partial_{i}b}{y-z_{i}}-\tilde{b}\partial_{y}b+\frac{2b}{(y-x)^{2}}+\frac{2\kappa-12}{(x-y)^{3}}-\frac{\tilde{\kappa}}{2}\partial_{yy}b=0\\
\frac{2\partial_{y}\tilde{b}}{x-y}+\sum_{i}\frac{2\partial_{i}\tilde{b}}{x-z_{i}}-b\partial_{x}\tilde{b}+\frac{2\tilde{b}}{(x-y)^{2}}+\frac{2\tilde{\kappa}-12}{(y-x)^{3}}-\frac{\kappa}{2}\partial_{xx}\tilde{b}=0\end{array}\right..</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
<div id="A2.SS2.SSS1.Px1.p34" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A2.SS2.SSS1.Px1.p34.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.SS2.SSS1.Px1.p34.1.1" class="ltx_text">Now, from the first equation, one can write:</span></p>
</div>
<div id="A2.SS2.SSS1.Px1.p35" class="ltx_para">
<table id="A2.Ex71" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A2.Ex71.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="b=\kappa\frac{\partial_{x}\psi}{\psi},\tilde{b}=\tilde{\kappa}\frac{\partial_{y}\psi}{\psi}" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>b</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>κ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mfrac><mrow><msub><mo>∂</mo><mi>x</mi></msub><mi>ψ</mi></mrow><mi>ψ</mi></mfrac></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi>b</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mo>=</mo><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi>κ</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mfrac><mrow><msub><mo>∂</mo><mi>y</mi></msub><mi>ψ</mi></mrow><mi>ψ</mi></mfrac></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">b=\kappa\frac{\partial_{x}\psi}{\psi},\tilde{b}=\tilde{\kappa}\frac{\partial_{y}\psi}{\psi}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
<div id="A2.SS2.SSS1.Px1.p36" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A2.SS2.SSS1.Px1.p36.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.SS2.SSS1.Px1.p36.1.1" class="ltx_text">for some non-vanishing function <math id="A2.SS2.SSS1.Px1.p36.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\psi" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>ψ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\psi</annotation></semantics></math> (at least locally).
It turns out that the second condition now writes:</span></p>
</div>
<div id="A2.SS2.SSS1.Px1.p37" class="ltx_para">
<table id="A2.Ex72" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A2.Ex72.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="-\kappa\partial_{x}\left(\frac{\frac{\bar{\kappa}}{2}\partial_{yy}\psi+\sum_{i}\frac{2\partial_{i}\psi}{z_{i}-y}+\frac{2\partial_{x}\psi}{x-y}+\left(1-\frac{6}{\kappa}\right)\frac{\psi}{(x-y)^{2}}}{\psi}\right)=0." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo>−</mo><mi>κ</mi><msub><mo lspace="0em">∂</mo><mi>x</mi></msub><mrow><mo>(</mo><mfrac><mrow><mrow><mfrac><mover accent="true"><mi>κ</mi><mo>¯</mo></mover><mn>2</mn></mfrac><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><msub><mo>∂</mo><mrow><mi>y</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>y</mi></mrow></msub><mi>ψ</mi></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.055em">+</mo><mrow><msub><mo>∑</mo><mi>i</mi></msub><mfrac><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><msub><mo>∂</mo><mi>i</mi></msub><mi>ψ</mi></mrow></mrow><mrow><msub><mi>z</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>−</mo><mi>y</mi></mrow></mfrac></mrow><mo>+</mo><mfrac><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><msub><mo>∂</mo><mi>x</mi></msub><mi>ψ</mi></mrow></mrow><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>−</mo><mi>y</mi></mrow></mfrac><mo>+</mo><mrow><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mfrac><mn>6</mn><mi>κ</mi></mfrac></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mfrac><mi>ψ</mi><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>−</mo><mi>y</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup></mfrac></mrow></mrow><mi>ψ</mi></mfrac><mo>)</mo></mrow><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">-\kappa\partial_{x}\left(\frac{\frac{\bar{\kappa}}{2}\partial_{yy}\psi+\sum_{i}\frac{2\partial_{i}\psi}{z_{i}-y}+\frac{2\partial_{x}\psi}{x-y}+\left(1-\frac{6}{\kappa}\right)\frac{\psi}{(x-y)^{2}}}{\psi}\right)=0.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
<div id="A2.SS2.SSS1.Px1.p38" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A2.SS2.SSS1.Px1.p38.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.SS2.SSS1.Px1.p38.1.1" class="ltx_text">Symmetrically, the last equation is:</span></p>
</div>
<div id="A2.SS2.SSS1.Px1.p39" class="ltx_para">
<table id="A2.Ex73" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A2.Ex73.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="-\tilde{\kappa}\partial_{y}\left(\frac{\frac{\kappa}{2}\partial_{xx}\psi+\sum_{i}\frac{2\partial_{i}\psi}{z_{i}-x}+\frac{2\partial_{y}\psi}{y-x}+\left(1-\frac{6}{\kappa}\right)\frac{\psi}{(y-x)^{2}}}{\psi}\right)=0." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo>−</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>κ</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><msub><mo lspace="0em">∂</mo><mi>y</mi></msub><mrow><mo>(</mo><mfrac><mrow><mrow><mfrac><mi>κ</mi><mn>2</mn></mfrac><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><msub><mo>∂</mo><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>x</mi></mrow></msub><mi>ψ</mi></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.055em">+</mo><mrow><msub><mo>∑</mo><mi>i</mi></msub><mfrac><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><msub><mo>∂</mo><mi>i</mi></msub><mi>ψ</mi></mrow></mrow><mrow><msub><mi>z</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>−</mo><mi>x</mi></mrow></mfrac></mrow><mo>+</mo><mfrac><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><msub><mo>∂</mo><mi>y</mi></msub><mi>ψ</mi></mrow></mrow><mrow><mi>y</mi><mo>−</mo><mi>x</mi></mrow></mfrac><mo>+</mo><mrow><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mfrac><mn>6</mn><mi>κ</mi></mfrac></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mfrac><mi>ψ</mi><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>y</mi><mo>−</mo><mi>x</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup></mfrac></mrow></mrow><mi>ψ</mi></mfrac><mo>)</mo></mrow><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">-\tilde{\kappa}\partial_{y}\left(\frac{\frac{\kappa}{2}\partial_{xx}\psi+\sum_{i}\frac{2\partial_{i}\psi}{z_{i}-x}+\frac{2\partial_{y}\psi}{y-x}+\left(1-\frac{6}{\kappa}\right)\frac{\psi}{(y-x)^{2}}}{\psi}\right)=0.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
<div id="A2.SS2.SSS1.Px1.p40" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A2.SS2.SSS1.Px1.p40.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.SS2.SSS1.Px1.p40.1.1" class="ltx_text">This means that a non-vanishing solution of</span></p>
</div>
<div id="A2.SS2.SSS1.Px1.p41" class="ltx_para">
<table id="A2.Ex74" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A2.Ex74.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\left\{\begin{array}[]{l}\frac{\kappa}{2}\partial_{xx}\psi+\sum_{i}\frac{2\partial_{i}\psi}{z_{i}-x}+\frac{2\partial_{y}\psi}{y-x}+\left(\left(1-\frac{6}{\tilde{\kappa}}\right)\frac{1}{(y-x)^{2}}+h_{1}(x,z)\right)\psi=0\\
\frac{\tilde{\kappa}}{2}\partial_{yy}\psi+\sum_{i}\frac{2\partial_{i}\psi}{z_{i}-y}+\frac{2\partial_{x}\psi}{x-y}+\left(\left(1-\frac{6}{\kappa}\right)\frac{1}{(x-y)^{2}}+h_{2}(y,z)\right)\psi=0\end{array}\right." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo>{</mo><mtable displaystyle="true" rowspacing="0pt"><mtr><mtd class="ltx_align_left" columnalign="left"><mrow><mrow><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="false"><mfrac><mi>κ</mi><mn>2</mn></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><msub><mo>∂</mo><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>x</mi></mrow></msub><mi>ψ</mi></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="false"><msub><mo>∑</mo><mi>i</mi></msub></mstyle><mstyle displaystyle="false"><mfrac><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><msub><mo>∂</mo><mi>i</mi></msub><mi>ψ</mi></mrow></mrow><mrow><msub><mi>z</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>−</mo><mi>x</mi></mrow></mfrac></mstyle></mrow><mo>+</mo><mstyle displaystyle="false"><mfrac><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><msub><mo>∂</mo><mi>y</mi></msub><mi>ψ</mi></mrow></mrow><mrow><mi>y</mi><mo>−</mo><mi>x</mi></mrow></mfrac></mstyle><mo>+</mo><mrow><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mrow><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mstyle displaystyle="false"><mfrac><mn>6</mn><mover accent="true"><mi>κ</mi><mo>~</mo></mover></mfrac></mstyle></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mstyle displaystyle="false"><mfrac><mn>1</mn><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>y</mi><mo>−</mo><mi>x</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup></mfrac></mstyle></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><msub><mi>h</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>z</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>ψ</mi></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow></mtd></mtr><mtr><mtd class="ltx_align_left" columnalign="left"><mrow><mrow><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="false"><mfrac><mover accent="true"><mi>κ</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mn>2</mn></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><msub><mo>∂</mo><mrow><mi>y</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>y</mi></mrow></msub><mi>ψ</mi></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="false"><msub><mo>∑</mo><mi>i</mi></msub></mstyle><mstyle displaystyle="false"><mfrac><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><msub><mo>∂</mo><mi>i</mi></msub><mi>ψ</mi></mrow></mrow><mrow><msub><mi>z</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>−</mo><mi>y</mi></mrow></mfrac></mstyle></mrow><mo>+</mo><mstyle displaystyle="false"><mfrac><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><msub><mo>∂</mo><mi>x</mi></msub><mi>ψ</mi></mrow></mrow><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>−</mo><mi>y</mi></mrow></mfrac></mstyle><mo>+</mo><mrow><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mrow><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mstyle displaystyle="false"><mfrac><mn>6</mn><mi>κ</mi></mfrac></mstyle></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mstyle displaystyle="false"><mfrac><mn>1</mn><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>−</mo><mi>y</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup></mfrac></mstyle></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><msub><mi>h</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>y</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>z</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>ψ</mi></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow></mtd></mtr></mtable><mphantom></mphantom></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\left\{\begin{array}[]{l}\frac{\kappa}{2}\partial_{xx}\psi+\sum_{i}\frac{2\partial_{i}\psi}{z_{i}-x}+\frac{2\partial_{y}\psi}{y-x}+\left(\left(1-\frac{6}{\tilde{\kappa}}\right)\frac{1}{(y-x)^{2}}+h_{1}(x,z)\right)\psi=0\\
\frac{\tilde{\kappa}}{2}\partial_{yy}\psi+\sum_{i}\frac{2\partial_{i}\psi}{z_{i}-y}+\frac{2\partial_{x}\psi}{x-y}+\left(\left(1-\frac{6}{\kappa}\right)\frac{1}{(x-y)^{2}}+h_{2}(y,z)\right)\psi=0\end{array}\right.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
<div id="A2.SS2.SSS1.Px1.p42" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A2.SS2.SSS1.Px1.p42.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.SS2.SSS1.Px1.p42.1.1" class="ltx_text">yields drift terms <math id="A2.SS2.SSS1.Px1.p42.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="b,\tilde{b}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>b</mi><mo>,</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>b</mi><mo>~</mo></mover></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">b,\tilde{b}</annotation></semantics></math> that satisfy the commutation condition. Obviously, these differential operators are infinitesimal generators of the SLEs, with an added coefficient before the constant term.</span></p>
</div>
<div id="A2.SS2.SSS1.Px1.p43" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A2.SS2.SSS1.Px1.p43.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.SS2.SSS1.Px1.p43.1.1" class="ltx_text">The problem is now to find functions <math id="A2.SS2.SSS1.Px1.p43.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="h_{1},h_{2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>h</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>h</mi><mn>2</mn></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">h_{1},h_{2}</annotation></semantics></math> such that the above system has solutions (integrability conditions). Note that we have not considered yet the conditions: <math id="A2.SS2.SSS1.Px1.p43.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="b,\tilde{b}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>b</mi><mo>,</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>b</mi><mo>~</mo></mover></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">b,\tilde{b}</annotation></semantics></math> translation invariant and homogeneous of degree ( -1 ). This implies that <math id="A2.SS2.SSS1.Px1.p43.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\psi" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>ψ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\psi</annotation></semantics></math> can be chosen to be translation invariant and homogeneous of some fixed degree. So assume that we are given <math id="A2.SS2.SSS1.Px1.p43.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="h_{1},h_{2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>h</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>h</mi><mn>2</mn></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">h_{1},h_{2}</annotation></semantics></math>, and a non-vanishing (translation-invariant, homogeneous) solution <math id="A2.SS2.SSS1.Px1.p43.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\psi" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>ψ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\psi</annotation></semantics></math> of this system. Let:</span></p>
<table id="A2.EGx1" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_eqnarray ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A2.Ex75"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A2.Ex75.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\mathcal{M}_{1}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℳ</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\mathcal{M}_{1}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_center ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A2.Ex75.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mo>=</mo><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A2.Ex75.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\frac{\kappa}{2}\partial_{xx}\psi+\sum_{i}\frac{2\partial_{i}\psi}{z_{i}-x}+\frac{2\partial_{y}\psi}{y-x}+\left(1-\frac{6}{\tilde{\kappa}}\right)\frac{1}{(y-x)^{2}}," display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mi>κ</mi><mn>2</mn></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><msub><mo>∂</mo><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>x</mi></mrow></msub><mi>ψ</mi></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munder><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mi>i</mi></munder></mstyle><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><msub><mo>∂</mo><mi>i</mi></msub><mi>ψ</mi></mrow></mrow><mrow><msub><mi>z</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>−</mo><mi>x</mi></mrow></mfrac></mstyle></mrow><mo>+</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><msub><mo>∂</mo><mi>y</mi></msub><mi>ψ</mi></mrow></mrow><mrow><mi>y</mi><mo>−</mo><mi>x</mi></mrow></mfrac></mstyle><mo>+</mo><mrow><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mn>6</mn><mover accent="true"><mi>κ</mi><mo>~</mo></mover></mfrac></mstyle></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mn>1</mn><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>y</mi><mo>−</mo><mi>x</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup></mfrac></mstyle></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\frac{\kappa}{2}\partial_{xx}\psi+\sum_{i}\frac{2\partial_{i}\psi}{z_{i}-x}+\frac{2\partial_{y}\psi}{y-x}+\left(1-\frac{6}{\tilde{\kappa}}\right)\frac{1}{(y-x)^{2}},</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A2.Ex76"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A2.Ex76.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\mathcal{M}_{2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℳ</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\mathcal{M}_{2}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_center ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A2.Ex76.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mo>=</mo><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A2.Ex76.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\frac{\tilde{\kappa}}{2}\partial_{yy}\psi+\sum_{i}\frac{2\partial_{i}\psi}{z_{i}-y}+\frac{2\partial_{x}\psi}{x-y}+\left(1-\frac{6}{\kappa}\right)\frac{1}{(x-y)^{2}}." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mover accent="true"><mi>κ</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mn>2</mn></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><msub><mo>∂</mo><mrow><mi>y</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>y</mi></mrow></msub><mi>ψ</mi></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munder><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mi>i</mi></munder></mstyle><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><msub><mo>∂</mo><mi>i</mi></msub><mi>ψ</mi></mrow></mrow><mrow><msub><mi>z</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>−</mo><mi>y</mi></mrow></mfrac></mstyle></mrow><mo>+</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><msub><mo>∂</mo><mi>x</mi></msub><mi>ψ</mi></mrow></mrow><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>−</mo><mi>y</mi></mrow></mfrac></mstyle><mo>+</mo><mrow><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mn>6</mn><mi>κ</mi></mfrac></mstyle></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mn>1</mn><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>−</mo><mi>y</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup></mfrac></mstyle></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\frac{\tilde{\kappa}}{2}\partial_{yy}\psi+\sum_{i}\frac{2\partial_{i}\psi}{z_{i}-y}+\frac{2\partial_{x}\psi}{x-y}+\left(1-\frac{6}{\kappa}\right)\frac{1}{(x-y)^{2}}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
<div id="A2.SS2.SSS1.Px1.p44" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A2.SS2.SSS1.Px1.p44.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.SS2.SSS1.Px1.p44.1.1" class="ltx_text">Then <math id="A2.SS2.SSS1.Px1.p44.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\psi" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>ψ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\psi</annotation></semantics></math> is annihilated by all operators in the left ideal generated by <math id="A2.SS2.SSS1.Px1.p44.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\left(\mathcal{M}_{1}+h_{1}\right),\left(\mathcal{M}_{2}+h_{2}\right)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℳ</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>+</mo><msub><mi>h</mi><mn>1</mn></msub></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow><mo>,</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℳ</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo>+</mo><msub><mi>h</mi><mn>2</mn></msub></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\left(\mathcal{M}_{1}+h_{1}\right),\left(\mathcal{M}_{2}+h_{2}\right)</annotation></semantics></math>, including in particular:</span></p>
</div>
<div id="A2.SS2.SSS1.Px1.p45" class="ltx_para">
<table id="A2.Ex77" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A2.Ex77X"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A2.Ex77X.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\mathcal{M}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℳ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\mathcal{M}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A2.Ex77X.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=\left[\mathcal{M}_{1}+h_{1},\mathcal{M}_{2}+h_{2}\right]+\frac{4}{(x-y)^{2}}\left(\left(\mathcal{M}_{1}+h_{1}\right)-\left(\mathcal{M}_{2}+h_{2}\right)\right)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mo>[</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℳ</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>+</mo><msub><mi>h</mi><mn>1</mn></msub></mrow><mo>,</mo><mrow><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℳ</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo>+</mo><msub><mi>h</mi><mn>2</mn></msub></mrow></mrow><mo>]</mo></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mn>4</mn><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>−</mo><mi>y</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℳ</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>+</mo><msub><mi>h</mi><mn>1</mn></msub></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℳ</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo>+</mo><msub><mi>h</mi><mn>2</mn></msub></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\left[\mathcal{M}_{1}+h_{1},\mathcal{M}_{2}+h_{2}\right]+\frac{4}{(x-y)^{2}}\left(\left(\mathcal{M}_{1}+h_{1}\right)-\left(\mathcal{M}_{2}+h_{2}\right)\right)</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A2.Ex77Xa"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A2.Ex77Xa.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=\left[\mathcal{M}_{1},\mathcal{M}_{2}\right]+\frac{4}{(x-y)^{2}}\left(\mathcal{M}_{1}-\mathcal{M}_{2}\right)+\left(\left[\mathcal{M}_{1},h_{2}\right]-\left[\mathcal{M}_{2},h_{1}\right]\right)+\frac{4\left(h_{1}-h_{2}\right)}{(x-y)^{2}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mo>[</mo><mrow><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℳ</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℳ</mi><mn>2</mn></msub></mrow><mo>]</mo></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mn>4</mn><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>−</mo><mi>y</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℳ</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>−</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℳ</mi><mn>2</mn></msub></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mrow><mo>[</mo><mrow><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℳ</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>h</mi><mn>2</mn></msub></mrow><mo>]</mo></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mo>[</mo><mrow><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℳ</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>h</mi><mn>1</mn></msub></mrow><mo>]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow><mo>+</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><mn>4</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>h</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>h</mi><mn>2</mn></msub></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>−</mo><mi>y</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup></mfrac></mstyle></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\left[\mathcal{M}_{1},\mathcal{M}_{2}\right]+\frac{4}{(x-y)^{2}}\left(\mathcal{M}_{1}-\mathcal{M}_{2}\right)+\left(\left[\mathcal{M}_{1},h_{2}\right]-\left[\mathcal{M}_{2},h_{1}\right]\right)+\frac{4\left(h_{1}-h_{2}\right)}{(x-y)^{2}}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A2.Ex77Xb"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A2.Ex77Xb.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=\frac{3(\kappa\tilde{\kappa}-16)(\kappa-\tilde{\kappa})}{\kappa\tilde{\kappa}(x-y)^{4}}+\left(\left(\frac{2\partial_{y}}{y-x}+\sum_{i}\frac{2\partial_{i}}{z_{i}-x}\right)h_{2}-\left(\frac{2\partial_{x}}{x-y}+\sum_{i}\frac{2\partial_{i}}{z_{i}-y}\right)h_{1}\right)+\frac{4\left(h_{1}-h_{2}\right)}{(x-y)^{2}}." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><mn>3</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>κ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>κ</mi><mo>~</mo></mover></mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>16</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>κ</mi><mo>−</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>κ</mi><mo>~</mo></mover></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mrow><mi>κ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>κ</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>−</mo><mi>y</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mn>4</mn></msup></mrow></mfrac></mstyle><mo>+</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mrow><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em">∂</mo><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>y</mi></msub></mrow><mrow><mi>y</mi><mo>−</mo><mi>x</mi></mrow></mfrac></mstyle><mo>+</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munder><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mi>i</mi></munder></mstyle><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em">∂</mo><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>i</mi></msub></mrow><mrow><msub><mi>z</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>−</mo><mi>x</mi></mrow></mfrac></mstyle></mrow></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>h</mi><mn>2</mn></msub></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em">∂</mo><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>x</mi></msub></mrow><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>−</mo><mi>y</mi></mrow></mfrac></mstyle><mo>+</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munder><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mi>i</mi></munder></mstyle><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em">∂</mo><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>i</mi></msub></mrow><mrow><msub><mi>z</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>−</mo><mi>y</mi></mrow></mfrac></mstyle></mrow></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>h</mi><mn>1</mn></msub></mrow></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow><mo>+</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><mn>4</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>h</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>h</mi><mn>2</mn></msub></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>−</mo><mi>y</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup></mfrac></mstyle></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\frac{3(\kappa\tilde{\kappa}-16)(\kappa-\tilde{\kappa})}{\kappa\tilde{\kappa}(x-y)^{4}}+\left(\left(\frac{2\partial_{y}}{y-x}+\sum_{i}\frac{2\partial_{i}}{z_{i}-x}\right)h_{2}-\left(\frac{2\partial_{x}}{x-y}+\sum_{i}\frac{2\partial_{i}}{z_{i}-y}\right)h_{1}\right)+\frac{4\left(h_{1}-h_{2}\right)}{(x-y)^{2}}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
<div id="A2.SS2.SSS1.Px1.p46" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A2.SS2.SSS1.Px1.p46.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.SS2.SSS1.Px1.p46.1.1" class="ltx_text">This is an operator of order 0 , so it must vanish identically. Considering the pole at <math id="A2.SS2.SSS1.Px1.p46.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="x=y" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>=</mo><mi>y</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">x=y</annotation></semantics></math>, this implies in particular <math id="A2.SS2.SSS1.Px1.p46.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\tilde{\kappa}\in\{\kappa,16/\kappa\}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi>κ</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mrow><mi>κ</mi><mo>,</mo><mrow><mn>16</mn><mo>/</mo><mi>κ</mi></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\tilde{\kappa}\in\{\kappa,16/\kappa\}</annotation></semantics></math>, since the fourth-order pole must vanish. Then the second-order pole must also vanish, so <math id="A2.SS2.SSS1.Px1.p46.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="h_{1}(x,z)=h(x,z),h_{2}(y,z)=h(y,z)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>h</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>z</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>h</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>z</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>h</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>y</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>z</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>h</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>y</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>z</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">h_{1}(x,z)=h(x,z),h_{2}(y,z)=h(y,z)</annotation></semantics></math> for some <math id="A2.SS2.SSS1.Px1.p46.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="h" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>h</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">h</annotation></semantics></math>. So this condition boils down to a functional equation on <math id="A2.SS2.SSS1.Px1.p46.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="h" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>h</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">h</annotation></semantics></math>.</span></p>
</div>
<div id="A2.SS2.SSS1.Px1.p47" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A2.SS2.SSS1.Px1.p47.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.SS2.SSS1.Px1.p47.1.1" class="ltx_text">For illustration, consider the following variation on an earlier example: a chordal <math id="A2.SS2.SSS1.Px1.p47.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathrm{SLE}_{8/3}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>SLE</mi><mrow><mn>8</mn><mo>/</mo><mn>3</mn></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathrm{SLE}_{8/3}</annotation></semantics></math> from <math id="A2.SS2.SSS1.Px1.p47.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="x" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>x</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">x</annotation></semantics></math> to <math id="A2.SS2.SSS1.Px1.p47.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="y" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>y</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">y</annotation></semantics></math> is conditioned not to intersect an independent restriction measure from <math id="A2.SS2.SSS1.Px1.p47.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="z" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>z</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">z</annotation></semantics></math> to <math id="A2.SS2.SSS1.Px1.p47.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\infty" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi mathvariant="normal">∞</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\infty</annotation></semantics></math> with index <math id="A2.SS2.SSS1.Px1.p47.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\nu" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>ν</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\nu</annotation></semantics></math>. Let <math id="A2.SS2.SSS1.Px1.p47.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\varphi(x,y,z)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>φ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>y</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>z</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\varphi(x,y,z)</annotation></semantics></math> be the probability of non-intersection. Then <math id="A2.SS2.SSS1.Px1.p47.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\varphi" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>φ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\varphi</annotation></semantics></math> is annihilated by the operator:</span></p>
</div>
<div id="A2.SS2.SSS1.Px1.p48" class="ltx_para">
<table id="A2.Ex78" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A2.Ex78.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\frac{\kappa}{2}\partial_{xx}+\frac{\kappa-6}{x-y}\partial_{x}+\frac{2}{y-x}\partial_{y}+\frac{2}{z-x}\partial_{z}-\frac{2\nu}{(x-z)^{2}}" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mfrac><mi>κ</mi><mn>2</mn></mfrac><mo lspace="0em">∂</mo><msub><mrow></mrow><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>x</mi></mrow></msub><mo>+</mo><mfrac><mrow><mi>κ</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>6</mn></mrow><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>−</mo><mi>y</mi></mrow></mfrac><mo lspace="0em">∂</mo><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>x</mi></msub><mo>+</mo><mfrac><mn>2</mn><mrow><mi>y</mi><mo>−</mo><mi>x</mi></mrow></mfrac><mo lspace="0em">∂</mo><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>y</mi></msub><mo>+</mo><mfrac><mn>2</mn><mrow><mi>z</mi><mo>−</mo><mi>x</mi></mrow></mfrac><mo lspace="0em">∂</mo><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>z</mi></msub><mo>−</mo><mfrac><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>ν</mi></mrow><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>−</mo><mi>z</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup></mfrac></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\frac{\kappa}{2}\partial_{xx}+\frac{\kappa-6}{x-y}\partial_{x}+\frac{2}{y-x}\partial_{y}+\frac{2}{z-x}\partial_{z}-\frac{2\nu}{(x-z)^{2}}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
<div id="A2.SS2.SSS1.Px1.p49" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A2.SS2.SSS1.Px1.p49.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.SS2.SSS1.Px1.p49.1.1" class="ltx_text">where <math id="A2.SS2.SSS1.Px1.p49.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\kappa=8/3" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>κ</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><mn>8</mn><mo>/</mo><mn>3</mn></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\kappa=8/3</annotation></semantics></math>. Obviously <math id="A2.SS2.SSS1.Px1.p49.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\varphi" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>φ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\varphi</annotation></semantics></math> can be expressed in terms of a hypergeometric function. If <math id="A2.SS2.SSS1.Px1.p49.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\psi=(y-x)^{-2\alpha}\varphi" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>ψ</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>y</mi><mo>−</mo><mi>x</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>α</mi></mrow></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>φ</mi></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\psi=(y-x)^{-2\alpha}\varphi</annotation></semantics></math>, <math id="A2.SS2.SSS1.Px1.p49.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\alpha=\alpha_{\kappa}=5/8" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>α</mi><mo>=</mo><msub><mi>α</mi><mi>κ</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><mn>5</mn><mo>/</mo><mn>8</mn></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\alpha=\alpha_{\kappa}=5/8</annotation></semantics></math>, then <math id="A2.SS2.SSS1.Px1.p49.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\psi" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>ψ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\psi</annotation></semantics></math> is annihilated by the conjugate operators:</span></p>
</div>
<div id="A2.SS2.SSS1.Px1.p50" class="ltx_para">
<table id="A2.Ex79" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A2.Ex79.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\frac{\kappa}{2}\partial_{xx}+\frac{2}{y-x}\partial_{y}+\frac{2}{z-x}\partial_{z}-\frac{2\alpha}{(x-y)^{2}}-\frac{2\nu}{(x-z)^{2}},\frac{\kappa}{2}\partial_{yy}+\frac{2}{x-y}\partial_{x}+\frac{2}{z-y}\partial_{z}-\frac{2\alpha}{(y-x)^{2}}-\frac{2\nu}{(y-z)^{2}}" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mfrac><mi>κ</mi><mn>2</mn></mfrac><mo lspace="0em">∂</mo><msub><mrow></mrow><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>x</mi></mrow></msub><mo>+</mo><mfrac><mn>2</mn><mrow><mi>y</mi><mo>−</mo><mi>x</mi></mrow></mfrac><mo lspace="0em">∂</mo><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>y</mi></msub><mo>+</mo><mfrac><mn>2</mn><mrow><mi>z</mi><mo>−</mo><mi>x</mi></mrow></mfrac><mo lspace="0em">∂</mo><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>z</mi></msub><mo>−</mo><mfrac><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>α</mi></mrow><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>−</mo><mi>y</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup></mfrac><mo>−</mo><mfrac><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>ν</mi></mrow><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>−</mo><mi>z</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup></mfrac><mo>,</mo><mfrac><mi>κ</mi><mn>2</mn></mfrac><mo lspace="0em">∂</mo><msub><mrow></mrow><mrow><mi>y</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>y</mi></mrow></msub><mo>+</mo><mfrac><mn>2</mn><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>−</mo><mi>y</mi></mrow></mfrac><mo lspace="0em">∂</mo><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>x</mi></msub><mo>+</mo><mfrac><mn>2</mn><mrow><mi>z</mi><mo>−</mo><mi>y</mi></mrow></mfrac><mo lspace="0em">∂</mo><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>z</mi></msub><mo>−</mo><mfrac><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>α</mi></mrow><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>y</mi><mo>−</mo><mi>x</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup></mfrac><mo>−</mo><mfrac><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>ν</mi></mrow><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>y</mi><mo>−</mo><mi>z</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup></mfrac></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\frac{\kappa}{2}\partial_{xx}+\frac{2}{y-x}\partial_{y}+\frac{2}{z-x}\partial_{z}-\frac{2\alpha}{(x-y)^{2}}-\frac{2\nu}{(x-z)^{2}},\frac{\kappa}{2}\partial_{yy}+\frac{2}{x-y}\partial_{x}+\frac{2}{z-y}\partial_{z}-\frac{2\alpha}{(y-x)^{2}}-\frac{2\nu}{(y-z)^{2}}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
<div id="A2.SS2.SSS1.Px1.p51" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A2.SS2.SSS1.Px1.p51.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.SS2.SSS1.Px1.p51.1.1" class="ltx_text">where we also use reversibility for <math id="A2.SS2.SSS1.Px1.p51.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathrm{SLE}_{8/3}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>SLE</mi><mrow><mn>8</mn><mo>/</mo><mn>3</mn></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathrm{SLE}_{8/3}</annotation></semantics></math>. It is easy to check that in general <math id="A2.SS2.SSS1.Px1.p51.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\tilde{\kappa}\in\{\kappa,16/\kappa\},h(x,z)=" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi>κ</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mi>κ</mi><mo>,</mo><mrow><mn>16</mn><mo>/</mo><mi>κ</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>h</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>z</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mphantom></mphantom></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\tilde{\kappa}\in\{\kappa,16/\kappa\},h(x,z)=</annotation></semantics></math> <math id="A2.SS2.SSS1.Px1.p51.m3" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="-2\nu/(x-z)^{2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>2</mn><mi>ν</mi><mo>/</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>−</mo><mi>z</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">-2\nu/(x-z)^{2}</annotation></semantics></math> is a solution of the integrability condition above. More generally, if <math id="A2.SS2.SSS1.Px1.p51.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="n" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>n</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">n</annotation></semantics></math> points <math id="A2.SS2.SSS1.Px1.p51.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="z_{1},\ldots,z_{n}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>z</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>z</mi><mi>n</mi></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">z_{1},\ldots,z_{n}</annotation></semantics></math> are marked on the real line, a (particular) solution of the integrability condition is given by <math id="A2.SS2.SSS1.Px1.p51.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\tilde{\kappa}\in\{\kappa,16/\kappa\}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi>κ</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mrow><mi>κ</mi><mo>,</mo><mrow><mn>16</mn><mo>/</mo><mi>κ</mi></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\tilde{\kappa}\in\{\kappa,16/\kappa\}</annotation></semantics></math>,</span></p>
</div>
<div id="A2.SS2.SSS1.Px1.p52" class="ltx_para">
<table id="A2.EGx2" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_eqnarray ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A2.Ex81"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A2.Ex80.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle h(x,z)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>h</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>z</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle h(x,z)</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_center ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A2.Ex80.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mo>=</mo><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A2.Ex80.m3" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\displaystyle-2\sum_{i}\frac{\mu_{i}}{\left(z_{i}-x\right)^{2}}-2\sum_{i&lt;j}\nu_{ij}\left(\frac{1}{z_{i}-x}-\frac{1}{z_{j}-x}\right)^{2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>2</mn><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munder><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mi>i</mi></munder></mstyle><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><msub><mi>μ</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><msup><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>z</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>−</mo><mi>x</mi></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup></mfrac></mstyle><mo>−</mo><mn>2</mn><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munder><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>&lt;</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow></munder></mstyle><msub><mi>ν</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow></msub><msup><mrow><mo>(</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mrow><msub><mi>z</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>−</mo><mi>x</mi></mrow></mfrac></mstyle><mo>−</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mrow><msub><mi>z</mi><mi>j</mi></msub><mo>−</mo><mi>x</mi></mrow></mfrac></mstyle><mo>)</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle-2\sum_{i}\frac{\mu_{i}}{\left(z_{i}-x\right)^{2}}-2\sum_{i&lt;j}\nu_{ij}\left(\frac{1}{z_{i}-x}-\frac{1}{z_{j}-x}\right)^{2}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr>
<tr class="ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_center ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A2.Ex81.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mo>=</mo><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A2.Ex81.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\sum_{i}\frac{\mu_{i}^{\prime}}{\left(z_{i}-x\right)^{2}}+\sum_{i&lt;j}\frac{\nu_{ij}^{\prime}}{\left(z_{i}-x\right)\left(z_{j}-x\right)}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munder><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mi>i</mi></munder></mstyle><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><msubsup><mi>μ</mi><mi>i</mi><mo>′</mo></msubsup><msup><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>z</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>−</mo><mi>x</mi></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup></mfrac></mstyle></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munder><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>&lt;</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow></munder></mstyle><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><msubsup><mi>ν</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow><mo>′</mo></msubsup><mrow><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>z</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>−</mo><mi>x</mi></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>z</mi><mi>j</mi></msub><mo>−</mo><mi>x</mi></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow></mfrac></mstyle></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\sum_{i}\frac{\mu_{i}^{\prime}}{\left(z_{i}-x\right)^{2}}+\sum_{i&lt;j}\frac{\nu_{ij}^{\prime}}{\left(z_{i}-x\right)\left(z_{j}-x\right)}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
<div id="A2.SS2.SSS1.Px1.p53" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A2.SS2.SSS1.Px1.p53.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.SS2.SSS1.Px1.p53.1.1" class="ltx_text">where <math id="A2.SS2.SSS1.Px1.p53.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mu_{i},\nu_{ij}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>μ</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>ν</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mu_{i},\nu_{ij}</annotation></semantics></math> are real parameters. When <math id="A2.SS2.SSS1.Px1.p53.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\kappa=\tilde{\kappa}=8/3,\mu_{i},\nu_{ij}\geq 0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>κ</mi><mo>=</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>κ</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mo>=</mo><mrow><mn>8</mn><mo>/</mo><mn>3</mn></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>μ</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><mrow><msub><mi>ν</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow></msub><mo>≥</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\kappa=\tilde{\kappa}=8/3,\mu_{i},\nu_{ij}\geq 0</annotation></semantics></math>, and <math id="A2.SS2.SSS1.Px1.p53.m3" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="x&lt;y&lt;z_{1}&lt;\cdots z_{n}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>&lt;</mo><mi>y</mi><mo>&lt;</mo><mi>z</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mn>1</mn></msub><mo rspace="0.1389em">&lt;</mo><mo lspace="0.1389em" rspace="0em">⋯</mo><mi>z</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>n</mi></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">x&lt;y&lt;z_{1}&lt;\cdots z_{n}</annotation></semantics></math>, it is easy to think of a probabilistic situation corresponding to this. Consider a chordal <math id="A2.SS2.SSS1.Px1.p53.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathrm{SLE}_{8/3}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>SLE</mi><mrow><mn>8</mn><mo>/</mo><mn>3</mn></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathrm{SLE}_{8/3}</annotation></semantics></math> from <math id="A2.SS2.SSS1.Px1.p53.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="x" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>x</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">x</annotation></semantics></math> to <math id="A2.SS2.SSS1.Px1.p53.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="y" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>y</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">y</annotation></semantics></math>, and condition it not to intersect independent one-sided restriction samples <math id="A2.SS2.SSS1.Px1.p53.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="z_{i}\leftrightarrow\infty" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>z</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">↔</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">∞</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">z_{i}\leftrightarrow\infty</annotation></semantics></math> (with index <math id="A2.SS2.SSS1.Px1.p53.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mu_{i}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>μ</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mu_{i}</annotation></semantics></math> ) and <math id="A2.SS2.SSS1.Px1.p53.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="z_{i}\leftrightarrow z_{j}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>z</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">↔</mo><msub><mi>z</mi><mi>j</mi></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">z_{i}\leftrightarrow z_{j}</annotation></semantics></math> (with index <math id="A2.SS2.SSS1.Px1.p53.m10" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\nu_{i,j}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>ν</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\nu_{i,j}</annotation></semantics></math> ). Then reversibility for the conditional SLE corresponds to a partition function <math id="A2.SS2.SSS1.Px1.p53.m11" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\psi" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>ψ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\psi</annotation></semantics></math> solving PDEs where <math id="A2.SS2.SSS1.Px1.p53.m12" class="ltx_Math" alttext="h" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>h</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">h</annotation></semantics></math> is as above.</span></p>
</div>
<div id="A2.SS2.SSS1.Px1.p54" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A2.SS2.SSS1.Px1.p54.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.SS2.SSS1.Px1.p54.1.1" class="ltx_text">∎</span></p>
</div>
</div>
<div id="A2.SS2.SSS1.Px1.p55" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent"><span class="ltx_inline-block"><svg id="A2.SS2.SSS1.Px1.p55.pic1" class="ltx_picture" height="86.23" overflow="visible" version="1.1" viewBox="0 0 429.64 86.23" width="429.64"><g style="--ltx-stroke-color:#000000;--ltx-fill-color:#000000;" fill="#000000" stroke="#000000" stroke-width="0.4pt" transform="translate(0,86.23) matrix(1 0 0 -1 0 0)"><g style="--ltx-fill-color:#4D4D4D;" fill="#4D4D4D" fill-opacity="1.0"><path style="stroke:none" d="M 0 4.63 L 0 81.6 C 0 84.16 2.07 86.23 4.63 86.23 L 425.01 86.23 C 427.56 86.23 429.64 84.16 429.64 81.6 L 429.64 4.63 C 429.64 2.07 427.56 0 425.01 0 L 4.63 0 C 2.07 0 0 2.07 0 4.63 Z"></path></g><g style="--ltx-fill-color:#F9F9F9;" fill="#F9F9F9" fill-opacity="1.0"><path style="stroke:none" d="M 0.69 4.63 L 0.69 67.36 L 428.94 67.36 L 428.94 4.63 C 428.94 2.45 427.18 0.69 425.01 0.69 L 4.63 0.69 C 2.45 0.69 0.69 2.45 0.69 4.63 Z"></path></g><g fill-opacity="1.0" transform="matrix(1.0 0.0 0.0 1.0 20.38 71.99)"><foreignObject style="--ltx-fo-width:24.44em;--ltx-fo-height:0.69em;--ltx-fo-depth:0em;font-size:10pt;" height="9.61" overflow="visible" transform="matrix(1 0 0 -1 0 9.61)" width="338.18"><span class="ltx_foreignobject_container"><span class="ltx_foreignobject_content">
<span id="A2.SS2.SSS1.Px1.p55.pic1.1" class="ltx_inline-block ltx_minipage ltx_align_bottom" style="width:24.44em;">
