</section>
</section>
<section id="A2.SS2.SSS2" class="ltx_subsubsection">
<h4 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsubsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsubsection">(b) </span>Applying classical results</h4>

<section id="A2.SS2.SSS2.Px1" class="ltx_paragraph">
<h5 class="ltx_title ltx_title_paragraph" style="--ltx-fg-color:#FF0000;">Problem 2b1</h5>

<div id="A2.SS2.SSS2.Px1.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A2.SS2.SSS2.Px1.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.SS2.SSS2.Px1.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text"></span>
<br class="ltx_break" style="--ltx-break-space:-10.0pt;"></p>
</div>
<div id="A2.SS2.SSS2.Px1.p2" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent"><span class="ltx_inline-block"><svg id="A2.SS2.SSS2.Px1.p2.pic1" class="ltx_picture" height="132.91" overflow="visible" version="1.1" viewBox="0 0 429.64 132.91" width="429.64"><g style="--ltx-stroke-color:#000000;--ltx-fill-color:#000000;" fill="#000000" stroke="#000000" stroke-width="0.4pt" transform="translate(0,132.91) matrix(1 0 0 -1 0 0)"><g style="--ltx-fill-color:#3D6666;" fill="#3D6666" fill-opacity="1.0"><path style="stroke:none" d="M 0 4.63 L 0 128.28 C 0 130.84 2.07 132.91 4.63 132.91 L 425.01 132.91 C 427.56 132.91 429.64 130.84 429.64 128.28 L 429.64 4.63 C 429.64 2.07 427.56 0 425.01 0 L 4.63 0 C 2.07 0 0 2.07 0 4.63 Z"></path></g><g style="--ltx-fill-color:#F9F9F9;" fill="#F9F9F9" fill-opacity="1.0"><path style="stroke:none" d="M 0.69 4.63 L 0.69 114.04 L 428.94 114.04 L 428.94 4.63 C 428.94 2.45 427.18 0.69 425.01 0.69 L 4.63 0.69 C 2.45 0.69 0.69 2.45 0.69 4.63 Z"></path></g><g fill-opacity="1.0" transform="matrix(1.0 0.0 0.0 1.0 20.38 118.67)"><foreignObject style="--ltx-fo-width:24.44em;--ltx-fo-height:0.69em;--ltx-fo-depth:0em;font-size:10pt;" height="9.61" overflow="visible" transform="matrix(1 0 0 -1 0 9.61)" width="338.18"><span class="ltx_foreignobject_container"><span class="ltx_foreignobject_content">
<span id="A2.SS2.SSS2.Px1.p2.pic1.1" class="ltx_inline-block ltx_minipage ltx_align_bottom" style="width:24.44em;">
<span id="A2.SS2.SSS2.Px1.p2.pic1.1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.SS2.SSS2.Px1.p2.pic1.1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold" style="--ltx-fg-color:#FFFFFF;">Problem</span></span>
</span></span></span></foreignObject></g><g fill-opacity="1.0" transform="matrix(1.0 0.0 0.0 1.0 20.38 14.66)"><foreignObject style="--ltx-fo-width:32.01em;--ltx-fo-height:6.33em;--ltx-fo-depth:0.16em;font-size:10pt;" height="89.73" overflow="visible" transform="matrix(1 0 0 -1 0 87.58)" width="442.93"><span class="ltx_foreignobject_container"><span class="ltx_foreignobject_content">
<span id="A2.SS2.SSS2.Px1.p2.pic1.2" class="ltx_inline-block ltx_minipage ltx_align_bottom" style="width:32.01em;">
<span id="A2.SS2.SSS2.Px1.p2.pic1.2.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.SS2.SSS2.Px1.p2.pic1.2.1.1" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:80%;--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">Apply the s-cobordism theorem to show that if <math id="A2.SS2.SSS2.Px1.p2.pic1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="M" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">M</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">M</annotation></semantics></math> is a smooth <math id="A2.SS2.SSS2.Px1.p2.pic1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="7" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">7</mn><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">7</annotation></semantics></math>-manifold homotopy equivalent to <math id="A2.SS2.SSS2.Px1.p2.pic1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="S^{1}\times S^{6}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msup><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">S</mi><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">1</mn></msup><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" lspace="0.222em" mathcolor="#000000" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><msup><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">S</mi><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">6</mn></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">S^{1}\times S^{6}</annotation></semantics></math>, which bounds an <math id="A2.SS2.SSS2.Px1.p2.pic1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="8" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">8</mn><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">8</annotation></semantics></math>-manifold <math id="A2.SS2.SSS2.Px1.p2.pic1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="W" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">W</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">W</annotation></semantics></math> homotopy equivalent to <math id="A2.SS2.SSS2.Px1.p2.pic1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="S^{1}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">S</mi><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">1</mn></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">S^{1}</annotation></semantics></math>, then <math id="A2.SS2.SSS2.Px1.p2.pic1.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="M" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">M</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">M</annotation></semantics></math> is diffeomorphic to <math id="A2.SS2.SSS2.Px1.p2.pic1.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="S^{1}\times S^{6}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msup><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">S</mi><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">1</mn></msup><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" lspace="0.222em" mathcolor="#000000" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><msup><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">S</mi><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">6</mn></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">S^{1}\times S^{6}</annotation></semantics></math>.</span></span><span class="ltx_inline-block"><svg id="A2.SS2.SSS2.Px1.p2.pic1.pic1" class="ltx_picture" color="#FF0000" height="18.24" overflow="visible" style="vertical-align:-4.1px" version="1.1" viewBox="0 0 18.24 18.24" width="18.24"><g style="--ltx-stroke-color:#FF0000;--ltx-fill-color:#FF0000;" fill="#FF0000" stroke="#FF0000" stroke-width="1.8pt" transform="translate(0,18.24) matrix(1 0 0 -1 0 0) translate(1.25,0) translate(0,1.25)"><path style="fill:none" d="M 0 0 L 15.75 15.75 M 0 15.75 L 15.75 0"></path></g></svg></span>
<span id="A2.SS2.SSS2.Px1.p2.pic1.2.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.SS2.SSS2.Px1.p2.pic1.2.2.1" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:80%;--ltx-fg-color:#FF0000;">GPT-5 thinking failed</span></span>
<span id="A2.SS2.SSS2.Px1.p2.pic1.2.3" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.SS2.SSS2.Px1.p2.pic1.2.3.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic" style="font-size:80%;--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">Proposed by Qiuyu Ren</span></span>
</span></span></span></foreignObject></g></g></svg></span>
</div>
<div id="A2.SS2.SSS2.Px1.1" class="ltx_proof">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_font_italic ltx_title_proof"><span id="A2.SS2.SSS2.Px1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Response of GPT-5-thinking</span>.</h6>
<div id="A2.SS2.SSS2.Px1.p3" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A2.SS2.SSS2.Px1.p3.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.SS2.SSS2.Px1.p3.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Set-up.<span id="A2.SS2.SSS2.Px1.p3.1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_medium">
Pick a homotopy equivalence <math id="A2.SS2.SSS2.Px1.p3.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="f\colon M\to S^{1}\times S^{6}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>f</mi><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mrow><mi>M</mi><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><mrow><msup><mi>S</mi><mn>1</mn></msup><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><msup><mi>S</mi><mn>6</mn></msup></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">f\colon M\to S^{1}\times S^{6}</annotation></semantics></math>. Since <math id="A2.SS2.SSS2.Px1.p3.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\pi_{1}(M)\cong\mathbb{Z}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>π</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>M</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>≅</mo><mi>ℤ</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\pi_{1}(M)\cong\mathbb{Z}</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="A2.SS2.SSS2.Px1.p3.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathrm{Wh}(\mathbb{Z})=0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>Wh</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>ℤ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathrm{Wh}(\mathbb{Z})=0</annotation></semantics></math>, every homotopy equivalence with this fundamental group is <em id="A2.SS2.SSS2.Px1.p3.1.1.1.1" class="ltx_emph ltx_font_italic">simple</em>.</span></span></p>
</div>
<div id="A2.SS2.SSS2.Px1.p4" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A2.SS2.SSS2.Px1.p4.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.SS2.SSS2.Px1.p4.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Step 1: Extend over the bounding <math id="A2.SS2.SSS2.Px1.p4.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="W" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>W</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">W</annotation></semantics></math>.<span id="A2.SS2.SSS2.Px1.p4.1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_medium">
Because <math id="A2.SS2.SSS2.Px1.p4.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="W\simeq S^{1}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>W</mi><mo>≃</mo><msup><mi>S</mi><mn>1</mn></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">W\simeq S^{1}</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="A2.SS2.SSS2.Px1.p4.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\partial W=M" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mo>∂</mo><mi>W</mi></mrow><mo>=</mo><mi>M</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\partial W=M</annotation></semantics></math>, Poincaré–Lefschetz duality gives</span></span></p>
<table id="A2.Ex82" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A2.Ex82.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="H_{k}(W,M)\;\cong\;H^{8-k}(W)\;=\;\begin{cases}\mathbb{Z}&amp;k=8,7,\\
0&amp;k\leq 6.\end{cases}" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>H</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>W</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>M</mi><mo rspace="0.280em" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.558em">≅</mo><mrow><msup><mi>H</mi><mrow><mn>8</mn><mo>−</mo><mi>k</mi></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>W</mi><mo rspace="0.280em" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.558em">=</mo><mrow><mo>{</mo><mtable columnspacing="5pt" displaystyle="true" rowspacing="0pt"><mtr><mtd class="ltx_align_left" columnalign="left"><mi>ℤ</mi></mtd><mtd class="ltx_align_left" columnalign="left"><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>8</mn></mrow><mo>,</mo><mn>7</mn></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow></mtd></mtr><mtr><mtd class="ltx_align_left" columnalign="left"><mn>0</mn></mtd><mtd class="ltx_align_left" columnalign="left"><mrow><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>≤</mo><mn>6</mn></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow></mtd></mtr></mtable></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">H_{k}(W,M)\;\cong\;H^{8-k}(W)\;=\;\begin{cases}\mathbb{Z}&amp;k=8,7,\\
0&amp;k\leq 6.\end{cases}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A2.SS2.SSS2.Px1.p4.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.SS2.SSS2.Px1.p4.2.1" class="ltx_text">Hence all relative cohomology groups <math id="A2.SS2.SSS2.Px1.p4.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="H^{k}(W,M;\pi_{k-1}(S^{6}))" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msup><mi>H</mi><mi>k</mi></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>W</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>M</mi><mo>,</mo><mrow><msub><mi>π</mi><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>S</mi><mn>6</mn></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">H^{k}(W,M;\pi_{k-1}(S^{6}))</annotation></semantics></math> (which would carry the primary obstructions to extending <math id="A2.SS2.SSS2.Px1.p4.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="f" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>f</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">f</annotation></semantics></math> into <math id="A2.SS2.SSS2.Px1.p4.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="S^{1}\times D^{7}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msup><mi>S</mi><mn>1</mn></msup><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><msup><mi>D</mi><mn>7</mn></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">S^{1}\times D^{7}</annotation></semantics></math>) vanish for <math id="A2.SS2.SSS2.Px1.p4.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="3\leq k\leq 7" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mn>3</mn><mo>≤</mo><mi>k</mi><mo>≤</mo><mn>7</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">3\leq k\leq 7</annotation></semantics></math>. Therefore <math id="A2.SS2.SSS2.Px1.p4.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="f" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>f</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">f</annotation></semantics></math> extends to a map of pairs</span></p>
<table id="A2.Ex83" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A2.Ex83.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="F\colon(W,M)\longrightarrow(S^{1}\times D^{7},\;S^{1}\times S^{6})" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>F</mi><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>W</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>M</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟶</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msup><mi>S</mi><mn>1</mn></msup><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><msup><mi>D</mi><mn>7</mn></msup></mrow><mo rspace="0.447em">,</mo><mrow><msup><mi>S</mi><mn>1</mn></msup><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><msup><mi>S</mi><mn>6</mn></msup></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">F\colon(W,M)\longrightarrow(S^{1}\times D^{7},\;S^{1}\times S^{6})</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A2.SS2.SSS2.Px1.p4.3" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.SS2.SSS2.Px1.p4.3.1" class="ltx_text">which induces an isomorphism on <math id="A2.SS2.SSS2.Px1.p4.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\pi_{1}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>π</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\pi_{1}</annotation></semantics></math> and has degree <math id="A2.SS2.SSS2.Px1.p4.m10" class="ltx_Math" alttext="1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mn>1</mn><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">1</annotation></semantics></math> on top homology (a degree-<math id="A2.SS2.SSS2.Px1.p4.m11" class="ltx_Math" alttext="1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mn>1</mn><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">1</annotation></semantics></math> normal map of pairs).</span></p>
</div>
<div id="A2.SS2.SSS2.Px1.p5" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A2.SS2.SSS2.Px1.p5.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.SS2.SSS2.Px1.p5.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Step 2: Surgery relative to the boundary.<span id="A2.SS2.SSS2.Px1.p5.1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_medium">
Perform surgery in the <em id="A2.SS2.SSS2.Px1.p5.1.1.1.1" class="ltx_emph ltx_font_italic">interior</em> of <math id="A2.SS2.SSS2.Px1.p5.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="W" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>W</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">W</annotation></semantics></math>, relative to <math id="A2.SS2.SSS2.Px1.p5.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\partial W=M" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mo>∂</mo><mi>W</mi></mrow><mo>=</mo><mi>M</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\partial W=M</annotation></semantics></math>, to improve <math id="A2.SS2.SSS2.Px1.p5.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="F" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>F</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">F</annotation></semantics></math> to a homotopy equivalence of pairs</span></span></p>
<table id="A2.Ex84" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A2.Ex84.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="F^{\prime}\colon(W^{\prime},M)\;\xrightarrow{\simeq}\;(S^{1}\times D^{7},\;S^{1}\times S^{6})." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msup><mi>F</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>W</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo>,</mo><mi>M</mi><mo rspace="0.280em" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mover accent="true"><mo>→</mo><mo mathsize="0.700em">≃</mo></mover><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msup><mi>S</mi><mn>1</mn></msup><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><msup><mi>D</mi><mn>7</mn></msup></mrow><mo rspace="0.447em">,</mo><mrow><msup><mi>S</mi><mn>1</mn></msup><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><msup><mi>S</mi><mn>6</mn></msup></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">F^{\prime}\colon(W^{\prime},M)\;\xrightarrow{\simeq}\;(S^{1}\times D^{7},\;S^{1}\times S^{6}).</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A2.SS2.SSS2.Px1.p5.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.SS2.SSS2.Px1.p5.2.1" class="ltx_text">There is no middle-dimensional obstruction: the potential obstruction lives in
<math id="A2.SS2.SSS2.Px1.p5.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="L_{8}(\mathbb{Z}[\mathbb{Z}])" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>L</mi><mn>8</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>ℤ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mi>ℤ</mi><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">L_{8}(\mathbb{Z}[\mathbb{Z}])</annotation></semantics></math> and is represented by a form built from <math id="A2.SS2.SSS2.Px1.p5.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="H_{4}(W,M;\mathbb{Z}[\mathbb{Z}])" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>H</mi><mn>4</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>W</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>M</mi><mo>,</mo><mrow><mi>ℤ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mi>ℤ</mi><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">H_{4}(W,M;\mathbb{Z}[\mathbb{Z}])</annotation></semantics></math>, but <math id="A2.SS2.SSS2.Px1.p5.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="H_{4}(W,M;\mathbb{Z}[\mathbb{Z}])=0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>H</mi><mn>4</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>W</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>M</mi><mo>,</mo><mrow><mi>ℤ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mi>ℤ</mi><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">H_{4}(W,M;\mathbb{Z}[\mathbb{Z}])=0</annotation></semantics></math> by the vanishing above, so the obstruction is zero. Thus the relative surgery goes through.</span></p>
</div>
<div id="A2.SS2.SSS2.Px1.p6" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A2.SS2.SSS2.Px1.p6.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.SS2.SSS2.Px1.p6.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Step 3: The resulting cobordism is an h-cobordism.<span id="A2.SS2.SSS2.Px1.p6.1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_medium">
Take the trace of the surgeries (equivalently, compare <math id="A2.SS2.SSS2.Px1.p6.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="M" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>M</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">M</annotation></semantics></math> with the new boundary <math id="A2.SS2.SSS2.Px1.p6.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="S^{1}\times S^{6}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msup><mi>S</mi><mn>1</mn></msup><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><msup><mi>S</mi><mn>6</mn></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">S^{1}\times S^{6}</annotation></semantics></math> via <math id="A2.SS2.SSS2.Px1.p6.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="F^{\prime}|_{\partial}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mrow><msup><mi>F</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow><mo>∂</mo></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">F^{\prime}|_{\partial}</annotation></semantics></math>). One obtains an 8-dimensional cobordism <math id="A2.SS2.SSS2.Px1.p6.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="U" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>U</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">U</annotation></semantics></math> from <math id="A2.SS2.SSS2.Px1.p6.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="M" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>M</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">M</annotation></semantics></math> to <math id="A2.SS2.SSS2.Px1.p6.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="S^{1}\times S^{6}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msup><mi>S</mi><mn>1</mn></msup><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><msup><mi>S</mi><mn>6</mn></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">S^{1}\times S^{6}</annotation></semantics></math> in which the inclusions of both ends are homotopy equivalences (handles occur only in indices <math id="A2.SS2.SSS2.Px1.p6.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="3,4,5" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mn>3</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>4</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>5</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">3,4,5</annotation></semantics></math>). Hence <math id="A2.SS2.SSS2.Px1.p6.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="U" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>U</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">U</annotation></semantics></math> is an <em id="A2.SS2.SSS2.Px1.p6.1.1.1.1" class="ltx_emph ltx_font_italic">h-cobordism</em> between <math id="A2.SS2.SSS2.Px1.p6.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="M" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>M</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">M</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="A2.SS2.SSS2.Px1.p6.m10" class="ltx_Math" alttext="S^{1}\times S^{6}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msup><mi>S</mi><mn>1</mn></msup><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><msup><mi>S</mi><mn>6</mn></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">S^{1}\times S^{6}</annotation></semantics></math>.</span></span></p>
</div>
<div id="A2.SS2.SSS2.Px1.p7" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A2.SS2.SSS2.Px1.p7.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.SS2.SSS2.Px1.p7.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Step 4: Apply s-cobordism.<span id="A2.SS2.SSS2.Px1.p7.1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_medium">
Here <math id="A2.SS2.SSS2.Px1.p7.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\dim U=8\geq 6" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mo rspace="0.167em">dim</mo><mi>U</mi></mrow><mo>=</mo><mn>8</mn><mo>≥</mo><mn>6</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\dim U=8\geq 6</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="A2.SS2.SSS2.Px1.p7.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\pi_{1}(U)\cong\mathbb{Z}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>π</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>U</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>≅</mo><mi>ℤ</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\pi_{1}(U)\cong\mathbb{Z}</annotation></semantics></math> has <math id="A2.SS2.SSS2.Px1.p7.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathrm{Wh}(\mathbb{Z})=0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>Wh</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>ℤ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathrm{Wh}(\mathbb{Z})=0</annotation></semantics></math>. Thus the Whitehead torsion of the h-cobordism vanishes, so <math id="A2.SS2.SSS2.Px1.p7.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="U" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>U</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">U</annotation></semantics></math> is an <em id="A2.SS2.SSS2.Px1.p7.1.1.1.1" class="ltx_emph ltx_font_italic">s-cobordism</em>. By the s-cobordism theorem, <math id="A2.SS2.SSS2.Px1.p7.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="U\cong M\times[0,1]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>U</mi><mo>≅</mo><mrow><mi>M</mi><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">U\cong M\times[0,1]</annotation></semantics></math> rel <math id="A2.SS2.SSS2.Px1.p7.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="M" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>M</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">M</annotation></semantics></math>. In particular, its top boundary is diffeomorphic to its bottom boundary:</span></span></p>
<table id="A2.Ex85" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A2.Ex85.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="M\;\cong\;S^{1}\times S^{6}." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>M</mi><mo lspace="0.558em" rspace="0.558em">≅</mo><mrow><msup><mi>S</mi><mn>1</mn></msup><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><msup><mi>S</mi><mn>6</mn></msup></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">M\;\cong\;S^{1}\times S^{6}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
<div id="A2.SS2.SSS2.Px1.p8" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A2.SS2.SSS2.Px1.p8.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.SS2.SSS2.Px1.p8.1.1" class="ltx_text">∎</span></p>
</div>
</div>
<div id="A2.SS2.SSS2.Px1.2" class="ltx_proof">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_font_italic ltx_title_proof"><span id="A2.SS2.SSS2.Px1.2.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Standard Solution</span>.</h6>
<div id="A2.SS2.SSS2.Px1.p9" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A2.SS2.SSS2.Px1.p9.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.SS2.SSS2.Px1.p9.1.1" class="ltx_text">Drill out the tubular neighborhood of a simple loop <math id="A2.SS2.SSS2.Px1.p9.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\gamma" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>γ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\gamma</annotation></semantics></math> in the interior of <math id="A2.SS2.SSS2.Px1.p9.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="W" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>W</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">W</annotation></semantics></math> that represents a generator of <math id="A2.SS2.SSS2.Px1.p9.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="H_{1}(W)\cong\mathbb{Z}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>H</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>W</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>≅</mo><mi>ℤ</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">H_{1}(W)\cong\mathbb{Z}</annotation></semantics></math> to obtain a cobordism <math id="A2.SS2.SSS2.Px1.p9.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="W^{\prime}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi>W</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">W^{\prime}</annotation></semantics></math> from <math id="A2.SS2.SSS2.Px1.p9.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="S^{1}\times S^{6}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msup><mi>S</mi><mn>1</mn></msup><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><msup><mi>S</mi><mn>6</mn></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">S^{1}\times S^{6}</annotation></semantics></math> to <math id="A2.SS2.SSS2.Px1.p9.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="M" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>M</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">M</annotation></semantics></math>. By homology long exact sequences plus the fact that <math id="A2.SS2.SSS2.Px1.p9.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\pi_{1}=\mathbb{Z}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>π</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>=</mo><mi>ℤ</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\pi_{1}=\mathbb{Z}</annotation></semantics></math> is abelian, one can show that <math id="A2.SS2.SSS2.Px1.p9.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="W^{\prime}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi>W</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">W^{\prime}</annotation></semantics></math> is an <math id="A2.SS2.SSS2.Px1.p9.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="h" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>h</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">h</annotation></semantics></math>-cobordism. Since the Whitehead group of <math id="A2.SS2.SSS2.Px1.p9.m10" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbb{Z}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>ℤ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbb{Z}</annotation></semantics></math> is trivial, <math id="A2.SS2.SSS2.Px1.p9.m11" class="ltx_Math" alttext="W^{\prime}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi>W</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">W^{\prime}</annotation></semantics></math> is an <math id="A2.SS2.SSS2.Px1.p9.m12" class="ltx_Math" alttext="s" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>s</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">s</annotation></semantics></math>-cobordism. The <math id="A2.SS2.SSS2.Px1.p9.m13" class="ltx_Math" alttext="s" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>s</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">s</annotation></semantics></math>-cobordism theorem implies that <math id="A2.SS2.SSS2.Px1.p9.m14" class="ltx_Math" alttext="W^{\prime}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi>W</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">W^{\prime}</annotation></semantics></math> is diffeomorphic to the trivial cobordism, hence the result.
∎</span></p>
</div>
</div>
<div id="A2.SS2.SSS2.Px1.p10" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent"><span class="ltx_inline-block"><svg id="A2.SS2.SSS2.Px1.p10.pic1" class="ltx_picture" height="84.08" overflow="visible" version="1.1" viewBox="0 0 429.64 84.08" width="429.64"><g style="--ltx-stroke-color:#000000;--ltx-fill-color:#000000;" fill="#000000" stroke="#000000" stroke-width="0.4pt" transform="translate(0,84.08) matrix(1 0 0 -1 0 0)"><g style="--ltx-fill-color:#4D4D4D;" fill="#4D4D4D" fill-opacity="1.0"><path style="stroke:none" d="M 0 4.63 L 0 79.45 C 0 82 2.07 84.08 4.63 84.08 L 425.01 84.08 C 427.56 84.08 429.64 82 429.64 79.45 L 429.64 4.63 C 429.64 2.07 427.56 0 425.01 0 L 4.63 0 C 2.07 0 0 2.07 0 4.63 Z"></path></g><g style="--ltx-fill-color:#F9F9F9;" fill="#F9F9F9" fill-opacity="1.0"><path style="stroke:none" d="M 0.69 4.63 L 0.69 65.21 L 428.94 65.21 L 428.94 4.63 C 428.94 2.45 427.18 0.69 425.01 0.69 L 4.63 0.69 C 2.45 0.69 0.69 2.45 0.69 4.63 Z"></path></g><g fill-opacity="1.0" transform="matrix(1.0 0.0 0.0 1.0 20.38 69.84)"><foreignObject style="--ltx-fo-width:24.44em;--ltx-fo-height:0.69em;--ltx-fo-depth:0em;font-size:10pt;" height="9.61" overflow="visible" transform="matrix(1 0 0 -1 0 9.61)" width="338.18"><span class="ltx_foreignobject_container"><span class="ltx_foreignobject_content">
<span id="A2.SS2.SSS2.Px1.p10.pic1.1" class="ltx_inline-block ltx_minipage ltx_align_bottom" style="width:24.44em;">
<span id="A2.SS2.SSS2.Px1.p10.pic1.1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.SS2.SSS2.Px1.p10.pic1.1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold" style="--ltx-fg-color:#FFFFFF;">Rubric</span></span>
</span></span></span></foreignObject></g><g fill-opacity="1.0" transform="matrix(1.0 0.0 0.0 1.0 20.38 12.5)"><foreignObject style="--ltx-fo-width:33.06em;--ltx-fo-height:2.96em;--ltx-fo-depth:0em;font-size:10pt;" height="40.9" overflow="visible" transform="matrix(1 0 0 -1 0 40.9)" width="457.46"><span class="ltx_foreignobject_container"><span class="ltx_foreignobject_content">
<span id="A2.SS2.SSS2.Px1.p10.pic1.2" class="ltx_inline-block ltx_minipage ltx_align_bottom" style="width:33.06em;">
<span id="A2.SS2.SSS2.Px1.p10.pic1.2.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.SS2.SSS2.Px1.p10.pic1.2.1.1" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:80%;--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">1 point if the solution is correct, most likely by building an h-cobordism between <math id="A2.SS2.SSS2.Px1.p10.pic1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="M" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">M</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">M</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="A2.SS2.SSS2.Px1.p10.pic1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="S^{1}\times S^{6}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msup><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">S</mi><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">1</mn></msup><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" lspace="0.222em" mathcolor="#000000" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><msup><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">S</mi><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">6</mn></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">S^{1}\times S^{6}</annotation></semantics></math>, arguing that it’s an s-cobordism, and applying the s-cobordism theorem to conclude.</span></span>
</span></span></span></foreignObject></g></g></svg></span>
</div>
<div id="A2.SS2.SSS2.Px1.p11" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent"><span class="ltx_inline-block"><svg id="A2.SS2.SSS2.Px1.p11.pic1" class="ltx_picture" height="54.13" overflow="visible" version="1.1" viewBox="0 0 429.64 54.13" width="429.64"><g style="--ltx-stroke-color:#000000;--ltx-fill-color:#000000;" fill="#000000" stroke="#000000" stroke-width="0.4pt" transform="translate(0,54.13) matrix(1 0 0 -1 0 0)"><g style="--ltx-fill-color:#5A996B;" fill="#5A996B" fill-opacity="1.0"><path style="stroke:none" d="M 0 4.63 L 0 49.51 C 0 52.06 2.07 54.13 4.63 54.13 L 425.01 54.13 C 427.56 54.13 429.64 52.06 429.64 49.51 L 429.64 4.63 C 429.64 2.07 427.56 0 425.01 0 L 4.63 0 C 2.07 0 0 2.07 0 4.63 Z"></path></g><g style="--ltx-fill-color:#F6FFF9;" fill="#F6FFF9" fill-opacity="1.0"><path style="stroke:none" d="M 0.69 4.63 L 0.69 35.38 L 428.94 35.38 L 428.94 4.63 C 428.94 2.45 427.18 0.69 425.01 0.69 L 4.63 0.69 C 2.45 0.69 0.69 2.45 0.69 4.63 Z"></path></g><g fill-opacity="1.0" transform="matrix(1.0 0.0 0.0 1.0 20.38 40.01)"><foreignObject style="--ltx-fo-width:24.44em;--ltx-fo-height:0.69em;--ltx-fo-depth:0em;font-size:10pt;" height="9.49" overflow="visible" transform="matrix(1 0 0 -1 0 9.49)" width="338.18"><span class="ltx_foreignobject_container"><span class="ltx_foreignobject_content">
