</span></span></span></foreignObject></g></g></svg></span>
</div>
</section>
<section id="A2.SS4.SSS1.Px2" class="ltx_paragraph">
<h5 class="ltx_title ltx_title_paragraph" style="--ltx-fg-color:#00E000;">Problem 4a2 </h5>

<div id="A2.SS4.SSS1.Px2.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A2.SS4.SSS1.Px2.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.SS4.SSS1.Px2.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text"></span>
<br class="ltx_break" style="--ltx-break-space:-10.0pt;"></p>
</div>
<div id="A2.SS4.SSS1.Px2.p2" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent"><span class="ltx_inline-block"><svg id="A2.SS4.SSS1.Px2.p2.pic1" class="ltx_picture" height="199.33" overflow="visible" version="1.1" viewBox="0 0 429.64 199.33" width="429.64"><g style="--ltx-stroke-color:#000000;--ltx-fill-color:#000000;" fill="#000000" stroke="#000000" stroke-width="0.4pt" transform="translate(0,199.33) matrix(1 0 0 -1 0 0)"><g style="--ltx-fill-color:#3D6666;" fill="#3D6666" fill-opacity="1.0"><path style="stroke:none" d="M 0 4.63 L 0 194.7 C 0 197.26 2.07 199.33 4.63 199.33 L 425.01 199.33 C 427.56 199.33 429.64 197.26 429.64 194.7 L 429.64 4.63 C 429.64 2.07 427.56 0 425.01 0 L 4.63 0 C 2.07 0 0 2.07 0 4.63 Z"></path></g><g style="--ltx-fill-color:#F9F9F9;" fill="#F9F9F9" fill-opacity="1.0"><path style="stroke:none" d="M 0.69 4.63 L 0.69 180.46 L 428.94 180.46 L 428.94 4.63 C 428.94 2.45 427.18 0.69 425.01 0.69 L 4.63 0.69 C 2.45 0.69 0.69 2.45 0.69 4.63 Z"></path></g><g fill-opacity="1.0" transform="matrix(1.0 0.0 0.0 1.0 20.38 185.09)"><foreignObject style="--ltx-fo-width:24.44em;--ltx-fo-height:0.69em;--ltx-fo-depth:0em;font-size:10pt;" height="9.61" overflow="visible" transform="matrix(1 0 0 -1 0 9.61)" width="338.18"><span class="ltx_foreignobject_container"><span class="ltx_foreignobject_content">
<span id="A2.SS4.SSS1.Px2.p2.pic1.1" class="ltx_inline-block ltx_minipage ltx_align_bottom" style="width:24.44em;">
<span id="A2.SS4.SSS1.Px2.p2.pic1.1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.SS4.SSS1.Px2.p2.pic1.1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold" style="--ltx-fg-color:#FFFFFF;">Problem</span></span>
</span></span></span></foreignObject></g><g fill-opacity="1.0" transform="matrix(1.0 0.0 0.0 1.0 20.38 14.66)"><foreignObject style="--ltx-fo-width:32.01em;--ltx-fo-height:11.13em;--ltx-fo-depth:0.16em;font-size:10pt;" height="156.15" overflow="visible" transform="matrix(1 0 0 -1 0 154)" width="442.93"><span class="ltx_foreignobject_container"><span class="ltx_foreignobject_content">
<span id="A2.SS4.SSS1.Px2.p2.pic1.2" class="ltx_inline-block ltx_minipage ltx_align_bottom" style="width:32.01em;">
<span id="A2.SS4.SSS1.Px2.p2.pic1.2.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.SS4.SSS1.Px2.p2.pic1.2.1.1" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:80%;--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">A man took 1000 rupees from his friend, and the money was gone. After that, he took 500 rupees from another friend. He spent 300 rupees on something and gave 200 rupees to each friend (100 rupees each). He also wanted to give an additional 900 rupees to the first friend and 400 rupees to the second friend. The total amount is 1300 rupees. He spent 300 rupees, so 1300 + 300 = 1600 rupees. However, he only brought 1500 rupees. What is the extra 100 rupees?</span></span><span class="ltx_inline-block"><svg id="A2.SS4.SSS1.Px2.p2.pic1.pic1" class="ltx_picture" color="#008000" height="18.24" overflow="visible" style="vertical-align:-4.1px" version="1.1" viewBox="0 0 18.24 18.24" width="18.24"><g style="--ltx-stroke-color:#009900;--ltx-fill-color:#009900;--ltx-fg-color:#009900;" color="#009900" fill="#009900" stroke="#009900" stroke-width="1.8pt" transform="translate(0,18.24) matrix(1 0 0 -1 0 0) translate(1.25,0) translate(0,1.25)"><path style="fill:none" d="M 0 7.87 L 5.51 0 L 15.75 15.75"></path></g></svg></span>
<span id="A2.SS4.SSS1.Px2.p2.pic1.2.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.SS4.SSS1.Px2.p2.pic1.2.2.1" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:80%;--ltx-fg-color:#008000;">GPT-5 thinking passed</span></span>
<span id="A2.SS4.SSS1.Px2.p2.pic1.2.3" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.SS4.SSS1.Px2.p2.pic1.2.3.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic" style="font-size:80%;--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">Proposed by Jiaxin Zhang</span></span>
</span></span></span></foreignObject></g></g></svg></span>
</div>
<div id="A2.SS4.SSS1.Px2.1" class="ltx_proof">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_font_italic ltx_title_proof"><span id="A2.SS4.SSS1.Px2.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Response of GPT-5-thinking</span>.</h6>
<div id="A2.SS4.SSS1.Px2.p3" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A2.SS4.SSS1.Px2.p3.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.SS4.SSS1.Px2.p3.1.1" class="ltx_text">There’s no missing money—just bad addition.</span></p>
</div>
<div id="A2.SS4.SSS1.Px2.p4" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A2.SS4.SSS1.Px2.p4.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.SS4.SSS1.Px2.p4.1.1" class="ltx_text">He borrowed <math id="A2.SS4.SSS1.Px2.p4.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="1500" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mn>1500</mn><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">1500</annotation></semantics></math> total. What happened to it?</span></p>
</div>
<div id="A2.SS4.SSS1.Px2.p5" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A2.SS4.SSS1.Px2.p5.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.SS4.SSS1.Px2.p5.1.1" class="ltx_text">* Lost <math id="A2.SS4.SSS1.Px2.p5.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="1000" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mn>1000</mn><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">1000</annotation></semantics></math>.
* Bought goods for <math id="A2.SS4.SSS1.Px2.p5.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="300" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mn>300</mn><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">300</annotation></semantics></math>.
* Repaid <math id="A2.SS4.SSS1.Px2.p5.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="100+100=200" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mn>100</mn><mo>+</mo><mn>100</mn></mrow><mo>=</mo><mn>200</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">100+100=200</annotation></semantics></math>.</span></p>
</div>
<div id="A2.SS4.SSS1.Px2.p6" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A2.SS4.SSS1.Px2.p6.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.SS4.SSS1.Px2.p6.1.1" class="ltx_text">So <math id="A2.SS4.SSS1.Px2.p6.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="1000+300+200=1500" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mn>1000</mn><mo>+</mo><mn>300</mn><mo>+</mo><mn>200</mn></mrow><mo>=</mo><mn>1500</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">1000+300+200=1500</annotation></semantics></math>. Accounted for exactly.</span></p>
</div>
<div id="A2.SS4.SSS1.Px2.p7" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A2.SS4.SSS1.Px2.p7.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.SS4.SSS1.Px2.p7.1.1" class="ltx_text">After repaying <math id="A2.SS4.SSS1.Px2.p7.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="200" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mn>200</mn><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">200</annotation></semantics></math>, he still owes <math id="A2.SS4.SSS1.Px2.p7.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="900" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mn>900</mn><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">900</annotation></semantics></math> to <math id="A2.SS4.SSS1.Px2.p7.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="X" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>X</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">X</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="A2.SS4.SSS1.Px2.p7.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="400" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mn>400</mn><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">400</annotation></semantics></math> to <math id="A2.SS4.SSS1.Px2.p7.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="Y" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>Y</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">Y</annotation></semantics></math>: total debt <math id="A2.SS4.SSS1.Px2.p7.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="1300" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mn>1300</mn><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">1300</annotation></semantics></math>. He also holds goods worth <math id="A2.SS4.SSS1.Px2.p7.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="300" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mn>300</mn><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">300</annotation></semantics></math>. Net shortfall <math id="A2.SS4.SSS1.Px2.p7.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="=1300-300=1000" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><mn>1300</mn><mo>−</mo><mn>300</mn></mrow><mo>=</mo><mn>1000</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">=1300-300=1000</annotation></semantics></math>, which is exactly the amount he lost.</span></p>
</div>
<div id="A2.SS4.SSS1.Px2.p8" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A2.SS4.SSS1.Px2.p8.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.SS4.SSS1.Px2.p8.1.1" class="ltx_text">The common “wrong” calculation adds debt to the purchase price: <math id="A2.SS4.SSS1.Px2.p8.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="900+400+300=1600" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mn>900</mn><mo>+</mo><mn>400</mn><mo>+</mo><mn>300</mn></mrow><mo>=</mo><mn>1600</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">900+400+300=1600</annotation></semantics></math>. That’s meaningless—you should **subtract** the value of what he still has from what he still owes, not add it.</span></p>
</div>
<div id="A2.SS4.SSS1.Px2.p9" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A2.SS4.SSS1.Px2.p9.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.SS4.SSS1.Px2.p9.1.1" class="ltx_text">∎</span></p>
</div>
</div>
<div id="A2.SS4.SSS1.Px2.2" class="ltx_proof">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_font_italic ltx_title_proof"><span id="A2.SS4.SSS1.Px2.2.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Standard Solution</span>.</h6>
<div id="A2.SS4.SSS1.Px2.p10" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A2.SS4.SSS1.Px2.p10.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.SS4.SSS1.Px2.p10.1.1" class="ltx_text">The mistake is adding debts and assets together. You should do debts minus assets, not add them.</span></p>
</div>
<div id="A2.SS4.SSS1.Px2.p11" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A2.SS4.SSS1.Px2.p11.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.SS4.SSS1.Px2.p11.1.1" class="ltx_text">Quick audit:</span></p>
</div>
<div id="A2.SS4.SSS1.Px2.p12" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A2.SS4.SSS1.Px2.p12.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.SS4.SSS1.Px2.p12.1.1" class="ltx_text">Borrowed: <math id="A2.SS4.SSS1.Px2.p12.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="1500" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mn>1500</mn><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">1500</annotation></semantics></math>
Lost: <math id="A2.SS4.SSS1.Px2.p12.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="1000" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mn>1000</mn><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">1000</annotation></semantics></math>
Purchase: <math id="A2.SS4.SSS1.Px2.p12.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="300" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mn>300</mn><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">300</annotation></semantics></math>
Repaid: <math id="A2.SS4.SSS1.Px2.p12.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="100+100=200" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mn>100</mn><mo>+</mo><mn>100</mn></mrow><mo>=</mo><mn>200</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">100+100=200</annotation></semantics></math></span></p>
</div>
<div id="A2.SS4.SSS1.Px2.p13" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A2.SS4.SSS1.Px2.p13.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.SS4.SSS1.Px2.p13.1.1" class="ltx_text">Check the flow: <math id="A2.SS4.SSS1.Px2.p13.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="1000+300+200=1500" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mn>1000</mn><mo>+</mo><mn>300</mn><mo>+</mo><mn>200</mn></mrow><mo>=</mo><mn>1500</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">1000+300+200=1500</annotation></semantics></math> — all accounted for.</span></p>
</div>
<div id="A2.SS4.SSS1.Px2.p14" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A2.SS4.SSS1.Px2.p14.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.SS4.SSS1.Px2.p14.1.1" class="ltx_text">Current position (after repaying <math id="A2.SS4.SSS1.Px2.p14.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="200" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mn>200</mn><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">200</annotation></semantics></math>):</span></p>
</div>
<div id="A2.SS4.SSS1.Px2.p15" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A2.SS4.SSS1.Px2.p15.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.SS4.SSS1.Px2.p15.1.1" class="ltx_text">Debts: owes <math id="A2.SS4.SSS1.Px2.p15.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="X=900" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>X</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>900</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">X=900</annotation></semantics></math>, owes <math id="A2.SS4.SSS1.Px2.p15.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="Y=400" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>Y</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>400</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">Y=400</annotation></semantics></math> → total <math id="A2.SS4.SSS1.Px2.p15.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="1300" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mn>1300</mn><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">1300</annotation></semantics></math>.
Assets: goods worth <math id="A2.SS4.SSS1.Px2.p15.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="300" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mn>300</mn><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">300</annotation></semantics></math>.</span></p>
</div>
<div id="A2.SS4.SSS1.Px2.p16" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A2.SS4.SSS1.Px2.p16.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.SS4.SSS1.Px2.p16.1.1" class="ltx_text">Net shortfall <math id="A2.SS4.SSS1.Px2.p16.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="=1300-300=1000" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><mn>1300</mn><mo>−</mo><mn>300</mn></mrow><mo>=</mo><mn>1000</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">=1300-300=1000</annotation></semantics></math>, exactly the amount he lost.</span></p>
</div>
<div id="A2.SS4.SSS1.Px2.p17" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A2.SS4.SSS1.Px2.p17.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.SS4.SSS1.Px2.p17.1.1" class="ltx_text">The bad calculation is <math id="A2.SS4.SSS1.Px2.p17.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="900+400+300=1600" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mn>900</mn><mo>+</mo><mn>400</mn><mo>+</mo><mn>300</mn></mrow><mo>=</mo><mn>1600</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">900+400+300=1600</annotation></semantics></math>. That wrongly adds the value of what he still has (<math id="A2.SS4.SSS1.Px2.p17.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="+300" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo>+</mo><mn>300</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">+300</annotation></semantics></math>) to what he still owes. The right move is to subtract it:</span></p>
</div>
<div id="A2.SS4.SSS1.Px2.p18" class="ltx_para">
<table id="A2.Ex106" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A2.Ex106.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(900+400)-300=1000." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>900</mn><mo>+</mo><mn>400</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>300</mn></mrow><mo>=</mo><mn>1000</mn></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(900+400)-300=1000.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
<div id="A2.SS4.SSS1.Px2.p19" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A2.SS4.SSS1.Px2.p19.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.SS4.SSS1.Px2.p19.1.1" class="ltx_text">∎</span></p>
</div>
</div>
<div id="A2.SS4.SSS1.Px2.p20" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent"><span class="ltx_inline-block"><svg id="A2.SS4.SSS1.Px2.p20.pic1" class="ltx_picture" height="69.62" overflow="visible" version="1.1" viewBox="0 0 429.64 69.62" width="429.64"><g style="--ltx-stroke-color:#000000;--ltx-fill-color:#000000;" fill="#000000" stroke="#000000" stroke-width="0.4pt" transform="translate(0,69.62) matrix(1 0 0 -1 0 0)"><g style="--ltx-fill-color:#4D4D4D;" fill="#4D4D4D" fill-opacity="1.0"><path style="stroke:none" d="M 0 4.63 L 0 65 C 0 67.55 2.07 69.62 4.63 69.62 L 425.01 69.62 C 427.56 69.62 429.64 67.55 429.64 65 L 429.64 4.63 C 429.64 2.07 427.56 0 425.01 0 L 4.63 0 C 2.07 0 0 2.07 0 4.63 Z"></path></g><g style="--ltx-fill-color:#F9F9F9;" fill="#F9F9F9" fill-opacity="1.0"><path style="stroke:none" d="M 0.69 4.63 L 0.69 50.76 L 428.94 50.76 L 428.94 4.63 C 428.94 2.45 427.18 0.69 425.01 0.69 L 4.63 0.69 C 2.45 0.69 0.69 2.45 0.69 4.63 Z"></path></g><g fill-opacity="1.0" transform="matrix(1.0 0.0 0.0 1.0 20.38 55.39)"><foreignObject style="--ltx-fo-width:24.44em;--ltx-fo-height:0.69em;--ltx-fo-depth:0em;font-size:10pt;" height="9.61" overflow="visible" transform="matrix(1 0 0 -1 0 9.61)" width="338.18"><span class="ltx_foreignobject_container"><span class="ltx_foreignobject_content">
<span id="A2.SS4.SSS1.Px2.p20.pic1.1" class="ltx_inline-block ltx_minipage ltx_align_bottom" style="width:24.44em;">
<span id="A2.SS4.SSS1.Px2.p20.pic1.1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.SS4.SSS1.Px2.p20.pic1.1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold" style="--ltx-fg-color:#FFFFFF;">Rubric</span></span>
</span></span></span></foreignObject></g><g fill-opacity="1.0" transform="matrix(1.0 0.0 0.0 1.0 20.38 14.66)"><foreignObject style="--ltx-fo-width:33.06em;--ltx-fo-height:1.76em;--ltx-fo-depth:0.16em;font-size:10pt;" height="26.44" overflow="visible" transform="matrix(1 0 0 -1 0 24.29)" width="457.46"><span class="ltx_foreignobject_container"><span class="ltx_foreignobject_content">
<span id="A2.SS4.SSS1.Px2.p20.pic1.2" class="ltx_inline-block ltx_minipage ltx_align_bottom" style="width:33.06em;">
<span id="A2.SS4.SSS1.Px2.p20.pic1.2.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.SS4.SSS1.Px2.p20.pic1.2.1.1" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:80%;--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">1.Correctly explains why we should subtract 300 instead of adding 300 — 1 point.</span></span>
</span></span></span></foreignObject></g></g></svg></span>
</div>
<div id="A2.SS4.SSS1.Px2.p21" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent"><span class="ltx_inline-block"><svg id="A2.SS4.SSS1.Px2.p21.pic1" class="ltx_picture" height="54.13" overflow="visible" version="1.1" viewBox="0 0 429.64 54.13" width="429.64"><g style="--ltx-stroke-color:#000000;--ltx-fill-color:#000000;" fill="#000000" stroke="#000000" stroke-width="0.4pt" transform="translate(0,54.13) matrix(1 0 0 -1 0 0)"><g style="--ltx-fill-color:#5A996B;" fill="#5A996B" fill-opacity="1.0"><path style="stroke:none" d="M 0 4.63 L 0 49.51 C 0 52.06 2.07 54.13 4.63 54.13 L 425.01 54.13 C 427.56 54.13 429.64 52.06 429.64 49.51 L 429.64 4.63 C 429.64 2.07 427.56 0 425.01 0 L 4.63 0 C 2.07 0 0 2.07 0 4.63 Z"></path></g><g style="--ltx-fill-color:#F6FFF9;" fill="#F6FFF9" fill-opacity="1.0"><path style="stroke:none" d="M 0.69 4.63 L 0.69 35.38 L 428.94 35.38 L 428.94 4.63 C 428.94 2.45 427.18 0.69 425.01 0.69 L 4.63 0.69 C 2.45 0.69 0.69 2.45 0.69 4.63 Z"></path></g><g fill-opacity="1.0" transform="matrix(1.0 0.0 0.0 1.0 20.38 40.01)"><foreignObject style="--ltx-fo-width:24.44em;--ltx-fo-height:0.69em;--ltx-fo-depth:0em;font-size:10pt;" height="9.49" overflow="visible" transform="matrix(1 0 0 -1 0 9.49)" width="338.18"><span class="ltx_foreignobject_container"><span class="ltx_foreignobject_content">
<span id="A2.SS4.SSS1.Px2.p21.pic1.1" class="ltx_inline-block ltx_minipage ltx_align_bottom" style="width:24.44em;">
<span id="A2.SS4.SSS1.Px2.p21.pic1.1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.SS4.SSS1.Px2.p21.pic1.1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold" style="--ltx-fg-color:#FFFFFF;">Score</span></span>
</span></span></span></foreignObject></g><g fill-opacity="1.0" transform="matrix(1.0 0.0 0.0 1.0 20.38 15.27)"><foreignObject style="--ltx-fo-width:33.06em;--ltx-fo-height:0.6em;--ltx-fo-depth:0.2em;font-size:10pt;" height="11.07" overflow="visible" transform="matrix(1 0 0 -1 0 8.3)" width="457.46"><span class="ltx_foreignobject_container"><span class="ltx_foreignobject_content">
<span id="A2.SS4.SSS1.Px2.p21.pic1.2" class="ltx_inline-block ltx_minipage ltx_align_bottom" style="width:33.06em;">
<span id="A2.SS4.SSS1.Px2.p21.pic1.2.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.SS4.SSS1.Px2.p21.pic1.2.1.1" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:80%;--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">1/1</span></span>
</span></span></span></foreignObject></g></g></svg></span>
</div>
<div id="A2.SS4.SSS1.Px2.p22" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent"><span class="ltx_inline-block"><svg id="A2.SS4.SSS1.Px2.p22.pic1" class="ltx_picture" height="53.02" overflow="visible" version="1.1" viewBox="0 0 429.64 53.02" width="429.64"><g style="--ltx-stroke-color:#000000;--ltx-fill-color:#000000;" fill="#000000" stroke="#000000" stroke-width="0.4pt" transform="translate(0,53.02) matrix(1 0 0 -1 0 0)"><g style="--ltx-fill-color:#B33674;" fill="#B33674" fill-opacity="1.0"><path style="stroke:none" d="M 0 4.63 L 0 48.39 C 0 50.95 2.07 53.02 4.63 53.02 L 425.01 53.02 C 427.56 53.02 429.64 50.95 429.64 48.39 L 429.64 4.63 C 429.64 2.07 427.56 0 425.01 0 L 4.63 0 C 2.07 0 0 2.07 0 4.63 Z"></path></g><g style="--ltx-fill-color:#FFF2F9;" fill="#FFF2F9" fill-opacity="1.0"><path style="stroke:none" d="M 0.69 4.63 L 0.69 34.15 L 428.94 34.15 L 428.94 4.63 C 428.94 2.45 427.18 0.69 425.01 0.69 L 4.63 0.69 C 2.45 0.69 0.69 2.45 0.69 4.63 Z"></path></g><g fill-opacity="1.0" transform="matrix(1.0 0.0 0.0 1.0 20.38 38.78)"><foreignObject style="--ltx-fo-width:24.44em;--ltx-fo-height:0.69em;--ltx-fo-depth:0em;font-size:10pt;" height="9.61" overflow="visible" transform="matrix(1 0 0 -1 0 9.61)" width="338.18"><span class="ltx_foreignobject_container"><span class="ltx_foreignobject_content">
<span id="A2.SS4.SSS1.Px2.p22.pic1.1" class="ltx_inline-block ltx_minipage ltx_align_bottom" style="width:24.44em;">
<span id="A2.SS4.SSS1.Px2.p22.pic1.1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.SS4.SSS1.Px2.p22.pic1.1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold" style="--ltx-fg-color:#FFFFFF;">Evaluation</span></span>
</span></span></span></foreignObject></g><g fill-opacity="1.0" transform="matrix(1.0 0.0 0.0 1.0 20.38 14.66)"><foreignObject style="--ltx-fo-width:33.06em;--ltx-fo-height:0.56em;--ltx-fo-depth:0.16em;font-size:10pt;" height="9.84" overflow="visible" transform="matrix(1 0 0 -1 0 7.69)" width="457.46"><span class="ltx_foreignobject_container"><span class="ltx_foreignobject_content">
<span id="A2.SS4.SSS1.Px2.p22.pic1.2" class="ltx_inline-block ltx_minipage ltx_align_bottom" style="width:33.06em;">
<span id="A2.SS4.SSS1.Px2.p22.pic1.2.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.SS4.SSS1.Px2.p22.pic1.2.1.1" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:80%;--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">The response clearly explains why 300 should be subtracted.</span></span>
</span></span></span></foreignObject></g></g></svg></span>
</div>
</section>
</section>
<section id="A2.SS4.SSS2" class="ltx_subsubsection">
<h4 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsubsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsubsection">(b) </span>Application of Problem-Solving Strategies</h4>

<section id="A2.SS4.SSS2.Px1" class="ltx_paragraph">
<h5 class="ltx_title ltx_title_paragraph" style="--ltx-fg-color:#FF0000;">Problem 4b1 </h5>

<div id="A2.SS4.SSS2.Px1.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A2.SS4.SSS2.Px1.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.SS4.SSS2.Px1.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text"></span>
<br class="ltx_break" style="--ltx-break-space:-10.0pt;"></p>
</div>
<div id="A2.SS4.SSS2.Px1.p2" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent"><span class="ltx_inline-block"><svg id="A2.SS4.SSS2.Px1.p2.pic1" class="ltx_picture" height="233.15" overflow="visible" version="1.1" viewBox="0 0 429.64 233.15" width="429.64"><g style="--ltx-stroke-color:#000000;--ltx-fill-color:#000000;" fill="#000000" stroke="#000000" stroke-width="0.4pt" transform="translate(0,233.15) matrix(1 0 0 -1 0 0)"><g style="--ltx-fill-color:#3D6666;" fill="#3D6666" fill-opacity="1.0"><path style="stroke:none" d="M 0 4.63 L 0 228.52 C 0 231.08 2.07 233.15 4.63 233.15 L 425.01 233.15 C 427.56 233.15 429.64 231.08 429.64 228.52 L 429.64 4.63 C 429.64 2.07 427.56 0 425.01 0 L 4.63 0 C 2.07 0 0 2.07 0 4.63 Z"></path></g><g style="--ltx-fill-color:#F9F9F9;" fill="#F9F9F9" fill-opacity="1.0"><path style="stroke:none" d="M 0.69 4.63 L 0.69 214.28 L 428.94 214.28 L 428.94 4.63 C 428.94 2.45 427.18 0.69 425.01 0.69 L 4.63 0.69 C 2.45 0.69 0.69 2.45 0.69 4.63 Z"></path></g><g fill-opacity="1.0" transform="matrix(1.0 0.0 0.0 1.0 20.38 218.91)"><foreignObject style="--ltx-fo-width:24.44em;--ltx-fo-height:0.69em;--ltx-fo-depth:0em;font-size:10pt;" height="9.61" overflow="visible" transform="matrix(1 0 0 -1 0 9.61)" width="338.18"><span class="ltx_foreignobject_container"><span class="ltx_foreignobject_content">
<span id="A2.SS4.SSS2.Px1.p2.pic1.1" class="ltx_inline-block ltx_minipage ltx_align_bottom" style="width:24.44em;">
<span id="A2.SS4.SSS2.Px1.p2.pic1.1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.SS4.SSS2.Px1.p2.pic1.1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold" style="--ltx-fg-color:#FFFFFF;">Problem</span></span>
</span></span></span></foreignObject></g><g fill-opacity="1.0" transform="matrix(1.0 0.0 0.0 1.0 20.38 14.66)"><foreignObject style="--ltx-fo-width:32.01em;--ltx-fo-height:13.57em;--ltx-fo-depth:0.16em;font-size:10pt;" height="189.97" overflow="visible" transform="matrix(1 0 0 -1 0 187.82)" width="442.93"><span class="ltx_foreignobject_container"><span class="ltx_foreignobject_content">
<span id="A2.SS4.SSS2.Px1.p2.pic1.2" class="ltx_inline-block ltx_minipage ltx_align_bottom" style="width:32.01em;">
<span id="A2.SS4.SSS2.Px1.p2.pic1.2.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.SS4.SSS2.Px1.p2.pic1.2.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold" style="font-size:80%;--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">(Induction)<span id="A2.SS4.SSS2.Px1.p2.pic1.2.1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_medium"> Let <math id="A2.SS4.SSS2.Px1.p2.pic1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="n\geq 3" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">n</mi><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">≥</mo><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">3</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">n\geq 3</annotation></semantics></math> be an odd integer. Color each cell of an <math id="A2.SS4.SSS2.Px1.p2.pic1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="n\times n" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">n</mi><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" lspace="0.222em" mathcolor="#000000" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">n</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">n\times n</annotation></semantics></math> grid either black or white. Two cells of the same color that share a vertex are called <em id="A2.SS4.SSS2.Px1.p2.pic1.2.1.1.1.1" class="ltx_emph ltx_font_italic">adjacent</em>. For any two cells <math id="A2.SS4.SSS2.Px1.p2.pic1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="a,b" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">a</mi><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">,</mo><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">b</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">a,b</annotation></semantics></math>, we say <math id="A2.SS4.SSS2.Px1.p2.pic1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="a" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">a</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">a</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="A2.SS4.SSS2.Px1.p2.pic1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="b" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">b</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">b</annotation></semantics></math> are <em id="A2.SS4.SSS2.Px1.p2.pic1.2.1.1.1.2" class="ltx_emph ltx_font_italic">connected</em> if there exists a sequence of cells</span></span></span>
<span id="A2.Ex107" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<span><span class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<span class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></span>
<span class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A2.Ex107.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="c_{1},\,c_{2},\,\dots,\,c_{k}" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" mathsize="0.800em">c</mi><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" mathsize="0.800em">1</mn></msub><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" mathsize="0.800em" rspace="0.337em">,</mo><msub><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" mathsize="0.800em">c</mi><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" mathsize="0.800em">2</mn></msub><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" mathsize="0.800em" rspace="0.337em">,</mo><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" mathsize="0.800em" mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" mathsize="0.800em" rspace="0.337em">,</mo><msub><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" mathsize="0.800em">c</mi><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" mathsize="0.800em">k</mi></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">c_{1},\,c_{2},\,\dots,\,c_{k}</annotation></semantics></math></span>
<span class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></span></span></span>
</span>
<span id="A2.SS4.SSS2.Px1.p2.pic1.2.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.SS4.SSS2.Px1.p2.pic1.2.2.1" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:80%;--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">with <math id="A2.SS4.SSS2.Px1.p2.pic1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="c_{1}=a" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">c</mi><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">1</mn></msub><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">=</mo><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">a</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">c_{1}=a</annotation></semantics></math>, <math id="A2.SS4.SSS2.Px1.p2.pic1.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="c_{k}=b" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">c</mi><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">k</mi></msub><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">=</mo><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">b</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">c_{k}=b</annotation></semantics></math>, and each <math id="A2.SS4.SSS2.Px1.p2.pic1.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="c_{i}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">c</mi><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">i</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">c_{i}</annotation></semantics></math> is adjacent to <math id="A2.SS4.SSS2.Px1.p2.pic1.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="c_{i+1}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">c</mi><mrow><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">i</mi><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">+</mo><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">1</mn></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">c_{i+1}</annotation></semantics></math> for <math id="A2.SS4.SSS2.Px1.p2.pic1.m10" class="ltx_Math" alttext="i=1,2,\dots,k-1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">i</mi><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">=</mo><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">1</mn></mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">,</mo><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">2</mn><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">,</mo><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">,</mo><mrow><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">k</mi><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">−</mo><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">1</mn></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">i=1,2,\dots,k-1</annotation></semantics></math>. Determine the largest positive integer <math id="A2.SS4.SSS2.Px1.p2.pic1.m11" class="ltx_Math" alttext="M" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">M</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">M</annotation></semantics></math> for which there is a coloring having <math id="A2.SS4.SSS2.Px1.p2.pic1.m12" class="ltx_Math" alttext="M" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">M</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">M</annotation></semantics></math> cells that are pairwise non<span id="A2.SS4.SSS2.Px1.p2.pic1.2.2.1.1" class="ltx_text">-</span>connected.</span></span><span class="ltx_inline-block"><svg id="A2.SS4.SSS2.Px1.p2.pic1.pic1" class="ltx_picture" color="#FF0000" height="18.24" overflow="visible" style="vertical-align:-4.1px" version="1.1" viewBox="0 0 18.24 18.24" width="18.24"><g style="--ltx-stroke-color:#FF0000;--ltx-fill-color:#FF0000;" fill="#FF0000" stroke="#FF0000" stroke-width="1.8pt" transform="translate(0,18.24) matrix(1 0 0 -1 0 0) translate(1.25,0) translate(0,1.25)"><path style="fill:none" d="M 0 0 L 15.75 15.75 M 0 15.75 L 15.75 0"></path></g></svg></span>
<span id="A2.SS4.SSS2.Px1.p2.pic1.2.3" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.SS4.SSS2.Px1.p2.pic1.2.3.1" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:80%;--ltx-fg-color:#FF0000;">GPT-5 thinking failed</span></span>
<span id="A2.SS4.SSS2.Px1.p2.pic1.2.4" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.SS4.SSS2.Px1.p2.pic1.2.4.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic" style="font-size:80%;--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">Proposed by Jiaxin Zhang</span></span>
</span></span></span></foreignObject></g></g></svg></span>
</div>
<div id="A2.SS4.SSS2.Px1.1" class="ltx_proof">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_font_italic ltx_title_proof"><span id="A2.SS4.SSS2.Px1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Response of GPT-5-thinking</span>.</h6>
<div id="A2.SS4.SSS2.Px1.p3" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A2.SS4.SSS2.Px1.p3.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.SS4.SSS2.Px1.p3.1.1" class="ltx_text">Here “adjacent” means same color and sharing a corner (so 8-neighborhood), hence any monochromatic path stays in one color. We seek the largest size of a family of cells, no two of which lie in the same monochromatic connected component. Equivalently, we want to maximize the total number of monochromatic components and then take one cell from each.</span></p>
</div>
<div id="A2.SS4.SSS2.Px1.p4" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A2.SS4.SSS2.Px1.p4.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.SS4.SSS2.Px1.p4.1.1" class="ltx_text">Let</span></p>
</div>
<div id="A2.SS4.SSS2.Px1.p5" class="ltx_para">
<table id="A2.Ex108" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A2.Ex108.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="T=\{(i,j):1\leq i,j\leq n,\ \ i,j\text{ odd}\},\qquad|T|=\Bigl(\frac{n+1}{2}\Bigr)^{2}," display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>T</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>i</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>j</mi><mo rspace="0.278em" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>≤</mo><mi>i</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>j</mi><mo>≤</mo><mi>n</mi><mo rspace="1.167em">,</mo><mi>i</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>j</mi><mtext> odd</mtext><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow><mo rspace="2.167em">,</mo><mo fence="false" rspace="0.167em" stretchy="false">|</mo><mi>T</mi><mo fence="false" stretchy="false">|</mo><mo lspace="0.167em">=</mo><msup><mrow><mo maxsize="1.600em" minsize="1.600em">(</mo><mfrac><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mn>2</mn></mfrac><mo maxsize="1.600em" minsize="1.600em">)</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">T=\{(i,j):1\leq i,j\leq n,\ \ i,j\text{ odd}\},\qquad|T|=\Bigl(\frac{n+1}{2}\Bigr)^{2},</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
<div id="A2.SS4.SSS2.Px1.p6" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A2.SS4.SSS2.Px1.p6.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.SS4.SSS2.Px1.p6.1.1" class="ltx_text">and let <math id="A2.SS4.SSS2.Px1.p6.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="U" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>U</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">U</annotation></semantics></math> be the complement (cells with at least one even coordinate).</span></p>
</div>
<div id="A2.SS4.SSS2.Px1.p7" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A2.SS4.SSS2.Px1.p7.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.SS4.SSS2.Px1.p7.1.1" class="ltx_text">Lower bound (construction)</span></p>
</div>
<div id="A2.SS4.SSS2.Px1.p8" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A2.SS4.SSS2.Px1.p8.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.SS4.SSS2.Px1.p8.1.1" class="ltx_text">Color every cell of <math id="A2.SS4.SSS2.Px1.p8.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="T" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>T</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">T</annotation></semantics></math> black and every cell of <math id="A2.SS4.SSS2.Px1.p8.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="U" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>U</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">U</annotation></semantics></math> white.
Then:</span></p>
</div>
<div id="A2.SS4.SSS2.Px1.p9" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A2.SS4.SSS2.Px1.p9.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.SS4.SSS2.Px1.p9.1.1" class="ltx_text">* No two black cells share a vertex (they are spaced by 2 in both directions), so **each black cell is an isolated black component**.
* The set <math id="A2.SS4.SSS2.Px1.p9.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="U" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>U</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">U</annotation></semantics></math> contains all even rows (and all even columns), so all white cells are **mutually connected** (one white component).</span></p>
</div>
<div id="A2.SS4.SSS2.Px1.p10" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A2.SS4.SSS2.Px1.p10.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.SS4.SSS2.Px1.p10.1.1" class="ltx_text">Thus the total number of monochromatic components is</span></p>
</div>
<div id="A2.SS4.SSS2.Px1.p11" class="ltx_para">
<table id="A2.Ex109" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A2.Ex109.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="|T|+1=\Bigl(\frac{n+1}{2}\Bigr)^{2}+1," display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mi>T</mi><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><msup><mrow><mo maxsize="1.600em" minsize="1.600em">(</mo><mfrac><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mn>2</mn></mfrac><mo maxsize="1.600em" minsize="1.600em">)</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">|T|+1=\Bigl(\frac{n+1}{2}\Bigr)^{2}+1,</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
<div id="A2.SS4.SSS2.Px1.p12" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A2.SS4.SSS2.Px1.p12.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.SS4.SSS2.Px1.p12.1.1" class="ltx_text">and we can choose one cell from each component to get a pairwise non-connected set of this size. Hence</span></p>
</div>
<div id="A2.SS4.SSS2.Px1.p13" class="ltx_para">
<table id="A2.Ex110" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A2.Ex110.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="M\ \geq\ \Bigl(\frac{n+1}{2}\Bigr)^{2}+1." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>M</mi><mo lspace="0.778em" rspace="0.778em">≥</mo><mrow><msup><mrow><mo maxsize="1.600em" minsize="1.600em">(</mo><mfrac><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mn>2</mn></mfrac><mo maxsize="1.600em" minsize="1.600em">)</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">M\ \geq\ \Bigl(\frac{n+1}{2}\Bigr)^{2}+1.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
<div id="A2.SS4.SSS2.Px1.p14" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A2.SS4.SSS2.Px1.p14.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.SS4.SSS2.Px1.p14.1.1" class="ltx_text">Upper bound</span></p>
</div>
<div id="A2.SS4.SSS2.Px1.p15" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A2.SS4.SSS2.Px1.p15.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.SS4.SSS2.Px1.p15.1.1" class="ltx_text">In any coloring, every monochromatic component is of one of two types:</span></p>
</div>
<div id="A2.SS4.SSS2.Px1.p16" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A2.SS4.SSS2.Px1.p16.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.SS4.SSS2.Px1.p16.1.1" class="ltx_text">* a **singleton** lying at some <math id="A2.SS4.SSS2.Px1.p16.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="t\in T" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>∈</mo><mi>T</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">t\in T</annotation></semantics></math> (this happens exactly when all 8 neighbors of <math id="A2.SS4.SSS2.Px1.p16.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="t" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>t</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">t</annotation></semantics></math> in <math id="A2.SS4.SSS2.Px1.p16.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="U" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>U</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">U</annotation></semantics></math> are the opposite color);
* a component that **meets <math id="A2.SS4.SSS2.Px1.p16.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="U" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>U</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">U</annotation></semantics></math>** (possibly also containing some vertices of <math id="A2.SS4.SSS2.Px1.p16.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="T" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>T</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">T</annotation></semantics></math>).</span></p>
</div>
<div id="A2.SS4.SSS2.Px1.p17" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A2.SS4.SSS2.Px1.p17.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.SS4.SSS2.Px1.p17.1.1" class="ltx_text">Since <math id="A2.SS4.SSS2.Px1.p17.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="T" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>T</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">T</annotation></semantics></math> has <math id="A2.SS4.SSS2.Px1.p17.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="|T|" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mi>T</mi><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">|T|</annotation></semantics></math> cells, there are at most <math id="A2.SS4.SSS2.Px1.p17.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="|T|" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mi>T</mi><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">|T|</annotation></semantics></math> singleton components.</span></p>
</div>
<div id="A2.SS4.SSS2.Px1.p18" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A2.SS4.SSS2.Px1.p18.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.SS4.SSS2.Px1.p18.1.1" class="ltx_text">All remaining components meet <math id="A2.SS4.SSS2.Px1.p18.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="U" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>U</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">U</annotation></semantics></math>. But for the purpose of maximizing the number of components (and thus the size of a pairwise non-connected selection), it is never beneficial to keep <math id="A2.SS4.SSS2.Px1.p18.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="U" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>U</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">U</annotation></semantics></math> split into several monochromatic components: from <math id="A2.SS4.SSS2.Px1.p18.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="U" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>U</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">U</annotation></semantics></math> we can choose **at most one** cell anyway (two cells of the same color in <math id="A2.SS4.SSS2.Px1.p18.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="U" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>U</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">U</annotation></semantics></math> would be connected within <math id="A2.SS4.SSS2.Px1.p18.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="U" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>U</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">U</annotation></semantics></math>; two of different colors are allowed, but we could already take one of them and keep all singletons from <math id="A2.SS4.SSS2.Px1.p18.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="T" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>T</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">T</annotation></semantics></math>). Merging the parts of <math id="A2.SS4.SSS2.Px1.p18.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="U" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>U</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">U</annotation></semantics></math> (by recoloring inside <math id="A2.SS4.SSS2.Px1.p18.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="U" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>U</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">U</annotation></semantics></math> if necessary) cannot decrease the maximum attainable size of a pairwise non-connected family, while it leaves the count of singletons in <math id="A2.SS4.SSS2.Px1.p18.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="T" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>T</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">T</annotation></semantics></math> unchanged. Therefore, in the maximizing situation there is **at most one** component meeting <math id="A2.SS4.SSS2.Px1.p18.m10" class="ltx_Math" alttext="U" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>U</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">U</annotation></semantics></math>.</span></p>
</div>
<div id="A2.SS4.SSS2.Px1.p19" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A2.SS4.SSS2.Px1.p19.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.SS4.SSS2.Px1.p19.1.1" class="ltx_text">Consequently, for any coloring the total number of monochromatic components is at most</span></p>
</div>
<div id="A2.SS4.SSS2.Px1.p20" class="ltx_para">
<table id="A2.Ex111" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A2.Ex111.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="|T|+1=\Bigl(\frac{n+1}{2}\Bigr)^{2}+1," display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mi>T</mi><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><msup><mrow><mo maxsize="1.600em" minsize="1.600em">(</mo><mfrac><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mn>2</mn></mfrac><mo maxsize="1.600em" minsize="1.600em">)</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">|T|+1=\Bigl(\frac{n+1}{2}\Bigr)^{2}+1,</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
<div id="A2.SS4.SSS2.Px1.p21" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A2.SS4.SSS2.Px1.p21.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.SS4.SSS2.Px1.p21.1.1" class="ltx_text">and hence</span></p>
</div>
<div id="A2.SS4.SSS2.Px1.p22" class="ltx_para">
<table id="A2.Ex112" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A2.Ex112.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="M\ \leq\ \Bigl(\frac{n+1}{2}\Bigr)^{2}+1." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>M</mi><mo lspace="0.778em" rspace="0.778em">≤</mo><mrow><msup><mrow><mo maxsize="1.600em" minsize="1.600em">(</mo><mfrac><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mn>2</mn></mfrac><mo maxsize="1.600em" minsize="1.600em">)</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">M\ \leq\ \Bigl(\frac{n+1}{2}\Bigr)^{2}+1.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
<div id="A2.SS4.SSS2.Px1.p23" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A2.SS4.SSS2.Px1.p23.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.SS4.SSS2.Px1.p23.1.1" class="ltx_text">Combining the two bounds,</span></p>
</div>
<div id="A2.SS4.SSS2.Px1.p24" class="ltx_para">
<table id="A2.Ex113" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A2.Ex113.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\boxed{\displaystyle M=\Bigl(\frac{n+1}{2}\Bigr)^{2}+1.}" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><menclose notation="box"><mrow><mrow><mi>M</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><msup><mrow><mo maxsize="1.600em" minsize="1.600em">(</mo><mfrac><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mn>2</mn></mfrac><mo maxsize="1.600em" minsize="1.600em">)</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow></menclose><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\boxed{\displaystyle M=\Bigl(\frac{n+1}{2}\Bigr)^{2}+1.}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
<div id="A2.SS4.SSS2.Px1.p25" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A2.SS4.SSS2.Px1.p25.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.SS4.SSS2.Px1.p25.1.1" class="ltx_text">∎</span></p>
</div>
</div>
<div id="A2.SS4.SSS2.Px1.2" class="ltx_proof">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_font_italic ltx_title_proof"><span id="A2.SS4.SSS2.Px1.2.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Standard Solution</span>.</h6>
<div id="A2.SS4.SSS2.Px1.p26" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A2.SS4.SSS2.Px1.p26.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.SS4.SSS2.Px1.p26.1.1" class="ltx_text">Consider the following generalization. Let <math id="A2.SS4.SSS2.Px1.p26.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="m,n\geq 3" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>m</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>n</mi></mrow><mo>≥</mo><mn>3</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">m,n\geq 3</annotation></semantics></math> be odd integers, and color each cell of an <math id="A2.SS4.SSS2.Px1.p26.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="m\times n" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>m</mi><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><mi>n</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">m\times n</annotation></semantics></math> grid black or white. Under a given coloring, the cells decompose into connected components (“clusters”) in which any two cells in the same cluster are connected by a sequence of same<span id="A2.SS4.SSS2.Px1.p26.1.1.1" class="ltx_text">-</span>colored cells sharing a vertex, and cells from different clusters are not connected. Denote the number of clusters by <math id="A2.SS4.SSS2.Px1.p26.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="K" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>K</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">K</annotation></semantics></math>.</span></p>
</div>
<div id="A2.SS4.SSS2.Px1.p27" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A2.SS4.SSS2.Px1.p27.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.SS4.SSS2.Px1.p27.1.1" class="ltx_text">We prove by induction on <math id="A2.SS4.SSS2.Px1.p27.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="m" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>m</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">m</annotation></semantics></math> that:</span></p>
<ol id="A2.I8" class="ltx_enumerate">
<li id="A2.I8.i1" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">1.</span> 
<div id="A2.I8.i1.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A2.I8.i1.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><math id="A2.I8.i1.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="K\leq\frac{1}{4}\,(m+1)(n+1)+1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>K</mi><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mrow><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mn>4</mn></mfrac><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>m</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">K\leq\frac{1}{4}\,(m+1)(n+1)+1</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>
</div></li>
<li id="A2.I8.i2" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">2.</span> 
<div id="A2.I8.i2.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A2.I8.i2.p1.1" class="ltx_p">If equality holds, i.e. <math id="A2.I8.i2.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="K=\frac{1}{4}\,(m+1)(n+1)+1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>K</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mn>4</mn></mfrac><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>m</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">K=\frac{1}{4}\,(m+1)(n+1)+1</annotation></semantics></math>, then each of the four corner cells is isolated (not connected to any other cell).</p>
</div></li>
</ol>
</div>
<div id="A2.SS4.SSS2.Px1.p28" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A2.SS4.SSS2.Px1.p28.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.SS4.SSS2.Px1.p28.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">Base case.</span><span id="A2.SS4.SSS2.Px1.p28.1.2" class="ltx_text"> When <math id="A2.SS4.SSS2.Px1.p28.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="m=n=3" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>m</mi><mo>=</mo><mi>n</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>3</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">m=n=3</annotation></semantics></math>, the outer ring of 8 cells can belong to at most 4 clusters of the opposite color from the center, so <math id="A2.SS4.SSS2.Px1.p28.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="K\leq 5" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>K</mi><mo>≤</mo><mn>5</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">K\leq 5</annotation></semantics></math>. Equality holds precisely when all four corner cells share the opposite color from the center cell, and hence are isolated.</span></p>
</div>
<div id="A2.SS4.SSS2.Px1.p29" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A2.SS4.SSS2.Px1.p29.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.SS4.SSS2.Px1.p29.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">Inductive step.</span><span id="A2.SS4.SSS2.Px1.p29.1.2" class="ltx_text"> Assume the claims hold for <math id="A2.SS4.SSS2.Px1.p29.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(m-2)\times n" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>m</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow><mo rspace="0.055em" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo rspace="0.222em">×</mo><mi>n</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(m-2)\times n</annotation></semantics></math>. Now consider an <math id="A2.SS4.SSS2.Px1.p29.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="m\times n" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>m</mi><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><mi>n</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">m\times n</annotation></semantics></math> grid with its second row split into <math id="A2.SS4.SSS2.Px1.p29.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="k" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>k</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">k</annotation></semantics></math> maximal alternating-color segments</span></p>
<table id="A2.Ex114" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A2.Ex114.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="A_{1},A_{2},\dots,A_{k}," display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>A</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>A</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>A</mi><mi>k</mi></msub></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">A_{1},A_{2},\dots,A_{k},</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A2.SS4.SSS2.Px1.p29.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.SS4.SSS2.Px1.p29.2.1" class="ltx_text">of lengths <math id="A2.SS4.SSS2.Px1.p29.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="x_{1},\dots,x_{k}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>x</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>k</mi></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">x_{1},\dots,x_{k}</annotation></semantics></math>. Let</span></p>
<table id="A2.Ex115" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A2.Ex115.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="P=\#\{\text{clusters containing a cell in row\lx@nobreakspace 1 but none in row\lx@nobreakspace 2}\}," display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>P</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>#</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mtext>clusters containing a cell in row 1 but none in row 2</mtext><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">P=\#\{\text{clusters containing a cell in row\lx@nobreakspace 1 but none in row\lx@nobreakspace 2}\},</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<table id="A2.Ex116" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A2.Ex116.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="Q=\#\{\text{clusters containing a cell in row\lx@nobreakspace 2 but none in row\lx@nobreakspace 3}\}," display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>Q</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>#</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mtext>clusters containing a cell in row 2 but none in row 3</mtext><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">Q=\#\{\text{clusters containing a cell in row\lx@nobreakspace 2 but none in row\lx@nobreakspace 3}\},</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<table id="A2.Ex117" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A2.Ex117.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="R=\#\{\text{clusters containing cells only in rows\lx@nobreakspace 3 through\lx@nobreakspace$m$}\}." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>R</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>#</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mrow><mtext>clusters containing cells only in rows 3 through </mtext><mi>m</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">R=\#\{\text{clusters containing cells only in rows\lx@nobreakspace 3 through\lx@nobreakspace$m$}\}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
<div id="A2.SS4.SSS2.Px1.p30" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A2.SS4.SSS2.Px1.p30.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.SS4.SSS2.Px1.p30.1.1" class="ltx_text">One shows</span></p>
<table id="A2.Ex118" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A2.Ex118.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="P\;\leq\;\Bigl\lceil\frac{x_{1}-1}{2}\Bigr\rceil+\Bigl\lceil\frac{x_{k}-1}{2}\Bigr\rceil+\sum_{i=2}^{k-1}\Bigl\lceil\frac{x_{i}-2}{2}\Bigr\rceil\;\leq\;\frac{n-k+2}{2}," display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>P</mi><mo lspace="0.558em" rspace="0.558em">≤</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">⌈</mo><mfrac><mrow><msub><mi>x</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mn>2</mn></mfrac><mo stretchy="false">⌉</mo></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">⌈</mo><mfrac><mrow><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mn>2</mn></mfrac><mo stretchy="false">⌉</mo></mrow><mo rspace="0.055em">+</mo><mrow><munderover><mo movablelimits="false" rspace="0em">∑</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></munderover><mrow><mo stretchy="false">⌈</mo><mfrac><mrow><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>−</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow><mn>2</mn></mfrac><mo rspace="0.280em" stretchy="false">⌉</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.558em">≤</mo><mfrac><mrow><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>−</mo><mi>k</mi></mrow><mo>+</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow><mn>2</mn></mfrac></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">P\;\leq\;\Bigl\lceil\frac{x_{1}-1}{2}\Bigr\rceil+\Bigl\lceil\frac{x_{k}-1}{2}\Bigr\rceil+\sum_{i=2}^{k-1}\Bigl\lceil\frac{x_{i}-2}{2}\Bigr\rceil\;\leq\;\frac{n-k+2}{2},</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A2.SS4.SSS2.Px1.p30.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.SS4.SSS2.Px1.p30.2.1" class="ltx_text">and</span></p>
<table id="A2.Ex119" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A2.Ex119.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="Q\;\leq\;\Bigl\lceil\frac{k}{2}\Bigr\rceil\;\leq\;\frac{k+1}{2}." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>Q</mi><mo lspace="0.558em" rspace="0.558em">≤</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">⌈</mo><mfrac><mi>k</mi><mn>2</mn></mfrac><mo rspace="0.280em" stretchy="false">⌉</mo></mrow><mo rspace="0.558em">≤</mo><mfrac><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mn>2</mn></mfrac></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">Q\;\leq\;\Bigl\lceil\frac{k}{2}\Bigr\rceil\;\leq\;\frac{k+1}{2}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A2.SS4.SSS2.Px1.p30.3" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.SS4.SSS2.Px1.p30.3.1" class="ltx_text">By the inductive hypothesis on the bottom <math id="A2.SS4.SSS2.Px1.p30.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(m-2)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>m</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(m-2)</annotation></semantics></math> rows,</span></p>
<table id="A2.Ex120" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A2.Ex120.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="R\;\leq\;\frac{1}{4}\,(m-1)(n+1)+1." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>R</mi><mo lspace="0.558em" rspace="0.558em">≤</mo><mrow><mrow><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mn>4</mn></mfrac><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>m</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">R\;\leq\;\frac{1}{4}\,(m-1)(n+1)+1.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A2.SS4.SSS2.Px1.p30.4" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.SS4.SSS2.Px1.p30.4.1" class="ltx_text">A careful case analysis shows that whenever
<math id="A2.SS4.SSS2.Px1.p30.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\;Q=\tfrac{k+1}{2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>Q</mi><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mn>2</mn></mfrac></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\;Q=\tfrac{k+1}{2}</annotation></semantics></math> (for odd <math id="A2.SS4.SSS2.Px1.p30.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="k" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>k</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">k</annotation></semantics></math>) or <math id="A2.SS4.SSS2.Px1.p30.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="Q=\tfrac{k}{2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>Q</mi><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mi>k</mi><mn>2</mn></mfrac></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">Q=\tfrac{k}{2}</annotation></semantics></math> (for even <math id="A2.SS4.SSS2.Px1.p30.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="k" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>k</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">k</annotation></semantics></math>), one actually has</span></p>
<table id="A2.Ex121" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A2.Ex121.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="R\;\leq\;\frac{1}{4}\,(m-1)(n+1)." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>R</mi><mo lspace="0.558em" rspace="0.558em">≤</mo><mrow><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mn>4</mn></mfrac><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>m</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">R\;\leq\;\frac{1}{4}\,(m-1)(n+1).</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A2.SS4.SSS2.Px1.p30.5" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.SS4.SSS2.Px1.p30.5.1" class="ltx_text">Hence</span></p>
<table id="A2.Ex122" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A2.Ex122.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="K=P+Q+R\;\leq\;\frac{n-k+2}{2}+\frac{k+1}{2}+\frac{1}{4}\,(m-1)(n+1)=\frac{1}{4}\,(m+1)(n+1)+1," display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>K</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>P</mi><mo>+</mo><mi>Q</mi><mo>+</mo><mi>R</mi></mrow><mo lspace="0.558em" rspace="0.558em">≤</mo><mrow><mfrac><mrow><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>−</mo><mi>k</mi></mrow><mo>+</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow><mn>2</mn></mfrac><mo>+</mo><mfrac><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mn>2</mn></mfrac><mo>+</mo><mrow><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mn>4</mn></mfrac><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>m</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mn>4</mn></mfrac><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>m</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">K=P+Q+R\;\leq\;\frac{n-k+2}{2}+\frac{k+1}{2}+\frac{1}{4}\,(m-1)(n+1)=\frac{1}{4}\,(m+1)(n+1)+1,</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A2.SS4.SSS2.Px1.p30.6" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.SS4.SSS2.Px1.p30.6.1" class="ltx_text">establishing (1).</span></p>
</div>
<div id="A2.SS4.SSS2.Px1.p31" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A2.SS4.SSS2.Px1.p31.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.SS4.SSS2.Px1.p31.1.1" class="ltx_text">Moreover, equality forces <math id="A2.SS4.SSS2.Px1.p31.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="k" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>k</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">k</annotation></semantics></math> odd and</span></p>
<table id="A2.Ex123" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A2.Ex123.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="P=\frac{n-k+2}{2}," display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>P</mi><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mrow><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>−</mo><mi>k</mi></mrow><mo>+</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow><mn>2</mn></mfrac></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">P=\frac{n-k+2}{2},</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A2.SS4.SSS2.Px1.p31.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.SS4.SSS2.Px1.p31.2.1" class="ltx_text">which implies that in row 1 both the first and last cells of each segment
are surrounded by three opposite-colored neighbours, so the four corners
must each lie in their own isolated cluster, proving (2).</span></p>
</div>
<div id="A2.SS4.SSS2.Px1.p32" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A2.SS4.SSS2.Px1.p32.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.SS4.SSS2.Px1.p32.1.1" class="ltx_text">Finally, in the special “checkerboard” colorings</span></p>
<table id="A2.Ex124" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A2.Ex124.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\begin{cases}\text{cell at }(i,j)\text{ is black if }ij\text{ is even},\\
\text{cell at }(i,j)\text{ is white if }ij\text{ is odd},\end{cases}" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo>{</mo><mtable columnspacing="5pt" displaystyle="true" rowspacing="0pt"><mtr><mtd class="ltx_align_left" columnalign="left"><mrow><mrow><mtext>cell at </mtext><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>i</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>j</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mtext> is black if </mtext><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>j</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mtext> is even</mtext></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow></mtd><mtd></mtd></mtr><mtr><mtd class="ltx_align_left" columnalign="left"><mrow><mrow><mtext>cell at </mtext><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>i</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>j</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mtext> is white if </mtext><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>j</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mtext> is odd</mtext></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow></mtd><mtd></mtd></mtr></mtable></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\begin{cases}\text{cell at }(i,j)\text{ is black if }ij\text{ is even},\\
\text{cell at }(i,j)\text{ is white if }ij\text{ is odd},\end{cases}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A2.SS4.SSS2.Px1.p32.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.SS4.SSS2.Px1.p32.2.1" class="ltx_text">one checks directly that</span></p>
<table id="A2.Ex125" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A2.Ex125.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="K\;=\;\frac{1}{4}\,(m+1)(n+1)+1." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>K</mi><mo lspace="0.558em" rspace="0.558em">=</mo><mrow><mrow><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mn>4</mn></mfrac><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>m</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">K\;=\;\frac{1}{4}\,(m+1)(n+1)+1.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A2.SS4.SSS2.Px1.p32.3" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.SS4.SSS2.Px1.p32.3.1" class="ltx_text">Therefore, the maximum number of pairwise non<span id="A2.SS4.SSS2.Px1.p32.3.1.1" class="ltx_text">-</span>connected cells is</span></p>
<table id="A2.Ex126" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A2.Ex126.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\boxed{M\;=\;\frac{1}{4}\,(n+1)^{2}+1}\quad(\text{when }m=n)." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><menclose notation="box"><mrow><mi>M</mi><mo lspace="0.558em" rspace="0.558em">=</mo><mrow><mrow><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mn>4</mn></mfrac><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mrow></menclose><mspace style="width:1em;" width="1em"></mspace><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mrow><mtext>when </mtext><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>m</mi></mrow><mo>=</mo><mi>n</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\boxed{M\;=\;\frac{1}{4}\,(n+1)^{2}+1}\quad(\text{when }m=n).</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A2.SS4.SSS2.Px1.p32.4" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.SS4.SSS2.Px1.p32.4.1" class="ltx_text">∎</span></p>
</div>
</div>
<div id="A2.SS4.SSS2.Px1.p33" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent"><span class="ltx_inline-block"><svg id="A2.SS4.SSS2.Px1.p33.pic1" class="ltx_picture" height="70.84" overflow="visible" version="1.1" viewBox="0 0 429.64 70.84" width="429.64"><g style="--ltx-stroke-color:#000000;--ltx-fill-color:#000000;" fill="#000000" stroke="#000000" stroke-width="0.4pt" transform="translate(0,70.84) matrix(1 0 0 -1 0 0)"><g style="--ltx-fill-color:#4D4D4D;" fill="#4D4D4D" fill-opacity="1.0"><path style="stroke:none" d="M 0 4.63 L 0 66.21 C 0 68.77 2.07 70.84 4.63 70.84 L 425.01 70.84 C 427.56 70.84 429.64 68.77 429.64 66.21 L 429.64 4.63 C 429.64 2.07 427.56 0 425.01 0 L 4.63 0 C 2.07 0 0 2.07 0 4.63 Z"></path></g><g style="--ltx-fill-color:#F9F9F9;" fill="#F9F9F9" fill-opacity="1.0"><path style="stroke:none" d="M 0.69 4.63 L 0.69 51.97 L 428.94 51.97 L 428.94 4.63 C 428.94 2.45 427.18 0.69 425.01 0.69 L 4.63 0.69 C 2.45 0.69 0.69 2.45 0.69 4.63 Z"></path></g><g fill-opacity="1.0" transform="matrix(1.0 0.0 0.0 1.0 20.38 56.6)"><foreignObject style="--ltx-fo-width:24.44em;--ltx-fo-height:0.69em;--ltx-fo-depth:0em;font-size:10pt;" height="9.61" overflow="visible" transform="matrix(1 0 0 -1 0 9.61)" width="338.18"><span class="ltx_foreignobject_container"><span class="ltx_foreignobject_content">
<span id="A2.SS4.SSS2.Px1.p33.pic1.1" class="ltx_inline-block ltx_minipage ltx_align_bottom" style="width:24.44em;">
<span id="A2.SS4.SSS2.Px1.p33.pic1.1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.SS4.SSS2.Px1.p33.pic1.1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold" style="--ltx-fg-color:#FFFFFF;">Rubric</span></span>
</span></span></span></foreignObject></g><g fill-opacity="1.0" transform="matrix(1.0 0.0 0.0 1.0 20.38 14.66)"><foreignObject style="--ltx-fo-width:33.06em;--ltx-fo-height:1.84em;--ltx-fo-depth:0.16em;font-size:10pt;" height="27.66" overflow="visible" transform="matrix(1 0 0 -1 0 25.5)" width="457.46"><span class="ltx_foreignobject_container"><span class="ltx_foreignobject_content">
<span id="A2.SS4.SSS2.Px1.p33.pic1.2" class="ltx_inline-block ltx_minipage ltx_align_bottom" style="width:33.06em;">
<span id="A2.SS4.SSS2.Px1.p33.pic1.2.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.SS4.SSS2.Px1.p33.pic1.2.1.1" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:80%;--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">1. Prove by induction that <math id="A2.SS4.SSS2.Px1.p33.pic1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="M=\frac{1}{4}(n+1)^{2}+1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">M</mi><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">=</mo><mrow><mrow><mfrac style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000"><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">1</mn><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">4</mn></mfrac><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">n</mi><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">+</mo><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">1</mn></mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">2</mn></msup></mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">+</mo><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">1</mn></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">M=\frac{1}{4}(n+1)^{2}+1</annotation></semantics></math></span></span>
<span id="A2.SS4.SSS2.Px1.p33.pic1.2.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.SS4.SSS2.Px1.p33.pic1.2.2.1" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:80%;--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">2. Construct a concrete example for the upper bound.</span></span>
</span></span></span></foreignObject></g></g></svg></span>
</div>
<div id="A2.SS4.SSS2.Px1.p34" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent"><span class="ltx_inline-block"><svg id="A2.SS4.SSS2.Px1.p34.pic1" class="ltx_picture" height="54.13" overflow="visible" version="1.1" viewBox="0 0 429.64 54.13" width="429.64"><g style="--ltx-stroke-color:#000000;--ltx-fill-color:#000000;" fill="#000000" stroke="#000000" stroke-width="0.4pt" transform="translate(0,54.13) matrix(1 0 0 -1 0 0)"><g style="--ltx-fill-color:#5A996B;" fill="#5A996B" fill-opacity="1.0"><path style="stroke:none" d="M 0 4.63 L 0 49.51 C 0 52.06 2.07 54.13 4.63 54.13 L 425.01 54.13 C 427.56 54.13 429.64 52.06 429.64 49.51 L 429.64 4.63 C 429.64 2.07 427.56 0 425.01 0 L 4.63 0 C 2.07 0 0 2.07 0 4.63 Z"></path></g><g style="--ltx-fill-color:#F6FFF9;" fill="#F6FFF9" fill-opacity="1.0"><path style="stroke:none" d="M 0.69 4.63 L 0.69 35.38 L 428.94 35.38 L 428.94 4.63 C 428.94 2.45 427.18 0.69 425.01 0.69 L 4.63 0.69 C 2.45 0.69 0.69 2.45 0.69 4.63 Z"></path></g><g fill-opacity="1.0" transform="matrix(1.0 0.0 0.0 1.0 20.38 40.01)"><foreignObject style="--ltx-fo-width:24.44em;--ltx-fo-height:0.69em;--ltx-fo-depth:0em;font-size:10pt;" height="9.49" overflow="visible" transform="matrix(1 0 0 -1 0 9.49)" width="338.18"><span class="ltx_foreignobject_container"><span class="ltx_foreignobject_content">
<span id="A2.SS4.SSS2.Px1.p34.pic1.1" class="ltx_inline-block ltx_minipage ltx_align_bottom" style="width:24.44em;">
<span id="A2.SS4.SSS2.Px1.p34.pic1.1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.SS4.SSS2.Px1.p34.pic1.1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold" style="--ltx-fg-color:#FFFFFF;">Score</span></span>
</span></span></span></foreignObject></g><g fill-opacity="1.0" transform="matrix(1.0 0.0 0.0 1.0 20.38 15.27)"><foreignObject style="--ltx-fo-width:33.06em;--ltx-fo-height:0.6em;--ltx-fo-depth:0.2em;font-size:10pt;" height="11.07" overflow="visible" transform="matrix(1 0 0 -1 0 8.3)" width="457.46"><span class="ltx_foreignobject_container"><span class="ltx_foreignobject_content">
<span id="A2.SS4.SSS2.Px1.p34.pic1.2" class="ltx_inline-block ltx_minipage ltx_align_bottom" style="width:33.06em;">
<span id="A2.SS4.SSS2.Px1.p34.pic1.2.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.SS4.SSS2.Px1.p34.pic1.2.1.1" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:80%;--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">1/2</span></span>
</span></span></span></foreignObject></g></g></svg></span>
</div>
<div id="A2.SS4.SSS2.Px1.p35" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent"><span class="ltx_inline-block"><svg id="A2.SS4.SSS2.Px1.p35.pic1" class="ltx_picture" height="156.18" overflow="visible" version="1.1" viewBox="0 0 429.64 156.18" width="429.64"><g style="--ltx-stroke-color:#000000;--ltx-fill-color:#000000;" fill="#000000" stroke="#000000" stroke-width="0.4pt" transform="translate(0,156.18) matrix(1 0 0 -1 0 0)"><g style="--ltx-fill-color:#B33674;" fill="#B33674" fill-opacity="1.0"><path style="stroke:none" d="M 0 4.63 L 0 151.55 C 0 154.11 2.07 156.18 4.63 156.18 L 425.01 156.18 C 427.56 156.18 429.64 154.11 429.64 151.55 L 429.64 4.63 C 429.64 2.07 427.56 0 425.01 0 L 4.63 0 C 2.07 0 0 2.07 0 4.63 Z"></path></g><g style="--ltx-fill-color:#FFF2F9;" fill="#FFF2F9" fill-opacity="1.0"><path style="stroke:none" d="M 0.69 4.63 L 0.69 137.32 L 428.94 137.32 L 428.94 4.63 C 428.94 2.45 427.18 0.69 425.01 0.69 L 4.63 0.69 C 2.45 0.69 0.69 2.45 0.69 4.63 Z"></path></g><g fill-opacity="1.0" transform="matrix(1.0 0.0 0.0 1.0 20.38 141.94)"><foreignObject style="--ltx-fo-width:24.44em;--ltx-fo-height:0.69em;--ltx-fo-depth:0em;font-size:10pt;" height="9.61" overflow="visible" transform="matrix(1 0 0 -1 0 9.61)" width="338.18"><span class="ltx_foreignobject_container"><span class="ltx_foreignobject_content">
<span id="A2.SS4.SSS2.Px1.p35.pic1.1" class="ltx_inline-block ltx_minipage ltx_align_bottom" style="width:24.44em;">
<span id="A2.SS4.SSS2.Px1.p35.pic1.1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.SS4.SSS2.Px1.p35.pic1.1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold" style="--ltx-fg-color:#FFFFFF;">Evaluation</span></span>
</span></span></span></foreignObject></g><g fill-opacity="1.0" transform="matrix(1.0 0.0 0.0 1.0 20.38 14.66)"><foreignObject style="--ltx-fo-width:33.06em;--ltx-fo-height:8.01em;--ltx-fo-depth:0.16em;font-size:10pt;" height="113" overflow="visible" transform="matrix(1 0 0 -1 0 110.85)" width="457.46"><span class="ltx_foreignobject_container"><span class="ltx_foreignobject_content">
<span id="A2.SS4.SSS2.Px1.p35.pic1.2" class="ltx_inline-block ltx_minipage ltx_align_bottom" style="width:33.06em;">
<span id="A2.SS4.SSS2.Px1.p35.pic1.2.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.SS4.SSS2.Px1.p35.pic1.2.1.1" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:80%;--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">1. The answer didn’t explain the reason for the following statement:</span></span>
<span id="A2.SS4.SSS2.Px1.p35.pic1.2.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.SS4.SSS2.Px1.p35.pic1.2.2.1" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:80%;--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">Therefore, in the maximizing situation there is **at most one** component meeting <math id="A2.SS4.SSS2.Px1.p35.pic1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="U" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">U</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">U</annotation></semantics></math>.</span></span>
<span id="A2.SS4.SSS2.Px1.p35.pic1.2.3" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.SS4.SSS2.Px1.p35.pic1.2.3.1" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:80%;--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">Consequently, for any coloring the total number of monochromatic components is at most</span></span>
<span id="A2.Ex127" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<span><span class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<span class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></span>
<span class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A2.Ex127.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="|T|+1=\Bigl(\frac{n+1}{2}\Bigr)^{2}+1," display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" maxsize="0.800em" minsize="0.800em" stretchy="true">|</mo><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" mathsize="0.800em">T</mi><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" maxsize="0.800em" minsize="0.800em" stretchy="true">|</mo></mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" mathsize="0.800em">+</mo><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" mathsize="0.800em">1</mn></mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" mathsize="0.800em">=</mo><mrow><msup><mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" maxsize="1.600em" minsize="1.600em">(</mo><mfrac style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000"><mrow><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" mathsize="0.800em">n</mi><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" mathsize="0.800em">+</mo><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" mathsize="0.800em">1</mn></mrow><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" mathsize="0.800em">2</mn></mfrac><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" maxsize="1.600em" minsize="1.600em">)</mo></mrow><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" mathsize="0.800em">2</mn></msup><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" mathsize="0.800em">+</mo><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" mathsize="0.800em">1</mn></mrow></mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" mathsize="0.800em">,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">|T|+1=\Bigl(\frac{n+1}{2}\Bigr)^{2}+1,</annotation></semantics></math></span>
<span class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></span></span></span>
</span>
<span id="A2.SS4.SSS2.Px1.p35.pic1.2.4" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.SS4.SSS2.Px1.p35.pic1.2.4.1" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:80%;--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">2. The example for the upper bound is correct.</span></span>
</span></span></span></foreignObject></g></g></svg></span>
</div>
</section>
<section id="A2.SS4.SSS2.Px2" class="ltx_paragraph">
<h5 class="ltx_title ltx_title_paragraph" style="--ltx-fg-color:#FF0000;">Problem 4b2</h5>

<div id="A2.SS4.SSS2.Px2.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A2.SS4.SSS2.Px2.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.SS4.SSS2.Px2.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text"></span>
<br class="ltx_break" style="--ltx-break-space:-10.0pt;"></p>
</div>
<div id="A2.SS4.SSS2.Px2.p2" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent"><span class="ltx_inline-block"><svg id="A2.SS4.SSS2.Px2.p2.pic1" class="ltx_picture" height="166.12" overflow="visible" version="1.1" viewBox="0 0 429.64 166.12" width="429.64"><g style="--ltx-stroke-color:#000000;--ltx-fill-color:#000000;" fill="#000000" stroke="#000000" stroke-width="0.4pt" transform="translate(0,166.12) matrix(1 0 0 -1 0 0)"><g style="--ltx-fill-color:#3D6666;" fill="#3D6666" fill-opacity="1.0"><path style="stroke:none" d="M 0 4.63 L 0 161.49 C 0 164.05 2.07 166.12 4.63 166.12 L 425.01 166.12 C 427.56 166.12 429.64 164.05 429.64 161.49 L 429.64 4.63 C 429.64 2.07 427.56 0 425.01 0 L 4.63 0 C 2.07 0 0 2.07 0 4.63 Z"></path></g><g style="--ltx-fill-color:#F9F9F9;" fill="#F9F9F9" fill-opacity="1.0"><path style="stroke:none" d="M 0.69 4.63 L 0.69 147.25 L 428.94 147.25 L 428.94 4.63 C 428.94 2.45 427.18 0.69 425.01 0.69 L 4.63 0.69 C 2.45 0.69 0.69 2.45 0.69 4.63 Z"></path></g><g fill-opacity="1.0" transform="matrix(1.0 0.0 0.0 1.0 20.38 151.88)"><foreignObject style="--ltx-fo-width:24.44em;--ltx-fo-height:0.69em;--ltx-fo-depth:0em;font-size:10pt;" height="9.61" overflow="visible" transform="matrix(1 0 0 -1 0 9.61)" width="338.18"><span class="ltx_foreignobject_container"><span class="ltx_foreignobject_content">
<span id="A2.SS4.SSS2.Px2.p2.pic1.1" class="ltx_inline-block ltx_minipage ltx_align_bottom" style="width:24.44em;">
<span id="A2.SS4.SSS2.Px2.p2.pic1.1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.SS4.SSS2.Px2.p2.pic1.1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold" style="--ltx-fg-color:#FFFFFF;">Problem</span></span>
</span></span></span></foreignObject></g><g fill-opacity="1.0" transform="matrix(1.0 0.0 0.0 1.0 20.38 14.66)"><foreignObject style="--ltx-fo-width:32.01em;--ltx-fo-height:8.73em;--ltx-fo-depth:0.16em;font-size:10pt;" height="122.94" overflow="visible" transform="matrix(1 0 0 -1 0 120.79)" width="442.93"><span class="ltx_foreignobject_container"><span class="ltx_foreignobject_content">
<span id="A2.SS4.SSS2.Px2.p2.pic1.2" class="ltx_inline-block ltx_minipage ltx_align_bottom" style="width:32.01em;">
<span id="A2.SS4.SSS2.Px2.p2.pic1.2.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.SS4.SSS2.Px2.p2.pic1.2.1.1" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:80%;--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">On a <math id="A2.SS4.SSS2.Px2.p2.pic1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="99\times 99" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">99</mn><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" lspace="0.222em" mathcolor="#000000" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">99</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">99\times 99</annotation></semantics></math> grid, you begin at the bottom<span id="A2.SS4.SSS2.Px2.p2.pic1.2.1.1.1" class="ltx_text">-</span>left cell and make a path that visits every cell exactly once. At each step you move to an unvisited cell sharing a side with your current position. After you have covered all cells, in how many distinct cells could your path end? Please rigorously justify your answer.</span></span><span class="ltx_inline-block"><svg id="A2.SS4.SSS2.Px2.p2.pic1.pic1" class="ltx_picture" color="#FF0000" height="18.24" overflow="visible" style="vertical-align:-4.1px" version="1.1" viewBox="0 0 18.24 18.24" width="18.24"><g style="--ltx-stroke-color:#FF0000;--ltx-fill-color:#FF0000;" fill="#FF0000" stroke="#FF0000" stroke-width="1.8pt" transform="translate(0,18.24) matrix(1 0 0 -1 0 0) translate(1.25,0) translate(0,1.25)"><path style="fill:none" d="M 0 0 L 15.75 15.75 M 0 15.75 L 15.75 0"></path></g></svg></span>
<span id="A2.SS4.SSS2.Px2.p2.pic1.2.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.SS4.SSS2.Px2.p2.pic1.2.2.1" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:80%;--ltx-fg-color:#FF0000;">GPT-5 thinking failed</span></span>
<span id="A2.SS4.SSS2.Px2.p2.pic1.2.3" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.SS4.SSS2.Px2.p2.pic1.2.3.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic" style="font-size:80%;--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">Proposed by Qiuyu Ren</span></span>
</span></span></span></foreignObject></g></g></svg></span>
</div>
<div id="A2.SS4.SSS2.Px2.1" class="ltx_proof">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_font_italic ltx_title_proof"><span id="A2.SS4.SSS2.Px2.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Response of GPT-5-thinking</span>.</h6>
<div id="A2.SS4.SSS2.Px2.p3" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A2.SS4.SSS2.Px2.p3.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.SS4.SSS2.Px2.p3.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Short answer:<span id="A2.SS4.SSS2.Px2.p3.1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_medium"> <math id="A2.SS4.SSS2.Px2.p3.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbf{4900}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mn>𝟒𝟗𝟎𝟎</mn><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbf{4900}</annotation></semantics></math>.</span></span></p>
</div>
<div id="A2.SS4.SSS2.Px2.p4" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A2.SS4.SSS2.Px2.p4.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.SS4.SSS2.Px2.p4.1.1" class="ltx_text">Color the grid like a chessboard, with the starting cell <math id="A2.SS4.SSS2.Px2.p4.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(1,1)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>1</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(1,1)</annotation></semantics></math> colored black. The grid has <math id="A2.SS4.SSS2.Px2.p4.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="99\cdot 99=9801" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mn>99</mn><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><mn>99</mn></mrow><mo>=</mo><mn>9801</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">99\cdot 99=9801</annotation></semantics></math> cells (odd). Any path that visits every cell exactly once alternates colors at each step, so its two endpoints must lie on the <em id="A2.SS4.SSS2.Px2.p4.1.1.1" class="ltx_emph ltx_font_italic">same</em> color when the total number of vertices is odd (because the path has <math id="A2.SS4.SSS2.Px2.p4.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="9800" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mn>9800</mn><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">9800</annotation></semantics></math> edges, an even number of color switches). Thus the end must be on a black cell. There are <math id="A2.SS4.SSS2.Px2.p4.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\frac{9801+1}{2}=4901" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mfrac><mrow><mn>9801</mn><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mn>2</mn></mfrac><mo>=</mo><mn>4901</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\frac{9801+1}{2}=4901</annotation></semantics></math> black cells. The start cannot also be the end (that would be a Hamiltonian cycle, impossible on an odd bipartite graph), so there are at most <math id="A2.SS4.SSS2.Px2.p4.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="4901-1=4900" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mn>4901</mn><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo>=</mo><mn>4900</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">4901-1=4900</annotation></semantics></math> possible ends.</span></p>
</div>
<div id="A2.SS4.SSS2.Px2.p5" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A2.SS4.SSS2.Px2.p5.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.SS4.SSS2.Px2.p5.1.1" class="ltx_text">It remains to show: from the bottom-left corner <math id="A2.SS4.SSS2.Px2.p5.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(1,1)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>1</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(1,1)</annotation></semantics></math>, there is a Hamiltonian path to every other black cell. We prove this by a standard “peel the border” induction.</span></p>
</div>
<div id="A2.SS4.SSS2.Px2.p6" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A2.SS4.SSS2.Px2.p6.1" class="ltx_p"><em id="A2.SS4.SSS2.Px2.p6.1.1" class="ltx_emph ltx_font_italic">Claim.</em><span id="A2.SS4.SSS2.Px2.p6.1.2" class="ltx_text"> On any odd <math id="A2.SS4.SSS2.Px2.p6.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(2k+1)\times(2k+1)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>k</mi></mrow><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo rspace="0.055em" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo rspace="0.222em">×</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>k</mi></mrow><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(2k+1)\times(2k+1)</annotation></semantics></math> grid, for any two distinct cells of the same color, there exists a Hamiltonian path between them.</span></p>
</div>
<div id="A2.SS4.SSS2.Px2.p7" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A2.SS4.SSS2.Px2.p7.1" class="ltx_p"><em id="A2.SS4.SSS2.Px2.p7.1.1" class="ltx_emph ltx_font_italic">Base case.</em><span id="A2.SS4.SSS2.Px2.p7.1.2" class="ltx_text"> For <math id="A2.SS4.SSS2.Px2.p7.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="3\times 3" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mn>3</mn><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><mn>3</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">3\times 3</annotation></semantics></math>, one checks directly (e.g., from <math id="A2.SS4.SSS2.Px2.p7.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(1,1)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>1</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(1,1)</annotation></semantics></math> you can end at any of the four other even-parity cells).</span></p>
</div>
<div id="A2.SS4.SSS2.Px2.p8" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A2.SS4.SSS2.Px2.p8.1" class="ltx_p"><em id="A2.SS4.SSS2.Px2.p8.1.1" class="ltx_emph ltx_font_italic">Inductive step.</em><span id="A2.SS4.SSS2.Px2.p8.1.2" class="ltx_text"> Suppose the claim holds for <math id="A2.SS4.SSS2.Px2.p8.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(2k-1)\times(2k-1)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>k</mi></mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo rspace="0.055em" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo rspace="0.222em">×</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>k</mi></mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(2k-1)\times(2k-1)</annotation></semantics></math>. Consider a <math id="A2.SS4.SSS2.Px2.p8.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(2k+1)\times(2k+1)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>k</mi></mrow><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo rspace="0.055em" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo rspace="0.222em">×</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>k</mi></mrow><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(2k+1)\times(2k+1)</annotation></semantics></math> board, start <math id="A2.SS4.SSS2.Px2.p8.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="S=(1,1)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>S</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>1</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">S=(1,1)</annotation></semantics></math>, and a target black cell <math id="A2.SS4.SSS2.Px2.p8.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="T\neq S" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>T</mi><mo>≠</mo><mi>S</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">T\neq S</annotation></semantics></math>.</span></p>
<ol id="A2.I9" class="ltx_enumerate">
<li id="A2.I9.i1" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">1.</span> 
<div id="A2.I9.i1.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A2.I9.i1.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.I9.i1.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Traverse the outer ring.</span> From <math id="A2.I9.i1.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(1,1)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>1</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(1,1)</annotation></semantics></math> go right along the bottom row to <math id="A2.I9.i1.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(2k+1,1)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>k</mi></mrow><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo>,</mo><mn>1</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(2k+1,1)</annotation></semantics></math>, then up the right column to <math id="A2.I9.i1.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(2k+1,2k+1)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>k</mi></mrow><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo>,</mo><mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>k</mi></mrow><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(2k+1,2k+1)</annotation></semantics></math>, then left along the top row to <math id="A2.I9.i1.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(1,2k+1)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>,</mo><mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>k</mi></mrow><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(1,2k+1)</annotation></semantics></math>, then down the left column to <math id="A2.I9.i1.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(1,2)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>2</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(1,2)</annotation></semantics></math>. This covers every cell of the outer 1-cell-thick border exactly once and stops at <math id="A2.I9.i1.p1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(1,2)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>2</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(1,2)</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>
</div></li>
<li id="A2.I9.i2" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">2.</span> 
<div id="A2.I9.i2.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A2.I9.i2.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.I9.i2.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Choose an entry to the inner square.</span> Let <math id="A2.I9.i2.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="E" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>E</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">E</annotation></semantics></math> be any inner-boundary cell with both coordinates even (e.g., <math id="A2.I9.i2.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(2,2)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>2</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>2</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(2,2)</annotation></semantics></math>), except if <math id="A2.I9.i2.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="T=(2,2)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>T</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>2</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>2</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">T=(2,2)</annotation></semantics></math> then pick a different even inner-boundary cell such as <math id="A2.I9.i2.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(2,4)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>2</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>4</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(2,4)</annotation></semantics></math>. From <math id="A2.I9.i2.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(1,2)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>2</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(1,2)</annotation></semantics></math> step to the adjacent inner-boundary cell that leads into <math id="A2.I9.i2.p1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="E" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>E</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">E</annotation></semantics></math> in one move; include all necessary outer-ring cells before that step so the outer ring is fully used. Now we have a simple path from <math id="A2.I9.i2.p1.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="S" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>S</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">S</annotation></semantics></math> to <math id="A2.I9.i2.p1.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="E" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>E</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">E</annotation></semantics></math> that has covered every border cell and no inner cell other than <math id="A2.I9.i2.p1.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="E" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>E</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">E</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>
</div></li>
<li id="A2.I9.i3" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">3.</span> 
<div id="A2.I9.i3.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A2.I9.i3.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.I9.i3.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Use the induction inside.</span> Remove the border: the remaining inner board is <math id="A2.I9.i3.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(2k-1)\times(2k-1)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>k</mi></mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo rspace="0.055em" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo rspace="0.222em">×</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>k</mi></mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(2k-1)\times(2k-1)</annotation></semantics></math>, still odd. The chessboard coloring restricts, and both <math id="A2.I9.i3.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="E" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>E</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">E</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="A2.I9.i3.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="T" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>T</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">T</annotation></semantics></math> are of the same color in the inner board. By the induction hypothesis, there is a Hamiltonian path in the inner board from <math id="A2.I9.i3.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="E" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>E</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">E</annotation></semantics></math> to <math id="A2.I9.i3.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="T" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>T</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">T</annotation></semantics></math> that covers all inner cells exactly once.</p>
</div></li>
</ol>
</div>
<div id="A2.SS4.SSS2.Px2.p9" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A2.SS4.SSS2.Px2.p9.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.SS4.SSS2.Px2.p9.1.1" class="ltx_text">Concatenating the outer-ring path <math id="A2.SS4.SSS2.Px2.p9.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="S\to E" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>S</mi><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><mi>E</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">S\to E</annotation></semantics></math> with the inner Hamiltonian path <math id="A2.SS4.SSS2.Px2.p9.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="E\to T" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>E</mi><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><mi>T</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">E\to T</annotation></semantics></math> gives a Hamiltonian path from <math id="A2.SS4.SSS2.Px2.p9.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="S" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>S</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">S</annotation></semantics></math> to <math id="A2.SS4.SSS2.Px2.p9.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="T" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>T</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">T</annotation></semantics></math> on the whole board. This completes the induction. Exactly the black cells except the start are possible ends, i.e.,</span></p>
<table id="A2.Ex128" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A2.Ex128.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\frac{99\cdot 99+1}{2}-1=\frac{9801-1}{2}=\boxed{4900}." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mfrac><mrow><mrow><mn>99</mn><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><mn>99</mn></mrow><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mn>2</mn></mfrac><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mrow><mn>9801</mn><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mn>2</mn></mfrac><mo>=</mo><menclose notation="box"><mn>4900</mn></menclose></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\frac{99\cdot 99+1}{2}-1=\frac{9801-1}{2}=\boxed{4900}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A2.SS4.SSS2.Px2.p9.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.SS4.SSS2.Px2.p9.2.1" class="ltx_text">∎</span></p>
</div>
</div>
<div id="A2.SS4.SSS2.Px2.2" class="ltx_proof">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_font_italic ltx_title_proof"><span id="A2.SS4.SSS2.Px2.2.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Standard Solution</span>.</h6>
<div id="A2.SS4.SSS2.Px2.p10" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A2.SS4.SSS2.Px2.p10.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.SS4.SSS2.Px2.p10.1.1" class="ltx_text">The answer is 4900. Checkerboard color the grid so that the bottom-left cell is colored black. For parity reason, the end cell of the path is black. Since there are 4900 black cells other than the starting one, the path can end at at most 4900 cells.</span></p>
</div>
<div id="A2.SS4.SSS2.Px2.p11" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A2.SS4.SSS2.Px2.p11.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.SS4.SSS2.Px2.p11.1.1" class="ltx_text">We show the path can indeed end at each of the black cell other than the starting one. In fact, we induct on <math id="A2.SS4.SSS2.Px2.p11.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="k" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>k</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">k</annotation></semantics></math> to show a path starting at the bottom-left cell in a checkerboard colored <math id="A2.SS4.SSS2.Px2.p11.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(2k+1)\times(2k+1)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>k</mi></mrow><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo rspace="0.055em" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo rspace="0.222em">×</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>k</mi></mrow><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(2k+1)\times(2k+1)</annotation></semantics></math> grid can end at any other cell sharing the same color as the starting one. When <math id="A2.SS4.SSS2.Px2.p11.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="k=1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">k=1</annotation></semantics></math> one can check this by hand.</span></p>
</div>
<div id="A2.SS4.SSS2.Px2.p12" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A2.SS4.SSS2.Px2.p12.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.SS4.SSS2.Px2.p12.1.1" class="ltx_text">Assume <math id="A2.SS4.SSS2.Px2.p12.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="k&gt;1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>&gt;</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">k&gt;1</annotation></semantics></math>. Label the cells in the natural way so that the bottom-left is <math id="A2.SS4.SSS2.Px2.p12.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(1,1)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>1</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(1,1)</annotation></semantics></math>.</span></p>
</div>
<div id="A2.SS4.SSS2.Px2.p13" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A2.SS4.SSS2.Px2.p13.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.SS4.SSS2.Px2.p13.1.1" class="ltx_text">One can take a path that first traverses the entire outer border of the grid and ends at <math id="A2.SS4.SSS2.Px2.p13.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(2,2)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>2</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>2</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(2,2)</annotation></semantics></math>; thus, by induction hypothesis, the path can end at any cell sharing the same color as <math id="A2.SS4.SSS2.Px2.p13.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(1,1)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>1</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(1,1)</annotation></semantics></math> that is not adjacent to the boundary and that is not <math id="A2.SS4.SSS2.Px2.p13.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(2,2)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>2</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>2</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(2,2)</annotation></semantics></math>. Similarly, one can take a path that first traverses <math id="A2.SS4.SSS2.Px2.p13.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(1,1)\sim(1,2k+1)\sim(2k+1,2k+1)\sim(2k+1,2k)\sim(2,2k)\sim(2,1)\sim(3,1)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>1</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>∼</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>,</mo><mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>k</mi></mrow><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>∼</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>k</mi></mrow><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo>,</mo><mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>k</mi></mrow><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>∼</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>k</mi></mrow><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo>,</mo><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>k</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>∼</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>2</mn><mo>,</mo><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>k</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>∼</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>2</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>1</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>∼</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>3</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>1</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(1,1)\sim(1,2k+1)\sim(2k+1,2k+1)\sim(2k+1,2k)\sim(2,2k)\sim(2,1)\sim(3,1)</annotation></semantics></math>; the induction hypothesis implies that the path can end at any cell sharing the same color as <math id="A2.SS4.SSS2.Px2.p13.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(1,1)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>1</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(1,1)</annotation></semantics></math> that is not in column <math id="A2.SS4.SSS2.Px2.p13.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="1,2" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">1,2</annotation></semantics></math> or row <math id="A2.SS4.SSS2.Px2.p13.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="2k,2k+1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>k</mi></mrow><mo>,</mo><mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>k</mi></mrow><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">2k,2k+1</annotation></semantics></math>, and that is not <math id="A2.SS4.SSS2.Px2.p13.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(3,1)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>3</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>1</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(3,1)</annotation></semantics></math>. Combining these two strategy, and use symmetry, we see that the path may end at any possible cell except possibly <math id="A2.SS4.SSS2.Px2.p13.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(2,2),(3,1)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>2</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>2</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>,</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>3</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>1</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(2,2),(3,1)</annotation></semantics></math> (and symmetrically <math id="A2.SS4.SSS2.Px2.p13.m10" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(1,3)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>3</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(1,3)</annotation></semantics></math>). For those two cases, we may explicitly take the path <math id="A2.SS4.SSS2.Px2.p13.m11" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(1,1)\sim(1,2k+1)\sim(2k+1,2k+1)\sim(2k+1,2k)\sim(2,2k)\sim(2,2k-1)\sim(2k+1,2k-1)\sim\cdots\sim(2k+1,3)\sim(2k+1,1)\sim(2k,1)\sim(2k,2)\sim\cdots\sim(4,1)\sim(4,2)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>1</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>∼</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>,</mo><mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>k</mi></mrow><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>∼</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>k</mi></mrow><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo>,</mo><mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>k</mi></mrow><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>∼</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>k</mi></mrow><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo>,</mo><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>k</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>∼</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>2</mn><mo>,</mo><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>k</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>∼</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>2</mn><mo>,</mo><mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>k</mi></mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>∼</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>k</mi></mrow><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo>,</mo><mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>k</mi></mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo rspace="0.1389em">∼</mo><mo lspace="0.1389em" rspace="0.1389em">⋯</mo><mo lspace="0.1389em">∼</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>k</mi></mrow><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo>,</mo><mn>3</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>∼</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>k</mi></mrow><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo>,</mo><mn>1</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>∼</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>k</mi></mrow><mo>,</mo><mn>1</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>∼</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>k</mi></mrow><mo>,</mo><mn>2</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo rspace="0.1389em">∼</mo><mo lspace="0.1389em" rspace="0.1389em">⋯</mo><mo lspace="0.1389em">∼</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>4</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>1</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>∼</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>4</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>2</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(1,1)\sim(1,2k+1)\sim(2k+1,2k+1)\sim(2k+1,2k)\sim(2,2k)\sim(2,2k-1)\sim(2k+1,2k-1)\sim\cdots\sim(2k+1,3)\sim(2k+1,1)\sim(2k,1)\sim(2k,2)\sim\cdots\sim(4,1)\sim(4,2)</annotation></semantics></math> that traverse everything except the square <math id="A2.SS4.SSS2.Px2.p13.m12" class="ltx_Math" alttext="[2,3]\times[1,2]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>3</mn></mrow><mo rspace="0.055em" stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><mo rspace="0.222em">×</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">[2,3]\times[1,2]</annotation></semantics></math>, and concatenate it to a path that ends at either <math id="A2.SS4.SSS2.Px2.p13.m13" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(3,1)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>3</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>1</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(3,1)</annotation></semantics></math> or <math id="A2.SS4.SSS2.Px2.p13.m14" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(2,2)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>2</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>2</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(2,2)</annotation></semantics></math>.
∎</span></p>
</div>
</div>
