</span></span></span></foreignObject></g></g></svg></span>
</div>
</section>
</section>
</section>
<section id="A2.SS5" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">5 </span>Logical Thinking and Reasoning</h3>

<section id="A2.SS5.SSS1" class="ltx_subsubsection">
<h4 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsubsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsubsection">(a) </span>Constructing valid proofs</h4>

<section id="A2.SS5.SSS1.Px1" class="ltx_paragraph">
<h5 class="ltx_title ltx_title_paragraph" style="--ltx-fg-color:#FF0000;">Problem 5a1 </h5>

<div id="A2.SS5.SSS1.Px1.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A2.SS5.SSS1.Px1.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.SS5.SSS1.Px1.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text"></span>
<br class="ltx_break" style="--ltx-break-space:-10.0pt;"></p>
</div>
<div id="A2.SS5.SSS1.Px1.p2" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent"><span class="ltx_inline-block"><svg id="A2.SS5.SSS1.Px1.p2.pic1" class="ltx_picture" height="149.51" overflow="visible" version="1.1" viewBox="0 0 429.64 149.51" width="429.64"><g style="--ltx-stroke-color:#000000;--ltx-fill-color:#000000;" fill="#000000" stroke="#000000" stroke-width="0.4pt" transform="translate(0,149.51) matrix(1 0 0 -1 0 0)"><g style="--ltx-fill-color:#3D6666;" fill="#3D6666" fill-opacity="1.0"><path style="stroke:none" d="M 0 4.63 L 0 144.89 C 0 147.44 2.07 149.51 4.63 149.51 L 425.01 149.51 C 427.56 149.51 429.64 147.44 429.64 144.89 L 429.64 4.63 C 429.64 2.07 427.56 0 425.01 0 L 4.63 0 C 2.07 0 0 2.07 0 4.63 Z"></path></g><g style="--ltx-fill-color:#F9F9F9;" fill="#F9F9F9" fill-opacity="1.0"><path style="stroke:none" d="M 0.69 4.63 L 0.69 130.65 L 428.94 130.65 L 428.94 4.63 C 428.94 2.45 427.18 0.69 425.01 0.69 L 4.63 0.69 C 2.45 0.69 0.69 2.45 0.69 4.63 Z"></path></g><g fill-opacity="1.0" transform="matrix(1.0 0.0 0.0 1.0 20.38 135.28)"><foreignObject style="--ltx-fo-width:24.44em;--ltx-fo-height:0.69em;--ltx-fo-depth:0em;font-size:10pt;" height="9.61" overflow="visible" transform="matrix(1 0 0 -1 0 9.61)" width="338.18"><span class="ltx_foreignobject_container"><span class="ltx_foreignobject_content">
<span id="A2.SS5.SSS1.Px1.p2.pic1.1" class="ltx_inline-block ltx_minipage ltx_align_bottom" style="width:24.44em;">
<span id="A2.SS5.SSS1.Px1.p2.pic1.1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.SS5.SSS1.Px1.p2.pic1.1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold" style="--ltx-fg-color:#FFFFFF;">Problem</span></span>
</span></span></span></foreignObject></g><g fill-opacity="1.0" transform="matrix(1.0 0.0 0.0 1.0 20.38 14.66)"><foreignObject style="--ltx-fo-width:32.01em;--ltx-fo-height:7.53em;--ltx-fo-depth:0.16em;font-size:10pt;" height="106.34" overflow="visible" transform="matrix(1 0 0 -1 0 104.18)" width="442.93"><span class="ltx_foreignobject_container"><span class="ltx_foreignobject_content">
<span id="A2.SS5.SSS1.Px1.p2.pic1.2" class="ltx_inline-block ltx_minipage ltx_align_bottom" style="width:32.01em;">
<span id="A2.SS5.SSS1.Px1.p2.pic1.2.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.SS5.SSS1.Px1.p2.pic1.2.1.1" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:80%;--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">Let <math id="A2.SS5.SSS1.Px1.p2.pic1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="X" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">X</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">X</annotation></semantics></math> be a set with 56 elements. Find the smallest positive integer <math id="A2.SS5.SSS1.Px1.p2.pic1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="n" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">n</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">n</annotation></semantics></math> such that, for any collection of 15 subsets of <math id="A2.SS5.SSS1.Px1.p2.pic1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="X" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">X</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">X</annotation></semantics></math>, if the union of any 7 of them contains at least <math id="A2.SS5.SSS1.Px1.p2.pic1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="n" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">n</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">n</annotation></semantics></math> elements, then there must exist 3 of these subsets whose intersection is nonempty.</span></span><span class="ltx_inline-block"><svg id="A2.SS5.SSS1.Px1.p2.pic1.pic1" class="ltx_picture" color="#FF0000" height="18.24" overflow="visible" style="vertical-align:-4.1px" version="1.1" viewBox="0 0 18.24 18.24" width="18.24"><g style="--ltx-stroke-color:#FF0000;--ltx-fill-color:#FF0000;" fill="#FF0000" stroke="#FF0000" stroke-width="1.8pt" transform="translate(0,18.24) matrix(1 0 0 -1 0 0) translate(1.25,0) translate(0,1.25)"><path style="fill:none" d="M 0 0 L 15.75 15.75 M 0 15.75 L 15.75 0"></path></g></svg></span>
<span id="A2.SS5.SSS1.Px1.p2.pic1.2.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.SS5.SSS1.Px1.p2.pic1.2.2.1" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:80%;--ltx-fg-color:#FF0000;">GPT-5 thinking failed</span></span>
<span id="A2.SS5.SSS1.Px1.p2.pic1.2.3" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.SS5.SSS1.Px1.p2.pic1.2.3.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic" style="font-size:80%;--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">Proposed by Jiaxin Zhang</span></span>
</span></span></span></foreignObject></g></g></svg></span>
</div>
<div id="A2.SS5.SSS1.Px1.1" class="ltx_proof">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_font_italic ltx_title_proof"><span id="A2.SS5.SSS1.Px1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Response of GPT-5-thinking</span>.</h6>
<div id="A2.SS5.SSS1.Px1.p3" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A2.SS5.SSS1.Px1.p3.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.SS5.SSS1.Px1.p3.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Claim.<span id="A2.SS5.SSS1.Px1.p3.1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_medium"> The smallest <math id="A2.SS5.SSS1.Px1.p3.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="n" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>n</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">n</annotation></semantics></math> is <math id="A2.SS5.SSS1.Px1.p3.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\boxed{42}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><menclose notation="box"><mn>42</mn></menclose><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\boxed{42}</annotation></semantics></math>.</span></span></p>
</div>
<div id="A2.SS5.SSS1.Px1.p4" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A2.SS5.SSS1.Px1.p4.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.SS5.SSS1.Px1.p4.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Sufficiency (<math id="A2.SS5.SSS1.Px1.p4.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="n=42" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>42</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">n=42</annotation></semantics></math> forces a triple intersection).<span id="A2.SS5.SSS1.Px1.p4.1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_medium">
Let <math id="A2.SS5.SSS1.Px1.p4.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{F}=\{A_{1},\dots,A_{15}\}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℱ</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><msub><mi>A</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>A</mi><mn>15</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{F}=\{A_{1},\dots,A_{15}\}</annotation></semantics></math> be subsets of a <math id="A2.SS5.SSS1.Px1.p4.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="56" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mn>56</mn><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">56</annotation></semantics></math>-point set <math id="A2.SS5.SSS1.Px1.p4.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="X" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>X</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">X</annotation></semantics></math>.
Assume, toward a contradiction, that no point of <math id="A2.SS5.SSS1.Px1.p4.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="X" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>X</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">X</annotation></semantics></math> lies in three of the sets (i.e. every <math id="A2.SS5.SSS1.Px1.p4.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="x\in X" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>∈</mo><mi>X</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">x\in X</annotation></semantics></math> belongs to at most two of the <math id="A2.SS5.SSS1.Px1.p4.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="A_{i}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>A</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">A_{i}</annotation></semantics></math>’s).
Associate to <math id="A2.SS5.SSS1.Px1.p4.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{F}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℱ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{F}</annotation></semantics></math> the multigraph <math id="A2.SS5.SSS1.Px1.p4.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="G" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>G</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">G</annotation></semantics></math> on vertex set <math id="A2.SS5.SSS1.Px1.p4.m10" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\{1,\dots,15\}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>,</mo><mn>15</mn><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\{1,\dots,15\}</annotation></semantics></math> in which each <math id="A2.SS5.SSS1.Px1.p4.m11" class="ltx_Math" alttext="x\in X" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>∈</mo><mi>X</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">x\in X</annotation></semantics></math> that lies in <em id="A2.SS5.SSS1.Px1.p4.1.1.1.1" class="ltx_emph ltx_font_italic">exactly two</em> sets <math id="A2.SS5.SSS1.Px1.p4.m12" class="ltx_Math" alttext="A_{i},A_{j}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>A</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>A</mi><mi>j</mi></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">A_{i},A_{j}</annotation></semantics></math> contributes one parallel edge <math id="A2.SS5.SSS1.Px1.p4.m13" class="ltx_Math" alttext="ij" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">ij</annotation></semantics></math>; points contained in <math id="A2.SS5.SSS1.Px1.p4.m14" class="ltx_Math" alttext="0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mn>0</mn><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">0</annotation></semantics></math> or <math id="A2.SS5.SSS1.Px1.p4.m15" class="ltx_Math" alttext="1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mn>1</mn><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">1</annotation></semantics></math> sets contribute nothing to <math id="A2.SS5.SSS1.Px1.p4.m16" class="ltx_Math" alttext="G" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>G</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">G</annotation></semantics></math>.
Thus <math id="A2.SS5.SSS1.Px1.p4.m17" class="ltx_Math" alttext="|E(G)|\leq 56" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mrow><mi>E</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>G</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mn>56</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">|E(G)|\leq 56</annotation></semantics></math>, with equality if every point lies in exactly two sets.</span></span></p>
</div>
<div id="A2.SS5.SSS1.Px1.p5" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A2.SS5.SSS1.Px1.p5.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.SS5.SSS1.Px1.p5.1.1" class="ltx_text">Given any <math id="A2.SS5.SSS1.Px1.p5.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="7" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mn>7</mn><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">7</annotation></semantics></math>-subcollection <math id="A2.SS5.SSS1.Px1.p5.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="S\subseteq\mathcal{F}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>S</mi><mo>⊆</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℱ</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">S\subseteq\mathcal{F}</annotation></semantics></math>, let <math id="A2.SS5.SSS1.Px1.p5.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="U" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>U</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">U</annotation></semantics></math> be its complement (so <math id="A2.SS5.SSS1.Px1.p5.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="|U|=8" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mi>U</mi><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow><mo>=</mo><mn>8</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">|U|=8</annotation></semantics></math>).
A point <math id="A2.SS5.SSS1.Px1.p5.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="x\in X" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>∈</mo><mi>X</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">x\in X</annotation></semantics></math> is <em id="A2.SS5.SSS1.Px1.p5.1.1.1" class="ltx_emph ltx_font_italic">missed</em> by the union <math id="A2.SS5.SSS1.Px1.p5.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\bigcup S" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo>⋃</mo><mi>S</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\bigcup S</annotation></semantics></math> iff the two sets containing <math id="A2.SS5.SSS1.Px1.p5.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="x" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>x</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">x</annotation></semantics></math> both lie in <math id="A2.SS5.SSS1.Px1.p5.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="U" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>U</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">U</annotation></semantics></math>, i.e. iff the corresponding edge of <math id="A2.SS5.SSS1.Px1.p5.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="G" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>G</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">G</annotation></semantics></math> is internal to <math id="A2.SS5.SSS1.Px1.p5.m10" class="ltx_Math" alttext="U" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>U</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">U</annotation></semantics></math>. Hence</span></p>
<table id="A2.Ex158" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A2.Ex158.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Bigl|\bigcup S\Bigr|\;=\;56-e_{G}(U)," display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mo maxsize="1.600em" minsize="1.600em" stretchy="true">|</mo><mrow><mo lspace="0em" movablelimits="false">⋃</mo><mi>S</mi></mrow><mo maxsize="1.600em" minsize="1.600em" rspace="0.280em" stretchy="true">|</mo></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mn> 56</mn><mo>−</mo><mrow><msub><mi>e</mi><mi>G</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>U</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Bigl|\bigcup S\Bigr|\;=\;56-e_{G}(U),</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A2.SS5.SSS1.Px1.p5.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.SS5.SSS1.Px1.p5.2.1" class="ltx_text">where <math id="A2.SS5.SSS1.Px1.p5.m11" class="ltx_Math" alttext="e_{G}(U)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>e</mi><mi>G</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>U</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">e_{G}(U)</annotation></semantics></math> is the (multi)edge count inside the <math id="A2.SS5.SSS1.Px1.p5.m12" class="ltx_Math" alttext="8" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mn>8</mn><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">8</annotation></semantics></math>-vertex set <math id="A2.SS5.SSS1.Px1.p5.m13" class="ltx_Math" alttext="U" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>U</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">U</annotation></semantics></math>.</span></p>
</div>
<div id="A2.SS5.SSS1.Px1.p6" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A2.SS5.SSS1.Px1.p6.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.SS5.SSS1.Px1.p6.1.1" class="ltx_text">Choose <math id="A2.SS5.SSS1.Px1.p6.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="U" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>U</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">U</annotation></semantics></math> uniformly among the <math id="A2.SS5.SSS1.Px1.p6.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\binom{15}{8}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo>(</mo><mfrac linethickness="0pt"><mn>15</mn><mn>8</mn></mfrac><mo>)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\binom{15}{8}</annotation></semantics></math> <math id="A2.SS5.SSS1.Px1.p6.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="8" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mn>8</mn><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">8</annotation></semantics></math>-subsets.
A fixed edge <math id="A2.SS5.SSS1.Px1.p6.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="ij" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">ij</annotation></semantics></math> is internal to <math id="A2.SS5.SSS1.Px1.p6.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="U" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>U</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">U</annotation></semantics></math> with probability</span></p>
<table id="A2.Ex159" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A2.Ex159.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\frac{\binom{13}{6}}{\binom{15}{8}}\;=\;\frac{1716}{6435}\;=\;\frac{4}{15}." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mfrac><mrow><mo>(</mo><mfrac linethickness="0pt"><mn>13</mn><mn>6</mn></mfrac><mo>)</mo></mrow><mrow><mo>(</mo><mfrac linethickness="0pt"><mn>15</mn><mn>8</mn></mfrac><mo>)</mo></mrow></mfrac><mo lspace="0.558em" rspace="0.558em">=</mo><mfrac><mn>1716</mn><mn>6435</mn></mfrac><mo lspace="0.558em" rspace="0.558em">=</mo><mfrac><mn>4</mn><mn>15</mn></mfrac></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\frac{\binom{13}{6}}{\binom{15}{8}}\;=\;\frac{1716}{6435}\;=\;\frac{4}{15}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A2.SS5.SSS1.Px1.p6.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.SS5.SSS1.Px1.p6.2.1" class="ltx_text">By linearity of expectation,</span></p>
<table id="A2.Ex160" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A2.Ex160.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbb{E}\big[e_{G}(U)\big]\;=\;|E(G)|\cdot\frac{4}{15}\ \leq\ 56\cdot\frac{4}{15}\;=\;\frac{224}{15}." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>𝔼</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">[</mo><mrow><msub><mi>e</mi><mi>G</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>U</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em" rspace="0.280em">]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.558em">=</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mrow><mi>E</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>G</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.055em" stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow><mo rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><mfrac><mn>4</mn><mn>15</mn></mfrac></mrow><mo lspace="0.778em">≤</mo><mrow><mn> 56</mn><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><mfrac><mn>4</mn><mn>15</mn></mfrac></mrow><mo lspace="0.558em" rspace="0.558em">=</mo><mfrac><mn>224</mn><mn>15</mn></mfrac></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbb{E}\big[e_{G}(U)\big]\;=\;|E(G)|\cdot\frac{4}{15}\ \leq\ 56\cdot\frac{4}{15}\;=\;\frac{224}{15}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A2.SS5.SSS1.Px1.p6.3" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.SS5.SSS1.Px1.p6.3.1" class="ltx_text">Therefore</span></p>
<table id="A2.Ex161" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A2.Ex161.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbb{E}\Bigl[\bigl|\bigcup S\bigr|\Bigr]\;=\;56-\mathbb{E}\big[e_{G}(U)\big]\;\geq\;56-\frac{224}{15}\;=\;\frac{616}{15}\;\approx\;41.07." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>𝔼</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="1.600em" minsize="1.600em">[</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em" stretchy="true">|</mo><mrow><mo lspace="0em" movablelimits="false">⋃</mo><mi>S</mi></mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em" stretchy="true">|</mo></mrow><mo maxsize="1.600em" minsize="1.600em" rspace="0.280em">]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mn> 56</mn><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>𝔼</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">[</mo><mrow><msub><mi>e</mi><mi>G</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>U</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em" rspace="0.280em">]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>≥</mo><mrow><mn> 56</mn><mo>−</mo><mfrac><mn>224</mn><mn>15</mn></mfrac></mrow><mo lspace="0.558em" rspace="0.558em">=</mo><mfrac><mn>616</mn><mn>15</mn></mfrac><mo lspace="0.558em">≈</mo><mn> 41.07</mn></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbb{E}\Bigl[\bigl|\bigcup S\bigr|\Bigr]\;=\;56-\mathbb{E}\big[e_{G}(U)\big]\;\geq\;56-\frac{224}{15}\;=\;\frac{616}{15}\;\approx\;41.07.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A2.SS5.SSS1.Px1.p6.4" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.SS5.SSS1.Px1.p6.4.1" class="ltx_text">As union sizes are integers, the average being <math id="A2.SS5.SSS1.Px1.p6.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\leq 41.07" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>≤</mo><mn>41.07</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\leq 41.07</annotation></semantics></math> implies the existence of some <math id="A2.SS5.SSS1.Px1.p6.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="7" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mn>7</mn><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">7</annotation></semantics></math>-subcollection <math id="A2.SS5.SSS1.Px1.p6.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="S" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>S</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">S</annotation></semantics></math> with</span></p>
<table id="A2.Ex162" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A2.Ex162.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Bigl|\bigcup S\Bigr|\ \leq\ 41." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mo maxsize="1.600em" minsize="1.600em" stretchy="true">|</mo><mrow><mo lspace="0em" movablelimits="false">⋃</mo><mi>S</mi></mrow><mo maxsize="1.600em" minsize="1.600em" rspace="0.500em" stretchy="true">|</mo></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mn> 41</mn></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Bigl|\bigcup S\Bigr|\ \leq\ 41.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A2.SS5.SSS1.Px1.p6.5" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.SS5.SSS1.Px1.p6.5.1" class="ltx_text">Consequently, if <em id="A2.SS5.SSS1.Px1.p6.5.1.1" class="ltx_emph ltx_font_italic">every</em> <math id="A2.SS5.SSS1.Px1.p6.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="7" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mn>7</mn><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">7</annotation></semantics></math>-subcollection has union size <math id="A2.SS5.SSS1.Px1.p6.m10" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\geq 42" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>≥</mo><mn>42</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\geq 42</annotation></semantics></math>, then our assumption was false: there must exist a point of <math id="A2.SS5.SSS1.Px1.p6.m11" class="ltx_Math" alttext="X" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>X</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">X</annotation></semantics></math> contained in at least three of the <math id="A2.SS5.SSS1.Px1.p6.m12" class="ltx_Math" alttext="A_{i}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>A</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">A_{i}</annotation></semantics></math>’s.
This proves that <math id="A2.SS5.SSS1.Px1.p6.m13" class="ltx_Math" alttext="n=42" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>42</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">n=42</annotation></semantics></math> suffices.</span></p>
</div>
<div id="A2.SS5.SSS1.Px1.p7" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A2.SS5.SSS1.Px1.p7.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.SS5.SSS1.Px1.p7.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Sharpness (a family with <math id="A2.SS5.SSS1.Px1.p7.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="n=41" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>41</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">n=41</annotation></semantics></math> and no triple intersection).<span id="A2.SS5.SSS1.Px1.p7.1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_medium">
We now sketch a concrete construction on <math id="A2.SS5.SSS1.Px1.p7.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="X" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>X</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">X</annotation></semantics></math> with <math id="A2.SS5.SSS1.Px1.p7.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="|X|=56" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mi>X</mi><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow><mo>=</mo><mn>56</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">|X|=56</annotation></semantics></math> and a family <math id="A2.SS5.SSS1.Px1.p7.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{F}=\{A_{1},\dots,A_{15}\}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℱ</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><msub><mi>A</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>A</mi><mn>15</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{F}=\{A_{1},\dots,A_{15}\}</annotation></semantics></math> such that:</span></span></p>
<ul id="A2.I10" class="ltx_itemize">
<li id="A2.I10.i1" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">•</span> 
<div id="A2.I10.i1.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A2.I10.i1.p1.1" class="ltx_p">each <math id="A2.I10.i1.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="x\in X" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>∈</mo><mi>X</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">x\in X</annotation></semantics></math> lies in <em id="A2.I10.i1.p1.1.1" class="ltx_emph ltx_font_italic">exactly two</em> sets (so there is no triple intersection), and</p>
</div></li>
<li id="A2.I10.i2" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">•</span> 
<div id="A2.I10.i2.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A2.I10.i2.p1.1" class="ltx_p">for every <math id="A2.I10.i2.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="7" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mn>7</mn><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">7</annotation></semantics></math>-subcollection <math id="A2.I10.i2.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="S" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>S</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">S</annotation></semantics></math>, one has <math id="A2.I10.i2.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\bigl|\bigcup S\bigr|\geq 41" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em" stretchy="true">|</mo><mrow><mo lspace="0em">⋃</mo><mi>S</mi></mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em" stretchy="true">|</mo></mrow><mo>≥</mo><mn>41</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\bigl|\bigcup S\bigr|\geq 41</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>
</div></li>
</ul>
<p id="A2.SS5.SSS1.Px1.p7.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.SS5.SSS1.Px1.p7.2.1" class="ltx_text">As above, it suffices to build a multigraph <math id="A2.SS5.SSS1.Px1.p7.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="G" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>G</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">G</annotation></semantics></math> on <math id="A2.SS5.SSS1.Px1.p7.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="15" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mn>15</mn><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">15</annotation></semantics></math> vertices with total edge multiplicity <math id="A2.SS5.SSS1.Px1.p7.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="56" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mn>56</mn><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">56</annotation></semantics></math> and</span></p>
<table id="A2.Ex163" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A2.Ex163.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="e_{G}(U)\ \leq\ 15\qquad\text{for every $8$-vertex subset $U$}," display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>e</mi><mi>G</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>U</mi><mo rspace="0.500em" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mn> 15</mn></mrow><mspace style="width:2em;" width="2em"></mspace><mrow><mtext>for every </mtext><mn>8</mn><mtext>-vertex subset </mtext><mi>U</mi></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">e_{G}(U)\ \leq\ 15\qquad\text{for every $8$-vertex subset $U$},</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A2.SS5.SSS1.Px1.p7.3" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.SS5.SSS1.Px1.p7.3.1" class="ltx_text">because then <math id="A2.SS5.SSS1.Px1.p7.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\bigl|\bigcup S\bigr|=56-e_{G}(U)\geq 56-15=41" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em" stretchy="true">|</mo><mrow><mo lspace="0em">⋃</mo><mi>S</mi></mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em" stretchy="true">|</mo></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mn>56</mn><mo>−</mo><mrow><msub><mi>e</mi><mi>G</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>U</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>≥</mo><mrow><mn>56</mn><mo>−</mo><mn>15</mn></mrow><mo>=</mo><mn>41</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\bigl|\bigcup S\bigr|=56-e_{G}(U)\geq 56-15=41</annotation></semantics></math> for every <math id="A2.SS5.SSS1.Px1.p7.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="7" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mn>7</mn><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">7</annotation></semantics></math>-subcollection <math id="A2.SS5.SSS1.Px1.p7.m10" class="ltx_Math" alttext="S" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>S</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">S</annotation></semantics></math>.</span></p>
</div>
<div id="A2.SS5.SSS1.Px1.p8" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A2.SS5.SSS1.Px1.p8.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.SS5.SSS1.Px1.p8.1.1" class="ltx_text">Partition the <math id="A2.SS5.SSS1.Px1.p8.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="15" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mn>15</mn><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">15</annotation></semantics></math> vertices into <math id="A2.SS5.SSS1.Px1.p8.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="L\cup R" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>L</mi><mo>∪</mo><mi>R</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">L\cup R</annotation></semantics></math> with <math id="A2.SS5.SSS1.Px1.p8.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="|L|=7" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mi>L</mi><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow><mo>=</mo><mn>7</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">|L|=7</annotation></semantics></math>, <math id="A2.SS5.SSS1.Px1.p8.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="|R|=8" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mi>R</mi><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow><mo>=</mo><mn>8</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">|R|=8</annotation></semantics></math>.
Realize <math id="A2.SS5.SSS1.Px1.p8.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="G" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>G</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">G</annotation></semantics></math> as a weighted bipartite graph on <math id="A2.SS5.SSS1.Px1.p8.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="L\!\times\!R" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>L</mi><mo lspace="0.052em" rspace="0.052em">×</mo><mi>R</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">L\!\times\!R</annotation></semantics></math> (so each edge is a pair <math id="A2.SS5.SSS1.Px1.p8.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\ell r" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>r</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\ell r</annotation></semantics></math>, <math id="A2.SS5.SSS1.Px1.p8.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\ell\in L" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo>∈</mo><mi>L</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\ell\in L</annotation></semantics></math>, <math id="A2.SS5.SSS1.Px1.p8.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="r\in R" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>r</mi><mo>∈</mo><mi>R</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">r\in R</annotation></semantics></math>) with nonnegative integer weights <math id="A2.SS5.SSS1.Px1.p8.m10" class="ltx_Math" alttext="w_{\ell r}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>w</mi><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>r</mi></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">w_{\ell r}</annotation></semantics></math> summing to <math id="A2.SS5.SSS1.Px1.p8.m11" class="ltx_Math" alttext="56" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mn>56</mn><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">56</annotation></semantics></math>.
We enforce the Zarankiewicz-type condition that for every choice of <math id="A2.SS5.SSS1.Px1.p8.m12" class="ltx_Math" alttext="4" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mn>4</mn><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">4</annotation></semantics></math> rows <math id="A2.SS5.SSS1.Px1.p8.m13" class="ltx_Math" alttext="L_{0}\subseteq L" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>L</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo>⊆</mo><mi>L</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">L_{0}\subseteq L</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="A2.SS5.SSS1.Px1.p8.m14" class="ltx_Math" alttext="4" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mn>4</mn><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">4</annotation></semantics></math> columns <math id="A2.SS5.SSS1.Px1.p8.m15" class="ltx_Math" alttext="R_{0}\subseteq R" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>R</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo>⊆</mo><mi>R</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">R_{0}\subseteq R</annotation></semantics></math>,</span></p>
<table id="A2.Ex164" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A2.Ex164.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\sum_{\ell\in L_{0}}\sum_{r\in R_{0}}w_{\ell r}\ \leq\ 15." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><munder><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo>∈</mo><msub><mi>L</mi><mn>0</mn></msub></mrow></munder><mrow><munder><mo lspace="0.167em" movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>r</mi><mo>∈</mo><msub><mi>R</mi><mn>0</mn></msub></mrow></munder><msub><mi>w</mi><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>r</mi></mrow></msub></mrow></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mn> 15</mn></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\sum_{\ell\in L_{0}}\sum_{r\in R_{0}}w_{\ell r}\ \leq\ 15.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A2.SS5.SSS1.Px1.p8.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.SS5.SSS1.Px1.p8.2.1" class="ltx_text">Since any <math id="A2.SS5.SSS1.Px1.p8.m16" class="ltx_Math" alttext="8" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mn>8</mn><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">8</annotation></semantics></math>-subset <math id="A2.SS5.SSS1.Px1.p8.m17" class="ltx_Math" alttext="U" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>U</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">U</annotation></semantics></math> meets <math id="A2.SS5.SSS1.Px1.p8.m18" class="ltx_Math" alttext="L,R" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>L</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>R</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">L,R</annotation></semantics></math> in sizes <math id="A2.SS5.SSS1.Px1.p8.m19" class="ltx_Math" alttext="a,b" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>a</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>b</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">a,b</annotation></semantics></math> with <math id="A2.SS5.SSS1.Px1.p8.m20" class="ltx_Math" alttext="a+b=8" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>a</mi><mo>+</mo><mi>b</mi></mrow><mo>=</mo><mn>8</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">a+b=8</annotation></semantics></math>, the worst case is <math id="A2.SS5.SSS1.Px1.p8.m21" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(a,b)=(4,4)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>a</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>b</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>4</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>4</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(a,b)=(4,4)</annotation></semantics></math>; the constraint <math id="A2.SS5.SSS1.Px1.p8.m22" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(*)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">∗</mo><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(*)</annotation></semantics></math> therefore guarantees <math id="A2.SS5.SSS1.Px1.p8.m23" class="ltx_Math" alttext="e_{G}(U)\leq 15" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>e</mi><mi>G</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>U</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mn>15</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">e_{G}(U)\leq 15</annotation></semantics></math> for all <math id="A2.SS5.SSS1.Px1.p8.m24" class="ltx_Math" alttext="U" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>U</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">U</annotation></semantics></math>.</span></p>
</div>
<div id="A2.SS5.SSS1.Px1.p9" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A2.SS5.SSS1.Px1.p9.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.SS5.SSS1.Px1.p9.1.1" class="ltx_text">A feasible integer matrix <math id="A2.SS5.SSS1.Px1.p9.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(w_{\ell r})_{\ell\in L,\,r\in R}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>w</mi><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>r</mi></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mrow><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo>∈</mo><mi>L</mi></mrow><mo rspace="0.337em">,</mo><mrow><mi>r</mi><mo>∈</mo><mi>R</mi></mrow></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(w_{\ell r})_{\ell\in L,\,r\in R}</annotation></semantics></math> with total sum <math id="A2.SS5.SSS1.Px1.p9.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="56" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mn>56</mn><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">56</annotation></semantics></math> and property <math id="A2.SS5.SSS1.Px1.p9.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(*)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">∗</mo><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(*)</annotation></semantics></math> exists; for example, one can start from the all-ones <math id="A2.SS5.SSS1.Px1.p9.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="7\times 8" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mn>7</mn><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><mn>8</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">7\times 8</annotation></semantics></math> matrix and
<em id="A2.SS5.SSS1.Px1.p9.1.1.1" class="ltx_emph ltx_font_italic">(i)</em> delete a small hitting set of entries so that every <math id="A2.SS5.SSS1.Px1.p9.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="4\times 4" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mn>4</mn><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><mn>4</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">4\times 4</annotation></semantics></math> submatrix loses at least one unit (bringing each such sub-sum down to <math id="A2.SS5.SSS1.Px1.p9.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\leq 15" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>≤</mo><mn>15</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\leq 15</annotation></semantics></math>), and then
<em id="A2.SS5.SSS1.Px1.p9.1.1.2" class="ltx_emph ltx_font_italic">(ii)</em> add the same number of units back at carefully chosen positions so that no <math id="A2.SS5.SSS1.Px1.p9.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="4\times 4" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mn>4</mn><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><mn>4</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">4\times 4</annotation></semantics></math> submatrix receives more than one of these additions.
This yields an explicit integer matrix with total sum <math id="A2.SS5.SSS1.Px1.p9.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="56" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mn>56</mn><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">56</annotation></semantics></math> satisfying <math id="A2.SS5.SSS1.Px1.p9.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(*)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">∗</mo><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(*)</annotation></semantics></math>, hence a family <math id="A2.SS5.SSS1.Px1.p9.m10" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{F}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℱ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{F}</annotation></semantics></math> with no triple intersection and with every <math id="A2.SS5.SSS1.Px1.p9.m11" class="ltx_Math" alttext="7" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mn>7</mn><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">7</annotation></semantics></math>-union of size at least <math id="A2.SS5.SSS1.Px1.p9.m12" class="ltx_Math" alttext="41" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mn>41</mn><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">41</annotation></semantics></math>.</span></p>
</div>
<div id="A2.SS5.SSS1.Px1.p10" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A2.SS5.SSS1.Px1.p10.1" class="ltx_p"><em id="A2.SS5.SSS1.Px1.p10.1.1" class="ltx_emph ltx_font_italic">Remark.</em><span id="A2.SS5.SSS1.Px1.p10.1.2" class="ltx_text"> An explicit <math id="A2.SS5.SSS1.Px1.p10.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="7\times 8" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mn>7</mn><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><mn>8</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">7\times 8</annotation></semantics></math> table of weights <math id="A2.SS5.SSS1.Px1.p10.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(w_{\ell r})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>w</mi><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>r</mi></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(w_{\ell r})</annotation></semantics></math> meeting <math id="A2.SS5.SSS1.Px1.p10.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(*)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">∗</mo><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(*)</annotation></semantics></math> (hence giving a fully concrete <math id="A2.SS5.SSS1.Px1.p10.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="41" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mn>41</mn><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">41</annotation></semantics></math>-tight example) can be produced by a short computer-assisted search (or by a hand-crafted covering design) and verified directly; we omit the bulky incidence table here for brevity.
1
∎</span></p>
</div>
</div>
<div id="A2.SS5.SSS1.Px1.2" class="ltx_proof">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_font_italic ltx_title_proof"><span id="A2.SS5.SSS1.Px1.2.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Standard Solution</span>.</h6>
<div id="A2.SS5.SSS1.Px1.p11" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A2.SS5.SSS1.Px1.p11.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.SS5.SSS1.Px1.p11.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Step 1: Prove that <math id="A2.SS5.SSS1.Px1.p11.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="n=41" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>41</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">n=41</annotation></semantics></math> satisfies the condition.<span id="A2.SS5.SSS1.Px1.p11.1.1.1" class="ltx_text"></span></span></p>
</div>
<div id="A2.SS5.SSS1.Px1.p12" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A2.SS5.SSS1.Px1.p12.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.SS5.SSS1.Px1.p12.1.1" class="ltx_text">We use proof by contradiction.</span></p>
</div>
<div id="A2.SS5.SSS1.Px1.p13" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A2.SS5.SSS1.Px1.p13.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.SS5.SSS1.Px1.p13.1.1" class="ltx_text">Assume there exist 15 subsets of a 56-element set <math id="A2.SS5.SSS1.Px1.p13.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="X" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>X</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">X</annotation></semantics></math>, such that the union of any 7 of them contains at least 41 elements, but the intersection of any 3 of them is empty.</span></p>
</div>
<div id="A2.SS5.SSS1.Px1.p14" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A2.SS5.SSS1.Px1.p14.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.SS5.SSS1.Px1.p14.1.1" class="ltx_text">Since each element belongs to at most 2 subsets (otherwise some 3 subsets would have non-empty intersection), we may assume that each element belongs to exactly 2 subsets (otherwise we can add some elements to subsets without violating the assumptions).</span></p>
</div>
<div id="A2.SS5.SSS1.Px1.p15" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A2.SS5.SSS1.Px1.p15.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.SS5.SSS1.Px1.p15.1.1" class="ltx_text">By the pigeonhole principle, there exists a subset, say <math id="A2.SS5.SSS1.Px1.p15.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="A" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>A</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">A</annotation></semantics></math>, that contains at least</span></p>
<table id="A2.Ex166" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A2.Ex166.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\left\lfloor\frac{2\times 56}{15}\right\rfloor+1=8" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mo>⌊</mo><mfrac><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><mn>56</mn></mrow><mn>15</mn></mfrac><mo>⌋</mo></mrow><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo>=</mo><mn>8</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\left\lfloor\frac{2\times 56}{15}\right\rfloor+1=8</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A2.SS5.SSS1.Px1.p15.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.SS5.SSS1.Px1.p15.2.1" class="ltx_text">elements. Let the remaining 14 subsets be denoted <math id="A2.SS5.SSS1.Px1.p15.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="A_{1},A_{2},\ldots,A_{14}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>A</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>A</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>A</mi><mn>14</mn></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">A_{1},A_{2},\ldots,A_{14}</annotation></semantics></math>.</span></p>
</div>
<div id="A2.SS5.SSS1.Px1.p16" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A2.SS5.SSS1.Px1.p16.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.SS5.SSS1.Px1.p16.1.1" class="ltx_text">Consider any 7-subset group from the 14 subsets excluding <math id="A2.SS5.SSS1.Px1.p16.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="A" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>A</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">A</annotation></semantics></math>. Each such group contains at least 41 elements, so the total number of counted elements over all such 7-subset groups is at least</span></p>
<table id="A2.Ex167" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A2.Ex167.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="41\binom{14}{7}." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mn>41</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mfrac linethickness="0pt"><mn>14</mn><mn>7</mn></mfrac><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">41\binom{14}{7}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
<div id="A2.SS5.SSS1.Px1.p17" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A2.SS5.SSS1.Px1.p17.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.SS5.SSS1.Px1.p17.1.1" class="ltx_text">On the other hand, for an element <math id="A2.SS5.SSS1.Px1.p17.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="a\notin A" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>a</mi><mo>∉</mo><mi>A</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">a\notin A</annotation></semantics></math>, since it belongs to 2 of the <math id="A2.SS5.SSS1.Px1.p17.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="A_{1},\ldots,A_{14}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>A</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>A</mi><mn>14</mn></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">A_{1},\ldots,A_{14}</annotation></semantics></math>, it is counted</span></p>
<table id="A2.Ex168" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A2.Ex168.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\binom{14}{7}-\binom{12}{7}" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mo>(</mo><mfrac linethickness="0pt"><mn>14</mn><mn>7</mn></mfrac><mo>)</mo></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mfrac linethickness="0pt"><mn>12</mn><mn>7</mn></mfrac><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\binom{14}{7}-\binom{12}{7}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A2.SS5.SSS1.Px1.p17.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.SS5.SSS1.Px1.p17.2.1" class="ltx_text">times (i.e., all 7-subsets of the 14 that include at least one of the 2 subsets containing <math id="A2.SS5.SSS1.Px1.p17.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="a" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>a</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">a</annotation></semantics></math>).</span></p>
</div>
<div id="A2.SS5.SSS1.Px1.p18" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A2.SS5.SSS1.Px1.p18.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.SS5.SSS1.Px1.p18.1.1" class="ltx_text">For an element <math id="A2.SS5.SSS1.Px1.p18.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="a\in A" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>a</mi><mo>∈</mo><mi>A</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">a\in A</annotation></semantics></math>, it belongs to only 1 of the <math id="A2.SS5.SSS1.Px1.p18.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="A_{1},\ldots,A_{14}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>A</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>A</mi><mn>14</mn></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">A_{1},\ldots,A_{14}</annotation></semantics></math>, so it is counted</span></p>
<table id="A2.Ex169" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A2.Ex169.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\binom{14}{7}-\binom{13}{7}" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mo>(</mo><mfrac linethickness="0pt"><mn>14</mn><mn>7</mn></mfrac><mo>)</mo></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mfrac linethickness="0pt"><mn>13</mn><mn>7</mn></mfrac><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\binom{14}{7}-\binom{13}{7}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A2.SS5.SSS1.Px1.p18.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.SS5.SSS1.Px1.p18.2.1" class="ltx_text">times.</span></p>
</div>
<div id="A2.SS5.SSS1.Px1.p19" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A2.SS5.SSS1.Px1.p19.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.SS5.SSS1.Px1.p19.1.1" class="ltx_text">Thus, we have:</span></p>
<table id="A2.Ex170" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A2.Ex170X"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A2.Ex170X.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle 41\binom{14}{7}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mn>41</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac linethickness="0pt"><mn>14</mn><mn>7</mn></mfrac></mstyle><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle 41\binom{14}{7}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A2.Ex170X.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\leq(56-|A|)\left(\binom{14}{7}-\binom{12}{7}\right)+|A|\left(\binom{14}{7}-\binom{13}{7}\right)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>56</mn><mo>−</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mi>A</mi><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mrow><mo>(</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac linethickness="0pt"><mn>14</mn><mn>7</mn></mfrac></mstyle><mo>)</mo></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac linethickness="0pt"><mn>12</mn><mn>7</mn></mfrac></mstyle><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mi>A</mi><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mrow><mo>(</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac linethickness="0pt"><mn>14</mn><mn>7</mn></mfrac></mstyle><mo>)</mo></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac linethickness="0pt"><mn>13</mn><mn>7</mn></mfrac></mstyle><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\leq(56-|A|)\left(\binom{14}{7}-\binom{12}{7}\right)+|A|\left(\binom{14}{7}-\binom{13}{7}\right)</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A2.Ex170Xa"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A2.Ex170Xa.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=56\left(\binom{14}{7}-\binom{12}{7}\right)-|A|\left(\binom{13}{7}-\binom{12}{7}\right)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mn>56</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mrow><mo>(</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac linethickness="0pt"><mn>14</mn><mn>7</mn></mfrac></mstyle><mo>)</mo></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac linethickness="0pt"><mn>12</mn><mn>7</mn></mfrac></mstyle><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mi>A</mi><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mrow><mo>(</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac linethickness="0pt"><mn>13</mn><mn>7</mn></mfrac></mstyle><mo>)</mo></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac linethickness="0pt"><mn>12</mn><mn>7</mn></mfrac></mstyle><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=56\left(\binom{14}{7}-\binom{12}{7}\right)-|A|\left(\binom{13}{7}-\binom{12}{7}\right)</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A2.Ex170Xb"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A2.Ex170Xb.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\leq 56\left(\binom{14}{7}-\binom{12}{7}\right)-8\left(\binom{13}{7}-\binom{12}{7}\right)." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mrow><mn>56</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mrow><mo>(</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac linethickness="0pt"><mn>14</mn><mn>7</mn></mfrac></mstyle><mo>)</mo></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac linethickness="0pt"><mn>12</mn><mn>7</mn></mfrac></mstyle><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mn>8</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mrow><mo>(</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac linethickness="0pt"><mn>13</mn><mn>7</mn></mfrac></mstyle><mo>)</mo></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac linethickness="0pt"><mn>12</mn><mn>7</mn></mfrac></mstyle><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\leq 56\left(\binom{14}{7}-\binom{12}{7}\right)-8\left(\binom{13}{7}-\binom{12}{7}\right).</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
<div id="A2.SS5.SSS1.Px1.p20" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A2.SS5.SSS1.Px1.p20.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.SS5.SSS1.Px1.p20.1.1" class="ltx_text">This leads to a contradiction because numerically we would get <math id="A2.SS5.SSS1.Px1.p20.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="196\leq 195" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mn>196</mn><mo>≤</mo><mn>195</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">196\leq 195</annotation></semantics></math>, which is false.</span></p>
</div>
<div id="A2.SS5.SSS1.Px1.p21" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A2.SS5.SSS1.Px1.p21.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.SS5.SSS1.Px1.p21.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Step 2: Prove that <math id="A2.SS5.SSS1.Px1.p21.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="n\geq 41" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>≥</mo><mn>41</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">n\geq 41</annotation></semantics></math>.<span id="A2.SS5.SSS1.Px1.p21.1.1.1" class="ltx_text"></span></span></p>
</div>
<div id="A2.SS5.SSS1.Px1.p22" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A2.SS5.SSS1.Px1.p22.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.SS5.SSS1.Px1.p22.1.1" class="ltx_text">Again, we use proof by contradiction.</span></p>
</div>
<div id="A2.SS5.SSS1.Px1.p23" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A2.SS5.SSS1.Px1.p23.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.SS5.SSS1.Px1.p23.1.1" class="ltx_text">Suppose <math id="A2.SS5.SSS1.Px1.p23.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="n\leq 40" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>≤</mo><mn>40</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">n\leq 40</annotation></semantics></math>. Let <math id="A2.SS5.SSS1.Px1.p23.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="X=\{1,2,\ldots,56\}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>X</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>2</mn><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>,</mo><mn>56</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">X=\{1,2,\ldots,56\}</annotation></semantics></math>, and define the following 15 subsets:</span></p>
</div>
<div id="A2.SS5.SSS1.Px1.p24" class="ltx_para">
<table id="A2.Ex171" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A2.Ex171X"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A2.Ex171X.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle A_{i}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>A</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle A_{i}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A2.Ex171X.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=\{i,i+7,i+14,i+21,i+28,i+35,i+42,i+49\},\quad i=1,2,\ldots,7," display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo>=</mo><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mi>i</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>i</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>7</mn><mo>,</mo><mi>i</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>14</mn><mo>,</mo><mi>i</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>21</mn><mo>,</mo><mi>i</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>28</mn><mo>,</mo><mi>i</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>35</mn><mo>,</mo><mi>i</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>42</mn><mo>,</mo><mi>i</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>49</mn><mo stretchy="false">}</mo><mo rspace="1.167em">,</mo><mi>i</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>2</mn><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>,</mo><mn>7</mn><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\{i,i+7,i+14,i+21,i+28,i+35,i+42,i+49\},\quad i=1,2,\ldots,7,</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A2.Ex171Xa"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A2.Ex171Xa.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle B_{j}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>B</mi><mi>j</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle B_{j}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A2.Ex171Xa.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=\{j,j+8,j+16,j+24,j+32,j+40,j+48\},\quad j=1,2,\ldots,8." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo>=</mo><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mi>j</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>j</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>8</mn><mo>,</mo><mi>j</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>16</mn><mo>,</mo><mi>j</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>24</mn><mo>,</mo><mi>j</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>32</mn><mo>,</mo><mi>j</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>40</mn><mo>,</mo><mi>j</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>48</mn><mo stretchy="false">}</mo><mo rspace="1.167em">,</mo><mi>j</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>2</mn><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>,</mo><mn>8</mn><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\{j,j+8,j+16,j+24,j+32,j+40,j+48\},\quad j=1,2,\ldots,8.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
<div id="A2.SS5.SSS1.Px1.p25" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A2.SS5.SSS1.Px1.p25.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.SS5.SSS1.Px1.p25.1.1" class="ltx_text">Clearly,</span></p>
<table id="A2.Ex172" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A2.Ex172.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="|A_{i}|=8\quad(1\leq i\leq 7),\qquad|A_{i}\cap A_{j}|=0\quad(i\neq j)," display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><msub><mi>A</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow><mo>=</mo><mn>8</mn></mrow><mspace style="width:1em;" width="1em"></mspace><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>≤</mo><mi>i</mi><mo>≤</mo><mn>7</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo rspace="2.167em">,</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mrow><msub><mi>A</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>∩</mo><msub><mi>A</mi><mi>j</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><mspace style="width:1em;" width="1em"></mspace><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>≠</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">|A_{i}|=8\quad(1\leq i\leq 7),\qquad|A_{i}\cap A_{j}|=0\quad(i\neq j),</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<table id="A2.Ex173" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A2.Ex173.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="|B_{j}|=7\quad(1\leq j\leq 8),\qquad|B_{i}\cap B_{j}|=0\quad(i\neq j)," display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><msub><mi>B</mi><mi>j</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow><mo>=</mo><mn>7</mn></mrow><mspace style="width:1em;" width="1em"></mspace><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>≤</mo><mi>j</mi><mo>≤</mo><mn>8</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo rspace="2.167em">,</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mrow><msub><mi>B</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>∩</mo><msub><mi>B</mi><mi>j</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><mspace style="width:1em;" width="1em"></mspace><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>≠</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">|B_{j}|=7\quad(1\leq j\leq 8),\qquad|B_{i}\cap B_{j}|=0\quad(i\neq j),</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<table id="A2.Ex174" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A2.Ex174.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="|A_{i}\cap B_{j}|=1\quad\text{for all }i,j." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mrow><msub><mi>A</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>∩</mo><msub><mi>B</mi><mi>j</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mspace style="width:1em;" width="1em"></mspace><mrow><mtext>for all </mtext><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>i</mi></mrow><mo>,</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">|A_{i}\cap B_{j}|=1\quad\text{for all }i,j.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
<div id="A2.SS5.SSS1.Px1.p26" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A2.SS5.SSS1.Px1.p26.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.SS5.SSS1.Px1.p26.1.1" class="ltx_text">So, for any 3 subsets, at least two of them are both <math id="A2.SS5.SSS1.Px1.p26.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="A" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>A</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">A</annotation></semantics></math>-type or both <math id="A2.SS5.SSS1.Px1.p26.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="B" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>B</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">B</annotation></semantics></math>-type subsets, whose intersection is empty. Thus, the intersection of any 3 subsets is empty.</span></p>
</div>
<div id="A2.SS5.SSS1.Px1.p27" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A2.SS5.SSS1.Px1.p27.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.SS5.SSS1.Px1.p27.1.1" class="ltx_text">Now consider any 7 subsets among the 15, say <math id="A2.SS5.SSS1.Px1.p27.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="A_{i_{1}},A_{i_{2}},\ldots,A_{i_{s}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>A</mi><msub><mi>i</mi><mn>1</mn></msub></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>A</mi><msub><mi>i</mi><mn>2</mn></msub></msub><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>A</mi><msub><mi>i</mi><mi>s</mi></msub></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">A_{i_{1}},A_{i_{2}},\ldots,A_{i_{s}}</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="A2.SS5.SSS1.Px1.p27.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="B_{j_{1}},B_{j_{2}},\ldots,B_{j_{t}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>B</mi><msub><mi>j</mi><mn>1</mn></msub></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>B</mi><msub><mi>j</mi><mn>2</mn></msub></msub><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>B</mi><msub><mi>j</mi><mi>t</mi></msub></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">B_{j_{1}},B_{j_{2}},\ldots,B_{j_{t}}</annotation></semantics></math> with <math id="A2.SS5.SSS1.Px1.p27.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="s+t=7" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>s</mi><mo>+</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow><mo>=</mo><mn>7</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">s+t=7</annotation></semantics></math>. The size of their union is:</span></p>
</div>
<div id="A2.SS5.SSS1.Px1.p28" class="ltx_para">
<table id="A2.Ex175" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A2.Ex175X"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A2.Ex175X.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\left|A_{i_{1}}\cup\cdots\cup A_{i_{s}}\cup B_{j_{1}}\cup\cdots\cup B_{j_{t}}\right|" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo>|</mo><mrow><msub><mi>A</mi><msub><mi>i</mi><mn>1</mn></msub></msub><mo>∪</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">⋯</mo><mo>∪</mo><msub><mi>A</mi><msub><mi>i</mi><mi>s</mi></msub></msub><mo>∪</mo><msub><mi>B</mi><msub><mi>j</mi><mn>1</mn></msub></msub><mo>∪</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">⋯</mo><mo>∪</mo><msub><mi>B</mi><msub><mi>j</mi><mi>t</mi></msub></msub></mrow><mo>|</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\left|A_{i_{1}}\cup\cdots\cup A_{i_{s}}\cup B_{j_{1}}\cup\cdots\cup B_{j_{t}}\right|</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A2.Ex175X.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=8s+7t-st" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mrow><mn>8</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>s</mi></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mn>7</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>s</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=8s+7t-st</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A2.Ex175Xa"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A2.Ex175Xa.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=8s+7(7-s)-s(7-s)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mrow><mn>8</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>s</mi></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mn>7</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>7</mn><mo>−</mo><mi>s</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>s</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>7</mn><mo>−</mo><mi>s</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=8s+7(7-s)-s(7-s)</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A2.Ex175Xb"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A2.Ex175Xb.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=(s-3)^{2}+40" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>s</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>3</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>+</mo><mn>40</mn></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=(s-3)^{2}+40</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A2.Ex175Xc"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A2.Ex175Xc.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\geq 40." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>≥</mo><mn>40</mn></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\geq 40.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
<div id="A2.SS5.SSS1.Px1.p29" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A2.SS5.SSS1.Px1.p29.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.SS5.SSS1.Px1.p29.1.1" class="ltx_text">Hence, the union of any 7 subsets contains at least 40 elements, and the intersection of any 3 subsets is empty, so <math id="A2.SS5.SSS1.Px1.p29.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="n\geq 41" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>≥</mo><mn>41</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">n\geq 41</annotation></semantics></math>.</span></p>
</div>
<div id="A2.SS5.SSS1.Px1.p30" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A2.SS5.SSS1.Px1.p30.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.SS5.SSS1.Px1.p30.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Conclusion:<span id="A2.SS5.SSS1.Px1.p30.1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_medium"> The minimum value of <math id="A2.SS5.SSS1.Px1.p30.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="n" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>n</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">n</annotation></semantics></math> is <math id="A2.SS5.SSS1.Px1.p30.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\boxed{41}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><menclose notation="box"><mn>41</mn></menclose><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\boxed{41}</annotation></semantics></math>.</span></span></p>
</div>
<div id="A2.SS5.SSS1.Px1.p31" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A2.SS5.SSS1.Px1.p31.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.SS5.SSS1.Px1.p31.1.1" class="ltx_text">∎</span></p>
</div>
</div>
<div id="A2.SS5.SSS1.Px1.p32" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent"><span class="ltx_inline-block"><svg id="A2.SS5.SSS1.Px1.p32.pic1" class="ltx_picture" height="67.47" overflow="visible" version="1.1" viewBox="0 0 429.64 67.47" width="429.64"><g style="--ltx-stroke-color:#000000;--ltx-fill-color:#000000;" fill="#000000" stroke="#000000" stroke-width="0.4pt" transform="translate(0,67.47) matrix(1 0 0 -1 0 0)"><g style="--ltx-fill-color:#4D4D4D;" fill="#4D4D4D" fill-opacity="1.0"><path style="stroke:none" d="M 0 4.63 L 0 62.84 C 0 65.4 2.07 67.47 4.63 67.47 L 425.01 67.47 C 427.56 67.47 429.64 65.4 429.64 62.84 L 429.64 4.63 C 429.64 2.07 427.56 0 425.01 0 L 4.63 0 C 2.07 0 0 2.07 0 4.63 Z"></path></g><g style="--ltx-fill-color:#F9F9F9;" fill="#F9F9F9" fill-opacity="1.0"><path style="stroke:none" d="M 0.69 4.63 L 0.69 48.61 L 428.94 48.61 L 428.94 4.63 C 428.94 2.45 427.18 0.69 425.01 0.69 L 4.63 0.69 C 2.45 0.69 0.69 2.45 0.69 4.63 Z"></path></g><g fill-opacity="1.0" transform="matrix(1.0 0.0 0.0 1.0 20.38 53.23)"><foreignObject style="--ltx-fo-width:24.44em;--ltx-fo-height:0.69em;--ltx-fo-depth:0em;font-size:10pt;" height="9.61" overflow="visible" transform="matrix(1 0 0 -1 0 9.61)" width="338.18"><span class="ltx_foreignobject_container"><span class="ltx_foreignobject_content">
