</section>
<section id="A2.SS5.SSS2.Px2" class="ltx_paragraph">
<h5 class="ltx_title ltx_title_paragraph" style="--ltx-fg-color:#00E000;">Problem 5b2 </h5>

<div id="A2.SS5.SSS2.Px2.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A2.SS5.SSS2.Px2.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.SS5.SSS2.Px2.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text"></span>
<br class="ltx_break" style="--ltx-break-space:-10.0pt;"></p>
</div>
<div id="A2.SS5.SSS2.Px2.p2" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent"><span class="ltx_inline-block"><svg id="A2.SS5.SSS2.Px2.p2.pic1" class="ltx_picture" height="234.18" overflow="visible" version="1.1" viewBox="0 0 429.64 234.18" width="429.64"><g style="--ltx-stroke-color:#000000;--ltx-fill-color:#000000;" fill="#000000" stroke="#000000" stroke-width="0.4pt" transform="translate(0,234.18) matrix(1 0 0 -1 0 0)"><g style="--ltx-fill-color:#3D6666;" fill="#3D6666" fill-opacity="1.0"><path style="stroke:none" d="M 0 4.63 L 0 229.55 C 0 232.11 2.07 234.18 4.63 234.18 L 425.01 234.18 C 427.56 234.18 429.64 232.11 429.64 229.55 L 429.64 4.63 C 429.64 2.07 427.56 0 425.01 0 L 4.63 0 C 2.07 0 0 2.07 0 4.63 Z"></path></g><g style="--ltx-fill-color:#F9F9F9;" fill="#F9F9F9" fill-opacity="1.0"><path style="stroke:none" d="M 0.69 4.63 L 0.69 215.32 L 428.94 215.32 L 428.94 4.63 C 428.94 2.45 427.18 0.69 425.01 0.69 L 4.63 0.69 C 2.45 0.69 0.69 2.45 0.69 4.63 Z"></path></g><g fill-opacity="1.0" transform="matrix(1.0 0.0 0.0 1.0 20.38 219.95)"><foreignObject style="--ltx-fo-width:24.44em;--ltx-fo-height:0.69em;--ltx-fo-depth:0em;font-size:10pt;" height="9.61" overflow="visible" transform="matrix(1 0 0 -1 0 9.61)" width="338.18"><span class="ltx_foreignobject_container"><span class="ltx_foreignobject_content">
<span id="A2.SS5.SSS2.Px2.p2.pic1.1" class="ltx_inline-block ltx_minipage ltx_align_bottom" style="width:24.44em;">
<span id="A2.SS5.SSS2.Px2.p2.pic1.1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.SS5.SSS2.Px2.p2.pic1.1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold" style="--ltx-fg-color:#FFFFFF;">Problem</span></span>
</span></span></span></foreignObject></g><g fill-opacity="1.0" transform="matrix(1.0 0.0 0.0 1.0 20.38 14.66)"><foreignObject style="--ltx-fo-width:32.01em;--ltx-fo-height:13.65em;--ltx-fo-depth:0.16em;font-size:10pt;" height="191" overflow="visible" transform="matrix(1 0 0 -1 0 188.85)" width="442.93"><span class="ltx_foreignobject_container"><span class="ltx_foreignobject_content">
<span id="A2.SS5.SSS2.Px2.p2.pic1.2" class="ltx_inline-block ltx_minipage ltx_align_bottom" style="width:32.01em;">
<span id="A2.SS5.SSS2.Px2.p2.pic1.2.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.SS5.SSS2.Px2.p2.pic1.2.1.1" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:80%;--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">Check the proof: A friend of mine came up with this proof that all perfect numbers are even. A little more advanced than your usual fake proof that <math id="A2.SS5.SSS2.Px2.p2.pic1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="0=1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">0</mn><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">=</mo><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">1</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">0=1</annotation></semantics></math>.</span></span>
<span id="A2.SS5.SSS2.Px2.p2.pic1.2.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.SS5.SSS2.Px2.p2.pic1.2.2.1" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:80%;--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">Assume</span></span>
<span id="A2.Ex182" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<span><span class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<span class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></span>
<span class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A2.Ex182.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="2n=\sum_{d\mid n}d" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" mathsize="0.800em">2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" mathsize="0.800em">n</mi></mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" mathsize="0.800em" rspace="0.111em">=</mo><mrow><munder><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" maxsize="0.800em" minsize="0.800em" movablelimits="false" stretchy="true">∑</mo><mrow><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" mathsize="0.800em">d</mi><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" fence="false" mathcolor="#000000">|</mo><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" mathsize="0.800em">n</mi></mrow></munder><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" mathsize="0.800em">d</mi></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">2n=\sum_{d\mid n}d</annotation></semantics></math></span>
<span class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></span></span></span>
</span>
<span id="A2.SS5.SSS2.Px2.p2.pic1.2.3" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.SS5.SSS2.Px2.p2.pic1.2.3.1" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:80%;--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">Then by Möbius inversion:</span></span>
<span id="A2.Ex183" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<span><span class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<span class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></span>
<span class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A2.Ex183.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="n=\sum_{d\mid n}2d\cdot\mu\left(\frac{n}{d}\right)" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" mathsize="0.800em">n</mi><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" mathsize="0.800em" rspace="0.111em">=</mo><mrow><mrow><munder><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" maxsize="0.800em" minsize="0.800em" movablelimits="false" stretchy="true">∑</mo><mrow><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" mathsize="0.800em">d</mi><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" fence="false" mathcolor="#000000">|</mo><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" mathsize="0.800em">n</mi></mrow></munder><mrow><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" mathsize="0.800em">2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" mathsize="0.800em">d</mi></mrow></mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" lspace="0.222em" mathcolor="#000000" mathsize="0.800em" rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><mrow><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" mathsize="0.800em">μ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">(</mo><mfrac style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000"><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" mathsize="0.800em">n</mi><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" mathsize="0.800em">d</mi></mfrac><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">n=\sum_{d\mid n}2d\cdot\mu\left(\frac{n}{d}\right)</annotation></semantics></math></span>
<span class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></span></span></span>
</span>
<span id="A2.SS5.SSS2.Px2.p2.pic1.2.4" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.SS5.SSS2.Px2.p2.pic1.2.4.1" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:80%;--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">and therefore <math id="A2.SS5.SSS2.Px2.p2.pic1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="n" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">n</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">n</annotation></semantics></math> is even.</span></span><span class="ltx_inline-block"><svg id="A2.SS5.SSS2.Px2.p2.pic1.pic1" class="ltx_picture" color="#008000" height="18.24" overflow="visible" style="vertical-align:-4.1px" version="1.1" viewBox="0 0 18.24 18.24" width="18.24"><g style="--ltx-stroke-color:#009900;--ltx-fill-color:#009900;--ltx-fg-color:#009900;" color="#009900" fill="#009900" stroke="#009900" stroke-width="1.8pt" transform="translate(0,18.24) matrix(1 0 0 -1 0 0) translate(1.25,0) translate(0,1.25)"><path style="fill:none" d="M 0 7.87 L 5.51 0 L 15.75 15.75"></path></g></svg></span>
<span id="A2.SS5.SSS2.Px2.p2.pic1.2.5" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.SS5.SSS2.Px2.p2.pic1.2.5.1" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:80%;--ltx-fg-color:#008000;">GPT-5 thinking passed</span></span>
<span id="A2.SS5.SSS2.Px2.p2.pic1.2.6" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.SS5.SSS2.Px2.p2.pic1.2.6.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic" style="font-size:80%;--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">Proposed by Jiaxin Zhang</span></span>
</span></span></span></foreignObject></g></g></svg></span>
</div>
<div id="A2.SS5.SSS2.Px2.1" class="ltx_proof">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_font_italic ltx_title_proof"><span id="A2.SS5.SSS2.Px2.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Response of GPT-5-thinking</span>.</h6>
<div id="Thmclaim2" class="ltx_theorem ltx_theorem_claim">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_title_theorem"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_theorem"><span id="Thmclaim2.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Claim 2</span></span><span id="Thmclaim2.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">.</span></h6>
<div id="Thmclaim2.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="Thmclaim2.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="Thmclaim2.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">The proposed proof is incorrect; in fact, the existence of odd perfect numbers is an open problem.</span></p>
</div>
</div>
<div id="A2.SS5.SSS2.Px2.1.2" class="ltx_proof">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_font_italic ltx_title_proof">Proof.</h6>
<div id="A2.SS5.SSS2.Px2.p3" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A2.SS5.SSS2.Px2.p3.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.SS5.SSS2.Px2.p3.1.1" class="ltx_text">Let <math id="A2.SS5.SSS2.Px2.p3.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\sigma(n)=\sum_{d\mid n}d" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>σ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>n</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.111em">=</mo><mrow><msub><mo>∑</mo><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo fence="false">|</mo><mi>n</mi></mrow></msub><mi>d</mi></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\sigma(n)=\sum_{d\mid n}d</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="A2.SS5.SSS2.Px2.p3.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathrm{Id}(n)=n" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>Id</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>n</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mi>n</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathrm{Id}(n)=n</annotation></semantics></math>. As arithmetic functions under Dirichlet convolution <math id="A2.SS5.SSS2.Px2.p3.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(f*g)(n)=\sum_{d\mid n}f(d)g(n/d)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>f</mi><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">∗</mo><mi>g</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>n</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.111em">=</mo><mrow><msub><mo>∑</mo><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo fence="false">|</mo><mi>n</mi></mrow></msub><mrow><mrow><mi>f</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>d</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>g</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>/</mo><mi>d</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(f*g)(n)=\sum_{d\mid n}f(d)g(n/d)</annotation></semantics></math>, we have</span></p>
<table id="A2.Ex184" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A2.Ex184.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\sigma=\mathbf{1}*\mathrm{Id}," display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>σ</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><mn>𝟏</mn><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">∗</mo><mi>Id</mi></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\sigma=\mathbf{1}*\mathrm{Id},</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A2.SS5.SSS2.Px2.p3.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.SS5.SSS2.Px2.p3.2.1" class="ltx_text">where <math id="A2.SS5.SSS2.Px2.p3.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbf{1}(n)\equiv 1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mn>𝟏</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>n</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>≡</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbf{1}(n)\equiv 1</annotation></semantics></math>. Möbius inversion then gives the <em id="A2.SS5.SSS2.Px2.p3.2.1.1" class="ltx_emph ltx_font_italic">functional</em> identity</span></p>
<table id="A2.Ex185" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A2.Ex185.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\mathrm{Id}\;=\;\mu*\sigma\quad\Longleftrightarrow\quad n\;=\;\sum_{d\mid n}\mu\!\left(\frac{n}{d}\right)\sigma(d)\qquad\text{for all }n\geq 1." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>Id</mi><mo lspace="0.558em" rspace="0.558em">=</mo><mi>μ</mi><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">∗</mo><mi>σ</mi><mo stretchy="false">⟺</mo><mi>n</mi><mo lspace="0.558em" rspace="0.391em">=</mo><munder><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo fence="false">|</mo><mi>n</mi></mrow></munder><mpadded style="width:0.433em;" width="0.433em"><mi>μ</mi></mpadded><mrow><mo>(</mo><mfrac><mi>n</mi><mi>d</mi></mfrac><mo>)</mo></mrow><mi>σ</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>d</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mtext>for all </mtext><mi>n</mi><mo>≥</mo><mn>1</mn><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathrm{Id}\;=\;\mu*\sigma\quad\Longleftrightarrow\quad n\;=\;\sum_{d\mid n}\mu\!\left(\frac{n}{d}\right)\sigma(d)\qquad\text{for all }n\geq 1.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
<div id="A2.SS5.SSS2.Px2.p4" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A2.SS5.SSS2.Px2.p4.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.SS5.SSS2.Px2.p4.1.1" class="ltx_text">If <math id="A2.SS5.SSS2.Px2.p4.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="n" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>n</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">n</annotation></semantics></math> is perfect, we have the <em id="A2.SS5.SSS2.Px2.p4.1.1.1" class="ltx_emph ltx_font_italic">numeric</em> equality <math id="A2.SS5.SSS2.Px2.p4.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\sigma(n)=2n" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>σ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>n</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>n</mi></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\sigma(n)=2n</annotation></semantics></math> for that particular <math id="A2.SS5.SSS2.Px2.p4.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="n" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>n</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">n</annotation></semantics></math>.
However, Möbius inversion applies to identities of functions (holding for every input), not to an equality that happens to hold at one value. From <math id="A2.SS5.SSS2.Px2.p4.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\sigma(n)=2n" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>σ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>n</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>n</mi></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\sigma(n)=2n</annotation></semantics></math> you may <em id="A2.SS5.SSS2.Px2.p4.1.1.2" class="ltx_emph ltx_font_italic">not</em> substitute <math id="A2.SS5.SSS2.Px2.p4.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\sigma(d)=2d" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>σ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>d</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>d</mi></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\sigma(d)=2d</annotation></semantics></math> for each divisor <math id="A2.SS5.SSS2.Px2.p4.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="d\mid n" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo fence="false">|</mo><mi>n</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">d\mid n</annotation></semantics></math>; doing so would tacitly assume every divisor <math id="A2.SS5.SSS2.Px2.p4.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="d" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>d</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">d</annotation></semantics></math> of <math id="A2.SS5.SSS2.Px2.p4.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="n" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>n</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">n</annotation></semantics></math> is itself perfect.</span></p>
</div>
<div id="A2.SS5.SSS2.Px2.p5" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A2.SS5.SSS2.Px2.p5.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.SS5.SSS2.Px2.p5.1.1" class="ltx_text">Indeed, if one (incorrectly) made that substitution,</span></p>
<table id="A2.Ex186" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A2.Ex186.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="n\stackrel{{\scriptstyle\phantom{\times}}}{{=}}\sum_{d\mid n}\mu\!\left(\frac{n}{d}\right)\sigma(d)\stackrel{{\scriptstyle\text{(wrong)}}}{{=}}\sum_{d\mid n}\mu\!\left(\frac{n}{d}\right)\,2d=2\sum_{d\mid n}\mu\!\left(\frac{n}{d}\right)d=2\,\varphi(n)," display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>n</mi><mover><mo rspace="0.111em">=</mo><mphantom></mphantom></mover><mrow><munder><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo fence="false">|</mo><mi>n</mi></mrow></munder><mrow><mrow><mpadded style="width:0.433em;" width="0.433em"><mi>μ</mi></mpadded><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mfrac><mi>n</mi><mi>d</mi></mfrac><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>σ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>d</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mover><mo rspace="0.111em">=</mo><mtext>(wrong)</mtext></mover><mrow><munder><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo fence="false">|</mo><mi>n</mi></mrow></munder><mrow><mrow><mpadded style="width:0.433em;" width="0.433em"><mi>μ</mi></mpadded><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mfrac><mi>n</mi><mi>d</mi></mfrac><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mn> 2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>d</mi></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><munder><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo fence="false">|</mo><mi>n</mi></mrow></munder><mrow><mrow><mpadded style="width:0.433em;" width="0.433em"><mi>μ</mi></mpadded><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mfrac><mi>n</mi><mi>d</mi></mfrac><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>d</mi></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>φ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>n</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">n\stackrel{{\scriptstyle\phantom{\times}}}{{=}}\sum_{d\mid n}\mu\!\left(\frac{n}{d}\right)\sigma(d)\stackrel{{\scriptstyle\text{(wrong)}}}{{=}}\sum_{d\mid n}\mu\!\left(\frac{n}{d}\right)\,2d=2\sum_{d\mid n}\mu\!\left(\frac{n}{d}\right)d=2\,\varphi(n),</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A2.SS5.SSS2.Px2.p5.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.SS5.SSS2.Px2.p5.2.1" class="ltx_text">using the standard identity <math id="A2.SS5.SSS2.Px2.p5.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\sum_{d\mid n}\mu(n/d)\,d=\varphi(n)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mo>∑</mo><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo fence="false">|</mo><mi>n</mi></mrow></msub><mrow><mrow><mi>μ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>/</mo><mi>d</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>d</mi></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>φ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>n</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\sum_{d\mid n}\mu(n/d)\,d=\varphi(n)</annotation></semantics></math>. This already contradicts known perfect numbers; for instance, for <math id="A2.SS5.SSS2.Px2.p5.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="n=6" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>6</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">n=6</annotation></semantics></math> we get <math id="A2.SS5.SSS2.Px2.p5.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="2\varphi(6)=4\neq 6" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>φ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>6</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mn>4</mn><mo>≠</mo><mn>6</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">2\varphi(6)=4\neq 6</annotation></semantics></math>.</span></p>
</div>
<div id="A2.SS5.SSS2.Px2.p6" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A2.SS5.SSS2.Px2.p6.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.SS5.SSS2.Px2.p6.1.1" class="ltx_text">Therefore the argument fails because it treats the pointwise equality <math id="A2.SS5.SSS2.Px2.p6.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\sigma(n)=2n" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>σ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>n</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>n</mi></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\sigma(n)=2n</annotation></semantics></math> as if it were the functional identity <math id="A2.SS5.SSS2.Px2.p6.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\sigma=2\,\mathrm{Id}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>σ</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>Id</mi></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\sigma=2\,\mathrm{Id}</annotation></semantics></math>, which it is not.
∎</span></p>
</div>
</div>
<div id="A2.SS5.SSS2.Px2.p7" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A2.SS5.SSS2.Px2.p7.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.SS5.SSS2.Px2.p7.1.1" class="ltx_text">∎</span></p>
</div>
</div>
<div id="A2.SS5.SSS2.Px2.2" class="ltx_proof">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_font_italic ltx_title_proof"><span id="A2.SS5.SSS2.Px2.2.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Standard Solution</span>.</h6>
<div id="A2.SS5.SSS2.Px2.p8" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A2.SS5.SSS2.Px2.p8.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.SS5.SSS2.Px2.p8.1.1" class="ltx_text">You may <em id="A2.SS5.SSS2.Px2.p8.1.1.1" class="ltx_emph ltx_font_italic">not</em> substitute <math id="A2.SS5.SSS2.Px2.p8.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\sigma(d)=2d" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>σ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>d</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>d</mi></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\sigma(d)=2d</annotation></semantics></math> for each divisor <math id="A2.SS5.SSS2.Px2.p8.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="d\mid n" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo fence="false">|</mo><mi>n</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">d\mid n</annotation></semantics></math>; doing so would tacitly assume every divisor <math id="A2.SS5.SSS2.Px2.p8.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="d" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>d</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">d</annotation></semantics></math> of <math id="A2.SS5.SSS2.Px2.p8.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="n" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>n</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">n</annotation></semantics></math> is itself perfect.
∎</span></p>
</div>
</div>
<div id="A2.SS5.SSS2.Px2.p9" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent"><span class="ltx_inline-block"><svg id="A2.SS5.SSS2.Px2.p9.pic1" class="ltx_picture" height="54.25" overflow="visible" version="1.1" viewBox="0 0 429.64 54.25" width="429.64"><g style="--ltx-stroke-color:#000000;--ltx-fill-color:#000000;" fill="#000000" stroke="#000000" stroke-width="0.4pt" transform="translate(0,54.25) matrix(1 0 0 -1 0 0)"><g style="--ltx-fill-color:#4D4D4D;" fill="#4D4D4D" fill-opacity="1.0"><path style="stroke:none" d="M 0 4.63 L 0 49.62 C 0 52.18 2.07 54.25 4.63 54.25 L 425.01 54.25 C 427.56 54.25 429.64 52.18 429.64 49.62 L 429.64 4.63 C 429.64 2.07 427.56 0 425.01 0 L 4.63 0 C 2.07 0 0 2.07 0 4.63 Z"></path></g><g style="--ltx-fill-color:#F9F9F9;" fill="#F9F9F9" fill-opacity="1.0"><path style="stroke:none" d="M 0.69 4.63 L 0.69 35.38 L 428.94 35.38 L 428.94 4.63 C 428.94 2.45 427.18 0.69 425.01 0.69 L 4.63 0.69 C 2.45 0.69 0.69 2.45 0.69 4.63 Z"></path></g><g fill-opacity="1.0" transform="matrix(1.0 0.0 0.0 1.0 20.38 40.01)"><foreignObject style="--ltx-fo-width:24.44em;--ltx-fo-height:0.69em;--ltx-fo-depth:0em;font-size:10pt;" height="9.61" overflow="visible" transform="matrix(1 0 0 -1 0 9.61)" width="338.18"><span class="ltx_foreignobject_container"><span class="ltx_foreignobject_content">
<span id="A2.SS5.SSS2.Px2.p9.pic1.1" class="ltx_inline-block ltx_minipage ltx_align_bottom" style="width:24.44em;">
<span id="A2.SS5.SSS2.Px2.p9.pic1.1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.SS5.SSS2.Px2.p9.pic1.1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold" style="--ltx-fg-color:#FFFFFF;">Rubric</span></span>
</span></span></span></foreignObject></g><g fill-opacity="1.0" transform="matrix(1.0 0.0 0.0 1.0 20.38 15.27)"><foreignObject style="--ltx-fo-width:33.06em;--ltx-fo-height:0.6em;--ltx-fo-depth:0.2em;font-size:10pt;" height="11.07" overflow="visible" transform="matrix(1 0 0 -1 0 8.3)" width="457.46"><span class="ltx_foreignobject_container"><span class="ltx_foreignobject_content">
<span id="A2.SS5.SSS2.Px2.p9.pic1.2" class="ltx_inline-block ltx_minipage ltx_align_bottom" style="width:33.06em;">
<span id="A2.SS5.SSS2.Px2.p9.pic1.2.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.SS5.SSS2.Px2.p9.pic1.2.1.1" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:80%;--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">Got 1 if it finds the error at <math id="A2.SS5.SSS2.Px2.p9.pic1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\sigma(d)=2d" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">σ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" stretchy="false">(</mo><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">d</mi><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">=</mo><mrow><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">d</mi></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\sigma(d)=2d</annotation></semantics></math></span></span>
</span></span></span></foreignObject></g></g></svg></span>
</div>
<div id="A2.SS5.SSS2.Px2.p10" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent"><span class="ltx_inline-block"><svg id="A2.SS5.SSS2.Px2.p10.pic1" class="ltx_picture" height="54.13" overflow="visible" version="1.1" viewBox="0 0 429.64 54.13" width="429.64"><g style="--ltx-stroke-color:#000000;--ltx-fill-color:#000000;" fill="#000000" stroke="#000000" stroke-width="0.4pt" transform="translate(0,54.13) matrix(1 0 0 -1 0 0)"><g style="--ltx-fill-color:#5A996B;" fill="#5A996B" fill-opacity="1.0"><path style="stroke:none" d="M 0 4.63 L 0 49.51 C 0 52.06 2.07 54.13 4.63 54.13 L 425.01 54.13 C 427.56 54.13 429.64 52.06 429.64 49.51 L 429.64 4.63 C 429.64 2.07 427.56 0 425.01 0 L 4.63 0 C 2.07 0 0 2.07 0 4.63 Z"></path></g><g style="--ltx-fill-color:#F6FFF9;" fill="#F6FFF9" fill-opacity="1.0"><path style="stroke:none" d="M 0.69 4.63 L 0.69 35.38 L 428.94 35.38 L 428.94 4.63 C 428.94 2.45 427.18 0.69 425.01 0.69 L 4.63 0.69 C 2.45 0.69 0.69 2.45 0.69 4.63 Z"></path></g><g fill-opacity="1.0" transform="matrix(1.0 0.0 0.0 1.0 20.38 40.01)"><foreignObject style="--ltx-fo-width:24.44em;--ltx-fo-height:0.69em;--ltx-fo-depth:0em;font-size:10pt;" height="9.49" overflow="visible" transform="matrix(1 0 0 -1 0 9.49)" width="338.18"><span class="ltx_foreignobject_container"><span class="ltx_foreignobject_content">
<span id="A2.SS5.SSS2.Px2.p10.pic1.1" class="ltx_inline-block ltx_minipage ltx_align_bottom" style="width:24.44em;">
<span id="A2.SS5.SSS2.Px2.p10.pic1.1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.SS5.SSS2.Px2.p10.pic1.1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold" style="--ltx-fg-color:#FFFFFF;">Score</span></span>
</span></span></span></foreignObject></g><g fill-opacity="1.0" transform="matrix(1.0 0.0 0.0 1.0 20.38 15.27)"><foreignObject style="--ltx-fo-width:33.06em;--ltx-fo-height:0.6em;--ltx-fo-depth:0.2em;font-size:10pt;" height="11.07" overflow="visible" transform="matrix(1 0 0 -1 0 8.3)" width="457.46"><span class="ltx_foreignobject_container"><span class="ltx_foreignobject_content">
<span id="A2.SS5.SSS2.Px2.p10.pic1.2" class="ltx_inline-block ltx_minipage ltx_align_bottom" style="width:33.06em;">
<span id="A2.SS5.SSS2.Px2.p10.pic1.2.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.SS5.SSS2.Px2.p10.pic1.2.1.1" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:80%;--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">1/1</span></span>
</span></span></span></foreignObject></g></g></svg></span>
</div>
<div id="A2.SS5.SSS2.Px2.p11" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent"><span class="ltx_inline-block"><svg id="A2.SS5.SSS2.Px2.p11.pic1" class="ltx_picture" height="53.02" overflow="visible" version="1.1" viewBox="0 0 429.64 53.02" width="429.64"><g style="--ltx-stroke-color:#000000;--ltx-fill-color:#000000;" fill="#000000" stroke="#000000" stroke-width="0.4pt" transform="translate(0,53.02) matrix(1 0 0 -1 0 0)"><g style="--ltx-fill-color:#B33674;" fill="#B33674" fill-opacity="1.0"><path style="stroke:none" d="M 0 4.63 L 0 48.39 C 0 50.95 2.07 53.02 4.63 53.02 L 425.01 53.02 C 427.56 53.02 429.64 50.95 429.64 48.39 L 429.64 4.63 C 429.64 2.07 427.56 0 425.01 0 L 4.63 0 C 2.07 0 0 2.07 0 4.63 Z"></path></g><g style="--ltx-fill-color:#FFF2F9;" fill="#FFF2F9" fill-opacity="1.0"><path style="stroke:none" d="M 0.69 4.63 L 0.69 34.15 L 428.94 34.15 L 428.94 4.63 C 428.94 2.45 427.18 0.69 425.01 0.69 L 4.63 0.69 C 2.45 0.69 0.69 2.45 0.69 4.63 Z"></path></g><g fill-opacity="1.0" transform="matrix(1.0 0.0 0.0 1.0 20.38 38.78)"><foreignObject style="--ltx-fo-width:24.44em;--ltx-fo-height:0.69em;--ltx-fo-depth:0em;font-size:10pt;" height="9.61" overflow="visible" transform="matrix(1 0 0 -1 0 9.61)" width="338.18"><span class="ltx_foreignobject_container"><span class="ltx_foreignobject_content">
<span id="A2.SS5.SSS2.Px2.p11.pic1.1" class="ltx_inline-block ltx_minipage ltx_align_bottom" style="width:24.44em;">
<span id="A2.SS5.SSS2.Px2.p11.pic1.1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.SS5.SSS2.Px2.p11.pic1.1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold" style="--ltx-fg-color:#FFFFFF;">Evaluation</span></span>
</span></span></span></foreignObject></g><g fill-opacity="1.0" transform="matrix(1.0 0.0 0.0 1.0 20.38 14.66)"><foreignObject style="--ltx-fo-width:33.06em;--ltx-fo-height:0.56em;--ltx-fo-depth:0.16em;font-size:10pt;" height="9.84" overflow="visible" transform="matrix(1 0 0 -1 0 7.69)" width="457.46"><span class="ltx_foreignobject_container"><span class="ltx_foreignobject_content">
<span id="A2.SS5.SSS2.Px2.p11.pic1.2" class="ltx_inline-block ltx_minipage ltx_align_bottom" style="width:33.06em;">
<span id="A2.SS5.SSS2.Px2.p11.pic1.2.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.SS5.SSS2.Px2.p11.pic1.2.1.1" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:80%;--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">It accurately found the error in the proof.</span></span>
</span></span></span></foreignObject></g></g></svg></span>
</div>
</section>
</section>
</section>
<section id="A2.SS6" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">6 </span>Writing and Presentation</h3>

<section id="A2.SS6.SSS1" class="ltx_subsubsection">
<h4 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsubsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsubsection">(a) </span>Writing clean structured proofs and definitions</h4>

<section id="A2.SS6.SSS1.Px1" class="ltx_paragraph">
<h5 class="ltx_title ltx_title_paragraph" style="--ltx-fg-color:#00E000;">Problem 6a1</h5>

<div id="A2.SS6.SSS1.Px1.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A2.SS6.SSS1.Px1.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.SS6.SSS1.Px1.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text"></span>
<br class="ltx_break" style="--ltx-break-space:-10.0pt;"></p>
</div>
<div id="A2.SS6.SSS1.Px1.p2" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent"><span class="ltx_inline-block"><svg id="A2.SS6.SSS1.Px1.p2.pic1" class="ltx_picture" height="406.45" overflow="visible" version="1.1" viewBox="0 0 429.64 406.45" width="429.64"><g style="--ltx-stroke-color:#000000;--ltx-fill-color:#000000;" fill="#000000" stroke="#000000" stroke-width="0.4pt" transform="translate(0,406.45) matrix(1 0 0 -1 0 0)"><g style="--ltx-fill-color:#3D6666;" fill="#3D6666" fill-opacity="1.0"><path style="stroke:none" d="M 0 4.63 L 0 401.82 C 0 404.38 2.07 406.45 4.63 406.45 L 425.01 406.45 C 427.56 406.45 429.64 404.38 429.64 401.82 L 429.64 4.63 C 429.64 2.07 427.56 0 425.01 0 L 4.63 0 C 2.07 0 0 2.07 0 4.63 Z"></path></g><g style="--ltx-fill-color:#F9F9F9;" fill="#F9F9F9" fill-opacity="1.0"><path style="stroke:none" d="M 0.69 4.63 L 0.69 387.59 L 428.94 387.59 L 428.94 4.63 C 428.94 2.45 427.18 0.69 425.01 0.69 L 4.63 0.69 C 2.45 0.69 0.69 2.45 0.69 4.63 Z"></path></g><g fill-opacity="1.0" transform="matrix(1.0 0.0 0.0 1.0 20.38 392.21)"><foreignObject style="--ltx-fo-width:24.44em;--ltx-fo-height:0.69em;--ltx-fo-depth:0em;font-size:10pt;" height="9.61" overflow="visible" transform="matrix(1 0 0 -1 0 9.61)" width="338.18"><span class="ltx_foreignobject_container"><span class="ltx_foreignobject_content">
<span id="A2.SS6.SSS1.Px1.p2.pic1.1" class="ltx_inline-block ltx_minipage ltx_align_bottom" style="width:24.44em;">
<span id="A2.SS6.SSS1.Px1.p2.pic1.1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.SS6.SSS1.Px1.p2.pic1.1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold" style="--ltx-fg-color:#FFFFFF;">Problem</span></span>
</span></span></span></foreignObject></g><g fill-opacity="1.0" transform="matrix(1.0 0.0 0.0 1.0 20.38 14.66)"><foreignObject style="--ltx-fo-width:32.01em;--ltx-fo-height:26.1em;--ltx-fo-depth:0.16em;font-size:10pt;" height="363.28" overflow="visible" transform="matrix(1 0 0 -1 0 361.12)" width="442.93"><span class="ltx_foreignobject_container"><span class="ltx_foreignobject_content">
<span id="A2.SS6.SSS1.Px1.p2.pic1.2" class="ltx_inline-block ltx_minipage ltx_align_bottom" style="width:32.01em;">
<span id="A2.SS6.SSS1.Px1.p2.pic1.2.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.SS6.SSS1.Px1.p2.pic1.2.1.1" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:80%;--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">Suppose there are 10000 fish, numbered from 1 to 10000 in increasing size.</span></span>
<span id="A2.SS6.SSS1.Px1.p2.pic1.2.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.SS6.SSS1.Px1.p2.pic1.2.2.1" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:80%;--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">The rules are as follows:</span></span>
<span id="A2.I13" class="ltx_itemize">
<span id="A2.I13.i1" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">•</span> 
<span id="A2.I13.i1.p1" class="ltx_para">
<span id="A2.I13.i1.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.I13.i1.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:80%;--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">A fish can only eat the fish that is exactly one rank smaller than itself (that is, fish </span><math id="A2.I13.i1.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="i" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" mathsize="0.800em">i</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">i</annotation></semantics></math><span id="A2.I13.i1.p1.1.2" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:80%;--ltx-fg-color:#000000;"> can only eat fish </span><math id="A2.I13.i1.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="i-1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" mathsize="0.800em">i</mi><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" mathsize="0.800em">−</mo><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" mathsize="0.800em">1</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">i-1</annotation></semantics></math><span id="A2.I13.i1.p1.1.3" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:80%;--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">).</span></span>
</span></span>
<span id="A2.I13.i2" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">•</span> 
<span id="A2.I13.i2.p1" class="ltx_para">
<span id="A2.I13.i2.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.I13.i2.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:80%;--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">Furthermore, for </span><math id="A2.I13.i2.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="i&gt;1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" mathsize="0.800em">i</mi><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" mathsize="0.800em">&gt;</mo><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" mathsize="0.800em">1</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">i&gt;1</annotation></semantics></math><span id="A2.I13.i2.p1.1.2" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:80%;--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">, fish </span><math id="A2.I13.i2.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="i+1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" mathsize="0.800em">i</mi><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" mathsize="0.800em">+</mo><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" mathsize="0.800em">1</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">i+1</annotation></semantics></math><span id="A2.I13.i2.p1.1.3" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:80%;--ltx-fg-color:#000000;"> can only eat fish </span><math id="A2.I13.i2.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="i" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" mathsize="0.800em">i</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">i</annotation></semantics></math><span id="A2.I13.i2.p1.1.4" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:80%;--ltx-fg-color:#000000;"> after fish </span><math id="A2.I13.i2.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="i" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" mathsize="0.800em">i</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">i</annotation></semantics></math><span id="A2.I13.i2.p1.1.5" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:80%;--ltx-fg-color:#000000;"> has eaten fish </span><math id="A2.I13.i2.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="i-1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" mathsize="0.800em">i</mi><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" mathsize="0.800em">−</mo><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" mathsize="0.800em">1</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">i-1</annotation></semantics></math><span id="A2.I13.i2.p1.1.6" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:80%;--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">.</span></span>
</span></span>
<span id="A2.I13.i3" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">•</span> 
<span id="A2.I13.i3.p1" class="ltx_para">
<span id="A2.I13.i3.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.I13.i3.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:80%;--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">Fish 1 cannot eat any other fish; it can only be eaten.</span></span>
</span></span>
</span>
<span id="A2.SS6.SSS1.Px1.p2.pic1.2.3" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.SS6.SSS1.Px1.p2.pic1.2.3.1" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:80%;--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">We assume:</span></span>
<span id="A2.I14" class="ltx_enumerate">
<span id="A2.I14.i1" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">1.</span> 
<span id="A2.I14.i1.p1" class="ltx_para">
<span id="A2.I14.i1.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.I14.i1.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:80%;--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">If there is a smaller fish available to eat, a larger fish will not pass up the opportunity.</span></span>
</span></span>
<span id="A2.I14.i2" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">2.</span> 
<span id="A2.I14.i2.p1" class="ltx_para">
<span id="A2.I14.i2.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.I14.i2.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:80%;--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">However, self-preservation takes priority: before eating a smaller fish, a fish must ensure that doing so will not lead to it being eaten.</span></span>
</span></span>
<span id="A2.I14.i3" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">3.</span> 
<span id="A2.I14.i3.p1" class="ltx_para">
<span id="A2.I14.i3.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.I14.i3.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:80%;--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">Every fish is infinitely intelligent, and they all know that, and they all know that they all know that, and so on (common knowledge).</span></span>
</span></span>
</span>
<span id="A2.SS6.SSS1.Px1.p2.pic1.2.4" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.SS6.SSS1.Px1.p2.pic1.2.4.1" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:80%;--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">Question: Will fish 1,2,3 survive?</span></span><span class="ltx_inline-block"><svg id="A2.SS6.SSS1.Px1.p2.pic1.pic1" class="ltx_picture" color="#008000" height="18.24" overflow="visible" style="vertical-align:-4.1px" version="1.1" viewBox="0 0 18.24 18.24" width="18.24"><g style="--ltx-stroke-color:#009900;--ltx-fill-color:#009900;--ltx-fg-color:#009900;" color="#009900" fill="#009900" stroke="#009900" stroke-width="1.8pt" transform="translate(0,18.24) matrix(1 0 0 -1 0 0) translate(1.25,0) translate(0,1.25)"><path style="fill:none" d="M 0 7.87 L 5.51 0 L 15.75 15.75"></path></g></svg></span>
<span id="A2.SS6.SSS1.Px1.p2.pic1.2.5" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.SS6.SSS1.Px1.p2.pic1.2.5.1" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:80%;--ltx-fg-color:#008000;">GPT-5 thinking passed</span></span>
<span id="A2.SS6.SSS1.Px1.p2.pic1.2.6" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.SS6.SSS1.Px1.p2.pic1.2.6.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic" style="font-size:80%;--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">Proposed by Qiuyu Ren</span></span>
</span></span></span></foreignObject></g></g></svg></span>
</div>
<div id="A2.SS6.SSS1.Px1.1" class="ltx_proof">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_font_italic ltx_title_proof"><span id="A2.SS6.SSS1.Px1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Response of GPT-5-thinking</span>.</h6>
<div id="A2.SS6.SSS1.Px1.p3" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A2.SS6.SSS1.Px1.p3.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.SS6.SSS1.Px1.p3.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Answer:<span id="A2.SS6.SSS1.Px1.p3.1.1.1" class="ltx_text"></span></span></p>
<ul id="A2.I15" class="ltx_itemize">
<li id="A2.I15.i1" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">•</span> 
<div id="A2.I15.i1.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A2.I15.i1.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Fish 1: <span id="A2.I15.i1.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">dies</span></p>
</div></li>
<li id="A2.I15.i2" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">•</span> 
<div id="A2.I15.i2.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A2.I15.i2.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Fish 2: <span id="A2.I15.i2.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">survives</span></p>
</div></li>
<li id="A2.I15.i3" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">•</span> 
<div id="A2.I15.i3.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A2.I15.i3.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Fish 3: <span id="A2.I15.i3.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">survives</span></p>
</div></li>
</ul>
</div>
<div id="A2.SS6.SSS1.Px1.p4" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A2.SS6.SSS1.Px1.p4.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.SS6.SSS1.Px1.p4.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Reasoning:<span id="A2.SS6.SSS1.Px1.p4.1.1.1" class="ltx_text"></span></span></p>
</div>
<div id="A2.SS6.SSS1.Px1.p5" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A2.SS6.SSS1.Px1.p5.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.SS6.SSS1.Px1.p5.1.1" class="ltx_text">Because of the “gate” rule — fish <math id="A2.SS6.SSS1.Px1.p5.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="i+1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">i+1</annotation></semantics></math> can only eat fish <math id="A2.SS6.SSS1.Px1.p5.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="i" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>i</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">i</annotation></semantics></math> after <math id="A2.SS6.SSS1.Px1.p5.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="i" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>i</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">i</annotation></semantics></math> has eaten <math id="A2.SS6.SSS1.Px1.p5.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="i-1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">i-1</annotation></semantics></math> — the only way any eating can start is if fish <math id="A2.SS6.SSS1.Px1.p5.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="2" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mn>2</mn><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">2</annotation></semantics></math> eats fish <math id="A2.SS6.SSS1.Px1.p5.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mn>1</mn><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">1</annotation></semantics></math>.</span></p>
</div>
<div id="A2.SS6.SSS1.Px1.p6" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A2.SS6.SSS1.Px1.p6.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.SS6.SSS1.Px1.p6.1.1" class="ltx_text">We ask: if <math id="A2.SS6.SSS1.Px1.p6.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="2" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mn>2</mn><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">2</annotation></semantics></math> eats <math id="A2.SS6.SSS1.Px1.p6.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mn>1</mn><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">1</annotation></semantics></math>, will <math id="A2.SS6.SSS1.Px1.p6.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="3" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mn>3</mn><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">3</annotation></semantics></math> then eat <math id="A2.SS6.SSS1.Px1.p6.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="2" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mn>2</mn><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">2</annotation></semantics></math>? Fish <math id="A2.SS6.SSS1.Px1.p6.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="3" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mn>3</mn><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">3</annotation></semantics></math> would only do that if it were safe from fish <math id="A2.SS6.SSS1.Px1.p6.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="4" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mn>4</mn><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">4</annotation></semantics></math>.</span></p>
</div>
<div id="A2.SS6.SSS1.Px1.p7" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A2.SS6.SSS1.Px1.p7.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.SS6.SSS1.Px1.p7.1.1" class="ltx_text">Work backwards from the top of the chain:</span></p>
<ul id="A2.I16" class="ltx_itemize">
<li id="A2.I16.i1" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">•</span> 
<div id="A2.I16.i1.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A2.I16.i1.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Fish <math id="A2.I16.i1.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="10000" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mn>10000</mn><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">10000</annotation></semantics></math> has no predator, so if enabled it would eat fish <math id="A2.I16.i1.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="9999" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mn>9999</mn><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">9999</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>
</div></li>
<li id="A2.I16.i2" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">•</span> 
<div id="A2.I16.i2.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A2.I16.i2.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Therefore, fish <math id="A2.I16.i2.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="9999" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mn>9999</mn><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">9999</annotation></semantics></math> will avoid eating <math id="A2.I16.i2.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="9998" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mn>9998</mn><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">9998</annotation></semantics></math> (to avoid being eaten by <math id="A2.I16.i2.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="10000" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mn>10000</mn><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">10000</annotation></semantics></math>).</p>
</div></li>
<li id="A2.I16.i3" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">•</span> 
<div id="A2.I16.i3.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A2.I16.i3.p1.1" class="ltx_p">This reasoning propagates downward in an alternating pattern: <math id="A2.I16.i3.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="9998" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mn>9998</mn><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">9998</annotation></semantics></math> would eat <math id="A2.I16.i3.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="9997" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mn>9997</mn><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">9997</annotation></semantics></math>, <math id="A2.I16.i3.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="9997" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mn>9997</mn><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">9997</annotation></semantics></math> would avoid <math id="A2.I16.i3.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="9996" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mn>9996</mn><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">9996</annotation></semantics></math>, and so on.</p>
</div></li>
</ul>
</div>
<div id="A2.SS6.SSS1.Px1.p8" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A2.SS6.SSS1.Px1.p8.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.SS6.SSS1.Px1.p8.1.1" class="ltx_text">Tracing this alternation shows that fish <math id="A2.SS6.SSS1.Px1.p8.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="4" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mn>4</mn><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">4</annotation></semantics></math> would eat fish <math id="A2.SS6.SSS1.Px1.p8.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="3" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mn>3</mn><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">3</annotation></semantics></math> if <math id="A2.SS6.SSS1.Px1.p8.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="3" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mn>3</mn><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">3</annotation></semantics></math> ever ate <math id="A2.SS6.SSS1.Px1.p8.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="2" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mn>2</mn><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">2</annotation></semantics></math>. Hence <math id="A2.SS6.SSS1.Px1.p8.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="3" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mn>3</mn><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">3</annotation></semantics></math> will <em id="A2.SS6.SSS1.Px1.p8.1.1.1" class="ltx_emph ltx_font_italic">not</em> eat <math id="A2.SS6.SSS1.Px1.p8.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="2" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mn>2</mn><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">2</annotation></semantics></math>.</span></p>
</div>
<div id="A2.SS6.SSS1.Px1.p9" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A2.SS6.SSS1.Px1.p9.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.SS6.SSS1.Px1.p9.1.1" class="ltx_text">Knowing this, fish <math id="A2.SS6.SSS1.Px1.p9.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="2" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mn>2</mn><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">2</annotation></semantics></math> sees it is safe to eat fish <math id="A2.SS6.SSS1.Px1.p9.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mn>1</mn><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">1</annotation></semantics></math>. Once <math id="A2.SS6.SSS1.Px1.p9.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mn>1</mn><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">1</annotation></semantics></math> is eaten, no further eating is possible.</span></p>
</div>
<div id="A2.SS6.SSS1.Px1.p10" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A2.SS6.SSS1.Px1.p10.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.SS6.SSS1.Px1.p10.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Conclusion:<span id="A2.SS6.SSS1.Px1.p10.1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_medium"> Fish <math id="A2.SS6.SSS1.Px1.p10.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mn>1</mn><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">1</annotation></semantics></math> dies, while fish <math id="A2.SS6.SSS1.Px1.p10.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="2" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mn>2</mn><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">2</annotation></semantics></math> and fish <math id="A2.SS6.SSS1.Px1.p10.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="3" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mn>3</mn><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">3</annotation></semantics></math> survive.</span></span></p>
</div>
<div id="A2.SS6.SSS1.Px1.p11" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A2.SS6.SSS1.Px1.p11.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.SS6.SSS1.Px1.p11.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Generalization:<span id="A2.SS6.SSS1.Px1.p11.1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_medium"> With an even total number of fish, only fish <math id="A2.SS6.SSS1.Px1.p11.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mn>1</mn><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">1</annotation></semantics></math> gets eaten; with an odd total, no fish eats at all.
∎</span></span></p>
</div>
</div>
<div id="A2.SS6.SSS1.Px1.2" class="ltx_proof">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_font_italic ltx_title_proof"><span id="A2.SS6.SSS1.Px1.2.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Standard Solution</span>.</h6>
<div id="A2.SS6.SSS1.Px1.p12" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A2.SS6.SSS1.Px1.p12.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.SS6.SSS1.Px1.p12.1.1" class="ltx_text">We use induction to prove that if there are odd number of fishes, no fish gets eaten, while if there are even number of fishes, exactly fish 1 gets eaten.</span></p>
</div>
<div id="A2.SS6.SSS1.Px1.p13" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A2.SS6.SSS1.Px1.p13.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.SS6.SSS1.Px1.p13.1.1" class="ltx_text">The base case when there’s only one fish is trivial.</span></p>
</div>
<div id="A2.SS6.SSS1.Px1.p14" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A2.SS6.SSS1.Px1.p14.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.SS6.SSS1.Px1.p14.1.1" class="ltx_text">For the induction step, suppose there are <math id="A2.SS6.SSS1.Px1.p14.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="n" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>n</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">n</annotation></semantics></math> fishes, <math id="A2.SS6.SSS1.Px1.p14.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="n&gt;1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>&gt;</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">n&gt;1</annotation></semantics></math>. If <math id="A2.SS6.SSS1.Px1.p14.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="n" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>n</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">n</annotation></semantics></math> is even, fish 2 knows that eating fish 1 is safe by induction hypothesis, so it eats fish 1 and no other fish gets eaten by induction hypothesis. Similarly, if <math id="A2.SS6.SSS1.Px1.p14.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="n" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>n</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">n</annotation></semantics></math> is odd, fish 2 knows that eating fish 1 is not safe by induction hypothesis, so it does not eat fish 1, and no fish gets eaten.</span></p>
</div>
<div id="A2.SS6.SSS1.Px1.p15" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A2.SS6.SSS1.Px1.p15.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.SS6.SSS1.Px1.p15.1.1" class="ltx_text">Consequently, when there are 10000 fishes, fish 1 gets eaten, while fishes 2,3 survive.
∎</span></p>
</div>
</div>
<div id="A2.SS6.SSS1.Px1.p16" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent"><span class="ltx_inline-block"><svg id="A2.SS6.SSS1.Px1.p16.pic1" class="ltx_picture" height="69.62" overflow="visible" version="1.1" viewBox="0 0 429.64 69.62" width="429.64"><g style="--ltx-stroke-color:#000000;--ltx-fill-color:#000000;" fill="#000000" stroke="#000000" stroke-width="0.4pt" transform="translate(0,69.62) matrix(1 0 0 -1 0 0)"><g style="--ltx-fill-color:#4D4D4D;" fill="#4D4D4D" fill-opacity="1.0"><path style="stroke:none" d="M 0 4.63 L 0 65 C 0 67.55 2.07 69.62 4.63 69.62 L 425.01 69.62 C 427.56 69.62 429.64 67.55 429.64 65 L 429.64 4.63 C 429.64 2.07 427.56 0 425.01 0 L 4.63 0 C 2.07 0 0 2.07 0 4.63 Z"></path></g><g style="--ltx-fill-color:#F9F9F9;" fill="#F9F9F9" fill-opacity="1.0"><path style="stroke:none" d="M 0.69 4.63 L 0.69 50.76 L 428.94 50.76 L 428.94 4.63 C 428.94 2.45 427.18 0.69 425.01 0.69 L 4.63 0.69 C 2.45 0.69 0.69 2.45 0.69 4.63 Z"></path></g><g fill-opacity="1.0" transform="matrix(1.0 0.0 0.0 1.0 20.38 55.39)"><foreignObject style="--ltx-fo-width:24.44em;--ltx-fo-height:0.69em;--ltx-fo-depth:0em;font-size:10pt;" height="9.61" overflow="visible" transform="matrix(1 0 0 -1 0 9.61)" width="338.18"><span class="ltx_foreignobject_container"><span class="ltx_foreignobject_content">
<span id="A2.SS6.SSS1.Px1.p16.pic1.1" class="ltx_inline-block ltx_minipage ltx_align_bottom" style="width:24.44em;">
<span id="A2.SS6.SSS1.Px1.p16.pic1.1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.SS6.SSS1.Px1.p16.pic1.1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold" style="--ltx-fg-color:#FFFFFF;">Rubric</span></span>
</span></span></span></foreignObject></g><g fill-opacity="1.0" transform="matrix(1.0 0.0 0.0 1.0 20.38 14.66)"><foreignObject style="--ltx-fo-width:33.06em;--ltx-fo-height:1.76em;--ltx-fo-depth:0.16em;font-size:10pt;" height="26.44" overflow="visible" transform="matrix(1 0 0 -1 0 24.29)" width="457.46"><span class="ltx_foreignobject_container"><span class="ltx_foreignobject_content">
<span id="A2.SS6.SSS1.Px1.p16.pic1.2" class="ltx_inline-block ltx_minipage ltx_align_bottom" style="width:33.06em;">
<span id="A2.SS6.SSS1.Px1.p16.pic1.2.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.SS6.SSS1.Px1.p16.pic1.2.1.1" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:80%;--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">2 point for correct answer and good explanation.
<br class="ltx_break">1 point off if the answer lacks clarity or contains unnecessary argument.</span></span>
</span></span></span></foreignObject></g></g></svg></span>
</div>
<div id="A2.SS6.SSS1.Px1.p17" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent"><span class="ltx_inline-block"><svg id="A2.SS6.SSS1.Px1.p17.pic1" class="ltx_picture" height="54.13" overflow="visible" version="1.1" viewBox="0 0 429.64 54.13" width="429.64"><g style="--ltx-stroke-color:#000000;--ltx-fill-color:#000000;" fill="#000000" stroke="#000000" stroke-width="0.4pt" transform="translate(0,54.13) matrix(1 0 0 -1 0 0)"><g style="--ltx-fill-color:#5A996B;" fill="#5A996B" fill-opacity="1.0"><path style="stroke:none" d="M 0 4.63 L 0 49.51 C 0 52.06 2.07 54.13 4.63 54.13 L 425.01 54.13 C 427.56 54.13 429.64 52.06 429.64 49.51 L 429.64 4.63 C 429.64 2.07 427.56 0 425.01 0 L 4.63 0 C 2.07 0 0 2.07 0 4.63 Z"></path></g><g style="--ltx-fill-color:#F6FFF9;" fill="#F6FFF9" fill-opacity="1.0"><path style="stroke:none" d="M 0.69 4.63 L 0.69 35.38 L 428.94 35.38 L 428.94 4.63 C 428.94 2.45 427.18 0.69 425.01 0.69 L 4.63 0.69 C 2.45 0.69 0.69 2.45 0.69 4.63 Z"></path></g><g fill-opacity="1.0" transform="matrix(1.0 0.0 0.0 1.0 20.38 40.01)"><foreignObject style="--ltx-fo-width:24.44em;--ltx-fo-height:0.69em;--ltx-fo-depth:0em;font-size:10pt;" height="9.49" overflow="visible" transform="matrix(1 0 0 -1 0 9.49)" width="338.18"><span class="ltx_foreignobject_container"><span class="ltx_foreignobject_content">
<span id="A2.SS6.SSS1.Px1.p17.pic1.1" class="ltx_inline-block ltx_minipage ltx_align_bottom" style="width:24.44em;">
