</section>
<section id="A2.SS7.SSS3" class="ltx_subsubsection">
<h4 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsubsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsubsection">(c) </span>Estimating numerically or asymptotically</h4>

<section id="A2.SS7.SSS3.Px1" class="ltx_paragraph">
<h5 class="ltx_title ltx_title_paragraph" style="--ltx-fg-color:#FF0000;">Problem 7c1 </h5>

<div id="A2.SS7.SSS3.Px1.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A2.SS7.SSS3.Px1.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.SS7.SSS3.Px1.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text"></span>
<br class="ltx_break" style="--ltx-break-space:-10.0pt;"></p>
</div>
<div id="A2.SS7.SSS3.Px1.p2" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent"><span class="ltx_inline-block"><svg id="A2.SS7.SSS3.Px1.p2.pic1" class="ltx_picture" height="116.31" overflow="visible" version="1.1" viewBox="0 0 429.64 116.31" width="429.64"><g style="--ltx-stroke-color:#000000;--ltx-fill-color:#000000;" fill="#000000" stroke="#000000" stroke-width="0.4pt" transform="translate(0,116.31) matrix(1 0 0 -1 0 0)"><g style="--ltx-fill-color:#3D6666;" fill="#3D6666" fill-opacity="1.0"><path style="stroke:none" d="M 0 4.63 L 0 111.68 C 0 114.23 2.07 116.31 4.63 116.31 L 425.01 116.31 C 427.56 116.31 429.64 114.23 429.64 111.68 L 429.64 4.63 C 429.64 2.07 427.56 0 425.01 0 L 4.63 0 C 2.07 0 0 2.07 0 4.63 Z"></path></g><g style="--ltx-fill-color:#F9F9F9;" fill="#F9F9F9" fill-opacity="1.0"><path style="stroke:none" d="M 0.69 4.63 L 0.69 97.44 L 428.94 97.44 L 428.94 4.63 C 428.94 2.45 427.18 0.69 425.01 0.69 L 4.63 0.69 C 2.45 0.69 0.69 2.45 0.69 4.63 Z"></path></g><g fill-opacity="1.0" transform="matrix(1.0 0.0 0.0 1.0 20.38 102.07)"><foreignObject style="--ltx-fo-width:24.44em;--ltx-fo-height:0.69em;--ltx-fo-depth:0em;font-size:10pt;" height="9.61" overflow="visible" transform="matrix(1 0 0 -1 0 9.61)" width="338.18"><span class="ltx_foreignobject_container"><span class="ltx_foreignobject_content">
<span id="A2.SS7.SSS3.Px1.p2.pic1.1" class="ltx_inline-block ltx_minipage ltx_align_bottom" style="width:24.44em;">
<span id="A2.SS7.SSS3.Px1.p2.pic1.1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.SS7.SSS3.Px1.p2.pic1.1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold" style="--ltx-fg-color:#FFFFFF;">Problem</span></span>
</span></span></span></foreignObject></g><g fill-opacity="1.0" transform="matrix(1.0 0.0 0.0 1.0 20.38 14.66)"><foreignObject style="--ltx-fo-width:32.01em;--ltx-fo-height:5.13em;--ltx-fo-depth:0.16em;font-size:10pt;" height="73.13" overflow="visible" transform="matrix(1 0 0 -1 0 70.97)" width="442.93"><span class="ltx_foreignobject_container"><span class="ltx_foreignobject_content">
<span id="A2.SS7.SSS3.Px1.p2.pic1.2" class="ltx_inline-block ltx_minipage ltx_align_bottom" style="width:32.01em;">
<span id="A2.SS7.SSS3.Px1.p2.pic1.2.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.SS7.SSS3.Px1.p2.pic1.2.1.1" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:80%;--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">Let <math id="A2.SS7.SSS3.Px1.p2.pic1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="x_{1}=1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">x</mi><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">1</mn></msub><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">=</mo><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">1</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">x_{1}=1</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="A2.SS7.SSS3.Px1.p2.pic1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="x_{n+1}=\frac{x_{n}}{n^{2}}+\frac{n^{2}}{x_{n}}+2,n\geqslant 1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">x</mi><mrow><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">n</mi><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">+</mo><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">1</mn></mrow></msub><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">=</mo><mrow><mfrac style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000"><msub><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">x</mi><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">n</mi></msub><msup><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">n</mi><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">2</mn></msup></mfrac><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">+</mo><mfrac style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000"><msup><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">n</mi><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">2</mn></msup><msub><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">x</mi><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">n</mi></msub></mfrac><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">+</mo><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">2</mn></mrow></mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">,</mo><mrow><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">n</mi><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">⩾</mo><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">1</mn></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">x_{n+1}=\frac{x_{n}}{n^{2}}+\frac{n^{2}}{x_{n}}+2,n\geqslant 1</annotation></semantics></math>. Is the coefficient of the third term in the asymptotic expansion of <math id="A2.SS7.SSS3.Px1.p2.pic1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="x_{n}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">x</mi><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">n</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">x_{n}</annotation></semantics></math> equal to <math id="A2.SS7.SSS3.Px1.p2.pic1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\frac{5}{8}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mfrac style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000"><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">5</mn><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">8</mn></mfrac><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\frac{5}{8}</annotation></semantics></math>?</span></span><span class="ltx_inline-block"><svg id="A2.SS7.SSS3.Px1.p2.pic1.pic1" class="ltx_picture" color="#FF0000" height="18.24" overflow="visible" style="vertical-align:-4.1px" version="1.1" viewBox="0 0 18.24 18.24" width="18.24"><g style="--ltx-stroke-color:#FF0000;--ltx-fill-color:#FF0000;" fill="#FF0000" stroke="#FF0000" stroke-width="1.8pt" transform="translate(0,18.24) matrix(1 0 0 -1 0 0) translate(1.25,0) translate(0,1.25)"><path style="fill:none" d="M 0 0 L 15.75 15.75 M 0 15.75 L 15.75 0"></path></g></svg></span>
<span id="A2.SS7.SSS3.Px1.p2.pic1.2.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.SS7.SSS3.Px1.p2.pic1.2.2.1" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:80%;--ltx-fg-color:#FF0000;">GPT-5 thinking failed</span></span>
<span id="A2.SS7.SSS3.Px1.p2.pic1.2.3" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.SS7.SSS3.Px1.p2.pic1.2.3.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic" style="font-size:80%;--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">Proposed by Jiaxin Zhang</span></span>
</span></span></span></foreignObject></g></g></svg></span>
</div>
<div id="A2.SS7.SSS3.Px1.1" class="ltx_proof">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_font_italic ltx_title_proof"><span id="A2.SS7.SSS3.Px1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Response of GPT-5-thinking</span>.</h6>
<div id="A2.SS7.SSS3.Px1.p3" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A2.SS7.SSS3.Px1.p3.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.SS7.SSS3.Px1.p3.1.1" class="ltx_text">Yes. In fact</span></p>
</div>
<div id="A2.SS7.SSS3.Px1.p4" class="ltx_para">
<table id="A2.Ex196" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A2.Ex196.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="x_{n}=n+\frac{1}{2}+\frac{5}{8n}+\frac{13}{16n^{2}}+O\!\left(\frac{1}{n^{3}}\right)." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>n</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>+</mo><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mn>2</mn></mfrac><mo>+</mo><mfrac><mn>5</mn><mrow><mn>8</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>n</mi></mrow></mfrac><mo>+</mo><mfrac><mn>13</mn><mrow><mn>16</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>n</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow></mfrac><mo>+</mo><mrow><mpadded style="width:0.621em;" width="0.621em"><mi>O</mi></mpadded><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mfrac><mn>1</mn><msup><mi>n</mi><mn>3</mn></msup></mfrac><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">x_{n}=n+\frac{1}{2}+\frac{5}{8n}+\frac{13}{16n^{2}}+O\!\left(\frac{1}{n^{3}}\right).</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
<div id="A2.SS7.SSS3.Px1.p5" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A2.SS7.SSS3.Px1.p5.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.SS7.SSS3.Px1.p5.1.1" class="ltx_text">Derivation.
Write <math id="A2.SS7.SSS3.Px1.p5.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="x_{n}=n+s_{n}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>n</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>+</mo><msub><mi>s</mi><mi>n</mi></msub></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">x_{n}=n+s_{n}</annotation></semantics></math>. Then</span></p>
</div>
<div id="A2.SS7.SSS3.Px1.p6" class="ltx_para">
<table id="A2.Ex197" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A2.Ex197.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="x_{n+1}\;=\;\frac{n+s_{n}}{n^{2}}+\frac{n^{2}}{n+s_{n}}+2\;=\;\frac{1}{n}+\frac{s_{n}}{n^{2}}\;+\;n\Big(1-\frac{s_{n}}{n}+\frac{s_{n}^{2}}{n^{2}}-\frac{s_{n}^{3}}{n^{3}}+\cdots\Big)+2." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>x</mi><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0.558em" rspace="0.558em">=</mo><mrow><mfrac><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>+</mo><msub><mi>s</mi><mi>n</mi></msub></mrow><msup><mi>n</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></mfrac><mo>+</mo><mfrac><msup><mi>n</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>+</mo><msub><mi>s</mi><mi>n</mi></msub></mrow></mfrac><mo>+</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow><mo lspace="0.558em" rspace="0.558em">=</mo><mrow><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mi>n</mi></mfrac><mo>+</mo><mfrac><msub><mi>s</mi><mi>n</mi></msub><msup><mi>n</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></mfrac><mo lspace="0.502em">+</mo><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="1.600em" minsize="1.600em">(</mo><mrow><mrow><mrow><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mfrac><msub><mi>s</mi><mi>n</mi></msub><mi>n</mi></mfrac></mrow><mo>+</mo><mfrac><msubsup><mi>s</mi><mi>n</mi><mn>2</mn></msubsup><msup><mi>n</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></mfrac></mrow><mo>−</mo><mfrac><msubsup><mi>s</mi><mi>n</mi><mn>3</mn></msubsup><msup><mi>n</mi><mn>3</mn></msup></mfrac></mrow><mo>+</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">⋯</mo></mrow><mo maxsize="1.600em" minsize="1.600em">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">x_{n+1}\;=\;\frac{n+s_{n}}{n^{2}}+\frac{n^{2}}{n+s_{n}}+2\;=\;\frac{1}{n}+\frac{s_{n}}{n^{2}}\;+\;n\Big(1-\frac{s_{n}}{n}+\frac{s_{n}^{2}}{n^{2}}-\frac{s_{n}^{3}}{n^{3}}+\cdots\Big)+2.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
<div id="A2.SS7.SSS3.Px1.p7" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A2.SS7.SSS3.Px1.p7.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.SS7.SSS3.Px1.p7.1.1" class="ltx_text">Hence</span></p>
</div>
<div id="A2.SS7.SSS3.Px1.p8" class="ltx_para">
<table id="A2.Ex198" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A2.Ex198.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="x_{n+1}=(n+1)+\Big(1-s_{n}+\frac{1+s_{n}^{2}}{n}+\frac{s_{n}-s_{n}^{3}}{n^{2}}+O(n^{-3})\Big)," display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>x</mi><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="1.600em" minsize="1.600em">(</mo><mrow><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>s</mi><mi>n</mi></msub></mrow><mo>+</mo><mfrac><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>+</mo><msubsup><mi>s</mi><mi>n</mi><mn>2</mn></msubsup></mrow><mi>n</mi></mfrac><mo>+</mo><mfrac><mrow><msub><mi>s</mi><mi>n</mi></msub><mo>−</mo><msubsup><mi>s</mi><mi>n</mi><mn>3</mn></msubsup></mrow><msup><mi>n</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></mfrac><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi>O</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>n</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>3</mn></mrow></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo maxsize="1.600em" minsize="1.600em">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">x_{n+1}=(n+1)+\Big(1-s_{n}+\frac{1+s_{n}^{2}}{n}+\frac{s_{n}-s_{n}^{3}}{n^{2}}+O(n^{-3})\Big),</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
<div id="A2.SS7.SSS3.Px1.p9" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A2.SS7.SSS3.Px1.p9.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.SS7.SSS3.Px1.p9.1.1" class="ltx_text">so</span></p>
</div>
<div id="A2.SS7.SSS3.Px1.p10" class="ltx_para">
<table id="A2.Ex199" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A2.Ex199.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="s_{n+1}=1-s_{n}+\frac{1+s_{n}^{2}}{n}+\frac{s_{n}-s_{n}^{3}}{n^{2}}+O\!\left(\frac{1}{n^{3}}\right)." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>s</mi><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>s</mi><mi>n</mi></msub></mrow><mo>+</mo><mfrac><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>+</mo><msubsup><mi>s</mi><mi>n</mi><mn>2</mn></msubsup></mrow><mi>n</mi></mfrac><mo>+</mo><mfrac><mrow><msub><mi>s</mi><mi>n</mi></msub><mo>−</mo><msubsup><mi>s</mi><mi>n</mi><mn>3</mn></msubsup></mrow><msup><mi>n</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></mfrac><mo>+</mo><mrow><mpadded style="width:0.621em;" width="0.621em"><mi>O</mi></mpadded><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mfrac><mn>1</mn><msup><mi>n</mi><mn>3</mn></msup></mfrac><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">s_{n+1}=1-s_{n}+\frac{1+s_{n}^{2}}{n}+\frac{s_{n}-s_{n}^{3}}{n^{2}}+O\!\left(\frac{1}{n^{3}}\right).</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
<div id="A2.SS7.SSS3.Px1.p11" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A2.SS7.SSS3.Px1.p11.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.SS7.SSS3.Px1.p11.1.1" class="ltx_text">Seek an expansion <math id="A2.SS7.SSS3.Px1.p11.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="s_{n}=\dfrac{1}{2}+\dfrac{A}{n}+\dfrac{B}{n^{2}}+O(n^{-3})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>s</mi><mi>n</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mn>2</mn></mfrac></mstyle><mo>+</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mi>A</mi><mi>n</mi></mfrac></mstyle><mo>+</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mi>B</mi><msup><mi>n</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></mfrac></mstyle><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi>O</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>n</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>3</mn></mrow></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">s_{n}=\dfrac{1}{2}+\dfrac{A}{n}+\dfrac{B}{n^{2}}+O(n^{-3})</annotation></semantics></math>. Then</span></p>
</div>
<div id="A2.SS7.SSS3.Px1.p12" class="ltx_para">
<table id="A2.Ex200" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A2.Ex200.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="s^{2}=\frac{1}{4}+\frac{A}{n}+\frac{A^{2}+B}{n^{2}}+O(n^{-3}),\qquad s^{3}=\frac{1}{8}+\frac{3A}{4n}+\frac{3A^{2}+\frac{3}{4}B}{n^{2}}+O(n^{-3})." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><msup><mi>s</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>=</mo><mrow><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mn>4</mn></mfrac><mo>+</mo><mfrac><mi>A</mi><mi>n</mi></mfrac><mo>+</mo><mfrac><mrow><msup><mi>A</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>+</mo><mi>B</mi></mrow><msup><mi>n</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></mfrac><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi>O</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>n</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>3</mn></mrow></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="2.167em">,</mo><mrow><msup><mi>s</mi><mn>3</mn></msup><mo>=</mo><mrow><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mn>8</mn></mfrac><mo>+</mo><mfrac><mrow><mn>3</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>A</mi></mrow><mrow><mn>4</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>n</mi></mrow></mfrac><mo>+</mo><mfrac><mrow><mrow><mn>3</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>A</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mfrac><mn>3</mn><mn>4</mn></mfrac><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>B</mi></mrow></mrow><msup><mi>n</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></mfrac><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi>O</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>n</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>3</mn></mrow></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">s^{2}=\frac{1}{4}+\frac{A}{n}+\frac{A^{2}+B}{n^{2}}+O(n^{-3}),\qquad s^{3}=\frac{1}{8}+\frac{3A}{4n}+\frac{3A^{2}+\frac{3}{4}B}{n^{2}}+O(n^{-3}).</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
<div id="A2.SS7.SSS3.Px1.p13" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A2.SS7.SSS3.Px1.p13.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.SS7.SSS3.Px1.p13.1.1" class="ltx_text">Plugging into the recursion gives</span></p>
</div>
<div id="A2.SS7.SSS3.Px1.p14" class="ltx_para">
<table id="A2.Ex201" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A2.Ex201.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="s_{n+1}=\frac{1}{2}+\Big(-A+\frac{5}{4}\Big)\frac{1}{n}+\Big(-B+A+\frac{3}{8}\Big)\frac{1}{n^{2}}+O\!\left(\frac{1}{n^{3}}\right)." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>s</mi><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mn>2</mn></mfrac><mo>+</mo><mrow><mrow><mo maxsize="1.600em" minsize="1.600em">(</mo><mrow><mrow><mo>−</mo><mi>A</mi></mrow><mo>+</mo><mfrac><mn>5</mn><mn>4</mn></mfrac></mrow><mo maxsize="1.600em" minsize="1.600em">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mi>n</mi></mfrac></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mrow><mo maxsize="1.600em" minsize="1.600em">(</mo><mrow><mrow><mo>−</mo><mi>B</mi></mrow><mo>+</mo><mi>A</mi><mo>+</mo><mfrac><mn>3</mn><mn>8</mn></mfrac></mrow><mo maxsize="1.600em" minsize="1.600em">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mfrac><mn>1</mn><msup><mi>n</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></mfrac></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mpadded style="width:0.621em;" width="0.621em"><mi>O</mi></mpadded><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mfrac><mn>1</mn><msup><mi>n</mi><mn>3</mn></msup></mfrac><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">s_{n+1}=\frac{1}{2}+\Big(-A+\frac{5}{4}\Big)\frac{1}{n}+\Big(-B+A+\frac{3}{8}\Big)\frac{1}{n^{2}}+O\!\left(\frac{1}{n^{3}}\right).</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
<div id="A2.SS7.SSS3.Px1.p15" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A2.SS7.SSS3.Px1.p15.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.SS7.SSS3.Px1.p15.1.1" class="ltx_text">But also</span></p>
</div>
<div id="A2.SS7.SSS3.Px1.p16" class="ltx_para">
<table id="A2.Ex202" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A2.Ex202.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="s_{n+1}=\frac{1}{2}+\frac{A}{n+1}+\frac{B}{(n+1)^{2}}+O(n^{-3})=\frac{1}{2}+\frac{A}{n}+\frac{B-A}{n^{2}}+O(n^{-3})." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>s</mi><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mn>2</mn></mfrac><mo>+</mo><mfrac><mi>A</mi><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mfrac><mo>+</mo><mfrac><mi>B</mi><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup></mfrac><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi>O</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>n</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>3</mn></mrow></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mn>2</mn></mfrac><mo>+</mo><mfrac><mi>A</mi><mi>n</mi></mfrac><mo>+</mo><mfrac><mrow><mi>B</mi><mo>−</mo><mi>A</mi></mrow><msup><mi>n</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></mfrac><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi>O</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>n</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>3</mn></mrow></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">s_{n+1}=\frac{1}{2}+\frac{A}{n+1}+\frac{B}{(n+1)^{2}}+O(n^{-3})=\frac{1}{2}+\frac{A}{n}+\frac{B-A}{n^{2}}+O(n^{-3}).</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
<div id="A2.SS7.SSS3.Px1.p17" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A2.SS7.SSS3.Px1.p17.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.SS7.SSS3.Px1.p17.1.1" class="ltx_text">Matching coefficients yields</span></p>
</div>
<div id="A2.SS7.SSS3.Px1.p18" class="ltx_para">
<table id="A2.Ex203" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A2.Ex203.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="A=-A+\frac{5}{4}\;\Rightarrow\;A=\frac{5}{8},\qquad B-A=-B+A+\frac{3}{8}\;\Rightarrow\;B=\frac{13}{16}." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>A</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mo>−</mo><mi>A</mi></mrow><mo>+</mo><mfrac><mn>5</mn><mn>4</mn></mfrac></mrow><mo lspace="0.558em" rspace="0.558em" stretchy="false">⇒</mo><mi>A</mi><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mn>5</mn><mn>8</mn></mfrac></mrow><mo rspace="2.167em">,</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>B</mi><mo>−</mo><mi>A</mi></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mo>−</mo><mi>B</mi></mrow><mo>+</mo><mi>A</mi><mo>+</mo><mfrac><mn>3</mn><mn>8</mn></mfrac></mrow><mo lspace="0.558em" rspace="0.558em" stretchy="false">⇒</mo><mi>B</mi><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mn>13</mn><mn>16</mn></mfrac></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">A=-A+\frac{5}{4}\;\Rightarrow\;A=\frac{5}{8},\qquad B-A=-B+A+\frac{3}{8}\;\Rightarrow\;B=\frac{13}{16}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
<div id="A2.SS7.SSS3.Px1.p19" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A2.SS7.SSS3.Px1.p19.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.SS7.SSS3.Px1.p19.1.1" class="ltx_text">Therefore</span></p>
</div>
<div id="A2.SS7.SSS3.Px1.p20" class="ltx_para">
<table id="A2.Ex204" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A2.Ex204.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="x_{n}=n+\frac{1}{2}+\frac{5}{8n}+\frac{13}{16n^{2}}+O\!\left(\frac{1}{n^{3}}\right)," display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>n</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>+</mo><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mn>2</mn></mfrac><mo>+</mo><mfrac><mn>5</mn><mrow><mn>8</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>n</mi></mrow></mfrac><mo>+</mo><mfrac><mn>13</mn><mrow><mn>16</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>n</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow></mfrac><mo>+</mo><mrow><mpadded style="width:0.621em;" width="0.621em"><mi>O</mi></mpadded><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mfrac><mn>1</mn><msup><mi>n</mi><mn>3</mn></msup></mfrac><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">x_{n}=n+\frac{1}{2}+\frac{5}{8n}+\frac{13}{16n^{2}}+O\!\left(\frac{1}{n^{3}}\right),</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
<div id="A2.SS7.SSS3.Px1.p21" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A2.SS7.SSS3.Px1.p21.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.SS7.SSS3.Px1.p21.1.1" class="ltx_text">so the coefficient of the third term is indeed <math id="A2.SS7.SSS3.Px1.p21.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\boxed{\frac{5}{8}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><menclose notation="box"><mfrac><mn>5</mn><mn>8</mn></mfrac></menclose><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\boxed{\frac{5}{8}}</annotation></semantics></math>.</span></p>
</div>
<div id="A2.SS7.SSS3.Px1.p22" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A2.SS7.SSS3.Px1.p22.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.SS7.SSS3.Px1.p22.1.1" class="ltx_text">∎</span></p>
</div>
</div>
<div id="A2.SS7.SSS3.Px1.2" class="ltx_proof">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_font_italic ltx_title_proof"><span id="A2.SS7.SSS3.Px1.2.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Standard Solution</span>.</h6>
<div id="A2.SS7.SSS3.Px1.p23" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A2.SS7.SSS3.Px1.p23.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.SS7.SSS3.Px1.p23.1.1" class="ltx_text">The third coefficients of the asymptotic expansion of <math id="A2.SS7.SSS3.Px1.p23.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\{x_{2n}\}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>n</mi></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\{x_{2n}\}</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="A2.SS7.SSS3.Px1.p23.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\{x_{2n+1}\}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>n</mi></mrow><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\{x_{2n+1}\}</annotation></semantics></math> converge to different values
<a href="https://mathoverflow.net/questions/384047/asymptotic-analysis-of-x-n1-fracx-nn2-fracn2x-n-2" title="" class="ltx_ref ltx_href">Math Stack Exchange discussion</a>.</span></p>
</div>
<div id="A2.SS7.SSS3.Px1.p24" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A2.SS7.SSS3.Px1.p24.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.SS7.SSS3.Px1.p24.1.1" class="ltx_text">Consider the substitutions</span></p>
</div>
<div id="A2.SS7.SSS3.Px1.p25" class="ltx_para">
<table id="A2.Ex205" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A2.Ex205.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="x_{n}=n+1/2+y_{n}/n,\quad y_{n}=u_{n}+5/8" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>n</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>+</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>/</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><msub><mi>y</mi><mi>n</mi></msub><mo>/</mo><mi>n</mi></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="1.167em">,</mo><mrow><msub><mi>y</mi><mi>n</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><msub><mi>u</mi><mi>n</mi></msub><mo>+</mo><mrow><mn>5</mn><mo>/</mo><mn>8</mn></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">x_{n}=n+1/2+y_{n}/n,\quad y_{n}=u_{n}+5/8</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
<div id="A2.SS7.SSS3.Px1.p26" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A2.SS7.SSS3.Px1.p26.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.SS7.SSS3.Px1.p26.1.1" class="ltx_text">Then <math id="A2.SS7.SSS3.Px1.p26.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="u_{1}=-9/8" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>u</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mn>1</mn></msub><mo rspace="0em">=</mo><mo lspace="0em">−</mo><mn>9</mn><mo>/</mo><mn>8</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">u_{1}=-9/8</annotation></semantics></math> and</span></p>
</div>
<div id="A2.SS7.SSS3.Px1.p27" class="ltx_para">
<table id="A2.Ex206" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A2.Ex206.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="u_{n+1}=f_{n}\left(u_{n}\right)" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>u</mi><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><msub><mi>f</mi><mi>n</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><msub><mi>u</mi><mi>n</mi></msub><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">u_{n+1}=f_{n}\left(u_{n}\right)</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
<div id="A2.SS7.SSS3.Px1.p28" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A2.SS7.SSS3.Px1.p28.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.SS7.SSS3.Px1.p28.1.1" class="ltx_text">for <math id="A2.SS7.SSS3.Px1.p28.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="n\geq 1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>≥</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">n\geq 1</annotation></semantics></math>, where</span></p>
</div>
<div id="A2.SS7.SSS3.Px1.p29" class="ltx_para">
<table id="A2.Ex207" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A2.Ex207.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="f_{n}(u):=\frac{-64n^{4}u-8n^{3}(4u-13)+n^{2}(56u+115)+n(96u+76)+4(8u+5)}{8n^{2}\left(8n^{2}+4n+8u+5\right)}." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>f</mi><mi>n</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>u</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>:=</mo><mfrac><mrow><mrow><mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mn>64</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>n</mi><mn>4</mn></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>u</mi></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mn>8</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>n</mi><mn>3</mn></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mrow><mn>4</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>u</mi></mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>13</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><msup><mi>n</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mrow><mn>56</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>u</mi></mrow><mo>+</mo><mn>115</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mrow><mn>96</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>u</mi></mrow><mo>+</mo><mn>76</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mn>4</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mrow><mn>8</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>u</mi></mrow><mo>+</mo><mn>5</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mrow><mn>8</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>n</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mrow><mn>8</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>n</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mn>4</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>n</mi></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mn>8</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>u</mi></mrow><mo>+</mo><mn>5</mn></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow></mfrac></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">f_{n}(u):=\frac{-64n^{4}u-8n^{3}(4u-13)+n^{2}(56u+115)+n(96u+76)+4(8u+5)}{8n^{2}\left(8n^{2}+4n+8u+5\right)}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
<div id="A2.SS7.SSS3.Px1.p30" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A2.SS7.SSS3.Px1.p30.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.SS7.SSS3.Px1.p30.1.1" class="ltx_text">Define <math id="A2.SS7.SSS3.Px1.p30.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="c_{n}(u)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>c</mi><mi>n</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>u</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">c_{n}(u)</annotation></semantics></math> by the identity</span></p>
</div>
<div id="A2.SS7.SSS3.Px1.p31" class="ltx_para">
<table id="A2.Ex208" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A2.Ex208.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="f_{n}(u)=-u+\frac{13}{8n}+\frac{c_{n}(u)}{n^{2}}" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>f</mi><mi>n</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>u</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mo>−</mo><mi>u</mi></mrow><mo>+</mo><mfrac><mn>13</mn><mrow><mn>8</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>n</mi></mrow></mfrac><mo>+</mo><mfrac><mrow><msub><mi>c</mi><mi>n</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>u</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><msup><mi>n</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></mfrac></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">f_{n}(u)=-u+\frac{13}{8n}+\frac{c_{n}(u)}{n^{2}}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
<div id="A2.SS7.SSS3.Px1.p32" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A2.SS7.SSS3.Px1.p32.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.SS7.SSS3.Px1.p32.1.1" class="ltx_text">so that</span></p>
</div>
<div id="A2.SS7.SSS3.Px1.p33" class="ltx_para">
<table id="A2.Ex209" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A2.Ex209.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="c_{n}(u)=\frac{n^{2}\left(64u^{2}+96u+63\right)+n(11-8u)+4(8u+5)}{8\left(8n^{2}+4n+8u+5\right)}." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>c</mi><mi>n</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>u</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mrow><mrow><msup><mi>n</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mrow><mn>64</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>u</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mn>96</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>u</mi></mrow><mo>+</mo><mn>63</mn></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>11</mn><mo>−</mo><mrow><mn>8</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>u</mi></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mn>4</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mrow><mn>8</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>u</mi></mrow><mo>+</mo><mn>5</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mrow><mn>8</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mrow><mn>8</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>n</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mn>4</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>n</mi></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mn>8</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>u</mi></mrow><mo>+</mo><mn>5</mn></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow></mfrac></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">c_{n}(u)=\frac{n^{2}\left(64u^{2}+96u+63\right)+n(11-8u)+4(8u+5)}{8\left(8n^{2}+4n+8u+5\right)}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
<div id="A2.SS7.SSS3.Px1.p34" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A2.SS7.SSS3.Px1.p34.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.SS7.SSS3.Px1.p34.1.1" class="ltx_text">Then for <math id="A2.SS7.SSS3.Px1.p34.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="n\geq 1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>≥</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">n\geq 1</annotation></semantics></math></span></p>
</div>
<div id="A2.SS7.SSS3.Px1.p35" class="ltx_para">
<table id="A2.Ex210" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A2.Ex210.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="u_{n+1}+u_{n}=\frac{13}{8n}+\frac{c_{n}(u)}{n^{2}}" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>u</mi><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mo>+</mo><msub><mi>u</mi><mi>n</mi></msub></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mfrac><mn>13</mn><mrow><mn>8</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>n</mi></mrow></mfrac><mo>+</mo><mfrac><mrow><msub><mi>c</mi><mi>n</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>u</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><msup><mi>n</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></mfrac></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">u_{n+1}+u_{n}=\frac{13}{8n}+\frac{c_{n}(u)}{n^{2}}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
<div id="A2.SS7.SSS3.Px1.p36" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A2.SS7.SSS3.Px1.p36.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.SS7.SSS3.Px1.p36.1.1" class="ltx_text">and for <math id="A2.SS7.SSS3.Px1.p36.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="n\geq 2" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>≥</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">n\geq 2</annotation></semantics></math></span></p>
</div>
<div id="A2.SS7.SSS3.Px1.p37" class="ltx_para">
<table id="A2.Ex211" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A2.Ex211.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="u_{n+1}=f_{n}\left(f_{n-1}\left(u_{n-1}\right)\right)=u_{n-1}-\frac{13}{8n(n-1)}+\frac{c_{n}\left(u_{n}\right)}{n^{2}}-\frac{c_{n-1}\left(u_{n-1}\right)}{(n-1)^{2}}." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>u</mi><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><msub><mi>f</mi><mi>n</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>f</mi><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><msub><mi>u</mi><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>u</mi><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mo>−</mo><mfrac><mn>13</mn><mrow><mn>8</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>n</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mfrac></mrow><mo>+</mo><mfrac><mrow><msub><mi>c</mi><mi>n</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><msub><mi>u</mi><mi>n</mi></msub><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow><msup><mi>n</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></mfrac></mrow><mo>−</mo><mfrac><mrow><msub><mi>c</mi><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><msub><mi>u</mi><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup></mfrac></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">u_{n+1}=f_{n}\left(f_{n-1}\left(u_{n-1}\right)\right)=u_{n-1}-\frac{13}{8n(n-1)}+\frac{c_{n}\left(u_{n}\right)}{n^{2}}-\frac{c_{n-1}\left(u_{n-1}\right)}{(n-1)^{2}}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
<div id="A2.SS7.SSS3.Px1.p38" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A2.SS7.SSS3.Px1.p38.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.SS7.SSS3.Px1.p38.1.1" class="ltx_text">Note that</span></p>
</div>
<div id="A2.SS7.SSS3.Px1.p39" class="ltx_para">
<table id="A2.Ex212" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A2.Ex212.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="u_{101}=-0.54\ldots,\quad u_{102}=0.56\ldots," display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>u</mi><mn>101</mn></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mn>0.54</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="1.167em">,</mo><mrow><msub><mi>u</mi><mn>102</mn></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><mn>0.56</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">u_{101}=-0.54\ldots,\quad u_{102}=0.56\ldots,</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
<div id="A2.SS7.SSS3.Px1.p40" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A2.SS7.SSS3.Px1.p40.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.SS7.SSS3.Px1.p40.1.1" class="ltx_text">and</span></p>
</div>
<div id="A2.SS7.SSS3.Px1.p41" class="ltx_para">
<table id="A2.Ex213" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A2.Ex213.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="0\leq c_{n}(u)\leq 3" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mn>0</mn><mo>≤</mo><mrow><msub><mi>c</mi><mi>n</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>u</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mn>3</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">0\leq c_{n}(u)\leq 3</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
<div id="A2.SS7.SSS3.Px1.p42" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A2.SS7.SSS3.Px1.p42.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.SS7.SSS3.Px1.p42.1.1" class="ltx_text">if <math id="A2.SS7.SSS3.Px1.p42.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="n\geq 10" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>≥</mo><mn>10</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">n\geq 10</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="A2.SS7.SSS3.Px1.p42.m2" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="u\in[-6/10,8/10]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>u</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mo lspace="0em">−</mo><mn>6</mn><mo>/</mo><mn>10</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>8</mn><mo>/</mo><mn>10</mn><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">u\in[-6/10,8/10]</annotation></semantics></math>. Therefore and because for natural <math id="A2.SS7.SSS3.Px1.p42.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="m\geq 102" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>m</mi><mo>≥</mo><mn>102</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">m\geq 102</annotation></semantics></math> we have</span></p>
</div>
<div id="A2.SS7.SSS3.Px1.p43" class="ltx_para">
<table id="A2.Ex214" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A2.Ex214.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\sum_{n=m}^{\infty}\left(\frac{13}{8n(n-1)}+\frac{3}{(n-1)^{2}}\right)&lt;\frac{5}{m-2}\leq 0.05" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>=</mo><mi>m</mi></mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">∞</mi></munderover><mrow><mo lspace="0em">(</mo><mrow><mfrac><mn>13</mn><mrow><mn>8</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>n</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mfrac><mo>+</mo><mfrac><mn>3</mn><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup></mfrac></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>&lt;</mo><mfrac><mn>5</mn><mrow><mi>m</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></mfrac><mo>≤</mo><mn>0.05</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\sum_{n=m}^{\infty}\left(\frac{13}{8n(n-1)}+\frac{3}{(n-1)^{2}}\right)&lt;\frac{5}{m-2}\leq 0.05</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A2.SS7.SSS3.Px1.p43.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.SS7.SSS3.Px1.p43.1.1" class="ltx_text">it follows from (2) and (3) by induction that for all <math id="A2.SS7.SSS3.Px1.p43.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="n\geq 101" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>≥</mo><mn>101</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">n\geq 101</annotation></semantics></math> we have <math id="A2.SS7.SSS3.Px1.p43.m2" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="u_{n}\in[-6/10,8/10]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>u</mi><mi>n</mi></msub><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mo lspace="0em">−</mo><mn>6</mn><mo>/</mo><mn>10</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>8</mn><mo>/</mo><mn>10</mn><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">u_{n}\in[-6/10,8/10]</annotation></semantics></math> and hence <math id="A2.SS7.SSS3.Px1.p43.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="0\leq c_{n}\left(u_{n}\right)\leq 3" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mn>0</mn><mo>≤</mo><mrow><msub><mi>c</mi><mi>n</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><msub><mi>u</mi><mi>n</mi></msub><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mn>3</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">0\leq c_{n}\left(u_{n}\right)\leq 3</annotation></semantics></math>. So, again by (2), the sequences ( <math id="A2.SS7.SSS3.Px1.p43.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="u_{2m}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>u</mi><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>m</mi></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">u_{2m}</annotation></semantics></math> ) and ( <math id="A2.SS7.SSS3.Px1.p43.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="u_{2m+1}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>u</mi><mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>m</mi></mrow><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">u_{2m+1}</annotation></semantics></math> ) are Cauchyconvergent and hence convergent. Moreover, by (1), <math id="A2.SS7.SSS3.Px1.p43.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="u_{n+1}+u_{n}\rightarrow 0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>u</mi><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mo>+</mo><msub><mi>u</mi><mi>n</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">u_{n+1}+u_{n}\rightarrow 0</annotation></semantics></math>.</span></p>
</div>
<div id="A2.SS7.SSS3.Px1.p44" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A2.SS7.SSS3.Px1.p44.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.SS7.SSS3.Px1.p44.1.1" class="ltx_text">Thus, indeed</span></p>
</div>
<div id="A2.SS7.SSS3.Px1.p45" class="ltx_para">
<table id="A2.Ex215" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A2.Ex215.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="y_{n+1}+y_{n}\rightarrow 5/4" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>y</mi><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mo>+</mo><msub><mi>y</mi><mi>n</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><mrow><mn>5</mn><mo>/</mo><mn>4</mn></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">y_{n+1}+y_{n}\rightarrow 5/4</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
<div id="A2.SS7.SSS3.Px1.p46" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A2.SS7.SSS3.Px1.p46.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.SS7.SSS3.Px1.p46.1.1" class="ltx_text">and the sequences <math id="A2.SS7.SSS3.Px1.p46.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\left(y_{2m}\right)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo>(</mo><msub><mi>y</mi><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>m</mi></mrow></msub><mo>)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\left(y_{2m}\right)</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="A2.SS7.SSS3.Px1.p46.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\left(y_{2m+1}\right)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo>(</mo><msub><mi>y</mi><mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>m</mi></mrow><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mo>)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\left(y_{2m+1}\right)</annotation></semantics></math> are convergent. (The limits of these two sequences can in principle be found numerically with any degree of accuracy – controlled by (2), say.)
∎</span></p>
</div>
</div>
<div id="A2.SS7.SSS3.Px1.p47" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent"><span class="ltx_inline-block"><svg id="A2.SS7.SSS3.Px1.p47.pic1" class="ltx_picture" height="69.62" overflow="visible" version="1.1" viewBox="0 0 429.64 69.62" width="429.64"><g style="--ltx-stroke-color:#000000;--ltx-fill-color:#000000;" fill="#000000" stroke="#000000" stroke-width="0.4pt" transform="translate(0,69.62) matrix(1 0 0 -1 0 0)"><g style="--ltx-fill-color:#4D4D4D;" fill="#4D4D4D" fill-opacity="1.0"><path style="stroke:none" d="M 0 4.63 L 0 65 C 0 67.55 2.07 69.62 4.63 69.62 L 425.01 69.62 C 427.56 69.62 429.64 67.55 429.64 65 L 429.64 4.63 C 429.64 2.07 427.56 0 425.01 0 L 4.63 0 C 2.07 0 0 2.07 0 4.63 Z"></path></g><g style="--ltx-fill-color:#F9F9F9;" fill="#F9F9F9" fill-opacity="1.0"><path style="stroke:none" d="M 0.69 4.63 L 0.69 50.76 L 428.94 50.76 L 428.94 4.63 C 428.94 2.45 427.18 0.69 425.01 0.69 L 4.63 0.69 C 2.45 0.69 0.69 2.45 0.69 4.63 Z"></path></g><g fill-opacity="1.0" transform="matrix(1.0 0.0 0.0 1.0 20.38 55.39)"><foreignObject style="--ltx-fo-width:24.44em;--ltx-fo-height:0.69em;--ltx-fo-depth:0em;font-size:10pt;" height="9.61" overflow="visible" transform="matrix(1 0 0 -1 0 9.61)" width="338.18"><span class="ltx_foreignobject_container"><span class="ltx_foreignobject_content">
<span id="A2.SS7.SSS3.Px1.p47.pic1.1" class="ltx_inline-block ltx_minipage ltx_align_bottom" style="width:24.44em;">
<span id="A2.SS7.SSS3.Px1.p47.pic1.1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.SS7.SSS3.Px1.p47.pic1.1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold" style="--ltx-fg-color:#FFFFFF;">Rubric</span></span>
</span></span></span></foreignObject></g><g fill-opacity="1.0" transform="matrix(1.0 0.0 0.0 1.0 20.38 14.66)"><foreignObject style="--ltx-fo-width:33.06em;--ltx-fo-height:1.76em;--ltx-fo-depth:0.16em;font-size:10pt;" height="26.44" overflow="visible" transform="matrix(1 0 0 -1 0 24.29)" width="457.46"><span class="ltx_foreignobject_container"><span class="ltx_foreignobject_content">
<span id="A2.SS7.SSS3.Px1.p47.pic1.2" class="ltx_inline-block ltx_minipage ltx_align_bottom" style="width:33.06em;">
<span id="A2.SS7.SSS3.Px1.p47.pic1.2.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.SS7.SSS3.Px1.p47.pic1.2.1.1" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:80%;--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">Got 1 point if it proves that the limits of <math id="A2.SS7.SSS3.Px1.p47.pic1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="a_{2n}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">a</mi><mrow><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">n</mi></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">a_{2n}</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="A2.SS7.SSS3.Px1.p47.pic1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="a_{2n+1}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">a</mi><mrow><mrow><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">n</mi></mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">+</mo><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">1</mn></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">a_{2n+1}</annotation></semantics></math> exist. 
<br class="ltx_break">Got 1 point if it proves that the two limits are not equal.</span></span>
</span></span></span></foreignObject></g></g></svg></span>
</div>
<div id="A2.SS7.SSS3.Px1.p48" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent"><span class="ltx_inline-block"><svg id="A2.SS7.SSS3.Px1.p48.pic1" class="ltx_picture" height="54.13" overflow="visible" version="1.1" viewBox="0 0 429.64 54.13" width="429.64"><g style="--ltx-stroke-color:#000000;--ltx-fill-color:#000000;" fill="#000000" stroke="#000000" stroke-width="0.4pt" transform="translate(0,54.13) matrix(1 0 0 -1 0 0)"><g style="--ltx-fill-color:#5A996B;" fill="#5A996B" fill-opacity="1.0"><path style="stroke:none" d="M 0 4.63 L 0 49.51 C 0 52.06 2.07 54.13 4.63 54.13 L 425.01 54.13 C 427.56 54.13 429.64 52.06 429.64 49.51 L 429.64 4.63 C 429.64 2.07 427.56 0 425.01 0 L 4.63 0 C 2.07 0 0 2.07 0 4.63 Z"></path></g><g style="--ltx-fill-color:#F6FFF9;" fill="#F6FFF9" fill-opacity="1.0"><path style="stroke:none" d="M 0.69 4.63 L 0.69 35.38 L 428.94 35.38 L 428.94 4.63 C 428.94 2.45 427.18 0.69 425.01 0.69 L 4.63 0.69 C 2.45 0.69 0.69 2.45 0.69 4.63 Z"></path></g><g fill-opacity="1.0" transform="matrix(1.0 0.0 0.0 1.0 20.38 40.01)"><foreignObject style="--ltx-fo-width:24.44em;--ltx-fo-height:0.69em;--ltx-fo-depth:0em;font-size:10pt;" height="9.49" overflow="visible" transform="matrix(1 0 0 -1 0 9.49)" width="338.18"><span class="ltx_foreignobject_container"><span class="ltx_foreignobject_content">
<span id="A2.SS7.SSS3.Px1.p48.pic1.1" class="ltx_inline-block ltx_minipage ltx_align_bottom" style="width:24.44em;">
<span id="A2.SS7.SSS3.Px1.p48.pic1.1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.SS7.SSS3.Px1.p48.pic1.1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold" style="--ltx-fg-color:#FFFFFF;">Score</span></span>
</span></span></span></foreignObject></g><g fill-opacity="1.0" transform="matrix(1.0 0.0 0.0 1.0 20.38 15.27)"><foreignObject style="--ltx-fo-width:33.06em;--ltx-fo-height:0.6em;--ltx-fo-depth:0.2em;font-size:10pt;" height="11.07" overflow="visible" transform="matrix(1 0 0 -1 0 8.3)" width="457.46"><span class="ltx_foreignobject_container"><span class="ltx_foreignobject_content">
<span id="A2.SS7.SSS3.Px1.p48.pic1.2" class="ltx_inline-block ltx_minipage ltx_align_bottom" style="width:33.06em;">
<span id="A2.SS7.SSS3.Px1.p48.pic1.2.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.SS7.SSS3.Px1.p48.pic1.2.1.1" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:80%;--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">0/2</span></span>
</span></span></span></foreignObject></g></g></svg></span>
</div>
<div id="A2.SS7.SSS3.Px1.p49" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent"><span class="ltx_inline-block"><svg id="A2.SS7.SSS3.Px1.p49.pic1" class="ltx_picture" height="100.68" overflow="visible" version="1.1" viewBox="0 0 429.64 100.68" width="429.64"><g style="--ltx-stroke-color:#000000;--ltx-fill-color:#000000;" fill="#000000" stroke="#000000" stroke-width="0.4pt" transform="translate(0,100.68) matrix(1 0 0 -1 0 0)"><g style="--ltx-fill-color:#B33674;" fill="#B33674" fill-opacity="1.0"><path style="stroke:none" d="M 0 4.63 L 0 96.05 C 0 98.61 2.07 100.68 4.63 100.68 L 425.01 100.68 C 427.56 100.68 429.64 98.61 429.64 96.05 L 429.64 4.63 C 429.64 2.07 427.56 0 425.01 0 L 4.63 0 C 2.07 0 0 2.07 0 4.63 Z"></path></g><g style="--ltx-fill-color:#FFF2F9;" fill="#FFF2F9" fill-opacity="1.0"><path style="stroke:none" d="M 0.69 4.63 L 0.69 81.81 L 428.94 81.81 L 428.94 4.63 C 428.94 2.45 427.18 0.69 425.01 0.69 L 4.63 0.69 C 2.45 0.69 0.69 2.45 0.69 4.63 Z"></path></g><g fill-opacity="1.0" transform="matrix(1.0 0.0 0.0 1.0 20.38 86.44)"><foreignObject style="--ltx-fo-width:24.44em;--ltx-fo-height:0.69em;--ltx-fo-depth:0em;font-size:10pt;" height="9.61" overflow="visible" transform="matrix(1 0 0 -1 0 9.61)" width="338.18"><span class="ltx_foreignobject_container"><span class="ltx_foreignobject_content">
<span id="A2.SS7.SSS3.Px1.p49.pic1.1" class="ltx_inline-block ltx_minipage ltx_align_bottom" style="width:24.44em;">
<span id="A2.SS7.SSS3.Px1.p49.pic1.1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.SS7.SSS3.Px1.p49.pic1.1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold" style="--ltx-fg-color:#FFFFFF;">Evaluation</span></span>
</span></span></span></foreignObject></g><g fill-opacity="1.0" transform="matrix(1.0 0.0 0.0 1.0 20.38 12.5)"><foreignObject style="--ltx-fo-width:33.06em;--ltx-fo-height:4.16em;--ltx-fo-depth:0em;font-size:10pt;" height="57.5" overflow="visible" transform="matrix(1 0 0 -1 0 57.5)" width="457.46"><span class="ltx_foreignobject_container"><span class="ltx_foreignobject_content">
<span id="A2.SS7.SSS3.Px1.p49.pic1.2" class="ltx_inline-block ltx_minipage ltx_align_bottom" style="width:33.06em;">
<span id="A2.SS7.SSS3.Px1.p49.pic1.2.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.SS7.SSS3.Px1.p49.pic1.2.1.1" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:80%;--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">The solution does not demonstrate either point. 
<br class="ltx_break">It neither proves the existence of the limits of the subsequences <math id="A2.SS7.SSS3.Px1.p49.pic1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="a_{2n}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">a</mi><mrow><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">n</mi></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">a_{2n}</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="A2.SS7.SSS3.Px1.p49.pic1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="a_{2n+1}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">a</mi><mrow><mrow><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">n</mi></mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">+</mo><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">1</mn></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">a_{2n+1}</annotation></semantics></math>, 
<br class="ltx_break">nor shows that the two limits are distinct.</span></span>
</span></span></span></foreignObject></g></g></svg></span>
</div>
</section>
</section>
<section id="A2.SS7.SSS4" class="ltx_subsubsection">
<h4 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsubsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsubsection">(d) </span>Aesthetic judgment</h4>

<section id="A2.SS7.SSS4.Px1" class="ltx_paragraph">
<h5 class="ltx_title ltx_title_paragraph" style="--ltx-fg-color:#00E000;">Problem 7d1 </h5>

<div id="A2.SS7.SSS4.Px1.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A2.SS7.SSS4.Px1.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.SS7.SSS4.Px1.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text"></span>
<br class="ltx_break" style="--ltx-break-space:-10.0pt;"></p>
</div>
<div id="A2.SS7.SSS4.Px1.p2" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent"><span class="ltx_inline-block"><svg id="A2.SS7.SSS4.Px1.p2.pic1" class="ltx_picture" height="531.4" overflow="visible" version="1.1" viewBox="0 0 429.64 531.4" width="429.64"><g style="--ltx-stroke-color:#000000;--ltx-fill-color:#000000;" fill="#000000" stroke="#000000" stroke-width="0.4pt" transform="translate(0,531.4) matrix(1 0 0 -1 0 0)"><g style="--ltx-fill-color:#3D6666;" fill="#3D6666" fill-opacity="1.0"><path style="stroke:none" d="M 0 4.63 L 0 526.77 C 0 529.33 2.07 531.4 4.63 531.4 L 425.01 531.4 C 427.56 531.4 429.64 529.33 429.64 526.77 L 429.64 4.63 C 429.64 2.07 427.56 0 425.01 0 L 4.63 0 C 2.07 0 0 2.07 0 4.63 Z"></path></g><g style="--ltx-fill-color:#F9F9F9;" fill="#F9F9F9" fill-opacity="1.0"><path style="stroke:none" d="M 0.69 4.63 L 0.69 512.53 L 428.94 512.53 L 428.94 4.63 C 428.94 2.45 427.18 0.69 425.01 0.69 L 4.63 0.69 C 2.45 0.69 0.69 2.45 0.69 4.63 Z"></path></g><g fill-opacity="1.0" transform="matrix(1.0 0.0 0.0 1.0 20.38 517.16)"><foreignObject style="--ltx-fo-width:24.44em;--ltx-fo-height:0.69em;--ltx-fo-depth:0em;font-size:10pt;" height="9.61" overflow="visible" transform="matrix(1 0 0 -1 0 9.61)" width="338.18"><span class="ltx_foreignobject_container"><span class="ltx_foreignobject_content">
<span id="A2.SS7.SSS4.Px1.p2.pic1.1" class="ltx_inline-block ltx_minipage ltx_align_bottom" style="width:24.44em;">
<span id="A2.SS7.SSS4.Px1.p2.pic1.1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.SS7.SSS4.Px1.p2.pic1.1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold" style="--ltx-fg-color:#FFFFFF;">Problem</span></span>
</span></span></span></foreignObject></g><g fill-opacity="1.0" transform="matrix(1.0 0.0 0.0 1.0 20.38 14.66)"><foreignObject style="--ltx-fo-width:32.01em;--ltx-fo-height:35.13em;--ltx-fo-depth:0.16em;font-size:10pt;" height="488.22" overflow="visible" transform="matrix(1 0 0 -1 0 486.07)" width="442.93"><span class="ltx_foreignobject_container"><span class="ltx_foreignobject_content">
<span id="A2.SS7.SSS4.Px1.p2.pic1.2" class="ltx_inline-block ltx_minipage ltx_align_bottom" style="width:32.01em;">
<span id="A2.SS7.SSS4.Px1.p2.pic1.2.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.SS7.SSS4.Px1.p2.pic1.2.1.1" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:80%;--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">In a finite sequence of real numbers the sum of any seven successive terms is negative and the sum of any eleven successive terms is positive. Determine the maximum number of terms in the sequence.</span></span>
<span id="A2.SS7.SSS4.Px1.p2.pic1.2.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.SS7.SSS4.Px1.p2.pic1.2.2.1" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:80%;--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">Solution 1: Construction for <math id="A2.SS7.SSS4.Px1.p2.pic1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="n=16" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">n</mi><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">=</mo><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">16</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">n=16</annotation></semantics></math>. Define</span></span>
<span id="A2.Ex216" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<span><span class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<span class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></span>
<span class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A2.Ex216.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="a_{j}=\begin{cases}-13,&amp;j\in\{3,7,10,14\},\\
5,&amp;\text{otherwise}.\end{cases}" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" mathsize="0.800em">a</mi><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" mathsize="0.800em">j</mi></msub><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" mathsize="0.800em">=</mo><mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">{</mo><mtable columnspacing="5pt" displaystyle="true" rowspacing="0pt"><mtr><mtd class="ltx_align_left" columnalign="left"><mrow><mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" mathsize="0.800em">−</mo><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" mathsize="0.800em">13</mn></mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" mathsize="0.800em">,</mo></mrow></mtd><mtd class="ltx_align_left" columnalign="left"><mrow><mrow><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" mathsize="0.800em">j</mi><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" mathsize="0.800em">∈</mo><mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" stretchy="false">{</mo><mrow><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" mathsize="0.800em">3</mn><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" mathsize="0.800em">,</mo><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" mathsize="0.800em">7</mn><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" mathsize="0.800em">,</mo><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" mathsize="0.800em">10</mn><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" mathsize="0.800em">,</mo><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" mathsize="0.800em">14</mn></mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow></mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" mathsize="0.800em">,</mo></mrow></mtd></mtr><mtr><mtd class="ltx_align_left" columnalign="left"><mrow><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" mathsize="0.800em">5</mn><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" mathsize="0.800em">,</mo></mrow></mtd><mtd class="ltx_align_left" columnalign="left"><mrow><mtext style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" mathsize="0.800em">otherwise</mtext><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" lspace="0em" mathcolor="#000000" mathsize="0.800em">.</mo></mrow></mtd></mtr></mtable></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">a_{j}=\begin{cases}-13,&amp;j\in\{3,7,10,14\},\\
5,&amp;\text{otherwise}.\end{cases}</annotation></semantics></math></span>
<span class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></span></span></span>
</span>
<span id="A2.SS7.SSS4.Px1.p2.pic1.2.3" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.SS7.SSS4.Px1.p2.pic1.2.3.1" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:80%;--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">Any block of 7 consecutive terms then has exactly two entries equal to <math id="A2.SS7.SSS4.Px1.p2.pic1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="-13" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">−</mo><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">13</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">-13</annotation></semantics></math> and five entries equal to <math id="A2.SS7.SSS4.Px1.p2.pic1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="5" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">5</mn><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">5</annotation></semantics></math>, so
<math id="A2.SS7.SSS4.Px1.p2.pic1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="5\cdot 5-2\cdot 13=-1&lt;0." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mrow><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">5</mn><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" lspace="0.222em" mathcolor="#000000" rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">5</mn></mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">−</mo><mrow><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">2</mn><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" lspace="0.222em" mathcolor="#000000" rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">13</mn></mrow></mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">=</mo><mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">−</mo><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">1</mn></mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">&lt;</mo><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">0</mn></mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" lspace="0em" mathcolor="#000000">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">5\cdot 5-2\cdot 13=-1&lt;0.</annotation></semantics></math>
Any block of 11 consecutive terms has exactly three entries equal to <math id="A2.SS7.SSS4.Px1.p2.pic1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="-13" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">−</mo><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">13</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">-13</annotation></semantics></math> and eight entries equal to <math id="A2.SS7.SSS4.Px1.p2.pic1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="5" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">5</mn><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">5</annotation></semantics></math>, so
<math id="A2.SS7.SSS4.Px1.p2.pic1.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="8\cdot 5-3\cdot 13=1&gt;0." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mrow><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">8</mn><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" lspace="0.222em" mathcolor="#000000" rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">5</mn></mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">−</mo><mrow><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">3</mn><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" lspace="0.222em" mathcolor="#000000" rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">13</mn></mrow></mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">=</mo><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">1</mn><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">&gt;</mo><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">0</mn></mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" lspace="0em" mathcolor="#000000">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">8\cdot 5-3\cdot 13=1&gt;0.</annotation></semantics></math>
Thus the sequence meets the requirements.</span></span>
<span id="A2.SS7.SSS4.Px1.p2.pic1.2.4" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.SS7.SSS4.Px1.p2.pic1.2.4.1" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:80%;--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">Non<span id="A2.SS7.SSS4.Px1.p2.pic1.2.4.1.1" class="ltx_text">-</span>existence for <math id="A2.SS7.SSS4.Px1.p2.pic1.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="n\geq 17" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">n</mi><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">≥</mo><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">17</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">n\geq 17</annotation></semantics></math>. One checks (for example by linear<span id="A2.SS7.SSS4.Px1.p2.pic1.2.4.1.2" class="ltx_text">-</span>programming or averaging arguments) that the system</span></span>
<span id="A2.Ex217" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<span><span class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<span class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></span>
<span class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A2.Ex217.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\sum_{j=i}^{i+6}a_{j}&lt;0,\hskip 8.50012pt\sum_{j=i}^{i+10}a_{j}&gt;0" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><munderover><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" maxsize="0.800em" minsize="0.800em" movablelimits="false" stretchy="true">∑</mo><mrow><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" mathsize="0.800em">j</mi><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" mathsize="0.800em">=</mo><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" mathsize="0.800em">i</mi></mrow><mrow><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" mathsize="0.800em">i</mi><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" mathsize="0.800em">+</mo><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" mathsize="0.800em">6</mn></mrow></munderover><mrow><msub><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" mathsize="0.800em">a</mi><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" mathsize="0.800em">j</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" mathsize="0.800em">&lt;</mo><mrow><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" mathsize="0.800em">0</mn><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" mathsize="0.800em" rspace="0.850em">,</mo><mrow><munderover><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" maxsize="0.800em" minsize="0.800em" movablelimits="false" stretchy="true">∑</mo><mrow><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" mathsize="0.800em">j</mi><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" mathsize="0.800em">=</mo><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" mathsize="0.800em">i</mi></mrow><mrow><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" mathsize="0.800em">i</mi><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" mathsize="0.800em">+</mo><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" mathsize="0.800em">10</mn></mrow></munderover><msub><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" mathsize="0.800em">a</mi><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" mathsize="0.800em">j</mi></msub></mrow></mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" mathsize="0.800em">&gt;</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" mathsize="0.800em">0</mn></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\sum_{j=i}^{i+6}a_{j}&lt;0,\hskip 8.50012pt\sum_{j=i}^{i+10}a_{j}&gt;0</annotation></semantics></math></span>
<span class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></span></span></span>
</span>
<span id="A2.SS7.SSS4.Px1.p2.pic1.2.5" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.SS7.SSS4.Px1.p2.pic1.2.5.1" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:80%;--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">for <math id="A2.SS7.SSS4.Px1.p2.pic1.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="1\leq i\leq n-6" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">1</mn><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">≤</mo><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">i</mi><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">≤</mo><mrow><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">n</mi><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">−</mo><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">6</mn></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">1\leq i\leq n-6</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="A2.SS7.SSS4.Px1.p2.pic1.m10" class="ltx_Math" alttext="1\leq i\leq n-10" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">1</mn><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">≤</mo><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">i</mi><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">≤</mo><mrow><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">n</mi><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">−</mo><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">10</mn></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">1\leq i\leq n-10</annotation></semantics></math> has no solution once <math id="A2.SS7.SSS4.Px1.p2.pic1.m11" class="ltx_Math" alttext="n\geq 17" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">n</mi><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">≥</mo><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">17</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">n\geq 17</annotation></semantics></math>.</span></span>
<span id="A2.SS7.SSS4.Px1.p2.pic1.2.6" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.SS7.SSS4.Px1.p2.pic1.2.6.1" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:80%;--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">Hence the maximum possible length is <math id="A2.SS7.SSS4.Px1.p2.pic1.m12" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\boxed{16}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><menclose notation="box"><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">16</mn></menclose><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\boxed{16}</annotation></semantics></math>.</span></span>
<span id="A2.SS7.SSS4.Px1.p2.pic1.2.7" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.SS7.SSS4.Px1.p2.pic1.2.7.1" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:80%;--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">Solution 2:
Let <math id="A2.SS7.SSS4.Px1.p2.pic1.m13" class="ltx_Math" alttext="x_{1},x_{2},\ldots" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">x</mi><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">1</mn></msub><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">,</mo><msub><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">x</mi><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">2</mn></msub><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">,</mo><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" mathvariant="normal">…</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">x_{1},x_{2},\ldots</annotation></semantics></math> be the given sequence and let <math id="A2.SS7.SSS4.Px1.p2.pic1.m14" class="ltx_Math" alttext="s_{n}=x_{1}+x_{2}+\ldots+x_{n}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">s</mi><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">n</mi></msub><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">=</mo><mrow><msub><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">x</mi><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">1</mn></msub><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">+</mo><msub><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">x</mi><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">2</mn></msub><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">+</mo><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">+</mo><msub><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">x</mi><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">n</mi></msub></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">s_{n}=x_{1}+x_{2}+\ldots+x_{n}</annotation></semantics></math>. The conditions from the hypothesis can be now written as <math id="A2.SS7.SSS4.Px1.p2.pic1.m15" class="ltx_Math" alttext="s_{n+7}&lt;s_{n}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">s</mi><mrow><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">n</mi><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">+</mo><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">7</mn></mrow></msub><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">&lt;</mo><msub><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">s</mi><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">n</mi></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">s_{n+7}&lt;s_{n}</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="A2.SS7.SSS4.Px1.p2.pic1.m16" class="ltx_Math" alttext="s_{n+11}&gt;s_{n}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">s</mi><mrow><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">n</mi><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">+</mo><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">11</mn></mrow></msub><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">&gt;</mo><msub><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">s</mi><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">n</mi></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">s_{n+11}&gt;s_{n}</annotation></semantics></math> for all <math id="A2.SS7.SSS4.Px1.p2.pic1.m17" class="ltx_Math" alttext="n\geq 1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">n</mi><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">≥</mo><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">1</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">n\geq 1</annotation></semantics></math>. We then have:
<math id="A2.SS7.SSS4.Px1.p2.pic1.m18" class="ltx_Math" alttext="0&lt;s_{11}&lt;s_{4}&lt;s_{15}&lt;s_{8}&lt;s_{1}&lt;s_{12}&lt;s_{5}&lt;s_{16}&lt;s_{9}&lt;s_{2}&lt;s_{13}&lt;s_{6}&lt;s_{17}&lt;s_{10}&lt;s_{3}&lt;s_{14}&lt;s_{7}&lt;0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">0</mn><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">&lt;</mo><msub><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">s</mi><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">11</mn></msub><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">&lt;</mo><msub><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">s</mi><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">4</mn></msub><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">&lt;</mo><msub><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">s</mi><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">15</mn></msub><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">&lt;</mo><msub><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">s</mi><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">8</mn></msub><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">&lt;</mo><msub><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">s</mi><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">1</mn></msub><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">&lt;</mo><msub><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">s</mi><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">12</mn></msub><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">&lt;</mo><msub><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">s</mi><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">5</mn></msub><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">&lt;</mo><msub><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">s</mi><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">16</mn></msub><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">&lt;</mo><msub><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">s</mi><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">9</mn></msub><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">&lt;</mo><msub><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">s</mi><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">2</mn></msub><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">&lt;</mo><msub><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">s</mi><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">13</mn></msub><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">&lt;</mo><msub><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">s</mi><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">6</mn></msub><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">&lt;</mo><msub><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">s</mi><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">17</mn></msub><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">&lt;</mo><msub><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">s</mi><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">10</mn></msub><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">&lt;</mo><msub><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">s</mi><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">3</mn></msub><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">&lt;</mo><msub><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">s</mi><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">14</mn></msub><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">&lt;</mo><msub><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">s</mi><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">7</mn></msub><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">&lt;</mo><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">0&lt;s_{11}&lt;s_{4}&lt;s_{15}&lt;s_{8}&lt;s_{1}&lt;s_{12}&lt;s_{5}&lt;s_{16}&lt;s_{9}&lt;s_{2}&lt;s_{13}&lt;s_{6}&lt;s_{17}&lt;s_{10}&lt;s_{3}&lt;s_{14}&lt;s_{7}&lt;0</annotation></semantics></math>, a contradiction.
Therefore, the sequence cannot have 17 terms. In order to show that 16 is the answer, just take 16 real numbers satisfying <math id="A2.SS7.SSS4.Px1.p2.pic1.m19" class="ltx_Math" alttext="s_{10}&lt;s_{3}&lt;s_{14}&lt;s_{7}&lt;0&lt;s_{11}&lt;s_{4}&lt;s_{15}&lt;s_{8}&lt;s_{1}&lt;s_{12}&lt;s_{5}&lt;s_{16}&lt;s_{9}&lt;s_{2}&lt;s_{13}&lt;s_{6}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">s</mi><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">10</mn></msub><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">&lt;</mo><msub><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">s</mi><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">3</mn></msub><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">&lt;</mo><msub><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">s</mi><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">14</mn></msub><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">&lt;</mo><msub><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">s</mi><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">7</mn></msub><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">&lt;</mo><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">0</mn><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">&lt;</mo><msub><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">s</mi><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">11</mn></msub><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">&lt;</mo><msub><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">s</mi><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">4</mn></msub><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">&lt;</mo><msub><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">s</mi><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">15</mn></msub><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">&lt;</mo><msub><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">s</mi><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">8</mn></msub><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">&lt;</mo><msub><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">s</mi><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">1</mn></msub><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">&lt;</mo><msub><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">s</mi><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">12</mn></msub><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">&lt;</mo><msub><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">s</mi><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">5</mn></msub><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">&lt;</mo><msub><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">s</mi><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">16</mn></msub><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">&lt;</mo><msub><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">s</mi><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">9</mn></msub><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">&lt;</mo><msub><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">s</mi><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">2</mn></msub><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">&lt;</mo><msub><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">s</mi><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">13</mn></msub><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">&lt;</mo><msub><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">s</mi><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">6</mn></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">s_{10}&lt;s_{3}&lt;s_{14}&lt;s_{7}&lt;0&lt;s_{11}&lt;s_{4}&lt;s_{15}&lt;s_{8}&lt;s_{1}&lt;s_{12}&lt;s_{5}&lt;s_{16}&lt;s_{9}&lt;s_{2}&lt;s_{13}&lt;s_{6}</annotation></semantics></math>. We have <math id="A2.SS7.SSS4.Px1.p2.pic1.m20" class="ltx_Math" alttext="x_{1}=s_{1}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">x</mi><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">1</mn></msub><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">=</mo><msub><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">s</mi><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">1</mn></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">x_{1}=s_{1}</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="A2.SS7.SSS4.Px1.p2.pic1.m21" class="ltx_Math" alttext="x_{n}=s_{n}-s_{n-1}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">x</mi><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">n</mi></msub><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">=</mo><mrow><msub><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">s</mi><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">n</mi></msub><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">−</mo><msub><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">s</mi><mrow><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">n</mi><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">−</mo><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">1</mn></mrow></msub></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">x_{n}=s_{n}-s_{n-1}</annotation></semantics></math> for <math id="A2.SS7.SSS4.Px1.p2.pic1.m22" class="ltx_Math" alttext="n\geq 2" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">n</mi><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">≥</mo><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">2</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">n\geq 2</annotation></semantics></math>. Thus we found all sequences with the given properties.</span></span>
<span id="A2.SS7.SSS4.Px1.p2.pic1.2.8" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.SS7.SSS4.Px1.p2.pic1.2.8.1" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:80%;--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">Which do you find more elegant, and why? Discuss in terms of simplicity, symmetry, or conceptual insight.</span></span><span class="ltx_inline-block"><svg id="A2.SS7.SSS4.Px1.p2.pic1.pic1" class="ltx_picture" color="#008000" height="18.24" overflow="visible" style="vertical-align:-4.1px" version="1.1" viewBox="0 0 18.24 18.24" width="18.24"><g style="--ltx-stroke-color:#009900;--ltx-fill-color:#009900;--ltx-fg-color:#009900;" color="#009900" fill="#009900" stroke="#009900" stroke-width="1.8pt" transform="translate(0,18.24) matrix(1 0 0 -1 0 0) translate(1.25,0) translate(0,1.25)"><path style="fill:none" d="M 0 7.87 L 5.51 0 L 15.75 15.75"></path></g></svg></span>
<span id="A2.SS7.SSS4.Px1.p2.pic1.2.9" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.SS7.SSS4.Px1.p2.pic1.2.9.1" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:80%;--ltx-fg-color:#008000;">GPT-5 thinking passed</span></span>
<span id="A2.SS7.SSS4.Px1.p2.pic1.2.10" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.SS7.SSS4.Px1.p2.pic1.2.10.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic" style="font-size:80%;--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">Proposed by Jiaxin Zhang</span></span>
</span></span></span></foreignObject></g></g></svg></span>
</div>
<div id="A2.SS7.SSS4.Px1.1" class="ltx_proof">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_font_italic ltx_title_proof"><span id="A2.SS7.SSS4.Px1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Response of GPT-5-thinking</span>.</h6>
<div id="A2.SS7.SSS4.Px1.p3" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A2.SS7.SSS4.Px1.p3.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.SS7.SSS4.Px1.p3.1.1" class="ltx_text">Both hit the right answer (16), but I’d call **Solution 2 more elegant**. Here’s why, along the three axes you asked for:</span></p>
</div>
<div id="A2.SS7.SSS4.Px1.p4" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A2.SS7.SSS4.Px1.p4.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.SS7.SSS4.Px1.p4.1.1" class="ltx_text">**Simplicity**</span></p>
</div>
<div id="A2.SS7.SSS4.Px1.p5" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A2.SS7.SSS4.Px1.p5.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.SS7.SSS4.Px1.p5.1.1" class="ltx_text">* *Solution 1*: the 16-term construction <math id="A2.SS7.SSS4.Px1.p5.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(-13,5,\dots)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>13</mn></mrow><mo>,</mo><mn>5</mn><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(-13,5,\dots)</annotation></semantics></math> is super easy to verify—great for existence. But the upper bound is left as “one checks (LP/averaging)”, i.e., it leans on heavier or unspecified machinery.
* *Solution 2*: once you pass to partial sums <math id="A2.SS7.SSS4.Px1.p5.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="s_{n}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>s</mi><mi>n</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">s_{n}</annotation></semantics></math>, the whole problem reduces to the clean rule</span></p>
</div>
<div id="A2.SS7.SSS4.Px1.p6" class="ltx_para">
<table id="A2.Ex218" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A2.Ex218.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="s_{n+11}&gt;s_{n}&gt;s_{n+7}," display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>s</mi><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>11</mn></mrow></msub><mo>&gt;</mo><msub><mi>s</mi><mi>n</mi></msub><mo>&gt;</mo><msub><mi>s</mi><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>7</mn></mrow></msub></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">s_{n+11}&gt;s_{n}&gt;s_{n+7},</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
<div id="A2.SS7.SSS4.Px1.p7" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A2.SS7.SSS4.Px1.p7.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.SS7.SSS4.Px1.p7.1.1" class="ltx_text">and a single interleaving chain gives <math id="A2.SS7.SSS4.Px1.p7.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="n\leq 16" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>≤</mo><mn>16</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">n\leq 16</annotation></semantics></math>. No guessing constants; no numeric fiddling.</span></p>
</div>
<div id="A2.SS7.SSS4.Px1.p8" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A2.SS7.SSS4.Px1.p8.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.SS7.SSS4.Px1.p8.1.1" class="ltx_text">**Symmetry**</span></p>
</div>
<div id="A2.SS7.SSS4.Px1.p9" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A2.SS7.SSS4.Px1.p9.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.SS7.SSS4.Px1.p9.1.1" class="ltx_text">* *Solution 1* breaks symmetry by picking specific values <math id="A2.SS7.SSS4.Px1.p9.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="5" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mn>5</mn><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">5</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="A2.SS7.SSS4.Px1.p9.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="-13" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>13</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">-13</annotation></semantics></math>.
* *Solution 2* treats the two window lengths <math id="A2.SS7.SSS4.Px1.p9.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="7" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mn>7</mn><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">7</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="A2.SS7.SSS4.Px1.p9.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="11" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mn>11</mn><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">11</annotation></semantics></math> on equal footing: the inequalities for <math id="A2.SS7.SSS4.Px1.p9.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="s_{n+7}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>s</mi><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>7</mn></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">s_{n+7}</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="A2.SS7.SSS4.Px1.p9.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="s_{n+11}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>s</mi><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>11</mn></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">s_{n+11}</annotation></semantics></math> interlace in a perfectly symmetric “zig-zag”. The number <math id="A2.SS7.SSS4.Px1.p9.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="16=7+11-2" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mn>16</mn><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mn>7</mn><mo>+</mo><mn>11</mn></mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">16=7+11-2</annotation></semantics></math> emerges naturally from this interleaving.</span></p>
</div>
<div id="A2.SS7.SSS4.Px1.p10" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A2.SS7.SSS4.Px1.p10.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.SS7.SSS4.Px1.p10.1.1" class="ltx_text">**Conceptual insight**</span></p>
</div>
<div id="A2.SS7.SSS4.Px1.p11" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A2.SS7.SSS4.Px1.p11.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.SS7.SSS4.Px1.p11.1.1" class="ltx_text">* *Solution 1* shows a witness and (with an external argument) a bound, but doesn’t reveal the mechanism.
* *Solution 2* exposes the core idea: the *order* constraints on partial sums force a long strictly increasing–decreasing chain that cannot wrap around if <math id="A2.SS7.SSS4.Px1.p11.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="n\geq 17" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>≥</mo><mn>17</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">n\geq 17</annotation></semantics></math>. This viewpoint generalizes: the method explains why, in this case, the maximal length is <math id="A2.SS7.SSS4.Px1.p11.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="7+11-2" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mn>7</mn><mo>+</mo><mn>11</mn></mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">7+11-2</annotation></semantics></math>.</span></p>
</div>
<div id="A2.SS7.SSS4.Px1.p12" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A2.SS7.SSS4.Px1.p12.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.SS7.SSS4.Px1.p12.1.1" class="ltx_text">**Best of both worlds:** use Solution 1 for a tiny, checkable construction of length <math id="A2.SS7.SSS4.Px1.p12.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="16" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mn>16</mn><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">16</annotation></semantics></math>, and Solution 2 for the clean, parameter-free upper bound. That combination is short, symmetric, and conceptually transparent.</span></p>
</div>
<div id="A2.SS7.SSS4.Px1.p13" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A2.SS7.SSS4.Px1.p13.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.SS7.SSS4.Px1.p13.1.1" class="ltx_text">∎</span></p>
</div>
</div>
<div id="A2.SS7.SSS4.Px1.p14" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent"><span class="ltx_inline-block"><svg id="A2.SS7.SSS4.Px1.p14.pic1" class="ltx_picture" height="102.83" overflow="visible" version="1.1" viewBox="0 0 429.64 102.83" width="429.64"><g style="--ltx-stroke-color:#000000;--ltx-fill-color:#000000;" fill="#000000" stroke="#000000" stroke-width="0.4pt" transform="translate(0,102.83) matrix(1 0 0 -1 0 0)"><g style="--ltx-fill-color:#4D4D4D;" fill="#4D4D4D" fill-opacity="1.0"><path style="stroke:none" d="M 0 4.63 L 0 98.2 C 0 100.76 2.07 102.83 4.63 102.83 L 425.01 102.83 C 427.56 102.83 429.64 100.76 429.64 98.2 L 429.64 4.63 C 429.64 2.07 427.56 0 425.01 0 L 4.63 0 C 2.07 0 0 2.07 0 4.63 Z"></path></g><g style="--ltx-fill-color:#F9F9F9;" fill="#F9F9F9" fill-opacity="1.0"><path style="stroke:none" d="M 0.69 4.63 L 0.69 83.97 L 428.94 83.97 L 428.94 4.63 C 428.94 2.45 427.18 0.69 425.01 0.69 L 4.63 0.69 C 2.45 0.69 0.69 2.45 0.69 4.63 Z"></path></g><g fill-opacity="1.0" transform="matrix(1.0 0.0 0.0 1.0 20.38 88.6)"><foreignObject style="--ltx-fo-width:24.44em;--ltx-fo-height:0.69em;--ltx-fo-depth:0em;font-size:10pt;" height="9.61" overflow="visible" transform="matrix(1 0 0 -1 0 9.61)" width="338.18"><span class="ltx_foreignobject_container"><span class="ltx_foreignobject_content">
<span id="A2.SS7.SSS4.Px1.p14.pic1.1" class="ltx_inline-block ltx_minipage ltx_align_bottom" style="width:24.44em;">
<span id="A2.SS7.SSS4.Px1.p14.pic1.1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.SS7.SSS4.Px1.p14.pic1.1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold" style="--ltx-fg-color:#FFFFFF;">Rubric</span></span>
</span></span></span></foreignObject></g><g fill-opacity="1.0" transform="matrix(1.0 0.0 0.0 1.0 20.38 14.66)"><foreignObject style="--ltx-fo-width:33.06em;--ltx-fo-height:4.16em;--ltx-fo-depth:0.16em;font-size:10pt;" height="59.65" overflow="visible" transform="matrix(1 0 0 -1 0 57.5)" width="457.46"><span class="ltx_foreignobject_container"><span class="ltx_foreignobject_content">
<span id="A2.SS7.SSS4.Px1.p14.pic1.2" class="ltx_inline-block ltx_minipage ltx_align_bottom" style="width:33.06em;">
<span id="A2.SS7.SSS4.Px1.p14.pic1.2.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.SS7.SSS4.Px1.p14.pic1.2.1.1" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:80%;--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">1. Solution 2 is more elegant.</span></span>
<span id="A2.SS7.SSS4.Px1.p14.pic1.2.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.SS7.SSS4.Px1.p14.pic1.2.2.1" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:80%;--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">2. Solution 1 provides an concrete examples and uses linear programming, which is hard to verify.</span></span>
<span id="A2.SS7.SSS4.Px1.p14.pic1.2.3" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.SS7.SSS4.Px1.p14.pic1.2.3.1" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:80%;--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">3. Solution 2 explains the reason and shows why the bound is 16.</span></span>
</span></span></span></foreignObject></g></g></svg></span>
</div>
<div id="A2.SS7.SSS4.Px1.p15" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent"><span class="ltx_inline-block"><svg id="A2.SS7.SSS4.Px1.p15.pic1" class="ltx_picture" height="54.13" overflow="visible" version="1.1" viewBox="0 0 429.64 54.13" width="429.64"><g style="--ltx-stroke-color:#000000;--ltx-fill-color:#000000;" fill="#000000" stroke="#000000" stroke-width="0.4pt" transform="translate(0,54.13) matrix(1 0 0 -1 0 0)"><g style="--ltx-fill-color:#5A996B;" fill="#5A996B" fill-opacity="1.0"><path style="stroke:none" d="M 0 4.63 L 0 49.51 C 0 52.06 2.07 54.13 4.63 54.13 L 425.01 54.13 C 427.56 54.13 429.64 52.06 429.64 49.51 L 429.64 4.63 C 429.64 2.07 427.56 0 425.01 0 L 4.63 0 C 2.07 0 0 2.07 0 4.63 Z"></path></g><g style="--ltx-fill-color:#F6FFF9;" fill="#F6FFF9" fill-opacity="1.0"><path style="stroke:none" d="M 0.69 4.63 L 0.69 35.38 L 428.94 35.38 L 428.94 4.63 C 428.94 2.45 427.18 0.69 425.01 0.69 L 4.63 0.69 C 2.45 0.69 0.69 2.45 0.69 4.63 Z"></path></g><g fill-opacity="1.0" transform="matrix(1.0 0.0 0.0 1.0 20.38 40.01)"><foreignObject style="--ltx-fo-width:24.44em;--ltx-fo-height:0.69em;--ltx-fo-depth:0em;font-size:10pt;" height="9.49" overflow="visible" transform="matrix(1 0 0 -1 0 9.49)" width="338.18"><span class="ltx_foreignobject_container"><span class="ltx_foreignobject_content">
