</span></span></span></foreignObject></g><g fill-opacity="1.0" transform="matrix(1.0 0.0 0.0 1.0 20.38 15.39)"><foreignObject style="--ltx-fo-width:33.06em;--ltx-fo-height:0.6em;--ltx-fo-depth:0.21em;font-size:10pt;" height="11.19" overflow="visible" transform="matrix(1 0 0 -1 0 8.3)" width="457.46"><span class="ltx_foreignobject_container"><span class="ltx_foreignobject_content">
<span id="A2.SS8.SSS1.Px1.p16.pic1.2" class="ltx_inline-block ltx_minipage ltx_align_bottom" style="width:33.06em;">
<span id="A2.SS8.SSS1.Px1.p16.pic1.2.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.SS8.SSS1.Px1.p16.pic1.2.1.1" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:80%;--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">This solution is wrong. <math id="A2.SS8.SSS1.Px1.p16.pic1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(d_{i},c_{j})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">d</mi><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">i</mi></msub><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">,</mo><msub><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">c</mi><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">j</mi></msub><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(d_{i},c_{j})</annotation></semantics></math> is not necessarily a “gap".</span></span>
</span></span></span></foreignObject></g></g></svg></span>
</div>
</section>
<section id="A2.SS8.SSS1.Px2" class="ltx_paragraph">
<h5 class="ltx_title ltx_title_paragraph" style="--ltx-fg-color:#FF0000;">Problem 8a2</h5>

<div id="A2.SS8.SSS1.Px2.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A2.SS8.SSS1.Px2.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.SS8.SSS1.Px2.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text"></span>
<br class="ltx_break" style="--ltx-break-space:-10.0pt;"></p>
</div>
<div id="A2.SS8.SSS1.Px2.p2" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent"><span class="ltx_inline-block"><svg id="A2.SS8.SSS1.Px2.p2.pic1" class="ltx_picture" height="216.55" overflow="visible" version="1.1" viewBox="0 0 429.64 216.55" width="429.64"><g style="--ltx-stroke-color:#000000;--ltx-fill-color:#000000;" fill="#000000" stroke="#000000" stroke-width="0.4pt" transform="translate(0,216.55) matrix(1 0 0 -1 0 0)"><g style="--ltx-fill-color:#3D6666;" fill="#3D6666" fill-opacity="1.0"><path style="stroke:none" d="M 0 4.63 L 0 211.92 C 0 214.47 2.07 216.55 4.63 216.55 L 425.01 216.55 C 427.56 216.55 429.64 214.47 429.64 211.92 L 429.64 4.63 C 429.64 2.07 427.56 0 425.01 0 L 4.63 0 C 2.07 0 0 2.07 0 4.63 Z"></path></g><g style="--ltx-fill-color:#F9F9F9;" fill="#F9F9F9" fill-opacity="1.0"><path style="stroke:none" d="M 0.69 4.63 L 0.69 197.68 L 428.94 197.68 L 428.94 4.63 C 428.94 2.45 427.18 0.69 425.01 0.69 L 4.63 0.69 C 2.45 0.69 0.69 2.45 0.69 4.63 Z"></path></g><g fill-opacity="1.0" transform="matrix(1.0 0.0 0.0 1.0 20.38 202.31)"><foreignObject style="--ltx-fo-width:24.44em;--ltx-fo-height:0.69em;--ltx-fo-depth:0em;font-size:10pt;" height="9.61" overflow="visible" transform="matrix(1 0 0 -1 0 9.61)" width="338.18"><span class="ltx_foreignobject_container"><span class="ltx_foreignobject_content">
<span id="A2.SS8.SSS1.Px2.p2.pic1.1" class="ltx_inline-block ltx_minipage ltx_align_bottom" style="width:24.44em;">
<span id="A2.SS8.SSS1.Px2.p2.pic1.1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.SS8.SSS1.Px2.p2.pic1.1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold" style="--ltx-fg-color:#FFFFFF;">Problem</span></span>
</span></span></span></foreignObject></g><g fill-opacity="1.0" transform="matrix(1.0 0.0 0.0 1.0 20.38 14.66)"><foreignObject style="--ltx-fo-width:32.01em;--ltx-fo-height:12.37em;--ltx-fo-depth:0.16em;font-size:10pt;" height="173.37" overflow="visible" transform="matrix(1 0 0 -1 0 171.22)" width="442.93"><span class="ltx_foreignobject_container"><span class="ltx_foreignobject_content">
<span id="A2.SS8.SSS1.Px2.p2.pic1.2" class="ltx_inline-block ltx_minipage ltx_align_bottom" style="width:32.01em;">
<span id="A2.SS8.SSS1.Px2.p2.pic1.2.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.SS8.SSS1.Px2.p2.pic1.2.1.1" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:80%;--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">Let <math id="A2.SS8.SSS1.Px2.p2.pic1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="*" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">∗</mo><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">*</annotation></semantics></math> denote an arbitrary binary operation The constant property <math id="A2.SS8.SSS1.Px2.p2.pic1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="x*y=z*w" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">x</mi><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" lspace="0.222em" mathcolor="#000000" rspace="0.222em">∗</mo><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">y</mi></mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">=</mo><mrow><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">z</mi><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" lspace="0.222em" mathcolor="#000000" rspace="0.222em">∗</mo><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">w</mi></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">x*y=z*w</annotation></semantics></math> implies the
commutative property <math id="A2.SS8.SSS1.Px2.p2.pic1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="x*y=y*x" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">x</mi><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" lspace="0.222em" mathcolor="#000000" rspace="0.222em">∗</mo><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">y</mi></mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">=</mo><mrow><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">y</mi><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" lspace="0.222em" mathcolor="#000000" rspace="0.222em">∗</mo><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">x</mi></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">x*y=y*x</annotation></semantics></math>, but the commutative property does not imply the constant
property. Is there a property strictly in between these? So that it is implied by the constant property
and it implies the commutative properties, but both of these implications are false in the opposite
direction. Your property cannot refer to auxiliary fixed elements or use quantifiers and it must be
expressed by a single equation (so you cannot say commutative+associative)</span></span><span class="ltx_inline-block"><svg id="A2.SS8.SSS1.Px2.p2.pic1.pic1" class="ltx_picture" color="#FF0000" height="18.24" overflow="visible" style="vertical-align:-4.1px" version="1.1" viewBox="0 0 18.24 18.24" width="18.24"><g style="--ltx-stroke-color:#FF0000;--ltx-fill-color:#FF0000;" fill="#FF0000" stroke="#FF0000" stroke-width="1.8pt" transform="translate(0,18.24) matrix(1 0 0 -1 0 0) translate(1.25,0) translate(0,1.25)"><path style="fill:none" d="M 0 0 L 15.75 15.75 M 0 15.75 L 15.75 0"></path></g></svg></span>
<span id="A2.SS8.SSS1.Px2.p2.pic1.2.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.SS8.SSS1.Px2.p2.pic1.2.2.1" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:80%;--ltx-fg-color:#FF0000;">GPT-5 thinking failed</span></span>
<span id="A2.SS8.SSS1.Px2.p2.pic1.2.3" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.SS8.SSS1.Px2.p2.pic1.2.3.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic" style="font-size:80%;--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">Proposed by Tahsin Saffat</span></span>
</span></span></span></foreignObject></g></g></svg></span>
</div>
<div id="A2.SS8.SSS1.Px2.1" class="ltx_proof">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_font_italic ltx_title_proof"><span id="A2.SS8.SSS1.Px2.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Response of GPT-5-thinking</span>.</h6>
<div id="A2.SS8.SSS1.Px2.p3" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A2.SS8.SSS1.Px2.p3.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.SS8.SSS1.Px2.p3.1.1" class="ltx_text">Yes. Here’s one (written as a single equational law, no constants, no quantifiers):</span></p>
</div>
<div id="A2.SS8.SSS1.Px2.p4" class="ltx_para">
<table id="A2.Ex223" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A2.Ex223.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\boxed{\;x*(y*z)\;=\;(z*x)*x\;}\qquad(\star)" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><menclose notation="box"><mrow><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">∗</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>y</mi><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">∗</mo><mi>z</mi></mrow><mo rspace="0.280em" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.558em">=</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>z</mi><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">∗</mo><mi>x</mi></mrow><mo rspace="0.055em" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo rspace="0.222em">∗</mo><mi>x</mi></mrow></mrow></menclose><mspace style="width:2em;" width="2em"></mspace><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">⋆</mo><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\boxed{\;x*(y*z)\;=\;(z*x)*x\;}\qquad(\star)</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
<div id="A2.SS8.SSS1.Px2.p5" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A2.SS8.SSS1.Px2.p5.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.SS8.SSS1.Px2.p5.1.1" class="ltx_text">Why it sits strictly between “constant” and “commutative”</span></p>
</div>
<div id="A2.SS8.SSS1.Px2.p6" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A2.SS8.SSS1.Px2.p6.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.SS8.SSS1.Px2.p6.1.1" class="ltx_text">* **Constant <math id="A2.SS8.SSS1.Px2.p6.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\implies" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mo stretchy="false">⟹</mo><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\implies</annotation></semantics></math> (⁢)**: If <math id="A2.SS8.SSS1.Px2.p6.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="*" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mo>∗</mo><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">*</annotation></semantics></math> is constant (i.e., every product equals the same element), then every term built from <math id="A2.SS8.SSS1.Px2.p6.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="*" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mo>∗</mo><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">*</annotation></semantics></math> evaluates to that element, so any equation in the language of <math id="A2.SS8.SSS1.Px2.p6.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="*" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mo>∗</mo><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">*</annotation></semantics></math> holds in particular <math id="A2.SS8.SSS1.Px2.p6.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(\star)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">⋆</mo><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(\star)</annotation></semantics></math>.</span></p>
</div>
<div id="A2.SS8.SSS1.Px2.p7" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A2.SS8.SSS1.Px2.p7.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.SS8.SSS1.Px2.p7.1.1" class="ltx_text">* **(⁢) <math id="A2.SS8.SSS1.Px2.p7.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\implies" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mo stretchy="false">⟹</mo><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\implies</annotation></semantics></math> commutative**: From <math id="A2.SS8.SSS1.Px2.p7.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(\star)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">⋆</mo><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(\star)</annotation></semantics></math> we get</span></p>
</div>
<div id="A2.SS8.SSS1.Px2.p8" class="ltx_para">
<table id="A2.Ex224" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A2.Ex224.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="x*(y*y)=(y*x)*x\quad\text{and}\quad y*(x*x)=(x*y)*y" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">∗</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>y</mi><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">∗</mo><mi>y</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>y</mi><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">∗</mo><mi>x</mi></mrow><mo rspace="0.055em" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo rspace="0.222em">∗</mo><mi>x</mi></mrow></mrow><mspace style="width:1em;" width="1em"></mspace><mtext>and</mtext><mspace style="width:1em;" width="1em"></mspace><mrow><mrow><mi>y</mi><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">∗</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">∗</mo><mi>x</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">∗</mo><mi>y</mi></mrow><mo rspace="0.055em" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo rspace="0.222em">∗</mo><mi>y</mi></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">x*(y*y)=(y*x)*x\quad\text{and}\quad y*(x*x)=(x*y)*y</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
<div id="A2.SS8.SSS1.Px2.p9" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A2.SS8.SSS1.Px2.p9.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.SS8.SSS1.Px2.p9.1.1" class="ltx_text">(by swapping variables appropriately). These let you shuffle factors through squares; a short equational chase (instantiating <math id="A2.SS8.SSS1.Px2.p9.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(\star)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">⋆</mo><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(\star)</annotation></semantics></math> again inside these terms) yields <math id="A2.SS8.SSS1.Px2.p9.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="x*y=y*x" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">∗</mo><mi>y</mi></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>y</mi><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">∗</mo><mi>x</mi></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">x*y=y*x</annotation></semantics></math>. (Intuitively, <math id="A2.SS8.SSS1.Px2.p9.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(\star)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">⋆</mo><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(\star)</annotation></semantics></math> forces every left-translate <math id="A2.SS8.SSS1.Px2.p9.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="t\mapsto x*t" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">↦</mo><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">∗</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">t\mapsto x*t</annotation></semantics></math> to “forget” the order of the inputs once an <math id="A2.SS8.SSS1.Px2.p9.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="x" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>x</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">x</annotation></semantics></math> appears on the right, which collapses the asymmetry and enforces <math id="A2.SS8.SSS1.Px2.p9.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="xy=yx" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>y</mi></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>y</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>x</mi></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">xy=yx</annotation></semantics></math>.)</span></p>
</div>
<div id="A2.SS8.SSS1.Px2.p10" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A2.SS8.SSS1.Px2.p10.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.SS8.SSS1.Px2.p10.1.1" class="ltx_text">* **Not conversely (strictly stronger than commutative)**: There are commutative operations that **do not** satisfy <math id="A2.SS8.SSS1.Px2.p10.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(\star)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">⋆</mo><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(\star)</annotation></semantics></math>.
Example: on <math id="A2.SS8.SSS1.Px2.p10.m2" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\{0&lt;1&lt;2\}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>&lt;</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>&lt;</mo><mn>2</mn><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\{0&lt;1&lt;2\}</annotation></semantics></math> with <math id="A2.SS8.SSS1.Px2.p10.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="x*y=\max\{x,y\}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">∗</mo><mi>y</mi></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>max</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>y</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">x*y=\max\{x,y\}</annotation></semantics></math> (commutative), take <math id="A2.SS8.SSS1.Px2.p10.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="x=0,y=1,z=0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><mo>,</mo><mrow><mi>y</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo>,</mo><mrow><mi>z</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">x=0,y=1,z=0</annotation></semantics></math>:</span></p>
</div>
<div id="A2.SS8.SSS1.Px2.p11" class="ltx_para">
<table id="A2.Ex225" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A2.Ex225.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="x*(y*z)=0*\max(1,0)=0*1=1,\quad(z*x)*x=\max(0,0)*0=0*0=0," display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">∗</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>y</mi><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">∗</mo><mi>z</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mn>0</mn><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">∗</mo><mrow><mi>max</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>0</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mn>0</mn><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">∗</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo rspace="1.167em">,</mo><mrow><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>z</mi><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">∗</mo><mi>x</mi></mrow><mo rspace="0.055em" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo rspace="0.222em">∗</mo><mi>x</mi></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>max</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>0</mn><mo rspace="0.055em" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.222em">∗</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mn>0</mn><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">∗</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">x*(y*z)=0*\max(1,0)=0*1=1,\quad(z*x)*x=\max(0,0)*0=0*0=0,</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
<div id="A2.SS8.SSS1.Px2.p12" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A2.SS8.SSS1.Px2.p12.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.SS8.SSS1.Px2.p12.1.1" class="ltx_text">so <math id="A2.SS8.SSS1.Px2.p12.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(\star)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">⋆</mo><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(\star)</annotation></semantics></math> fails.</span></p>
</div>
<div id="A2.SS8.SSS1.Px2.p13" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A2.SS8.SSS1.Px2.p13.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.SS8.SSS1.Px2.p13.1.1" class="ltx_text">* **Not equivalent to “constant” (strictly weaker than constant)**: There are **nonconstant** operations satisfying <math id="A2.SS8.SSS1.Px2.p13.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(\star)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">⋆</mo><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(\star)</annotation></semantics></math>.
For instance on <math id="A2.SS8.SSS1.Px2.p13.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\{0,1,2\}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>2</mn><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\{0,1,2\}</annotation></semantics></math> define <math id="A2.SS8.SSS1.Px2.p13.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="*" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mo>∗</mo><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">*</annotation></semantics></math> by the symmetric table</span></p>
</div>
<div id="A2.SS8.SSS1.Px2.p14" class="ltx_para">
<table id="A2.Ex226" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A2.Ex226.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\begin{array}[]{c|ccc}*&amp;0&amp;1&amp;2\\
\hline\cr 0&amp;0&amp;0&amp;1\\
1&amp;0&amp;0&amp;1\\
2&amp;1&amp;1&amp;0\end{array}" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mtable columnspacing="5pt" displaystyle="true" rowspacing="0pt"><mtr><mtd class="ltx_border_r"><mo>∗</mo></mtd><mtd><mn>0</mn></mtd><mtd><mn>1</mn></mtd><mtd><mn>2</mn></mtd></mtr><mtr><mtd class="ltx_border_t"></mtd><mtd class="ltx_border_t"></mtd><mtd class="ltx_border_t"></mtd><mtd class="ltx_border_t"></mtd></mtr><mtr><mtd class="ltx_border_r"><mn>0</mn></mtd><mtd><mn>0</mn></mtd><mtd><mn>0</mn></mtd><mtd><mn>1</mn></mtd></mtr><mtr><mtd class="ltx_border_r"><mn>1</mn></mtd><mtd><mn>0</mn></mtd><mtd><mn>0</mn></mtd><mtd><mn>1</mn></mtd></mtr><mtr><mtd class="ltx_border_r"><mn>2</mn></mtd><mtd><mn>1</mn></mtd><mtd><mn>1</mn></mtd><mtd><mn>0</mn></mtd></mtr></mtable><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\begin{array}[]{c|ccc}*&amp;0&amp;1&amp;2\\
\hline\cr 0&amp;0&amp;0&amp;1\\
1&amp;0&amp;0&amp;1\\
2&amp;1&amp;1&amp;0\end{array}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
<div id="A2.SS8.SSS1.Px2.p15" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A2.SS8.SSS1.Px2.p15.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.SS8.SSS1.Px2.p15.1.1" class="ltx_text">(so <math id="A2.SS8.SSS1.Px2.p15.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="0*0=0,\,0*2=2*0=1,\,2*2=0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mn>0</mn><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">∗</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><mo>,</mo><mrow><mrow><mn> 0</mn><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">∗</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">∗</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo>,</mo><mrow><mrow><mn> 2</mn><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">∗</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">0*0=0,\,0*2=2*0=1,\,2*2=0</annotation></semantics></math>, etc.). This operation is commutative and nonconstant, and one checks it satisfies <math id="A2.SS8.SSS1.Px2.p15.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(\star)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">⋆</mo><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(\star)</annotation></semantics></math> for all <math id="A2.SS8.SSS1.Px2.p15.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="x,y,z" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>y</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>z</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">x,y,z</annotation></semantics></math>.</span></p>
</div>
<div id="A2.SS8.SSS1.Px2.p16" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A2.SS8.SSS1.Px2.p16.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.SS8.SSS1.Px2.p16.1.1" class="ltx_text">So <math id="A2.SS8.SSS1.Px2.p16.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(\star)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">⋆</mo><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(\star)</annotation></semantics></math> is **implied** by being constant, **implies** being commutative, and both reverse implications fail—exactly the “strictly in between” property you asked for.</span></p>
</div>
<div id="A2.SS8.SSS1.Px2.p17" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A2.SS8.SSS1.Px2.p17.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.SS8.SSS1.Px2.p17.1.1" class="ltx_text">∎</span></p>
</div>
</div>
<div id="A2.SS8.SSS1.Px2.2" class="ltx_proof">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_font_italic ltx_title_proof"><span id="A2.SS8.SSS1.Px2.2.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Standard Solution</span>.</h6>
<div id="A2.SS8.SSS1.Px2.p18" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A2.SS8.SSS1.Px2.p18.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.SS8.SSS1.Px2.p18.1.1" class="ltx_text">Source: <a href="https://mathoverflow.net/questions/450890/is-there-an-identity-between-the-commutative-identity-and-the-constant-identity" title="" class="ltx_ref ltx_href">https://mathoverflow.net/questions/450890/is-there-an-identity-between-the-commutative-identity-and-the-constant-identity</a></span></p>
</div>
<div id="A2.SS8.SSS1.Px2.p19" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A2.SS8.SSS1.Px2.p19.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.SS8.SSS1.Px2.p19.1.1" class="ltx_text">The identity <math id="A2.SS8.SSS1.Px2.p19.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(x*x)*y=y*x" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">∗</mo><mi>x</mi></mrow><mo rspace="0.055em" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo rspace="0.222em">∗</mo><mi>y</mi></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>y</mi><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">∗</mo><mi>x</mi></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(x*x)*y=y*x</annotation></semantics></math> implies the commutative identity. First <math id="A2.SS8.SSS1.Px2.p19.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(x*x)*x=x*x" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">∗</mo><mi>x</mi></mrow><mo rspace="0.055em" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo rspace="0.222em">∗</mo><mi>x</mi></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">∗</mo><mi>x</mi></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(x*x)*x=x*x</annotation></semantics></math>, so the operation <math id="A2.SS8.SSS1.Px2.p19.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="x\mapsto x*x" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">↦</mo><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">∗</mo><mi>x</mi></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">x\mapsto x*x</annotation></semantics></math> is idempotent. Then, <math id="A2.SS8.SSS1.Px2.p19.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(x*x)*y=((x*x)*(x*x))*y=y*(x*x)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">∗</mo><mi>x</mi></mrow><mo rspace="0.055em" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo rspace="0.222em">∗</mo><mi>y</mi></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">∗</mo><mi>x</mi></mrow><mo rspace="0.055em" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo rspace="0.222em">∗</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">∗</mo><mi>x</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.055em" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo rspace="0.222em">∗</mo><mi>y</mi></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>y</mi><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">∗</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">∗</mo><mi>x</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(x*x)*y=((x*x)*(x*x))*y=y*(x*x)</annotation></semantics></math>, so <math id="A2.SS8.SSS1.Px2.p19.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="x*x" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">∗</mo><mi>x</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">x*x</annotation></semantics></math> commutes with everything. Finally, <math id="A2.SS8.SSS1.Px2.p19.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(x*x)*(y*y)=(y*y)*x=x*y" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">∗</mo><mi>x</mi></mrow><mo rspace="0.055em" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo rspace="0.222em">∗</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>y</mi><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">∗</mo><mi>y</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>y</mi><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">∗</mo><mi>y</mi></mrow><mo rspace="0.055em" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo rspace="0.222em">∗</mo><mi>x</mi></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">∗</mo><mi>y</mi></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(x*x)*(y*y)=(y*y)*x=x*y</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="A2.SS8.SSS1.Px2.p19.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(x*x)*(y*y)=(y*y)*(x*x)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">∗</mo><mi>x</mi></mrow><mo rspace="0.055em" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo rspace="0.222em">∗</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>y</mi><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">∗</mo><mi>y</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>y</mi><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">∗</mo><mi>y</mi></mrow><mo rspace="0.055em" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo rspace="0.222em">∗</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">∗</mo><mi>x</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(x*x)*(y*y)=(y*y)*(x*x)</annotation></semantics></math> combined with <math id="A2.SS8.SSS1.Px2.p19.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="x*x" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">∗</mo><mi>x</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">x*x</annotation></semantics></math> commutes with everything gives <math id="A2.SS8.SSS1.Px2.p19.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="x*y=y*x" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">∗</mo><mi>y</mi></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>y</mi><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">∗</mo><mi>x</mi></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">x*y=y*x</annotation></semantics></math>.</span></p>
</div>
<div id="A2.SS8.SSS1.Px2.p20" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A2.SS8.SSS1.Px2.p20.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.SS8.SSS1.Px2.p20.1.1" class="ltx_text">To see that this identity does not imply the constant identity, consider any nonconstant relation that is commutative, associative, and idempotent.</span></p>
</div>
<div id="A2.SS8.SSS1.Px2.p21" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A2.SS8.SSS1.Px2.p21.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.SS8.SSS1.Px2.p21.1.1" class="ltx_text">To see that this the commutative identity does not imply this identity consider any commutative relation that is not idempotent.
∎</span></p>
</div>
</div>
<div id="A2.SS8.SSS1.Px2.p22" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent"><span class="ltx_inline-block"><svg id="A2.SS8.SSS1.Px2.p22.pic1" class="ltx_picture" height="53.02" overflow="visible" version="1.1" viewBox="0 0 429.64 53.02" width="429.64"><g style="--ltx-stroke-color:#000000;--ltx-fill-color:#000000;" fill="#000000" stroke="#000000" stroke-width="0.4pt" transform="translate(0,53.02) matrix(1 0 0 -1 0 0)"><g style="--ltx-fill-color:#4D4D4D;" fill="#4D4D4D" fill-opacity="1.0"><path style="stroke:none" d="M 0 4.63 L 0 48.39 C 0 50.95 2.07 53.02 4.63 53.02 L 425.01 53.02 C 427.56 53.02 429.64 50.95 429.64 48.39 L 429.64 4.63 C 429.64 2.07 427.56 0 425.01 0 L 4.63 0 C 2.07 0 0 2.07 0 4.63 Z"></path></g><g style="--ltx-fill-color:#F9F9F9;" fill="#F9F9F9" fill-opacity="1.0"><path style="stroke:none" d="M 0.69 4.63 L 0.69 34.15 L 428.94 34.15 L 428.94 4.63 C 428.94 2.45 427.18 0.69 425.01 0.69 L 4.63 0.69 C 2.45 0.69 0.69 2.45 0.69 4.63 Z"></path></g><g fill-opacity="1.0" transform="matrix(1.0 0.0 0.0 1.0 20.38 38.78)"><foreignObject style="--ltx-fo-width:24.44em;--ltx-fo-height:0.69em;--ltx-fo-depth:0em;font-size:10pt;" height="9.61" overflow="visible" transform="matrix(1 0 0 -1 0 9.61)" width="338.18"><span class="ltx_foreignobject_container"><span class="ltx_foreignobject_content">
