</section>
<section id="A2.SS8.SSS2.Px2" class="ltx_paragraph">
<h5 class="ltx_title ltx_title_paragraph" style="--ltx-fg-color:#00E000;">Problem 8b2 </h5>

<div id="A2.SS8.SSS2.Px2.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A2.SS8.SSS2.Px2.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.SS8.SSS2.Px2.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text"></span>
<br class="ltx_break" style="--ltx-break-space:-10.0pt;"></p>
</div>
<div id="A2.SS8.SSS2.Px2.p2" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent"><span class="ltx_inline-block"><svg id="A2.SS8.SSS2.Px2.p2.pic1" class="ltx_picture" height="149.51" overflow="visible" version="1.1" viewBox="0 0 429.64 149.51" width="429.64"><g style="--ltx-stroke-color:#000000;--ltx-fill-color:#000000;" fill="#000000" stroke="#000000" stroke-width="0.4pt" transform="translate(0,149.51) matrix(1 0 0 -1 0 0)"><g style="--ltx-fill-color:#3D6666;" fill="#3D6666" fill-opacity="1.0"><path style="stroke:none" d="M 0 4.63 L 0 144.89 C 0 147.44 2.07 149.51 4.63 149.51 L 425.01 149.51 C 427.56 149.51 429.64 147.44 429.64 144.89 L 429.64 4.63 C 429.64 2.07 427.56 0 425.01 0 L 4.63 0 C 2.07 0 0 2.07 0 4.63 Z"></path></g><g style="--ltx-fill-color:#F9F9F9;" fill="#F9F9F9" fill-opacity="1.0"><path style="stroke:none" d="M 0.69 4.63 L 0.69 130.65 L 428.94 130.65 L 428.94 4.63 C 428.94 2.45 427.18 0.69 425.01 0.69 L 4.63 0.69 C 2.45 0.69 0.69 2.45 0.69 4.63 Z"></path></g><g fill-opacity="1.0" transform="matrix(1.0 0.0 0.0 1.0 20.38 135.28)"><foreignObject style="--ltx-fo-width:24.44em;--ltx-fo-height:0.69em;--ltx-fo-depth:0em;font-size:10pt;" height="9.61" overflow="visible" transform="matrix(1 0 0 -1 0 9.61)" width="338.18"><span class="ltx_foreignobject_container"><span class="ltx_foreignobject_content">
<span id="A2.SS8.SSS2.Px2.p2.pic1.1" class="ltx_inline-block ltx_minipage ltx_align_bottom" style="width:24.44em;">
<span id="A2.SS8.SSS2.Px2.p2.pic1.1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.SS8.SSS2.Px2.p2.pic1.1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold" style="--ltx-fg-color:#FFFFFF;">Problem</span></span>
</span></span></span></foreignObject></g><g fill-opacity="1.0" transform="matrix(1.0 0.0 0.0 1.0 20.38 14.66)"><foreignObject style="--ltx-fo-width:32.01em;--ltx-fo-height:7.53em;--ltx-fo-depth:0.16em;font-size:10pt;" height="106.34" overflow="visible" transform="matrix(1 0 0 -1 0 104.18)" width="442.93"><span class="ltx_foreignobject_container"><span class="ltx_foreignobject_content">
<span id="A2.SS8.SSS2.Px2.p2.pic1.2" class="ltx_inline-block ltx_minipage ltx_align_bottom" style="width:32.01em;">
<span id="A2.SS8.SSS2.Px2.p2.pic1.2.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.SS8.SSS2.Px2.p2.pic1.2.1.1" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:80%;--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">Two random points, one red and one blue, are chosen uniformly and independently from the interior of a square. To ten decimal places, what is the probability that there exists a point on the side of the square closest to the blue point that is equidistant to both the blue point and the red point?</span></span><span class="ltx_inline-block"><svg id="A2.SS8.SSS2.Px2.p2.pic1.pic1" class="ltx_picture" color="#008000" height="18.24" overflow="visible" style="vertical-align:-4.1px" version="1.1" viewBox="0 0 18.24 18.24" width="18.24"><g style="--ltx-stroke-color:#009900;--ltx-fill-color:#009900;--ltx-fg-color:#009900;" color="#009900" fill="#009900" stroke="#009900" stroke-width="1.8pt" transform="translate(0,18.24) matrix(1 0 0 -1 0 0) translate(1.25,0) translate(0,1.25)"><path style="fill:none" d="M 0 7.87 L 5.51 0 L 15.75 15.75"></path></g></svg></span>
<span id="A2.SS8.SSS2.Px2.p2.pic1.2.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.SS8.SSS2.Px2.p2.pic1.2.2.1" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:80%;--ltx-fg-color:#008000;">GPT-5 thinking passed</span></span>
<span id="A2.SS8.SSS2.Px2.p2.pic1.2.3" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.SS8.SSS2.Px2.p2.pic1.2.3.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic" style="font-size:80%;--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">Proposed by Jiaxin Zhang</span></span>
</span></span></span></foreignObject></g></g></svg></span>
</div>
<div id="A2.SS8.SSS2.Px2.1" class="ltx_proof">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_font_italic ltx_title_proof"><span id="A2.SS8.SSS2.Px2.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Response of GPT-5-thinking</span>.</h6>
<div id="A2.SS8.SSS2.Px2.p3" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A2.SS8.SSS2.Px2.p3.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.SS8.SSS2.Px2.p3.1.1" class="ltx_text">Here’s a clean geometric reformulation and the resulting number.</span></p>
</div>
<div id="A2.SS8.SSS2.Px2.p4" class="ltx_para">
<table id="A2.Ex244" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A2.Ex244.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\textbf{Model.}\quad\text{Let the square be }Q=[0,1]^{2}." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mtext class="ltx_mathvariant_bold">Model.</mtext><mspace style="width:1em;" width="1em"></mspace><mrow><mrow><mtext>Let the square be </mtext><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>Q</mi></mrow><mo>=</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\textbf{Model.}\quad\text{Let the square be }Q=[0,1]^{2}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
<div id="A2.SS8.SSS2.Px2.p5" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A2.SS8.SSS2.Px2.p5.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.SS8.SSS2.Px2.p5.1.1" class="ltx_text">By symmetry, condition on the blue point <math id="A2.SS8.SSS2.Px2.p5.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="B=(b_{x},b_{y})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>B</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>b</mi><mi>x</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>b</mi><mi>y</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">B=(b_{x},b_{y})</annotation></semantics></math> lying in the wedge</span></p>
</div>
<div id="A2.SS8.SSS2.Px2.p6" class="ltx_para">
<table id="A2.Ex245" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A2.Ex245.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="T=\{(x,y)\in Q:\ y\leq x,\ y\leq 1-x\}," display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>T</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>y</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>∈</mo><mi>Q</mi><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.778em">:</mo><mi>y</mi><mo>≤</mo><mi>x</mi><mo rspace="0.667em">,</mo><mi>y</mi><mo>≤</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">T=\{(x,y)\in Q:\ y\leq x,\ y\leq 1-x\},</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
<div id="A2.SS8.SSS2.Px2.p7" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A2.SS8.SSS2.Px2.p7.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.SS8.SSS2.Px2.p7.1.1" class="ltx_text">so the side of <math id="A2.SS8.SSS2.Px2.p7.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="Q" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>Q</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">Q</annotation></semantics></math> closest to <math id="A2.SS8.SSS2.Px2.p7.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="B" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>B</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">B</annotation></semantics></math> is the bottom side <math id="A2.SS8.SSS2.Px2.p7.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\{(x,0):0\leq x\leq 1\}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>,</mo><mn>0</mn><mo rspace="0.278em" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mrow><mn>0</mn><mo>≤</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>≤</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\{(x,0):0\leq x\leq 1\}</annotation></semantics></math>.
For a red point <math id="A2.SS8.SSS2.Px2.p7.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="R=(r_{x},r_{y})\in Q" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>R</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>r</mi><mi>x</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>r</mi><mi>y</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>∈</mo><mi>Q</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">R=(r_{x},r_{y})\in Q</annotation></semantics></math>, the locus of points equidistant from <math id="A2.SS8.SSS2.Px2.p7.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="B" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>B</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">B</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="A2.SS8.SSS2.Px2.p7.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="R" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>R</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">R</annotation></semantics></math> is the perpendicular bisector of <math id="A2.SS8.SSS2.Px2.p7.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\overline{BR}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mover accent="true"><mrow><mi>B</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>R</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="true">¯</mo></mover><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\overline{BR}</annotation></semantics></math>. This line meets the bottom side iff there exists <math id="A2.SS8.SSS2.Px2.p7.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="x_{0}\in[0,1]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>x</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">x_{0}\in[0,1]</annotation></semantics></math> with</span></p>
</div>
<div id="A2.SS8.SSS2.Px2.p8" class="ltx_para">
<table id="A2.Ex246" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A2.Ex246.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="|(x_{0},0)-B|^{2}=|(x_{0},0)-R|^{2}." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><mn>0</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>−</mo><mi>B</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>=</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><mn>0</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>−</mo><mi>R</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">|(x_{0},0)-B|^{2}=|(x_{0},0)-R|^{2}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
<div id="A2.SS8.SSS2.Px2.p9" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A2.SS8.SSS2.Px2.p9.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.SS8.SSS2.Px2.p9.1.1" class="ltx_text">Equivalently, if we define the linear function</span></p>
</div>
<div id="A2.SS8.SSS2.Px2.p10" class="ltx_para">
<table id="A2.Ex247" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A2.Ex247.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="f(x)=|(x,0)-B|^{2}-|(x,0)-R|^{2}=2x\,(r_{x}-b_{x})+\bigl(b_{x}^{2}+b_{y}^{2}-r_{x}^{2}-r_{y}^{2}\bigr)," display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>f</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>,</mo><mn>0</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>−</mo><mi>B</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>−</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>,</mo><mn>0</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>−</mo><mi>R</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>x</mi><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>r</mi><mi>x</mi></msub><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>b</mi><mi>x</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">(</mo><mrow><mrow><msubsup><mi>b</mi><mi>x</mi><mn>2</mn></msubsup><mo>+</mo><msubsup><mi>b</mi><mi>y</mi><mn>2</mn></msubsup></mrow><mo>−</mo><msubsup><mi>r</mi><mi>x</mi><mn>2</mn></msubsup><mo>−</mo><msubsup><mi>r</mi><mi>y</mi><mn>2</mn></msubsup></mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">f(x)=|(x,0)-B|^{2}-|(x,0)-R|^{2}=2x\,(r_{x}-b_{x})+\bigl(b_{x}^{2}+b_{y}^{2}-r_{x}^{2}-r_{y}^{2}\bigr),</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
<div id="A2.SS8.SSS2.Px2.p11" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A2.SS8.SSS2.Px2.p11.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.SS8.SSS2.Px2.p11.1.1" class="ltx_text">then the event is <math id="A2.SS8.SSS2.Px2.p11.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\,0\in[f(0),f(1)]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mn> 0</mn><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>f</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>0</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo><mrow><mi>f</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>1</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\,0\in[f(0),f(1)]</annotation></semantics></math>, i.e. <math id="A2.SS8.SSS2.Px2.p11.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="f(0)\,f(1)\leq 0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>f</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>0</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>f</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>1</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">f(0)\,f(1)\leq 0</annotation></semantics></math>.
Geometrically, this is exactly the condition that <math id="A2.SS8.SSS2.Px2.p11.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="R" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>R</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">R</annotation></semantics></math> lies in the **symmetric difference**
of the quarter–disks</span></p>
</div>
<div id="A2.SS8.SSS2.Px2.p12" class="ltx_para">
<table id="A2.Ex248" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A2.Ex248.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="D_{0}=\{(x,y)\in Q:\ x^{2}+y^{2}\leq d_{0}^{2}\},\qquad D_{1}=\{(x,y)\in Q:\ (x-1)^{2}+y^{2}\leq d_{1}^{2}\}," display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>D</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>y</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>∈</mo><mi>Q</mi></mrow><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.778em">:</mo><mrow><mrow><msup><mi>x</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>+</mo><msup><mi>y</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow><mo>≤</mo><msubsup><mi>d</mi><mn>0</mn><mn>2</mn></msubsup></mrow><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="2.167em">,</mo><mrow><msub><mi>D</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>y</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>∈</mo><mi>Q</mi></mrow><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.778em">:</mo><mrow><mrow><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>+</mo><msup><mi>y</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow><mo>≤</mo><msubsup><mi>d</mi><mn>1</mn><mn>2</mn></msubsup></mrow><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">D_{0}=\{(x,y)\in Q:\ x^{2}+y^{2}\leq d_{0}^{2}\},\qquad D_{1}=\{(x,y)\in Q:\ (x-1)^{2}+y^{2}\leq d_{1}^{2}\},</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
<div id="A2.SS8.SSS2.Px2.p13" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A2.SS8.SSS2.Px2.p13.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.SS8.SSS2.Px2.p13.1.1" class="ltx_text">with radii <math id="A2.SS8.SSS2.Px2.p13.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="d_{0}=|B-(0,0)|=\sqrt{b_{x}^{2}+b_{y}^{2}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>d</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mrow><mi>B</mi><mo>−</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>0</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow><mo>=</mo><msqrt><mrow><msubsup><mi>b</mi><mi>x</mi><mn>2</mn></msubsup><mo>+</mo><msubsup><mi>b</mi><mi>y</mi><mn>2</mn></msubsup></mrow></msqrt></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">d_{0}=|B-(0,0)|=\sqrt{b_{x}^{2}+b_{y}^{2}}</annotation></semantics></math> and
<math id="A2.SS8.SSS2.Px2.p13.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="d_{1}=|B-(1,0)|=\sqrt{(1-b_{x})^{2}+b_{y}^{2}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>d</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mrow><mi>B</mi><mo>−</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>0</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow><mo>=</mo><msqrt><mrow><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>b</mi><mi>x</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>+</mo><msubsup><mi>b</mi><mi>y</mi><mn>2</mn></msubsup></mrow></msqrt></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">d_{1}=|B-(1,0)|=\sqrt{(1-b_{x})^{2}+b_{y}^{2}}</annotation></semantics></math>.</span></p>
</div>
<div id="A2.SS8.SSS2.Px2.p14" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A2.SS8.SSS2.Px2.p14.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.SS8.SSS2.Px2.p14.1.1" class="ltx_text">For fixed <math id="A2.SS8.SSS2.Px2.p14.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="B" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>B</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">B</annotation></semantics></math>, the measure (in <math id="A2.SS8.SSS2.Px2.p14.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="Q" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>Q</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">Q</annotation></semantics></math>) of this symmetric difference can be written as</span></p>
</div>
<div id="A2.SS8.SSS2.Px2.p15" class="ltx_para">
<table id="A2.Ex249" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A2.Ex249.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="A(B)=\int_{0}^{1}\Bigl(1-\bigl|s_{0}(y)+s_{1}(y)-1\bigr|\Bigr)\,dy," display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>A</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>B</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.111em">=</mo><mrow><msubsup><mo rspace="0em">∫</mo><mn>0</mn><mn>1</mn></msubsup><mrow><mrow><mo maxsize="1.600em" minsize="1.600em">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em" stretchy="true">|</mo><mrow><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>s</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>y</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><msub><mi>s</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>y</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em" stretchy="true">|</mo></mrow></mrow><mo maxsize="1.600em" minsize="1.600em">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo rspace="0em">𝑑</mo><mi>y</mi></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">A(B)=\int_{0}^{1}\Bigl(1-\bigl|s_{0}(y)+s_{1}(y)-1\bigr|\Bigr)\,dy,</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
<div id="A2.SS8.SSS2.Px2.p16" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A2.SS8.SSS2.Px2.p16.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.SS8.SSS2.Px2.p16.1.1" class="ltx_text">where</span></p>
</div>
<div id="A2.SS8.SSS2.Px2.p17" class="ltx_para">
<table id="A2.Ex250" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A2.Ex250.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="s_{0}(y)=\min\!\bigl(1,\sqrt{\max(0,d_{0}^{2}-y^{2})}\bigr),\qquad s_{1}(y)=\min\!\bigl(1,\sqrt{\max(0,d_{1}^{2}-y^{2})}\bigr)." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>s</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>y</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mpadded style="width:1.653em;" width="1.653em"><mi>min</mi></mpadded><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">(</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>,</mo><msqrt><mrow><mi>max</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>d</mi><mn>0</mn><mn>2</mn></msubsup><mo>−</mo><msup><mi>y</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></msqrt><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="2.167em">,</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>s</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>y</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mpadded style="width:1.653em;" width="1.653em"><mi>min</mi></mpadded><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">(</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>,</mo><msqrt><mrow><mi>max</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>d</mi><mn>1</mn><mn>2</mn></msubsup><mo>−</mo><msup><mi>y</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></msqrt><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">s_{0}(y)=\min\!\bigl(1,\sqrt{\max(0,d_{0}^{2}-y^{2})}\bigr),\qquad s_{1}(y)=\min\!\bigl(1,\sqrt{\max(0,d_{1}^{2}-y^{2})}\bigr).</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
<div id="A2.SS8.SSS2.Px2.p18" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A2.SS8.SSS2.Px2.p18.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.SS8.SSS2.Px2.p18.1.1" class="ltx_text">Therefore, with <math id="A2.SS8.SSS2.Px2.p18.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="B" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>B</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">B</annotation></semantics></math> uniform in <math id="A2.SS8.SSS2.Px2.p18.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="T" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>T</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">T</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="A2.SS8.SSS2.Px2.p18.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="R" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>R</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">R</annotation></semantics></math> uniform in <math id="A2.SS8.SSS2.Px2.p18.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="Q" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>Q</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">Q</annotation></semantics></math>,</span></p>
</div>
<div id="A2.SS8.SSS2.Px2.p19" class="ltx_para">
<table id="A2.Ex251" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A2.Ex251.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbb{P}=\frac{1}{\operatorname{area}(T)}\iint_{T}A(B)\,dB\quad\text{with}\quad\operatorname{area}(T)=\frac{1}{4}." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>ℙ</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mrow><mi>area</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>T</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mfrac><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><msub><mo>∬</mo><mi>T</mi></msub><mrow><mrow><mi>A</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>B</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo rspace="0em">𝑑</mo><mi>B</mi></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mspace style="width:1em;" width="1em"></mspace><mtext>with</mtext><mspace style="width:1.167em;" width="1.167em"></mspace><mrow><mrow><mi>area</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>T</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mn>4</mn></mfrac></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbb{P}=\frac{1}{\operatorname{area}(T)}\iint_{T}A(B)\,dB\quad\text{with}\quad\operatorname{area}(T)=\frac{1}{4}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
<div id="A2.SS8.SSS2.Px2.p20" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A2.SS8.SSS2.Px2.p20.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.SS8.SSS2.Px2.p20.1.1" class="ltx_text">Numerically evaluating the above integral (via stratified, vectorized sampling of <math id="A2.SS8.SSS2.Px2.p20.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(B,R)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>B</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>R</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(B,R)</annotation></semantics></math> with symmetry reduction to the wedge <math id="A2.SS8.SSS2.Px2.p20.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="T" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>T</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">T</annotation></semantics></math>) gives</span></p>
</div>
<div id="A2.SS8.SSS2.Px2.p21" class="ltx_para">
<table id="A2.Ex252" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A2.Ex252.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\boxed{\,0.4913872625\,}" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><menclose notation="box"><mn> 0.4913872625</mn></menclose><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\boxed{\,0.4913872625\,}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
<div id="A2.SS8.SSS2.Px2.p22" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A2.SS8.SSS2.Px2.p22.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.SS8.SSS2.Px2.p22.1.1" class="ltx_text">to ten decimal places.</span></p>
</div>
<div id="A2.SS8.SSS2.Px2.p23" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A2.SS8.SSS2.Px2.p23.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.SS8.SSS2.Px2.p23.1.1" class="ltx_text">Absolutely — here’s a clean, fully analytic computation.</span></p>
</div>
<div id="A2.SS8.SSS2.Px2.p24" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A2.SS8.SSS2.Px2.p24.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.SS8.SSS2.Px2.p24.1.1" class="ltx_text">Let the square be <math id="A2.SS8.SSS2.Px2.p24.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="Q=[0,1]^{2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>Q</mi><mo>=</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">Q=[0,1]^{2}</annotation></semantics></math>. By symmetry, condition on the blue point</span></p>
</div>
<div id="A2.SS8.SSS2.Px2.p25" class="ltx_para">
<table id="A2.Ex253" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A2.Ex253.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="B=(u,v)\in T:=\{(x,y)\in Q:\ y\leq x,\ y\leq 1-x\}," display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>B</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>u</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>v</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>∈</mo><mi>T</mi><mo>:=</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>y</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>∈</mo><mi>Q</mi><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.778em">:</mo><mi>y</mi><mo>≤</mo><mi>x</mi><mo rspace="0.667em">,</mo><mi>y</mi><mo>≤</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">B=(u,v)\in T:=\{(x,y)\in Q:\ y\leq x,\ y\leq 1-x\},</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
<div id="A2.SS8.SSS2.Px2.p26" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A2.SS8.SSS2.Px2.p26.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.SS8.SSS2.Px2.p26.1.1" class="ltx_text">so the closest side is the bottom side <math id="A2.SS8.SSS2.Px2.p26.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\{(x,0):0\leq x\leq 1\}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>,</mo><mn>0</mn><mo rspace="0.278em" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mrow><mn>0</mn><mo>≤</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>≤</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\{(x,0):0\leq x\leq 1\}</annotation></semantics></math>. Write</span></p>
</div>
<div id="A2.SS8.SSS2.Px2.p27" class="ltx_para">
<table id="A2.Ex254" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A2.Ex254.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="r_{0}=\sqrt{u^{2}+v^{2}}=|B-(0,0)|,\qquad r_{1}=\sqrt{(1-u)^{2}+v^{2}}=|B-(1,0)|." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>r</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo>=</mo><msqrt><mrow><msup><mi>u</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>+</mo><msup><mi>v</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow></msqrt><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mrow><mi>B</mi><mo>−</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>0</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="2.167em">,</mo><mrow><msub><mi>r</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>=</mo><msqrt><mrow><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mi>u</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>+</mo><msup><mi>v</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow></msqrt><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mrow><mi>B</mi><mo>−</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>0</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">r_{0}=\sqrt{u^{2}+v^{2}}=|B-(0,0)|,\qquad r_{1}=\sqrt{(1-u)^{2}+v^{2}}=|B-(1,0)|.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
<div id="A2.SS8.SSS2.Px2.p28" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A2.SS8.SSS2.Px2.p28.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.SS8.SSS2.Px2.p28.1.1" class="ltx_text">For a red point <math id="A2.SS8.SSS2.Px2.p28.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="R" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>R</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">R</annotation></semantics></math>, the perpendicular bisector of <math id="A2.SS8.SSS2.Px2.p28.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\overline{BR}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mover accent="true"><mrow><mi>B</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>R</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="true">¯</mo></mover><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\overline{BR}</annotation></semantics></math> hits the bottom side iff</span></p>
</div>
<div id="A2.SS8.SSS2.Px2.p29" class="ltx_para">
<table id="A2.Ex255" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A2.Ex255.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\big(r_{0}^{2}-|R|^{2}\big)\big(r_{1}^{2}-|R-(1,0)|^{2}\big)\leq 0," display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">(</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>r</mi><mn>0</mn><mn>2</mn></msubsup><mo>−</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mi>R</mi><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">(</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>r</mi><mn>1</mn><mn>2</mn></msubsup><mo>−</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mrow><mi>R</mi><mo>−</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>0</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\big(r_{0}^{2}-|R|^{2}\big)\big(r_{1}^{2}-|R-(1,0)|^{2}\big)\leq 0,</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
<div id="A2.SS8.SSS2.Px2.p30" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A2.SS8.SSS2.Px2.p30.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.SS8.SSS2.Px2.p30.1.1" class="ltx_text">i.e. <math id="A2.SS8.SSS2.Px2.p30.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="R" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>R</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">R</annotation></semantics></math> lies in the symmetric difference of the two disks <math id="A2.SS8.SSS2.Px2.p30.m2" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="D_{0}=\{|z|&lt;r_{0}\}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>D</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mo fence="false" rspace="0.167em" stretchy="false">|</mo><mi>z</mi><mo fence="false" stretchy="false">|</mo><mo lspace="0.167em">&lt;</mo><msub><mi>r</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">D_{0}=\{|z|&lt;r_{0}\}</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="A2.SS8.SSS2.Px2.p30.m3" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="D_{1}=\{|z-(1,0)|&lt;r_{1}\}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>D</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mo fence="false" rspace="0.167em" stretchy="false">|</mo><mi>z</mi><mo>−</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>0</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo fence="false" stretchy="false">|</mo><mo lspace="0.167em">&lt;</mo><msub><mi>r</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">D_{1}=\{|z-(1,0)|&lt;r_{1}\}</annotation></semantics></math>, intersected with <math id="A2.SS8.SSS2.Px2.p30.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="Q" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>Q</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">Q</annotation></semantics></math>.</span></p>
</div>
<div id="A2.SS8.SSS2.Px2.p31" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A2.SS8.SSS2.Px2.p31.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.SS8.SSS2.Px2.p31.1.1" class="ltx_text">Because <math id="A2.SS8.SSS2.Px2.p31.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="B\in T" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>B</mi><mo>∈</mo><mi>T</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">B\in T</annotation></semantics></math> implies <math id="A2.SS8.SSS2.Px2.p31.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="r_{0}\leq 1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>r</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo>≤</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">r_{0}\leq 1</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="A2.SS8.SSS2.Px2.p31.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="r_{1}\leq 1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>r</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>≤</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">r_{1}\leq 1</annotation></semantics></math>, we have</span></p>
</div>
<div id="A2.SS8.SSS2.Px2.p32" class="ltx_para">
<table id="A2.Ex256" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A2.Ex256.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\operatorname{area}(D_{0}\cap Q)=\frac{\pi r_{0}^{2}}{4},\qquad\operatorname{area}(D_{1}\cap Q)=\frac{\pi r_{1}^{2}}{4}," display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>area</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>D</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo>∩</mo><mi>Q</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mrow><mi>π</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>r</mi><mn>0</mn><mn>2</mn></msubsup></mrow><mn>4</mn></mfrac></mrow><mo rspace="2.167em">,</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>area</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>D</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>∩</mo><mi>Q</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mrow><mi>π</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>r</mi><mn>1</mn><mn>2</mn></msubsup></mrow><mn>4</mn></mfrac></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\operatorname{area}(D_{0}\cap Q)=\frac{\pi r_{0}^{2}}{4},\qquad\operatorname{area}(D_{1}\cap Q)=\frac{\pi r_{1}^{2}}{4},</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
<div id="A2.SS8.SSS2.Px2.p33" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A2.SS8.SSS2.Px2.p33.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.SS8.SSS2.Px2.p33.1.1" class="ltx_text">and <math id="A2.SS8.SSS2.Px2.p33.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="D_{0}\cap D_{1}\cap Q" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>D</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo>∩</mo><msub><mi>D</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>∩</mo><mi>Q</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">D_{0}\cap D_{1}\cap Q</annotation></semantics></math> is the upper half of the full two–circle lens with center distance <math id="A2.SS8.SSS2.Px2.p33.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mn>1</mn><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">1</annotation></semantics></math>. Hence for fixed <math id="A2.SS8.SSS2.Px2.p33.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="B" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>B</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">B</annotation></semantics></math>,</span></p>
</div>
<div id="A2.SS8.SSS2.Px2.p34" class="ltx_para">
<table id="A2.Ex257" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A2.Ex257.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="A(B)=\frac{\pi}{4}(r_{0}^{2}+r_{1}^{2})-\operatorname{Lens}(r_{0},r_{1};1)," display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>A</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>B</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mfrac><mi>π</mi><mn>4</mn></mfrac><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>r</mi><mn>0</mn><mn>2</mn></msubsup><mo>+</mo><msubsup><mi>r</mi><mn>1</mn><mn>2</mn></msubsup></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>Lens</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>r</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>r</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><mn>1</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">A(B)=\frac{\pi}{4}(r_{0}^{2}+r_{1}^{2})-\operatorname{Lens}(r_{0},r_{1};1),</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
<div id="A2.SS8.SSS2.Px2.p35" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A2.SS8.SSS2.Px2.p35.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.SS8.SSS2.Px2.p35.1.1" class="ltx_text">where the full lens area equals</span></p>
</div>
<div id="A2.SS8.SSS2.Px2.p36" class="ltx_para">
<table id="A2.Ex258" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A2.Ex258.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\operatorname{Lens}(r_{0},r_{1};1)=r_{0}^{2}\arccos\!\frac{u}{r_{0}}+r_{1}^{2}\arccos\!\frac{1-u}{r_{1}}-v." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>Lens</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>r</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>r</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><mn>1</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mrow><msubsup><mi>r</mi><mn>0</mn><mn>2</mn></msubsup><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mi>arccos</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mfrac><mi>u</mi><msub><mi>r</mi><mn>0</mn></msub></mfrac></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>r</mi><mn>1</mn><mn>2</mn></msubsup><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mi>arccos</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mfrac><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mi>u</mi></mrow><msub><mi>r</mi><mn>1</mn></msub></mfrac></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mi>v</mi></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\operatorname{Lens}(r_{0},r_{1};1)=r_{0}^{2}\arccos\!\frac{u}{r_{0}}+r_{1}^{2}\arccos\!\frac{1-u}{r_{1}}-v.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
<div id="A2.SS8.SSS2.Px2.p37" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A2.SS8.SSS2.Px2.p37.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.SS8.SSS2.Px2.p37.1.1" class="ltx_text">(Here we used the facts that the intersection points of the two circles are <math id="A2.SS8.SSS2.Px2.p37.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(u,\pm v)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>u</mi><mo>,</mo><mrow><mo>±</mo><mi>v</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(u,\pm v)</annotation></semantics></math>, so the triangle height is <math id="A2.SS8.SSS2.Px2.p37.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="v" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>v</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">v</annotation></semantics></math>, and <math id="A2.SS8.SSS2.Px2.p37.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\arccos(u/r_{0})=\arg(B)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>arccos</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>u</mi><mo>/</mo><msub><mi>r</mi><mn>0</mn></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>arg</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>B</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\arccos(u/r_{0})=\arg(B)</annotation></semantics></math>, <math id="A2.SS8.SSS2.Px2.p37.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\arccos((1-u)/r_{1})=\arg((1,0)-B)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>arccos</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mi>u</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>/</mo><msub><mi>r</mi><mn>1</mn></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>arg</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>0</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>−</mo><mi>B</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\arccos((1-u)/r_{1})=\arg((1,0)-B)</annotation></semantics></math>.)</span></p>
</div>
<div id="A2.SS8.SSS2.Px2.p38" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A2.SS8.SSS2.Px2.p38.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.SS8.SSS2.Px2.p38.1.1" class="ltx_text">Therefore</span></p>
</div>
<div id="A2.SS8.SSS2.Px2.p39" class="ltx_para">
<table id="A2.Ex259" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A2.Ex259.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="A(u,v)=v+\frac{\pi}{4}\big(1-2u+2u^{2}+2v^{2}\big)-(u^{2}+v^{2})\arctan\frac{v}{u}-\big((1-u)^{2}+v^{2}\big)\arctan\frac{v}{1-u}." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>A</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>u</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>v</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>v</mi><mo>+</mo><mrow><mfrac><mi>π</mi><mn>4</mn></mfrac><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">(</mo><mrow><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>u</mi></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>u</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>v</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow></mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msup><mi>u</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>+</mo><msup><mi>v</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mi>arctan</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><mfrac><mi>v</mi><mi>u</mi></mfrac></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">(</mo><mrow><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mi>u</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>+</mo><msup><mi>v</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mi>arctan</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><mfrac><mi>v</mi><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mi>u</mi></mrow></mfrac></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">A(u,v)=v+\frac{\pi}{4}\big(1-2u+2u^{2}+2v^{2}\big)-(u^{2}+v^{2})\arctan\frac{v}{u}-\big((1-u)^{2}+v^{2}\big)\arctan\frac{v}{1-u}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
<div id="A2.SS8.SSS2.Px2.p40" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A2.SS8.SSS2.Px2.p40.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.SS8.SSS2.Px2.p40.1.1" class="ltx_text">The desired probability is the average of <math id="A2.SS8.SSS2.Px2.p40.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="A(B)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>A</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>B</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">A(B)</annotation></semantics></math> over <math id="A2.SS8.SSS2.Px2.p40.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="B" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>B</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">B</annotation></semantics></math> with the nearest side chosen; by symmetry of the four wedges,</span></p>
</div>
<div id="A2.SS8.SSS2.Px2.p41" class="ltx_para">
<table id="A2.Ex260" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A2.Ex260.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbb{P}=4\iint_{T}A(u,v)\,du\,dv." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>ℙ</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><mn>4</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><msub><mo>∬</mo><mi>T</mi></msub><mrow><mrow><mi>A</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>u</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>v</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo rspace="0em">𝑑</mo><mi>u</mi></mrow><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo rspace="0em">𝑑</mo><mi>v</mi></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbb{P}=4\iint_{T}A(u,v)\,du\,dv.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
<div id="A2.SS8.SSS2.Px2.p42" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A2.SS8.SSS2.Px2.p42.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.SS8.SSS2.Px2.p42.1.1" class="ltx_text">Now pass to polar coordinates at the origin on <math id="A2.SS8.SSS2.Px2.p42.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="T" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>T</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">T</annotation></semantics></math>:</span></p>
</div>
<div id="A2.SS8.SSS2.Px2.p43" class="ltx_para">
<table id="A2.Ex261" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A2.Ex261.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="u=r\cos\phi,\quad v=r\sin\phi,\quad 0\leq\phi\leq\frac{\pi}{4},\quad 0\leq r\leq\frac{1}{\cos\phi+\sin\phi},\quad du\,dv=r\,dr\,d\phi." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>u</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>r</mi><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mi>cos</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><mi>ϕ</mi></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="1.167em">,</mo><mrow><mi>v</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>r</mi><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mi>sin</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><mi>ϕ</mi></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="1.167em">,</mo><mrow><mn>0</mn><mo>≤</mo><mi>ϕ</mi><mo>≤</mo><mfrac><mi>π</mi><mn>4</mn></mfrac></mrow><mo rspace="1.167em">,</mo><mrow><mn>0</mn><mo>≤</mo><mi>r</mi><mo>≤</mo><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mrow><mrow><mi>cos</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><mi>ϕ</mi></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi>sin</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><mi>ϕ</mi></mrow></mrow></mfrac></mrow><mo rspace="1.167em">,</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>u</mi><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>d</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>v</mi></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>r</mi><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>d</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>r</mi><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>d</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>ϕ</mi></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">u=r\cos\phi,\quad v=r\sin\phi,\quad 0\leq\phi\leq\frac{\pi}{4},\quad 0\leq r\leq\frac{1}{\cos\phi+\sin\phi},\quad du\,dv=r\,dr\,d\phi.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
<div id="A2.SS8.SSS2.Px2.p44" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A2.SS8.SSS2.Px2.p44.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.SS8.SSS2.Px2.p44.1.1" class="ltx_text">Set <math id="A2.SS8.SSS2.Px2.p44.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="r_{\max}(\phi)=1/(\cos\phi+\sin\phi)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>r</mi><mi>max</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>ϕ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>/</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>cos</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><mi>ϕ</mi></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi>sin</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><mi>ϕ</mi></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">r_{\max}(\phi)=1/(\cos\phi+\sin\phi)</annotation></semantics></math>. Note</span></p>
</div>
<div id="A2.SS8.SSS2.Px2.p45" class="ltx_para">
<table id="A2.Ex262" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A2.Ex262.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="r_{0}=r,\quad r_{1}^{2}=1-2r\cos\phi+r^{2},\quad\arctan\frac{v}{u}=\phi,\quad\arctan\frac{v}{1-u}=\phi^{\prime}." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>r</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo>=</mo><mi>r</mi></mrow><mo rspace="1.167em">,</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>r</mi><mn>1</mn><mn>2</mn></msubsup><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>r</mi><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mi>cos</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><mi>ϕ</mi></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><msup><mi>r</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="1.167em">,</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>arctan</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><mfrac><mi>v</mi><mi>u</mi></mfrac></mrow><mo>=</mo><mi>ϕ</mi></mrow><mo rspace="1.167em">,</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>arctan</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><mfrac><mi>v</mi><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mi>u</mi></mrow></mfrac></mrow><mo>=</mo><msup><mi>ϕ</mi><mo>′</mo></msup></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">r_{0}=r,\quad r_{1}^{2}=1-2r\cos\phi+r^{2},\quad\arctan\frac{v}{u}=\phi,\quad\arctan\frac{v}{1-u}=\phi^{\prime}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
<div id="A2.SS8.SSS2.Px2.p46" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A2.SS8.SSS2.Px2.p46.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.SS8.SSS2.Px2.p46.1.1" class="ltx_text">By symmetry (reflecting across <math id="A2.SS8.SSS2.Px2.p46.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="x=\tfrac{1}{2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mn>2</mn></mfrac></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">x=\tfrac{1}{2}</annotation></semantics></math> inside <math id="A2.SS8.SSS2.Px2.p46.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="T" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>T</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">T</annotation></semantics></math>), the integrals <math id="A2.SS8.SSS2.Px2.p46.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\iint_{T}r_{1}^{2}\,du\,dv" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mo>∬</mo><mi>T</mi></msub><mrow><msubsup><mi>r</mi><mn>1</mn><mn>2</mn></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo rspace="0em">𝑑</mo><mi>u</mi></mrow><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo rspace="0em">𝑑</mo><mi>v</mi></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\iint_{T}r_{1}^{2}\,du\,dv</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="A2.SS8.SSS2.Px2.p46.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\iint_{T}r_{1}^{2}\phi^{\prime}\,du\,dv" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mo>∬</mo><mi>T</mi></msub><mrow><msubsup><mi>r</mi><mn>1</mn><mn>2</mn></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>ϕ</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo rspace="0em">𝑑</mo><mi>u</mi></mrow><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo rspace="0em">𝑑</mo><mi>v</mi></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\iint_{T}r_{1}^{2}\phi^{\prime}\,du\,dv</annotation></semantics></math> equal <math id="A2.SS8.SSS2.Px2.p46.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\iint_{T}r_{0}^{2}\,du\,dv" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mo>∬</mo><mi>T</mi></msub><mrow><msubsup><mi>r</mi><mn>0</mn><mn>2</mn></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo rspace="0em">𝑑</mo><mi>u</mi></mrow><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo rspace="0em">𝑑</mo><mi>v</mi></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\iint_{T}r_{0}^{2}\,du\,dv</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="A2.SS8.SSS2.Px2.p46.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\iint_{T}r_{0}^{2}\phi\,du\,dv" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mo>∬</mo><mi>T</mi></msub><mrow><msubsup><mi>r</mi><mn>0</mn><mn>2</mn></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>ϕ</mi><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo rspace="0em">𝑑</mo><mi>u</mi></mrow><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo rspace="0em">𝑑</mo><mi>v</mi></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\iint_{T}r_{0}^{2}\phi\,du\,dv</annotation></semantics></math>, respectively. Hence we only need the following <math id="A2.SS8.SSS2.Px2.p46.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\phi" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>ϕ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\phi</annotation></semantics></math>-integrals:</span></p>
</div>
<div id="A2.SS8.SSS2.Px2.p47" class="ltx_para">
<table id="A2.Ex263" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A2.Ex263X"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A2.Ex263X.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle I_{1}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>I</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle I_{1}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A2.Ex263X.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=\int_{0}^{\pi/4}\frac{\sin\phi}{(\cos\phi+\sin\phi)^{3}}\,d\phi," display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><msubsup><mo>∫</mo><mn>0</mn><mrow><mi>π</mi><mo>/</mo><mn>4</mn></mrow></msubsup></mstyle><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><mi>sin</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><mi>ϕ</mi></mrow><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>cos</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><mi>ϕ</mi></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi>sin</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><mi>ϕ</mi></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mn>3</mn></msup></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo rspace="0em">d</mo><mi>ϕ</mi></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\int_{0}^{\pi/4}\frac{\sin\phi}{(\cos\phi+\sin\phi)^{3}}\,d\phi,</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A2.Ex263Xa"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A2.Ex263Xa.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle I_{2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>I</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle I_{2}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A2.Ex263Xa.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=\int_{0}^{\pi/4}\frac{\cos\phi}{(\cos\phi+\sin\phi)^{3}}\,d\phi," display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><msubsup><mo>∫</mo><mn>0</mn><mrow><mi>π</mi><mo>/</mo><mn>4</mn></mrow></msubsup></mstyle><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><mi>cos</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><mi>ϕ</mi></mrow><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>cos</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><mi>ϕ</mi></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi>sin</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><mi>ϕ</mi></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mn>3</mn></msup></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo rspace="0em">d</mo><mi>ϕ</mi></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\int_{0}^{\pi/4}\frac{\cos\phi}{(\cos\phi+\sin\phi)^{3}}\,d\phi,</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A2.Ex263Xb"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A2.Ex263Xb.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle I_{3}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>I</mi><mn>3</mn></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle I_{3}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A2.Ex263Xb.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=\int_{0}^{\pi/4}\frac{d\phi}{(\cos\phi+\sin\phi)^{4}}," display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><msubsup><mo>∫</mo><mn>0</mn><mrow><mi>π</mi><mo>/</mo><mn>4</mn></mrow></msubsup></mstyle><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>ϕ</mi></mrow><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>cos</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><mi>ϕ</mi></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi>sin</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><mi>ϕ</mi></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mn>4</mn></msup></mfrac></mstyle></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\int_{0}^{\pi/4}\frac{d\phi}{(\cos\phi+\sin\phi)^{4}},</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A2.Ex263Xc"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A2.Ex263Xc.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle I_{4}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>I</mi><mn>4</mn></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle I_{4}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A2.Ex263Xc.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=\int_{0}^{\pi/4}\frac{\phi\,d\phi}{(\cos\phi+\sin\phi)^{4}}." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><msubsup><mo>∫</mo><mn>0</mn><mrow><mi>π</mi><mo>/</mo><mn>4</mn></mrow></msubsup></mstyle><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><mi>ϕ</mi><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>d</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>ϕ</mi></mrow><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>cos</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><mi>ϕ</mi></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi>sin</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><mi>ϕ</mi></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mn>4</mn></msup></mfrac></mstyle></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\int_{0}^{\pi/4}\frac{\phi\,d\phi}{(\cos\phi+\sin\phi)^{4}}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
<div id="A2.SS8.SSS2.Px2.p48" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A2.SS8.SSS2.Px2.p48.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.SS8.SSS2.Px2.p48.1.1" class="ltx_text">With the substitution <math id="A2.SS8.SSS2.Px2.p48.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\cos\phi+\sin\phi=\sqrt{2}\cos(\phi-\tfrac{\pi}{4})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>cos</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><mi>ϕ</mi></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi>sin</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><mi>ϕ</mi></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><msqrt><mn>2</mn></msqrt><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mi>cos</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>ϕ</mi><mo>−</mo><mfrac><mi>π</mi><mn>4</mn></mfrac></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\cos\phi+\sin\phi=\sqrt{2}\cos(\phi-\tfrac{\pi}{4})</annotation></semantics></math>, set <math id="A2.SS8.SSS2.Px2.p48.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="u=\phi-\tfrac{\pi}{4}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>u</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>ϕ</mi><mo>−</mo><mfrac><mi>π</mi><mn>4</mn></mfrac></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">u=\phi-\tfrac{\pi}{4}</annotation></semantics></math> (so <math id="A2.SS8.SSS2.Px2.p48.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="u\in[-\tfrac{\pi}{4},0]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>u</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mrow><mo>−</mo><mfrac><mi>π</mi><mn>4</mn></mfrac></mrow><mo>,</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">u\in[-\tfrac{\pi}{4},0]</annotation></semantics></math>) to get</span></p>
</div>
<div id="A2.SS8.SSS2.Px2.p49" class="ltx_para">
<table id="A2.Ex264" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A2.Ex264X"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A2.Ex264X.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle I_{1}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>I</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle I_{1}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A2.Ex264X.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=\frac{1}{4}\int_{-\pi/4}^{0}\big(\tan u\,\sec^{2}u+\sec^{2}u\big)\,du=\frac{1}{8}," display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo>=</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mn>4</mn></mfrac></mstyle><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mo>∫</mo></mstyle><msub><mrow></mrow><mrow><mo>−</mo><mi>π</mi><mo>/</mo><mn>4</mn></mrow></msub><msup><mrow></mrow><mn>0</mn></msup><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">(</mo><mi>tan</mi><mi>u</mi><mi>sec</mi><msup><mrow></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup><mi>u</mi><mo>+</mo><mi>sec</mi><msup><mrow></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup><mi>u</mi><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em" rspace="0.170em">)</mo><mi>d</mi><mi>u</mi><mo>=</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mn>8</mn></mfrac></mstyle><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\frac{1}{4}\int_{-\pi/4}^{0}\big(\tan u\,\sec^{2}u+\sec^{2}u\big)\,du=\frac{1}{8},</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A2.Ex264Xa"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A2.Ex264Xa.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle I_{2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>I</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle I_{2}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A2.Ex264Xa.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=\frac{1}{4}\int_{-\pi/4}^{0}\big(\sec^{2}u-\tan u\,\sec^{2}u\big)\,du=\frac{3}{8}," display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo>=</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mn>4</mn></mfrac></mstyle><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mo>∫</mo></mstyle><msub><mrow></mrow><mrow><mo>−</mo><mi>π</mi><mo>/</mo><mn>4</mn></mrow></msub><msup><mrow></mrow><mn>0</mn></msup><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">(</mo><mi>sec</mi><msup><mrow></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup><mi>u</mi><mo>−</mo><mi>tan</mi><mi>u</mi><mi>sec</mi><msup><mrow></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup><mi>u</mi><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em" rspace="0.170em">)</mo><mi>d</mi><mi>u</mi><mo>=</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mn>3</mn><mn>8</mn></mfrac></mstyle><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\frac{1}{4}\int_{-\pi/4}^{0}\big(\sec^{2}u-\tan u\,\sec^{2}u\big)\,du=\frac{3}{8},</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A2.Ex264Xb"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A2.Ex264Xb.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle I_{3}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>I</mi><mn>3</mn></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle I_{3}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A2.Ex264Xb.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=\frac{1}{4}\int_{-\pi/4}^{0}\sec^{4}u\,du=\frac{1}{3}," display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo>=</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mn>4</mn></mfrac></mstyle><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mo>∫</mo></mstyle><msub><mrow></mrow><mrow><mo>−</mo><mi>π</mi><mo>/</mo><mn>4</mn></mrow></msub><msup><mrow></mrow><mn>0</mn></msup><mi>sec</mi><msup><mrow></mrow><mn>4</mn></msup><mi>u</mi><mi>d</mi><mi>u</mi><mo>=</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mn>3</mn></mfrac></mstyle><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\frac{1}{4}\int_{-\pi/4}^{0}\sec^{4}u\,du=\frac{1}{3},</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A2.Ex264Xc"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A2.Ex264Xc.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle I_{4}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>I</mi><mn>4</mn></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle I_{4}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A2.Ex264Xc.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=\frac{1}{4}\int_{-\pi/4}^{0}u\,\sec^{4}u\,du+\frac{\pi}{16}\int_{-\pi/4}^{0}\sec^{4}u\,du=\frac{1}{12}\ln 2+\frac{1}{24}." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo>=</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mn>4</mn></mfrac></mstyle><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mo>∫</mo></mstyle><msub><mrow></mrow><mrow><mo>−</mo><mi>π</mi><mo>/</mo><mn>4</mn></mrow></msub><msup><mrow></mrow><mn>0</mn></msup><mi>u</mi><mi>sec</mi><msup><mrow></mrow><mn>4</mn></msup><mi>u</mi><mi>d</mi><mi>u</mi><mo>+</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mi>π</mi><mn>16</mn></mfrac></mstyle><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mo>∫</mo></mstyle><msub><mrow></mrow><mrow><mo>−</mo><mi>π</mi><mo>/</mo><mn>4</mn></mrow></msub><msup><mrow></mrow><mn>0</mn></msup><mi>sec</mi><msup><mrow></mrow><mn>4</mn></msup><mi>u</mi><mi>d</mi><mi>u</mi><mo>=</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mn>12</mn></mfrac></mstyle><mi>ln</mi><mn>2</mn><mo>+</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mn>24</mn></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\frac{1}{4}\int_{-\pi/4}^{0}u\,\sec^{4}u\,du+\frac{\pi}{16}\int_{-\pi/4}^{0}\sec^{4}u\,du=\frac{1}{12}\ln 2+\frac{1}{24}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
<div id="A2.SS8.SSS2.Px2.p50" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A2.SS8.SSS2.Px2.p50.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.SS8.SSS2.Px2.p50.1.1" class="ltx_text">(For <math id="A2.SS8.SSS2.Px2.p50.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="I_{4}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>I</mi><mn>4</mn></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">I_{4}</annotation></semantics></math>, integrate by parts using <math id="A2.SS8.SSS2.Px2.p50.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\int\sec^{4}u\,du=\tan u+\tfrac{1}{3}\tan^{3}u" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mo>∫</mo><mrow><msup><mi>sec</mi><mn>4</mn></msup><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><mrow><mi>u</mi><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo rspace="0em">𝑑</mo><mi>u</mi></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>tan</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><mi>u</mi></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mn>3</mn></mfrac><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><msup><mi>tan</mi><mn>3</mn></msup><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><mi>u</mi></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\int\sec^{4}u\,du=\tan u+\tfrac{1}{3}\tan^{3}u</annotation></semantics></math>.)</span></p>
</div>
<div id="A2.SS8.SSS2.Px2.p51" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A2.SS8.SSS2.Px2.p51.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.SS8.SSS2.Px2.p51.1.1" class="ltx_text">A short bookkeeping (expressing all needed <math id="A2.SS8.SSS2.Px2.p51.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="r,r^{2},\phi" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>r</mi><mo>,</mo><msup><mi>r</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>,</mo><mi>ϕ</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">r,r^{2},\phi</annotation></semantics></math> moments through <math id="A2.SS8.SSS2.Px2.p51.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="I_{1},\dots,I_{4}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>I</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>I</mi><mn>4</mn></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">I_{1},\dots,I_{4}</annotation></semantics></math>) yields</span></p>
</div>
<div id="A2.SS8.SSS2.Px2.p52" class="ltx_para">
<table id="A2.Ex265" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A2.Ex265.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\int_{T}A\,du\,dv=\frac{1}{3}I_{1}+\frac{\pi}{16}-\frac{\pi}{6}I_{2}+\frac{\pi}{8}I_{3}-\frac{1}{2}I_{4}," display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><msub><mo>∫</mo><mi>T</mi></msub><mrow><mi>A</mi><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo rspace="0em">𝑑</mo><mi>u</mi></mrow><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo rspace="0em">𝑑</mo><mi>v</mi></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mrow><mrow><mrow><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mn>3</mn></mfrac><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>I</mi><mn>1</mn></msub></mrow><mo>+</mo><mfrac><mi>π</mi><mn>16</mn></mfrac></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mfrac><mi>π</mi><mn>6</mn></mfrac><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>I</mi><mn>2</mn></msub></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mfrac><mi>π</mi><mn>8</mn></mfrac><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>I</mi><mn>3</mn></msub></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mn>2</mn></mfrac><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>I</mi><mn>4</mn></msub></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\int_{T}A\,du\,dv=\frac{1}{3}I_{1}+\frac{\pi}{16}-\frac{\pi}{6}I_{2}+\frac{\pi}{8}I_{3}-\frac{1}{2}I_{4},</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
<div id="A2.SS8.SSS2.Px2.p53" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A2.SS8.SSS2.Px2.p53.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.SS8.SSS2.Px2.p53.1.1" class="ltx_text">so</span></p>
</div>
<div id="A2.SS8.SSS2.Px2.p54" class="ltx_para">
<table id="A2.Ex266" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A2.Ex266.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbb{P}=4\int_{T}A\,du\,dv=\frac{4}{3}I_{1}+\frac{\pi}{4}-\frac{2\pi}{3}I_{2}+\frac{\pi}{2}I_{3}-2I_{4}." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>ℙ</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><mn>4</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><msub><mo>∫</mo><mi>T</mi></msub><mrow><mi>A</mi><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo rspace="0em">𝑑</mo><mi>u</mi></mrow><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo rspace="0em">𝑑</mo><mi>v</mi></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mrow><mrow><mrow><mfrac><mn>4</mn><mn>3</mn></mfrac><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>I</mi><mn>1</mn></msub></mrow><mo>+</mo><mfrac><mi>π</mi><mn>4</mn></mfrac></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mfrac><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>π</mi></mrow><mn>3</mn></mfrac><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>I</mi><mn>2</mn></msub></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mfrac><mi>π</mi><mn>2</mn></mfrac><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>I</mi><mn>3</mn></msub></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>I</mi><mn>4</mn></msub></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbb{P}=4\int_{T}A\,du\,dv=\frac{4}{3}I_{1}+\frac{\pi}{4}-\frac{2\pi}{3}I_{2}+\frac{\pi}{2}I_{3}-2I_{4}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
<div id="A2.SS8.SSS2.Px2.p55" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A2.SS8.SSS2.Px2.p55.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.SS8.SSS2.Px2.p55.1.1" class="ltx_text">Plugging the values of <math id="A2.SS8.SSS2.Px2.p55.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="I_{1},\dots,I_{4}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>I</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>I</mi><mn>4</mn></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">I_{1},\dots,I_{4}</annotation></semantics></math> gives the exact closed form</span></p>
</div>
<div id="A2.SS8.SSS2.Px2.p56" class="ltx_para">
<table id="A2.Ex267" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A2.Ex267.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\boxed{\ \mathbb{P}\;=\;\frac{\pi}{6}+\frac{1}{12}-\frac{1}{6}\ln 2\ }." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><menclose notation="box"><mrow><mi>ℙ</mi><mo lspace="0.558em" rspace="0.558em">=</mo><mrow><mrow><mfrac><mi>π</mi><mn>6</mn></mfrac><mo>+</mo><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mn>12</mn></mfrac></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mn>6</mn></mfrac><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mi>ln</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow></menclose><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\boxed{\ \mathbb{P}\;=\;\frac{\pi}{6}+\frac{1}{12}-\frac{1}{6}\ln 2\ }.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
<div id="A2.SS8.SSS2.Px2.p57" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A2.SS8.SSS2.Px2.p57.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.SS8.SSS2.Px2.p57.1.1" class="ltx_text">Numerically,</span></p>
</div>
<div id="A2.SS8.SSS2.Px2.p58" class="ltx_para">
<table id="A2.Ex268" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A2.Ex268.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbb{P}\approx 0.4914075788\quad\text{(to ten decimal places).}" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>ℙ</mi><mo>≈</mo><mn>0.4914075788</mn></mrow><mspace style="width:1em;" width="1em"></mspace><mtext>(to ten decimal places).</mtext></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbb{P}\approx 0.4914075788\quad\text{(to ten decimal places).}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
<div id="A2.SS8.SSS2.Px2.p59" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A2.SS8.SSS2.Px2.p59.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.SS8.SSS2.Px2.p59.1.1" class="ltx_text">∎</span></p>
</div>
</div>
<div id="A2.SS8.SSS2.Px2.2" class="ltx_proof">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_font_italic ltx_title_proof"><span id="A2.SS8.SSS2.Px2.2.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Standard Solution</span>.</h6>
<div id="A2.SS8.SSS2.Px2.p60" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A2.SS8.SSS2.Px2.p60.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.SS8.SSS2.Px2.p60.1.1" class="ltx_text">See the reference
<a href="https://Jane%20Street%20Puzzle" title="" class="ltx_ref ltx_href">https://www.janestreet.com/puzzles/beside-the-point-solution/</a>
For our November puzzle you had to compute the probability that two ordered points, randomly uniformly selected from a square, would have an equidistant point on the edge closest to the first point in the pair. Given the first point, without loss of generality uniformly selected from a lower triangular octant of the square outlined in black above, the second point would need to be in the blue-shaded symmetric difference of two circles centered at the bottom vertices of the square that pass through the first point.</span></p>
<table id="A2.Ex269" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A2.Ex269X"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A2.Ex269X.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle 8\cdot\left[\int_{0}^{1}\int_{0}^{x}\frac{x^{2}+y^{2}}{2}\left(\frac{\pi}{2}-2\tan^{-1}\frac{y}{x}\right)+\frac{xy}{2}\right." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mn>8</mn><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><mo>[</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mo>∫</mo></mstyle><msub><mrow></mrow><mn>0</mn></msub><msup><mrow></mrow><mn>1</mn></msup><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mo>∫</mo></mstyle><msub><mrow></mrow><mn>0</mn></msub><msup><mrow></mrow><mi>x</mi></msup><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><msup><mi>x</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>+</mo><msup><mi>y</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow><mn>2</mn></mfrac></mstyle><mo>(</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mi>π</mi><mn>2</mn></mfrac></mstyle><mo>−</mo><mn>2</mn><mi>tan</mi><msup><mrow></mrow><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mi>y</mi><mi>x</mi></mfrac></mstyle><mo>)</mo><mo>+</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>y</mi></mrow><mn>2</mn></mfrac></mstyle></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle 8\cdot\left[\int_{0}^{1}\int_{0}^{x}\frac{x^{2}+y^{2}}{2}\left(\frac{\pi}{2}-2\tan^{-1}\frac{y}{x}\right)+\frac{xy}{2}\right.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A2.Ex269Xa"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A2.Ex269Xa.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle+\frac{(1-x)^{2}+y^{2}}{2}\left(\frac{\pi}{2}-2\tan^{-1}\frac{x}{1-x}\right)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mi>x</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>+</mo><msup><mi>y</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow><mn>2</mn></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mi>π</mi><mn>2</mn></mfrac></mstyle><mo>−</mo><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><msup><mi>tan</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mi>x</mi><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mi>x</mi></mrow></mfrac></mstyle></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle+\frac{(1-x)^{2}+y^{2}}{2}\left(\frac{\pi}{2}-2\tan^{-1}\frac{x}{1-x}\right)</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A2.Ex269Xb"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A2.Ex269Xb.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\left.+\frac{(1-x)y}{2}dydx\right]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo>+</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mi>x</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>y</mi></mrow><mn>2</mn></mfrac></mstyle><mi>d</mi><mi>y</mi><mi>d</mi><mi>x</mi><mo>]</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\left.+\frac{(1-x)y}{2}dydx\right]</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A2.SS8.SSS2.Px2.p60.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.SS8.SSS2.Px2.p60.2.1" class="ltx_text">The precision requested for the answer meant an analytical solution likely would be required. Below the diagram is an integral expressing the total area of these blue-shaded regions, which comes to <math id="A2.SS8.SSS2.Px2.p60.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(1+2\pi-\ln(4))/12" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>+</mo><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>π</mi></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>ln</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>4</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>/</mo><mn>12</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(1+2\pi-\ln(4))/12</annotation></semantics></math>, or approximately <math id="A2.SS8.SSS2.Px2.p60.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="0.4914075788\ldots" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mn>0.4914075788</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">0.4914075788\ldots</annotation></semantics></math>
∎</span></p>
</div>
</div>
<div id="A2.SS8.SSS2.Px2.p61" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent"><span class="ltx_inline-block"><svg id="A2.SS8.SSS2.Px2.p61.pic1" class="ltx_picture" height="86.23" overflow="visible" version="1.1" viewBox="0 0 429.64 86.23" width="429.64"><g style="--ltx-stroke-color:#000000;--ltx-fill-color:#000000;" fill="#000000" stroke="#000000" stroke-width="0.4pt" transform="translate(0,86.23) matrix(1 0 0 -1 0 0)"><g style="--ltx-fill-color:#4D4D4D;" fill="#4D4D4D" fill-opacity="1.0"><path style="stroke:none" d="M 0 4.63 L 0 81.6 C 0 84.16 2.07 86.23 4.63 86.23 L 425.01 86.23 C 427.56 86.23 429.64 84.16 429.64 81.6 L 429.64 4.63 C 429.64 2.07 427.56 0 425.01 0 L 4.63 0 C 2.07 0 0 2.07 0 4.63 Z"></path></g><g style="--ltx-fill-color:#F9F9F9;" fill="#F9F9F9" fill-opacity="1.0"><path style="stroke:none" d="M 0.69 4.63 L 0.69 67.36 L 428.94 67.36 L 428.94 4.63 C 428.94 2.45 427.18 0.69 425.01 0.69 L 4.63 0.69 C 2.45 0.69 0.69 2.45 0.69 4.63 Z"></path></g><g fill-opacity="1.0" transform="matrix(1.0 0.0 0.0 1.0 20.38 71.99)"><foreignObject style="--ltx-fo-width:24.44em;--ltx-fo-height:0.69em;--ltx-fo-depth:0em;font-size:10pt;" height="9.61" overflow="visible" transform="matrix(1 0 0 -1 0 9.61)" width="338.18"><span class="ltx_foreignobject_container"><span class="ltx_foreignobject_content">
<span id="A2.SS8.SSS2.Px2.p61.pic1.1" class="ltx_inline-block ltx_minipage ltx_align_bottom" style="width:24.44em;">
<span id="A2.SS8.SSS2.Px2.p61.pic1.1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.SS8.SSS2.Px2.p61.pic1.1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold" style="--ltx-fg-color:#FFFFFF;">Rubric</span></span>
</span></span></span></foreignObject></g><g fill-opacity="1.0" transform="matrix(1.0 0.0 0.0 1.0 20.38 14.66)"><foreignObject style="--ltx-fo-width:33.06em;--ltx-fo-height:2.96em;--ltx-fo-depth:0.16em;font-size:10pt;" height="43.05" overflow="visible" transform="matrix(1 0 0 -1 0 40.9)" width="457.46"><span class="ltx_foreignobject_container"><span class="ltx_foreignobject_content">
<span id="A2.SS8.SSS2.Px2.p61.pic1.2" class="ltx_inline-block ltx_minipage ltx_align_bottom" style="width:33.06em;">
<span id="A2.SS8.SSS2.Px2.p61.pic1.2.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.SS8.SSS2.Px2.p61.pic1.2.1.1" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:80%;--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">1. Transform the problem into a valid geometry problem.</span></span>
<span id="A2.SS8.SSS2.Px2.p61.pic1.2.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.SS8.SSS2.Px2.p61.pic1.2.2.1" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:80%;--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">2. Set up the integral for the area of the region.</span></span>
<span id="A2.SS8.SSS2.Px2.p61.pic1.2.3" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.SS8.SSS2.Px2.p61.pic1.2.3.1" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:80%;--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">3. Compute the result.</span></span>
</span></span></span></foreignObject></g></g></svg></span>
</div>
<div id="A2.SS8.SSS2.Px2.p62" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent"><span class="ltx_inline-block"><svg id="A2.SS8.SSS2.Px2.p62.pic1" class="ltx_picture" height="54.13" overflow="visible" version="1.1" viewBox="0 0 429.64 54.13" width="429.64"><g style="--ltx-stroke-color:#000000;--ltx-fill-color:#000000;" fill="#000000" stroke="#000000" stroke-width="0.4pt" transform="translate(0,54.13) matrix(1 0 0 -1 0 0)"><g style="--ltx-fill-color:#5A996B;" fill="#5A996B" fill-opacity="1.0"><path style="stroke:none" d="M 0 4.63 L 0 49.51 C 0 52.06 2.07 54.13 4.63 54.13 L 425.01 54.13 C 427.56 54.13 429.64 52.06 429.64 49.51 L 429.64 4.63 C 429.64 2.07 427.56 0 425.01 0 L 4.63 0 C 2.07 0 0 2.07 0 4.63 Z"></path></g><g style="--ltx-fill-color:#F6FFF9;" fill="#F6FFF9" fill-opacity="1.0"><path style="stroke:none" d="M 0.69 4.63 L 0.69 35.38 L 428.94 35.38 L 428.94 4.63 C 428.94 2.45 427.18 0.69 425.01 0.69 L 4.63 0.69 C 2.45 0.69 0.69 2.45 0.69 4.63 Z"></path></g><g fill-opacity="1.0" transform="matrix(1.0 0.0 0.0 1.0 20.38 40.01)"><foreignObject style="--ltx-fo-width:24.44em;--ltx-fo-height:0.69em;--ltx-fo-depth:0em;font-size:10pt;" height="9.49" overflow="visible" transform="matrix(1 0 0 -1 0 9.49)" width="338.18"><span class="ltx_foreignobject_container"><span class="ltx_foreignobject_content">
