</section>
</section>
</section>
<section id="A2.SS9" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">9 </span>Learning New Knowledge</h3>

<section id="A2.SS9.SSS1" class="ltx_subsubsection">
<h4 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsubsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsubsection">(a) </span>Reading and understanding advanced materials</h4>

<section id="A2.SS9.SSS1.Px1" class="ltx_paragraph">
<h5 class="ltx_title ltx_title_paragraph" style="--ltx-fg-color:#00E000;">Problem 9a1 </h5>

<div id="A2.SS9.SSS1.Px1.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A2.SS9.SSS1.Px1.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.SS9.SSS1.Px1.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text"></span>
<br class="ltx_break" style="--ltx-break-space:-10.0pt;"></p>
</div>
<div id="A2.SS9.SSS1.Px1.p2" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent"><span class="ltx_inline-block"><svg id="A2.SS9.SSS1.Px1.p2.pic1" class="ltx_picture" height="276.97" overflow="visible" version="1.1" viewBox="0 0 429.64 276.97" width="429.64"><g style="--ltx-stroke-color:#000000;--ltx-fill-color:#000000;" fill="#000000" stroke="#000000" stroke-width="0.4pt" transform="translate(0,276.97) matrix(1 0 0 -1 0 0)"><g style="--ltx-fill-color:#3D6666;" fill="#3D6666" fill-opacity="1.0"><path style="stroke:none" d="M 0 4.63 L 0 272.34 C 0 274.9 2.07 276.97 4.63 276.97 L 425.01 276.97 C 427.56 276.97 429.64 274.9 429.64 272.34 L 429.64 4.63 C 429.64 2.07 427.56 0 425.01 0 L 4.63 0 C 2.07 0 0 2.07 0 4.63 Z"></path></g><g style="--ltx-fill-color:#F9F9F9;" fill="#F9F9F9" fill-opacity="1.0"><path style="stroke:none" d="M 0.69 4.63 L 0.69 258.1 L 428.94 258.1 L 428.94 4.63 C 428.94 2.45 427.18 0.69 425.01 0.69 L 4.63 0.69 C 2.45 0.69 0.69 2.45 0.69 4.63 Z"></path></g><g fill-opacity="1.0" transform="matrix(1.0 0.0 0.0 1.0 20.38 262.73)"><foreignObject style="--ltx-fo-width:24.44em;--ltx-fo-height:0.69em;--ltx-fo-depth:0em;font-size:10pt;" height="9.61" overflow="visible" transform="matrix(1 0 0 -1 0 9.61)" width="338.18"><span class="ltx_foreignobject_container"><span class="ltx_foreignobject_content">
<span id="A2.SS9.SSS1.Px1.p2.pic1.1" class="ltx_inline-block ltx_minipage ltx_align_bottom" style="width:24.44em;">
<span id="A2.SS9.SSS1.Px1.p2.pic1.1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.SS9.SSS1.Px1.p2.pic1.1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold" style="--ltx-fg-color:#FFFFFF;">Problem</span></span>
</span></span></span></foreignObject></g><g fill-opacity="1.0" transform="matrix(1.0 0.0 0.0 1.0 20.38 14.66)"><foreignObject style="--ltx-fo-width:32.01em;--ltx-fo-height:16.74em;--ltx-fo-depth:0.16em;font-size:10pt;" height="233.79" overflow="visible" transform="matrix(1 0 0 -1 0 231.64)" width="442.93"><span class="ltx_foreignobject_container"><span class="ltx_foreignobject_content">
<span id="A2.SS9.SSS1.Px1.p2.pic1.2" class="ltx_inline-block ltx_minipage ltx_align_bottom" style="width:32.01em;">
<span id="A2.SS9.SSS1.Px1.p2.pic1.2.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.SS9.SSS1.Px1.p2.pic1.2.1.1" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:80%;--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">You are reading the paper <a href="https://arxiv.org/pdf/2006.08574" title="" class="ltx_ref ltx_href">Large deviations of multichordal <math class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathrm{SLE}_{0+}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">SLE</mi><mrow><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">0</mn><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">+</mo></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathrm{SLE}_{0+}</annotation></semantics></math>, real rational functions, and zeta-regularized determinants of Laplacians</a> <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citep">[<a href="#bib.bib11" title="" class="ltx_ref">Peltola and Wang, 2024</a>]</cite> and encounter the following concept:</span></span>
<span id="A2.SS9.SSS1.Px1.p2.pic1.2.2" class="ltx_quote">
<span id="A2.SS9.SSS1.Px1.p2.pic1.2.2.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.SS9.SSS1.Px1.p2.pic1.2.2.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold" style="font-size:80%;--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">Loewner potential</span></span>
</span>
<span id="A2.I22" class="ltx_enumerate">
<span id="A2.I22.i1" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">1.</span> 
<span id="A2.I22.i1.p1" class="ltx_para">
<span id="A2.I22.i1.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.I22.i1.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:80%;--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">Identify the concept and explain its context.</span></span>
</span></span>
<span id="A2.I22.i2" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">2.</span> 
<span id="A2.I22.i2.p1" class="ltx_para">
<span id="A2.I22.i2.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.I22.i2.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:80%;--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">What are the relations between Loewner energy and Loewner potential?</span></span>
</span></span>
<span id="A2.I22.i3" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">3.</span> 
<span id="A2.I22.i3.p1" class="ltx_para">
<span id="A2.I22.i3.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.I22.i3.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:80%;--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">How do we apply it to the deterministic limit of multiple chordal SLE systems?</span></span>
</span></span>
</span><span class="ltx_inline-block"><svg id="A2.SS9.SSS1.Px1.p2.pic1.pic1" class="ltx_picture" color="#008000" height="18.24" overflow="visible" style="vertical-align:-4.1px" version="1.1" viewBox="0 0 18.24 18.24" width="18.24"><g style="--ltx-stroke-color:#009900;--ltx-fill-color:#009900;--ltx-fg-color:#009900;" color="#009900" fill="#009900" stroke="#009900" stroke-width="1.8pt" transform="translate(0,18.24) matrix(1 0 0 -1 0 0) translate(1.25,0) translate(0,1.25)"><path style="fill:none" d="M 0 7.87 L 5.51 0 L 15.75 15.75"></path></g></svg></span>
<span id="A2.SS9.SSS1.Px1.p2.pic1.2.3" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.SS9.SSS1.Px1.p2.pic1.2.3.1" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:80%;--ltx-fg-color:#008000;">GPT-5 thinking passed</span></span>
<span id="A2.SS9.SSS1.Px1.p2.pic1.2.4" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.SS9.SSS1.Px1.p2.pic1.2.4.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic" style="font-size:80%;--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">Proposed by Jiaxin Zhang</span></span>
</span></span></span></foreignObject></g></g></svg></span>
</div>
<div id="A2.SS9.SSS1.Px1.1" class="ltx_proof">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_font_italic ltx_title_proof"><span id="A2.SS9.SSS1.Px1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Response of GPT-5-thinking</span>.</h6>
<div id="A2.SS9.SSS1.Px1.p3" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A2.SS9.SSS1.Px1.p3.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.SS9.SSS1.Px1.p3.1.1" class="ltx_text">Loewner potential and its role</span></p>
</div>
<div id="A2.SS9.SSS1.Px1.p4" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A2.SS9.SSS1.Px1.p4.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.SS9.SSS1.Px1.p4.1.1" class="ltx_text">1. Definition of the Loewner potential</span></p>
</div>
<div id="A2.SS9.SSS1.Px1.p5" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A2.SS9.SSS1.Px1.p5.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.SS9.SSS1.Px1.p5.1.1" class="ltx_text">For a multichord <math id="A2.SS9.SSS1.Px1.p5.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\gamma=(\gamma_{1},\dots,\gamma_{n})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>γ</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>γ</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>γ</mi><mi>n</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\gamma=(\gamma_{1},\dots,\gamma_{n})</annotation></semantics></math> in a domain <math id="A2.SS9.SSS1.Px1.p5.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="D" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>D</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">D</annotation></semantics></math> with boundary points
<math id="A2.SS9.SSS1.Px1.p5.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="x_{1}&lt;\dots&lt;x_{2n}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>x</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>&lt;</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">⋯</mi><mo>&lt;</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>n</mi></mrow></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">x_{1}&lt;\dots&lt;x_{2n}</annotation></semantics></math> paired by a link pattern <math id="A2.SS9.SSS1.Px1.p5.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\alpha" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>α</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\alpha</annotation></semantics></math>, the <em id="A2.SS9.SSS1.Px1.p5.1.1.1" class="ltx_emph ltx_font_italic">Loewner potential</em> is the functional</span></p>
<table id="A2.E5" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A2.E5.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="H_{D}(\gamma)=\frac{1}{12}\sum_{j=1}^{n}I_{D;x_{a_{j}},x_{b_{j}}}(\gamma_{j})\;+\;m_{D}(\gamma)\;-\;\frac{1}{4}\sum_{j=1}^{n}\log P_{D;x_{a_{j}},x_{b_{j}}}," display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>H</mi><mi>D</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>γ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mrow><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mn>12</mn></mfrac><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>j</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>n</mi></munderover><mrow><msub><mi>I</mi><mrow><mi>D</mi><mo>;</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><msub><mi>a</mi><mi>j</mi></msub></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><msub><mi>b</mi><mi>j</mi></msub></msub></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>γ</mi><mi>j</mi></msub><mo rspace="0.280em" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.502em">+</mo><mrow><msub><mi>m</mi><mi>D</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>γ</mi><mo rspace="0.280em" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.502em">−</mo><mrow><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mn>4</mn></mfrac><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>j</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>n</mi></munderover><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><msub><mi>P</mi><mrow><mi>D</mi><mo>;</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><msub><mi>a</mi><mi>j</mi></msub></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><msub><mi>b</mi><mi>j</mi></msub></msub></mrow></msub></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">H_{D}(\gamma)=\frac{1}{12}\sum_{j=1}^{n}I_{D;x_{a_{j}},x_{b_{j}}}(\gamma_{j})\;+\;m_{D}(\gamma)\;-\;\frac{1}{4}\sum_{j=1}^{n}\log P_{D;x_{a_{j}},x_{b_{j}}},</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(5)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A2.SS9.SSS1.Px1.p5.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.SS9.SSS1.Px1.p5.2.1" class="ltx_text">where <math id="A2.SS9.SSS1.Px1.p5.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="I_{D;x,y}(\gamma)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>I</mi><mrow><mi>D</mi><mo>;</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>y</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>γ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">I_{D;x,y}(\gamma)</annotation></semantics></math> is the (single-chord) Loewner energy, <math id="A2.SS9.SSS1.Px1.p5.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="m_{D}(\gamma)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>m</mi><mi>D</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>γ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">m_{D}(\gamma)</annotation></semantics></math> is a Brownian loop–measure interaction term, and <math id="A2.SS9.SSS1.Px1.p5.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="P_{D;x,y}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>P</mi><mrow><mi>D</mi><mo>;</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>y</mi></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">P_{D;x,y}</annotation></semantics></math> denotes the Poisson excursion kernel.</span></p>
</div>
<div id="A2.SS9.SSS1.Px1.p6" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A2.SS9.SSS1.Px1.p6.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.SS9.SSS1.Px1.p6.1.1" class="ltx_text">For smooth chords, <math id="A2.SS9.SSS1.Px1.p6.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="H_{D}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>H</mi><mi>D</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">H_{D}</annotation></semantics></math> also has a spectral representation:</span></p>
<table id="A2.E6" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A2.E6.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="H_{D}(\gamma)=\log\det\nolimits_{\zeta}\Delta_{D}\;-\!\!\sum_{C\ \mathrm{comp.\ of}D\setminus\bigcup_{i}\gamma_{i}}\!\!\log\det\nolimits_{\zeta}\Delta_{C}\;-\;n\,\lambda,\qquad\lambda=\tfrac{1}{2}\log\pi." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>H</mi><mi>D</mi></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>γ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>=</mo><mi>log</mi><msub><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0.167em">det</mo><mi>ζ</mi></msub><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mi>D</mi></msub><mpadded style="width:0.632em;" width="0.632em"><mo>−</mo></mpadded><munder><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>C</mi><mo lspace="0.410em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>comp</mi></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.567em">.</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>of</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>D</mi></mrow><mo>∖</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="false"><msub><mo maxsize="0.700em" minsize="0.700em" stretchy="true">⋃</mo><mi>i</mi></msub></mstyle><msub><mi>γ</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></mrow></mrow></mrow></munder><mi>log</mi><msub><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0.167em">det</mo><mi>ζ</mi></msub><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mi>C</mi></msub><mo rspace="0.502em">−</mo><mi>n</mi><mi>λ</mi><mo rspace="2.167em">,</mo><mi>λ</mi><mo>=</mo><mstyle displaystyle="false"><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mn>2</mn></mfrac></mstyle><mi>log</mi><mi>π</mi><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">H_{D}(\gamma)=\log\det\nolimits_{\zeta}\Delta_{D}\;-\!\!\sum_{C\ \mathrm{comp.\ of}D\setminus\bigcup_{i}\gamma_{i}}\!\!\log\det\nolimits_{\zeta}\Delta_{C}\;-\;n\,\lambda,\qquad\lambda=\tfrac{1}{2}\log\pi.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(6)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A2.SS9.SSS1.Px1.p6.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.SS9.SSS1.Px1.p6.2.1" class="ltx_text">Thus <math id="A2.SS9.SSS1.Px1.p6.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="H" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>H</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">H</annotation></semantics></math> behaves as a conformally covariant “global potential” attached to the configuration.</span></p>
</div>
<div id="A2.SS9.SSS1.Px1.p7" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A2.SS9.SSS1.Px1.p7.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.SS9.SSS1.Px1.p7.1.1" class="ltx_text">2. Relation to Loewner energy</span></p>
</div>
<div id="A2.SS9.SSS1.Px1.p8" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A2.SS9.SSS1.Px1.p8.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.SS9.SSS1.Px1.p8.1.1" class="ltx_text">For a single chord, the <em id="A2.SS9.SSS1.Px1.p8.1.1.1" class="ltx_emph ltx_font_italic">Loewner energy</em> is the Dirichlet energy of the (capacity–parametrized) driving function <math id="A2.SS9.SSS1.Px1.p8.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="W" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>W</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">W</annotation></semantics></math>:</span></p>
<table id="A2.E7" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A2.E7.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="I_{D;x,y}(\gamma)=\frac{1}{2}\int_{0}^{\infty}\dot{W}_{t}^{2}\,dt," display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>I</mi><mrow><mi>D</mi><mo>;</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>y</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>γ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mn>2</mn></mfrac><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><msubsup><mo>∫</mo><mn>0</mn><mi mathvariant="normal">∞</mi></msubsup><mrow><msubsup><mover accent="true"><mi>W</mi><mo>˙</mo></mover><mi>t</mi><mn>2</mn></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo rspace="0em">𝑑</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">I_{D;x,y}(\gamma)=\frac{1}{2}\int_{0}^{\infty}\dot{W}_{t}^{2}\,dt,</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(7)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A2.SS9.SSS1.Px1.p8.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.SS9.SSS1.Px1.p8.2.1" class="ltx_text">which vanishes exactly when <math id="A2.SS9.SSS1.Px1.p8.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\gamma" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>γ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\gamma</annotation></semantics></math> is the hyperbolic geodesic between <math id="A2.SS9.SSS1.Px1.p8.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="x" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>x</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">x</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="A2.SS9.SSS1.Px1.p8.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="y" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>y</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">y</annotation></semantics></math>.</span></p>
</div>
<div id="A2.SS9.SSS1.Px1.p9" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A2.SS9.SSS1.Px1.p9.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.SS9.SSS1.Px1.p9.1.1" class="ltx_text">For multiple chords, the <em id="A2.SS9.SSS1.Px1.p9.1.1.1" class="ltx_emph ltx_font_italic">multichordal Loewner energy</em> is the good rate function in the large deviation principle. It is defined from the potential by subtracting the minimal possible value of <math id="A2.SS9.SSS1.Px1.p9.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="H" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>H</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">H</annotation></semantics></math> for the given boundary data and halving:</span></p>
<table id="A2.E8" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A2.E8.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="M_{D}^{\alpha}(x_{1},\dots,x_{2n}):=\inf_{\gamma\in X_{\alpha}}H_{D}(\gamma),\qquad I_{D}^{\alpha}(\gamma):=\frac{1}{2}\Big(H_{D}(\gamma)-M_{D}^{\alpha}(x_{1},\dots,x_{2n})\Big)\geq 0." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mrow><msubsup><mi>M</mi><mi>D</mi><mi>α</mi></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>n</mi></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.1389em">:=</mo><mrow><munder><mo lspace="0.1389em" movablelimits="false" rspace="0.167em">inf</mo><mrow><mi>γ</mi><mo>∈</mo><msub><mi>X</mi><mi>α</mi></msub></mrow></munder><mrow><msub><mi>H</mi><mi>D</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>γ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="2.167em">,</mo><mrow><mrow><msubsup><mi>I</mi><mi>D</mi><mi>α</mi></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>γ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>:=</mo><mrow><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mn>2</mn></mfrac><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="1.600em" minsize="1.600em">(</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>H</mi><mi>D</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>γ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>M</mi><mi>D</mi><mi>α</mi></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>n</mi></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo maxsize="1.600em" minsize="1.600em">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>≥</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">M_{D}^{\alpha}(x_{1},\dots,x_{2n}):=\inf_{\gamma\in X_{\alpha}}H_{D}(\gamma),\qquad I_{D}^{\alpha}(\gamma):=\frac{1}{2}\Big(H_{D}(\gamma)-M_{D}^{\alpha}(x_{1},\dots,x_{2n})\Big)\geq 0.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(8)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A2.SS9.SSS1.Px1.p9.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.SS9.SSS1.Px1.p9.2.1" class="ltx_text">Hence <math id="A2.SS9.SSS1.Px1.p9.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="H" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>H</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">H</annotation></semantics></math> encodes both the individual chord energies and their interaction, while <math id="A2.SS9.SSS1.Px1.p9.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="I" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>I</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">I</annotation></semantics></math> is the normalized, non-negative rate function. Moreover, the minimal potential admits a semiclassical interpretation:</span></p>
<table id="A2.E9" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A2.E9.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="-\lim_{\kappa\to 0^{+}}\,\kappa\,\log Z_{\alpha}(D;x_{1},\dots,x_{2n})=\tfrac{1}{2}\,M_{D}^{\alpha}(x_{1},\dots,x_{2n})," display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo>−</mo><munder><mo lspace="0em" movablelimits="false" rspace="0.167em">lim</mo><mrow><mi>κ</mi><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><msup><mn>0</mn><mo>+</mo></msup></mrow></munder><mi>κ</mi><mi>log</mi><msub><mi>Z</mi><mi>α</mi></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>D</mi><mo>;</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>n</mi></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>=</mo><mstyle displaystyle="false"><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mn>2</mn></mfrac></mstyle><msubsup><mi>M</mi><mi>D</mi><mi>α</mi></msubsup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>n</mi></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">-\lim_{\kappa\to 0^{+}}\,\kappa\,\log Z_{\alpha}(D;x_{1},\dots,x_{2n})=\tfrac{1}{2}\,M_{D}^{\alpha}(x_{1},\dots,x_{2n}),</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(9)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A2.SS9.SSS1.Px1.p9.3" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.SS9.SSS1.Px1.p9.3.1" class="ltx_text">so that <math id="A2.SS9.SSS1.Px1.p9.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="U:=\tfrac{1}{2}M_{D}^{\alpha}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>U</mi><mo>:=</mo><mrow><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mn>2</mn></mfrac><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>M</mi><mi>D</mi><mi>α</mi></msubsup></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">U:=\tfrac{1}{2}M_{D}^{\alpha}</annotation></semantics></math> acts as a Hamilton–Jacobi potential for the system.</span></p>
</div>
<div id="A2.SS9.SSS1.Px1.p10" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A2.SS9.SSS1.Px1.p10.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.SS9.SSS1.Px1.p10.1.1" class="ltx_text">3. Deterministic limit of multiple chordal SLE</span></p>
</div>
<div id="A2.SS9.SSS1.Px1.p11" class="ltx_para">
<ul id="A2.I23" class="ltx_itemize">
<li id="A2.I23.i1" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">•</span> 
<div id="A2.I23.i1.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A2.I23.i1.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.I23.i1.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Large deviations and limit shape.</span> The laws of multichordal <math id="A2.I23.i1.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathrm{SLE}_{\kappa}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>SLE</mi><mi>κ</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathrm{SLE}_{\kappa}</annotation></semantics></math> satisfy a strong LDP with good rate function <math id="A2.I23.i1.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="I_{D}^{\alpha}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mi>I</mi><mi>D</mi><mi>α</mi></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">I_{D}^{\alpha}</annotation></semantics></math>. As <math id="A2.I23.i1.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\kappa\to 0^{+}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>κ</mi><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><msup><mn>0</mn><mo>+</mo></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\kappa\to 0^{+}</annotation></semantics></math>, the random multichords converge (in probability, in the Hausdorff topology) to the unique minimizer of <math id="A2.I23.i1.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="H_{D}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>H</mi><mi>D</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">H_{D}</annotation></semantics></math> in <math id="A2.I23.i1.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="X_{\alpha}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>X</mi><mi>α</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">X_{\alpha}</annotation></semantics></math>—a geodesic multichord.</p>
</div></li>
<li id="A2.I23.i2" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">•</span> 
<div id="A2.I23.i2.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A2.I23.i2.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.I23.i2.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Rational function description.</span> In the upper half-plane with marked points <math id="A2.I23.i2.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="x_{1}&lt;\dots&lt;x_{2n}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>x</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>&lt;</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">⋯</mi><mo>&lt;</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>n</mi></mrow></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">x_{1}&lt;\dots&lt;x_{2n}</annotation></semantics></math>, each minimizer/geodesic multichord is the <em id="A2.I23.i2.p1.1.2" class="ltx_emph ltx_font_italic">real locus of a real rational function</em> of degree <math id="A2.I23.i2.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="n+1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">n+1</annotation></semantics></math> with critical points <math id="A2.I23.i2.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\{x_{1},\dots,x_{2n}\}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>n</mi></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\{x_{1},\dots,x_{2n}\}</annotation></semantics></math>. This ensures uniqueness (one for each link pattern) and ties the limit to real enumerative geometry (Shapiro’s conjecture).</p>
</div></li>
<li id="A2.I23.i3" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">•</span> 
<div id="A2.I23.i3.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A2.I23.i3.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.I23.i3.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Deterministic dynamics and PDE.</span> Writing <math id="A2.I23.i3.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="U=\tfrac{1}{2}M_{D}^{\alpha}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>U</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mn>2</mn></mfrac><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>M</mi><mi>D</mi><mi>α</mi></msubsup></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">U=\tfrac{1}{2}M_{D}^{\alpha}</annotation></semantics></math>, the driving function <math id="A2.I23.i3.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="W_{t}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>W</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">W_{t}</annotation></semantics></math> of the minimizing chord solves</p>
<table id="A2.Ex270" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A2.Ex270.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\dot{W}_{t}=-\,\partial_{a_{j}}U(V_{1}(t),\dots,W_{t},\dots,V_{2n}(t)),\qquad\dot{V}_{i}(t)=\frac{2}{V_{i}(t)-W_{t}}," display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>W</mi><mo>˙</mo></mover><mi>t</mi></msub><mo rspace="0em">=</mo><mo lspace="0em">−</mo><msub><mo>∂</mo><msub><mi>a</mi><mi>j</mi></msub></msub><mi>U</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>V</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>W</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>V</mi><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>n</mi></mrow></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo rspace="2.167em">,</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>V</mi><mo>˙</mo></mover><mi>i</mi></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mn>2</mn><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>V</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>W</mi><mi>t</mi></msub></mrow></mfrac><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\dot{W}_{t}=-\,\partial_{a_{j}}U(V_{1}(t),\dots,W_{t},\dots,V_{2n}(t)),\qquad\dot{V}_{i}(t)=\frac{2}{V_{i}(t)-W_{t}},</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A2.I23.i3.p1.2" class="ltx_p">and <math id="A2.I23.i3.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="U" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>U</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">U</annotation></semantics></math> satisfies the system of quadratic first-order PDEs that arise as the <math id="A2.I23.i3.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="c\to-\infty" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>c</mi><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><mrow><mo>−</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">∞</mi></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">c\to-\infty</annotation></semantics></math> (semiclassical) limit of the level-two BPZ equations. These encode the deterministic “hydrodynamics” of the <math id="A2.I23.i3.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\kappa\to 0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>κ</mi><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\kappa\to 0</annotation></semantics></math> limit.</p>
</div></li>
</ul>
</div>
<div id="A2.SS9.SSS1.Px1.p12" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A2.SS9.SSS1.Px1.p12.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.SS9.SSS1.Px1.p12.1.1" class="ltx_text">In summary, the Loewner potential <math id="A2.SS9.SSS1.Px1.p12.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="H" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>H</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">H</annotation></semantics></math> is the global conformally covariant functional whose minimizers describe the deterministic shapes emerging in the small-<math id="A2.SS9.SSS1.Px1.p12.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\kappa" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>κ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\kappa</annotation></semantics></math> limit; the Loewner energy <math id="A2.SS9.SSS1.Px1.p12.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="I" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>I</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">I</annotation></semantics></math> is the corresponding non-negative rate function governing fluctuations around them.</span></p>
</div>
<div id="A2.SS9.SSS1.Px1.p13" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A2.SS9.SSS1.Px1.p13.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.SS9.SSS1.Px1.p13.1.1" class="ltx_text">∎</span></p>
</div>
</div>
<div id="A2.SS9.SSS1.Px1.2" class="ltx_proof">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_font_italic ltx_title_proof"><span id="A2.SS9.SSS1.Px1.2.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Standard Solution</span>.</h6>
<div id="A2.SS9.SSS1.Px1.p14" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A2.SS9.SSS1.Px1.p14.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.SS9.SSS1.Px1.p14.1.1" class="ltx_text">See the paper <a href="https://arxiv.org/pdf/2006.08574" title="" class="ltx_ref ltx_href">Large deviations of multichordal <math class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathrm{SLE}_{0+}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>SLE</mi><mrow><mn>0</mn><mo>+</mo></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathrm{SLE}_{0+}</annotation></semantics></math>, real rational functions, and zeta-regularized determinants of Laplacians</a>.
Loewner potential and its role</span></p>
</div>
<div id="A2.SS9.SSS1.Px1.p15" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A2.SS9.SSS1.Px1.p15.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.SS9.SSS1.Px1.p15.1.1" class="ltx_text">1. Definition of the Loewner potential</span></p>
</div>
<div id="A2.SS9.SSS1.Px1.p16" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A2.SS9.SSS1.Px1.p16.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.SS9.SSS1.Px1.p16.1.1" class="ltx_text">For a multichord <math id="A2.SS9.SSS1.Px1.p16.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\gamma=(\gamma_{1},\dots,\gamma_{n})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>γ</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>γ</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>γ</mi><mi>n</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\gamma=(\gamma_{1},\dots,\gamma_{n})</annotation></semantics></math> in a domain <math id="A2.SS9.SSS1.Px1.p16.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="D" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>D</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">D</annotation></semantics></math> with boundary points
<math id="A2.SS9.SSS1.Px1.p16.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="x_{1}&lt;\dots&lt;x_{2n}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>x</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>&lt;</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">⋯</mi><mo>&lt;</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>n</mi></mrow></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">x_{1}&lt;\dots&lt;x_{2n}</annotation></semantics></math> paired by a link pattern <math id="A2.SS9.SSS1.Px1.p16.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\alpha" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>α</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\alpha</annotation></semantics></math>, the <em id="A2.SS9.SSS1.Px1.p16.1.1.1" class="ltx_emph ltx_font_italic">Loewner potential</em> is the functional</span></p>
<table id="A2.E10" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A2.E10.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="H_{D}(\gamma)=\frac{1}{12}\sum_{j=1}^{n}I_{D;x_{a_{j}},x_{b_{j}}}(\gamma_{j})\;+\;m_{D}(\gamma)\;-\;\frac{1}{4}\sum_{j=1}^{n}\log P_{D;x_{a_{j}},x_{b_{j}}}," display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>H</mi><mi>D</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>γ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mrow><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mn>12</mn></mfrac><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>j</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>n</mi></munderover><mrow><msub><mi>I</mi><mrow><mi>D</mi><mo>;</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><msub><mi>a</mi><mi>j</mi></msub></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><msub><mi>b</mi><mi>j</mi></msub></msub></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>γ</mi><mi>j</mi></msub><mo rspace="0.280em" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.502em">+</mo><mrow><msub><mi>m</mi><mi>D</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>γ</mi><mo rspace="0.280em" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.502em">−</mo><mrow><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mn>4</mn></mfrac><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>j</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>n</mi></munderover><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><msub><mi>P</mi><mrow><mi>D</mi><mo>;</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><msub><mi>a</mi><mi>j</mi></msub></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><msub><mi>b</mi><mi>j</mi></msub></msub></mrow></msub></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">H_{D}(\gamma)=\frac{1}{12}\sum_{j=1}^{n}I_{D;x_{a_{j}},x_{b_{j}}}(\gamma_{j})\;+\;m_{D}(\gamma)\;-\;\frac{1}{4}\sum_{j=1}^{n}\log P_{D;x_{a_{j}},x_{b_{j}}},</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(10)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A2.SS9.SSS1.Px1.p16.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.SS9.SSS1.Px1.p16.2.1" class="ltx_text">where <math id="A2.SS9.SSS1.Px1.p16.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="I_{D;x,y}(\gamma)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>I</mi><mrow><mi>D</mi><mo>;</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>y</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>γ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">I_{D;x,y}(\gamma)</annotation></semantics></math> is the (single-chord) Loewner energy, <math id="A2.SS9.SSS1.Px1.p16.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="m_{D}(\gamma)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>m</mi><mi>D</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>γ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">m_{D}(\gamma)</annotation></semantics></math> is a Brownian loop–measure interaction term, and <math id="A2.SS9.SSS1.Px1.p16.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="P_{D;x,y}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>P</mi><mrow><mi>D</mi><mo>;</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>y</mi></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">P_{D;x,y}</annotation></semantics></math> denotes the Poisson excursion kernel.</span></p>
</div>
<div id="A2.SS9.SSS1.Px1.p17" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A2.SS9.SSS1.Px1.p17.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.SS9.SSS1.Px1.p17.1.1" class="ltx_text">For smooth chords, <math id="A2.SS9.SSS1.Px1.p17.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="H_{D}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>H</mi><mi>D</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">H_{D}</annotation></semantics></math> also has a spectral representation:</span></p>
<table id="A2.E11" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A2.E11.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="H_{D}(\gamma)=\log\det\nolimits_{\zeta}\Delta_{D}\;-\!\!\sum_{C\ \mathrm{comp.\ of}D\setminus\bigcup_{i}\gamma_{i}}\!\!\log\det\nolimits_{\zeta}\Delta_{C}\;-\;n\,\lambda,\qquad\lambda=\tfrac{1}{2}\log\pi." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>H</mi><mi>D</mi></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>γ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>=</mo><mi>log</mi><msub><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0.167em">det</mo><mi>ζ</mi></msub><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mi>D</mi></msub><mpadded style="width:0.632em;" width="0.632em"><mo>−</mo></mpadded><munder><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>C</mi><mo lspace="0.410em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>comp</mi></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.567em">.</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>of</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>D</mi></mrow><mo>∖</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="false"><msub><mo maxsize="0.700em" minsize="0.700em" stretchy="true">⋃</mo><mi>i</mi></msub></mstyle><msub><mi>γ</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></mrow></mrow></mrow></munder><mi>log</mi><msub><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0.167em">det</mo><mi>ζ</mi></msub><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mi>C</mi></msub><mo rspace="0.502em">−</mo><mi>n</mi><mi>λ</mi><mo rspace="2.167em">,</mo><mi>λ</mi><mo>=</mo><mstyle displaystyle="false"><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mn>2</mn></mfrac></mstyle><mi>log</mi><mi>π</mi><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">H_{D}(\gamma)=\log\det\nolimits_{\zeta}\Delta_{D}\;-\!\!\sum_{C\ \mathrm{comp.\ of}D\setminus\bigcup_{i}\gamma_{i}}\!\!\log\det\nolimits_{\zeta}\Delta_{C}\;-\;n\,\lambda,\qquad\lambda=\tfrac{1}{2}\log\pi.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(11)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A2.SS9.SSS1.Px1.p17.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.SS9.SSS1.Px1.p17.2.1" class="ltx_text">Thus <math id="A2.SS9.SSS1.Px1.p17.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="H" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>H</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">H</annotation></semantics></math> behaves as a conformally covariant “global potential” attached to the configuration.</span></p>
</div>
<div id="A2.SS9.SSS1.Px1.p18" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A2.SS9.SSS1.Px1.p18.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.SS9.SSS1.Px1.p18.1.1" class="ltx_text">2. Relation to Loewner energy</span></p>
</div>
<div id="A2.SS9.SSS1.Px1.p19" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A2.SS9.SSS1.Px1.p19.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.SS9.SSS1.Px1.p19.1.1" class="ltx_text">For a single chord, the <em id="A2.SS9.SSS1.Px1.p19.1.1.1" class="ltx_emph ltx_font_italic">Loewner energy</em> is the Dirichlet energy of the (capacity–parametrized) driving function <math id="A2.SS9.SSS1.Px1.p19.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="W" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>W</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">W</annotation></semantics></math>:</span></p>
<table id="A2.E12" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A2.E12.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="I_{D;x,y}(\gamma)=\frac{1}{2}\int_{0}^{\infty}\dot{W}_{t}^{2}\,dt," display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>I</mi><mrow><mi>D</mi><mo>;</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>y</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>γ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mn>2</mn></mfrac><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><msubsup><mo>∫</mo><mn>0</mn><mi mathvariant="normal">∞</mi></msubsup><mrow><msubsup><mover accent="true"><mi>W</mi><mo>˙</mo></mover><mi>t</mi><mn>2</mn></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo rspace="0em">𝑑</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">I_{D;x,y}(\gamma)=\frac{1}{2}\int_{0}^{\infty}\dot{W}_{t}^{2}\,dt,</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(12)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A2.SS9.SSS1.Px1.p19.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.SS9.SSS1.Px1.p19.2.1" class="ltx_text">which vanishes exactly when <math id="A2.SS9.SSS1.Px1.p19.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\gamma" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>γ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\gamma</annotation></semantics></math> is the hyperbolic geodesic between <math id="A2.SS9.SSS1.Px1.p19.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="x" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>x</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">x</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="A2.SS9.SSS1.Px1.p19.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="y" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>y</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">y</annotation></semantics></math>.</span></p>
</div>
<div id="A2.SS9.SSS1.Px1.p20" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A2.SS9.SSS1.Px1.p20.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.SS9.SSS1.Px1.p20.1.1" class="ltx_text">For multiple chords, the <em id="A2.SS9.SSS1.Px1.p20.1.1.1" class="ltx_emph ltx_font_italic">multichordal Loewner energy</em> is the good rate function in the large deviation principle. It is defined from the potential by subtracting the minimal possible value of <math id="A2.SS9.SSS1.Px1.p20.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="H" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>H</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">H</annotation></semantics></math> for the given boundary data and halving:</span></p>
<table id="A2.E13" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A2.E13.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="M_{D}^{\alpha}(x_{1},\dots,x_{2n}):=\inf_{\gamma\in X_{\alpha}}H_{D}(\gamma),\qquad I_{D}^{\alpha}(\gamma):=\frac{1}{2}\Big(H_{D}(\gamma)-M_{D}^{\alpha}(x_{1},\dots,x_{2n})\Big)\geq 0." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mrow><msubsup><mi>M</mi><mi>D</mi><mi>α</mi></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>n</mi></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.1389em">:=</mo><mrow><munder><mo lspace="0.1389em" movablelimits="false" rspace="0.167em">inf</mo><mrow><mi>γ</mi><mo>∈</mo><msub><mi>X</mi><mi>α</mi></msub></mrow></munder><mrow><msub><mi>H</mi><mi>D</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>γ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="2.167em">,</mo><mrow><mrow><msubsup><mi>I</mi><mi>D</mi><mi>α</mi></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>γ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>:=</mo><mrow><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mn>2</mn></mfrac><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="1.600em" minsize="1.600em">(</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>H</mi><mi>D</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>γ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>M</mi><mi>D</mi><mi>α</mi></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>n</mi></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo maxsize="1.600em" minsize="1.600em">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>≥</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">M_{D}^{\alpha}(x_{1},\dots,x_{2n}):=\inf_{\gamma\in X_{\alpha}}H_{D}(\gamma),\qquad I_{D}^{\alpha}(\gamma):=\frac{1}{2}\Big(H_{D}(\gamma)-M_{D}^{\alpha}(x_{1},\dots,x_{2n})\Big)\geq 0.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(13)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A2.SS9.SSS1.Px1.p20.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.SS9.SSS1.Px1.p20.2.1" class="ltx_text">Hence <math id="A2.SS9.SSS1.Px1.p20.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="H" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>H</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">H</annotation></semantics></math> encodes both the individual chord energies and their interaction, while <math id="A2.SS9.SSS1.Px1.p20.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="I" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>I</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">I</annotation></semantics></math> is the normalized, non-negative rate function. Moreover, the minimal potential admits a semiclassical interpretation:</span></p>
<table id="A2.E14" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A2.E14.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="-\lim_{\kappa\to 0^{+}}\,\kappa\,\log Z_{\alpha}(D;x_{1},\dots,x_{2n})=\tfrac{1}{2}\,M_{D}^{\alpha}(x_{1},\dots,x_{2n})," display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo>−</mo><munder><mo lspace="0em" movablelimits="false" rspace="0.167em">lim</mo><mrow><mi>κ</mi><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><msup><mn>0</mn><mo>+</mo></msup></mrow></munder><mi>κ</mi><mi>log</mi><msub><mi>Z</mi><mi>α</mi></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>D</mi><mo>;</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>n</mi></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>=</mo><mstyle displaystyle="false"><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mn>2</mn></mfrac></mstyle><msubsup><mi>M</mi><mi>D</mi><mi>α</mi></msubsup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>n</mi></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">-\lim_{\kappa\to 0^{+}}\,\kappa\,\log Z_{\alpha}(D;x_{1},\dots,x_{2n})=\tfrac{1}{2}\,M_{D}^{\alpha}(x_{1},\dots,x_{2n}),</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(14)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A2.SS9.SSS1.Px1.p20.3" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.SS9.SSS1.Px1.p20.3.1" class="ltx_text">so that <math id="A2.SS9.SSS1.Px1.p20.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="U:=\tfrac{1}{2}M_{D}^{\alpha}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>U</mi><mo>:=</mo><mrow><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mn>2</mn></mfrac><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>M</mi><mi>D</mi><mi>α</mi></msubsup></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">U:=\tfrac{1}{2}M_{D}^{\alpha}</annotation></semantics></math> acts as a Hamilton–Jacobi potential for the system.</span></p>
</div>
<div id="A2.SS9.SSS1.Px1.p21" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A2.SS9.SSS1.Px1.p21.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.SS9.SSS1.Px1.p21.1.1" class="ltx_text">3. Deterministic limit of multiple chordal SLE</span></p>
</div>
<div id="A2.SS9.SSS1.Px1.p22" class="ltx_para">
<ul id="A2.I24" class="ltx_itemize">
<li id="A2.I24.i1" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">•</span> 
<div id="A2.I24.i1.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A2.I24.i1.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.I24.i1.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Large deviations and limit shape.</span> The laws of multichordal <math id="A2.I24.i1.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathrm{SLE}_{\kappa}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>SLE</mi><mi>κ</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathrm{SLE}_{\kappa}</annotation></semantics></math> satisfy a strong LDP with good rate function <math id="A2.I24.i1.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="I_{D}^{\alpha}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mi>I</mi><mi>D</mi><mi>α</mi></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">I_{D}^{\alpha}</annotation></semantics></math>. As <math id="A2.I24.i1.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\kappa\to 0^{+}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>κ</mi><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><msup><mn>0</mn><mo>+</mo></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\kappa\to 0^{+}</annotation></semantics></math>, the random multichords converge (in probability, in the Hausdorff topology) to the unique minimizer of <math id="A2.I24.i1.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="H_{D}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>H</mi><mi>D</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">H_{D}</annotation></semantics></math> in <math id="A2.I24.i1.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="X_{\alpha}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>X</mi><mi>α</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">X_{\alpha}</annotation></semantics></math>—a geodesic multichord.</p>
</div></li>
<li id="A2.I24.i2" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">•</span> 
<div id="A2.I24.i2.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A2.I24.i2.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.I24.i2.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Rational function description.</span> In the upper half-plane with marked points <math id="A2.I24.i2.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="x_{1}&lt;\dots&lt;x_{2n}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>x</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>&lt;</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">⋯</mi><mo>&lt;</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>n</mi></mrow></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">x_{1}&lt;\dots&lt;x_{2n}</annotation></semantics></math>, each minimizer/geodesic multichord is the <em id="A2.I24.i2.p1.1.2" class="ltx_emph ltx_font_italic">real locus of a real rational function</em> of degree <math id="A2.I24.i2.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="n+1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">n+1</annotation></semantics></math> with critical points <math id="A2.I24.i2.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\{x_{1},\dots,x_{2n}\}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>n</mi></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\{x_{1},\dots,x_{2n}\}</annotation></semantics></math>. This ensures uniqueness (one for each link pattern) and ties the limit to real enumerative geometry (Shapiro’s conjecture).</p>
</div></li>
<li id="A2.I24.i3" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">•</span> 
<div id="A2.I24.i3.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A2.I24.i3.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.I24.i3.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Deterministic dynamics and PDE.</span> Writing <math id="A2.I24.i3.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="U=\tfrac{1}{2}M_{D}^{\alpha}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>U</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mn>2</mn></mfrac><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>M</mi><mi>D</mi><mi>α</mi></msubsup></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">U=\tfrac{1}{2}M_{D}^{\alpha}</annotation></semantics></math>, the driving function <math id="A2.I24.i3.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="W_{t}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>W</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">W_{t}</annotation></semantics></math> of the minimizing chord solves</p>
<table id="A2.Ex271" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A2.Ex271.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\dot{W}_{t}=-\,\partial_{a_{j}}U(V_{1}(t),\dots,W_{t},\dots,V_{2n}(t)),\qquad\dot{V}_{i}(t)=\frac{2}{V_{i}(t)-W_{t}}," display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>W</mi><mo>˙</mo></mover><mi>t</mi></msub><mo rspace="0em">=</mo><mo lspace="0em">−</mo><msub><mo>∂</mo><msub><mi>a</mi><mi>j</mi></msub></msub><mi>U</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>V</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>W</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>V</mi><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>n</mi></mrow></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo rspace="2.167em">,</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>V</mi><mo>˙</mo></mover><mi>i</mi></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mn>2</mn><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>V</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>W</mi><mi>t</mi></msub></mrow></mfrac><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\dot{W}_{t}=-\,\partial_{a_{j}}U(V_{1}(t),\dots,W_{t},\dots,V_{2n}(t)),\qquad\dot{V}_{i}(t)=\frac{2}{V_{i}(t)-W_{t}},</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A2.I24.i3.p1.2" class="ltx_p">and <math id="A2.I24.i3.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="U" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>U</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">U</annotation></semantics></math> satisfies the system of quadratic first-order PDEs that arise as the <math id="A2.I24.i3.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="c\to-\infty" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>c</mi><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><mrow><mo>−</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">∞</mi></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">c\to-\infty</annotation></semantics></math> (semiclassical) limit of the level-two BPZ equations. These encode the deterministic “hydrodynamics” of the <math id="A2.I24.i3.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\kappa\to 0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>κ</mi><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\kappa\to 0</annotation></semantics></math> limit.</p>
</div></li>
</ul>
</div>
<div id="A2.SS9.SSS1.Px1.p23" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A2.SS9.SSS1.Px1.p23.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.SS9.SSS1.Px1.p23.1.1" class="ltx_text">In summary, the Loewner potential <math id="A2.SS9.SSS1.Px1.p23.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="H" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>H</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">H</annotation></semantics></math> is the global conformally covariant functional whose minimizers describe the deterministic shapes emerging in the small-<math id="A2.SS9.SSS1.Px1.p23.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\kappa" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>κ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\kappa</annotation></semantics></math> limit; the Loewner energy <math id="A2.SS9.SSS1.Px1.p23.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="I" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>I</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">I</annotation></semantics></math> is the corresponding non-negative rate function governing fluctuations around them.
∎</span></p>
</div>
</div>
<div id="A2.SS9.SSS1.Px1.p24" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent"><span class="ltx_inline-block"><svg id="A2.SS9.SSS1.Px1.p24.pic1" class="ltx_picture" height="147.27" overflow="visible" version="1.1" viewBox="0 0 429.64 147.27" width="429.64"><g style="--ltx-stroke-color:#000000;--ltx-fill-color:#000000;" fill="#000000" stroke="#000000" stroke-width="0.4pt" transform="translate(0,147.27) matrix(1 0 0 -1 0 0)"><g style="--ltx-fill-color:#4D4D4D;" fill="#4D4D4D" fill-opacity="1.0"><path style="stroke:none" d="M 0 4.63 L 0 142.64 C 0 145.19 2.07 147.27 4.63 147.27 L 425.01 147.27 C 427.56 147.27 429.64 145.19 429.64 142.64 L 429.64 4.63 C 429.64 2.07 427.56 0 425.01 0 L 4.63 0 C 2.07 0 0 2.07 0 4.63 Z"></path></g><g style="--ltx-fill-color:#F9F9F9;" fill="#F9F9F9" fill-opacity="1.0"><path style="stroke:none" d="M 0.69 4.63 L 0.69 128.4 L 428.94 128.4 L 428.94 4.63 C 428.94 2.45 427.18 0.69 425.01 0.69 L 4.63 0.69 C 2.45 0.69 0.69 2.45 0.69 4.63 Z"></path></g><g fill-opacity="1.0" transform="matrix(1.0 0.0 0.0 1.0 20.38 133.03)"><foreignObject style="--ltx-fo-width:24.44em;--ltx-fo-height:0.69em;--ltx-fo-depth:0em;font-size:10pt;" height="9.61" overflow="visible" transform="matrix(1 0 0 -1 0 9.61)" width="338.18"><span class="ltx_foreignobject_container"><span class="ltx_foreignobject_content">
<span id="A2.SS9.SSS1.Px1.p24.pic1.1" class="ltx_inline-block ltx_minipage ltx_align_bottom" style="width:24.44em;">
<span id="A2.SS9.SSS1.Px1.p24.pic1.1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.SS9.SSS1.Px1.p24.pic1.1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold" style="--ltx-fg-color:#FFFFFF;">Rubric</span></span>
</span></span></span></foreignObject></g><g fill-opacity="1.0" transform="matrix(1.0 0.0 0.0 1.0 20.38 14.66)"><foreignObject style="--ltx-fo-width:33.06em;--ltx-fo-height:7.37em;--ltx-fo-depth:0.16em;font-size:10pt;" height="104.09" overflow="visible" transform="matrix(1 0 0 -1 0 101.93)" width="457.46"><span class="ltx_foreignobject_container"><span class="ltx_foreignobject_content">
<span id="A2.SS9.SSS1.Px1.p24.pic1.2" class="ltx_inline-block ltx_minipage ltx_align_bottom" style="width:33.06em;">
<span id="A2.I25" class="ltx_enumerate">
<span id="A2.I25.i1" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">1.</span> 
<span id="A2.I25.i1.p1" class="ltx_para">
<span id="A2.I25.i1.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.I25.i1.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:80%;--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">Identify the concept and explain its context.</span></span>
</span></span>
<span id="A2.I25.i2" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">2.</span> 
<span id="A2.I25.i2.p1" class="ltx_para">
<span id="A2.I25.i2.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.I25.i2.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:80%;--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">Explain the relations between Loewner energy and potential.</span></span>
</span></span>
<span id="A2.I25.i3" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">3.</span> 
<span id="A2.I25.i3.p1" class="ltx_para">
<span id="A2.I25.i3.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.I25.i3.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:80%;--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">Explain the large deviation principle.</span></span>
</span></span>
</span>
<span id="A2.SS9.SSS1.Px1.p24.pic1.2.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.SS9.SSS1.Px1.p24.pic1.2.1.1" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:80%;--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">Each item is worth 1 point.</span></span>
</span></span></span></foreignObject></g></g></svg></span>
</div>
<div id="A2.SS9.SSS1.Px1.p25" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent"><span class="ltx_inline-block"><svg id="A2.SS9.SSS1.Px1.p25.pic1" class="ltx_picture" height="54.13" overflow="visible" version="1.1" viewBox="0 0 429.64 54.13" width="429.64"><g style="--ltx-stroke-color:#000000;--ltx-fill-color:#000000;" fill="#000000" stroke="#000000" stroke-width="0.4pt" transform="translate(0,54.13) matrix(1 0 0 -1 0 0)"><g style="--ltx-fill-color:#5A996B;" fill="#5A996B" fill-opacity="1.0"><path style="stroke:none" d="M 0 4.63 L 0 49.51 C 0 52.06 2.07 54.13 4.63 54.13 L 425.01 54.13 C 427.56 54.13 429.64 52.06 429.64 49.51 L 429.64 4.63 C 429.64 2.07 427.56 0 425.01 0 L 4.63 0 C 2.07 0 0 2.07 0 4.63 Z"></path></g><g style="--ltx-fill-color:#F6FFF9;" fill="#F6FFF9" fill-opacity="1.0"><path style="stroke:none" d="M 0.69 4.63 L 0.69 35.38 L 428.94 35.38 L 428.94 4.63 C 428.94 2.45 427.18 0.69 425.01 0.69 L 4.63 0.69 C 2.45 0.69 0.69 2.45 0.69 4.63 Z"></path></g><g fill-opacity="1.0" transform="matrix(1.0 0.0 0.0 1.0 20.38 40.01)"><foreignObject style="--ltx-fo-width:24.44em;--ltx-fo-height:0.69em;--ltx-fo-depth:0em;font-size:10pt;" height="9.49" overflow="visible" transform="matrix(1 0 0 -1 0 9.49)" width="338.18"><span class="ltx_foreignobject_container"><span class="ltx_foreignobject_content">
