</section>
</section>
<section id="A2.SS9.SSS2" class="ltx_subsubsection">
<h4 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsubsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsubsection">(b) </span>Self-directed learning</h4>

<section id="A2.SS9.SSS2.Px1" class="ltx_paragraph">
<h5 class="ltx_title ltx_title_paragraph" style="--ltx-fg-color:#FF0000;">Problem 9b1 </h5>

<div id="A2.SS9.SSS2.Px1.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A2.SS9.SSS2.Px1.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.SS9.SSS2.Px1.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text"></span>
<br class="ltx_break" style="--ltx-break-space:-10.0pt;"></p>
</div>
<div id="A2.SS9.SSS2.Px1.p2" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent"><span class="ltx_inline-block"><svg id="A2.SS9.SSS2.Px1.p2.pic1" class="ltx_picture" height="249.29" overflow="visible" version="1.1" viewBox="0 0 429.64 249.29" width="429.64"><g style="--ltx-stroke-color:#000000;--ltx-fill-color:#000000;" fill="#000000" stroke="#000000" stroke-width="0.4pt" transform="translate(0,249.29) matrix(1 0 0 -1 0 0)"><g style="--ltx-fill-color:#3D6666;" fill="#3D6666" fill-opacity="1.0"><path style="stroke:none" d="M 0 4.63 L 0 244.67 C 0 247.22 2.07 249.29 4.63 249.29 L 425.01 249.29 C 427.56 249.29 429.64 247.22 429.64 244.67 L 429.64 4.63 C 429.64 2.07 427.56 0 425.01 0 L 4.63 0 C 2.07 0 0 2.07 0 4.63 Z"></path></g><g style="--ltx-fill-color:#F9F9F9;" fill="#F9F9F9" fill-opacity="1.0"><path style="stroke:none" d="M 0.69 4.63 L 0.69 230.43 L 428.94 230.43 L 428.94 4.63 C 428.94 2.45 427.18 0.69 425.01 0.69 L 4.63 0.69 C 2.45 0.69 0.69 2.45 0.69 4.63 Z"></path></g><g fill-opacity="1.0" transform="matrix(1.0 0.0 0.0 1.0 20.38 235.06)"><foreignObject style="--ltx-fo-width:24.44em;--ltx-fo-height:0.69em;--ltx-fo-depth:0em;font-size:10pt;" height="9.61" overflow="visible" transform="matrix(1 0 0 -1 0 9.61)" width="338.18"><span class="ltx_foreignobject_container"><span class="ltx_foreignobject_content">
<span id="A2.SS9.SSS2.Px1.p2.pic1.1" class="ltx_inline-block ltx_minipage ltx_align_bottom" style="width:24.44em;">
<span id="A2.SS9.SSS2.Px1.p2.pic1.1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.SS9.SSS2.Px1.p2.pic1.1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold" style="--ltx-fg-color:#FFFFFF;">Problem</span></span>
</span></span></span></foreignObject></g><g fill-opacity="1.0" transform="matrix(1.0 0.0 0.0 1.0 20.38 14.66)"><foreignObject style="--ltx-fo-width:32.01em;--ltx-fo-height:14.74em;--ltx-fo-depth:0.16em;font-size:10pt;" height="206.12" overflow="visible" transform="matrix(1 0 0 -1 0 203.96)" width="442.93"><span class="ltx_foreignobject_container"><span class="ltx_foreignobject_content">
<span id="A2.SS9.SSS2.Px1.p2.pic1.2" class="ltx_inline-block ltx_minipage ltx_align_bottom" style="width:32.01em;">
<span id="A2.SS9.SSS2.Px1.p2.pic1.2.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.SS9.SSS2.Px1.p2.pic1.2.1.1" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:80%;--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">You are reading <a href="https://arxiv.org/abs/2505.16093" title="" class="ltx_ref ltx_href">Multiple chordal SLE(<math class="ltx_Math" alttext="\kappa" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">κ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\kappa</annotation></semantics></math>) and quantum Calogero-Moser system</a> <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citep">[<a href="#bib.bib16" title="" class="ltx_ref">Zhang, 2025</a>]</cite> and encounter the following concept:</span></span>
<span id="A2.SS9.SSS2.Px1.p2.pic1.2.2" class="ltx_quote">
<span id="A2.SS9.SSS2.Px1.p2.pic1.2.2.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.SS9.SSS2.Px1.p2.pic1.2.2.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold" style="font-size:80%;--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">Local chordal multiple SLE systems</span></span>
</span>
<span id="A2.I32" class="ltx_enumerate">
<span id="A2.I32.i1" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">1.</span> 
<span id="A2.I32.i1.p1" class="ltx_para">
<span id="A2.I32.i1.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.I32.i1.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:80%;--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">Please generalize the concept to the multiple radial case.</span></span>
</span></span>
<span id="A2.I32.i2" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">2.</span> 
<span id="A2.I32.i2.p1" class="ltx_para">
<span id="A2.I32.i2.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.I32.i2.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:80%;--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">Please define the compatible family of measures for multiple radial SLE systems.</span></span>
</span></span>
</span><span class="ltx_inline-block"><svg id="A2.SS9.SSS2.Px1.p2.pic1.pic1" class="ltx_picture" color="#FF0000" height="18.24" overflow="visible" style="vertical-align:-4.1px" version="1.1" viewBox="0 0 18.24 18.24" width="18.24"><g style="--ltx-stroke-color:#FF0000;--ltx-fill-color:#FF0000;" fill="#FF0000" stroke="#FF0000" stroke-width="1.8pt" transform="translate(0,18.24) matrix(1 0 0 -1 0 0) translate(1.25,0) translate(0,1.25)"><path style="fill:none" d="M 0 0 L 15.75 15.75 M 0 15.75 L 15.75 0"></path></g></svg></span>
<span id="A2.SS9.SSS2.Px1.p2.pic1.2.3" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.SS9.SSS2.Px1.p2.pic1.2.3.1" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:80%;--ltx-fg-color:#FF0000;">GPT-5 thinking failed</span></span>
<span id="A2.SS9.SSS2.Px1.p2.pic1.2.4" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.SS9.SSS2.Px1.p2.pic1.2.4.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic" style="font-size:80%;--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">Proposed by Jiaxin Zhang</span></span>
</span></span></span></foreignObject></g></g></svg></span>
</div>
<div id="A2.SS9.SSS2.Px1.1" class="ltx_proof">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_font_italic ltx_title_proof"><span id="A2.SS9.SSS2.Px1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Response of GPT-5-thinking</span>.</h6>
<div id="A2.SS9.SSS2.Px1.p3" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A2.SS9.SSS2.Px1.p3.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.SS9.SSS2.Px1.p3.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Can you generalize the concept to multiple radial case<span id="A2.SS9.SSS2.Px1.p3.1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_medium">
Setup.
Fix <math id="A2.SS9.SSS2.Px1.p3.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\kappa&gt;0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>κ</mi><mo>&gt;</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\kappa&gt;0</annotation></semantics></math>. In the unit disk <math id="A2.SS9.SSS2.Px1.p3.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbb{D}=\{z:|z|&lt;1\}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>𝔻</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mi>z</mi><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mi>z</mi><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow><mo>&lt;</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbb{D}=\{z:|z|&lt;1\}</annotation></semantics></math>, mark <math id="A2.SS9.SSS2.Px1.p3.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="n\geq 1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>≥</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">n\geq 1</annotation></semantics></math> boundary points
<math id="A2.SS9.SSS2.Px1.p3.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="X=(x_{1},\dots,x_{n})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>X</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>n</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">X=(x_{1},\dots,x_{n})</annotation></semantics></math> with <math id="A2.SS9.SSS2.Px1.p3.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="x_{j}=\mathrm{e}^{i\theta_{j}}\in\mathbb{T}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>j</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><msup><mi mathvariant="normal">e</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>θ</mi><mi>j</mi></msub></mrow></msup><mo>∈</mo><mi>𝕋</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">x_{j}=\mathrm{e}^{i\theta_{j}}\in\mathbb{T}</annotation></semantics></math> (listed in counterclockwise
order) and a target point at the origin <math id="A2.SS9.SSS2.Px1.p3.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mn>0</mn><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">0</annotation></semantics></math>.
Write <math id="A2.SS9.SSS2.Px1.p3.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Theta=(\theta_{1},\dots,\theta_{n})\in\mathbb{R}^{n}/2\pi\mathbb{Z}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Θ</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>θ</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>θ</mi><mi>n</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mrow><msup><mi>ℝ</mi><mi>n</mi></msup><mo>/</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>π</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>ℤ</mi></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Theta=(\theta_{1},\dots,\theta_{n})\in\mathbb{R}^{n}/2\pi\mathbb{Z}</annotation></semantics></math> for the angle
coordinates, defined modulo a common rotation.</span></span></p>
</div>
<div id="A2.SS9.SSS2.Px1.p4" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A2.SS9.SSS2.Px1.p4.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.SS9.SSS2.Px1.p4.1.1" class="ltx_text">Define the radial Loewner vector field acting on a boundary angle <math id="A2.SS9.SSS2.Px1.p4.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\phi" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>ϕ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\phi</annotation></semantics></math> from a
driving angle <math id="A2.SS9.SSS2.Px1.p4.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\vartheta" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>ϑ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\vartheta</annotation></semantics></math> by</span></p>
<table id="A2.Ex284" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A2.Ex284.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="V^{\mathrm{rad}}(\phi\mid\vartheta)\;:=\;2\,\cot\!\frac{\phi-\vartheta}{2}\,." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><msup><mi>V</mi><mi>rad</mi></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>ϕ</mi><mo fence="true" lspace="0em" rspace="0em">∣</mo><mi>ϑ</mi><mo rspace="0.280em" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>:=</mo><mrow><mn> 2</mn><mo lspace="0.337em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mi>cot</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mfrac><mrow><mi>ϕ</mi><mo>−</mo><mi>ϑ</mi></mrow><mn>2</mn></mfrac></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0.170em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">V^{\mathrm{rad}}(\phi\mid\vartheta)\;:=\;2\,\cot\!\frac{\phi-\vartheta}{2}\,.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
<div id="A2.SS9.SSS2.Px1.p5" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A2.SS9.SSS2.Px1.p5.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.SS9.SSS2.Px1.p5.1.1" class="ltx_text">Radial multiple partition functions.
Let <math id="A2.SS9.SSS2.Px1.p5.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="h=\dfrac{6-\kappa}{2\kappa}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>h</mi><mo>=</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><mn>6</mn><mo>−</mo><mi>κ</mi></mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>κ</mi></mrow></mfrac></mstyle></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">h=\dfrac{6-\kappa}{2\kappa}</annotation></semantics></math>.
A <em id="A2.SS9.SSS2.Px1.p5.1.1.1" class="ltx_emph ltx_font_italic">radial <math id="A2.SS9.SSS2.Px1.p5.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="n" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>n</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">n</annotation></semantics></math>-point partition function</em> is a positive <math id="A2.SS9.SSS2.Px1.p5.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="C^{2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi>C</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">C^{2}</annotation></semantics></math> function
<math id="A2.SS9.SSS2.Px1.p5.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="Z=Z(\Theta)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>Z</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>Z</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">Θ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">Z=Z(\Theta)</annotation></semantics></math> on the configuration space (modulo global rotation) such that:</span></p>
</div>
<div id="A2.SS9.SSS2.Px1.p6" class="ltx_para">
<ul id="A2.I33" class="ltx_itemize">
<li id="A2.I33.ix1" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">(Cov)</span> 
<div id="A2.I33.ix1.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A2.I33.ix1.p1.1" class="ltx_p">(<em id="A2.I33.ix1.p1.1.1" class="ltx_emph ltx_font_italic">Rotation covariance</em>) <math id="A2.I33.ix1.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="Z" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>Z</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">Z</annotation></semantics></math> is invariant under
<math id="A2.I33.ix1.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\theta_{j}\mapsto\theta_{j}+\alpha" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>θ</mi><mi>j</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">↦</mo><mrow><msub><mi>θ</mi><mi>j</mi></msub><mo>+</mo><mi>α</mi></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\theta_{j}\mapsto\theta_{j}+\alpha</annotation></semantics></math> for all <math id="A2.I33.ix1.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="j" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>j</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">j</annotation></semantics></math> and all <math id="A2.I33.ix1.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\alpha\in\mathbb{R}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>α</mi><mo>∈</mo><mi>ℝ</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\alpha\in\mathbb{R}</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>
</div></li>
<li id="A2.I33.ix2" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">(BPZ)</span> 
<div id="A2.I33.ix2.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A2.I33.ix2.p1.1" class="ltx_p">(<em id="A2.I33.ix2.p1.1.1" class="ltx_emph ltx_font_italic">Radial null-state / Ward system</em>)
For each <math id="A2.I33.ix2.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="i=1,\dots,n" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>n</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">i=1,\dots,n</annotation></semantics></math>,</p>
<table id="A2.E15" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A2.E15.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\Bigg[\frac{\kappa}{2}\,\partial_{\theta_{i}}^{2}+\sum_{j\neq i}V^{\mathrm{rad}}(\theta_{j}\mid\theta_{i})\,\partial_{\theta_{j}}+2h\sum_{j\neq i}\partial_{\theta_{j}}V^{\mathrm{rad}}(\theta_{j}\mid\theta_{i})\Bigg]Z\;=\;0." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mo maxsize="2.600em" minsize="2.600em">[</mo><mfrac><mi>κ</mi><mn>2</mn></mfrac><msubsup><mo>∂</mo><msub><mi>θ</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mn>2</mn></msubsup><mo rspace="0.055em">+</mo><munder><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>j</mi><mo>≠</mo><mi>i</mi></mrow></munder><msup><mi>V</mi><mi>rad</mi></msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>θ</mi><mi>j</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.167em">∣</mo><msub><mi>θ</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><msub><mo>∂</mo><msub><mi>θ</mi><mi>j</mi></msub></msub><mo>+</mo><mn>2</mn><mi>h</mi><munder><mo movablelimits="false" rspace="0em">∑</mo><mrow><mi>j</mi><mo>≠</mo><mi>i</mi></mrow></munder><msub><mo>∂</mo><msub><mi>θ</mi><mi>j</mi></msub></msub><msup><mi>V</mi><mi>rad</mi></msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>θ</mi><mi>j</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.167em">∣</mo><msub><mi>θ</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo maxsize="2.600em" minsize="2.600em">]</mo></mrow><mi>Z</mi><mo lspace="0.558em">=</mo><mn> 0</mn><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Bigg[\frac{\kappa}{2}\,\partial_{\theta_{i}}^{2}+\sum_{j\neq i}V^{\mathrm{rad}}(\theta_{j}\mid\theta_{i})\,\partial_{\theta_{j}}+2h\sum_{j\neq i}\partial_{\theta_{j}}V^{\mathrm{rad}}(\theta_{j}\mid\theta_{i})\Bigg]Z\;=\;0.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(15)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A2.I33.ix2.p1.2" class="ltx_p">Equivalently, in half–angle form,</p>
<table id="A2.Ex285" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A2.Ex285.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\frac{\kappa}{2}\,\partial_{\theta_{i}}^{2}Z+\sum_{j\neq i}\!\cot\!\frac{\theta_{j}-\theta_{i}}{2}\,\partial_{\theta_{j}}Z+\frac{6-\kappa}{\kappa}\sum_{j\neq i}\!\csc^{2}\!\frac{\theta_{j}-\theta_{i}}{2}\,Z=0." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mrow><mfrac><mi>κ</mi><mn>2</mn></mfrac><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><msubsup><mo>∂</mo><msub><mi>θ</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mn>2</mn></msubsup><mi>Z</mi></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.055em">+</mo><mrow><munder><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>j</mi><mo>≠</mo><mi>i</mi></mrow></munder><mrow><mrow><mi>cot</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mfrac><mrow><msub><mi>θ</mi><mi>j</mi></msub><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>θ</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></mrow><mn>2</mn></mfrac></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><msub><mo>∂</mo><msub><mi>θ</mi><mi>j</mi></msub></msub><mi>Z</mi></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mfrac><mrow><mn>6</mn><mo>−</mo><mi>κ</mi></mrow><mi>κ</mi></mfrac><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><munder><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>j</mi><mo>≠</mo><mi>i</mi></mrow></munder><mrow><msup><mi>csc</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><mrow><mfrac><mrow><msub><mi>θ</mi><mi>j</mi></msub><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>θ</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></mrow><mn>2</mn></mfrac><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>Z</mi></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\frac{\kappa}{2}\,\partial_{\theta_{i}}^{2}Z+\sum_{j\neq i}\!\cot\!\frac{\theta_{j}-\theta_{i}}{2}\,\partial_{\theta_{j}}Z+\frac{6-\kappa}{\kappa}\sum_{j\neq i}\!\csc^{2}\!\frac{\theta_{j}-\theta_{i}}{2}\,Z=0.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div></li>
<li id="A2.I33.ix3" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">(Fusion)</span> 
<div id="A2.I33.ix3.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A2.I33.ix3.p1.1" class="ltx_p">(<em id="A2.I33.ix3.p1.1.1" class="ltx_emph ltx_font_italic">Boundary OPE asymptotics</em>)
When <math id="A2.I33.ix3.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\theta_{i+1}\downarrow\theta_{i}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>θ</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">↓</mo><msub><mi>θ</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\theta_{i+1}\downarrow\theta_{i}</annotation></semantics></math>, one has</p>
<table id="A2.Ex286" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A2.Ex286.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="Z(\Theta)\;\asymp\;(\theta_{i+1}-\theta_{i})^{\frac{6-\kappa}{2\kappa}}\;Z(\Theta^{(i,i+1)})," display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>Z</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">Θ</mi><mo rspace="0.280em" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.558em">≍</mo><mrow><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>θ</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>θ</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mfrac><mrow><mn>6</mn><mo>−</mo><mi>κ</mi></mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>κ</mi></mrow></mfrac></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>Z</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi mathvariant="normal">Θ</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>i</mi><mo>,</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">Z(\Theta)\;\asymp\;(\theta_{i+1}-\theta_{i})^{\frac{6-\kappa}{2\kappa}}\;Z(\Theta^{(i,i+1)}),</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A2.I33.ix3.p1.2" class="ltx_p">where <math id="A2.I33.ix3.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Theta^{(i,i+1)}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi mathvariant="normal">Θ</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>i</mi><mo>,</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Theta^{(i,i+1)}</annotation></semantics></math> is the configuration with the pair <math id="A2.I33.ix3.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(i,i+1)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>i</mi><mo>,</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(i,i+1)</annotation></semantics></math> fused.</p>
</div></li>
</ul>
</div>
<div id="A2.SS9.SSS2.Px1.p7" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A2.SS9.SSS2.Px1.p7.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.SS9.SSS2.Px1.p7.1.1" class="ltx_text">Definition (Local radial multiple SLE<math id="A2.SS9.SSS2.Px1.p7.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(\kappa)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>κ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(\kappa)</annotation></semantics></math>).
A <em id="A2.SS9.SSS2.Px1.p7.1.1.1" class="ltx_emph ltx_font_italic">local radial multiple SLE<math id="A2.SS9.SSS2.Px1.p7.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(\kappa)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>κ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(\kappa)</annotation></semantics></math> system with partition function <math id="A2.SS9.SSS2.Px1.p7.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="Z" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>Z</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">Z</annotation></semantics></math></em>
is a family of random growing hulls in <math id="A2.SS9.SSS2.Px1.p7.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbb{D}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>𝔻</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbb{D}</annotation></semantics></math> described as follows.</span></p>
</div>
<div id="A2.SS9.SSS2.Px1.p8" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A2.SS9.SSS2.Px1.p8.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.SS9.SSS2.Px1.p8.1.1" class="ltx_text">On any time interval during which the <em id="A2.SS9.SSS2.Px1.p8.1.1.1" class="ltx_emph ltx_font_italic">active index</em> is <math id="A2.SS9.SSS2.Px1.p8.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="i\in\{1,\dots,n\}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>n</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">i\in\{1,\dots,n\}</annotation></semantics></math>,
we run the radial Loewner equation with capacity parametrization <math id="A2.SS9.SSS2.Px1.p8.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="g_{t}^{\prime}(0)=\mathrm{e}^{t}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msubsup><mi>g</mi><mi>t</mi><mo>′</mo></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>0</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><msup><mi>e</mi><mi>t</mi></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">g_{t}^{\prime}(0)=\mathrm{e}^{t}</annotation></semantics></math>:</span></p>
<table id="A2.E16" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A2.E16.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\partial_{t}g_{t}(z)=-\,g_{t}(z)\,\frac{\mathrm{e}^{iW_{t}}+g_{t}(z)}{\mathrm{e}^{iW_{t}}-g_{t}(z)},\qquad g_{0}(z)=z," display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mrow><msub><mo>∂</mo><mi>t</mi></msub><mrow><msub><mi>g</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>z</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><msub><mi>g</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>z</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mfrac><mrow><msup><mi>e</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>W</mi><mi>t</mi></msub></mrow></msup><mo>+</mo><mrow><msub><mi>g</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>z</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mrow><msup><mi>e</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>W</mi><mi>t</mi></msub></mrow></msup><mo>−</mo><mrow><msub><mi>g</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>z</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mfrac></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="2.167em">,</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>g</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>z</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mi>z</mi></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\partial_{t}g_{t}(z)=-\,g_{t}(z)\,\frac{\mathrm{e}^{iW_{t}}+g_{t}(z)}{\mathrm{e}^{iW_{t}}-g_{t}(z)},\qquad g_{0}(z)=z,</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(16)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A2.SS9.SSS2.Px1.p8.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.SS9.SSS2.Px1.p8.2.1" class="ltx_text">driven by an angle process <math id="A2.SS9.SSS2.Px1.p8.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="W_{t}\in\mathbb{R}/2\pi\mathbb{Z}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>W</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>ℝ</mi><mo>/</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>π</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>ℤ</mi></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">W_{t}\in\mathbb{R}/2\pi\mathbb{Z}</annotation></semantics></math> solving</span></p>
<table id="A2.E17" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A2.E17.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathrm{d}W_{t}=\sqrt{\kappa}\,\mathrm{d}B_{t}+\kappa\,\partial_{\theta_{i}}\log Z(\Theta_{t})\,\mathrm{d}t," display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>W</mi><mi>t</mi></msub></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><msqrt><mi>κ</mi></msqrt><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>d</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>B</mi><mi>t</mi></msub></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi>κ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><msub><mo rspace="0.167em">∂</mo><msub><mi>θ</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></msub><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>Z</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Θ</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>d</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathrm{d}W_{t}=\sqrt{\kappa}\,\mathrm{d}B_{t}+\kappa\,\partial_{\theta_{i}}\log Z(\Theta_{t})\,\mathrm{d}t,</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(17)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A2.SS9.SSS2.Px1.p8.3" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.SS9.SSS2.Px1.p8.3.1" class="ltx_text">where <math id="A2.SS9.SSS2.Px1.p8.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="B_{t}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>B</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">B_{t}</annotation></semantics></math> is a standard one–dimensional Brownian motion. The non–active
boundary angles evolve deterministically under the Loewner flow:</span></p>
<table id="A2.E18" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A2.E18.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathrm{d}\Theta_{t}^{\,j}=V^{\mathrm{rad}}\!\big(\Theta_{t}^{\,j}\,\big|\,W_{t}\big)\,\mathrm{d}t,\qquad j\neq i," display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi mathvariant="normal">Θ</mi><mi>t</mi><mi>j</mi></msubsup></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><msup><mi>V</mi><mi>rad</mi></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">(</mo><msubsup><mi mathvariant="normal">Θ</mi><mi>t</mi><mi>j</mi></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" mathsize="1.200em" rspace="0.170em">|</mo><msub><mi>W</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>d</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="2.167em">,</mo><mrow><mi>j</mi><mo>≠</mo><mi>i</mi></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathrm{d}\Theta_{t}^{\,j}=V^{\mathrm{rad}}\!\big(\Theta_{t}^{\,j}\,\big|\,W_{t}\big)\,\mathrm{d}t,\qquad j\neq i,</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(18)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A2.SS9.SSS2.Px1.p8.4" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.SS9.SSS2.Px1.p8.4.1" class="ltx_text">and the active label tracks the tip:
<math id="A2.SS9.SSS2.Px1.p8.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Theta_{t}^{\,i}=W_{t}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msubsup><mi mathvariant="normal">Θ</mi><mi>t</mi><mi>i</mi></msubsup><mo>=</mo><msub><mi>W</mi><mi>t</mi></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Theta_{t}^{\,i}=W_{t}</annotation></semantics></math>.
(Equivalently, <math id="A2.SS9.SSS2.Px1.p8.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Theta_{t}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Θ</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Theta_{t}</annotation></semantics></math> solves (<a href="#A2.E18" title="Equation 18 ‣ Response of GPT-5-thinking. ‣ Problem 9b1 ‣ (b) Self-directed learning ‣ 9 Learning New Knowledge ‣ Appendix B Model Responses and Evaluations ‣ GAUSS: Benchmarking Structured Mathematical Skills for Large Language Models" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">18</span></a>) for all <math id="A2.SS9.SSS2.Px1.p8.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="j" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>j</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">j</annotation></semantics></math>
with the convention <math id="A2.SS9.SSS2.Px1.p8.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Theta_{t}^{\,i}=W_{t}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msubsup><mi mathvariant="normal">Θ</mi><mi>t</mi><mi>i</mi></msubsup><mo>=</mo><msub><mi>W</mi><mi>t</mi></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Theta_{t}^{\,i}=W_{t}</annotation></semantics></math>.)</span></p>
</div>
<div id="A2.SS9.SSS2.Px1.p9" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A2.SS9.SSS2.Px1.p9.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.SS9.SSS2.Px1.p9.1.1" class="ltx_text">The <em id="A2.SS9.SSS2.Px1.p9.1.1.1" class="ltx_emph ltx_font_italic">locality</em> means we only grow one tip at a time; the <em id="A2.SS9.SSS2.Px1.p9.1.1.2" class="ltx_emph ltx_font_italic">multiple</em> system
is obtained by concatenating such infinitesimal steps while allowing the active
index to change. The defining requirement is the <em id="A2.SS9.SSS2.Px1.p9.1.1.3" class="ltx_emph ltx_font_italic">commutation</em> (or
<em id="A2.SS9.SSS2.Px1.p9.1.1.4" class="ltx_emph ltx_font_italic">consistency</em>) of different growth orders: the laws obtained by first
growing near <math id="A2.SS9.SSS2.Px1.p9.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="x_{i}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">x_{i}</annotation></semantics></math> for a small time and then near <math id="A2.SS9.SSS2.Px1.p9.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="x_{j}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>j</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">x_{j}</annotation></semantics></math>, and vice versa, agree
up to a deterministic time–change. This commutation is equivalent to the BPZ
system (<a href="#A2.E15" title="Equation 15 ‣ item (BPZ) ‣ Response of GPT-5-thinking. ‣ Problem 9b1 ‣ (b) Self-directed learning ‣ 9 Learning New Knowledge ‣ Appendix B Model Responses and Evaluations ‣ GAUSS: Benchmarking Structured Mathematical Skills for Large Language Models" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">15</span></a>) for <math id="A2.SS9.SSS2.Px1.p9.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="Z" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>Z</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">Z</annotation></semantics></math>, and conversely (<a href="#A2.E15" title="Equation 15 ‣ item (BPZ) ‣ Response of GPT-5-thinking. ‣ Problem 9b1 ‣ (b) Self-directed learning ‣ 9 Learning New Knowledge ‣ Appendix B Model Responses and Evaluations ‣ GAUSS: Benchmarking Structured Mathematical Skills for Large Language Models" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">15</span></a>)
ensures the Markovian concatenations commute.</span></p>
</div>
<div id="A2.SS9.SSS2.Px1.p10" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A2.SS9.SSS2.Px1.p10.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.SS9.SSS2.Px1.p10.1.1" class="ltx_text">Conformal covariance and general domains.
Let <math id="A2.SS9.SSS2.Px1.p10.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="D" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>D</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">D</annotation></semantics></math> be simply connected with target <math id="A2.SS9.SSS2.Px1.p10.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="z_{\ast}\in D" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>z</mi><mo>∗</mo></msub><mo>∈</mo><mi>D</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">z_{\ast}\in D</annotation></semantics></math> and boundary marks
<math id="A2.SS9.SSS2.Px1.p10.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="x_{1},\dots,x_{n}\in\partial D" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>x</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>,</mo><mrow><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>n</mi></msub><mo rspace="0.111em">∈</mo><mrow><mo>∂</mo><mi>D</mi></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">x_{1},\dots,x_{n}\in\partial D</annotation></semantics></math>. Fix a conformal map
<math id="A2.SS9.SSS2.Px1.p10.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\psi:D\to\mathbb{D}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>ψ</mi><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mrow><mi>D</mi><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><mi>𝔻</mi></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\psi:D\to\mathbb{D}</annotation></semantics></math> with <math id="A2.SS9.SSS2.Px1.p10.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\psi(z_{\ast})=0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>ψ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>z</mi><mo>∗</mo></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\psi(z_{\ast})=0</annotation></semantics></math>.
Transport the construction above via <math id="A2.SS9.SSS2.Px1.p10.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\psi" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>ψ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\psi</annotation></semantics></math>; the capacity time is the radial
capacity at <math id="A2.SS9.SSS2.Px1.p10.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="z_{\ast}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>z</mi><mo>∗</mo></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">z_{\ast}</annotation></semantics></math>, i.e. the normalization <math id="A2.SS9.SSS2.Px1.p10.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="g_{t}(z_{\ast})=0,\ g_{t}^{\prime}(z_{\ast})=\mathrm{e}^{t}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>g</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>z</mi><mo>∗</mo></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><mo rspace="0.667em">,</mo><mrow><mrow><msubsup><mi>g</mi><mi>t</mi><mo>′</mo></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>z</mi><mo>∗</mo></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><msup><mi>e</mi><mi>t</mi></msup></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">g_{t}(z_{\ast})=0,\ g_{t}^{\prime}(z_{\ast})=\mathrm{e}^{t}</annotation></semantics></math>.
Under postcomposition by a disk automorphism fixing <math id="A2.SS9.SSS2.Px1.p10.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mn>0</mn><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">0</annotation></semantics></math> (a rotation), <math id="A2.SS9.SSS2.Px1.p10.m10" class="ltx_Math" alttext="Z" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>Z</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">Z</annotation></semantics></math> is
invariant; under a general <math id="A2.SS9.SSS2.Px1.p10.m11" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\psi" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>ψ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\psi</annotation></semantics></math> the boundary tensorial factor is absorbed in the
definition of <math id="A2.SS9.SSS2.Px1.p10.m12" class="ltx_Math" alttext="Z_{D}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>Z</mi><mi>D</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">Z_{D}</annotation></semantics></math> by the usual weight <math id="A2.SS9.SSS2.Px1.p10.m13" class="ltx_Math" alttext="h" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>h</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">h</annotation></semantics></math> at boundary insertions.</span></p>
</div>
<div id="A2.SS9.SSS2.Px1.p11" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A2.SS9.SSS2.Px1.p11.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.SS9.SSS2.Px1.p11.1.1" class="ltx_text">Remarks.</span></p>
<ul id="A2.I34" class="ltx_itemize">
<li id="A2.I34.i1" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">•</span> 
<div id="A2.I34.i1.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A2.I34.i1.p1.1" class="ltx_p">For <math id="A2.I34.i1.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="n=1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">n=1</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="A2.I34.i1.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="Z\equiv\text{const}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>Z</mi><mo>≡</mo><mtext>const</mtext></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">Z\equiv\text{const}</annotation></semantics></math> the SDE (<a href="#A2.E17" title="Equation 17 ‣ Response of GPT-5-thinking. ‣ Problem 9b1 ‣ (b) Self-directed learning ‣ 9 Learning New Knowledge ‣ Appendix B Model Responses and Evaluations ‣ GAUSS: Benchmarking Structured Mathematical Skills for Large Language Models" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">17</span></a>) reduces to
<math id="A2.I34.i1.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="dW_{t}=\sqrt{\kappa}\,dB_{t}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>W</mi><mi>t</mi></msub></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><msqrt><mi>κ</mi></msqrt><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>d</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>B</mi><mi>t</mi></msub></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">dW_{t}=\sqrt{\kappa}\,dB_{t}</annotation></semantics></math>, and we recover the standard radial SLE<math id="A2.I34.i1.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(\kappa)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>κ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(\kappa)</annotation></semantics></math>
from <math id="A2.I34.i1.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="x_{1}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>x</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">x_{1}</annotation></semantics></math> to <math id="A2.I34.i1.p1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mn>0</mn><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">0</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>
</div></li>
<li id="A2.I34.i2" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">•</span> 
<div id="A2.I34.i2.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A2.I34.i2.p1.1" class="ltx_p">The operators in (<a href="#A2.E15" title="Equation 15 ‣ item (BPZ) ‣ Response of GPT-5-thinking. ‣ Problem 9b1 ‣ (b) Self-directed learning ‣ 9 Learning New Knowledge ‣ Appendix B Model Responses and Evaluations ‣ GAUSS: Benchmarking Structured Mathematical Skills for Large Language Models" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">15</span></a>) are the radial counterparts of the
chordal ones (replace <math id="A2.I34.i2.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\frac{2}{x_{j}-x_{i}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mfrac><mn>2</mn><mrow><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>j</mi></msub><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></mrow></mfrac><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\frac{2}{x_{j}-x_{i}}</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="A2.I34.i2.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\frac{2}{(x_{j}-x_{i})^{2}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mfrac><mn>2</mn><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>j</mi></msub><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup></mfrac><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\frac{2}{(x_{j}-x_{i})^{2}}</annotation></semantics></math> by
<math id="A2.I34.i2.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="V^{\mathrm{rad}}(\theta_{j}\mid\theta_{i})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msup><mi>V</mi><mi>rad</mi></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>θ</mi><mi>j</mi></msub><mo fence="true" lspace="0em" rspace="0em">∣</mo><msub><mi>θ</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">V^{\mathrm{rad}}(\theta_{j}\mid\theta_{i})</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="A2.I34.i2.p1.m4" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="-\partial_{\theta_{j}}V^{\mathrm{rad}}(\theta_{j}\mid\theta_{i})=\csc^{2}\frac{\theta_{j}-\theta_{i}}{2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo rspace="0.055em">−</mo><msub><mo>∂</mo><msub><mi>θ</mi><mi>j</mi></msub></msub><msup><mi>V</mi><mi>rad</mi></msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>θ</mi><mi>j</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.167em">∣</mo><msub><mi>θ</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>=</mo><msup><mi>csc</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mfrac><mrow><msub><mi>θ</mi><mi>j</mi></msub><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>θ</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></mrow><mn>2</mn></mfrac></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">-\partial_{\theta_{j}}V^{\mathrm{rad}}(\theta_{j}\mid\theta_{i})=\csc^{2}\frac{\theta_{j}-\theta_{i}}{2}</annotation></semantics></math>).</p>
</div></li>
<li id="A2.I34.i3" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">•</span> 
<div id="A2.I34.i3.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A2.I34.i3.p1.1" class="ltx_p">For <math id="A2.I34.i3.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\kappa\leq 4" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>κ</mi><mo>≤</mo><mn>4</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\kappa\leq 4</annotation></semantics></math>, the local system can be <em id="A2.I34.i3.p1.1.1" class="ltx_emph ltx_font_italic">globalized</em> into <math id="A2.I34.i3.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="n" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>n</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">n</annotation></semantics></math> simple,
pairwise disjoint curves aimed at <math id="A2.I34.i3.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mn>0</mn><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">0</annotation></semantics></math>; for <math id="A2.I34.i3.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\kappa&gt;4" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>κ</mi><mo>&gt;</mo><mn>4</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\kappa&gt;4</annotation></semantics></math> one obtains non–simple
curves with the usual SLE self–touching features. As in the chordal case,
distinct pure solutions <math id="A2.I34.i3.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="Z" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>Z</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">Z</annotation></semantics></math> correspond to different topological connectivities.</p>
</div></li>
<li id="A2.I34.i4" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">•</span> 
<div id="A2.I34.i4.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A2.I34.i4.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Via a Cayley transform between <math id="A2.I34.i4.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbb{D}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>𝔻</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbb{D}</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="A2.I34.i4.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbb{H}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>ℍ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbb{H}</annotation></semantics></math> sending <math id="A2.I34.i4.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mn>0</mn><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">0</annotation></semantics></math> to
<math id="A2.I34.i4.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\infty" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi mathvariant="normal">∞</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\infty</annotation></semantics></math>, this definition matches the chordal local multiple SLE after the
standard change of variables of the vector fields and boundary weights.</p>
</div></li>
</ul>
</div>
<div id="A2.SS9.SSS2.Px1.p12" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A2.SS9.SSS2.Px1.p12.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.SS9.SSS2.Px1.p12.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Summary.</span>
<em id="A2.SS9.SSS2.Px1.p12.1.2" class="ltx_emph ltx_font_italic">Local radial multiple SLE<math id="A2.SS9.SSS2.Px1.p12.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(\kappa)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>κ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(\kappa)</annotation></semantics></math></em> is obtained from the chordal notion by:
work in <math id="A2.SS9.SSS2.Px1.p12.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbb{D}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>𝔻</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbb{D}</annotation></semantics></math> with radial capacity, replace the boundary vector field
<math id="A2.SS9.SSS2.Px1.p12.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="2/(x-\xi)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo>/</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>−</mo><mi>ξ</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">2/(x-\xi)</annotation></semantics></math> by <math id="A2.SS9.SSS2.Px1.p12.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="2\cot\!\big(\frac{\theta-\vartheta}{2}\big)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mpadded style="width:1.109em;" width="1.109em"><mi>cot</mi></mpadded><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">(</mo><mfrac><mrow><mi>θ</mi><mo>−</mo><mi>ϑ</mi></mrow><mn>2</mn></mfrac><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">2\cot\!\big(\frac{\theta-\vartheta}{2}\big)</annotation></semantics></math>, prescribe the
driving SDE <math id="A2.SS9.SSS2.Px1.p12.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="dW_{t}=\sqrt{\kappa}\,dB_{t}+\kappa\,\partial_{\theta_{i}}\log Z\,dt" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>W</mi><mi>t</mi></msub></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><msqrt><mi>κ</mi></msqrt><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>d</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>B</mi><mi>t</mi></msub></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi>κ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><msub><mo rspace="0.167em">∂</mo><msub><mi>θ</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></msub><mrow><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><mi>Z</mi></mrow><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>d</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">dW_{t}=\sqrt{\kappa}\,dB_{t}+\kappa\,\partial_{\theta_{i}}\log Z\,dt</annotation></semantics></math>,
move the passive angles by the radial vector field, and require the partition
function <math id="A2.SS9.SSS2.Px1.p12.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="Z" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>Z</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">Z</annotation></semantics></math> to satisfy the radial BPZ/Ward system (<a href="#A2.E15" title="Equation 15 ‣ item (BPZ) ‣ Response of GPT-5-thinking. ‣ Problem 9b1 ‣ (b) Self-directed learning ‣ 9 Learning New Knowledge ‣ Appendix B Model Responses and Evaluations ‣ GAUSS: Benchmarking Structured Mathematical Skills for Large Language Models" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">15</span></a>) and
fusion asymptotics. The commutation of local growths at different tips is then
equivalent to (<a href="#A2.E15" title="Equation 15 ‣ item (BPZ) ‣ Response of GPT-5-thinking. ‣ Problem 9b1 ‣ (b) Self-directed learning ‣ 9 Learning New Knowledge ‣ Appendix B Model Responses and Evaluations ‣ GAUSS: Benchmarking Structured Mathematical Skills for Large Language Models" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">15</span></a>), exactly paralleling the chordal theory.</p>
</div>
<div id="A2.SS9.SSS2.Px1.p13" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A2.SS9.SSS2.Px1.p13.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.SS9.SSS2.Px1.p13.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Can you define the compatible family of measures<span id="A2.SS9.SSS2.Px1.p13.1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_medium">
Fix <math id="A2.SS9.SSS2.Px1.p13.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\kappa&gt;0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>κ</mi><mo>&gt;</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\kappa&gt;0</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="A2.SS9.SSS2.Px1.p13.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="n\geq 1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>≥</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">n\geq 1</annotation></semantics></math>. A <em id="A2.SS9.SSS2.Px1.p13.1.1.1.1" class="ltx_emph ltx_font_italic">radial <math id="A2.SS9.SSS2.Px1.p13.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="n" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>n</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">n</annotation></semantics></math>–configuration</em> is a triple</span></span></p>
<table id="A2.Ex287" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A2.Ex287.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(D;x_{1},\dots,x_{n};z_{\ast})," display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>D</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>n</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>z</mi><mo>∗</mo></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(D;x_{1},\dots,x_{n};z_{\ast}),</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A2.SS9.SSS2.Px1.p13.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.SS9.SSS2.Px1.p13.2.1" class="ltx_text">where <math id="A2.SS9.SSS2.Px1.p13.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="D\subsetneq\mathbb{C}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>D</mi><mo>⊊</mo><mi>ℂ</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">D\subsetneq\mathbb{C}</annotation></semantics></math> is simply connected, <math id="A2.SS9.SSS2.Px1.p13.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="z_{\ast}\in D" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>z</mi><mo>∗</mo></msub><mo>∈</mo><mi>D</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">z_{\ast}\in D</annotation></semantics></math>, and
<math id="A2.SS9.SSS2.Px1.p13.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="x_{1},\dots,x_{n}\in\partial D" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>x</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>,</mo><mrow><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>n</mi></msub><mo rspace="0.111em">∈</mo><mrow><mo>∂</mo><mi>D</mi></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">x_{1},\dots,x_{n}\in\partial D</annotation></semantics></math> are distinct boundary points listed
counterclockwise.
Choose a conformal chart <math id="A2.SS9.SSS2.Px1.p13.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\psi:D\to\mathbb{D}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>ψ</mi><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mrow><mi>D</mi><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><mi>𝔻</mi></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\psi:D\to\mathbb{D}</annotation></semantics></math> with <math id="A2.SS9.SSS2.Px1.p13.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\psi(z_{\ast})=0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>ψ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>z</mi><mo>∗</mo></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\psi(z_{\ast})=0</annotation></semantics></math> and
<math id="A2.SS9.SSS2.Px1.p13.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\psi(x_{j})=\mathrm{e}^{i\theta_{j}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>ψ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>j</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><msup><mi>e</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>θ</mi><mi>j</mi></msub></mrow></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\psi(x_{j})=\mathrm{e}^{i\theta_{j}}</annotation></semantics></math>; write
<math id="A2.SS9.SSS2.Px1.p13.m10" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Theta=(\theta_{1},\dots,\theta_{n})\in(\mathbb{R}/2\pi\mathbb{Z})^{n}/\mathrm{Rot}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Θ</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>θ</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>θ</mi><mi>n</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>∈</mo><mrow><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>ℝ</mi><mo>/</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>π</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>ℤ</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mi>n</mi></msup><mo>/</mo><mi>Rot</mi></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Theta=(\theta_{1},\dots,\theta_{n})\in(\mathbb{R}/2\pi\mathbb{Z})^{n}/\mathrm{Rot}</annotation></semantics></math> for the angles
modulo overall rotation. Set the <em id="A2.SS9.SSS2.Px1.p13.2.1.1" class="ltx_emph ltx_font_italic">radial vector field</em></span></p>
<table id="A2.Ex288" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A2.Ex288.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="V^{\mathrm{rad}}(\phi\mid\vartheta)\;:=\;2\,\cot\!\frac{\phi-\vartheta}{2},\qquad h:=\frac{6-\kappa}{2\kappa}." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mrow><msup><mi>V</mi><mi>rad</mi></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>ϕ</mi><mo fence="true" lspace="0em" rspace="0em">∣</mo><mi>ϑ</mi><mo rspace="0.280em" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>:=</mo><mrow><mn> 2</mn><mo lspace="0.337em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mi>cot</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mfrac><mrow><mi>ϕ</mi><mo>−</mo><mi>ϑ</mi></mrow><mn>2</mn></mfrac></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="2.167em">,</mo><mrow><mi>h</mi><mo>:=</mo><mfrac><mrow><mn>6</mn><mo>−</mo><mi>κ</mi></mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>κ</mi></mrow></mfrac></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">V^{\mathrm{rad}}(\phi\mid\vartheta)\;:=\;2\,\cot\!\frac{\phi-\vartheta}{2},\qquad h:=\frac{6-\kappa}{2\kappa}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
<div id="A2.SS9.SSS2.Px1.p14" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A2.SS9.SSS2.Px1.p14.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.SS9.SSS2.Px1.p14.1.1" class="ltx_text">Radial multiple partition function.
A positive <math id="A2.SS9.SSS2.Px1.p14.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="C^{2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi>C</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">C^{2}</annotation></semantics></math> function <math id="A2.SS9.SSS2.Px1.p14.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="Z=Z(\Theta)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>Z</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>Z</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">Θ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">Z=Z(\Theta)</annotation></semantics></math> on the configuration space is a
<em id="A2.SS9.SSS2.Px1.p14.1.1.1" class="ltx_emph ltx_font_italic">radial multiple partition function</em> if for each <math id="A2.SS9.SSS2.Px1.p14.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="i=1,\dots,n" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>n</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">i=1,\dots,n</annotation></semantics></math>,</span></p>
<table id="A2.E19" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A2.E19.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\Bigg[\frac{\kappa}{2}\,\partial_{\theta_{i}}^{2}+\sum_{j\neq i}V^{\mathrm{rad}}(\theta_{j}\mid\theta_{i})\,\partial_{\theta_{j}}+2h\sum_{j\neq i}\partial_{\theta_{j}}V^{\mathrm{rad}}(\theta_{j}\mid\theta_{i})\Bigg]Z\;=\;0," display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mo maxsize="2.600em" minsize="2.600em">[</mo><mfrac><mi>κ</mi><mn>2</mn></mfrac><msubsup><mo>∂</mo><msub><mi>θ</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mn>2</mn></msubsup><mo rspace="0.055em">+</mo><munder><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>j</mi><mo>≠</mo><mi>i</mi></mrow></munder><msup><mi>V</mi><mi>rad</mi></msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>θ</mi><mi>j</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.167em">∣</mo><msub><mi>θ</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><msub><mo>∂</mo><msub><mi>θ</mi><mi>j</mi></msub></msub><mo>+</mo><mn>2</mn><mi>h</mi><munder><mo movablelimits="false" rspace="0em">∑</mo><mrow><mi>j</mi><mo>≠</mo><mi>i</mi></mrow></munder><msub><mo>∂</mo><msub><mi>θ</mi><mi>j</mi></msub></msub><msup><mi>V</mi><mi>rad</mi></msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>θ</mi><mi>j</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.167em">∣</mo><msub><mi>θ</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo maxsize="2.600em" minsize="2.600em">]</mo></mrow><mi>Z</mi><mo lspace="0.558em">=</mo><mn> 0</mn><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Bigg[\frac{\kappa}{2}\,\partial_{\theta_{i}}^{2}+\sum_{j\neq i}V^{\mathrm{rad}}(\theta_{j}\mid\theta_{i})\,\partial_{\theta_{j}}+2h\sum_{j\neq i}\partial_{\theta_{j}}V^{\mathrm{rad}}(\theta_{j}\mid\theta_{i})\Bigg]Z\;=\;0,</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(19)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A2.SS9.SSS2.Px1.p14.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.SS9.SSS2.Px1.p14.2.1" class="ltx_text">and <math id="A2.SS9.SSS2.Px1.p14.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="Z" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>Z</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">Z</annotation></semantics></math> is invariant under a common rotation of all angles. (These are the
radial BPZ/Ward equations.)</span></p>
</div>
<div id="A2.SS9.SSS2.Px1.p15" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A2.SS9.SSS2.Px1.p15.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.SS9.SSS2.Px1.p15.1.1" class="ltx_text">Base (one–leg) radial SLE dynamics.
Fix an index <math id="A2.SS9.SSS2.Px1.p15.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="i" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>i</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">i</annotation></semantics></math>. In the disk chart, let <math id="A2.SS9.SSS2.Px1.p15.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(g_{t})_{t\geq 0}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>g</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>≥</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(g_{t})_{t\geq 0}</annotation></semantics></math> be the radial Loewner
flow normalized by <math id="A2.SS9.SSS2.Px1.p15.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="g_{t}(0)=0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>g</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>0</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">g_{t}(0)=0</annotation></semantics></math>, <math id="A2.SS9.SSS2.Px1.p15.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="g_{t}^{\prime}(0)=\mathrm{e}^{t}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msubsup><mi>g</mi><mi>t</mi><mo>′</mo></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>0</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><msup><mi>e</mi><mi>t</mi></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">g_{t}^{\prime}(0)=\mathrm{e}^{t}</annotation></semantics></math>,</span></p>
<table id="A2.Ex289" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A2.Ex289.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\partial_{t}g_{t}(z)=-\,g_{t}(z)\,\frac{\mathrm{e}^{iW_{t}}+g_{t}(z)}{\mathrm{e}^{iW_{t}}-g_{t}(z)},\qquad g_{0}(z)=z," display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mrow><msub><mo>∂</mo><mi>t</mi></msub><mrow><msub><mi>g</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>z</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><msub><mi>g</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>z</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mfrac><mrow><msup><mi>e</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>W</mi><mi>t</mi></msub></mrow></msup><mo>+</mo><mrow><msub><mi>g</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>z</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mrow><msup><mi>e</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>W</mi><mi>t</mi></msub></mrow></msup><mo>−</mo><mrow><msub><mi>g</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>z</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mfrac></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="2.167em">,</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>g</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>z</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mi>z</mi></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\partial_{t}g_{t}(z)=-\,g_{t}(z)\,\frac{\mathrm{e}^{iW_{t}}+g_{t}(z)}{\mathrm{e}^{iW_{t}}-g_{t}(z)},\qquad g_{0}(z)=z,</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A2.SS9.SSS2.Px1.p15.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.SS9.SSS2.Px1.p15.2.1" class="ltx_text">driven by <math id="A2.SS9.SSS2.Px1.p15.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="W_{t}=\sqrt{\kappa}\,B_{t}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>W</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><msqrt><mi>κ</mi></msqrt><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>B</mi><mi>t</mi></msub></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">W_{t}=\sqrt{\kappa}\,B_{t}</annotation></semantics></math>; the passive angles evolve by</span></p>
<table id="A2.E20" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A2.E20.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathrm{d}\Theta_{t}^{\,j}=V^{\mathrm{rad}}\!\big(\Theta_{t}^{\,j}\,\big|\,W_{t}\big)\,\mathrm{d}t,\qquad j\neq i,\qquad\Theta_{t}^{\,i}=W_{t}\ (\mathrm{mod}\ 2\pi)." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi mathvariant="normal">Θ</mi><mi>t</mi><mi>j</mi></msubsup></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><msup><mi>V</mi><mi>rad</mi></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">(</mo><msubsup><mi mathvariant="normal">Θ</mi><mi>t</mi><mi>j</mi></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" mathsize="1.200em" rspace="0.170em">|</mo><msub><mi>W</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>d</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="2.167em">,</mo><mrow><mi>j</mi><mo>≠</mo><mi>i</mi></mrow><mo rspace="2.167em">,</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi mathvariant="normal">Θ</mi><mi>t</mi><mi>i</mi></msubsup><mo>=</mo><mrow><msub><mi>W</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>mod</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mn> 2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>π</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathrm{d}\Theta_{t}^{\,j}=V^{\mathrm{rad}}\!\big(\Theta_{t}^{\,j}\,\big|\,W_{t}\big)\,\mathrm{d}t,\qquad j\neq i,\qquad\Theta_{t}^{\,i}=W_{t}\ (\mathrm{mod}\ 2\pi).</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(20)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A2.SS9.SSS2.Px1.p15.3" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.SS9.SSS2.Px1.p15.3.1" class="ltx_text">Let <math id="A2.SS9.SSS2.Px1.p15.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{F}_{t}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℱ</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{F}_{t}</annotation></semantics></math> be the Loewner filtration and <math id="A2.SS9.SSS2.Px1.p15.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="T_{\ast}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>T</mi><mo>∗</mo></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">T_{\ast}</annotation></semantics></math> the <em id="A2.SS9.SSS2.Px1.p15.3.1.1" class="ltx_emph ltx_font_italic">continuation
threshold</em> (first time some marked angle collides with the tip or is swallowed).
Write <math id="A2.SS9.SSS2.Px1.p15.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbf{P}^{(i)}_{D;X}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mi>𝐏</mi><mrow><mi>D</mi><mo>;</mo><mi>X</mi></mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>i</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbf{P}^{(i)}_{D;X}</annotation></semantics></math> for the law of the hull generated by (<a href="#A2.E20" title="Equation 20 ‣ Response of GPT-5-thinking. ‣ Problem 9b1 ‣ (b) Self-directed learning ‣ 9 Learning New Knowledge ‣ Appendix B Model Responses and Evaluations ‣ GAUSS: Benchmarking Structured Mathematical Skills for Large Language Models" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">20</span></a>)
up to <math id="A2.SS9.SSS2.Px1.p15.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="T_{\ast}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>T</mi><mo>∗</mo></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">T_{\ast}</annotation></semantics></math> (standard radial SLE<sub id="A2.SS9.SSS2.Px1.p15.3.1.2" class="ltx_sub"><span id="A2.SS9.SSS2.Px1.p15.3.1.2.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">κ</span></sub> from <math id="A2.SS9.SSS2.Px1.p15.m11" class="ltx_Math" alttext="x_{i}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">x_{i}</annotation></semantics></math>).</span></p>
</div>
<div id="Thmdefinition1" class="ltx_theorem ltx_theorem_definition">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_title_theorem"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_theorem"><span id="Thmdefinition1.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Definition 1</span></span><span id="Thmdefinition1.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold"> </span>(Compatible family for local radial multiple SLE<sub id="Thmdefinition1.4" class="ltx_sub"><span id="Thmdefinition1.4.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">κ</span></sub> with <math id="Thmdefinition1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="Z" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>Z</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">Z</annotation></semantics></math>)<span id="Thmdefinition1.5" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">.</span></h6>
<div id="Thmdefinition1.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="Thmdefinition1.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="Thmdefinition1.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">Let <math id="Thmdefinition1.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="Z" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>Z</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">Z</annotation></semantics></math> satisfy (<a href="#A2.E15" title="Equation 15 ‣ item (BPZ) ‣ Response of GPT-5-thinking. ‣ Problem 9b1 ‣ (b) Self-directed learning ‣ 9 Learning New Knowledge ‣ Appendix B Model Responses and Evaluations ‣ GAUSS: Benchmarking Structured Mathematical Skills for Large Language Models" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">15</span></a>). A <em id="Thmdefinition1.p1.1.1.1" class="ltx_emph ltx_font_upright">compatible family of measures</em>
is a collection</span></p>
<table id="A2.Ex290" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A2.Ex290.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\Big\{\;\mathbf{P}^{(i),Z}_{D;X}(\,\cdot\,;\tau)\;:\;(D;X;z_{\ast})\ \text{a radial $n$--configuration},\ i\in\{1,\dots,n\},\ \tau\ \text{$\mathcal{F}_{t}$\textendash stopping, }\tau&lt;T_{\ast}\;\Big\}" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo rspace="0.280em" stretchy="false">{</mo><msubsup><mi>𝐏</mi><mrow><mi>D</mi><mo>;</mo><mi>X</mi></mrow><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>i</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>,</mo><mi>Z</mi></mrow></msubsup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mo>⋅</mo><mo>;</mo><mi>τ</mi><mo rspace="0.558em" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo rspace="0.558em">:</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>D</mi><mo>;</mo><mi>X</mi><mo>;</mo><msub><mi>z</mi><mo>∗</mo></msub><mo rspace="0.500em" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mrow><mtext class="ltx_mathvariant_italic">a radial </mtext><mi>n</mi><mtext class="ltx_mathvariant_italic">–configuration</mtext></mrow><mo rspace="0.667em">,</mo><mi>i</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>n</mi><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow><mo rspace="0.667em">,</mo><mi>τ</mi><mrow><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℱ</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mtext class="ltx_mathvariant_italic">–stopping, </mtext></mrow><mi>τ</mi><mo>&lt;</mo><msub><mi>T</mi><mo>∗</mo></msub><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Big\{\;\mathbf{P}^{(i),Z}_{D;X}(\,\cdot\,;\tau)\;:\;(D;X;z_{\ast})\ \text{a radial $n$--configuration},\ i\in\{1,\dots,n\},\ \tau\ \text{$\mathcal{F}_{t}$\textendash stopping, }\tau&lt;T_{\ast}\;\Big\}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="Thmdefinition1.p1.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="Thmdefinition1.p1.2.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">on initial Loewner hulls <math id="Thmdefinition1.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="K[0,\tau]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>K</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mi>τ</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">K[0,\tau]</annotation></semantics></math> such that the following hold.</span></p>
<ol id="A2.I35" class="ltx_enumerate">
<li id="A2.I35.ix1" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">(AC)</span> 
<div id="A2.I35.ix1.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A2.I35.ix1.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.I35.ix1.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold ltx_font_italic">Local absolute continuity.</span><span id="A2.I35.ix1.p1.1.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">
For each </span><math id="A2.I35.ix1.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(D;X;z_{\ast})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>D</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>X</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>z</mi><mo>∗</mo></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(D;X;z_{\ast})</annotation></semantics></math><span id="A2.I35.ix1.p1.1.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">, </span><math id="A2.I35.ix1.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="i" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>i</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">i</annotation></semantics></math><span id="A2.I35.ix1.p1.1.4" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic"> and </span><math id="A2.I35.ix1.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\tau&lt;T_{\ast}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>τ</mi><mo>&lt;</mo><msub><mi>T</mi><mo>∗</mo></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\tau&lt;T_{\ast}</annotation></semantics></math><span id="A2.I35.ix1.p1.1.5" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">,</span></p>
<table id="A2.Ex291" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A2.Ex291.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\frac{\mathrm{d}\mathbf{P}^{(i),Z}_{D;X}(\,\cdot\,;\tau)}{\mathrm{d}\mathbf{P}^{(i)}_{D;X}(\,\cdot\,;\tau)}\Bigg|_{\mathcal{F}_{\tau}}=\frac{M^{(i)}_{\tau}}{M^{(i)}_{0}},\qquad M^{(i)}_{t}\;:=\;Z(\Theta_{t})\,\prod_{j\neq i}\big|g_{t}^{\prime}(\psi(x_{j}))\big|^{h}," display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><msub><mrow><mfrac><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>𝐏</mi><mrow><mi>D</mi><mo>;</mo><mi>X</mi></mrow><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>i</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>,</mo><mi>Z</mi></mrow></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mo>⋅</mo><mo>,</mo><mi>τ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>𝐏</mi><mrow><mi>D</mi><mo>;</mo><mi>X</mi></mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>i</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mo>⋅</mo><mo>,</mo><mi>τ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mfrac><mo maxsize="2.600em" minsize="2.600em" stretchy="true">|</mo></mrow><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℱ</mi><mi>τ</mi></msub></msub><mo>=</mo><mfrac><msubsup><mi>M</mi><mi>τ</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>i</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup><msubsup><mi>M</mi><mn>0</mn><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>i</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup></mfrac></mrow><mo rspace="2.167em">,</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>M</mi><mi>t</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>i</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup><mo rspace="0.558em">:=</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>Z</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Θ</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0.337em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><munder><mo movablelimits="false" rspace="0em">∏</mo><mrow><mi>j</mi><mo>≠</mo><mi>i</mi></mrow></munder><msup><mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em" stretchy="true">|</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>g</mi><mi>t</mi><mo>′</mo></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>ψ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>j</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em" stretchy="true">|</mo></mrow><mi>h</mi></msup></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\frac{\mathrm{d}\mathbf{P}^{(i),Z}_{D;X}(\,\cdot\,;\tau)}{\mathrm{d}\mathbf{P}^{(i)}_{D;X}(\,\cdot\,;\tau)}\Bigg|_{\mathcal{F}_{\tau}}=\frac{M^{(i)}_{\tau}}{M^{(i)}_{0}},\qquad M^{(i)}_{t}\;:=\;Z(\Theta_{t})\,\prod_{j\neq i}\big|g_{t}^{\prime}(\psi(x_{j}))\big|^{h},</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A2.I35.ix1.p1.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.I35.ix1.p1.2.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">where </span><math id="A2.I35.ix1.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="M^{(i)}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi>M</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>i</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">M^{(i)}</annotation></semantics></math><span id="A2.I35.ix1.p1.2.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic"> is an </span><math id="A2.I35.ix1.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{F}_{t}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℱ</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{F}_{t}</annotation></semantics></math><span id="A2.I35.ix1.p1.2.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">–local martingale under
</span><math id="A2.I35.ix1.p1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbf{P}^{(i)}_{D;X}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mi>𝐏</mi><mrow><mi>D</mi><mo>;</mo><mi>X</mi></mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>i</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbf{P}^{(i)}_{D;X}</annotation></semantics></math><span id="A2.I35.ix1.p1.2.4" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic"> (by (</span><a href="#A2.E15" title="Equation 15 ‣ item (BPZ) ‣ Response of GPT-5-thinking. ‣ Problem 9b1 ‣ (b) Self-directed learning ‣ 9 Learning New Knowledge ‣ Appendix B Model Responses and Evaluations ‣ GAUSS: Benchmarking Structured Mathematical Skills for Large Language Models" class="ltx_ref ltx_font_italic"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">15</span></a><span id="A2.I35.ix1.p1.2.5" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">)). Equivalently, under
</span><math id="A2.I35.ix1.p1.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbf{P}^{(i),Z}_{D;X}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mi>𝐏</mi><mrow><mi>D</mi><mo>;</mo><mi>X</mi></mrow><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>i</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>,</mo><mi>Z</mi></mrow></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbf{P}^{(i),Z}_{D;X}</annotation></semantics></math><span id="A2.I35.ix1.p1.2.6" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic"> the driving satisfies</span></p>
<table id="A2.Ex292" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A2.Ex292.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathrm{d}W_{t}=\sqrt{\kappa}\,\mathrm{d}B_{t}+\kappa\,\partial_{\theta_{i}}\log Z(\Theta_{t})\,\mathrm{d}t,\quad\text{with }\Theta_{t}\text{ evolving by \eqref{eq:passive}.}" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>W</mi><mi>t</mi></msub></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><msqrt><mi>κ</mi></msqrt><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>d</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>B</mi><mi>t</mi></msub></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi>κ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><msub><mo rspace="0.167em">∂</mo><msub><mi>θ</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></msub><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>Z</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Θ</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>d</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="1.167em">,</mo><mrow><mtext class="ltx_mathvariant_italic">with </mtext><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Θ</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mtext class="ltx_mathvariant_italic"> evolving by (</mtext><mtext class="ltx_mathvariant_italic"><a href="#A2.E20" title="Equation 20 ‣ Response of GPT-5-thinking. ‣ Problem 9b1 ‣ (b) Self-directed learning ‣ 9 Learning New Knowledge ‣ Appendix B Model Responses and Evaluations ‣ GAUSS: Benchmarking Structured Mathematical Skills for Large Language Models" class="ltx_ref ltx_font_italic"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">20</span></a></mtext><mtext class="ltx_mathvariant_italic">).</mtext></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathrm{d}W_{t}=\sqrt{\kappa}\,\mathrm{d}B_{t}+\kappa\,\partial_{\theta_{i}}\log Z(\Theta_{t})\,\mathrm{d}t,\quad\text{with }\Theta_{t}\text{ evolving by \eqref{eq:passive}.}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div></li>
<li id="A2.I35.ix2" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">(DM)</span> 
<div id="A2.I35.ix2.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A2.I35.ix2.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.I35.ix2.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold ltx_font_italic">Domain Markov/concatenation.</span><span id="A2.I35.ix2.p1.1.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">
If </span><math id="A2.I35.ix2.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="0\leq\sigma\leq\tau&lt;T_{\ast}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mn>0</mn><mo>≤</mo><mi>σ</mi><mo>≤</mo><mi>τ</mi><mo>&lt;</mo><msub><mi>T</mi><mo>∗</mo></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">0\leq\sigma\leq\tau&lt;T_{\ast}</annotation></semantics></math><span id="A2.I35.ix2.p1.1.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic"> are stopping times, then under
</span><math id="A2.I35.ix2.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbf{P}^{(i),Z}_{D;X}(\,\cdot\,;\tau)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msubsup><mi>𝐏</mi><mrow><mi>D</mi><mo>;</mo><mi>X</mi></mrow><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>i</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>,</mo><mi>Z</mi></mrow></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mo>⋅</mo><mo>,</mo><mi>τ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbf{P}^{(i),Z}_{D;X}(\,\cdot\,;\tau)</annotation></semantics></math><span id="A2.I35.ix2.p1.1.4" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic"> and conditionally on </span><math id="A2.I35.ix2.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{F}_{\sigma}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℱ</mi><mi>σ</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{F}_{\sigma}</annotation></semantics></math><span id="A2.I35.ix2.p1.1.5" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">,
the </span><em id="A2.I35.ix2.p1.1.6" class="ltx_emph">future</em><span id="A2.I35.ix2.p1.1.7" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic"> hull (recentered by </span><math id="A2.I35.ix2.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="g_{\sigma}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>g</mi><mi>σ</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">g_{\sigma}</annotation></semantics></math><span id="A2.I35.ix2.p1.1.8" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic"> and with updated marked points
</span><math id="A2.I35.ix2.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="X_{\sigma}=g_{\sigma}(X)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>X</mi><mi>σ</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><msub><mi>g</mi><mi>σ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>X</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">X_{\sigma}=g_{\sigma}(X)</annotation></semantics></math><span id="A2.I35.ix2.p1.1.9" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">) has law
</span><math id="A2.I35.ix2.p1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbf{P}^{(i),Z}_{g_{\sigma}(D\setminus K[0,\sigma]);\,X_{\sigma}}(\,\cdot\,;\tau-\sigma)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msubsup><mi>𝐏</mi><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>g</mi><mi>σ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>D</mi><mo>∖</mo><mrow><mi>K</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mi>σ</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.337em">;</mo><msub><mi>X</mi><mi>σ</mi></msub></mrow><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>i</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>,</mo><mi>Z</mi></mrow></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mo>⋅</mo><mo>,</mo><mrow><mi>τ</mi><mo>−</mo><mi>σ</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbf{P}^{(i),Z}_{g_{\sigma}(D\setminus K[0,\sigma]);\,X_{\sigma}}(\,\cdot\,;\tau-\sigma)</annotation></semantics></math><span id="A2.I35.ix2.p1.1.10" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">.
In particular, the measure obtained by sampling to time </span><math id="A2.I35.ix2.p1.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\sigma" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>σ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\sigma</annotation></semantics></math><span id="A2.I35.ix2.p1.1.11" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic"> and then
continuing with the same family to time </span><math id="A2.I35.ix2.p1.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\tau" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>τ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\tau</annotation></semantics></math><span id="A2.I35.ix2.p1.1.12" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic"> coincides with
</span><math id="A2.I35.ix2.p1.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbf{P}^{(i),Z}_{D;X}(\,\cdot\,;\tau)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msubsup><mi>𝐏</mi><mrow><mi>D</mi><mo>;</mo><mi>X</mi></mrow><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>i</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>,</mo><mi>Z</mi></mrow></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mo>⋅</mo><mo>,</mo><mi>τ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbf{P}^{(i),Z}_{D;X}(\,\cdot\,;\tau)</annotation></semantics></math><span id="A2.I35.ix2.p1.1.13" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">.</span></p>
</div></li>
<li id="A2.I35.ix3" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">(Comm)</span> 
<div id="A2.I35.ix3.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A2.I35.ix3.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.I35.ix3.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold ltx_font_italic">Commutation of local growths.</span><span id="A2.I35.ix3.p1.1.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">
For any distinct </span><math id="A2.I35.ix3.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="i\neq j" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>≠</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">i\neq j</annotation></semantics></math><span id="A2.I35.ix3.p1.1.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic"> and bounded stopping times </span><math id="A2.I35.ix3.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\tau_{i},\tau_{j}&lt;T_{\ast}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>τ</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><mrow><msub><mi>τ</mi><mi>j</mi></msub><mo>&lt;</mo><msub><mi>T</mi><mo>∗</mo></msub></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\tau_{i},\tau_{j}&lt;T_{\ast}</annotation></semantics></math><span id="A2.I35.ix3.p1.1.4" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">,
the joint law of the pair of initial hulls obtained by the two orders</span></p>
<table id="A2.Ex293" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A2.Ex293.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\big(\text{first grow near }x_{i}\text{ to }\tau_{i}\ \text{then }x_{j}\text{ to }\tau_{j}\big)\quad\text{and}\quad\big(\text{first }x_{j}\text{ then }x_{i}\big)" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">(</mo><mrow><mtext class="ltx_mathvariant_italic">first grow near </mtext><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mtext class="ltx_mathvariant_italic"> to </mtext><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>τ</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mtext class="ltx_mathvariant_italic">then </mtext><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>j</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mtext class="ltx_mathvariant_italic"> to </mtext><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>τ</mi><mi>j</mi></msub></mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">)</mo></mrow><mspace style="width:1em;" width="1em"></mspace><mtext class="ltx_mathvariant_italic">and</mtext><mspace style="width:1em;" width="1em"></mspace><mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">(</mo><mrow><mtext class="ltx_mathvariant_italic">first </mtext><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>j</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mtext class="ltx_mathvariant_italic"> then </mtext><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\big(\text{first grow near }x_{i}\text{ to }\tau_{i}\ \text{then }x_{j}\text{ to }\tau_{j}\big)\quad\text{and}\quad\big(\text{first }x_{j}\text{ then }x_{i}\big)</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A2.I35.ix3.p1.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.I35.ix3.p1.2.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">agree after the obvious conformal recentering and a deterministic capacity
time–change. (Equivalently, the </span><math id="A2.I35.ix3.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\sigma" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>σ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\sigma</annotation></semantics></math><span id="A2.I35.ix3.p1.2.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">–algebras generated by these two-step
procedures define the same projective family.) This commutation holds iff </span><math id="A2.I35.ix3.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="Z" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>Z</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">Z</annotation></semantics></math><span id="A2.I35.ix3.p1.2.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">
solves the BPZ system (</span><a href="#A2.E15" title="Equation 15 ‣ item (BPZ) ‣ Response of GPT-5-thinking. ‣ Problem 9b1 ‣ (b) Self-directed learning ‣ 9 Learning New Knowledge ‣ Appendix B Model Responses and Evaluations ‣ GAUSS: Benchmarking Structured Mathematical Skills for Large Language Models" class="ltx_ref ltx_font_italic"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">15</span></a><span id="A2.I35.ix3.p1.2.4" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">).</span></p>
</div></li>
<li id="A2.I35.ix4" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">(Cov)</span> 
<div id="A2.I35.ix4.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A2.I35.ix4.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.I35.ix4.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold ltx_font_italic">Conformal covariance.</span><span id="A2.I35.ix4.p1.1.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">
If </span><math id="A2.I35.ix4.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\phi:D\!\to\!D^{\prime}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>ϕ</mi><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mrow><mi>D</mi><mo lspace="0.108em" rspace="0.108em" stretchy="false">→</mo><msup><mi>D</mi><mo>′</mo></msup></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\phi:D\!\to\!D^{\prime}</annotation></semantics></math><span id="A2.I35.ix4.p1.1.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic"> is conformal with </span><math id="A2.I35.ix4.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\phi(z_{\ast})=z^{\prime}_{\ast}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>ϕ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>z</mi><mo>∗</mo></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><msubsup><mi>z</mi><mo>∗</mo><mo>′</mo></msubsup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\phi(z_{\ast})=z^{\prime}_{\ast}</annotation></semantics></math><span id="A2.I35.ix4.p1.1.4" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic"> and
</span><math id="A2.I35.ix4.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\phi(x_{k})=x^{\prime}_{k}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>ϕ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><msubsup><mi>x</mi><mi>k</mi><mo>′</mo></msubsup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\phi(x_{k})=x^{\prime}_{k}</annotation></semantics></math><span id="A2.I35.ix4.p1.1.5" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">, then the image measure of
</span><math id="A2.I35.ix4.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbf{P}^{(i),Z}_{D;X}(\,\cdot\,;\tau)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msubsup><mi>𝐏</mi><mrow><mi>D</mi><mo>;</mo><mi>X</mi></mrow><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>i</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>,</mo><mi>Z</mi></mrow></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mo>⋅</mo><mo>,</mo><mi>τ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbf{P}^{(i),Z}_{D;X}(\,\cdot\,;\tau)</annotation></semantics></math><span id="A2.I35.ix4.p1.1.6" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic"> under </span><math id="A2.I35.ix4.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\phi" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>ϕ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\phi</annotation></semantics></math><span id="A2.I35.ix4.p1.1.7" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic"> equals
</span><math id="A2.I35.ix4.p1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbf{P}^{(i),Z_{D^{\prime}}}_{D^{\prime};X^{\prime}}(\,\cdot\,;\tau^{\prime})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msubsup><mi>𝐏</mi><mrow><msup><mi>D</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo>;</mo><msup><mi>X</mi><mo>′</mo></msup></mrow><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>i</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>Z</mi><msup><mi>D</mi><mo>′</mo></msup></msub></mrow></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mo>⋅</mo><mo>,</mo><msup><mi>τ</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbf{P}^{(i),Z_{D^{\prime}}}_{D^{\prime};X^{\prime}}(\,\cdot\,;\tau^{\prime})</annotation></semantics></math><span id="A2.I35.ix4.p1.1.8" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">, where </span><math id="A2.I35.ix4.p1.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\tau^{\prime}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi>τ</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\tau^{\prime}</annotation></semantics></math><span id="A2.I35.ix4.p1.1.9" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic"> is the radial
capacity time in </span><math id="A2.I35.ix4.p1.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="D^{\prime}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi>D</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">D^{\prime}</annotation></semantics></math><span id="A2.I35.ix4.p1.1.10" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic"> (i.e. normalized by </span><math id="A2.I35.ix4.p1.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="g_{t}^{\prime}(z^{\prime}_{\ast})=\mathrm{e}^{t}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msubsup><mi>g</mi><mi>t</mi><mo>′</mo></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msubsup><mi>z</mi><mo>∗</mo><mo>′</mo></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><msup><mi>e</mi><mi>t</mi></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">g_{t}^{\prime}(z^{\prime}_{\ast})=\mathrm{e}^{t}</annotation></semantics></math><span id="A2.I35.ix4.p1.1.11" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">), and
</span><math id="A2.I35.ix4.p1.m10" class="ltx_Math" alttext="Z_{D^{\prime}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>Z</mi><msup><mi>D</mi><mo>′</mo></msup></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">Z_{D^{\prime}}</annotation></semantics></math><span id="A2.I35.ix4.p1.1.12" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic"> is the transport of </span><math id="A2.I35.ix4.p1.m11" class="ltx_Math" alttext="Z" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>Z</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">Z</annotation></semantics></math><span id="A2.I35.ix4.p1.1.13" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic"> with boundary weight </span><math id="A2.I35.ix4.p1.m12" class="ltx_Math" alttext="h" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>h</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">h</annotation></semantics></math><span id="A2.I35.ix4.p1.1.14" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic"> at each marked
point (rotation invariance in </span><math id="A2.I35.ix4.p1.m13" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbb{D}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>𝔻</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbb{D}</annotation></semantics></math><span id="A2.I35.ix4.p1.1.15" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">).</span></p>
</div></li>
</ol>
</div>
</div>
<div id="A2.SS9.SSS2.Px1.p16" class="ltx_para">
<ul id="A2.I36" class="ltx_itemize">
<li id="A2.I36.i1" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">•</span> 
<div id="A2.I36.i1.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A2.I36.i1.p1.1" class="ltx_p">The choice of the product factor <math id="A2.I36.i1.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\prod_{j\neq i}|g_{t}^{\prime}(\psi(x_{j}))|^{h}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mo>∏</mo><mrow><mi>j</mi><mo>≠</mo><mi>i</mi></mrow></msub><msup><mrow><mo lspace="0em" stretchy="false">|</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>g</mi><mi>t</mi><mo>′</mo></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>ψ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>j</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow><mi>h</mi></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\prod_{j\neq i}|g_{t}^{\prime}(\psi(x_{j}))|^{h}</annotation></semantics></math>
matches the <math id="A2.I36.i1.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="2h\sum_{j\neq i}\partial_{\theta_{j}}V^{\mathrm{rad}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>h</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><msub><mo rspace="0em">∑</mo><mrow><mi>j</mi><mo>≠</mo><mi>i</mi></mrow></msub><mrow><msub><mo>∂</mo><msub><mi>θ</mi><mi>j</mi></msub></msub><msup><mi>V</mi><mi>rad</mi></msup></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">2h\sum_{j\neq i}\partial_{\theta_{j}}V^{\mathrm{rad}}</annotation></semantics></math> term in
(<a href="#A2.E15" title="Equation 15 ‣ item (BPZ) ‣ Response of GPT-5-thinking. ‣ Problem 9b1 ‣ (b) Self-directed learning ‣ 9 Learning New Knowledge ‣ Appendix B Model Responses and Evaluations ‣ GAUSS: Benchmarking Structured Mathematical Skills for Large Language Models" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">15</span></a>); in the angular coordinate dynamics (<a href="#A2.E20" title="Equation 20 ‣ Response of GPT-5-thinking. ‣ Problem 9b1 ‣ (b) Self-directed learning ‣ 9 Learning New Knowledge ‣ Appendix B Model Responses and Evaluations ‣ GAUSS: Benchmarking Structured Mathematical Skills for Large Language Models" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">20</span></a>),
<math id="A2.I36.i1.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="M^{(i)}_{t}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mi>M</mi><mi>t</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>i</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">M^{(i)}_{t}</annotation></semantics></math> is a local martingale under the base law, hence (AC) is a Girsanov
tilt producing the drift <math id="A2.I36.i1.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\kappa\,\partial_{\theta_{i}}\log Z" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>κ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><msub><mo rspace="0.167em">∂</mo><msub><mi>θ</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></msub><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><mi>Z</mi></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\kappa\,\partial_{\theta_{i}}\log Z</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>
</div></li>
<li id="A2.I36.i2" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">•</span> 
<div id="A2.I36.i2.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A2.I36.i2.p1.1" class="ltx_p">For <math id="A2.I36.i2.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="n=1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">n=1</annotation></semantics></math> and constant <math id="A2.I36.i2.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="Z" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>Z</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">Z</annotation></semantics></math>, the family reduces to the usual radial
SLE<sub id="A2.I36.i2.p1.1.1" class="ltx_sub"><span id="A2.I36.i2.p1.1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">κ</span></sub>. For <math id="A2.I36.i2.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\kappa\leq 4" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>κ</mi><mo>≤</mo><mn>4</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\kappa\leq 4</annotation></semantics></math>, compatible families associated with <em id="A2.I36.i2.p1.1.2" class="ltx_emph ltx_font_italic">pure</em>
<math id="A2.I36.i2.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="Z" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>Z</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">Z</annotation></semantics></math> globalize to <math id="A2.I36.i2.p1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="n" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>n</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">n</annotation></semantics></math> simple curves aimed at <math id="A2.I36.i2.p1.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="z_{\ast}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>z</mi><mo>∗</mo></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">z_{\ast}</annotation></semantics></math>; different pure <math id="A2.I36.i2.p1.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="Z" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>Z</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">Z</annotation></semantics></math> encode
different connectivity types. The chordal notion is recovered from the radial
one via a Cayley transform sending <math id="A2.I36.i2.p1.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="z_{\ast}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>z</mi><mo>∗</mo></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">z_{\ast}</annotation></semantics></math> to <math id="A2.I36.i2.p1.m10" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\infty" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi mathvariant="normal">∞</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\infty</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>
</div></li>
</ul>
<p id="A2.SS9.SSS2.Px1.p16.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.SS9.SSS2.Px1.p16.1.1" class="ltx_text">∎</span></p>
</div>
</div>
<div id="A2.SS9.SSS2.Px1.2" class="ltx_proof">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_font_italic ltx_title_proof"><span id="A2.SS9.SSS2.Px1.2.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Standard Solution</span>.</h6>
<div id="A2.SS9.SSS2.Px1.p17" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A2.SS9.SSS2.Px1.p17.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.SS9.SSS2.Px1.p17.1.1" class="ltx_text">Definition 1.1 (Localization of Measures). Let <math id="A2.SS9.SSS2.Px1.p17.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Omega\subsetneq\mathbb{C}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Ω</mi><mo>⊊</mo><mi>ℂ</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Omega\subsetneq\mathbb{C}</annotation></semantics></math> be a simply connected domain with an interior marked point <math id="A2.SS9.SSS2.Px1.p17.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="u\in\Omega" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>u</mi><mo>∈</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">Ω</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">u\in\Omega</annotation></semantics></math>. Let <math id="A2.SS9.SSS2.Px1.p17.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="z_{1},z_{2},\ldots,z_{n}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>z</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>z</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>z</mi><mi>n</mi></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">z_{1},z_{2},\ldots,z_{n}</annotation></semantics></math> denote distinct prime ends of <math id="A2.SS9.SSS2.Px1.p17.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\partial\Omega" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo>∂</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">Ω</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\partial\Omega</annotation></semantics></math>, and let <math id="A2.SS9.SSS2.Px1.p17.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="U_{1},U_{2},\ldots,U_{n}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>U</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>U</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>U</mi><mi>n</mi></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">U_{1},U_{2},\ldots,U_{n}</annotation></semantics></math> be closed neighborhoods of <math id="A2.SS9.SSS2.Px1.p17.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="z_{1},z_{2},\ldots,z_{n}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>z</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>z</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>z</mi><mi>n</mi></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">z_{1},z_{2},\ldots,z_{n}</annotation></semantics></math> in <math id="A2.SS9.SSS2.Px1.p17.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Omega" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi mathvariant="normal">Ω</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Omega</annotation></semantics></math> such that:
- <math id="A2.SS9.SSS2.Px1.p17.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="U_{i}\cap U_{j}=\emptyset" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>U</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>∩</mo><msub><mi>U</mi><mi>j</mi></msub></mrow><mo>=</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">∅</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">U_{i}\cap U_{j}=\emptyset</annotation></semantics></math> for all <math id="A2.SS9.SSS2.Px1.p17.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="1\leq i&lt;j\leq n" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>≤</mo><mi>i</mi><mo>&lt;</mo><mi>j</mi><mo>≤</mo><mi>n</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">1\leq i&lt;j\leq n</annotation></semantics></math>,
- None of the <math id="A2.SS9.SSS2.Px1.p17.m10" class="ltx_Math" alttext="U_{j}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>U</mi><mi>j</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">U_{j}</annotation></semantics></math> contain the interior point <math id="A2.SS9.SSS2.Px1.p17.m11" class="ltx_Math" alttext="q" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>q</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">q</annotation></semantics></math>.</span></p>
</div>
<div id="A2.SS9.SSS2.Px1.p18" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A2.SS9.SSS2.Px1.p18.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.SS9.SSS2.Px1.p18.1.1" class="ltx_text">We consider the measures</span></p>
</div>
<div id="A2.SS9.SSS2.Px1.p19" class="ltx_para">
<table id="A2.Ex294" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A2.Ex294.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbb{P}_{\left(\Omega;z_{1},z_{2},\ldots,z_{n},q\right)}^{\left(U_{1},U_{2},\ldots,U_{n}\right)}" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mi>ℙ</mi><mrow><mo>(</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">Ω</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>z</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>z</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>z</mi><mi>n</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><mi>q</mi><mo>)</mo></mrow><mrow><mo>(</mo><msub><mi>U</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>U</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>U</mi><mi>n</mi></msub><mo>)</mo></mrow></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbb{P}_{\left(\Omega;z_{1},z_{2},\ldots,z_{n},q\right)}^{\left(U_{1},U_{2},\ldots,U_{n}\right)}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
<div id="A2.SS9.SSS2.Px1.p20" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A2.SS9.SSS2.Px1.p20.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.SS9.SSS2.Px1.p20.1.1" class="ltx_text">defined on <math id="A2.SS9.SSS2.Px1.p20.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="n" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>n</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">n</annotation></semantics></math>-tuples of unparametrized continuous curves in <math id="A2.SS9.SSS2.Px1.p20.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Omega" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi mathvariant="normal">Ω</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Omega</annotation></semantics></math>. Each curve <math id="A2.SS9.SSS2.Px1.p20.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\eta^{(j)}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi>η</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>j</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\eta^{(j)}</annotation></semantics></math> begins at <math id="A2.SS9.SSS2.Px1.p20.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="z_{j}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>z</mi><mi>j</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">z_{j}</annotation></semantics></math> and exits <math id="A2.SS9.SSS2.Px1.p20.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="U_{j}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>U</mi><mi>j</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">U_{j}</annotation></semantics></math> almost surely.</span></p>
</div>
<div id="A2.SS9.SSS2.Px1.p21" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A2.SS9.SSS2.Px1.p21.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.SS9.SSS2.Px1.p21.1.1" class="ltx_text">A family of such measures indexed by different choices of ( <math id="A2.SS9.SSS2.Px1.p21.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="U_{1},U_{2},\ldots,U_{n}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>U</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>U</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>U</mi><mi>n</mi></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">U_{1},U_{2},\ldots,U_{n}</annotation></semantics></math> ) is called compatible if for all <math id="A2.SS9.SSS2.Px1.p21.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="U_{j}\subset U_{j}^{\prime}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>U</mi><mi>j</mi></msub><mo>⊂</mo><msubsup><mi>U</mi><mi>j</mi><mo>′</mo></msubsup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">U_{j}\subset U_{j}^{\prime}</annotation></semantics></math>, the measure</span></p>
</div>
<div id="A2.SS9.SSS2.Px1.p22" class="ltx_para">
<table id="A2.Ex295" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A2.Ex295.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbb{P}_{\left(\Omega;z_{1},z_{2},\ldots,z_{n},q\right)}^{\left(U_{1},U_{2},\ldots,U_{n}\right)}" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mi>ℙ</mi><mrow><mo>(</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">Ω</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>z</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>z</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>z</mi><mi>n</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><mi>q</mi><mo>)</mo></mrow><mrow><mo>(</mo><msub><mi>U</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>U</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>U</mi><mi>n</mi></msub><mo>)</mo></mrow></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbb{P}_{\left(\Omega;z_{1},z_{2},\ldots,z_{n},q\right)}^{\left(U_{1},U_{2},\ldots,U_{n}\right)}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
<div id="A2.SS9.SSS2.Px1.p23" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A2.SS9.SSS2.Px1.p23.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.SS9.SSS2.Px1.p23.1.1" class="ltx_text">is obtained by restricting the curves under</span></p>
</div>
<div id="A2.SS9.SSS2.Px1.p24" class="ltx_para">
<table id="A2.Ex296" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A2.Ex296.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbb{P}_{\left(\Omega;z_{1},z_{2},\ldots,z_{n},q\right)}^{\left(U_{1}^{\prime},U_{2}^{\prime},\ldots,U_{n}^{\prime}\right)}" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mi>ℙ</mi><mrow><mo>(</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">Ω</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>z</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>z</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>z</mi><mi>n</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><mi>q</mi><mo>)</mo></mrow><mrow><mo>(</mo><msubsup><mi>U</mi><mn>1</mn><mo>′</mo></msubsup><mo>,</mo><msubsup><mi>U</mi><mn>2</mn><mo>′</mo></msubsup><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>,</mo><msubsup><mi>U</mi><mi>n</mi><mo>′</mo></msubsup><mo>)</mo></mrow></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbb{P}_{\left(\Omega;z_{1},z_{2},\ldots,z_{n},q\right)}^{\left(U_{1}^{\prime},U_{2}^{\prime},\ldots,U_{n}^{\prime}\right)}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
<div id="A2.SS9.SSS2.Px1.p25" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A2.SS9.SSS2.Px1.p25.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.SS9.SSS2.Px1.p25.1.1" class="ltx_text">to the portions of the curves that remain inside the subdomains <math id="A2.SS9.SSS2.Px1.p25.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="U_{j}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>U</mi><mi>j</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">U_{j}</annotation></semantics></math> before their first exit.
Definition 1.2 (Local multiple radial <math id="A2.SS9.SSS2.Px1.p25.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\operatorname{SLE}(\kappa)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>SLE</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>κ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\operatorname{SLE}(\kappa)</annotation></semantics></math> ). The locally commuting <math id="A2.SS9.SSS2.Px1.p25.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="n" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>n</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">n</annotation></semantics></math>-radial <math id="A2.SS9.SSS2.Px1.p25.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\operatorname{SLE}(\kappa)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>SLE</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>κ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\operatorname{SLE}(\kappa)</annotation></semantics></math> is a compatible family of measures</span></p>
</div>
<div id="A2.SS9.SSS2.Px1.p26" class="ltx_para">
<table id="A2.Ex297" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A2.Ex297.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbb{P}_{\left(\Omega;z_{1},z_{2},\ldots,z_{n},q\right)}^{\left(U_{1},U_{2},\ldots,U_{n}\right)}" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mi>ℙ</mi><mrow><mo>(</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">Ω</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>z</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>z</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>z</mi><mi>n</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><mi>q</mi><mo>)</mo></mrow><mrow><mo>(</mo><msub><mi>U</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>U</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>U</mi><mi>n</mi></msub><mo>)</mo></mrow></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbb{P}_{\left(\Omega;z_{1},z_{2},\ldots,z_{n},q\right)}^{\left(U_{1},U_{2},\ldots,U_{n}\right)}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
<div id="A2.SS9.SSS2.Px1.p27" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A2.SS9.SSS2.Px1.p27.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.SS9.SSS2.Px1.p27.1.1" class="ltx_text">on <math id="A2.SS9.SSS2.Px1.p27.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="n" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>n</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">n</annotation></semantics></math>-tuples of continuous, non-self-crossing curves <math id="A2.SS9.SSS2.Px1.p27.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\left(\gamma^{(1)},\gamma^{(2)},\ldots,\gamma^{(n)}\right)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo>(</mo><msup><mi>γ</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>1</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msup><mo>,</mo><msup><mi>γ</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>2</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msup><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>,</mo><msup><mi>γ</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>n</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msup><mo>)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\left(\gamma^{(1)},\gamma^{(2)},\ldots,\gamma^{(n)}\right)</annotation></semantics></math> for all simply connected domains <math id="A2.SS9.SSS2.Px1.p27.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Omega" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi mathvariant="normal">Ω</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Omega</annotation></semantics></math> with marked points ( <math id="A2.SS9.SSS2.Px1.p27.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="z_{1},z_{2},\ldots,z_{n},q" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>z</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>z</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>z</mi><mi>n</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><mi>q</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">z_{1},z_{2},\ldots,z_{n},q</annotation></semantics></math> ) and target sets ( <math id="A2.SS9.SSS2.Px1.p27.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="U_{1},U_{2},\ldots,U_{n}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>U</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>U</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>U</mi><mi>n</mi></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">U_{1},U_{2},\ldots,U_{n}</annotation></semantics></math> ). These measures satisfy the following conditions:
(i) Conformal invariance: If <math id="A2.SS9.SSS2.Px1.p27.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\varphi:\Omega\rightarrow\Omega^{\prime}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>φ</mi><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Ω</mi><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><msup><mi mathvariant="normal">Ω</mi><mo>′</mo></msup></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\varphi:\Omega\rightarrow\Omega^{\prime}</annotation></semantics></math> is a conformal map, then the pullback measure satisfies</span></p>
</div>
<div id="A2.SS9.SSS2.Px1.p28" class="ltx_para">
<table id="A2.Ex298" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A2.Ex298.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\varphi^{*}\mathbb{P}_{\left(\Omega^{\prime};\varphi\left(z_{1}\right),\varphi\left(z_{2}\right),\ldots,\varphi\left(z_{n}\right),\varphi(q)\right)}^{\left(\varphi\left(U_{1}\right),\varphi\left(U_{2}\right),\ldots,\varphi\left(U_{n}\right)\right)}=\mathbb{P}_{\left(\Omega;z_{1},z_{2},\ldots,z_{n},u\right)}^{\left(U_{1},U_{2},\ldots,U_{n}\right)}." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><msup><mi>φ</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>ℙ</mi><mrow><mo>(</mo><msup><mi mathvariant="normal">Ω</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo>,</mo><mrow><mi>φ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><msub><mi>z</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo><mrow><mi>φ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><msub><mi>z</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>,</mo><mrow><mi>φ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><msub><mi>z</mi><mi>n</mi></msub><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo><mrow><mi>φ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>q</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mi>φ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><msub><mi>U</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo><mrow><mi>φ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><msub><mi>U</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>,</mo><mrow><mi>φ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><msub><mi>U</mi><mi>n</mi></msub><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow></msubsup></mrow><mo>=</mo><msubsup><mi>ℙ</mi><mrow><mo>(</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">Ω</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>z</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>z</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>z</mi><mi>n</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><mi>u</mi><mo>)</mo></mrow><mrow><mo>(</mo><msub><mi>U</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>U</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>U</mi><mi>n</mi></msub><mo>)</mo></mrow></msubsup></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\varphi^{*}\mathbb{P}_{\left(\Omega^{\prime};\varphi\left(z_{1}\right),\varphi\left(z_{2}\right),\ldots,\varphi\left(z_{n}\right),\varphi(q)\right)}^{\left(\varphi\left(U_{1}\right),\varphi\left(U_{2}\right),\ldots,\varphi\left(U_{n}\right)\right)}=\mathbb{P}_{\left(\Omega;z_{1},z_{2},\ldots,z_{n},u\right)}^{\left(U_{1},U_{2},\ldots,U_{n}\right)}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
<div id="A2.SS9.SSS2.Px1.p29" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A2.SS9.SSS2.Px1.p29.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.SS9.SSS2.Px1.p29.1.1" class="ltx_text">It suffices to describe the measure when <math id="A2.SS9.SSS2.Px1.p29.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\left(\Omega;z_{1},z_{2},\ldots,z_{n},q\right)=\left(\mathbb{D};z_{1},z_{2},\ldots,z_{n},0\right)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mo>(</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">Ω</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>z</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>z</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>z</mi><mi>n</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><mi>q</mi><mo>)</mo></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mi>𝔻</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>z</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>z</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>z</mi><mi>n</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\left(\Omega;z_{1},z_{2},\ldots,z_{n},q\right)=\left(\mathbb{D};z_{1},z_{2},\ldots,z_{n},0\right)</annotation></semantics></math>. The definition for arbitrary <math id="A2.SS9.SSS2.Px1.p29.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Omega" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi mathvariant="normal">Ω</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Omega</annotation></semantics></math> with a marked interior point <math id="A2.SS9.SSS2.Px1.p29.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="q" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>q</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">q</annotation></semantics></math> can then be extended by pulling back via a conformal equivalence <math id="A2.SS9.SSS2.Px1.p29.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\varphi:\Omega\rightarrow\mathbb{D}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>φ</mi><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Ω</mi><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><mi>𝔻</mi></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\varphi:\Omega\rightarrow\mathbb{D}</annotation></semantics></math> mapping <math id="A2.SS9.SSS2.Px1.p29.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="q" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>q</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">q</annotation></semantics></math> to 0 .
(ii) Domain Markov property: Let <math id="A2.SS9.SSS2.Px1.p29.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\left(\gamma^{(1)},\gamma^{(2)},\ldots,\gamma^{(n)}\right)\sim\mathbb{P}_{\left(\mathbb{D};z_{1},z_{2},\ldots,z_{n},q\right)}^{\left(U_{1},U_{2},\ldots,U_{n}\right)}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mo>(</mo><msup><mi>γ</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>1</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msup><mo>,</mo><msup><mi>γ</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>2</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msup><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>,</mo><msup><mi>γ</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>n</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msup><mo>)</mo></mrow><mo>∼</mo><msubsup><mi>ℙ</mi><mrow><mo>(</mo><mi>𝔻</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>z</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>z</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>z</mi><mi>n</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><mi>q</mi><mo>)</mo></mrow><mrow><mo>(</mo><msub><mi>U</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>U</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>U</mi><mi>n</mi></msub><mo>)</mo></mrow></msubsup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\left(\gamma^{(1)},\gamma^{(2)},\ldots,\gamma^{(n)}\right)\sim\mathbb{P}_{\left(\mathbb{D};z_{1},z_{2},\ldots,z_{n},q\right)}^{\left(U_{1},U_{2},\ldots,U_{n}\right)}</annotation></semantics></math>, and parametrize <math id="A2.SS9.SSS2.Px1.p29.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\gamma^{(j)}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi>γ</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>j</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\gamma^{(j)}</annotation></semantics></math> by their own capacity in <math id="A2.SS9.SSS2.Px1.p29.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbb{D}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>𝔻</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbb{D}</annotation></semantics></math>. For stopping times <math id="A2.SS9.SSS2.Px1.p29.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbf{t}=\left(t_{1},t_{2},\ldots,t_{n}\right)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>𝐭</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><msub><mi>t</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>t</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>t</mi><mi>n</mi></msub><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbf{t}=\left(t_{1},t_{2},\ldots,t_{n}\right)</annotation></semantics></math>, define</span></p>
</div>
<div id="A2.SS9.SSS2.Px1.p30" class="ltx_para">
<table id="A2.Ex299" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A2.Ex299.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\tilde{U}_{j}=U_{j}\backslash\gamma_{\left[0,t_{j}\right]}^{(j)},\quad\tilde{\gamma}^{(j)}=\gamma^{(j)}\backslash\gamma_{\left[0,t_{j}\right]}^{(j)},\quad\tilde{\Omega}=\mathbb{D}\backslash\bigcup_{j=1}^{n}\gamma_{\left[0,t_{j}\right]}^{(j)}" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>U</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mi>j</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><msub><mi>U</mi><mi>j</mi></msub><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">\</mo><msubsup><mi>γ</mi><mrow><mo>[</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>t</mi><mi>j</mi></msub><mo>]</mo></mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>j</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="1.167em">,</mo><mrow><msup><mover accent="true"><mi>γ</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>j</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msup><mo>=</mo><mrow><msup><mi>γ</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>j</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">\</mo><msubsup><mi>γ</mi><mrow><mo>[</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>t</mi><mi>j</mi></msub><mo>]</mo></mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>j</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="1.167em">,</mo><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi mathvariant="normal">Ω</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>𝔻</mi><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.055em">\</mo><mrow><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">⋃</mo><mrow><mi>j</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>n</mi></munderover><msubsup><mi>γ</mi><mrow><mo>[</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>t</mi><mi>j</mi></msub><mo>]</mo></mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>j</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\tilde{U}_{j}=U_{j}\backslash\gamma_{\left[0,t_{j}\right]}^{(j)},\quad\tilde{\gamma}^{(j)}=\gamma^{(j)}\backslash\gamma_{\left[0,t_{j}\right]}^{(j)},\quad\tilde{\Omega}=\mathbb{D}\backslash\bigcup_{j=1}^{n}\gamma_{\left[0,t_{j}\right]}^{(j)}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
<div id="A2.SS9.SSS2.Px1.p31" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A2.SS9.SSS2.Px1.p31.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.SS9.SSS2.Px1.p31.1.1" class="ltx_text">Then, conditionally on the initial segments <math id="A2.SS9.SSS2.Px1.p31.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\bigcup_{j=1}^{n}\gamma_{\left[0,t_{j}\right]}^{(j)}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msubsup><mo>⋃</mo><mrow><mi>j</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>n</mi></msubsup><msubsup><mi>γ</mi><mrow><mo>[</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>t</mi><mi>j</mi></msub><mo>]</mo></mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>j</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\bigcup_{j=1}^{n}\gamma_{\left[0,t_{j}\right]}^{(j)}</annotation></semantics></math>, we have</span></p>
</div>
<div id="A2.SS9.SSS2.Px1.p32" class="ltx_para">
<table id="A2.Ex300" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A2.Ex300.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\left(\tilde{\gamma}^{(1)},\tilde{\gamma}^{(2)},\ldots,\tilde{\gamma}^{(n)}\right)\sim\mathbb{P}_{\left(\tilde{\Omega};\gamma_{t_{1}}^{(1)},\gamma_{t_{2}}^{(2)},\ldots,\gamma_{t_{n}}^{(n)},q\right)}^{\left(\tilde{U}_{1},\tilde{U}_{2},\ldots,\tilde{U}_{n}\right)}" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mo>(</mo><msup><mover accent="true"><mi>γ</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>1</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msup><mo>,</mo><msup><mover accent="true"><mi>γ</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>2</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msup><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>,</mo><msup><mover accent="true"><mi>γ</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>n</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msup><mo>)</mo></mrow><mo>∼</mo><msubsup><mi>ℙ</mi><mrow><mo>(</mo><mover accent="true"><mi mathvariant="normal">Ω</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mo>,</mo><msubsup><mi>γ</mi><msub><mi>t</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>1</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup><mo>,</mo><msubsup><mi>γ</mi><msub><mi>t</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>2</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>,</mo><msubsup><mi>γ</mi><msub><mi>t</mi><mi>n</mi></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>n</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup><mo>,</mo><mi>q</mi><mo>)</mo></mrow><mrow><mo>(</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>U</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>U</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mn>2</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>U</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mi>n</mi></msub><mo>)</mo></mrow></msubsup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\left(\tilde{\gamma}^{(1)},\tilde{\gamma}^{(2)},\ldots,\tilde{\gamma}^{(n)}\right)\sim\mathbb{P}_{\left(\tilde{\Omega};\gamma_{t_{1}}^{(1)},\gamma_{t_{2}}^{(2)},\ldots,\gamma_{t_{n}}^{(n)},q\right)}^{\left(\tilde{U}_{1},\tilde{U}_{2},\ldots,\tilde{U}_{n}\right)}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
<div id="A2.SS9.SSS2.Px1.p33" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A2.SS9.SSS2.Px1.p33.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.SS9.SSS2.Px1.p33.1.1" class="ltx_text">(iii) Absolute Continuity with respect to independent SLE <math id="A2.SS9.SSS2.Px1.p33.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(\kappa):" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>κ</mi><mo rspace="0.278em" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mphantom></mphantom></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(\kappa):</annotation></semantics></math> Let <math id="A2.SS9.SSS2.Px1.p33.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\left(\gamma^{(1)},\gamma^{(2)},\ldots,\gamma^{(n)}\right)\sim\mathbb{P}_{\left(\mathbb{D};z_{1},z_{2},\ldots,z_{n},0\right)}^{\left(U_{1},U_{2},\ldots,U_{n}\right)}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mo>(</mo><msup><mi>γ</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>1</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msup><mo>,</mo><msup><mi>γ</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>2</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msup><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>,</mo><msup><mi>γ</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>n</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msup><mo>)</mo></mrow><mo>∼</mo><msubsup><mi>ℙ</mi><mrow><mo>(</mo><mi>𝔻</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>z</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>z</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>z</mi><mi>n</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>)</mo></mrow><mrow><mo>(</mo><msub><mi>U</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>U</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>U</mi><mi>n</mi></msub><mo>)</mo></mrow></msubsup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\left(\gamma^{(1)},\gamma^{(2)},\ldots,\gamma^{(n)}\right)\sim\mathbb{P}_{\left(\mathbb{D};z_{1},z_{2},\ldots,z_{n},0\right)}^{\left(U_{1},U_{2},\ldots,U_{n}\right)}</annotation></semantics></math>. Let <math id="A2.SS9.SSS2.Px1.p33.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="z_{j}(t)=e^{i\theta_{j}(t)}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>z</mi><mi>j</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><msup><mi>e</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>θ</mi><mi>j</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">z_{j}(t)=e^{i\theta_{j}(t)}</annotation></semantics></math>, the capacity-parametrized Loewner driving function <math id="A2.SS9.SSS2.Px1.p33.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="t\mapsto\theta_{j}(t)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">↦</mo><mrow><msub><mi>θ</mi><mi>j</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">t\mapsto\theta_{j}(t)</annotation></semantics></math> for <math id="A2.SS9.SSS2.Px1.p33.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\gamma^{(j)}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi>γ</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>j</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\gamma^{(j)}</annotation></semantics></math> satisfies</span></p>
</div>
<div id="A2.SS9.SSS2.Px1.p34" class="ltx_para">
<table id="A2.Ex301" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A2.Ex301X"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A2.Ex301X.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\mathrm{d}\theta_{j}(t)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>θ</mi><mi>j</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\mathrm{d}\theta_{j}(t)</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A2.Ex301X.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=\sqrt{\kappa}\mathrm{d}B_{j}(t)+b_{j}(\boldsymbol{\theta}(t))\mathrm{d}t" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><msqrt><mi>κ</mi></msqrt><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>d</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>B</mi><mi>j</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><msub><mi>b</mi><mi>j</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>𝜽</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>d</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\sqrt{\kappa}\mathrm{d}B_{j}(t)+b_{j}(\boldsymbol{\theta}(t))\mathrm{d}t</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A2.Ex301Xa"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A2.Ex301Xa.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\mathrm{~d}\theta_{k}(t)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>θ</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\mathrm{~d}\theta_{k}(t)</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A2.Ex301Xa.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=\cot\left(\frac{\theta_{k}(t)-\theta_{j}(t)}{2}\right)\mathrm{d}t,\quad k\neq j" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>cot</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>θ</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><msub><mi>θ</mi><mi>j</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mn>2</mn></mfrac></mstyle><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>d</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="1.167em">,</mo><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>≠</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\cot\left(\frac{\theta_{k}(t)-\theta_{j}(t)}{2}\right)\mathrm{d}t,\quad k\neq j</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
<div id="A2.SS9.SSS2.Px1.p35" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A2.SS9.SSS2.Px1.p35.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.SS9.SSS2.Px1.p35.1.1" class="ltx_text">where <math id="A2.SS9.SSS2.Px1.p35.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="B_{j}(t)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>B</mi><mi>j</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">B_{j}(t)</annotation></semantics></math> are independent standard Brownian motions, and <math id="A2.SS9.SSS2.Px1.p35.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="b_{j}(\boldsymbol{\theta})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>b</mi><mi>j</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝜽</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">b_{j}(\boldsymbol{\theta})</annotation></semantics></math> are <math id="A2.SS9.SSS2.Px1.p35.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="C^{2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi>C</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">C^{2}</annotation></semantics></math> functions on the chamber</span></p>
</div>
<div id="A2.SS9.SSS2.Px1.p36" class="ltx_para">
<table id="A2.Ex302" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A2.Ex302.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathfrak{X}^{n}=\left\{\left(\theta_{1},\theta_{2},\ldots,\theta_{n}\right)\in\mathbb{R}^{n}\mid\theta_{1}&lt;\theta_{2}&lt;\cdots&lt;\theta_{n}&lt;\theta_{1}+2\pi\right\}." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msup><mi>𝔛</mi><mi>n</mi></msup><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo>{</mo><mrow><mrow><mo>(</mo><msub><mi>θ</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>θ</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>θ</mi><mi>n</mi></msub><mo>)</mo></mrow><mo>∈</mo><msup><mi>ℝ</mi><mi>n</mi></msup></mrow><mo fence="true" lspace="0em" rspace="0em">∣</mo><mrow><msub><mi>θ</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>&lt;</mo><msub><mi>θ</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo rspace="0.1389em">&lt;</mo><mo lspace="0.1389em" rspace="0.1389em">⋯</mo><mo lspace="0.1389em">&lt;</mo><msub><mi>θ</mi><mi>n</mi></msub><mo>&lt;</mo><mrow><msub><mi>θ</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>+</mo><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>π</mi></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>}</mo></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathfrak{X}^{n}=\left\{\left(\theta_{1},\theta_{2},\ldots,\theta_{n}\right)\in\mathbb{R}^{n}\mid\theta_{1}&lt;\theta_{2}&lt;\cdots&lt;\theta_{n}&lt;\theta_{1}+2\pi\right\}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A2.SS9.SSS2.Px1.p36.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.SS9.SSS2.Px1.p36.1.1" class="ltx_text">Theorem 1.3. For a local multiple radial <math id="A2.SS9.SSS2.Px1.p36.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="SLE(\kappa)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>S</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>L</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>E</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>κ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">SLE(\kappa)</annotation></semantics></math> system in the unit disk <math id="A2.SS9.SSS2.Px1.p36.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbb{D}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>𝔻</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbb{D}</annotation></semantics></math> with boundary points <math id="A2.SS9.SSS2.Px1.p36.m3" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="z_{1}=e^{i\theta_{1}},z_{2}=e^{i\theta_{2}},\ldots,z_{n}=e^{i\theta_{n}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>z</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>=</mo><mi>e</mi><msup><mrow></mrow><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>θ</mi><mn>1</mn></msub></mrow></msup><mo>,</mo><mi>z</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mn>2</mn></msub><mo>=</mo><mi>e</mi><msup><mrow></mrow><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>θ</mi><mn>2</mn></msub></mrow></msup><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>z</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>n</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mi>e</mi><msup><mrow></mrow><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>θ</mi><mi>n</mi></msub></mrow></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">z_{1}=e^{i\theta_{1}},z_{2}=e^{i\theta_{2}},\ldots,z_{n}=e^{i\theta_{n}}</annotation></semantics></math> and a marked point at <math id="A2.SS9.SSS2.Px1.p36.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="q=0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>q</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">q=0</annotation></semantics></math>, there exists a positive partition function <math id="A2.SS9.SSS2.Px1.p36.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\psi(\boldsymbol{\theta})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>ψ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝜽</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\psi(\boldsymbol{\theta})</annotation></semantics></math> such that the drift term <math id="A2.SS9.SSS2.Px1.p36.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="b_{j}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>b</mi><mi>j</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">b_{j}</annotation></semantics></math> in equation (1.2) satisfies</span></p>
</div>
<div id="A2.SS9.SSS2.Px1.p37" class="ltx_para">
<table id="A2.Ex303" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A2.Ex303.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="b_{j}=\kappa\frac{\partial_{j}\psi}{\psi},\quad j=1,2,\ldots,n" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>b</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>j</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mi>κ</mi><mfrac><mrow><msub><mo>∂</mo><mi>j</mi></msub><mi>ψ</mi></mrow><mi>ψ</mi></mfrac><mo rspace="1.167em">,</mo><mi>j</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>2</mn><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>n</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">b_{j}=\kappa\frac{\partial_{j}\psi}{\psi},\quad j=1,2,\ldots,n</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
<div id="A2.SS9.SSS2.Px1.p38" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A2.SS9.SSS2.Px1.p38.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.SS9.SSS2.Px1.p38.1.1" class="ltx_text">Moreover, <math id="A2.SS9.SSS2.Px1.p38.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\psi(\boldsymbol{\theta})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>ψ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝜽</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\psi(\boldsymbol{\theta})</annotation></semantics></math> satisfies the null vector equation</span></p>
</div>
<div id="A2.SS9.SSS2.Px1.p39" class="ltx_para">
<table id="A2.Ex304" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A2.Ex304.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\frac{\kappa}{2}\partial_{ii}\psi+\sum_{j\neq i}\cot\left(\frac{\theta_{j}-\theta_{i}}{2}\right)\partial_{i}\psi+\left(1-\frac{6}{\kappa}\right)\sum_{j\neq i}\frac{1}{4\sin^{2}\left(\frac{\theta_{j}-\theta_{i}}{2}\right)}\psi-h\psi=0" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mrow><mfrac><mi>κ</mi><mn>2</mn></mfrac><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><msub><mo>∂</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>i</mi></mrow></msub><mi>ψ</mi></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.055em">+</mo><mrow><munder><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>j</mi><mo>≠</mo><mi>i</mi></mrow></munder><mrow><mrow><mi>cot</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mfrac><mrow><msub><mi>θ</mi><mi>j</mi></msub><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>θ</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></mrow><mn>2</mn></mfrac><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><msub><mo>∂</mo><mi>i</mi></msub><mi>ψ</mi></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mfrac><mn>6</mn><mi>κ</mi></mfrac></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><munder><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>j</mi><mo>≠</mo><mi>i</mi></mrow></munder><mrow><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mrow><mn>4</mn><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><msup><mi>sin</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mfrac><mrow><msub><mi>θ</mi><mi>j</mi></msub><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>θ</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></mrow><mn>2</mn></mfrac><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mfrac><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>ψ</mi></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>h</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>ψ</mi></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\frac{\kappa}{2}\partial_{ii}\psi+\sum_{j\neq i}\cot\left(\frac{\theta_{j}-\theta_{i}}{2}\right)\partial_{i}\psi+\left(1-\frac{6}{\kappa}\right)\sum_{j\neq i}\frac{1}{4\sin^{2}\left(\frac{\theta_{j}-\theta_{i}}{2}\right)}\psi-h\psi=0</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
<div id="A2.SS9.SSS2.Px1.p40" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A2.SS9.SSS2.Px1.p40.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.SS9.SSS2.Px1.p40.1.1" class="ltx_text">for some constant <math id="A2.SS9.SSS2.Px1.p40.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="h" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>h</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">h</annotation></semantics></math>.
Furthermore, there exists a real constant <math id="A2.SS9.SSS2.Px1.p40.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\omega" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>ω</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\omega</annotation></semantics></math> such that for all <math id="A2.SS9.SSS2.Px1.p40.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\theta\in\mathbb{R}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>θ</mi><mo>∈</mo><mi>ℝ</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\theta\in\mathbb{R}</annotation></semantics></math>,</span></p>
</div>
<div id="A2.SS9.SSS2.Px1.p41" class="ltx_para">
<table id="A2.Ex305" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A2.Ex305.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\psi\left(\theta_{1}+\theta,\ldots,\theta_{n}+\theta\right)=e^{-\omega\theta}\psi\left(\theta_{1},\ldots,\theta_{n}\right)" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>ψ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>θ</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>+</mo><mi>θ</mi></mrow><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>,</mo><mrow><msub><mi>θ</mi><mi>n</mi></msub><mo>+</mo><mi>θ</mi></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><msup><mi>e</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>ω</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>θ</mi></mrow></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>ψ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><msub><mi>θ</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>θ</mi><mi>n</mi></msub><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\psi\left(\theta_{1}+\theta,\ldots,\theta_{n}+\theta\right)=e^{-\omega\theta}\psi\left(\theta_{1},\ldots,\theta_{n}\right)</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
<div id="A2.SS9.SSS2.Px1.p42" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A2.SS9.SSS2.Px1.p42.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.SS9.SSS2.Px1.p42.1.1" class="ltx_text">5</span></p>
</div>
<div id="A2.SS9.SSS2.Px1.p43" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A2.SS9.SSS2.Px1.p43.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.SS9.SSS2.Px1.p43.1.1" class="ltx_text">Conversely, given a positive partition function <math id="A2.SS9.SSS2.Px1.p43.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\psi(\boldsymbol{\theta})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>ψ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝜽</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\psi(\boldsymbol{\theta})</annotation></semantics></math> satisfying both the null vector equation (1.2) and the rotation invariance condition (1.3), consider the multiple radial Loewner chain
the multiple radial SLE <math id="A2.SS9.SSS2.Px1.p43.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(\kappa)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>κ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(\kappa)</annotation></semantics></math> Loewner chain as a normalized conformal map <math id="A2.SS9.SSS2.Px1.p43.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="g_{t}=g_{t}(z)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>g</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><msub><mi>g</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>z</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">g_{t}=g_{t}(z)</annotation></semantics></math>, with the initial condition <math id="A2.SS9.SSS2.Px1.p43.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="g_{0}(z)=z" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>g</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>z</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mi>z</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">g_{0}(z)=z</annotation></semantics></math> and the evolution given by the Loewner equation</span></p>
</div>
<div id="A2.SS9.SSS2.Px1.p44" class="ltx_para">
<table id="A2.Ex306" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A2.Ex306.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\partial_{t}g_{t}(z)=\sum_{j=1}^{n}\nu_{j}(t)g_{t}(z)\frac{z_{j}(t)+g_{t}(z)}{z_{j}(t)-g_{t}(z)},\quad g_{0}(z)=z" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><msub><mo>∂</mo><mi>t</mi></msub><mrow><msub><mi>g</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>z</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.111em">=</mo><mrow><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>j</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>n</mi></munderover><mrow><msub><mi>ν</mi><mi>j</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>g</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>z</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mfrac><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>z</mi><mi>j</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><msub><mi>g</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>z</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>z</mi><mi>j</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><msub><mi>g</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>z</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mfrac></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="1.167em">,</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>g</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>z</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mi>z</mi></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\partial_{t}g_{t}(z)=\sum_{j=1}^{n}\nu_{j}(t)g_{t}(z)\frac{z_{j}(t)+g_{t}(z)}{z_{j}(t)-g_{t}(z)},\quad g_{0}(z)=z</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
<div id="A2.SS9.SSS2.Px1.p45" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A2.SS9.SSS2.Px1.p45.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.SS9.SSS2.Px1.p45.1.1" class="ltx_text">The Loewner chain for the covering map <math id="A2.SS9.SSS2.Px1.p45.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="h_{t}(z)=-i\log\left(g_{t}\left(e^{iz}\right)\right)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>h</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>z</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>g</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><msup><mi>e</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>z</mi></mrow></msup><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">h_{t}(z)=-i\log\left(g_{t}\left(e^{iz}\right)\right)</annotation></semantics></math> is given by</span></p>
</div>
<div id="A2.SS9.SSS2.Px1.p46" class="ltx_para">
<table id="A2.Ex307" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A2.Ex307.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\partial_{t}h_{t}(z)=\sum_{j=1}^{n}\nu_{j}(t)\cot\left(\frac{h_{t}(z)-\theta_{j}(t)}{2}\right),\quad h_{0}(z)=z" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><msub><mo>∂</mo><mi>t</mi></msub><mrow><msub><mi>h</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>z</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.111em">=</mo><mrow><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>j</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>n</mi></munderover><mrow><msub><mi>ν</mi><mi>j</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mi>cot</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mfrac><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>h</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>z</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><msub><mi>θ</mi><mi>j</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mn>2</mn></mfrac><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="1.167em">,</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>h</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>z</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mi>z</mi></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\partial_{t}h_{t}(z)=\sum_{j=1}^{n}\nu_{j}(t)\cot\left(\frac{h_{t}(z)-\theta_{j}(t)}{2}\right),\quad h_{0}(z)=z</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
<div id="A2.SS9.SSS2.Px1.p47" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A2.SS9.SSS2.Px1.p47.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.SS9.SSS2.Px1.p47.1.1" class="ltx_text">driven by the functions <math id="A2.SS9.SSS2.Px1.p47.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\theta_{j}(t)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>θ</mi><mi>j</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\theta_{j}(t)</annotation></semantics></math>, for <math id="A2.SS9.SSS2.Px1.p47.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="j=1,\ldots,n" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>j</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>n</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">j=1,\ldots,n</annotation></semantics></math>, evolving as</span></p>
</div>
<div id="A2.SS9.SSS2.Px1.p48" class="ltx_para">
<table id="A2.Ex308" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A2.Ex308.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="d\theta_{j}=\nu_{j}(t)\frac{\partial_{j}\log\psi(\boldsymbol{\theta})}{\partial\theta_{j}}dt+\sum_{k\neq j}\nu_{k}(t)\cot\left(\frac{\theta_{j}-\theta_{k}}{2}\right)dt+\sqrt{\kappa}dB_{t}^{j}" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>θ</mi><mi>j</mi></msub></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>ν</mi><mi>j</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mfrac><mrow><msub><mo>∂</mo><mi>j</mi></msub><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><mrow><mi>ψ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝜽</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mrow><mo>∂</mo><msub><mi>θ</mi><mi>j</mi></msub></mrow></mfrac><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>d</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow><mo rspace="0.055em">+</mo><mrow><munder><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>≠</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow></munder><mrow><msub><mi>ν</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mi>cot</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mfrac><mrow><msub><mi>θ</mi><mi>j</mi></msub><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>θ</mi><mi>k</mi></msub></mrow><mn>2</mn></mfrac><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>d</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><msqrt><mi>κ</mi></msqrt><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>d</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>B</mi><mi>t</mi><mi>j</mi></msubsup></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">d\theta_{j}=\nu_{j}(t)\frac{\partial_{j}\log\psi(\boldsymbol{\theta})}{\partial\theta_{j}}dt+\sum_{k\neq j}\nu_{k}(t)\cot\left(\frac{\theta_{j}-\theta_{k}}{2}\right)dt+\sqrt{\kappa}dB_{t}^{j}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
<div id="A2.SS9.SSS2.Px1.p49" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A2.SS9.SSS2.Px1.p49.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.SS9.SSS2.Px1.p49.1.1" class="ltx_text">where <math id="A2.SS9.SSS2.Px1.p49.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\boldsymbol{\nu}=\left(\nu_{1},\ldots,\nu_{n}\right)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>𝝂</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><msub><mi>ν</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>ν</mi><mi>n</mi></msub><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\boldsymbol{\nu}=\left(\nu_{1},\ldots,\nu_{n}\right)</annotation></semantics></math> is a set of capacity parametrizations, with each <math id="A2.SS9.SSS2.Px1.p49.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\nu_{i}:[0,\infty)\rightarrow[0,\infty)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>ν</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">∞</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">∞</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\nu_{i}:[0,\infty)\rightarrow[0,\infty)</annotation></semantics></math> assumed to be measurable. Here, <math id="A2.SS9.SSS2.Px1.p49.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="B^{j}(t)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msup><mi>B</mi><mi>j</mi></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">B^{j}(t)</annotation></semantics></math> denotes a set of independent Brownian motion.</span></p>
</div>
<div id="A2.SS9.SSS2.Px1.p50" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A2.SS9.SSS2.Px1.p50.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.SS9.SSS2.Px1.p50.1.1" class="ltx_text">This process defines a local multiple radial SLE <math id="A2.SS9.SSS2.Px1.p50.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(\kappa)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>κ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(\kappa)</annotation></semantics></math> system.</span></p>
</div>
<div id="A2.SS9.SSS2.Px1.p51" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A2.SS9.SSS2.Px1.p51.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.SS9.SSS2.Px1.p51.1.1" class="ltx_text">∎</span></p>
</div>
</div>
<div id="A2.SS9.SSS2.Px1.p52" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent"><span class="ltx_inline-block"><svg id="A2.SS9.SSS2.Px1.p52.pic1" class="ltx_picture" height="147.27" overflow="visible" version="1.1" viewBox="0 0 429.64 147.27" width="429.64"><g style="--ltx-stroke-color:#000000;--ltx-fill-color:#000000;" fill="#000000" stroke="#000000" stroke-width="0.4pt" transform="translate(0,147.27) matrix(1 0 0 -1 0 0)"><g style="--ltx-fill-color:#4D4D4D;" fill="#4D4D4D" fill-opacity="1.0"><path style="stroke:none" d="M 0 4.63 L 0 142.64 C 0 145.19 2.07 147.27 4.63 147.27 L 425.01 147.27 C 427.56 147.27 429.64 145.19 429.64 142.64 L 429.64 4.63 C 429.64 2.07 427.56 0 425.01 0 L 4.63 0 C 2.07 0 0 2.07 0 4.63 Z"></path></g><g style="--ltx-fill-color:#F9F9F9;" fill="#F9F9F9" fill-opacity="1.0"><path style="stroke:none" d="M 0.69 4.63 L 0.69 128.4 L 428.94 128.4 L 428.94 4.63 C 428.94 2.45 427.18 0.69 425.01 0.69 L 4.63 0.69 C 2.45 0.69 0.69 2.45 0.69 4.63 Z"></path></g><g fill-opacity="1.0" transform="matrix(1.0 0.0 0.0 1.0 20.38 133.03)"><foreignObject style="--ltx-fo-width:24.44em;--ltx-fo-height:0.69em;--ltx-fo-depth:0em;font-size:10pt;" height="9.61" overflow="visible" transform="matrix(1 0 0 -1 0 9.61)" width="338.18"><span class="ltx_foreignobject_container"><span class="ltx_foreignobject_content">
<span id="A2.SS9.SSS2.Px1.p52.pic1.1" class="ltx_inline-block ltx_minipage ltx_align_bottom" style="width:24.44em;">
<span id="A2.SS9.SSS2.Px1.p52.pic1.1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.SS9.SSS2.Px1.p52.pic1.1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold" style="--ltx-fg-color:#FFFFFF;">Rubric</span></span>
</span></span></span></foreignObject></g><g fill-opacity="1.0" transform="matrix(1.0 0.0 0.0 1.0 20.38 14.66)"><foreignObject style="--ltx-fo-width:33.06em;--ltx-fo-height:7.37em;--ltx-fo-depth:0.16em;font-size:10pt;" height="104.09" overflow="visible" transform="matrix(1 0 0 -1 0 101.93)" width="457.46"><span class="ltx_foreignobject_container"><span class="ltx_foreignobject_content">
<span id="A2.SS9.SSS2.Px1.p52.pic1.2" class="ltx_inline-block ltx_minipage ltx_align_bottom" style="width:33.06em;">
<span id="A2.I37" class="ltx_enumerate">
<span id="A2.I37.i1" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">1.</span> 
<span id="A2.I37.i1.p1" class="ltx_para">
<span id="A2.I37.i1.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.I37.i1.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:80%;--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">Specifying the radial Loewner equation in the unit disk.</span></span>
</span></span>
<span id="A2.I37.i2" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">2.</span> 
<span id="A2.I37.i2.p1" class="ltx_para">
<span id="A2.I37.i2.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.I37.i2.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:80%;--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">Define the local compatible measure.</span></span>
</span></span>
<span id="A2.I37.i3" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">3.</span> 
<span id="A2.I37.i3.p1" class="ltx_para">
<span id="A2.I37.i3.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.I37.i3.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:80%;--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">Derive the driving SDEs and commutation relations.</span></span>
</span></span>
</span>
<span id="A2.SS9.SSS2.Px1.p52.pic1.2.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.SS9.SSS2.Px1.p52.pic1.2.1.1" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:80%;--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">Each item is worth 1 point.</span></span>
</span></span></span></foreignObject></g></g></svg></span>
</div>
<div id="A2.SS9.SSS2.Px1.p53" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent"><span class="ltx_inline-block"><svg id="A2.SS9.SSS2.Px1.p53.pic1" class="ltx_picture" height="54.13" overflow="visible" version="1.1" viewBox="0 0 429.64 54.13" width="429.64"><g style="--ltx-stroke-color:#000000;--ltx-fill-color:#000000;" fill="#000000" stroke="#000000" stroke-width="0.4pt" transform="translate(0,54.13) matrix(1 0 0 -1 0 0)"><g style="--ltx-fill-color:#5A996B;" fill="#5A996B" fill-opacity="1.0"><path style="stroke:none" d="M 0 4.63 L 0 49.51 C 0 52.06 2.07 54.13 4.63 54.13 L 425.01 54.13 C 427.56 54.13 429.64 52.06 429.64 49.51 L 429.64 4.63 C 429.64 2.07 427.56 0 425.01 0 L 4.63 0 C 2.07 0 0 2.07 0 4.63 Z"></path></g><g style="--ltx-fill-color:#F6FFF9;" fill="#F6FFF9" fill-opacity="1.0"><path style="stroke:none" d="M 0.69 4.63 L 0.69 35.38 L 428.94 35.38 L 428.94 4.63 C 428.94 2.45 427.18 0.69 425.01 0.69 L 4.63 0.69 C 2.45 0.69 0.69 2.45 0.69 4.63 Z"></path></g><g fill-opacity="1.0" transform="matrix(1.0 0.0 0.0 1.0 20.38 40.01)"><foreignObject style="--ltx-fo-width:24.44em;--ltx-fo-height:0.69em;--ltx-fo-depth:0em;font-size:10pt;" height="9.49" overflow="visible" transform="matrix(1 0 0 -1 0 9.49)" width="338.18"><span class="ltx_foreignobject_container"><span class="ltx_foreignobject_content">
