</span></span></span></foreignObject></g></g></svg></span>
</div>
</section>
</section>
<section id="A2.SS11.SSS2" class="ltx_subsubsection">
<h4 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsubsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsubsection">(b) </span>Developing unifying theories</h4>

<section id="A2.SS11.SSS2.Px1" class="ltx_paragraph">
<h5 class="ltx_title ltx_title_paragraph" style="--ltx-fg-color:#FF0000;">Problem 11b1 </h5>

<div id="A2.SS11.SSS2.Px1.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A2.SS11.SSS2.Px1.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.SS11.SSS2.Px1.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text"></span>
<br class="ltx_break" style="--ltx-break-space:-10.0pt;"></p>
</div>
<div id="A2.SS11.SSS2.Px1.p2" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent"><span class="ltx_inline-block"><svg id="A2.SS11.SSS2.Px1.p2.pic1" class="ltx_picture" height="454.39" overflow="visible" version="1.1" viewBox="0 0 429.64 454.39" width="429.64"><g style="--ltx-stroke-color:#000000;--ltx-fill-color:#000000;" fill="#000000" stroke="#000000" stroke-width="0.4pt" transform="translate(0,454.39) matrix(1 0 0 -1 0 0)"><g style="--ltx-fill-color:#3D6666;" fill="#3D6666" fill-opacity="1.0"><path style="stroke:none" d="M 0 4.63 L 0 449.76 C 0 452.32 2.07 454.39 4.63 454.39 L 425.01 454.39 C 427.56 454.39 429.64 452.32 429.64 449.76 L 429.64 4.63 C 429.64 2.07 427.56 0 425.01 0 L 4.63 0 C 2.07 0 0 2.07 0 4.63 Z"></path></g><g style="--ltx-fill-color:#F9F9F9;" fill="#F9F9F9" fill-opacity="1.0"><path style="stroke:none" d="M 0.69 4.63 L 0.69 435.52 L 428.94 435.52 L 428.94 4.63 C 428.94 2.45 427.18 0.69 425.01 0.69 L 4.63 0.69 C 2.45 0.69 0.69 2.45 0.69 4.63 Z"></path></g><g fill-opacity="1.0" transform="matrix(1.0 0.0 0.0 1.0 20.38 440.15)"><foreignObject style="--ltx-fo-width:24.44em;--ltx-fo-height:0.69em;--ltx-fo-depth:0em;font-size:10pt;" height="9.61" overflow="visible" transform="matrix(1 0 0 -1 0 9.61)" width="338.18"><span class="ltx_foreignobject_container"><span class="ltx_foreignobject_content">
<span id="A2.SS11.SSS2.Px1.p2.pic1.1" class="ltx_inline-block ltx_minipage ltx_align_bottom" style="width:24.44em;">
<span id="A2.SS11.SSS2.Px1.p2.pic1.1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.SS11.SSS2.Px1.p2.pic1.1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold" style="--ltx-fg-color:#FFFFFF;">Problem</span></span>
</span></span></span></foreignObject></g><g fill-opacity="1.0" transform="matrix(1.0 0.0 0.0 1.0 20.38 14.66)"><foreignObject style="--ltx-fo-width:32.01em;--ltx-fo-height:29.56em;--ltx-fo-depth:0.16em;font-size:10pt;" height="411.21" overflow="visible" transform="matrix(1 0 0 -1 0 409.06)" width="442.93"><span class="ltx_foreignobject_container"><span class="ltx_foreignobject_content">
<span id="A2.SS11.SSS2.Px1.p2.pic1.2" class="ltx_inline-block ltx_minipage ltx_align_bottom" style="width:32.01em;">
<span id="A2.SS11.SSS2.Px1.p2.pic1.2.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.SS11.SSS2.Px1.p2.pic1.2.1.1" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:80%;--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">Consider the following three “twist” operations:</span></span>
<span id="A2.I42" class="ltx_enumerate">
<span id="A2.I42.ix1" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">(1)</span> 
<span id="A2.I42.ix1.p1" class="ltx_para">
<span id="A2.I42.ix1.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.I42.ix1.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:80%;--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">If </span><math id="A2.I42.ix1.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Sigma" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" mathsize="0.800em" mathvariant="normal">Σ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Sigma</annotation></semantics></math><span id="A2.I42.ix1.p1.1.2" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:80%;--ltx-fg-color:#000000;"> is an oriented surface and </span><math id="A2.I42.ix1.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\gamma\subset\Sigma" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" mathsize="0.800em">γ</mi><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" mathsize="0.800em">⊂</mo><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" mathsize="0.800em" mathvariant="normal">Σ</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\gamma\subset\Sigma</annotation></semantics></math><span id="A2.I42.ix1.p1.1.3" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:80%;--ltx-fg-color:#000000;"> is an embedded curve, one can perform a Dehn twist along </span><math id="A2.I42.ix1.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\gamma" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" mathsize="0.800em">γ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\gamma</annotation></semantics></math><span id="A2.I42.ix1.p1.1.4" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:80%;--ltx-fg-color:#000000;"> to create a mapping class of </span><math id="A2.I42.ix1.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Sigma" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" mathsize="0.800em" mathvariant="normal">Σ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Sigma</annotation></semantics></math><span id="A2.I42.ix1.p1.1.5" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:80%;--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">.</span></span>
</span></span>
<span id="A2.I42.ix2" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">(2)</span> 
<span id="A2.I42.ix2.p1" class="ltx_para">
<span id="A2.I42.ix2.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.I42.ix2.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:80%;--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">If </span><math id="A2.I42.ix2.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="M" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" mathsize="0.800em">M</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">M</annotation></semantics></math><span id="A2.I42.ix2.p1.1.2" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:80%;--ltx-fg-color:#000000;"> is an oriented </span><math id="A2.I42.ix2.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="3" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" mathsize="0.800em">3</mn><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">3</annotation></semantics></math><span id="A2.I42.ix2.p1.1.3" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:80%;--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">-manifold and </span><math id="A2.I42.ix2.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="T\subset M" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" mathsize="0.800em">T</mi><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" mathsize="0.800em">⊂</mo><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" mathsize="0.800em">M</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">T\subset M</annotation></semantics></math><span id="A2.I42.ix2.p1.1.4" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:80%;--ltx-fg-color:#000000;"> is an embedded torus, </span><math id="A2.I42.ix2.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\gamma\subset T" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" mathsize="0.800em">γ</mi><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" mathsize="0.800em">⊂</mo><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" mathsize="0.800em">T</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\gamma\subset T</annotation></semantics></math><span id="A2.I42.ix2.p1.1.5" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:80%;--ltx-fg-color:#000000;"> is an essential simple closed curve, one can perform a Dehn twist along </span><math id="A2.I42.ix2.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="T" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" mathsize="0.800em">T</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">T</annotation></semantics></math><span id="A2.I42.ix2.p1.1.6" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:80%;--ltx-fg-color:#000000;"> in the </span><math id="A2.I42.ix2.p1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\gamma" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" mathsize="0.800em">γ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\gamma</annotation></semantics></math><span id="A2.I42.ix2.p1.1.7" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:80%;--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">-direction to create a mapping class of </span><math id="A2.I42.ix2.p1.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="M" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" mathsize="0.800em">M</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">M</annotation></semantics></math><span id="A2.I42.ix2.p1.1.8" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:80%;--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">.</span></span>
</span></span>
<span id="A2.I42.ix3" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">(3)</span> 
<span id="A2.I42.ix3.p1" class="ltx_para">
<span id="A2.I42.ix3.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.I42.ix3.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:80%;--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">If </span><math id="A2.I42.ix3.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="X" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" mathsize="0.800em">X</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">X</annotation></semantics></math><span id="A2.I42.ix3.p1.1.2" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:80%;--ltx-fg-color:#000000;"> is a smooth oriented </span><math id="A2.I42.ix3.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="4" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" mathsize="0.800em">4</mn><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">4</annotation></semantics></math><span id="A2.I42.ix3.p1.1.3" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:80%;--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">-manifold and </span><math id="A2.I42.ix3.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="S\subset X" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" mathsize="0.800em">S</mi><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" mathsize="0.800em">⊂</mo><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" mathsize="0.800em">X</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">S\subset X</annotation></semantics></math><span id="A2.I42.ix3.p1.1.4" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:80%;--ltx-fg-color:#000000;"> is smoothly embedded </span><math id="A2.I42.ix3.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="2" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" mathsize="0.800em">2</mn><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">2</annotation></semantics></math><span id="A2.I42.ix3.p1.1.5" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:80%;--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">-sphere with self-intersection number </span><math id="A2.I42.ix3.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="-2" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" mathsize="0.800em">−</mo><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" mathsize="0.800em">2</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">-2</annotation></semantics></math><span id="A2.I42.ix3.p1.1.6" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:80%;--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">, one can construct a mapping class of </span><math id="A2.I42.ix3.p1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="X" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" mathsize="0.800em">X</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">X</annotation></semantics></math><span id="A2.I42.ix3.p1.1.7" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:80%;--ltx-fg-color:#000000;"> obtained by the identity outside a tubular neighborhood </span><math id="A2.I42.ix3.p1.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\nu S" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" mathsize="0.800em">ν</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" mathsize="0.800em">S</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\nu S</annotation></semantics></math><span id="A2.I42.ix3.p1.1.8" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:80%;--ltx-fg-color:#000000;"> of </span><math id="A2.I42.ix3.p1.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="S" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" mathsize="0.800em">S</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">S</annotation></semantics></math><span id="A2.I42.ix3.p1.1.9" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:80%;--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">, and the time </span><math id="A2.I42.ix3.p1.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\pi" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" mathsize="0.800em">π</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\pi</annotation></semantics></math><span id="A2.I42.ix3.p1.1.10" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:80%;--ltx-fg-color:#000000;"> map of the geodesic flow on </span><math id="A2.I42.ix3.p1.m10" class="ltx_Math" alttext="DTS^{2}\cong\nu S" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" mathsize="0.800em">D</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" mathsize="0.800em">T</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" mathsize="0.800em">S</mi><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" mathsize="0.800em">2</mn></msup></mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" mathsize="0.800em">≅</mo><mrow><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" mathsize="0.800em">ν</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" mathsize="0.800em">S</mi></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">DTS^{2}\cong\nu S</annotation></semantics></math><span id="A2.I42.ix3.p1.1.11" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:80%;--ltx-fg-color:#000000;"> inside </span><math id="A2.I42.ix3.p1.m11" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\nu S" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" mathsize="0.800em">ν</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" mathsize="0.800em">S</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\nu S</annotation></semantics></math><span id="A2.I42.ix3.p1.1.12" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:80%;--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">, where </span><math id="A2.I42.ix3.p1.m12" class="ltx_Math" alttext="DTS^{2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" mathsize="0.800em">D</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" mathsize="0.800em">T</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" mathsize="0.800em">S</mi><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" mathsize="0.800em">2</mn></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">DTS^{2}</annotation></semantics></math><span id="A2.I42.ix3.p1.1.13" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:80%;--ltx-fg-color:#000000;"> denotes the unit disk bundle of the tangent bundle of the unit sphere </span><math id="A2.I42.ix3.p1.m13" class="ltx_Math" alttext="S^{2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" mathsize="0.800em">S</mi><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" mathsize="0.800em">2</mn></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">S^{2}</annotation></semantics></math><span id="A2.I42.ix3.p1.1.14" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:80%;--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">.</span></span>
</span></span>
</span>
<span id="A2.SS11.SSS2.Px1.p2.pic1.2.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.SS11.SSS2.Px1.p2.pic1.2.2.1" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:80%;--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">What is essentially going on that allows one to perform such twist operations? Please:</span></span>
<span id="A2.I43" class="ltx_enumerate">
<span id="A2.I43.ix1" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">i.</span> 
<span id="A2.I43.ix1.p1" class="ltx_para">
<span id="A2.I43.ix1.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.I43.ix1.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:80%;--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">Formulate a generalization of the twist operation that encompasses all three operations above as special cases.</span></span>
</span></span>
<span id="A2.I43.ix2" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">ii.</span> 
<span id="A2.I43.ix2.p1" class="ltx_para">
<span id="A2.I43.ix2.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.I43.ix2.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:80%;--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">Formulate a generalization of the first two twist operations that is not a generalization of the third operation.</span></span>
</span></span>
</span><span class="ltx_inline-block"><svg id="A2.SS11.SSS2.Px1.p2.pic1.pic1" class="ltx_picture" color="#FF0000" height="18.24" overflow="visible" style="vertical-align:-4.1px" version="1.1" viewBox="0 0 18.24 18.24" width="18.24"><g style="--ltx-stroke-color:#FF0000;--ltx-fill-color:#FF0000;" fill="#FF0000" stroke="#FF0000" stroke-width="1.8pt" transform="translate(0,18.24) matrix(1 0 0 -1 0 0) translate(1.25,0) translate(0,1.25)"><path style="fill:none" d="M 0 0 L 15.75 15.75 M 0 15.75 L 15.75 0"></path></g></svg></span>
<span id="A2.SS11.SSS2.Px1.p2.pic1.2.3" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.SS11.SSS2.Px1.p2.pic1.2.3.1" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:80%;--ltx-fg-color:#FF0000;">GPT-5 thinking failed</span></span>
<span id="A2.SS11.SSS2.Px1.p2.pic1.2.4" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.SS11.SSS2.Px1.p2.pic1.2.4.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic" style="font-size:80%;--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">Proposed by Qiuyu Ren</span></span>
</span></span></span></foreignObject></g></g></svg></span>
</div>
<div id="A2.SS11.SSS2.Px1.1" class="ltx_proof">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_font_italic ltx_title_proof"><span id="A2.SS11.SSS2.Px1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Response of GPT-5-thinking</span>.</h6>
<div id="A2.SS11.SSS2.Px1.p3" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A2.SS11.SSS2.Px1.p3.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.SS11.SSS2.Px1.p3.1.1" class="ltx_text">The common feature behind all three “twist” operations is the existence of a submanifold with a well–understood neighborhood, so that there is a canonical compactly supported diffeomorphism of the fiber (often a Dehn twist–type map) which can be applied fiberwise and extended by the identity outside.</span></p>
</div>
<div id="A2.SS11.SSS2.Px1.p4" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A2.SS11.SSS2.Px1.p4.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.SS11.SSS2.Px1.p4.1.1" class="ltx_text">(i) One generalization that encompasses all three can be stated as follows.
Let <math id="A2.SS11.SSS2.Px1.p4.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="M" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>M</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">M</annotation></semantics></math> be a smooth oriented manifold, and let <math id="A2.SS11.SSS2.Px1.p4.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="E\subset M" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>E</mi><mo>⊂</mo><mi>M</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">E\subset M</annotation></semantics></math> be an embedded sub-bundle <math id="A2.SS11.SSS2.Px1.p4.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\pi:E\to B" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>π</mi><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mrow><mi>E</mi><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><mi>B</mi></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\pi:E\to B</annotation></semantics></math> with compact fiber <math id="A2.SS11.SSS2.Px1.p4.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="F" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>F</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">F</annotation></semantics></math> and trivialized collar of <math id="A2.SS11.SSS2.Px1.p4.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\partial E" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo>∂</mo><mi>E</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\partial E</annotation></semantics></math>. Suppose <math id="A2.SS11.SSS2.Px1.p4.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\tau_{F}\in\mathrm{Diff}_{c}(F,\partial F)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>τ</mi><mi>F</mi></msub><mo>∈</mo><mrow><msub><mi>Diff</mi><mi>c</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>F</mi><mo rspace="0em">,</mo><mrow><mo>∂</mo><mi>F</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\tau_{F}\in\mathrm{Diff}_{c}(F,\partial F)</annotation></semantics></math> is a compactly supported diffeomorphism of <math id="A2.SS11.SSS2.Px1.p4.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="F" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>F</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">F</annotation></semantics></math> equal to the identity near <math id="A2.SS11.SSS2.Px1.p4.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\partial F" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo>∂</mo><mi>F</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\partial F</annotation></semantics></math>. Using a bump function in the normal direction, apply <math id="A2.SS11.SSS2.Px1.p4.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\tau_{F}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>τ</mi><mi>F</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\tau_{F}</annotation></semantics></math> fiberwise (constant along <math id="A2.SS11.SSS2.Px1.p4.m10" class="ltx_Math" alttext="B" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>B</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">B</annotation></semantics></math>), tapering to the identity near <math id="A2.SS11.SSS2.Px1.p4.m11" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\partial E" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo>∂</mo><mi>E</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\partial E</annotation></semantics></math>, and extend by the identity outside <math id="A2.SS11.SSS2.Px1.p4.m12" class="ltx_Math" alttext="E" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>E</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">E</annotation></semantics></math>. The resulting mapping class <math id="A2.SS11.SSS2.Px1.p4.m13" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\tau_{(E,\pi,\tau_{F})}\in\pi_{0}(\mathrm{Diff}_{c}(M))" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>τ</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>E</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>π</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>τ</mi><mi>F</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msub><mo>∈</mo><mrow><msub><mi>π</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>Diff</mi><mi>c</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>M</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\tau_{(E,\pi,\tau_{F})}\in\pi_{0}(\mathrm{Diff}_{c}(M))</annotation></semantics></math> depends only on the data up to isotopy.</span></p>
</div>
<div id="A2.SS11.SSS2.Px1.p5" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A2.SS11.SSS2.Px1.p5.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.SS11.SSS2.Px1.p5.1.1" class="ltx_text">Specializations:
- If <math id="A2.SS11.SSS2.Px1.p5.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="M=\Sigma^{2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>M</mi><mo>=</mo><msup><mi mathvariant="normal">Σ</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">M=\Sigma^{2}</annotation></semantics></math>, <math id="A2.SS11.SSS2.Px1.p5.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="E=\nu\gamma\cong S^{1}\times I" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>E</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>ν</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>γ</mi></mrow><mo>≅</mo><mrow><msup><mi>S</mi><mn>1</mn></msup><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><mi>I</mi></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">E=\nu\gamma\cong S^{1}\times I</annotation></semantics></math> viewed as a bundle over <math id="A2.SS11.SSS2.Px1.p5.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\gamma" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>γ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\gamma</annotation></semantics></math> with fiber an interval, and <math id="A2.SS11.SSS2.Px1.p5.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\tau_{F}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>τ</mi><mi>F</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\tau_{F}</annotation></semantics></math> the standard annular Dehn twist, one recovers the classical surface Dehn twist.
- If <math id="A2.SS11.SSS2.Px1.p5.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="M^{3}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi>M</mi><mn>3</mn></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">M^{3}</annotation></semantics></math> contains a torus <math id="A2.SS11.SSS2.Px1.p5.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="T" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>T</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">T</annotation></semantics></math> with essential curve <math id="A2.SS11.SSS2.Px1.p5.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\gamma" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>γ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\gamma</annotation></semantics></math>, <math id="A2.SS11.SSS2.Px1.p5.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="E=\nu T\cong T^{2}\times I" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>E</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>ν</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>T</mi></mrow><mo>≅</mo><mrow><msup><mi>T</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><mi>I</mi></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">E=\nu T\cong T^{2}\times I</annotation></semantics></math> with fiber <math id="A2.SS11.SSS2.Px1.p5.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="T^{2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi>T</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">T^{2}</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="A2.SS11.SSS2.Px1.p5.m10" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\tau_{F}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>τ</mi><mi>F</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\tau_{F}</annotation></semantics></math> the torus Dehn twist along <math id="A2.SS11.SSS2.Px1.p5.m11" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\gamma" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>γ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\gamma</annotation></semantics></math>, one recovers the torus twist.
- If <math id="A2.SS11.SSS2.Px1.p5.m12" class="ltx_Math" alttext="X^{4}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi>X</mi><mn>4</mn></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">X^{4}</annotation></semantics></math> contains a smoothly embedded <math id="A2.SS11.SSS2.Px1.p5.m13" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(-2)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(-2)</annotation></semantics></math>–sphere <math id="A2.SS11.SSS2.Px1.p5.m14" class="ltx_Math" alttext="S" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>S</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">S</annotation></semantics></math>, <math id="A2.SS11.SSS2.Px1.p5.m15" class="ltx_Math" alttext="E" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>E</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">E</annotation></semantics></math> is the unit disk bundle of <math id="A2.SS11.SSS2.Px1.p5.m16" class="ltx_Math" alttext="TS^{2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>T</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>S</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">TS^{2}</annotation></semantics></math> with fiber <math id="A2.SS11.SSS2.Px1.p5.m17" class="ltx_Math" alttext="D^{2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi>D</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">D^{2}</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="A2.SS11.SSS2.Px1.p5.m18" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\tau_{F}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>τ</mi><mi>F</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\tau_{F}</annotation></semantics></math> the time–<math id="A2.SS11.SSS2.Px1.p5.m19" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\pi" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>π</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\pi</annotation></semantics></math> geodesic flow map, one recovers the 4–dimensional sphere twist.</span></p>
</div>
<div id="A2.SS11.SSS2.Px1.p6" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A2.SS11.SSS2.Px1.p6.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.SS11.SSS2.Px1.p6.1.1" class="ltx_text">(ii) A generalization of (1) and (2) that is not a generalization of (3) is the cut–and–reglue construction along a two–sided hypersurface.
Let <math id="A2.SS11.SSS2.Px1.p6.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="M^{n}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi>M</mi><mi>n</mi></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">M^{n}</annotation></semantics></math> be an oriented manifold and <math id="A2.SS11.SSS2.Px1.p6.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="H^{n-1}\subset M" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msup><mi>H</mi><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup><mo>⊂</mo><mi>M</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">H^{n-1}\subset M</annotation></semantics></math> a two–sided embedded hypersurface with a product neighborhood <math id="A2.SS11.SSS2.Px1.p6.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\nu H\cong H\times[-1,1]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>ν</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>H</mi></mrow><mo>≅</mo><mrow><mi>H</mi><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo>,</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\nu H\cong H\times[-1,1]</annotation></semantics></math>. Given a mapping class <math id="A2.SS11.SSS2.Px1.p6.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="[\phi]\in\mathrm{MCG}(H,\partial H)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mi>ϕ</mi><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mi>MCG</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>H</mi><mo rspace="0em">,</mo><mrow><mo>∂</mo><mi>H</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">[\phi]\in\mathrm{MCG}(H,\partial H)</annotation></semantics></math> supported away from <math id="A2.SS11.SSS2.Px1.p6.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\partial H" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo>∂</mo><mi>H</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\partial H</annotation></semantics></math>, define a self–homeomorphism of <math id="A2.SS11.SSS2.Px1.p6.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="M" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>M</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">M</annotation></semantics></math> by cutting along <math id="A2.SS11.SSS2.Px1.p6.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="H" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>H</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">H</annotation></semantics></math> and regluing by <math id="A2.SS11.SSS2.Px1.p6.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\phi" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>ϕ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\phi</annotation></semantics></math>. Equivalently, realize it by a diffeomorphism supported in <math id="A2.SS11.SSS2.Px1.p6.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\nu H" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>ν</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>H</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\nu H</annotation></semantics></math> that restricts to <math id="A2.SS11.SSS2.Px1.p6.m10" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\phi" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>ϕ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\phi</annotation></semantics></math> on <math id="A2.SS11.SSS2.Px1.p6.m11" class="ltx_Math" alttext="H\times\{0\}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>H</mi><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mn>0</mn><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">H\times\{0\}</annotation></semantics></math> and is the identity near <math id="A2.SS11.SSS2.Px1.p6.m12" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\partial(\nu H)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo>∂</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>ν</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>H</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\partial(\nu H)</annotation></semantics></math>.</span></p>
</div>
<div id="A2.SS11.SSS2.Px1.p7" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A2.SS11.SSS2.Px1.p7.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.SS11.SSS2.Px1.p7.1.1" class="ltx_text">In the case <math id="A2.SS11.SSS2.Px1.p7.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="n=2" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">n=2</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="A2.SS11.SSS2.Px1.p7.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="H" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>H</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">H</annotation></semantics></math> an annulus around a simple closed curve, one recovers the surface Dehn twist. In the case <math id="A2.SS11.SSS2.Px1.p7.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="n=3" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>3</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">n=3</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="A2.SS11.SSS2.Px1.p7.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="H" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>H</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">H</annotation></semantics></math> a torus, one recovers the torus twist. This framework does not apply to the <math id="A2.SS11.SSS2.Px1.p7.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(-2)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(-2)</annotation></semantics></math>–sphere twist, which is supported near a codimension–two submanifold and uses the geodesic–flow model rather than cutting along a hypersurface.
∎</span></p>
</div>
</div>
<div id="A2.SS11.SSS2.Px1.2" class="ltx_proof">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_font_italic ltx_title_proof"><span id="A2.SS11.SSS2.Px1.2.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Standard Solution</span>.</h6>
<div id="A2.SS11.SSS2.Px1.p8" class="ltx_para">
<ol id="A2.I44" class="ltx_enumerate">
<li id="A2.I44.ix1" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">i.</span> 
<div id="A2.I44.ix1.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A2.I44.ix1.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Let <math id="A2.I44.ix1.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="M" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>M</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">M</annotation></semantics></math> be a smooth oriented manifold and <math id="A2.I44.ix1.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="N\subset M" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>N</mi><mo>⊂</mo><mi>M</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">N\subset M</annotation></semantics></math> be a closed embedded oriented submanifold. Given a (say smooth) mapping class <math id="A2.I44.ix1.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\phi" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>ϕ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\phi</annotation></semantics></math> of the tubular neighborhood <math id="A2.I44.ix1.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\nu N" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>ν</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>N</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\nu N</annotation></semantics></math> of <math id="A2.I44.ix1.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="N" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>N</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">N</annotation></semantics></math> rel boundary, namely a class in <math id="A2.I44.ix1.p1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\pi_{0}(\mathrm{Diff}_{\partial}(\nu N))" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>π</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>Diff</mi><mo>∂</mo></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>ν</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>N</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\pi_{0}(\mathrm{Diff}_{\partial}(\nu N))</annotation></semantics></math>, one can “implant” it into <math id="A2.I44.ix1.p1.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="M" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>M</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">M</annotation></semantics></math> to get a mapping class of <math id="A2.I44.ix1.p1.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="M" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>M</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">M</annotation></semantics></math> by extending <math id="A2.I44.ix1.p1.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\phi" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>ϕ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\phi</annotation></semantics></math> by identity outside <math id="A2.I44.ix1.p1.m10" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\nu N" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>ν</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>N</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\nu N</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>
</div></li>
<li id="A2.I44.ix2" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">ii.</span> 
<div id="A2.I44.ix2.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A2.I44.ix2.p1.1" class="ltx_p">In the case when <math id="A2.I44.ix2.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="N\subset M" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>N</mi><mo>⊂</mo><mi>M</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">N\subset M</annotation></semantics></math> is of codimension <math id="A2.I44.ix2.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mn>1</mn><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">1</annotation></semantics></math> and is two-sided, we know <math id="A2.I44.ix2.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\nu N\cong I\times N" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>ν</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>N</mi></mrow><mo>≅</mo><mrow><mi>I</mi><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><mi>N</mi></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\nu N\cong I\times N</annotation></semantics></math>. For any <math id="A2.I44.ix2.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\alpha\in\pi_{1}(\mathrm{Diff}(N),id_{N})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>α</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><msub><mi>π</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>Diff</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>N</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>d</mi><mi>N</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\alpha\in\pi_{1}(\mathrm{Diff}(N),id_{N})</annotation></semantics></math>, one can “implant” it near <math id="A2.I44.ix2.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="N" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>N</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">N</annotation></semantics></math> by picking a based loop in <math id="A2.I44.ix2.p1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathrm{Diff}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>Diff</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathrm{Diff}</annotation></semantics></math> representing <math id="A2.I44.ix2.p1.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\alpha" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>α</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\alpha</annotation></semantics></math>, put it into <math id="A2.I44.ix2.p1.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="I\times N\cong\nu N" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>I</mi><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><mi>N</mi></mrow><mo>≅</mo><mrow><mi>ν</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>N</mi></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">I\times N\cong\nu N</annotation></semantics></math> and extend by identity outside <math id="A2.I44.ix2.p1.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\nu N" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>ν</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>N</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\nu N</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>
</div></li>
</ol>
<p id="A2.SS11.SSS2.Px1.p8.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.SS11.SSS2.Px1.p8.1.1" class="ltx_text">∎</span></p>
</div>
</div>
<div id="A2.SS11.SSS2.Px1.p9" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent"><span class="ltx_inline-block"><svg id="A2.SS11.SSS2.Px1.p9.pic1" class="ltx_picture" height="104.06" overflow="visible" version="1.1" viewBox="0 0 429.64 104.06" width="429.64"><g style="--ltx-stroke-color:#000000;--ltx-fill-color:#000000;" fill="#000000" stroke="#000000" stroke-width="0.4pt" transform="translate(0,104.06) matrix(1 0 0 -1 0 0)"><g style="--ltx-fill-color:#4D4D4D;" fill="#4D4D4D" fill-opacity="1.0"><path style="stroke:none" d="M 0 4.63 L 0 99.43 C 0 101.99 2.07 104.06 4.63 104.06 L 425.01 104.06 C 427.56 104.06 429.64 101.99 429.64 99.43 L 429.64 4.63 C 429.64 2.07 427.56 0 425.01 0 L 4.63 0 C 2.07 0 0 2.07 0 4.63 Z"></path></g><g style="--ltx-fill-color:#F9F9F9;" fill="#F9F9F9" fill-opacity="1.0"><path style="stroke:none" d="M 0.69 4.63 L 0.69 85.2 L 428.94 85.2 L 428.94 4.63 C 428.94 2.45 427.18 0.69 425.01 0.69 L 4.63 0.69 C 2.45 0.69 0.69 2.45 0.69 4.63 Z"></path></g><g fill-opacity="1.0" transform="matrix(1.0 0.0 0.0 1.0 20.38 89.83)"><foreignObject style="--ltx-fo-width:24.44em;--ltx-fo-height:0.69em;--ltx-fo-depth:0em;font-size:10pt;" height="9.61" overflow="visible" transform="matrix(1 0 0 -1 0 9.61)" width="338.18"><span class="ltx_foreignobject_container"><span class="ltx_foreignobject_content">
<span id="A2.SS11.SSS2.Px1.p9.pic1.1" class="ltx_inline-block ltx_minipage ltx_align_bottom" style="width:24.44em;">
<span id="A2.SS11.SSS2.Px1.p9.pic1.1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.SS11.SSS2.Px1.p9.pic1.1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold" style="--ltx-fg-color:#FFFFFF;">Rubric</span></span>
</span></span></span></foreignObject></g><g fill-opacity="1.0" transform="matrix(1.0 0.0 0.0 1.0 20.38 15.27)"><foreignObject style="--ltx-fo-width:33.06em;--ltx-fo-height:4.2em;--ltx-fo-depth:0.2em;font-size:10pt;" height="60.88" overflow="visible" transform="matrix(1 0 0 -1 0 58.12)" width="457.46"><span class="ltx_foreignobject_container"><span class="ltx_foreignobject_content">
<span id="A2.SS11.SSS2.Px1.p9.pic1.2" class="ltx_inline-block ltx_minipage ltx_align_bottom" style="width:33.06em;">
<span id="A2.SS11.SSS2.Px1.p9.pic1.2.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.SS11.SSS2.Px1.p9.pic1.2.1.1" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:80%;--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">1 point for a reasonable simultaneous generalization (part i).
<br class="ltx_break">1 point for a reasonable generalization to (1)(2) that is not a generalization of (3), for example by exploiting the product structure of the tubular neighborhood (part (ii)).</span></span>
</span></span></span></foreignObject></g></g></svg></span>
</div>
<div id="A2.SS11.SSS2.Px1.p10" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent"><span class="ltx_inline-block"><svg id="A2.SS11.SSS2.Px1.p10.pic1" class="ltx_picture" height="54.13" overflow="visible" version="1.1" viewBox="0 0 429.64 54.13" width="429.64"><g style="--ltx-stroke-color:#000000;--ltx-fill-color:#000000;" fill="#000000" stroke="#000000" stroke-width="0.4pt" transform="translate(0,54.13) matrix(1 0 0 -1 0 0)"><g style="--ltx-fill-color:#5A996B;" fill="#5A996B" fill-opacity="1.0"><path style="stroke:none" d="M 0 4.63 L 0 49.51 C 0 52.06 2.07 54.13 4.63 54.13 L 425.01 54.13 C 427.56 54.13 429.64 52.06 429.64 49.51 L 429.64 4.63 C 429.64 2.07 427.56 0 425.01 0 L 4.63 0 C 2.07 0 0 2.07 0 4.63 Z"></path></g><g style="--ltx-fill-color:#F6FFF9;" fill="#F6FFF9" fill-opacity="1.0"><path style="stroke:none" d="M 0.69 4.63 L 0.69 35.38 L 428.94 35.38 L 428.94 4.63 C 428.94 2.45 427.18 0.69 425.01 0.69 L 4.63 0.69 C 2.45 0.69 0.69 2.45 0.69 4.63 Z"></path></g><g fill-opacity="1.0" transform="matrix(1.0 0.0 0.0 1.0 20.38 40.01)"><foreignObject style="--ltx-fo-width:24.44em;--ltx-fo-height:0.69em;--ltx-fo-depth:0em;font-size:10pt;" height="9.49" overflow="visible" transform="matrix(1 0 0 -1 0 9.49)" width="338.18"><span class="ltx_foreignobject_container"><span class="ltx_foreignobject_content">
<span id="A2.SS11.SSS2.Px1.p10.pic1.1" class="ltx_inline-block ltx_minipage ltx_align_bottom" style="width:24.44em;">
