<span id="A2.SS12.SSS1.Px1.p16.pic1.1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.SS12.SSS1.Px1.p16.pic1.1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold" style="--ltx-fg-color:#FFFFFF;">Evaluation</span></span>
</span></span></span></foreignObject></g><g fill-opacity="1.0" transform="matrix(1.0 0.0 0.0 1.0 20.38 15.27)"><foreignObject style="--ltx-fo-width:33.06em;--ltx-fo-height:1.8em;--ltx-fo-depth:0.2em;font-size:10pt;" height="27.67" overflow="visible" transform="matrix(1 0 0 -1 0 24.91)" width="457.46"><span class="ltx_foreignobject_container"><span class="ltx_foreignobject_content">
<span id="A2.SS12.SSS1.Px1.p16.pic1.2" class="ltx_inline-block ltx_minipage ltx_align_bottom" style="width:33.06em;">
<span id="A2.SS12.SSS1.Px1.p16.pic1.2.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.SS12.SSS1.Px1.p16.pic1.2.1.1" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:80%;--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">The questions mentioned in the answer are meaningful,
such as: (1) restriction and locality, (2) reversibility, and (3) near-critical scaling limits.</span></span>
</span></span></span></foreignObject></g></g></svg></span>
</div>
</section>
</section>
<section id="A2.SS12.SSS2" class="ltx_subsubsection">
<h4 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsubsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsubsection">(b) </span>Inventing new methods or approaches</h4>

<section id="A2.SS12.SSS2.Px1" class="ltx_paragraph">
<h5 class="ltx_title ltx_title_paragraph" style="--ltx-fg-color:#00E000;">Problem 12b1 </h5>

<div id="A2.SS12.SSS2.Px1.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A2.SS12.SSS2.Px1.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.SS12.SSS2.Px1.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text"></span>
<br class="ltx_break" style="--ltx-break-space:-10.0pt;"></p>
</div>
<div id="A2.SS12.SSS2.Px1.p2" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent"><span class="ltx_inline-block"><svg id="A2.SS12.SSS2.Px1.p2.pic1" class="ltx_picture" height="127.74" overflow="visible" version="1.1" viewBox="0 0 429.64 127.74" width="429.64"><g style="--ltx-stroke-color:#000000;--ltx-fill-color:#000000;" fill="#000000" stroke="#000000" stroke-width="0.4pt" transform="translate(0,127.74) matrix(1 0 0 -1 0 0)"><g style="--ltx-fill-color:#3D6666;" fill="#3D6666" fill-opacity="1.0"><path style="stroke:none" d="M 0 4.63 L 0 123.11 C 0 125.67 2.07 127.74 4.63 127.74 L 425.01 127.74 C 427.56 127.74 429.64 125.67 429.64 123.11 L 429.64 4.63 C 429.64 2.07 427.56 0 425.01 0 L 4.63 0 C 2.07 0 0 2.07 0 4.63 Z"></path></g><g style="--ltx-fill-color:#F9F9F9;" fill="#F9F9F9" fill-opacity="1.0"><path style="stroke:none" d="M 0.69 4.63 L 0.69 108.87 L 428.94 108.87 L 428.94 4.63 C 428.94 2.45 427.18 0.69 425.01 0.69 L 4.63 0.69 C 2.45 0.69 0.69 2.45 0.69 4.63 Z"></path></g><g fill-opacity="1.0" transform="matrix(1.0 0.0 0.0 1.0 20.38 113.5)"><foreignObject style="--ltx-fo-width:24.44em;--ltx-fo-height:0.69em;--ltx-fo-depth:0em;font-size:10pt;" height="9.61" overflow="visible" transform="matrix(1 0 0 -1 0 9.61)" width="338.18"><span class="ltx_foreignobject_container"><span class="ltx_foreignobject_content">
<span id="A2.SS12.SSS2.Px1.p2.pic1.1" class="ltx_inline-block ltx_minipage ltx_align_bottom" style="width:24.44em;">
<span id="A2.SS12.SSS2.Px1.p2.pic1.1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.SS12.SSS2.Px1.p2.pic1.1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold" style="--ltx-fg-color:#FFFFFF;">Problem</span></span>
</span></span></span></foreignObject></g><g fill-opacity="1.0" transform="matrix(1.0 0.0 0.0 1.0 20.38 14.66)"><foreignObject style="--ltx-fo-width:32.01em;--ltx-fo-height:5.96em;--ltx-fo-depth:0.16em;font-size:10pt;" height="84.56" overflow="visible" transform="matrix(1 0 0 -1 0 82.41)" width="442.93"><span class="ltx_foreignobject_container"><span class="ltx_foreignobject_content">
<span id="A2.SS12.SSS2.Px1.p2.pic1.2" class="ltx_inline-block ltx_minipage ltx_align_bottom" style="width:32.01em;">
<span id="A2.SS12.SSS2.Px1.p2.pic1.2.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.SS12.SSS2.Px1.p2.pic1.2.1.1" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:80%;--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">Find at least two solutions to 1977 IMO Problem 2:
In a finite sequence of real numbers the sum of any seven successive terms is negative and the sum of any eleven successive terms is positive. Determine the maximum number of terms in the sequence.</span></span>
<span id="A2.SS12.SSS2.Px1.p2.pic1.2.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.SS12.SSS2.Px1.p2.pic1.2.2.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic" style="font-size:80%;--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">Proposed by Jiaxin Zhang</span></span>
</span></span></span></foreignObject></g></g></svg></span>
</div>
<div id="A2.SS12.SSS2.Px1.1" class="ltx_proof">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_font_italic ltx_title_proof">IMO 1977/2.</h6>
<div id="A2.SS12.SSS2.Px1.p3" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A2.SS12.SSS2.Px1.p3.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.SS12.SSS2.Px1.p3.1.1" class="ltx_text">In a finite sequence of real numbers the sum of any seven successive terms is negative
and the sum of any eleven successive terms is positive. Determine the maximum number of terms.</span></p>
</div>
<div id="A2.SS12.SSS2.Px1.p4" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A2.SS12.SSS2.Px1.p4.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.SS12.SSS2.Px1.p4.1.1" class="ltx_text">The maximum possible length is <math id="A2.SS12.SSS2.Px1.p4.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\boxed{16}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><menclose notation="box"><mn>16</mn></menclose><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\boxed{16}</annotation></semantics></math>.</span></p>
</div>
<div id="A2.SS12.SSS2.Px1.1.1" class="ltx_proof">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_font_italic ltx_title_proof">Upper bound I: double-counting of sliding blocks.</h6>
<div id="A2.SS12.SSS2.Px1.p5" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A2.SS12.SSS2.Px1.p5.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.SS12.SSS2.Px1.p5.1.1" class="ltx_text">Let <math id="A2.SS12.SSS2.Px1.p5.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="a_{1},\dots,a_{n}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>a</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>a</mi><mi>n</mi></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">a_{1},\dots,a_{n}</annotation></semantics></math> be the sequence. For <math id="A2.SS12.SSS2.Px1.p5.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="L\in\{7,11\}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>L</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mrow><mn>7</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>11</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">L\in\{7,11\}</annotation></semantics></math> define</span></p>
<table id="A2.Ex361" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A2.Ex361.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="S_{k}^{(L)}\;=\;\sum_{i=0}^{L-1}a_{k+i}\qquad(1\leq k\leq n-L+1)." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><msubsup><mi>S</mi><mi>k</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>L</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup><mo lspace="0.558em" rspace="0.391em">=</mo><mrow><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><mrow><mi>L</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></munderover><msub><mi>a</mi><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>+</mo><mi>i</mi></mrow></msub></mrow></mrow><mspace style="width:2em;" width="2em"></mspace><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>≤</mo><mi>k</mi><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>−</mo><mi>L</mi></mrow><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">S_{k}^{(L)}\;=\;\sum_{i=0}^{L-1}a_{k+i}\qquad(1\leq k\leq n-L+1).</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A2.SS12.SSS2.Px1.p5.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.SS12.SSS2.Px1.p5.2.1" class="ltx_text">The hypotheses say <math id="A2.SS12.SSS2.Px1.p5.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="S_{k}^{(7)}&lt;0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msubsup><mi>S</mi><mi>k</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>7</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup><mo>&lt;</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">S_{k}^{(7)}&lt;0</annotation></semantics></math> for all <math id="A2.SS12.SSS2.Px1.p5.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="k" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>k</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">k</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="A2.SS12.SSS2.Px1.p5.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="S_{k}^{(11)}&gt;0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msubsup><mi>S</mi><mi>k</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>11</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup><mo>&gt;</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">S_{k}^{(11)}&gt;0</annotation></semantics></math> for all <math id="A2.SS12.SSS2.Px1.p5.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="k" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>k</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">k</annotation></semantics></math>.</span></p>
</div>
<div id="A2.SS12.SSS2.Px1.p6" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A2.SS12.SSS2.Px1.p6.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.SS12.SSS2.Px1.p6.1.1" class="ltx_text">Assume <math id="A2.SS12.SSS2.Px1.p6.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="n\geq 17" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>≥</mo><mn>17</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">n\geq 17</annotation></semantics></math>. Consider the total sums</span></p>
<table id="A2.Ex362" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A2.Ex362.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Sigma_{7}:=\sum_{k=1}^{\,n-6}S_{k}^{(7)},\qquad\Sigma_{11}:=\sum_{k=1}^{\,n-10}S_{k}^{(11)}." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Σ</mi><mn>7</mn></msub><mo rspace="0.111em">:=</mo><mrow><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>6</mn></mrow></munderover><msubsup><mi>S</mi><mi>k</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>7</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="2.167em">,</mo><mrow><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Σ</mi><mn>11</mn></msub><mo rspace="0.111em">:=</mo><mrow><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>10</mn></mrow></munderover><msubsup><mi>S</mi><mi>k</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>11</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Sigma_{7}:=\sum_{k=1}^{\,n-6}S_{k}^{(7)},\qquad\Sigma_{11}:=\sum_{k=1}^{\,n-10}S_{k}^{(11)}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A2.SS12.SSS2.Px1.p6.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.SS12.SSS2.Px1.p6.2.1" class="ltx_text">Each <math id="A2.SS12.SSS2.Px1.p6.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="a_{i}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>a</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">a_{i}</annotation></semantics></math> appears in <math id="A2.SS12.SSS2.Px1.p6.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Sigma_{L}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Σ</mi><mi>L</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Sigma_{L}</annotation></semantics></math> with multiplicity</span></p>
<table id="A2.Ex363" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A2.Ex363.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="m_{L}(i)=\#\{k:\ 1\leq k\leq n-L+1,\ k\leq i\leq k+L-1\}=\bigl|\,[i-L+1,i]\cap[1,n-L+1]\,\bigr|." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>m</mi><mi>L</mi></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>i</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>=</mo><mi>#</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mi>k</mi><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mn> 1</mn><mo>≤</mo><mi>k</mi><mo>≤</mo><mi>n</mi><mo>−</mo><mi>L</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn><mo rspace="0.667em">,</mo><mi>k</mi><mo>≤</mo><mi>i</mi><mo>≤</mo><mi>k</mi><mo>+</mo><mi>L</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow><mo rspace="0em">=</mo><mo fence="false" maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em" rspace="0.337em" stretchy="true">|</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mi>i</mi><mo>−</mo><mi>L</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>,</mo><mi>i</mi><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><mo>∩</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>,</mo><mi>n</mi><mo>−</mo><mi>L</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn><mo rspace="0.170em" stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><mo fence="false" maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em" stretchy="true">|</mo><mo lspace="0.167em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">m_{L}(i)=\#\{k:\ 1\leq k\leq n-L+1,\ k\leq i\leq k+L-1\}=\bigl|\,[i-L+1,i]\cap[1,n-L+1]\,\bigr|.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A2.SS12.SSS2.Px1.p6.3" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.SS12.SSS2.Px1.p6.3.1" class="ltx_text">For <math id="A2.SS12.SSS2.Px1.p6.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="n=17" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>17</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">n=17</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="A2.SS12.SSS2.Px1.p6.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="L\in\{7,11\}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>L</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mrow><mn>7</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>11</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">L\in\{7,11\}</annotation></semantics></math> one checks</span></p>
<table id="A2.Ex364" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A2.Ex364.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="m_{7}(i)=m_{11}(i)=\min\{\,i,\;18-i,\;7\,\}\qquad(1\leq i\leq 17)." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>m</mi><mn>7</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>i</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><msub><mi>m</mi><mn>11</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>i</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>min</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo rspace="0.170em" stretchy="false">{</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>,</mo><mrow><mn> 18</mn><mo>−</mo><mi>i</mi></mrow><mo>,</mo><mn> 7</mn></mrow><mo lspace="0.170em" stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mspace style="width:2em;" width="2em"></mspace><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>≤</mo><mi>i</mi><mo>≤</mo><mn>17</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">m_{7}(i)=m_{11}(i)=\min\{\,i,\;18-i,\;7\,\}\qquad(1\leq i\leq 17).</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A2.SS12.SSS2.Px1.p6.4" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.SS12.SSS2.Px1.p6.4.1" class="ltx_text">Hence <math id="A2.SS12.SSS2.Px1.p6.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Sigma_{7}=\sum_{i=1}^{17}m_{7}(i)a_{i}=\sum_{i=1}^{17}m_{11}(i)a_{i}=\Sigma_{11}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Σ</mi><mn>7</mn></msub><mo rspace="0.111em">=</mo><mrow><msubsup><mo>∑</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mn>17</mn></msubsup><mrow><msub><mi>m</mi><mn>7</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>i</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>a</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.111em">=</mo><mrow><msubsup><mo>∑</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mn>17</mn></msubsup><mrow><msub><mi>m</mi><mn>11</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>i</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>a</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Σ</mi><mn>11</mn></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Sigma_{7}=\sum_{i=1}^{17}m_{7}(i)a_{i}=\sum_{i=1}^{17}m_{11}(i)a_{i}=\Sigma_{11}</annotation></semantics></math>.
But <math id="A2.SS12.SSS2.Px1.p6.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Sigma_{7}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Σ</mi><mn>7</mn></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Sigma_{7}</annotation></semantics></math> is a sum of <math id="A2.SS12.SSS2.Px1.p6.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="n-6=11" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>6</mn></mrow><mo>=</mo><mn>11</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">n-6=11</annotation></semantics></math> negative numbers, so <math id="A2.SS12.SSS2.Px1.p6.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Sigma_{7}&lt;0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Σ</mi><mn>7</mn></msub><mo>&lt;</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Sigma_{7}&lt;0</annotation></semantics></math>, while
<math id="A2.SS12.SSS2.Px1.p6.m10" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Sigma_{11}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Σ</mi><mn>11</mn></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Sigma_{11}</annotation></semantics></math> is a sum of <math id="A2.SS12.SSS2.Px1.p6.m11" class="ltx_Math" alttext="n-10=7" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>10</mn></mrow><mo>=</mo><mn>7</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">n-10=7</annotation></semantics></math> positive numbers, so <math id="A2.SS12.SSS2.Px1.p6.m12" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Sigma_{11}&gt;0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Σ</mi><mn>11</mn></msub><mo>&gt;</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Sigma_{11}&gt;0</annotation></semantics></math>, a contradiction.
Therefore <math id="A2.SS12.SSS2.Px1.p6.m13" class="ltx_Math" alttext="n\leq 16" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>≤</mo><mn>16</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">n\leq 16</annotation></semantics></math>.
∎</span></p>
</div>
</div>
<div id="A2.SS12.SSS2.Px1.1.2" class="ltx_proof">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_font_italic ltx_title_proof">Upper bound II: prefix-sum/minimum argument.</h6>
<div id="A2.SS12.SSS2.Px1.p7" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A2.SS12.SSS2.Px1.p7.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.SS12.SSS2.Px1.p7.1.1" class="ltx_text">Let <math id="A2.SS12.SSS2.Px1.p7.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="A_{0}:=0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>A</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo>:=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">A_{0}:=0</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="A2.SS12.SSS2.Px1.p7.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="A_{k}:=\sum_{i=1}^{k}a_{i}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>A</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><mo rspace="0.111em">:=</mo><mrow><msubsup><mo>∑</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>k</mi></msubsup><msub><mi>a</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">A_{k}:=\sum_{i=1}^{k}a_{i}</annotation></semantics></math> for <math id="A2.SS12.SSS2.Px1.p7.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="1\leq k\leq n" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>≤</mo><mi>k</mi><mo>≤</mo><mi>n</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">1\leq k\leq n</annotation></semantics></math>.
The conditions are equivalent to</span></p>
<table id="A2.Ex365" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A2.Ex365.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="A_{i+7}-A_{i}&lt;0\quad(0\leq i\leq n-7),\qquad A_{i+11}-A_{i}&gt;0\quad(0\leq i\leq n-11)." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>A</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>7</mn></mrow></msub><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>A</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></mrow><mo>&lt;</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><mspace style="width:1em;" width="1em"></mspace><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>0</mn><mo>≤</mo><mi>i</mi><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>7</mn></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo rspace="2.167em">,</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>A</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>11</mn></mrow></msub><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>A</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></mrow><mo>&gt;</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><mspace style="width:1em;" width="1em"></mspace><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>0</mn><mo>≤</mo><mi>i</mi><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>11</mn></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">A_{i+7}-A_{i}&lt;0\quad(0\leq i\leq n-7),\qquad A_{i+11}-A_{i}&gt;0\quad(0\leq i\leq n-11).</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A2.SS12.SSS2.Px1.p7.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.SS12.SSS2.Px1.p7.2.1" class="ltx_text">Assume <math id="A2.SS12.SSS2.Px1.p7.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="n\geq 17" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>≥</mo><mn>17</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">n\geq 17</annotation></semantics></math> and choose <math id="A2.SS12.SSS2.Px1.p7.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="m\in\{0,1,\dots,17\}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>m</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mrow><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>,</mo><mn>17</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">m\in\{0,1,\dots,17\}</annotation></semantics></math> with <math id="A2.SS12.SSS2.Px1.p7.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="A_{m}=\min\{A_{0},\dots,A_{17}\}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>A</mi><mi>m</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>min</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><msub><mi>A</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>A</mi><mn>17</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">A_{m}=\min\{A_{0},\dots,A_{17}\}</annotation></semantics></math>.
If <math id="A2.SS12.SSS2.Px1.p7.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="m\leq 10" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>m</mi><mo>≤</mo><mn>10</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">m\leq 10</annotation></semantics></math>, then <math id="A2.SS12.SSS2.Px1.p7.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="A_{m+7}-A_{m}&lt;0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>A</mi><mrow><mi>m</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>7</mn></mrow></msub><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>A</mi><mi>m</mi></msub></mrow><mo>&lt;</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">A_{m+7}-A_{m}&lt;0</annotation></semantics></math> gives <math id="A2.SS12.SSS2.Px1.p7.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="A_{m+7}&lt;A_{m}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>A</mi><mrow><mi>m</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>7</mn></mrow></msub><mo>&lt;</mo><msub><mi>A</mi><mi>m</mi></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">A_{m+7}&lt;A_{m}</annotation></semantics></math>, contradicting minimality.
If <math id="A2.SS12.SSS2.Px1.p7.m10" class="ltx_Math" alttext="m\geq 11" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>m</mi><mo>≥</mo><mn>11</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">m\geq 11</annotation></semantics></math>, then <math id="A2.SS12.SSS2.Px1.p7.m11" class="ltx_Math" alttext="A_{m}-A_{m-11}&gt;0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>A</mi><mi>m</mi></msub><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>A</mi><mrow><mi>m</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>11</mn></mrow></msub></mrow><mo>&gt;</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">A_{m}-A_{m-11}&gt;0</annotation></semantics></math> gives <math id="A2.SS12.SSS2.Px1.p7.m12" class="ltx_Math" alttext="A_{m}&gt;A_{m-11}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>A</mi><mi>m</mi></msub><mo>&gt;</mo><msub><mi>A</mi><mrow><mi>m</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>11</mn></mrow></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">A_{m}&gt;A_{m-11}</annotation></semantics></math>, again a contradiction.
Thus <math id="A2.SS12.SSS2.Px1.p7.m13" class="ltx_Math" alttext="n\leq 16" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>≤</mo><mn>16</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">n\leq 16</annotation></semantics></math>.
∎</span></p>
</div>
</div>
<div id="A2.SS12.SSS2.Px1.p8" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A2.SS12.SSS2.Px1.p8.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.SS12.SSS2.Px1.p8.1.1" class="ltx_text">Sharpness (<math id="A2.SS12.SSS2.Px1.p8.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="n=16" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>16</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">n=16</annotation></semantics></math> is attainable).
Place large negatives at positions <math id="A2.SS12.SSS2.Px1.p8.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="3,7,10,14" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mn>3</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>7</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>10</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>14</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">3,7,10,14</annotation></semantics></math> and a small positive value elsewhere.
Then every block of <math id="A2.SS12.SSS2.Px1.p8.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="7" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mn>7</mn><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">7</annotation></semantics></math> consecutive indices contains exactly <math id="A2.SS12.SSS2.Px1.p8.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="2" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mn>2</mn><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">2</annotation></semantics></math> of these four positions,
and every block of <math id="A2.SS12.SSS2.Px1.p8.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="11" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mn>11</mn><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">11</annotation></semantics></math> consecutive indices contains exactly <math id="A2.SS12.SSS2.Px1.p8.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="3" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mn>3</mn><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">3</annotation></semantics></math> of them; hence if</span></p>
<table id="A2.Ex366" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A2.Ex366.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="a_{i}=\begin{cases}-p&amp;\text{for }i\in\{3,7,10,14\},\\
q&amp;\text{otherwise},\end{cases}\qquad\text{with }5q-2p&lt;0\ \text{ and }\ 8q-3p&gt;0," display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>a</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo>{</mo><mtable columnspacing="5pt" displaystyle="true" rowspacing="0pt"><mtr><mtd class="ltx_align_left" columnalign="left"><mrow><mo>−</mo><mi>p</mi></mrow></mtd><mtd class="ltx_align_left" columnalign="left"><mrow><mrow><mrow><mtext>for </mtext><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>i</mi></mrow><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mrow><mn>3</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>7</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>10</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>14</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow></mtd></mtr><mtr><mtd class="ltx_align_left" columnalign="left"><mi>q</mi></mtd><mtd class="ltx_align_left" columnalign="left"><mrow><mtext>otherwise</mtext><mo>,</mo></mrow></mtd></mtr></mtable></mrow></mrow><mspace style="width:2em;" width="2em"></mspace><mrow><mrow><mrow><mtext>with </mtext><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mn>5</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>q</mi></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>p</mi></mrow></mrow><mo>&lt;</mo><mrow><mrow><mn>0</mn><mo lspace="0.500em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mtext> and </mtext><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mn> 8</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>q</mi></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mn>3</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>p</mi></mrow></mrow><mo>&gt;</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">a_{i}=\begin{cases}-p&amp;\text{for }i\in\{3,7,10,14\},\\
q&amp;\text{otherwise},\end{cases}\qquad\text{with }5q-2p&lt;0\ \text{ and }\ 8q-3p&gt;0,</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A2.SS12.SSS2.Px1.p8.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.SS12.SSS2.Px1.p8.2.1" class="ltx_text">all <math id="A2.SS12.SSS2.Px1.p8.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="7" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mn>7</mn><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">7</annotation></semantics></math>-sums are negative and all <math id="A2.SS12.SSS2.Px1.p8.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="11" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mn>11</mn><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">11</annotation></semantics></math>-sums are positive. Choosing, for instance,
<math id="A2.SS12.SSS2.Px1.p8.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(q,p)=(5,13)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>q</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>p</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>5</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>13</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(q,p)=(5,13)</annotation></semantics></math> or <math id="A2.SS12.SSS2.Px1.p8.m10" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(q,p)=(7,18)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>q</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>p</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>7</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>18</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(q,p)=(7,18)</annotation></semantics></math> yields two explicit solutions:</span></p>
<table id="A2.Ex367" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A2.Ex367X"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A2.Ex367X.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\text{Solution A:}\quad(5,\,5,\,-13,\,5,\,5,\,5,\,-13,\,5,\,5,\,-13,\,5,\,5,\,5,\,-13,\,5,\,5)," display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mtext>Solution A:</mtext><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>5</mn><mo>,</mo><mn> 5</mn><mo>,</mo><mo lspace="0em">−</mo><mn>13</mn><mo>,</mo><mn> 5</mn><mo>,</mo><mn> 5</mn><mo>,</mo><mn> 5</mn><mo>,</mo><mo lspace="0em">−</mo><mn>13</mn><mo>,</mo><mn> 5</mn><mo>,</mo><mn> 5</mn><mo>,</mo><mo lspace="0em">−</mo><mn>13</mn><mo>,</mo><mn> 5</mn><mo>,</mo><mn> 5</mn><mo>,</mo><mn> 5</mn><mo>,</mo><mo lspace="0em">−</mo><mn>13</mn><mo>,</mo><mn> 5</mn><mo>,</mo><mn> 5</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\text{Solution A:}\quad(5,\,5,\,-13,\,5,\,5,\,5,\,-13,\,5,\,5,\,-13,\,5,\,5,\,5,\,-13,\,5,\,5),</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A2.Ex367Xa"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A2.Ex367Xa.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\text{Solution B:}\quad(7,\,7,\,-18,\,7,\,7,\,7,\,-18,\,7,\,7,\,-18,\,7,\,7,\,7,\,-18,\,7,\,7)." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mtext>Solution B:</mtext><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>7</mn><mo>,</mo><mn> 7</mn><mo>,</mo><mo lspace="0em">−</mo><mn>18</mn><mo>,</mo><mn> 7</mn><mo>,</mo><mn> 7</mn><mo>,</mo><mn> 7</mn><mo>,</mo><mo lspace="0em">−</mo><mn>18</mn><mo>,</mo><mn> 7</mn><mo>,</mo><mn> 7</mn><mo>,</mo><mo lspace="0em">−</mo><mn>18</mn><mo>,</mo><mn> 7</mn><mo>,</mo><mn> 7</mn><mo>,</mo><mn> 7</mn><mo>,</mo><mo lspace="0em">−</mo><mn>18</mn><mo>,</mo><mn> 7</mn><mo>,</mo><mn> 7</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\text{Solution B:}\quad(7,\,7,\,-18,\,7,\,7,\,7,\,-18,\,7,\,7,\,-18,\,7,\,7,\,7,\,-18,\,7,\,7).</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A2.SS12.SSS2.Px1.p8.3" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.SS12.SSS2.Px1.p8.3.1" class="ltx_text">In A, each <math id="A2.SS12.SSS2.Px1.p8.m11" class="ltx_Math" alttext="7" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mn>7</mn><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">7</annotation></semantics></math>-sum equals <math id="A2.SS12.SSS2.Px1.p8.m12" class="ltx_Math" alttext="5\cdot 5-2\cdot 13=-1&lt;0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mn>5</mn><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><mn>5</mn></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><mn>13</mn></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo>&lt;</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">5\cdot 5-2\cdot 13=-1&lt;0</annotation></semantics></math> and each <math id="A2.SS12.SSS2.Px1.p8.m13" class="ltx_Math" alttext="11" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mn>11</mn><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">11</annotation></semantics></math>-sum equals <math id="A2.SS12.SSS2.Px1.p8.m14" class="ltx_Math" alttext="8\cdot 5-3\cdot 13=1&gt;0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mn>8</mn><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><mn>5</mn></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mn>3</mn><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><mn>13</mn></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>&gt;</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">8\cdot 5-3\cdot 13=1&gt;0</annotation></semantics></math>.
In B, each <math id="A2.SS12.SSS2.Px1.p8.m15" class="ltx_Math" alttext="7" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mn>7</mn><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">7</annotation></semantics></math>-sum equals <math id="A2.SS12.SSS2.Px1.p8.m16" class="ltx_Math" alttext="5\cdot 7-2\cdot 18=-1&lt;0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mn>5</mn><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><mn>7</mn></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><mn>18</mn></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo>&lt;</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">5\cdot 7-2\cdot 18=-1&lt;0</annotation></semantics></math> and each <math id="A2.SS12.SSS2.Px1.p8.m17" class="ltx_Math" alttext="11" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mn>11</mn><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">11</annotation></semantics></math>-sum equals <math id="A2.SS12.SSS2.Px1.p8.m18" class="ltx_Math" alttext="8\cdot 7-3\cdot 18=2&gt;0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mn>8</mn><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><mn>7</mn></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mn>3</mn><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><mn>18</mn></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mn>2</mn><mo>&gt;</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">8\cdot 7-3\cdot 18=2&gt;0</annotation></semantics></math>.
Therefore the maximum length is <math id="A2.SS12.SSS2.Px1.p8.m19" class="ltx_Math" alttext="16" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mn>16</mn><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">16</annotation></semantics></math>.</span></p>
</div>
<div id="A2.SS12.SSS2.Px1.p9" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A2.SS12.SSS2.Px1.p9.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.SS12.SSS2.Px1.p9.1.1" class="ltx_text">∎</span></p>
</div>
</div>
<div id="A2.SS12.SSS2.Px1.2" class="ltx_proof">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_font_italic ltx_title_proof"><span id="A2.SS12.SSS2.Px1.2.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Standard Solution</span>.</h6>
<div id="A2.SS12.SSS2.Px1.p10" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A2.SS12.SSS2.Px1.p10.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.SS12.SSS2.Px1.p10.1.1" class="ltx_text">Solution 1: Construction for <math id="A2.SS12.SSS2.Px1.p10.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="n=16" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>16</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">n=16</annotation></semantics></math>. Define</span></p>
<table id="A2.Ex368" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A2.Ex368.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="a_{j}=\begin{cases}-13,&amp;j\in\{3,7,10,14\},\\
5,&amp;\text{otherwise}.\end{cases}" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>a</mi><mi>j</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo>{</mo><mtable columnspacing="5pt" displaystyle="true" rowspacing="0pt"><mtr><mtd class="ltx_align_left" columnalign="left"><mrow><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>13</mn></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow></mtd><mtd class="ltx_align_left" columnalign="left"><mrow><mrow><mi>j</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mrow><mn>3</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>7</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>10</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>14</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow></mtd></mtr><mtr><mtd class="ltx_align_left" columnalign="left"><mrow><mn>5</mn><mo>,</mo></mrow></mtd><mtd class="ltx_align_left" columnalign="left"><mrow><mtext>otherwise</mtext><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow></mtd></mtr></mtable></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">a_{j}=\begin{cases}-13,&amp;j\in\{3,7,10,14\},\\
5,&amp;\text{otherwise}.\end{cases}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A2.SS12.SSS2.Px1.p10.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.SS12.SSS2.Px1.p10.2.1" class="ltx_text">Any block of 7 consecutive terms then has exactly two entries equal to <math id="A2.SS12.SSS2.Px1.p10.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="-13" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>13</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">-13</annotation></semantics></math> and five entries equal to <math id="A2.SS12.SSS2.Px1.p10.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="5" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mn>5</mn><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">5</annotation></semantics></math>, so
<math id="A2.SS12.SSS2.Px1.p10.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="5\cdot 5-2\cdot 13=-1&lt;0." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mrow><mn>5</mn><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><mn>5</mn></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><mn>13</mn></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo>&lt;</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">5\cdot 5-2\cdot 13=-1&lt;0.</annotation></semantics></math>
Any block of 11 consecutive terms has exactly three entries equal to <math id="A2.SS12.SSS2.Px1.p10.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="-13" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>13</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">-13</annotation></semantics></math> and eight entries equal to <math id="A2.SS12.SSS2.Px1.p10.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="5" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mn>5</mn><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">5</annotation></semantics></math>, so
<math id="A2.SS12.SSS2.Px1.p10.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="8\cdot 5-3\cdot 13=1&gt;0." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mrow><mn>8</mn><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><mn>5</mn></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mn>3</mn><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><mn>13</mn></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>&gt;</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">8\cdot 5-3\cdot 13=1&gt;0.</annotation></semantics></math>
Thus the sequence meets the requirements.</span></p>
</div>
<div id="A2.SS12.SSS2.Px1.p11" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A2.SS12.SSS2.Px1.p11.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.SS12.SSS2.Px1.p11.1.1" class="ltx_text">Non<span id="A2.SS12.SSS2.Px1.p11.1.1.1" class="ltx_text">-</span>existence for <math id="A2.SS12.SSS2.Px1.p11.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="n\geq 17" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>≥</mo><mn>17</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">n\geq 17</annotation></semantics></math>. One checks (for example by linear<span id="A2.SS12.SSS2.Px1.p11.1.1.2" class="ltx_text">-</span>programming or averaging arguments) that the system</span></p>
<table id="A2.Ex369" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A2.Ex369.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\sum_{j=i}^{i+6}a_{j}&lt;0,\quad\sum_{j=i}^{i+10}a_{j}&gt;0" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>j</mi><mo>=</mo><mi>i</mi></mrow><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>6</mn></mrow></munderover><msub><mi>a</mi><mi>j</mi></msub></mrow><mo>&lt;</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><mo rspace="1.000em">,</mo><mrow><mrow><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>j</mi><mo>=</mo><mi>i</mi></mrow><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>10</mn></mrow></munderover><msub><mi>a</mi><mi>j</mi></msub></mrow><mo>&gt;</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\sum_{j=i}^{i+6}a_{j}&lt;0,\quad\sum_{j=i}^{i+10}a_{j}&gt;0</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A2.SS12.SSS2.Px1.p11.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.SS12.SSS2.Px1.p11.2.1" class="ltx_text">for <math id="A2.SS12.SSS2.Px1.p11.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="1\leq i\leq n-6" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>≤</mo><mi>i</mi><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>6</mn></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">1\leq i\leq n-6</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="A2.SS12.SSS2.Px1.p11.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="1\leq i\leq n-10" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>≤</mo><mi>i</mi><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>10</mn></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">1\leq i\leq n-10</annotation></semantics></math> has no solution once <math id="A2.SS12.SSS2.Px1.p11.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="n\geq 17" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>≥</mo><mn>17</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">n\geq 17</annotation></semantics></math>.</span></p>
</div>
<div id="A2.SS12.SSS2.Px1.p12" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A2.SS12.SSS2.Px1.p12.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.SS12.SSS2.Px1.p12.1.1" class="ltx_text">Hence the maximum possible length is <math id="A2.SS12.SSS2.Px1.p12.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\boxed{16}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><menclose notation="box"><mn>16</mn></menclose><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\boxed{16}</annotation></semantics></math>.</span></p>
</div>
<div id="A2.SS12.SSS2.Px1.p13" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A2.SS12.SSS2.Px1.p13.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.SS12.SSS2.Px1.p13.1.1" class="ltx_text">Solution 2:
Let <math id="A2.SS12.SSS2.Px1.p13.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="x_{1},x_{2},\ldots" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>x</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">x_{1},x_{2},\ldots</annotation></semantics></math> be the given sequence and let <math id="A2.SS12.SSS2.Px1.p13.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="s_{n}=x_{1}+x_{2}+\ldots+x_{n}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>s</mi><mi>n</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><msub><mi>x</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>+</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo>+</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>+</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>n</mi></msub></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">s_{n}=x_{1}+x_{2}+\ldots+x_{n}</annotation></semantics></math>. The conditions from the hypothesis can be now written as <math id="A2.SS12.SSS2.Px1.p13.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="s_{n+7}&lt;s_{n}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>s</mi><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>7</mn></mrow></msub><mo>&lt;</mo><msub><mi>s</mi><mi>n</mi></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">s_{n+7}&lt;s_{n}</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="A2.SS12.SSS2.Px1.p13.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="s_{n+11}&gt;s_{n}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>s</mi><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>11</mn></mrow></msub><mo>&gt;</mo><msub><mi>s</mi><mi>n</mi></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">s_{n+11}&gt;s_{n}</annotation></semantics></math> for all <math id="A2.SS12.SSS2.Px1.p13.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="n\geq 1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>≥</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">n\geq 1</annotation></semantics></math>. We then have:
<math id="A2.SS12.SSS2.Px1.p13.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="0&lt;s_{11}&lt;s_{4}&lt;s_{15}&lt;s_{8}&lt;s_{1}&lt;s_{12}&lt;s_{5}&lt;s_{16}&lt;s_{9}&lt;s_{2}&lt;s_{13}&lt;s_{6}&lt;s_{17}&lt;s_{10}&lt;s_{3}&lt;s_{14}&lt;s_{7}&lt;0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mn>0</mn><mo>&lt;</mo><msub><mi>s</mi><mn>11</mn></msub><mo>&lt;</mo><msub><mi>s</mi><mn>4</mn></msub><mo>&lt;</mo><msub><mi>s</mi><mn>15</mn></msub><mo>&lt;</mo><msub><mi>s</mi><mn>8</mn></msub><mo>&lt;</mo><msub><mi>s</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>&lt;</mo><msub><mi>s</mi><mn>12</mn></msub><mo>&lt;</mo><msub><mi>s</mi><mn>5</mn></msub><mo>&lt;</mo><msub><mi>s</mi><mn>16</mn></msub><mo>&lt;</mo><msub><mi>s</mi><mn>9</mn></msub><mo>&lt;</mo><msub><mi>s</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo>&lt;</mo><msub><mi>s</mi><mn>13</mn></msub><mo>&lt;</mo><msub><mi>s</mi><mn>6</mn></msub><mo>&lt;</mo><msub><mi>s</mi><mn>17</mn></msub><mo>&lt;</mo><msub><mi>s</mi><mn>10</mn></msub><mo>&lt;</mo><msub><mi>s</mi><mn>3</mn></msub><mo>&lt;</mo><msub><mi>s</mi><mn>14</mn></msub><mo>&lt;</mo><msub><mi>s</mi><mn>7</mn></msub><mo>&lt;</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">0&lt;s_{11}&lt;s_{4}&lt;s_{15}&lt;s_{8}&lt;s_{1}&lt;s_{12}&lt;s_{5}&lt;s_{16}&lt;s_{9}&lt;s_{2}&lt;s_{13}&lt;s_{6}&lt;s_{17}&lt;s_{10}&lt;s_{3}&lt;s_{14}&lt;s_{7}&lt;0</annotation></semantics></math>, a contradiction.
Therefore, the sequence cannot have 17 terms. In order to show that 16 is the answer, just take 16 real numbers satisfying <math id="A2.SS12.SSS2.Px1.p13.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="s_{10}&lt;s_{3}&lt;s_{14}&lt;s_{7}&lt;0&lt;s_{11}&lt;s_{4}&lt;s_{15}&lt;s_{8}&lt;s_{1}&lt;s_{12}&lt;s_{5}&lt;s_{16}&lt;s_{9}&lt;s_{2}&lt;s_{13}&lt;s_{6}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>s</mi><mn>10</mn></msub><mo>&lt;</mo><msub><mi>s</mi><mn>3</mn></msub><mo>&lt;</mo><msub><mi>s</mi><mn>14</mn></msub><mo>&lt;</mo><msub><mi>s</mi><mn>7</mn></msub><mo>&lt;</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>&lt;</mo><msub><mi>s</mi><mn>11</mn></msub><mo>&lt;</mo><msub><mi>s</mi><mn>4</mn></msub><mo>&lt;</mo><msub><mi>s</mi><mn>15</mn></msub><mo>&lt;</mo><msub><mi>s</mi><mn>8</mn></msub><mo>&lt;</mo><msub><mi>s</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>&lt;</mo><msub><mi>s</mi><mn>12</mn></msub><mo>&lt;</mo><msub><mi>s</mi><mn>5</mn></msub><mo>&lt;</mo><msub><mi>s</mi><mn>16</mn></msub><mo>&lt;</mo><msub><mi>s</mi><mn>9</mn></msub><mo>&lt;</mo><msub><mi>s</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo>&lt;</mo><msub><mi>s</mi><mn>13</mn></msub><mo>&lt;</mo><msub><mi>s</mi><mn>6</mn></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">s_{10}&lt;s_{3}&lt;s_{14}&lt;s_{7}&lt;0&lt;s_{11}&lt;s_{4}&lt;s_{15}&lt;s_{8}&lt;s_{1}&lt;s_{12}&lt;s_{5}&lt;s_{16}&lt;s_{9}&lt;s_{2}&lt;s_{13}&lt;s_{6}</annotation></semantics></math>. We have <math id="A2.SS12.SSS2.Px1.p13.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="x_{1}=s_{1}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>x</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>=</mo><msub><mi>s</mi><mn>1</mn></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">x_{1}=s_{1}</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="A2.SS12.SSS2.Px1.p13.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="x_{n}=s_{n}-s_{n-1}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>n</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><msub><mi>s</mi><mi>n</mi></msub><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>s</mi><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">x_{n}=s_{n}-s_{n-1}</annotation></semantics></math> for <math id="A2.SS12.SSS2.Px1.p13.m10" class="ltx_Math" alttext="n\geq 2" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>≥</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">n\geq 2</annotation></semantics></math>. Thus we found all sequences with the given properties.</span></p>
</div>
<div id="A2.SS12.SSS2.Px1.p14" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A2.SS12.SSS2.Px1.p14.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.SS12.SSS2.Px1.p14.1.1" class="ltx_text">∎</span></p>
</div>
</div>
<div id="A2.SS12.SSS2.Px1.p15" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent"><span class="ltx_inline-block"><svg id="A2.SS12.SSS2.Px1.p15.pic1" class="ltx_picture" height="54.25" overflow="visible" version="1.1" viewBox="0 0 429.64 54.25" width="429.64"><g style="--ltx-stroke-color:#000000;--ltx-fill-color:#000000;" fill="#000000" stroke="#000000" stroke-width="0.4pt" transform="translate(0,54.25) matrix(1 0 0 -1 0 0)"><g style="--ltx-fill-color:#4D4D4D;" fill="#4D4D4D" fill-opacity="1.0"><path style="stroke:none" d="M 0 4.63 L 0 49.62 C 0 52.18 2.07 54.25 4.63 54.25 L 425.01 54.25 C 427.56 54.25 429.64 52.18 429.64 49.62 L 429.64 4.63 C 429.64 2.07 427.56 0 425.01 0 L 4.63 0 C 2.07 0 0 2.07 0 4.63 Z"></path></g><g style="--ltx-fill-color:#F9F9F9;" fill="#F9F9F9" fill-opacity="1.0"><path style="stroke:none" d="M 0.69 4.63 L 0.69 35.38 L 428.94 35.38 L 428.94 4.63 C 428.94 2.45 427.18 0.69 425.01 0.69 L 4.63 0.69 C 2.45 0.69 0.69 2.45 0.69 4.63 Z"></path></g><g fill-opacity="1.0" transform="matrix(1.0 0.0 0.0 1.0 20.38 40.01)"><foreignObject style="--ltx-fo-width:24.44em;--ltx-fo-height:0.69em;--ltx-fo-depth:0em;font-size:10pt;" height="9.61" overflow="visible" transform="matrix(1 0 0 -1 0 9.61)" width="338.18"><span class="ltx_foreignobject_container"><span class="ltx_foreignobject_content">
